INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (14260,'f5775ed929','hey whats up im new and i c that un on the site so im jw how to post pics and vids?'),(14261,'65c8e327aa','hey im new im sending pm\'s to everyone i admier for there great work and maybe you can answer one of my questions on breaking news\r\n :cool:'),(14262,'65c8e327aa','hey im new im sending pm\'s to everyone i admier for there great work and maybe you can answer one of my questions on breaking news\r\n :cool:'),(16864,'f13911d0f6','ok, I am going to use the edit button from now on, ok, just so You know. :cool:'),(14264,'feeedfc66c','hey do u know where i can find ne how to\'s to make a body kit'),(14265,'fa5503e36b','There\'s no real step by step post, That I know of, on how to do a body kit.\r\nWhat you\'ll need to do depends totally on what body and what kind of kit you want. Try looking through the forums for ahh5hit\'s posts and darktari\"s posts. If I remember correctly they have posted some nice pictorials that you could follow.\r\nGood luck.'),(12493,'f4d329ba6a','[quote:f4d329ba6a=\"ph2t\"]Hey man, had a chance to look at this stuff further.\r\n\r\nFirst, just to confirm your results, is this correct?  I just wanted to confirm what I said confused me in my previous PM about the results for reverse. So the Grey wire stays at 2.54V all the time?  Hmmm....\r\n\r\n[img:f4d329ba6a]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/se_fet/results.jpg[/img:f4d329ba6a]\r\n\r\nHere\'s the excel spreadsheet I\'m using, just update that. :)\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/se_fet/results.xls[/url]\r\n\r\n\r\nTasks:\r\n\r\n1) Could you take some readings again but this time for 50% throttle in fwd and rev please.  I just want to see if the Grey wire changes potential or not.  Don\'t worry about the readings you get at this level of throttle, just record and advise. :)\r\n\r\n2) Could you take some pics of the pcb from every angle you believe important.  Inlcuding the wires that go to the motor.  Also the chassis containing the battery.\r\n\r\n3) What batteries are in these cars?  Are their two or just one?  The 1.8V you describe is a wierd value.\r\n\r\nFor all these tasks I\'ve set you up an FTP account to upload the pics/data to.\r\n\r\nSite: ftp.prahranpianos.com\r\nusername: crazydave@prahranpia\r\npwd: bitpimps\r\n\r\nYes the username is that format with the domain choped off.\r\n\r\nOnce again thanks for this.  With what you have given me already I think it can be done.  I just need some more info to confirm things.\r\n\r\nThanks mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:f4d329ba6a]Hey, what\'s up?\r\n\r\nYep you got the chart correct. I\'ll get those other readings, and the clearest pics I can possibly take this afternoon after work. \r\n\r\nTo answer question 3. The battery is 2 batteries, about half the size of a 1/4 AAA, stacked up and shrink wrapped so it looks like one battery that\'s a little longer than a standard one. With that in mind 2.8v makes sense at 1.4v per battery.\r\n\r\n...and thanks for hooking me up with server space for the pics. My wife gets sick of me wasting all her space for my \'silly\' cars.\r\n\r\nDave');
