7330');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21837,'b7505e8b1d','how do you set up a gallery on bitpimps?\r\n\r\n  I cant seem to find something on it.'),(21838,'b7505e8b1d','how do you set up a gallery on bitpimps?\r\n\r\n  I cant seem to find something on it.'),(21840,'e769515166','[quote:e769515166=\"VooDooMafia\"]how do you set up a gallery on bitpimps?\r\n\r\n  I cant seem to find something on it.[/quote:e769515166]you gotta register in the Galleries first, then once I know you\'ve registered, I can give you the proper permissions to create your own albums and stuff.'),(21841,'1a0eeb52f3','when I hit the register link it brings me to http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/register.php\r\n\r\nbut I get errors.  Is the page down?'),(21842,'1a0eeb52f3','when I hit the register link it brings me to http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/register.php\r\n\r\nbut I get errors.  Is the page down?'),(21854,'72b3e37c57','[quote:72b3e37c57=\"PINGO\"]okay but here ind denmark you cant by dogede challenger and them så do you no the name of a online shop? and at homie.tv you just cant buy one homi i relly want \"big spokey\" ore big dopey but i have to buy a set fore 25 dollars :???:[/quote:72b3e37c57]www.radioshack.com sells zipzaps, not sure if they ship to denmark or not.\r\nyour best bet for both the car/body or homie will be to make a post in the \"Lookin\' To Score\" forum and ask if anyone has what you want for sale.'),(21844,'85a7e82179','[quote:85a7e82179=\"VooDooMafia\"]when I hit the register link it brings me to http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/register.php\r\n\r\nbut I get errors.  Is the page down?[/quote:85a7e82179]well shiat.\r\nI can\'t believe that wasn\'t caught before. thanks man.\r\n\r\nok, try it now.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21845,'a3851ac66d','OK cool that worked lol\r\n\r\nLet me know on the PB\'s\r\n\r\n  I will also be updating the post with more stuff aswell.'),(21846,'a3851ac66d','OK cool that worked lol\r\n\r\nLet me know on the PB\'s\r\n\r\n  I will also be updating the post with more stuff aswell.'),(21850,'12dd91a781','you interested in that stuff?\r\n\r\n  If not let me know so I can repost it.'),(21852,'5fd1ec5172','Good stuff\r\n\r\nthanks'),(21853,'12dd91a781','you interested in that stuff?\r\n\r\n  If not let me know so I can repost it.'),(21848,'6c68e24dcb','[quote:6c68e24dcb=\"VooDooMafia\"]OK cool that worked lol\r\n\r\nLet me know on the PB\'s\r\n\r\n  I will also be updating the post with more stuff aswell.[/quote:6c68e24dcb]aight, got you all set to make your albums, you should see like 3 new buttons now when you login to the Galleries.'),(21849,'5fd1ec5172','Good stuff\r\n\r\nthanks'),(21860,'35455ae1e8','[quote:35455ae1e8=\"PINGO\"]i have ben cheated many times soo i dont know if i want to buy in here... yo dont have other sites? \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\naniway thanks[/quote:35455ae1e8]you haven\'t been cheated from this site, you\'ve never been here.\r\n(unless you meant you have been cheated in the past at places like ebay)\r\n\r\nno, I\'m sorry I don\'t have any other sites - I\'m not a shop - this is a personal and independant site.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21861,'96cf2e6485','i ment like ebay and many danish sites.... do you no why you cant buy set 1,2,3 in homis?'),(23846,'3da6005b3f','voodoopetek@yahoo.com is my yahoo \r\nbut I work till 3:30am tonight'),(34383,'5205be2f03','Good idea. The internal\'s of the metl-tech controller look pretty straitforward to remove. Keep me posted'),(34384,'c098ec8fcf','Thats good, i heard his first model was trigger type controller, and he changed it to this crap.  :???: What controller do you plan on using? I\'m sure you could get an epoch controller for a good price, i think SG219 was selling one for $7.50.'),(26641,'4c86c18ee5','hey my msn is : riisj@gbpackersfan.com ... Idont want to buy somthing i dont have monny'),(21864,'6a412cd236','[quote:6a412cd236=\"PINGO\"]i ment like ebay and many danish sites.... do you no why you cant buy set 1,2,3 in homis?[/quote:6a412cd236]I have no idea.\r\nmaybe they stopped making those series?'),(21865,'59e7aeafa8','Hey Cabo, your editing on that video of Payaso\'d car was excellent.\r\n\r\nWhen you flashed the black screens in the strobe effect, how did you get it to line up with the music so perfect?\r\n\r\nI\'ve been thinking about that, and I was thinking I could sit down with the song, and map out the precise times of events in the song, but it just doen\'t seem like they\'d end up falling precisely on the beat like that.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21866,'6a412cd236','[quote:6a412cd236=\"PINGO\"]i ment like ebay and many danish sites.... do you no why you cant buy set 1,2,3 in homis?[/quote:6a412cd236]I have no idea.\r\nmaybe they stopped making those series?'),(21867,'fa6f9fe1a1','okay thanks fore the help'),(21868,'4499558509','http://stagg44.tripod.com/MOV00907.MPG\r\nCopy and paste that.  It shows i tried to go with the normal controls and it didnt work, but when i pressed the button and hit the controls it did go, and ill even show you in a race after i fix up my 49.mhz car. or if i get the money to by another one.  and id apreciate it if you did not call me a lier or anything like that, becase it does work.'),(21869,'fd3e44d72c','dude you are so full of shit. neither the way you first described or your cicruit diagram would work. crack that controller open and show me. lol.'),(26220,'8829824ab4','lol sorry dude actually i have a cuda body untouched you can have ill even throw in the challenger. i need your address again.'),(23922,'94335a9b2e','Are ther econtrollers and crysals with those cars? or will I need to look for some?\r\n\r\n  I just ordered the range parts so I will have them in and ready.\r\n\r\n  Is ther ea tut on fixing that?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21872,'ee4aa5d097','k here \r\n[img:ee4aa5d097]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v149/LiLStagg/crystal.bmp[/img:ee4aa5d097]\r\nThe silver thing is teh Crystal, connected to the switch. then the two wires goto teh other crystal.\r\nOk, tell me this if you still dont belive me, Why would i lie about that?  Its nothing that special?  if it was somthing else, like making my car jump, then i\'d be suspiciouse, but not over this.\r\n\r\nNow, would you like me to take a few more pictures?'),(21873,'1e308223cf','ya ones that i can see'),(23297,'d85ad0f77a','lol im still slack ass. i have two channels. i think 1 and 6 take your pick.'),(23927,'b34b62fac9','OK cool\r\n\r\n  Yea I think I will get a few nellys and have CD install them and maybe try one myself.\r\n\r\n  I bet it makes them muscle cars even that more bitchen with the nelly'),(23931,'14e5c24ab4','how the drifting?\r\n\r\n  I still need to send some vids of the drifting with the drift kits, its nice dude more like real drifting then just power sliding around.'),(21877,'da2c10dd7e','sure, y not.  here you go, and when i am done and if you still dont belive me, ill just show you a video, after i either do a PCB swap, or get another car that is 49.mhz.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23962,'204cf6e10d','Dude whast your yahoo name?'),(21879,'23273e8791','[img:23273e8791]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v149/LiLStagg/pic1.bmp[/img:23273e8791]\r\nthat fine?'),(21926,'800e71086e','OK dude $$ has been sent to gurmitbatra@hotmail.com'),(21927,'c122ba92ea',':lol: I hear ya dude, I\'ve been swimming 1 time this year in my pool and just dropped $280.00 for a pump and $200.00 for an automatic pool clean (again, too lazy to vacuum it lol)\r\nI\'m a fuckin moron for spending that shit, but it\'s better to keep the wife happy.\r\nanyways.\r\nhow\'d ya like it? I mean is it a big piece of shit?\r\nfor $10.00 I\'d probably try it out unless you recommend not to because it\'s just too friggin boring - I trust ya.\r\nI\'ve been looking over my shit, and so far I\'m not really seeing anything I think would make you happy. I mean, you\'re selling off all this bit/zip stuff and that\'s about all I have.\r\nI\'m more than happy to trade you some of my old painted shells or something but I\'m not sure that\'s what you want or would be happy with. I\'ve also got some Palmero homies I could send ya, but again - I have no clue if you\'re even really into homies and if you\'d be happy with that.\r\nthat\'s the majority of the \'cool\' stuff I have to get rid of, if that\'s something you might be interested in - let me (this all refering to the pullback by the way - unless you want a few painted shells or something, which I\'d be willing to do)\r\n[quote:c122ba92ea=\"VooDooMafia\"]I was going to sell it for 10 bucks plus shipping\r\n\r\n  Its beeen used once but since I am a lazy fucker and have not opened my pool (for the last 4 years lol) I dont think I will get much use of it[/quote:c122ba92ea]'),(21928,'800e71086e','OK dude $$ has been sent to gurmitbatra@hotmail.com');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21930,'3ec592840e','Yeaa dude we tried to get our pool filled in but it was gonna cost 10 grand :(\r\n\r\n  I take the cover off once in a while and toss the caimens in it when its cleaning time but thats about it lol.\r\n\r\n  The Sub.  Well its kinda fun yea cause its got lights and shit for underwater.  What was really fun with it is when we took it to the pet shop and dropped it in there HUGE fresh water display tank and sat back 20 feet and watched people with a confused look on there face.\r\n\r\n  Other then that I ran it in the kids plastic pool( i like those kind just dump and store lol) and the bath tub.\r\n\r\n  So I would have to say if you have your pool open then you would prolly have fun with it and even more so if you have a underwater video camera.\r\n\r\n  As for the pullbacks yea man Painted Cdun shells are always welcom lol.  The one I got from you before and the one from Crazydave almost never get used cause they are in teh display case lol.\r\n\r\n   I thought I was going to get rid of this extra bit stuff thats not being used but I find myself just buyin more lol.  Just ordered a hook launcher for the wild Char-G from HJL or whatever its called and planning on sending some of teh ZZ\'s and my SE to dave for some shit to get done lol.\r\n\r\n  I just cant put the little guys down.\r\n\r\nPete'),(21931,'9a674a69a6','Ok dude, have you sent 18 dollars Canadian or USD?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21932,'1557b53825','USD my friend\r\n\r\n  I figured you were talking in US money so I sent it in US :)\r\n\r\nI always deal in US as I sell to more peeps in the US and buy from more peeeps in the US.'),(21933,'1557b53825','USD my friend\r\n\r\n  I figured you were talking in US money so I sent it in US :)\r\n\r\nI always deal in US as I sell to more peeps in the US and buy from more peeeps in the US.'),(21935,'a9e87ac9ce','lol, ok....thanks bro!  :-)'),(21936,'78d9be741b','yea np let me kow when you get it or have your dad check or whatever you need to do.'),(21937,'78d9be741b','yea np let me kow when you get it or have your dad check or whatever you need to do.'),(21938,'3ec592840e','Yeaa dude we tried to get our pool filled in but it was gonna cost 10 grand :(\r\n\r\n  I take the cover off once in a while and toss the caimens in it when its cleaning time but thats about it lol.\r\n\r\n  The Sub.  Well its kinda fun yea cause its got lights and shit for underwater.  What was really fun with it is when we took it to the pet shop and dropped it in there HUGE fresh water display tank and sat back 20 feet and watched people with a confused look on there face.\r\n\r\n  Other then that I ran it in the kids plastic pool( i like those kind just dump and store lol) and the bath tub.\r\n\r\n  So I would have to say if you have your pool open then you would prolly have fun with it and even more so if you have a underwater video camera.\r\n\r\n  As for the pullbacks yea man Painted Cdun shells are always welcom lol.  The one I got from you before and the one from Crazydave almost never get used cause they are in teh display case lol.\r\n\r\n   I thought I was going to get rid of this extra bit stuff thats not being used but I find myself just buyin more lol.  Just ordered a hook launcher for the wild Char-G from HJL or whatever its called and planning on sending some of teh ZZ\'s and my SE to dave for some shit to get done lol.\r\n\r\n  I just cant put the little guys down.\r\n\r\nPete'),(21939,'acd5282603','Just teh for AE86 I want $6.00 plus shipping');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37908,'c7b633d9de','I think I\'ll give myself a quick skoolin on premiere....I\'ll get back to you soon.\r\nThanks for the advice :-o'),(28313,'f7566755cb','Hey,\r\nMake of list of what you would like (MT PCB..etc)\r\nThen we can work shipping and get each others address\'\r\n\r\nAlso I was looking at your resin stuff again..have You ever tried copying your body shells or rims or anything like, or would it not work?\r\nThanks'),(28503,'9b4abe7525','[quote:9b4abe7525=\"JDM-R34\"]Hey CDub\r\nI was looking for the thread where You give props to people who\'ve You have done biz-naz with, I didn\'t find it anywhere, is it still on this site?\r\nThanks[/quote:9b4abe7525]Here ya go: http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1183'),(35740,'528ef6201c','Ok cool , pics are up ;)'),(25491,'2e7b787f91','can soder the 2 cells on your 2 cell mod for me'),(34728,'f6d8dc707a','[quote:f6d8dc707a=\"ph2t\"]also, I think we both posted in the \"competition hell\" post at the same time, so I don\'t really understand the context of your response, is it that the xcrl shit is the shitbag? lol....\r\n\r\nearly day at work and a fuck all sleep night, so I\'m slow today.[/quote:f6d8dc707a]\r\nAbsolutely. I think we both mis-understood each other.\r\nYes - I think those dudes are jokes, I think that\'s obvious though.\r\n\r\nI guess the point I was trying to get across was that if he\'s a shitball, and you\'re not - I think that would show.\r\nTherefore, you going on the offensive, IMO, is like you bringing yourself down to his level. Something that you obviously don\'t [i:f6d8dc707a]need[/i:f6d8dc707a] to do, but I can understand why you would.\r\nTo me, and again - this is just my opinion, worrying about a shitball and taking action against it, almost cheapens you (for lack of better wording).\r\nI\'ll re-itterate though, I totally could understand where you might feel \"attacked\" and feel compelled to respond. I\'ve done it myself many times.\r\n\r\nMy comment about \"money\" wasn\'t directed soley at you or anyone. It was a generalization.\r\nI feel that when money is the ultimate motivator (not saying it is for you), it breeds the \"crook\" (for lack of a better term) in all of us.\r\nI don\'t want to see a good guy get burnt over his emotions.\r\nHell, I don\'t even know what road you were going down with your post, I just made a decision to try to be pro-active.\r\nI think ultimately it backfired, but hey - it\'s supposed to be the thought that counts right? lol\r\n\r\nAnyways, I hope that helps explain my comments and position on the whole matter.\r\nTo be honest. It really doesn\'t involve me, and overall - I\'m not losing any sleep over the entire thread. I just thought I was being helpful, but I think I worded it wrong or something and it failed to be helpful and was instead confusing.\r\n\r\nWhew. Fuck. That was a mouthful. :lol:'),(21943,'20b7f7fc8e','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=51870&amp;highlight=#51870\r\n\r\ntotally missed it.\r\n\r\nill sell it to ya for $8. i think its proportional.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21944,'c258201286','alright, I gotta have the sub, and at least 1 pullback.\r\nhere\'s what I got to trade ya, if don\'t want any, fine, if you want em all, fine - we might be\r\n able to work something out, if you want just a few, that\'s fine too, if you want part trade\r\n and part $, that\'s fine as well - it\'s all your decision.\r\njust name me a price and we\'ll work from there.\r\n\r\ngo to my gallery if you want to see more pics.\r\n\r\nCustom chopped and painted shell:\r\n[img:c258201286]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/accord_prototype_01.jpg[/img:c258201286]\r\n(I like this one, never been run with - no scratches.)\r\n\r\nCustom puttied and painted shell:\r\n[img:c258201286]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/gtrr32_candyapple_01.jpg[/img:c258201286]\r\n(I like this one because it really is themed after Kermit the Frog and isn\'t pussy.)\r\n(It has been raced a few times and there\'s a battle scar on the hood, but that\'s about it. I can show more pics if needed.)\r\n\r\nCustom painted Accord Waggon:\r\n[img:c258201286]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/accord_seafoam_01.jpg[/img:c258201286]\r\n(I like this one for it\'s uniqueness, run only a few times, no scratches that I can see.)\r\n\r\nCustom painted expirmental S-2000:\r\n[img:c258201286]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/s2k_blue_fade_multi_01.jpg[/img:c258201286]\r\n(I don\'t like this one, I used liquid mask to do it and the line work just isn\'t what I would have liked to see.)\r\n\r\nCustom painted RX7:\r\n[img:c258201286]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/gtrr34_silver_fade_01.jpg[/img:c258201286]\r\n(I didn\'t like this one because I used \'silver leaf\' which wrinkles to give the effect of a leaf, but other than that - it\'s cool)\r\n\r\nCustom painted WRX:\r\n[img:c258201286]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/wrx_blue_yellow_01.jpg[/img:c258201286]\r\n(I\'ve added some decals to it since this picture. It\'s my red-headed step child of the garage, doesn\'t get much play or respect.)\r\n\r\nlet me know.\r\n[quote:c258201286=\"VooDooMafia\"]Yeaa dude we tried to get our pool filled in but it was gonna cost 10 grand :(\r\n\r\n  I take the cover off once in a while and toss the caimens in it when its cleaning time but thats about it lol.\r\n\r\n  The Sub.  Well its kinda fun yea cause its got lights and shit for underwater.  What was really fun with it is when we took it to the pet shop and dropped it in there HUGE fresh water display tank and sat back 20 feet and watched people with a confused look on there face.\r\n\r\n  Other then that I ran it in the kids plastic pool( i like those kind just dump and store lol) and the bath tub.\r\n\r\n  So I would have to say if you have your pool open then you would prolly have fun with it and even more so if you have a underwater video camera.\r\n\r\n  As for the pullbacks yea man Painted Cdun shells are always welcom lol.  The one I got from you before and the one from Crazydave almost never get used cause they are in teh display case lol.\r\n\r\n   I thought I was going to get rid of this extra bit stuff thats not being used but I find myself just buyin more lol.  Just ordered a hook launcher for the wild Char-G from HJL or whatever its called and planning on sending some of teh ZZ\'s and my SE to dave for some shit to get done lol.\r\n\r\n  I just cant put the little guys down.\r\n\r\nPete[/quote:c258201286]'),(21945,'bcd1a55a49','The first 3 catch my eye for sure dude.  My wife needs that frog car lol.\r\n\r\n  So yea I am interested in those so let me know what you wanna do for them.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35505,'6b2fde9831',':-)'),(21951,'bd120ebeb2','NSX pullback Ill buy it for 5 shipped??  Or more ?'),(21952,'c241863a76','Perfection red Modena on pullback chassis.\r\nanD nsx pull back 10 shipped'),(21953,'d5e60ba342','will you sell your Epoch??  lookin for one'),(21954,'634382bd0d','I am open to offers bro.'),(21956,'c6453d847d','Ill take the Ae86 for 5 shiped\r\n\r\nI aint got paypal but i can money order'),(21957,'624accf503','13 shipped for the lambo shell and the ae86 and the skyline pull back\r\n\r\nsound good pm me back'),(21960,'d25aecfee1','the only thing left that you mentioned is the lambo\r\n\r\n  I might have another ae86 packed away somewhere but I am going to be asking $6 + shipping for them as they are hard to find and teh shipping killed me when I brought them over from Hong kong.'),(21961,'d25aecfee1','the only thing left that you mentioned is the lambo\r\n\r\n  I might have another ae86 packed away somewhere but I am going to be asking $6 + shipping for them as they are hard to find and teh shipping killed me when I brought them over from Hong kong.'),(23155,'1f3b834320','lol, my bad, I thought that since Finks, Sessiz and jowlz were spamming the site, then I assumed that all of the Bitpimps were in it....lol, I\'ll admit it, I fucked up there....:oops: \r\n\r\nI\'m a mod there, but only of a few sections, I\'m not a global mod or anything, so I can\'t IP/ban em....I guess I\'ll just have to notify the admin there and settle things myself....\r\n\r\nI\'ll admit I was being stupid accusing you and the whole site of spamming RCmod, I guess I was just so pissed/shocked I didn\'t think....my bad.... \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:1f3b834320=\"CaboWabo\"]hey moron.\r\nwhy are you sending this to me?\r\nI didn\'t go do shit.\r\nthat quote isn\'t mine - I haven\'t even been to that site in ages and probably a total of 10 times in its life.\r\nbetter get your facts straight.\r\n\r\nI can\'t believe you\'re claiming I\'d go do that, after all the help and support I\'ve given you?\r\nI ain\'t tellin\' nobody shit - I\'m not doing anything for you.\r\nwhy don\'t you go show off some of the balls you think you grew and tell \'em yourself?\r\n[quote:1f3b834320=\"Son_Gokou\"]...as to come to RCmod and spam just because of my moderatorship there. \r\n\r\nTell the others that I don\'t want any trouble from them just because I\'m a mod there...jowlz even registered there under the name \"crotchy goku\" and started shit, and sent me this PM:\r\n\r\n[quote:1f3b834320]why was i banned and all my posts deleted?? after all the leniency you have been given i figured youd have a level head. lol this site is a joke.[/quote:1f3b834320]\r\n\r\nwtf did I ever do to you guys?[/quote:1f3b834320][/quote:1f3b834320]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22382,'e37b4ea672','Things have actually been good, MK at MRCC is still a thorn in my side but sometimes people are that way.  The good thing is the more he disses R7R the more members we get....LOL\r\n\r\nI can\'t get that damn chat to work, something with my server, need to ask tech, oh well the MiRC is working and it does not eat Bandwidth....LOL\r\n\r\n\r\nI may be posting later asking for writers or article ideas, I will of course give credit and link back to the Bit pimps or any threads pertaining to the article.  I would like to get more forums to participate in the Mag I think it will help it\'s evolution.  But you never know I might see resistance from other forums, I figure no mater what, people will always pick there main forum and check out all the others.\r\n\r\n\r\nWell ttyl\r\nRipper'),(21965,'5f279bd0cc','Ok if you find the other Ae86 Ill prolly buy it Ill get he lambo from you need your adress im goin by money order I don\'t know when prolly in 2 days because im looking to buy an epcoh for 89$ at Tiny rc so yeah and stuff from ahh shit and by the way do you have anything for superslicks?'),(21966,'f5c9a23940','no super slick stuff\r\n\r\nAs for epochs I think if you look at riper777777 site he has them cheaper .');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21967,'f5c9a23940','no super slick stuff\r\n\r\nAs for epochs I think if you look at riper777777 site he has them cheaper .'),(21968,'c964cc8f60','dude, CD, in NO WAY was I trying to misrepresent you, slander you, or any negative intention of the sort. Maybe it was the way I talked about something I didn\'t know shit about....my bad....\r\n\r\nIf I offended you or anything of the sort, then I\'M SORRY, ok? Is there anything I can do to make it up to ya? Pay you some cash or any shiat of the sort?'),(21969,'c4f5a4d5c3','[quote:c4f5a4d5c3=\"Son_Gokou\"]dude, CD, in NO WAY was I trying to misrepresent you, slander you, or any negative intention of the sort. Maybe it was the way I talked about something I didn\'t know shit about....my bad....\r\n\r\nIf I offended you or anything of the sort, then I\'M SORRY, ok? Is there anything I can do to make it up to ya? Pay you some cash or any shiat of the sort?[/quote:c4f5a4d5c3]This is what I hate more than anything, and what I think agitates people about you. People who make up imformation off the top their head, and then present it as fact. In other words, spouting bullshit. \r\n\r\nI know you didn\'t intend to offend me, so I\'m sorry if I was harsh, but that\'s what I don\'t understand is why you do it. Why do you say things before you know if they\'re true or not? Especially knowing it\'s gonna get you in trouble every time.\r\n\r\nThat\'s what offended me, that you were talking about me, without knowing the truth, not what you said, just that you didn\'t know what you where saying, and it\'s about [i:c4f5a4d5c3]me[/i:c4f5a4d5c3].\r\n\r\nTell you what, apology accepted, just don\'t talk about me publicly again, and I\'ll stand behind the original deal, $10+shipping. Oh, and considering SG\'s post in that thread, I\'m gonna have to insist, cash up front. ;)\r\n\r\nDave'),(21970,'386a1e0027','I have to zoom in on the timelines as far as possible.\r\nI suck at explaining shit so I\'ll just tell you my process.\r\nfirst off though, I think the tools we use probably make all the difference and the video application used is critical.\r\nI use Adobe Premiere for video editing and putting the final compilation together. I highly suggest Premiere, the pro\'s can\'t be wrong and that\'s what they use.\r\nI use SoundForge for audio editing and exporting my final \'soundtrack\' (that ends up being imported in to Premiere). I\'m guessing you could probably use a variety of applications here, it\'s probably not as important as the video application.\r\nI first import my clips in Premiere and figure out what splices from the several movies I\'ll be using. I then try to put them in an order I want them.\r\nAs I\'m doing this, I start to think about an audio track that I want with the video. This part as you is going to give an overall feel to your video so it\'s pretty important in my eyes.\r\nOnce I figure out the track sequence of the video and choose the audio track I want to play, I then start editing my video to precisely what I want - trying to keep in mind the audio track that I want to play.\r\nOnce I get the video clips all cut-up and spliced together how I want, I play my video - w/out audio (test) just to see what it looks like, etc.\r\nNow I import my audio track to SoundForge and start cutting it down to the exact pieces I want and the exact time of the entire video.\r\nOnce finished, I import the audio track to Premiere and add it to the video and test it again for sync. Then edit as needed from there.\r\n\r\nThat\'s the process I\'ve used most and it works, but it\'s rather cumbersome, I know there\'s probably a better process.\r\nI\'m thinking next time I make a movie, I\'m going to pick the audio track sooner and import it and play it against what I have.\r\n\r\nIt seems easier to sync the video to audio rather than vice versa.\r\n\r\nI still would love to see a compilation video like hog tried to start.\r\nit\'s so hard though because a lot of time the only video you can really work with is the original and nobody posts those.\r\n[quote:386a1e0027=\"crazydave\"]Hey Cabo, your editing on that video of Payaso\'d car was excellent.\r\n\r\nWhen you flashed the black screens in the strobe effect, how did you get it to line up with the music so perfect?\r\n\r\nI\'ve been thinking about that, and I was thinking I could sit down with the song, and map out the precise times of events in the song, but it just doen\'t seem like they\'d end up falling precisely on the beat like that.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:386a1e0027]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21971,'ef298d85ce','Well damn, that is a pain, I never put that much effort into my vids, because it takes all day as it is, and I don\'t have the patience for things that take more than a day.\r\n\r\nWell damn, nice work man, I guess, you put even more effort than I realized into your vids.\r\n\r\nI listen to music until I picture a vid in my head, then I shoot my clips in the order I expect them to be. By the time I crop down my clips, I\'m left with a bunch of little tiny ones, I just string them together in the order I imagined, and I use the slow mo stuff to stretch out parts when I\'m waiting for the song to transistion. \r\n\r\nI was using Ulead, but I think it\'s crap, and I\'m looking for other options. I didn\'t like Windows Movie Maker, that came with XP. I have a feeling feeling Premiere aint cheap. You got a hook up on that?\r\n\r\nWhen I did Baja Trippin\' it was coincidence it fit with the music, but on later ones I was trying to sync it up more, and it\'s pretty tricky.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:ef298d85ce]I still would love to see a compilation video like hog tried to start. \r\nit\'s so hard though because a lot of time the only video you can really work with is the original and nobody posts those. [/quote:ef298d85ce]Yeah you know I had 40megs of raw footage stashed up on my Cox server for Hog. Then he had his problems and disappeared, now all that stuff is lost. I gotta shoot some more stuff. We gotta stop talking about that vid, and just do it. :lol:'),(21972,'2cd7bc1b39','sure\r\n\r\nshipping will be wround 3 bucks or so (anymore I will cover any less I send back');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21977,'bd120ebeb2','NSX pullback Ill buy it for 5 shipped??  Or more ?'),(21978,'c241863a76','Perfection red Modena on pullback chassis.\r\nanD nsx pull back 10 shipped'),(21979,'13c7e180fd','CD,\r\n\r\nI read the posts so I know you don\'t do work for others like Microamps, and others.  But I respect your work and if your services are available, let me know.  (ie: fets, wheels) and what prices.  I\'m in Pa.  Thanks\r\n\r\nKvik369'),(23428,'117a6a2a77','ok. give me a few days since its the weekend. i can ship a 49mhz controller if you really need one but it would help me on shipping not to. also if you need it i have either an nkok or motorworks charger. \r\n\r\nit also has about an hour of running in it. the shell has maybe 15 minutes of running. its a simple design but its effective and you will break it if you hit things. anything else from america if its cheap and light?'),(21981,'bcd1a55a49','The first 3 catch my eye for sure dude.  My wife needs that frog car lol.\r\n\r\n  So yea I am interested in those so let me know what you wanna do for them.'),(21982,'ef298d85ce','Well damn, that is a pain, I never put that much effort into my vids, because it takes all day as it is, and I don\'t have the patience for things that take more than a day.\r\n\r\nWell damn, nice work man, I guess, you put even more effort than I realized into your vids.\r\n\r\nI listen to music until I picture a vid in my head, then I shoot my clips in the order I expect them to be. By the time I crop down my clips, I\'m left with a bunch of little tiny ones, I just string them together in the order I imagined, and I use the slow mo stuff to stretch out parts when I\'m waiting for the song to transistion. \r\n\r\nI was using Ulead, but I think it\'s crap, and I\'m looking for other options. I didn\'t like Windows Movie Maker, that came with XP. I have a feeling feeling Premiere aint cheap. You got a hook up on that?\r\n\r\nWhen I did Baja Trippin\' it was coincidence it fit with the music, but on later ones I was trying to sync it up more, and it\'s pretty tricky.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:ef298d85ce]I still would love to see a compilation video like hog tried to start. \r\nit\'s so hard though because a lot of time the only video you can really work with is the original and nobody posts those. [/quote:ef298d85ce]Yeah you know I had 40megs of raw footage stashed up on my Cox server for Hog. Then he had his problems and disappeared, now all that stuff is lost. I gotta shoot some more stuff. We gotta stop talking about that vid, and just do it. :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21983,'c97e3b8f3a','I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.'),(26088,'01f4437ae9','yo can you please soder the 2 cells on the 2 cell mod for me\r\n\r\ncause i suck at sodering'),(26089,'60e0282ae0','[quote:60e0282ae0=\"Bigg\"]yo can you please soder the 2 cells on the 2 cell mod for me\r\n\r\ncause i suck at sodering[/quote:60e0282ae0]sorry bro, but I just don\'t have time to offer my services at the moment.\r\n\r\nI\'ll give you 2 ideas that should get it completed for you though:\r\n1.) make a post in the \"Lookin\' To Score\" forum. (if you meet the criteria to post there)\r\n2.) practice on something, even just wires and a piece of metal. eventually, I know you can do this - because I suck at soldering too and I can do a dual cell.\r\n\r\ngood luck holmes.'),(25502,'55ba712420','Like I said its all good I am sure whatever you decide will be fine.'),(33750,'9d0e281a55','[quote:9d0e281a55=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Can a ZZSE board take 3-cells w/o a FET mod? I\'ve searched and all I\'ve seen were FET posts and topics\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx[/quote:9d0e281a55]\r\n\r\nyep, no problems with 3 cells mate. :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35435,'a4cd0293ad','Sup pimpin I need your mailing info so that i can shoot you my ZZMT for the FET upgade i can put it in the mail tomorrow.'),(29596,'5b47565ca6','http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=5975536112&amp;rd=1&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:5b47565ca6]http://www.xtremeglobaltrader.com/xgtliquidator/ebay/Hobbico/HCAC0426/HobbicoHCAC0426.jpg[/img:5b47565ca6]'),(29362,'eea75dc073','Sorry for the delayed responses, I\'ve been busy as hell. Anyhow, how about a brand new Gloria shell (the one painted green) in trade for that blue shell? Let me know, then we\'ll trade addresses and ship \'em out... I can get it in the mail tomorrow.\r\n\r\nSWG is a cool-ass dude to just hand such a hard-to-come-by shell right over to ya... it\'s Christmas in May, yo.\r\n\r\nlater,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(36223,'f86da47952','[quote:f86da47952=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:f86da47952=\"sg219\"]If you can, let me know when your going to post. That way all the winners can go up at one time.\r\n\r\nI sorta would like to pick someone that doesn\'t place. \r\n\r\nProbably Hiroto\'s ride. :???: \r\n\r\n\r\nLater[/quote:f86da47952]\r\nAlright, looks like it\'s gonna be Sporttracguy, steelwoolghandi, and 45tr0.\r\nSo pick your mystery winner.\r\nChedderSpreader\'s post will probably be made tonight or tomorrow.\r\nFeel free to edit the post and your choice.\r\nIt\'ll be looked at enough - the winner won\'t miss it.\r\n\r\nBy the way, thanks for puttin up a prize for another pimp. :-o[/quote:f86da47952]\r\n\r\n\r\nHiroto... :-o  :-o'),(32090,'b0e35eacc8','[quote:b0e35eacc8=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hi,\r\n\r\nSorry for the delay in reply. I havent checked my emails in a while. Lets see, I still have everything that you listed and I do remember that I do have some of the mini cooper roof tops. I\'ll check to make sure. I\'ll get back to you shortly and sorry for the delay in reply.\r\n\r\nJDM[/quote:b0e35eacc8]\r\n\r\nThat\'s cool man, it\'s summer... too quick, and I\'d have been worried.  :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21986,'991de79c6e','[quote:991de79c6e=\"hogjowlz\"]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=51870&amp;highlight=#51870\r\n\r\ntotally missed it.\r\n\r\nill sell it to ya for $8. i think its proportional.[/quote:991de79c6e]are you crazy? you ran me over'),(21987,'13c7e180fd','CD,\r\n\r\nI read the posts so I know you don\'t do work for others like Microamps, and others.  But I respect your work and if your services are available, let me know.  (ie: fets, wheels) and what prices.  I\'m in Pa.  Thanks\r\n\r\nKvik369'),(21989,'c97e3b8f3a','I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.'),(21990,'983870d38f','[quote:983870d38f=\"CaboWabo\"]I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.[/quote:983870d38f]Well then I\'d probably be grateful. :-D \r\n\r\nI\'m using RAD tools to covert the quicktime clips to .avis now, and they\'re coming out so much clearer, I really hate to stick them in Ulead and fuck them up now. \r\n\r\nThat\'s what\'s been hanging me up from doing my Prostocker vid.\r\n\r\nDave'),(21991,'dfc75e22a3','[quote:dfc75e22a3=\"kvik369\"]CD,\r\n\r\nI read the posts so I know you don\'t do work for others like Microamps, and others.  But I respect your work and if your services are available, let me know.  (ie: fets, wheels) and what prices.  I\'m in Pa.  Thanks\r\n\r\nKvik369[/quote:dfc75e22a3]Yeah sure, I\'d be happy do some mods for ya. I just don\'t like dealing with the general public.\r\n\r\n\r\nI mostly just do FET mods for people. I\'ve been charging 10+shipping. I could probably do a wheel mod if your interested, but not sure what I\'d charge for that.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21992,'10b9fd5b1e','Ok cool -\r\n\r\nI definately have a few more cars to fet. (Damn radio shack) What about the se\'s?  Did you guys figure that one out.'),(21993,'4c834e18a2','[quote:4c834e18a2=\"VooDooMafia\"]The first 3 catch my eye for sure dude.  My wife needs that frog car lol.\r\n\r\n  So yea I am interested in those so let me know what you wanna do for them.[/quote:4c834e18a2]cool, well what do you think, those 3 worth it to you for the sub and a pullback?'),(33609,'cb970dbb11','How much for this?\r\n\r\n[img:cb970dbb11]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10004/DSC03400.JPG[/img:cb970dbb11]\r\n\r\nJust the truck w/o the controller but with all the other electronics?\r\nI\'d like a serious price, but don\'t take me too seriously (yet).\r\n\r\n[quote:cb970dbb11=\"payaso\"]As far as nitro, I just have the T, and the Revo for now. Thinkin about getting another, but I\'d have to sell one of thse first. :sad: [/quote:cb970dbb11] That was the reason I asked.\r\n\r\nMaxx &lt;-- same name, corny huh?  :lol:'),(21995,'3d1bc7e3e5','Whatever dude\r\n\r\n  I am easy to trade with lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (21996,'10b9fd5b1e','Ok cool -\r\n\r\nI definately have a few more cars to fet. (Damn radio shack) What about the se\'s?  Did you guys figure that one out.'),(21997,'983870d38f','[quote:983870d38f=\"CaboWabo\"]I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.[/quote:983870d38f]Well then I\'d probably be grateful. :-D \r\n\r\nI\'m using RAD tools to covert the quicktime clips to .avis now, and they\'re coming out so much clearer, I really hate to stick them in Ulead and fuck them up now. \r\n\r\nThat\'s what\'s been hanging me up from doing my Prostocker vid.\r\n\r\nDave'),(21999,'b41ee0b288','[quote:b41ee0b288=\"crazydave\"][quote:b41ee0b288=\"CaboWabo\"]I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.[/quote:b41ee0b288]Well then I\'d probably be grateful. :-D \r\n\r\nI\'m using RAD tools to covert the quicktime clips to .avis now, and they\'re coming out so much clearer, I really hate to stick them in Ulead and fuck them up now. \r\n\r\nThat\'s what\'s been hanging me up from doing my Prostocker vid.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:b41ee0b288]well alright then, I\'ll burn ya a copy.\r\nyou might want to check out some info on it: http://www.adobe.com/products/premiere/main.html\r\nThough I don\'t have Premeire Pro, I\'ve got 6.5 (I think 1 version before Pro)'),(22000,'3d1bc7e3e5','Whatever dude\r\n\r\n  I am easy to trade with lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22001,'5f283b2c86','I forgot to ask. So did you get a chance to give that SE a going over? If so, what\'s the verdict? Does it stack up against Payaso\'s car? (You\'d have to try a faster motor... of coarse, but I thought I\'d throw that out there anyways)\r\n\r\nDave'),(22002,'b41ee0b288','[quote:b41ee0b288=\"crazydave\"][quote:b41ee0b288=\"CaboWabo\"]I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.[/quote:b41ee0b288]Well then I\'d probably be grateful. :-D \r\n\r\nI\'m using RAD tools to covert the quicktime clips to .avis now, and they\'re coming out so much clearer, I really hate to stick them in Ulead and fuck them up now. \r\n\r\nThat\'s what\'s been hanging me up from doing my Prostocker vid.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:b41ee0b288]well alright then, I\'ll burn ya a copy.\r\nyou might want to check out some info on it: http://www.adobe.com/products/premiere/main.html\r\nThough I don\'t have Premeire Pro, I\'ve got 6.5 (I think 1 version before Pro)'),(22004,'5f283b2c86','I forgot to ask. So did you get a chance to give that SE a going over? If so, what\'s the verdict? Does it stack up against Payaso\'s car? (You\'d have to try a faster motor... of coarse, but I thought I\'d throw that out there anyways)\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22005,'a7d77c4937','[quote:a7d77c4937=\"VooDooMafia\"]I am easy[/quote:a7d77c4937]and that\'s why we like ya - no need for expensive dinners, just straight to the humpin lol\r\n\r\nokay man, consider it a deal.\r\nI\'m at work right now, but will get everything packaged up tonight when I get home.\r\nsend me an address where I should ship it to.\r\n\r\nyou can send my shit here:\r\nScott Lix\r\n16 Crystal Lake Drive\r\nSt. Peters, MO 63376'),(22007,'7d88924ff6','[quote:7d88924ff6=\"crazydave\"]I forgot to ask. So did you get a chance to give that SE a going over? If so, what\'s the verdict? Does it stack up against Payaso\'s car? (You\'d have to try a faster motor... of coarse, but I thought I\'d throw that out there anyways)\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:7d88924ff6]not really, not enough for a good judgement. I was busy with typical house crap this weekend and fucking up that shell lol\r\nI told myself last night though that I\'m going to go through at least 10 charges tonight lol\r\nso far (with same motor you had in it) it\'s looking good. I\'m pretty sure it\'s gonna be right there with payaso\'s.\r\nI think he had that purple zz motor in his though, I\'m going to be putting in a Vanquish.\r\nI\'m betting the Vanquish is gonna make this fucker scream.'),(22008,'21e57e949e','Peter Kostecki\r\n20 Water St\r\nThorold Ontario\r\nL2V 2K3\r\nCanada\r\n\r\n  what pullback did you want or just a chassie? What color rims?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22009,'5f58d06b78','[quote:5f58d06b78=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:5f58d06b78=\"crazydave\"][quote:5f58d06b78=\"CaboWabo\"]I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.[/quote:5f58d06b78]Well then I\'d probably be grateful. :-D \r\n\r\nI\'m using RAD tools to covert the quicktime clips to .avis now, and they\'re coming out so much clearer, I really hate to stick them in Ulead and fuck them up now. \r\n\r\nThat\'s what\'s been hanging me up from doing my Prostocker vid.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:5f58d06b78]well alright then, I\'ll burn ya a copy.\r\nyou might want to check out some info on it: http://www.adobe.com/products/premiere/main.html\r\nThough I don\'t have Premeire Pro, I\'ve got 6.5 (I think 1 version before Pro)[/quote:5f58d06b78]Yeah, I think I can work with Premier. The interface looks real similar to the ulead, I can work with that, but hopefully it\'ll give me a lot more control, and obviously export to a higher quality.\r\n\r\nIt was saying Pro is optimized for XP, you know if 6.5 works with XP? I know I\'ve been having compatibility issues since we switched to XP. \r\n\r\nDave'),(22010,'7d88924ff6','[quote:7d88924ff6=\"crazydave\"]I forgot to ask. So did you get a chance to give that SE a going over? If so, what\'s the verdict? Does it stack up against Payaso\'s car? (You\'d have to try a faster motor... of coarse, but I thought I\'d throw that out there anyways)\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:7d88924ff6]not really, not enough for a good judgement. I was busy with typical house crap this weekend and fucking up that shell lol\r\nI told myself last night though that I\'m going to go through at least 10 charges tonight lol\r\nso far (with same motor you had in it) it\'s looking good. I\'m pretty sure it\'s gonna be right there with payaso\'s.\r\nI think he had that purple zz motor in his though, I\'m going to be putting in a Vanquish.\r\nI\'m betting the Vanquish is gonna make this fucker scream.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22012,'5f58d06b78','[quote:5f58d06b78=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:5f58d06b78=\"crazydave\"][quote:5f58d06b78=\"CaboWabo\"]I could probably burn ya a copy of premiere and send it down.\r\nI think you\'ll like it.[/quote:5f58d06b78]Well then I\'d probably be grateful. :-D \r\n\r\nI\'m using RAD tools to covert the quicktime clips to .avis now, and they\'re coming out so much clearer, I really hate to stick them in Ulead and fuck them up now. \r\n\r\nThat\'s what\'s been hanging me up from doing my Prostocker vid.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:5f58d06b78]well alright then, I\'ll burn ya a copy.\r\nyou might want to check out some info on it: http://www.adobe.com/products/premiere/main.html\r\nThough I don\'t have Premeire Pro, I\'ve got 6.5 (I think 1 version before Pro)[/quote:5f58d06b78]Yeah, I think I can work with Premier. The interface looks real similar to the ulead, I can work with that, but hopefully it\'ll give me a lot more control, and obviously export to a higher quality.\r\n\r\nIt was saying Pro is optimized for XP, you know if 6.5 works with XP? I know I\'ve been having compatibility issues since we switched to XP. \r\n\r\nDave'),(22013,'f14c6129b4','[quote:f14c6129b4=\"crazydave\"]Yeah, I think I can work with Premier. The interface looks real similar to the ulead, I can work with that, but hopefully it\'ll give me a lot more control, and obviously export to a higher quality.\r\n\r\nIt was saying Pro is optimized for XP, you know if 6.5 works with XP? I know I\'ve been having compatibility issues since we switched to XP. \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:f14c6129b4]yea it should work.\r\nI\'m running XP Pro and it works on mine no problems.\r\nand there\'s a shitload of export options, you can even make your own export profiles.\r\nthis things nails. lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22014,'c6e6323cd0','gimme a pullback with silver rims pwease.\r\n\r\nif it comes with a shell, that\'d be cool - if not, that\'s fine too.'),(22015,'89a46c0135','[quote:89a46c0135=\"CaboWabo\"]I think he had that purple zz motor in his though, I\'m going to be putting in a Vanquish.\r\nI\'m betting the Vanquish is gonna make this fucker scream.[/quote:89a46c0135]Cool! I wanted some kind of positive input before I wrote the tutorial, and so far that\'s good enough for me. \r\n\r\nBe interested to hear how it does with that Vanquish. So far I\'ve found that purple ZZ motor to be the best all around motor for the SE, but I\'ve been meaning to try a 4.2, now that I we got the last step with the jumpered resistors, and I stacked my FETs.\r\n\r\nNotice how you can see your stacked FETs sticking out that front hold down thing on the chassis. I dig that because it reminds me of a injector scoop or a tunmnel ram sticking out a hood, ya know?\r\n\r\ndave'),(22016,'f14c6129b4','[quote:f14c6129b4=\"crazydave\"]Yeah, I think I can work with Premier. The interface looks real similar to the ulead, I can work with that, but hopefully it\'ll give me a lot more control, and obviously export to a higher quality.\r\n\r\nIt was saying Pro is optimized for XP, you know if 6.5 works with XP? I know I\'ve been having compatibility issues since we switched to XP. \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:f14c6129b4]yea it should work.\r\nI\'m running XP Pro and it works on mine no problems.\r\nand there\'s a shitload of export options, you can even make your own export profiles.\r\nthis things nails. lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22017,'89a46c0135','[quote:89a46c0135=\"CaboWabo\"]I think he had that purple zz motor in his though, I\'m going to be putting in a Vanquish.\r\nI\'m betting the Vanquish is gonna make this fucker scream.[/quote:89a46c0135]Cool! I wanted some kind of positive input before I wrote the tutorial, and so far that\'s good enough for me. \r\n\r\nBe interested to hear how it does with that Vanquish. So far I\'ve found that purple ZZ motor to be the best all around motor for the SE, but I\'ve been meaning to try a 4.2, now that I we got the last step with the jumpered resistors, and I stacked my FETs.\r\n\r\nNotice how you can see your stacked FETs sticking out that front hold down thing on the chassis. I dig that because it reminds me of a injector scoop or a tunmnel ram sticking out a hood, ya know?\r\n\r\ndave'),(22019,'5249513c0f','[quote:5249513c0f=\"kvik369\"]Ok cool -\r\n\r\nI definately have a few more cars to fet. (Damn radio shack) What about the se\'s?  Did you guys figure that one out.[/quote:5249513c0f]Yeah, I can do up a SE pretty good like.  \r\n\r\nSo how many cars you looking to have done? I need to make sure I got enough FETs.\r\n\r\nDave'),(37024,'c3a653b4e9','I\'ll send w/e i find :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22021,'c4f5a4d5c3','[quote:c4f5a4d5c3=\"Son_Gokou\"]dude, CD, in NO WAY was I trying to misrepresent you, slander you, or any negative intention of the sort. Maybe it was the way I talked about something I didn\'t know shit about....my bad....\r\n\r\nIf I offended you or anything of the sort, then I\'M SORRY, ok? Is there anything I can do to make it up to ya? Pay you some cash or any shiat of the sort?[/quote:c4f5a4d5c3]This is what I hate more than anything, and what I think agitates people about you. People who make up imformation off the top their head, and then present it as fact. In other words, spouting bullshit. \r\n\r\nI know you didn\'t intend to offend me, so I\'m sorry if I was harsh, but that\'s what I don\'t understand is why you do it. Why do you say things before you know if they\'re true or not? Especially knowing it\'s gonna get you in trouble every time.\r\n\r\nThat\'s what offended me, that you were talking about me, without knowing the truth, not what you said, just that you didn\'t know what you where saying, and it\'s about [i:c4f5a4d5c3]me[/i:c4f5a4d5c3].\r\n\r\nTell you what, apology accepted, just don\'t talk about me publicly again, and I\'ll stand behind the original deal, $10+shipping. Oh, and considering SG\'s post in that thread, I\'m gonna have to insist, cash up front. ;)\r\n\r\nDave'),(22023,'ac03580fcc','[quote:ac03580fcc=\"crazydave\"]Notice how you can see your stacked FETs sticking out that front hold down thing on the chassis. I dig that because it reminds me of a injector scoop or a tunmnel ram sticking out a hood, ya know?\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:ac03580fcc]yea actually I did, I was digging that too but I was making up some back to the future flux capacitor theory to explain it away lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22026,'86f6e75fc9','Hey man you still around?\r\n\r\n\r\n  I was gone for a few months but still here :)\r\n\r\n  Just wondering what you been upto.\r\n\r\nL8r bro'),(22027,'6e370df186','Ok, what\'s the address where I ship the items to?'),(22028,'f899022c25','Peter Kostecki\r\n20 Water St.\r\nThorold Ontario\r\nL2V 2K3\r\nCanada\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIt should have also been in your paypal account if you click on the transaction details.'),(22030,'8460ff725f','*bows at your feet*'),(22031,'a1eaac28aa','[quote:a1eaac28aa=\"kvik369\"]As of right now , 2 se\'s and one regular zip and maybe an ms.  Not exactly sure yet. [/quote:a1eaac28aa]Ok, that\'s cool, I can cover that\r\n\r\n[quote:a1eaac28aa] Has any one  figured out how to fet the Nikko jeep?(the same one that Hog just dualed).   Microamps told me he couldn\'t do it .[/quote:a1eaac28aa]I was gonna work on it when I have spare time. \r\n\r\nI believe it can be done fairly easily, just need the time to get into it. It seems like micro_amps wont figure out anything that he doesn\'t see a market for. Sucks because it brings a lot of people to me asking me to figure things out, and I\'m really not an electronics expert.\r\n\r\ndave'),(28222,'9d68f0d4b7','Honestly I always use the Import Tunerz.  Why?  Because they are always the same size.  The Joda I used recently and were great, but on different dicast they are a different scale.  It all depends on what kind of car you are modding.  If it\'s a asian car, Import Tunerz all the way, if it\'s an euro or american car, possibly the Joda\'s.  Bottome line, what ever you think would work best with the style you are modding.  Hope this helps.  What ever you do, keep us updated on what you do.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22035,'daab5170d4','Thanks pimp!  :-)'),(25798,'ecbe7c345c','killer, I need to ask my bro what server we are doing.  My friends and I are all mother fuckers you would dig.  And like I said before, we are playing Horde.  I have a ton of friends that don\'t know anyone other than me so will be playing on that server and it would be bad ass if you were one of em.  I\'ll PM you the instant he tells me the name of the server.  Should be later tonight.  How many East coast PvP servers are there?  If it helps I think the name starts w/ a D or B... weak I know but well...  :-)'),(22038,'d5e60ba342','will you sell your Epoch??  lookin for one'),(22039,'92d7727a2a','Sorry, actually the epoch is being shipped out sometime this week..'),(30755,'2e61691ce0','Hey micro_man, sorry bro, but a few hours before you replied i got a different offer. Thanks alot though bro! If you ever need anything just ask.'),(23738,'8378f5afdc','sorry dude i was out of town all week. ill box her up tonight and take her to the post office tomorrow. \r\n\r\ncar + 27mhz tx and charger\r\n\r\nsorry about the delay.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25925,'e4e3a8beae','Hey, I got all my shit hooked up, my server is Bleeding Hollow and our guild is literally the 2nd biggest on the server.  Important to note is that it is huge, but not filled w/ 15 year olds, the average age is high 20\'s early 30\'s.  Great group of people and we use the program team speak wich in it\'sself is a killer ap.  Give me a Tell.  Like I said, name is Finks, only lvl 10 atm due to only playing for 2 days.  Oh and Evil is the only way.  If you are down HJ you are more than welcome to join us, I\'ll put in a good word for ya.'),(22044,'455fc97e2d','got it today dude thanks\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks for teh extra s2k :)'),(22045,'2e0e5f3c7f',':-)'),(22046,'2e0e5f3c7f',':-)'),(22251,'61902ee76d','I don\'t think anyone has contacted you yet, sorry about that.\r\nand if they have, please let me know.\r\n\r\nanyways, congratulations on your winning bid.\r\nyou have a few payment options, you\'re choice.\r\nyou can either send cash or money order (US funds only)\r\nor\r\nyou can pay via paypal.\r\n\r\nlet me know which you prefer to do.\r\nonce payment is received, your car will be shipped.\r\n\r\nthanks for helping support bitPimps!'),(23933,'14e5c24ab4','how the drifting?\r\n\r\n  I still need to send some vids of the drifting with the drift kits, its nice dude more like real drifting then just power sliding around.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30947,'2601350a16','Cool deal.  :cool:'),(24529,'6a1af48455','Dude!\r\n\r\nwhat can i say but thanks!\r\n\r\n\r\nyeah i tried the radioshack order line/website they dont do international orders, thats why i was having such a hard time getting parts.\r\n\r\nokay here is my addy.\r\n\r\n39 Moate ave\r\nBrighton-le-Sands Sydney\r\nNSW Australia\r\n2216\r\n\r\nthanks again for the help.\r\n\r\n\r\n :D'),(22148,'ce834e4c8b','Well, just got off the phone w/ my ex-manager and he said $20 each.  Not the best deal in the world, but a deal none the less.  Tell me what you think.  BTW I know there is a white supra in there, used but white :)'),(22055,'e5dd831cca','money order is fine  Just make sure its a international one.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPeter Kostecki\r\n20 Water St.\r\nThorold Ontario\r\nL2V 2K3\r\nCanada\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you can do paypal let me know.'),(22057,'5f4e08f209','It\'s good to see you around, Azimov.  :-)'),(28906,'eb37f68d5a','You are welcome....\r\n\r\nIn case you are wondering what the hell I\'m talking about....\r\n\r\nI sent that on Sat. night I think and I was drinking beer....Spaten Optimator, which is a dark German beer with a fairly high alc%. I saw you were online and hoped you would see it before you logged off....no such like.\r\n\r\nCracka out....');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28909,'f57ba20428','So,how about the price?'),(22060,'f64ef46d50','did you make that reader??\r\nIs there any way i can get it???'),(22062,'5f4e08f209','It\'s good to see you around, Azimov.  :-)'),(22063,'e27fa99821','Thanks. But, I ain\'t been far.'),(37509,'5f26e74e7e','[quote:5f26e74e7e=\"45tr0\"]sorry dude, i forgot to get back to you!\r\nyeah, it made it here safe and sound, 2 weeks to the day after you sent it. quickest shipping yet from the states!\r\nBy that point, the blowout thread had gone a bit cold so i didn\'t bother postin there, but i shoulda messaged you back.  \r\nSorry man, slackage on my behalf.[/quote:5f26e74e7e]\r\nOh dude, no problem. It happens to us all.\r\nI honestly was thinking it didn\'t make it there yet, the tracking page didn\'t have any information on it since it left here.\r\nCool, glad it got there. :-o'),(37510,'3617c7d600','That sounds good. Like I said, I was never in it to make cash so didn\'t know what reasonable would be for people. Can you do paypal or plan on MO? If paypal, my account is clxfiles@yahoo.com \r\nif MO send it to \r\n\r\nattn: Rodney Tapia \r\n7208 Johnson Dr. \r\nPleasanton, CA 94503 \r\n\r\nWhat\'s your real name so I know who to expect from and what to send when I receive? \r\nAlso, what address do I send it to?'),(37511,'5ab037f7e5','Im VERY Interested in this, i just have a few questions like does it come withe the original manuals and instructions? Does it come with the Porshe Body? And can i see a few more pics of it? Also does it come with battery and charger?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22068,'92d7727a2a','Sorry, actually the epoch is being shipped out sometime this week..'),(22069,'e27fa99821','Thanks. But, I ain\'t been far.'),(28448,'2b3362f0e2','Hey,\r\nThats cool, Your giving me a controller too? Thats cool i wasn\'t expecting that, I don\'t have the controller for the MT though... :???: umm let\'s see, well here\'s a pic though of everything, one last shot, oh yeah my address is on that padded envelope it\'s just cut off, out of the picture, and I\'ll try to get over to the post office tomorrow, and I\'ll probably do the same type of shipping as You, I\'ll keep You up to date on everything, such as when I ship out the MT stuff.\r\n[img:2b3362f0e2]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10039/DSC00793.JPG[/img:2b3362f0e2]\r\nThe small stuff such as springs and washers, steering spring etc. is in the small bag, can\'t really see them though from that pic.\r\nThanks'),(28449,'8c50fd6402','well I tested the car I was going to send you and found out that the controller was broke.  I am going to send you the same type of car, but the frequency is 27hz instead of 49.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28450,'8c50fd6402','well I tested the car I was going to send you and found out that the controller was broke.  I am going to send you the same type of car, but the frequency is 27hz instead of 49.'),(22072,'7995d99fa1','Got the CDs. Thanks man. :-) \r\n\r\nI did like the Zappa a lot more than Joe\'s garage, but it wasd up and down for me. It\'s weird, it\'s I\'ll be digging one bar, hating the next bar, perplexed by another, etc.. It was like he kept throwing in unexpected changes, and it sometimes didn\'t sit well with me. I don\'t know, gotta give a lot more listens to be fair.\r\n\r\nI dug the Andre Williams. Really trashy, I like that. I got a lotta really trashy sounding stuff you might like.\r\n\r\nI really dug the Mars Volta. Not sure about the vocals. Why that a guy or a girl? KInda reminded me of the singer from At the Drive In. The music almost sounded like a progressive rock version of At The Drive In. Anyways, it got my interest, and stuck with me to the end. I just sat there smoking out listening to it. I almost fell asleep. That\'s good thing, when I really get into music, it puts me to sleep. :lol: \r\n\r\nThat Fu Manchu was much better than Daredevil. Daredevil drones, and grooves, and drones some more, for 20 tracks, and never seems to get going the way that one did by the 3rd track, or at least I don\'t think it did. Never made through all 20 tracks.  :grin: \r\n\r\nFu Manchu reminds me, check out, http://www.gearheadmagazine.com/\r\n\r\nYou\'ll love it, it all about hot rods and garage rock. They got their own label, Fu Manchu has been released on it.\r\n\r\nAnyways, thanks again, I love getting new music. I\'ll be getting some stuff out to you real soon.\r\n\r\ndave'),(28089,'9d1a67658a','Here go to this link, it will brighten your mood.  I did it and it\'s beeing shipped out the 18th.  FREE BABY!\r\n[url=http://www.rcmod.com/viewtopic.php?t=3649]Click Here Because Your Gay![/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27299,'4cdb173ccf','This is from Admin at RCmod.\r\n\r\n\r\n\"I made you a moderator of the \"Unrelated Talk\". Welcome to our site! I know people give you poop all the time but I figured out what it really is...you want to see the site excel. I like your style and even though I don\'t always agree with the poop you start with some of the mods, I have given you a chance to shine as moderator. Show us how you can help this site grow!\"\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\nAdmin\r\n\r\nThis dude must have a real head on his shoulders.  :shock: \r\nI can\'t believe dude made me a mod.'),(34744,'facf55d3e0','[quote:facf55d3e0=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:facf55d3e0=\"ph2t\"]lol, man, it\'s all good.  I know where you\'re comming from. I didn\'t mis-interpret, it\'s cool.  I know what you mean about the arguments n stuff, I tried to word my statements as carefully as I can, but sometimes it\'s like \"fuck it\", lol........[/quote:facf55d3e0]\r\nUnderstood. Can we go smoke a bowl yet? lol[/quote:facf55d3e0]\r\n\r\nlol, I say we meet up a hue\'s.....try out that new doohicky of his.........'),(25386,'6d10768958','np, have a look around the site... this problems been encountered before many a time.   there will be information about this in topics like \"tab lowering\"   and motor clip fix in the how to section.   \r\n\r\n you\'ll learn a lot more that way, and by reading up on the older pages you will have fun along the way...   enjoy... z.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23673,'99611be840','Dave, any chance you can do a FET mod for me? I bid $53.00 on your Camaro to support the site but I still got outbid :sad:'),(23674,'14c8b8104c','[quote:14c8b8104c=\"Sugarfoot\"]Dave, any chance you can do a FET mod for me? I bid $53.00 on your Camaro to support the site but I still got outbid :sad:[/quote:14c8b8104c]Yeah, that bithigh guy is on a rampage, it\'s crazy, I think he\'s a bit high... or something. :lol: \r\n\r\nYeah I\'ll do you a FET mod. I just charge people $10 + return shipping. I usually get cars out the following monday, providing I don\'t happen run out of FETs.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested, let me know, and I\'ll get you my info.\r\n\r\nDave'),(23678,'b0947d0174','Yeah, let\'s trade \'em... you can send the Challenger to me at:\r\n\r\nMat Mathey\r\n3104 SE 39th Avenue\r\nPortland, OR  97202\r\n\r\nSend me your address, and I\'ll get the hummer in the mail Monday.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMat (hue35)'),(24930,'00f09c1f41','I got your wheels back in the mail yesterday... WTF   I put the wrong addy on it, and they sent it back here to me..\r\n\r\n\r\nI apologize for the delay man, and you\'re probably thinkin what the fuck is this wanker doin, but rest assured that I\'m on it, and they\'re on their way to you for sure.. PM me when you get em...\r\n\r\nYou\'ll have to fine tune em when you get em since all Bit chassis\' are slightly different with the way the knuckles sit and all.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31652,'889c8ca8f5','yes , it said around 1-2weeks wich is the middle of the range postage , \r\notherwise it would have been twice as much .\r\nbtw : have you posted the hummer yet ?'),(31653,'899da7d259','I\'ll be doing that ASAP. My girlfriend is on vacation, and since she works two jobs, I\'ve been seeing as much of her as I can. I had to return the motor set I bought for you because some ass had already returned it and put the green gear/motor in it replacing the orange. I didn\'t notice until yesterday. I got you a new one with the correct motors and gears! :)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(33283,'f676cd7b31','[quote:f676cd7b31=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:f676cd7b31=\"ph2t\"][quote:f676cd7b31=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:f676cd7b31=\"ph2t\"]hey dude, I\'ll take it all.\r\n\r\nI see you\'re asking for $6 shipped.  How about we make it $10 for all that.  So take $10 off the price of the deluxe fix and ship it all down together.\r\n\r\nhow does that sound?\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:f676cd7b31]\r\n\r\nSounds great ph2t i should be able to ship next week as im waiting for a payment.\r\n\r\nBtw do you have a site you reccomend for dry bearings for a mini-z?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:f676cd7b31]\r\n\r\nI think the mini-zracer.com shop has dry \"enduro\" bearings, but I\'m not sure.  Otherwise just buy a set of yeah racing ones from rcmart and soak them in turps and then let \'em dry.  \r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:f676cd7b31]\r\n\r\nThanks ph2t\r\n\r\nBtw how\'d you get to score a Evo over in aussie?[/quote:f676cd7b31]\r\n\r\nmade 505 an offer you couldn\'t refuse.  I\'m teaming up with my mate that runs ausmicro.com to get out the mosfets for this baby.  so I neededa chassis to test, market, etc..'),(34737,'14dfea370d','[quote:14dfea370d=\"ph2t\"]lol, man, it\'s all good.  I know where you\'re comming from. I didn\'t mis-interpret, it\'s cool.  I know what you mean about the arguments n stuff, I tried to word my statements as carefully as I can, but sometimes it\'s like \"fuck it\", lol........[/quote:14dfea370d]\r\nUnderstood. Can we go smoke a bowl yet? lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34522,'30e368c863','I just sent my paypal payment. Thanks for the hookup SWG!'),(27463,'802ca0fedc','I was cruise\'n thru cleaning up my favorite sites and ran acrosos this....\r\n[img:802ca0fedc]http://www.jdmtoys.com/bitcharg/images/bigimages/gp05.jpg[/img:802ca0fedc]\r\nIn a Pull Back.....  Check it here:\r\n\r\n http://www.jdmtoys.com/bitcharg/bodies.htm\r\n\r\nGood Luck !'),(31546,'7cb2e27ca5','I have no idea if it\'ll get there in time, but I think it\'ll make it.  I sent it priority insured.'),(24976,'89acca3d1d','Yo if you want the mini-z let me know I also have 4 xmods for trade too 2 are lithuim 1 has hobby class EP and 1 stock Camaro I am look for 1/43-1/64 scale cars motorcycles buses for my city.if you are intersted hit me on msn.'),(25480,'50d26c62e5','Sorry dude I am out of town on a biz trip have had no time to log in, damn these 17 hour days :(.  I will ask the wife if anything came in.  Did you get the box of loot I sent.'),(22081,'7e56331db1','The items are sent.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31538,'057579848d','Well I\'d like to say thank you for the props.\r\n\r\nI am a much more active member at ripper7racing. In fact I am a moderator over there. We have an online magazine, which, I\'m happy to say that in our past issue, I wrote a tutorial/article on lowering a bit. The link to the magazine is [url=http://www.ripper7racing.com/Magazine/]here[/url]. When you get there, click on \"Micros and Minis\", which will take you to our current issue. I believe my article is the last one.\r\n\r\nThe pics in the mag are a little small, so if you want, here is a link to my r7r gallery, where I have the larger pics: [url=http://www.ripper7racing.com/galleries/profile.php?uid=22]link![/url] Click on lowering mod tutorial.\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'d like to also invite you to r7r. It is a bit more friendly of a community than bitPimps(not that BP is bad).\r\n\r\nAnyway, whether or not you join us at r7r is not important. Make sure you take pics and don\'t forget who told you how to lower  :-o \r\n\r\nFeel free to PM me back anytime.\r\n\r\nGood luck,\r\n~midget_man1387~'),(36427,'701539e140','[quote:701539e140=\"MafiaS\"]Superly, I am not sure you know the answer to this question but I figured you knew alot and could maybe help my friend and I...\r\n\r\nMy buddy that i am getting the Iwaver with, he would like to know one thing, perhaps you would know the answer?\r\n\r\nWe are both new to this scale and i didnt want to give him the wrong answer...\r\n\r\nHe asked to ask you guys\r\n\r\n&quot;if i can install a novak esc and a novak receiver for micro cars in place of the one it has, and if i can replace the standard iwaver servo with a Hitec HS-81&quot;[/quote:701539e140]\r\n\r\nSorry man, can\'t help ya. I know nothing about electronics from larger scale r/c stuff.\r\n\r\nWhile a lot of dudes got into bits after already being into bigger scales, I started with bits and am working up to 1:24.\r\n\r\nSomeone like betty.k or ph2t, or LBRC would probably be able to answer that.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32866,'af728a0cfa','Hold on a second and I\'ll check.\r\n\r\nNeed some advice if you don\'t mind too.  Someone wants to trade me thier Sportmaxx with a Megatech Q1.6 Chianelli and tuned pipe for my Novak SS5800 BL system.  I\'ve not heard much about Megatech engines, so I\'m torn on the trade.  What are your thoughts?\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(26722,'db07b6c4b0','[quote:db07b6c4b0=\"honda_s2000\"]hey cabo ,\r\nyou know the post about the \" whirly doos \" i gona pick 2 up for my local newsagents for £4 each , il use one to mod ( im gona need luck ) and the other just for messing , but more to the point\r\n1. would you kindly look inside and see what motor is in there for me , im guessing a hardwired bu ti would be wrong ,\r\n2.would you be interested ( because you have one ) in some mods for them , i know it sound silly , but i think they have some potential , also could you look for any other specs for me , ie , how many cells im guessing one , but im not 100%\r\ncheers,\r\npeace out  :cool: \r\nh20[/quote:db07b6c4b0]I don\'t have one anymore to rip open and give you specs on, sorry.\r\nIf I remember correctly, the motor was hard wired.\r\nHere\'s a little convo I had about them:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2943\r\n\r\nYou might try asking ph2t for the specs you\'re looking for - he may remember some specs.\r\n\r\nSorry I couldn\'t help ya more - good luck!'),(26724,'05ce9fe38e','[quote:05ce9fe38e=\"honda_s2000\"]49 castle hill\r\neast leake\r\nloughbrough\r\nleic,\r\nLE12 6LU[/quote:05ce9fe38e]\r\n\r\nNot that I don\'t think you know your own address, but when I went to the Post Office today to check on some shipping costs, they couldn\'t give me one.  It might just be an idiot at the service counter, but I have never seen an addy like this either.\r\n\r\nWhat country?  \r\n\r\nCould double check that this is the [b:05ce9fe38e]exact way[/b:05ce9fe38e] to have it written on the package.  (capital letters, spelling, line by line)\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nP.S.  I just want to make sure any transaction that we may do goes smoothly and arrives safe and sound. :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33358,'09c2d106d7','fuck, you\'re on early!  I haven\'t even left for work yet!  lol....\r\n\r\nyou didn\'t see chris per chance?  (hoping.......)\r\n\r\nfuck I\'m annoying......\r\n\r\n :)'),(22086,'0af8f616a8','[quote:0af8f616a8=\"kvik369\"]Do you have one? - if not I can send you one with the other cars to experiment on.  By the way, where are you - CA ?[/quote:0af8f616a8]The Nikko car? Yeah I got one. \r\n\r\nI\'m in AZ.\r\n\r\nI\'m wondering what micro_amps means by it being similar to a super bit, I don\'t see the comparison. It looks nearly identical to a Motorworks car to me.\r\n\r\ndave'),(23199,'fb679929a3','no offense towards you or biohazard or anyone else from that site i know. it was mainly against charliebrownku. you dont gota like what i did but you should be able to laugh. i really dont even hate him i just had to get some revenge lol.'),(22089,'9ce1373d31','[quote:9ce1373d31=\"kvik369\"]I don\'t know but thats what he told me.  So I\'ll send 2 SE\'s, a H1 hummer and a regular zip(what about a pcb swap with an ms - if so I\'ll send an ms also) Getting sick of me yet? Let me know the price and the send info.\r\ntanx\r\n\r\nkvik369\r\n\r\nkvik369@netzero.com[/quote:9ce1373d31]Ok, cool. \r\n\r\nI got an extra 27mhz cannonball PCB if you\'d like me to swap that in. It identical to a MS one.\r\n\r\nYou can send your stuff to:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd #1131\r\nPhoenix AZ, 85033\r\n\r\nYou can include payment, or paypal me at davesmojoe@yahoo.com. \r\n\r\nDave'),(22090,'9ce1373d31','[quote:9ce1373d31=\"kvik369\"]I don\'t know but thats what he told me.  So I\'ll send 2 SE\'s, a H1 hummer and a regular zip(what about a pcb swap with an ms - if so I\'ll send an ms also) Getting sick of me yet? Let me know the price and the send info.\r\ntanx\r\n\r\nkvik369\r\n\r\nkvik369@netzero.com[/quote:9ce1373d31]Ok, cool. \r\n\r\nI got an extra 27mhz cannonball PCB if you\'d like me to swap that in. It identical to a MS one.\r\n\r\nYou can send your stuff to:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd #1131\r\nPhoenix AZ, 85033\r\n\r\nYou can include payment, or paypal me at davesmojoe@yahoo.com. \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25965,'fb748a14b5','you suck :-)'),(22094,'d5ab55ff42','[quote:d5ab55ff42=\"hue35\"]The Mars Volta dude is the singer from At the Drive-In... for some reason I though you might dig that. That disc is pretty fun, I litened to the shit out of it when I got it.. maybe got a little burned out, but I\'m good with it now. The drummer is a motherfucker.[/quote:d5ab55ff42]Oh ok, it all makes sense now. :lol: \r\n\r\nThat drummer is smoking. I love crazy technical drummers like that. :grin: \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:d5ab55ff42]... by the way, I just picked up The first Detroit Cobras disc at the record store I occasionally pick up a copy of gearhead... God Damn... they\'re fun as hell. [/quote:d5ab55ff42]That the one with Bad Girl and Midnight Blues? I love that one, lots of great covers.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:d5ab55ff42]You got the red gear, right?\r\n\r\nlater[/quote:d5ab55ff42]Yeah man, thanks, I forgot, more toys to play with. :-D \r\n\r\nDave'),(22095,'7945ac2ffb','Yo, you on AIM right now?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22096,'7945ac2ffb','Yo, you on AIM right now?'),(22097,'b176a6edaa','Nah, don\'t have time right now. Was just browsing the forums before logging off to run some errands. We can do it later though.'),(23929,'b41432b31a','nelly makes them way way way more fun dude. the install isnt that hard.'),(22100,'b176a6edaa','Nah, don\'t have time right now. Was just browsing the forums before logging off to run some errands. We can do it later though.'),(22101,'e9a23272e8','Ok cool thanks, it\'s VERY nice to see you again.  :-)'),(22104,'42257ac686','you\'re sending them to me? and not payaso?\r\n\r\n\r\nmy address is \r\n\r\n\r\nBrian Gaynor\r\n316 Delaware Avenue\r\nLorain, OH 44052'),(36934,'ac63023a53','found a flash plugin for DW on the exchange. makes great little gallery swf files.\r\n\r\nstoli.ca\r\n\r\npassword is bumbum.'),(36935,'c41e5e8b75','show and tell.  :-o \r\n\r\nyou could use fiberglass (G10) instead... roughly half price for twice the sheet area. i personally like the material a lot, it\'s almost as stiff as cf, but cheaper, dyable in many colors, and doesn\'t conduct electricity.\r\n\r\nbut cf is the bling-bling material of RC.'),(34058,'c102f75e13','you really dont like me do ya');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37796,'657a5515e0','Sorry I haven\'t got back to you. I\'m waiting for the money to be deposited in my paypal acct. It usually takes about 3 days. Thanks for your patience pimp! :)'),(37270,'0b75571300','Never mind, I\'m gettin my bro to get the stuff for me, I\'ll pay him back when he comes home.'),(36752,'97a8196b32','I\'ll take the link for \r\nPhatnotes and WebIS toolbox\r\n\r\nThanx for the hook up man, my dad thanks you too. They\'re for him.'),(35053,'8d594c2a5e','Sick man, just let me know when ever its cool. \r\n\r\nPs. you know where i can get a sweet deal on the original Xmods?'),(28117,'1853ea9f9a','Whats up you little all kinds of RC havin\' bitch???'),(22132,'8a1a8e7290','[quote:8a1a8e7290=\"kvik369\"]I wanted to swap it with a ms 2 speed (also put the zip pcb back into the ms - if thats not  a prob.  You didn\'t tell me a price (I prefer paypal unless you want a check - I hate mailing cash) \r\n2 se\'s  - 1 H1 hummer - 1 zip/ms pcb swap[/quote:8a1a8e7290]Oh, I see, ok we\'ll do the MS swap then. The Zip Zap board will not fit in a bit, I can stick the Cannonball one in there instead if you like, and just send the ZZ PCB back.\r\n\r\nPrice is $10 a car. Shipping should only be a couple bucks, unless you want Priorty mail, I think that\'s $3.85, but I think it\'s more if it\'s over a pound. You can get a quote at www.usps.com my zip is 85033.\r\n\r\nPaypal\'s fine, I gave you the address for that didn\'t I? Well just in case, it\'s davesmoejoe@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nDave'),(22109,'e9a23272e8','Ok cool thanks, it\'s VERY nice to see you again.  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37423,'73d3aa1693','My sister.'),(32463,'96c5d6e139','I know man, but I was so disapointed that my shit busted that I sorta let it out.  :lol:'),(34569,'3253cafff3','Anytime.  I\'ve been pretty busy recently.  I\'m usually not this Busy.  \r\n\r\nI\'ve got some projects that should have been done ages ago.  Stand by for one of the fastest bits ever made.  I also want to put some time into an Xmod that I picked up a couple months ago.'),(29967,'8190b46e4a','If they have one when I grab mine, would you want me to pick one up for you?\r\n\r\nIt won\'t proably be until afer the 4th of July, but if you still want one, let me know.\r\n\r\nI need to save up for my annual 4th of July party.'),(34268,'8a531c7f8a','[quote:8a531c7f8a=\"sessiz\"]Is....\r\n\r\nYahya Mangir\r\n435 Hamilton street\r\nAlbany NY 12203\r\n\r\nBy the way, did ya get the cash? :???:[/quote:8a531c7f8a]\r\n\r\nYah I got it sorry I did not let you know got it yesterday and forgot to PM ya!\r\n\r\nthanks man I know you will like the TVR :-) \r\n\r\nAaron'),(37100,'43a87212fb','Hi Cabo!\r\nI have seen something that for me is against BP policies and philosophy, the last member called &quot;Juzi\'s Mom&quot; has a website that is NOT (Ithink) related to BP.\r\ncan you check it?\r\nI think she\'s not interested in bits...should be banned!\r\nI might be wrong but..you never know.\r\nthks 4 taking te time to read.\r\nMad_Maxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30011,'4d1c4e8a10','Hey microman, i have money coming into my paypal account to pay for some ebay shit i bought, and don\'t know if i\'ll have $4.00, but can you just send them in an envelope for the cost of the stamp and i\'ll send you what i have in my paypal, which should be about 2 bucks but if i have 4 in my account i\'ll send it right away. Thanks alot'),(30505,'95bd64a9d0','ok thanks for sending it  , later .'),(30550,'19a1e71141','hi swg i got the paymnet for the reciver i will send it out the first chance i get , thanks , matt .'),(27602,'074d6374ed','[quote:074d6374ed=\"micro_man\"]ok my dad said it no problem for him to pay pal you , he will help me do it after he gets out of work tomorow . thanks , later.[/quote:074d6374ed]\r\n\r\nNo problem dude.\r\n\r\nWhenever. :cool: \r\n\r\nI\'ll get it out monday.\r\n\r\nMike'),(25633,'0e90f68610','Cool, already got a detail tutorial. I think dude stayed up all night putting it together, because he didn\'t have this last night. :lol: \r\n\r\nhttp://members.cox.net/codesuidae/FetModMT.html\r\n\r\nDave'),(22114,'810ee5700c','[quote:810ee5700c=\"sessiz\"][quote:810ee5700c=\"crazydave\"]Hey Sezziz, I\'m looking forward to seeing that poster you\'re making.\r\n\r\nYou gots some skillz man, is graphic arts something you make money off of, or you just spending too much timein front of the computer? :lol: \r\n\r\nAnyways, you can send that to:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n6751 W Indian School Rd.\r\nApt # 1150\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\n\r\n.and thanks man, this is something I\'m gonna hang on to.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:810ee5700c]\r\n\r\nI fucked up man. I just got the poster I sent ya back. I fucked up on the zip, instead of 85033 I had put down 85003. Sorry about that man, I\'ll re-send it out god willing tomorrow.\r\nOnce again I apologize man. :([/quote:810ee5700c]That\'s perfect, I forgot to tell you I moved. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'ve been getting my forwarded mail, but I was afraid the poster would get lost, but now I can just give you my new address, so it\'s all cool. 8-) \r\n\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School rd. #1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37484,'35953b6835','Cuase I got other things going on. That\'s also why you piss me off by wasting my fucking time with your lil kid bullshit. Now take my lil bit of advice or don\'t. Your choice to make.'),(34805,'0fbd729de5','good christ - another internet illiterate fuck.\r\n\r\nI\'ll leave \"JordanQ\" in your all-too-capable hands?\r\n\r\n[/quote]'),(34806,'0fbd729de5','good christ - another internet illiterate fuck.\r\n\r\nI\'ll leave \"JordanQ\" in your all-too-capable hands?\r\n\r\n[/quote]'),(34807,'f74398cece','No fuckin shit man. For fucks sake the kid can\'t even spell \"what\" correctly. Unfortunatly I gotta get outta here so I\'m just gonna lock that shit down. I pray to the all mighty internet gods that he posts another bullshit thread when I\'m around. :lol:'),(32288,'67c00f9a19','thanks, you know you coulda just replied to my thread in the dumpster lol'),(32289,'e3b5a2bb20','The dumpster smells :-)'),(25018,'409b298fe4','[quote:409b298fe4=\"Sugarfoot\"]Here it be Dave,\r\n\r\nRobert Estrada\r\n1312 Dougall Ave.\r\nWindsor, Ont.\r\nN8X 1R5\r\nCanada[/quote:409b298fe4]Your car is on the way. I sent it regular postage. Not sure how long that will take to your neck of the woods, but I know when me and Voodoomafia ship stuff back and forth, it takes anywhere from 2 weeks to 2 months. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22123,'09072e7f44','vbmaster\r\n\r\nI shelfed the project.  nothing available.\r\n\r\nBut you can make one...a bit of HW....a bit of SW...and some time.\r\n\r\nTime is what I don\'t have.\r\n\r\nreport on your progress.  pimps would be excited.\r\n\r\n\r\n-nox'),(22124,'f0f51fee7d','Hey bro, how much of a hard on do you have for that old school Mini you got from SDog?  Willing to part with it for some sheckles?  PM me either way.'),(33808,'e38872fada','haha it\'s certainly no problem. I appreciate the PM. I\'m sure you guys don\'t let SHAUN know  :-o \r\n\r\nWhat is up we these twats nowadays anyway? They make me feel 28, not 18!! \r\n\r\nI\'m glad I never was a n00b. I was new, but certainly no n00b lol\r\n\r\ngod, I miss the old days. When I was basically the only teenage pimp. But it makes me feel good to be the [b:e38872fada]original[/b:e38872fada] teenage bitPimp! haha\r\n\r\nanyway, thanks pimp!!\r\n~midget  8-)  &lt;--- is that copyrighted by anyone? lol'),(22127,'6cf75bdd50','This isn\'t one of those where the hell is my package kinda posts, but more of a when did you ship it cuz I don\'t trust my neighbors one 8-)   Thanks bro, can\'t wait to drive this puppy hard :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25481,'05c93a18df','If you dont have the xmods, whatever dude you tell me I am easy :)'),(23749,'46fc2b5b25','i got a little space. email them to me\r\n\r\nmyaaiko@comcast.net'),(26027,'d242853398','Go here www.reduxguild.org and fight w/ me 8-)'),(22136,'317c80dfd1','alrighty then, sweet, thanks man!'),(22137,'bc5ba4d160','[quote:bc5ba4d160=\"Finks\"]This isn\'t one of those where the hell is my package kinda posts, but more of a when did you ship it cuz I don\'t trust my neighbors one 8-)   Thanks bro, can\'t wait to drive this puppy hard :cool:[/quote:bc5ba4d160]Sorry dude, I could fill your ear full of excuses all day long, but the jist of it is...my kid started school last week. (he\'s 4 we got him in the head start program), we had a babysitter lined up, but she flaked, and we were totally screwed. \r\n\r\nAt any rate, your package got put off, and instead of filling you up with excuses, I thought it would be best to inform you when it actually shipped.\r\n\r\nI am very sorry, this is not usually like me, but we got our shit straightened out now, my wife started her new schedule today, and I already had definate plans to hit the PO tomorrow. \r\n\r\nIf you\'d like I could splurge for the insurance, and shipping confirmation, so you don\'t have to worry about the neighbors, I owe you that much at least.\r\n\r\nDave'),(33958,'357ee97a29','[quote:357ee97a29=\"chrome\"]Sent you an email about your Evo.  Let me know if you got pictures or anything.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...[/quote:357ee97a29]\r\n\r\nHit ya back, I fixed the piece using the inside of a ink pen sanded the knuckle down a bit and glued it on using a dab of hot glue and then some plastic cement glue it works perfectly,and its a perfect fit for a screw.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33959,'16e6680f3f','tomorrow I will receive my salary of this month and will decide wether I am able to pay my debts and buy the ZZMT'),(35321,'f901cf22af','Motor'),(35322,'078c95aed8','[quote:078c95aed8=\"LBRC\"]Motor[/quote:078c95aed8]\r\n\r\nThanks for all the help LBRC i appreciate it! :-)'),(23810,'46ff37578b','dude the nelly with the stage 2 goes waaaay to fast.'),(25082,'f1d3bd7838','Hi Dave,\r\n\r\nI\'ve been watching you post for a long time and I have to say I\'m very impressed.\r\n\r\nI hear you can do a MOSFET mod to a ZZ SE?\r\n\r\nIf you\'re doing them for others (like me   :-)  ) how much do you charge?\r\n\r\nCan you also fix the unequal steering in the SE?  I have the Torrino and it steers more to one side than the other.\r\n\r\nWell, keep up the good work.  I hope to hear from you,\r\n\r\nLove Doc   :cool:'),(24434,'2793f77650','[quote:2793f77650=\"DarkTari\"]Whatcha wanna know   :???:[/quote:2793f77650]\r\n\r\n\r\nWell how to paint so damn good... Do you use an airbrush.. I got a testors air brush that rawks but no air . i need to get a compressor thingy'),(24435,'f302437865','I use Dupli-Color Auto paint.  You already have an airbrush, you need this\r\n\r\nhttp://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=34843');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37121,'524405791c','[quote:524405791c=\"sessiz\"]I figured as much man...sorry. :-([/quote:524405791c]\r\nIt\'s cool... sorry I was short with ya, but it was just about GO time!\r\n\r\nOK, now, have at it... I deleted your post, but if you could put it up again, that\'d be perfect... or somethin\' like it, anyway.\r\n\r\nMan, this shit is almost the all-time funniest shit ever... god damn, just when you think we\'re out of dumb fucks....\r\n\r\n :lol:'),(25259,'980e337f73','Sure did DT. I wrote a thank you post hailing your greatness. I want to personally thank you so much. No one has ever done something like that for me before. My wife was suspicious at first and then [b:980e337f73]]BAM[/b:980e337f73] I hits her ass up wit the permission slip and she backed down.  :-D  It was great! \r\n\r\nI\'ve already started moddin these puppies, and as soon as I get back to Maine, I\'ll have my tools to finish them.  As a thank you, I\'d like to donate a rig for whatever contest you guys come up wit. I promise, It\'ll be off the hook. Also If you have another Auction, I have some projects in the future that would go over well. I just want to help out in any way I can.  When I get back to Portland, I\'ll have my old high payin job back, so my pimp stick won\'t be limp ever again.\r\n\r\nHere\'s a preveiw of what you\'re donated rigs are gonna look like. I\'ve got some body mods and killer colors picked out for these.\r\n[img:980e337f73]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v456/HirotoR34/stupasupra.jpg[/img:980e337f73]\r\n[img:980e337f73]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v456/HirotoR34/sickline34.jpg[/img:980e337f73]'),(35571,'35ad5f3ab8','[quote:35ad5f3ab8=\"crazydave\"]Yeah, that did help. Thanks. I\'m going for the F-150, but I\'m curious, how much does that slammed suspension help, and what if I cut a coil or 2 out?\r\n\r\nI don\'t need to be faster than the cars, just as long as I can possibly run with them.[/quote:35ad5f3ab8]\r\n\r\nThe truck is VERY slow compared to the car. In a drag, the car doubles it\'s lead every 10 ft (approximately). If you really want a truck get it, AWD is a must. But if you want to race, get the car. The truck can\'t even keep up with Gen1 Xmods  :o . Unless you\'re racing other trucks  :-? \r\n\r\nI\'m saving my 500th post, hence the PM\'s.\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35037,'426d6d5925','Hiroto do you just have Xmods, or do you have some mini Z as well...\r\n\r\nJust curious because I want to buy an Xmod but I am worried MiniZ might be better.'),(35038,'95c443a65f','You selling anything, or want to give anything away? I am dying for a some pullback wheels, and that green lambo is my favorite bit of all time, the sad part is I can not find it anywhere!!!'),(32068,'469cd386e9','[quote:469cd386e9=\"kvik369\"]Hey CD - whats up?\r\n\r\nDon\'t mean to bust your chops, but can I have a status report.\r\n\r\n(It helps with my post office if I know to look out for something)\r\n\r\nTanx\r\n\r\nVik[/quote:469cd386e9]Hey, what\'s up? \r\n\r\nI had a problem with the first FET order, put in the wrong card # or something. I ordered them again second day priorty, so I should have the FETs tomorrow. Either way, I won\'t make it to the PO until Monday, so that is my projected finish date. I\'ll let you know as soon as I\'m done.\r\n\r\nSorry for the delay, I\'ve just been sucking at everything I do lately. :-( \r\n\r\ndave'),(36912,'25375a83e9','[quote:25375a83e9=\"Stoli\"]hey mang, could ya gimmie a call tonight and give me a hand with iframes stuff. [/quote:25375a83e9]\r\nWe\'ll probably be out most of the night so if we need to do the phone thing, it\'ll have to be tomorrow or something.\r\n[quote:25375a83e9=\"Stoli\"]Basically I want to have images on the left and when you click the images on the left an embedded media player on the right plays the video without opening a new page etc.[/quote:25375a83e9]\r\nThat\'s going to be tricky. I\'m not even sure if it work at all with movies, guess it might depend on how it\'s implemented.\r\nBasically, what you\'re wanting to do is change the I-Frame source to the movie file. Try Googling for &quot;iframe dynamic content&quot;. There\'s examples there, just not exact to what you\'re wanting to do. That means you\'ll have to modify or extend the script for your own needs.\r\n\r\nMy suggestion though would be, for movies, just embed the movies in separate pages and either use the IFrame to load those pages, or just use regular frames.\r\nI don\'t really remember seeing any sites that loaded movies without a page refresh. I think that\'d get way too taxing on peoples Internet connections (if it works at all).\r\n[quote:25375a83e9=\"Stoli\"]Also do you have any good scripts for a photo gallery. I wanna have a page come up with 8 thumbnails on the top and when you click a thumb it comes up 640x480 underneath the thumbs. each thumb you click will then appear in the window below and replace the current 640x480 image.?[/quote:25375a83e9]\r\nWell, if you have PHP and MySQL, you can find some gallery software that will pretty much handle whatever. There are several free ones out there.\r\nIf not, you might want to try using DIVs (or IFrames). You would be doing something very similar to what you wanted to do to your videos.\r\nBasically, when you click the thumbnail, you\'d call a JavaScript function that fill the DIV or IFrame with the content you passed to the JavaScript. Dreamweaver I believe will help write out the scripts and shit for you if you\'re having troubles.\r\n[quote:25375a83e9=\"Stoli\"]Make sense? I tried the iframes thingy and between Daniel and I we cann get it to work right. Same wiuth some of the photo viewers we have tried. I got one to work but not very well. I have tried programs like magic gallery but cannot find a crack for the program and all images are watermarked. I found a work around for the watermark but it will take forever to resize and copy and paste 200+ images.[/quote:25375a83e9]\r\nTotally, I understand. The problem is trying to explain it. It\'s near impossible for me to give you just a &quot;canned&quot; script that would work for you because I don\'t have enough intimate knowledge about your project. How things look, how they are expected to work, where images and movies are stored, what technologies do you have access to on your server, etc.\r\nThere\'s just too many variables there.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32978,'ed63d26838','So do you do any mods?   \r\n\r\nThe faster motors do help, but there are some mods that will REALLY wake up the cars.  Super Bits seem to be limited more than the Pro and Sport models.\r\n\r\nWhen I first got started, the \"Bit Racers\" were available here under the name \"Kitt Racers\" sold through hotwheels.  They were a wonderful source of Bit / MS parts.'),(36043,'b634fafb4b','[b:b634fafb4b]BRA[/b:b634fafb4b]-fuckin-[b:b634fafb4b]VO[/b:b634fafb4b]  :-o \r\n\r\n[quote:b634fafb4b]Can a single user win multiple places? \r\nYea, I suppose they can [b:b634fafb4b]if we want to be dickheads about it.* [/b:b634fafb4b]\r\nWe\'ve already ran into at least 1 case where a single user could\'ve/should\'ve walked away with 2 or 3 places - but what\'s that say about us? \r\nThink of it like this, if we kept SuperFly as a user (not moderator), he\'d win everytime and nobody else would ever get a shot. \r\nI\'m positive participation would drop to about 3 or 4 people in that case. [/quote:b634fafb4b]\r\n\r\nThis is exactly what I was sayin last time. If we did that, this contest would \r\nnot be worth havin ! I felt I had to plead my case last time and they reluctantly gave in.\r\n\r\nI Luv the \"You\'re sucking the fun outta these Contests\" statement at the end!  It was worded as not to offend but to get the point across  :-o \r\n\r\n[b:b634fafb4b][size=24:b634fafb4b]THANX !![/size:b634fafb4b][/b:b634fafb4b]  8-)'),(34632,'faf6b17548','thanks any good and free hosting sites you know of for me to use');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37602,'516e644ab1','[quote:516e644ab1=\"pimpsmurf\"][quote=PimpSmurf]I don\'t agree with everything the libertarians (base = liberty, not liberal) believe, just 95% of it. They are pretty far right wing. Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative. [/quote:516e644ab1]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t say liberals, I said libertarians. And they do indeed. There are a couple libertarian talk shows on talkradio and shortwave and they are most libertarians (about 75%) see Bush as more liberal than conservative.\r\n\r\nThe problem with all these labels is you have to define them. The problem with the LP is most members of the LP vote for republicans in states that are close. No need to have another sex-junkie in the White House.\r\n\r\nYou are seeing fault where there is non. I have not contradicted myself on this issue because it is an issue of beliefs. You are retreating, which is OK. I\'m not willing to argue a point (argue, not fight) that the other side isn\'t willing to bring ideas to the table.\r\n\r\nThanks anyway man. It was fun (except the gay sex.)\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote]\r\n :lol: You\'re a joke anymore to me dude.\r\nIf you can\'t even see the flaws in your posts, the contradictions, and just even general false statements you make - I can\'t help you.\r\nNobody can.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know what you\'re stuck on with the gay sex thing unless it\'s burned into your memory from you last gay experience or something.\r\n\r\nAnyways, I\'m not retreating. I own this place. You don\'t.\r\nIf I don\'t want it to be a political forum, guess what? It won\'t be.\r\nI\'ve let you go on long enough spewing your bullshit. Now I\'m putting a stop to it.\r\n\r\nIf you can\'t go back to what this forum is about, I\'m affraid you\'ll just have to leave - and guess who else can make that happen? Yup, me!\r\n\r\nGo bite your pillow.'),(37217,'c8fe53194c','The package went out today. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34636,'384b4fe2d2','[quote:384b4fe2d2=\"Sporttracguy\"]Hey man, Ive been searching and searching and i cant find any sort of a diagram to FET the zzse.  Since you seem to be well educated on the subject i figure ill go right to the source.  Do you have or know of a good tuttorial on doing an FET upgrade on the SE?\r\n\r\nAlso, Im trying to find the best place to order the FETs, any good places come to mind?\r\n\r\nThanks man\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:384b4fe2d2]I\'ve held off on doing a SE tutorial, because codesuidae has already done one, its at codesuidae.net but I think the way its arranged can be very confusing, and I\'m afraid anyone that follows that step by step might have some issues. \r\n\r\nYou know what? The info on FETs here is all spread out, and kinda confusing too. Give me until this weekend, I\'m gonna try to put together some kind of all inclusive article on FET mods.\r\n\r\nI get my FETs at digikey.com. They are cheap there, but theres a $5 surcharge on orders under $25. $5 is 10 FETs, so I always order 55 FETs, puts my order just over $25 before shipping. The #s are IRLML2502 for the N-channels, and IRLML6401 for the P-channels.\r\n\r\nDave'),(37326,'f8b1ac3b5d','Hey man, ive been doing some searching on the site and i cant seem to find the answer im looking for. Im installing an iwaver pcb in my zzse buggy but im a little confused about what to do with the steering POT. Do i use the existing zzse pot or do i use the iwaver pot??? ALso, ive been reading that i need to install 10k ohm resistors on the pot (whatever pot i end up using) Do What wires do i need to solder these to? The iwaver pot only has two wires but the se has three so im a little confused on the issue.\r\n\r\nAny help would be great\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37710,'74a2be13fa','lol no problems\r\n\r\nonce again a clean deal with skylinekid! that makes like what? 5?'),(37711,'7cfb36e3e9','Alright just got word from my uncle, he said its cool but asked kindly if you could include the extra 2 dollar fee that paypal yanks away from the money sent to his account.\r\n\r\nso it was 20 for the chassis\', 15 for the controllers, 2 for the pp fee?\r\n\r\nIf that is not cool please let me know, if you are ready send me your shipping info and i will most likely try and ship it 2morrow\r\n\r\nPaypal the money to  \r\n\r\nsstirpe@sympatico.ca.'),(37595,'3d0665fddf','I gotta go....You win. :lol:'),(35120,'7b629a6787','Hue, let\'s put it this way man. I\'ve searched every mall and LHS around me. All they told me was \"those are dicontinued your best bet is ebay, or something online.\"\r\n\r\nWhen I hit this older LHS I found these speed sets, they seemed pretty expensive and thinking because they were known as \"speed sets\" they came faster, so if you had a controller it was\'nt that bad of a deal. I am not saying what I did was not wrong or anything I am just explaining that I did\'nt have the intention of scraping the loose change from everyone\'s pocket. I paid 13 bucks for em, actually 13 47 or some shit like that each. As you pointed out to me that is about 10-11 dollars U.S. I wanted to give them away for 8 bucks shipped. Still I loose out but like i told Cabo in one of my PMs before I went Post crazy (I asked for his approval) I wanted to try and hook the pimps up, I thought this was a good deal. \r\n\r\nMoral is, i thought wrong. Made a mistake, but it was not like I was asking for it man. I said to myself \"I got a ton of these, and if the pimps think it is a really good deal I dont mind giving them more, in fact if a person were to buy more than 1, i would have done a deal and lowered it more, just to get rid of them.\" \r\n\r\nNow the site you showed me really put me in place, but I was\'nt doing anything to edge my reputation here at bitpimps. I\'ve learned my lesson as my other profile. I am spitting out some what decent mods. I write daily to the experts and ask them for advice on Xmods, Mini Z and Micros as well. I do this for love of the Hobby, not for money. Please do not get that impression.\r\n\r\nI realize that by you puttin me in my spot on the Fo\' Sale post, was to teach me a lesson, but I\'m all heart for the hobby, so if there is a problem just contact me directly. I hate being blasted infront of everyone. If I\'ve made a mistake and you think it is definately obvious putting me on display is killing me, directly detailing where I went wrong, as a 1 on 1 type of thing would be more appreciated. \r\n\r\nI spoke to Cabo once before, and asked him to delete the Post, or lock it, w.e he had to do. He told me it was done, and i\'m glad he had done it. To me it is not a money loss or gain about the speed sets. To me I wish to at least maintain respect from you or any other pimp.\r\n\r\nMy apologies Hue35\r\n\r\nSam...'),(31244,'fcdd90934c','Hey man, I got the package today... everything is perfect, thanks to your awesome packaging job! Thanks again, I\'ll spread the word.\r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31049,'740e0ff3b6','[quote:740e0ff3b6=\"MotorGong\"][quote:740e0ff3b6=\"blindrider3\"][quote:740e0ff3b6=\"MotorGong\"]dude, look at the picture that chaoscauser posted.\r\nthe one of his car. look at the quality of the photo, the style of\r\ncouch everything is on.....all looks like it is from the seventies.\r\nIt\'s before my time, too, but I\'ve seen old photos, seen the Seventies Show, etc.\r\n\r\nGet it?\r\n\r\n\r\n-Motor :)[/quote:740e0ff3b6]\r\n\r\nOhhhh I didn\'t even notice the homies lol[/quote:740e0ff3b6]\r\n\r\n\r\nYep hahaha\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nYes, the homies, but do you get the joke now? Did ya read the whole thread?[/quote:740e0ff3b6]'),(35746,'0828197ea5','Let me know, I could get them easily here!'),(32973,'d382151671','OK as I alluded to in the thread I of course am pissed as hell about the group buy and thought I would vent that frustration more constructively.  \r\n\r\nMy proposal is to hold a contest  for everyone, even those not involved in the group buy to write the best email to Michael and his Mini Speeder crew.  All letters will be posted here and then all will be mailed to this fuckwad.  \r\n\r\nAlso as we like to do here in the Hood, hopefully the contest could be advertised at other sites so that the whole community knows about this Douche.  \r\n\r\nOh and as for a prize for the winner, I got ya covered.  I have the Custom Porsche that I wanted to donate to the hopefully revitalization of the auction block.  You know, the one that looks like my RotM Porsche?  \r\n\r\nAnyhow, let me know if I am going overboard or if this is something that the hood would support.  Thanks\r\n\r\nFinks'),(36318,'ddccc18d04','well that just blew my mind!\r\n\r\nI\'ve been trippin around at a dance festival all weekend, covered in mud and higher than Edmund Hilary, and i come home to find a placing waiting for me in the blowout!  What a trip!\r\n\r\nI never woulda thunk it.\r\n\r\nThanks for having us all around Cabo - this is one fine place you\'ve got here.  Its my home on them internets. \r\n\r\nAnyways, anough of my drug induced warm-n-fuzzball sentiment! Now to collect my shiat!\r\n\r\nMy postal address is:\r\n\r\nMichael Frawley \r\nPO BOX 2010\r\nTOOWONG QLD 4066\r\nAUSTRALIA\r\n\r\nThanks again for making this whole she-bang possible cabo.  you rock!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37360,'040b17b821','Hey man, i saw a post about you needing a set of zzse lights?  Do you still need some or did you get your hands on a set?\r\n\r\nTHey still had a set or two up at my RS,, if you cant get your hands on a set just let me know,, \r\n\r\nSTG'),(29341,'47c005c5e0','Settle down... you\'re too fuckin\' hyper. Just chill a notch.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(37149,'d67160487b','[quote:d67160487b=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]And I also feel a little used. :-? \r\n\r\n :lol:[/quote:d67160487b]\r\n\r\nSorry dude... I think I may have gone a little too subtle, but if he comes back it\'ll be worth it. :-o'),(37150,'83b2b1ff3e','No worries.  I shoulda noticed the post count on three at least.  It\'s all in good humor.'),(32198,'383c7bd014','Yo DT, shipped out the bit on my lunch break. I packed it up really tight. Sent parcel post. Should by there by end of the week. Damn you got a good deal! Keep you\'re eyes peeled, cuz I might have to sell off a lot of my other bits. I have some really cool sets, but I have two or more of a lot of them. I\'m going to sell my dups off cuz I just don\'t have the time for them, and I need to the $. C\'est la vie. Later.'),(36032,'9dfb984fa2','[quote:9dfb984fa2=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:9dfb984fa2=\"DarkTari\"]C-Dub,\r\n\r\nMan what has happened here?  Voting used to be so easy, pick your choices, add up the points and pick your winners!  Goddamn, it seems like every contest it gets more difficult!  Shit \"USED\" to run so smuth with these, now it\'s a fuckin bunch of complaining and wishwashing back and forth!  This shit ain\'t fun no more and every contest it becomes less fun!  All started with trying to give one entrant 2 prizes which I wasn\'t gonna stand for, that shit was just fuckin rediculous!  We never had no shit like that happen in the past! So what if you voted for a car that didn\'t make the cut, points are all that count period!  Man I just don\'t know anymore.\r\nI voted for Hirotos Ferrari, it didn\'t make the cut but I\'m not changing my vote to something I don\'t like as much just to go with what everybody else likes! Fuck Dat! It just doesn\'t make the cut!\r\n\r\nI think YOU know what I\'m saying without saying it :???:[/quote:9dfb984fa2]\r\nI totally hear ya.\r\nI was just thinking to myself yesterday, \"after 11 contests and 3 years, you\'d think we\'d have a system down by now\". lol\r\n\r\nI can see both sides of the arguement, I just think it\'s being blown out of proportion. Whatever.\r\nLike usual, [b:9dfb984fa2]I just wanna get this put to bed.[/b:9dfb984fa2]\r\nEver notice none of this stuff ever comes up until it\'s crunch time? :lol:[/quote:9dfb984fa2]\r\n\r\nIn the famous word of Kwikbb...... [b:9dfb984fa2]\"WORD\"[/b:9dfb984fa2]  :cool: \r\n\r\nThat\'s because there ain\'t much participation until then!  You put out the word after we got the contest rules established about prizes and not one fuckin response, not one!  That right there really dissapointed me with our\r\nMods! And it aint like they don\'t have have !   Now I Guarantee you that when we do this \"Race Theme\" contest, we won\'t even have to mention prizes!  Wanna wager?  And let\'s not just to see.  LOL  \r\n\r\nOn another subject, the \"bitPimp My Ride\" idea I\'m just gonna have to run with on my own, and I don\'t mind at all!  I gave them a chance to volunteer.  There were 17 views with only you responding so I\'m going to announce it after we get the finals outta the way and I\'m going to advertise the shop doing the modz as [b:9dfb984fa2]Team DarkTari Racing[/b:9dfb984fa2] (like Pimp My Ride uses Califorina Customs)  If someone volunteers after we start this, I\'ll give their shop credit for the mod. I\'m gonna set up a whole theme following MTV\'s program using Homies as shop workers and maybe make up a garage too.  But believe me it\'ll be done up, Pimp Style fo sho!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37835,'6eb97b9f5c','definitely, I was thinking deans would do charging duties...I\'ll do you up a custom shell. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to add a bit o green :-o'),(28986,'48cd177165','Hey man,why don\'t you answer?\r\nHow about the cars?'),(37047,'896bc4af36','I will send all my xtra AWD stuff ur way tommorow, you\'ll like it garenteed :-)'),(37048,'9607d39e8f','nice, i really appreciate it man!'),(37238,'17267db555','Good job on that mrcc thing brother. Only thing that woulda made it better would have been this sentence &quot;Sessiz is awesome, barticus sucks penis monsters.&quot;  :lol:'),(37576,'df12a7045a','[quote:df12a7045a=\"99skyline\"]Ok.  That sounds good. I\'m expecting to recieve a Yellow Honda Civic from clxfiles soon so that will be the body I customize.  I don\'t want to screw up right away so I\'m just going to ask you this:  Do you lower the body before you paint it or after?\r\n\r\nThanks for being so nice about this and all of your help so far.[/quote:df12a7045a]good question, you lower before you paint, this way if the car get\'s scratched while you\'re doing your lowering, it won\'t ruin your nice paintjob.\r\n\r\nThere is more than one way to lower so you got some work ahead of you, to find the way that\'s easiest for you.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(35801,'72075f18bb','Dave man I am always here big guy! \r\n\r\nJust post me somtin when you are interested, if you don\'t got cash we could do a swap for some xmod stuff if you got any extra. I know you got crazy RC skills so it would be a pleasure man!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36053,'296da7b3a8','Alrighty, you stuff is already sent.  :-D'),(36054,'2edd7007d6','You sent it today? I thought you said 2morrow?'),(35803,'57039634c8','Try to find a good motor and stack the fets, I recomend a 4x2 stack, do the 6 cell and you will see a greatly noticably increase in speed, it is by far one of the cheapest, easyest and most efficient mods ever. I will even send you an extra battery case for it!!!!!!! I will also pack you 1 or 2 extra tie rods!!!!!! Try doing a mono shock aswell, some like it, some dont, its worth a shot!!!!\r\n\r\nYou can get some fets from the XCRL store at  http://xcrl.vstore.ca/\r\nI will nudge Admin to get something you want if its out of stock.\r\n\r\nSome good tuts at  http://www.freewebs.com/xcrl/  , just click on tutorials on the left side. \r\n\r\nA new but good and friendly fourm that all this belongs to is XCRL,  http://s9.invisionfree.com/XCRL_Forums/index.php?act=idx  I have been a friend of the admin since before talk of a fourm ever arose, a little over a year. Enjoy all this newfound freedom and have fun with your 1/28 scale expiriance.!!!!!\r\n\r\n\r\nBTW 2 more things came to mind, #1 centering your servo, #2  http://www.one28thrc.com/index.htm\r\n\r\nHave Fun :-o'),(28989,'b49975122f','I told you it would be better to find someone else to get you the cars.  there are other members here that would be happy to do it for you. I was going to send you a few free RC cars then you wanted me to send you the Zip Zaps then you sent me a rude email becuse I did not get you the price fast enough for the cars like I said in my last PM I think you should ask someone else.\r\n\r\nI hope you can work it out with someone and they can get you the cars.\r\nAaron\r\nsteelwoolghandi');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29721,'62a2097d72','Ok, lately I\'ve been torn. Getting a little bored with bits, and the guitar\'s been nagging at me. It sucks because its a decision I have to make first thing every morning when I wake up and go to the john. I have to decide, do I want to stare at the Musician\'s Friend catalog, or the Tower Hobbies catalog.  :lol: \r\n\r\nAnyways, what exactly I want to do has just been determined.\r\n\r\nI built this website about 4 years ago, and forgot about it. http://guitarkit.tripod.com/\r\n\r\nI just checked my email today and found this, an email from Saga!\r\n\r\n[quote:62a2097d72]Hi Dave, \r\n \r\nNice job with the Saga Guitar Kit site.  We have always envisioned something like this, but our manpower has made it difficult to put something like this together to date.  Thanks for making it possible for the proud owners of these kits to show off their work.\r\n \r\nI wonder if you would allow me to like to your site.  You are also welcome to put a link to our site.  I think having a non-related source providing the information you do would be more meaningful and credible.\r\n \r\nAlso, I have of guitar kits that people have sent me  that you might find interesting.  \r\n \r\nLet me know your thoughts.\r\nBest Regards,\r\nSaga Musical Instruments\r\n\r\nDavid Gartland\r\nMarketing\r\nwww.sagamusic.com[/quote:62a2097d72] \r\n\r\nHoly crap, I didn\'t think anyone even noticed that site!  I didn\'t even know the address, I had to go searching for it. :lol:\r\n\r\nSo now I want to set it up on its own domain, and build it in php so I can add a gallery where users can upload their own pics, and a forum. I got a local dealer that sells the guitars that said if I get it on my own domain, they\'ll offer up a saga guitar kit as a prize for a contest, but that was a while ago, I hope I can still get their interest.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile I\'m gonna pull out my leopard skin T-style and finish that bitch up.\r\n\r\nCool, I got projects. :-) \r\n\r\nI\'m pretty proud right now, so I had to tell someone. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave'),(28993,'fb200cb122','Hi,I\'m sorry I didnt write you but I didnt know how much I could spend.\r\n\r\nIs it a problem if I can only send money the normal way? \r\nIn Hungary(I\'m living there)there is no paypal-account cuz we dont use euro.\r\n\r\nI hope it will be allright,if no,just tell me.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28994,'86ab35e64d','[quote:86ab35e64d=\"betula66\"]Hi,I\'m sorry I didnt write you but I didnt know how much I could spend.\r\n\r\nIs it a problem if I can only send money the normal way? \r\nIn Hungary(I\'m living there)there is no paypal-account cuz we dont use euro.\r\n\r\nI hope it will be allright,if no,just tell me.[/quote:86ab35e64d]\r\n\r\nYes, that\'s fine. Tell me what you want, I\'ll get it, and I\'ll ship it when I recieve money.'),(28998,'cf1ee6e205','[quote:cf1ee6e205=\"betula66\"]So I\'d need 2 monster trucks,(a bigfoot bodied and the other is all the same to me),a motor kit and a tire kit(for monsters of course).\r\n\r\nOn the net its 64$ I think. How much should I send you?\r\n\r\nOn the net I saw it like this:\r\n\r\nZipZaps® Monster Truck Micro RC Tire and Wheel Kit ZipZaps® Monster Truck Micro RC Performance Booster Upgrade Kit[/quote:cf1ee6e205]\r\n\r\nI\'ll go by Radio Shack this weekend and see how much everything is. Sometimes they go on sale price that starts on Sunday. I\'ll need to check on shipping costs as well. What is your address?'),(36127,'4d455c8bcb','Dave,\r\nIf I get a lead on some, for a good price, would you be interrested?\r\n\r\n[img:4d455c8bcb]http://capsule.rc.online.fr/images_v2/forum/oatures/Dsc00350.jpg[/img:4d455c8bcb]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36155,'9253783525','Cool !  I\'ll keep you informed.\r\n\r\nI was also looking into getting a [b:9253783525]Metl-Tech[/b:9253783525]\r\n\r\n[img:9253783525]http://img457.imageshack.us/img457/8326/tc026ud.jpg[/img:9253783525]\r\n[img:9253783525]http://img481.imageshack.us/img481/1493/metlccj2du.jpg[/img:9253783525]'),(32263,'e7e35f1214','Hey just wanted to let you know I was unable to send your stuff Monday like I promised but got it out today (been having a bad work week)!\r\n\r\nI sent some extras and sent your DVD seperate as it would not fit in the box. thanks so much hope you like the stuff!\r\n\r\nAaron\r\n\r\nSWG'),(35671,'055460a0a7','Heh... I didn\'t even see the link to the auctions. I\'m outta my fuckin\' mind.\r\n\r\n$50 for 2, shipped?  These are about $16 each at Dinball... I haven\'t looked in a few weeks, but that\'s where the price was last month. Let me look around a bit and get back to ya... if these have dried up, I might go for that, but I was thinkin\' more like $40 shipped in my head.\r\n\r\nTalk to ya in a few...'),(34068,'175c6d3e54','y arent you on msn');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37532,'a64b9e8368','Why do you not like me I am just couris.'),(34073,'4627d2f2d8','Y dont you like me'),(34080,'119b1083ae','Dude, why in the fucking world would you make a post in SWG\'s VW Bus thread, and all you have to say that\'s on topic is, \"nice\", then you go on about getting blue paint at WalMart? What the fuck are you thinking? DO NOT MAKE SUCH USELESS POSTS, OR YOU WILL BE BANNED!!!\r\n\r\nhue35'),(32580,'1075ce8f9f','Allright man.  I\'ll ship it out as soon as it goes through.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(30359,'4a40f269f0','[quote:4a40f269f0=\"R Kustasz\"]Where did you get your JMK camera / transmitter / receiver?  About how much did it cost?\r\n\r\nIt looks cool.  Is the picture quality and transmission range ok?[/quote:4a40f269f0]\r\nI never bought one, just posted it cause it looked interesting.  bettyk bought one a while ago, hit \'em up.'),(29961,'17069c4a23','I forgot all about the Silver one. :?   I\'ll have to go grab one at RS.  \r\n\r\nI really meant just the Red and White ones that were discontinued.  I totally forgot all about the Silver one coming out awhile back.\r\n\r\nGood lookin\' out.   :cool: \r\n\r\nMike (SG219)'),(33819,'3f4d217620','Hey, I have a question for you.  When you made the wheelie bar out of the copper rod, you soldered it together right?  Did you use a soldering iron, or some kind of torch?  Thanks in advance.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36375,'97e22704f0','Yeah, I was actually driving a truck pulling a boat. not nearly as fun at driving boats. haha\r\n\r\nI just found some tire foams under my bed! haha\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(35124,'dcd87d63a6','No, I just haven\'t got around to fixin\' it yet... I switched ISPs and lost my other server space. Thanks, though.\r\n\r\nhue35'),(32528,'da28eb43ba','[quote:da28eb43ba]Greg Maffei \r\nGrey Matter \r\n431 NW Flanders, #203 \r\nPortland, Oregon 97209[/quote:da28eb43ba]\r\n\r\nJust sending a confirmation to make sure this is a valid addy for you.  Also I will be sending both yours and Hue\'s stuff in the same box as you asked earlier if that\'s still fine.'),(31678,'2b4ceb7181','[quote:2b4ceb7181=\"pimpsmurf\"]you want me to address it to stagg? lol\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:2b4ceb7181]\r\nehh Brian Stagg actually, lol.  Now you know were my names from. hah.'),(32575,'84b8ffe3c6','[quote:84b8ffe3c6=\"Finks\"]Yeah sorry, was a typo. \r\n\r\nAs far as what you are getting, honestly you got off very light w/ only the Black civic for the black minivan swap.  Hope it will be worth the wait.[/quote:84b8ffe3c6]\r\nCool  8-)'),(33002,'e3b0e5c1bf','ok man, well im going to give the shipping place hell and see what turns up,, if i cant find the bodies ill refund your cash,, Sorry about this, i dont know what the deal is\r\n\r\nThanks for waiting\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36775,'f2189b0912','[quote:f2189b0912=\"Sporttracguy\"]is the RS4 ready to go except electronics?  Or will i need the belts and what not?  Does it have a servo in it?\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:f2189b0912]\r\n\r\n\r\nYou\'ll need...\r\n\r\nBatteries\r\nServo\r\nRX\r\nTX\r\n\r\nI\'m including the stock motor, but it sucks.  So you could say you\'ll need a motor too.\r\n\r\n\r\nEverything else is there. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMike'),(33464,'4e830916d1','Hey, no problem.  I would like to see pics of the Mini but be warned, there would be another shipment of stuff to your house.  -Cameron'),(36795,'6e737cb822','[quote:6e737cb822=\"steelwoolghandi\"]Got your money out today also I added something to the letter so be carfull when you open it.\r\n\r\nthanks man!  :-)[/quote:6e737cb822]\r\n\r\n\r\nYour stuff hit the road today too. :-o \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMike'),(34358,'72354cc7bd','Try here http://www.sleepy-fish.com/Sagaris.htm\r\n\r\nand here\r\n\r\nhttp://www.racinggreentvr.com/models/sagaris.asp\r\n\r\nand here\r\n\r\nhttp://www.tvr-eng.co.uk/intro.html#tamext3\r\n\r\nGood luck :lol:'),(36807,'37c93a7c6b','[quote:37c93a7c6b=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:37c93a7c6b=\"ph2t\"]hey man, I know, slack late response.  You\'ve prolyl figured out the problem now.\r\n\r\nI take it was a DNS issue?  You running an exchange box in a BIND DNS environment?\r\n\r\nhttp://www.msexchange.org/ is an excellent site for all things exchange, just search the forums there, it may help.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:37c93a7c6b]\r\nThanks holmes. Nah, wasn\'t a DNS issue. I still have some residual issues left-over but the main part is working now. Our network is so convoluted it\'s not even funny.\r\nI\'ve been going through that site, found some helpful info, but most really didn\'t apply to my particular situation. Again, probably just because of how our network is setup.\r\nI like coding much better than network admin. lol[/quote:37c93a7c6b]\r\n\r\ncool, no worries.  I inhereited the worse fucken network known to man when I started here.  Now it\'s good.  Took me a year to get shit sorted....\r\n\r\nfucken dumbarse admins........');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29040,'64c28195f3','I\'m really sorry for that rude email, I didn\'t intend to be a jerk.(By the way that message in which you wrote that you were in the shops--&gt;I got that after I sent you My message)\r\nSo I\'m really sorry,and I hope ther\'s no anger among us.'),(29041,'ea2cc2fd46','Hey,man! :-) \r\nI just wanted to ask you if you have any doubts about the payment?\r\nA time ago I was trying to trade with someone else, but he refused it because I wanted to pay like this.\r\nP.S:I don\'t need your last name, I heard it would be necessary, but I looked for it on the net, and its not essential at all.\r\nHave a further nice day! :cool:'),(29042,'e76f56fb46','[quote:e76f56fb46=\"betula66\"]Hey,man! :-) \r\nI just wanted to ask you if you have any doubts about the payment?\r\nA time ago I was trying to trade with someone else, but he refused it because I wanted to pay like this.\r\nP.S:I don\'t need your last name, I heard it would be necessary, but I looked for it on the net, and its not essential at all.\r\nHave a further nice day! :cool:[/quote:e76f56fb46]\r\n\r\nNo doubts, I\'m cool. Like I said, I\'ll let you know final total cost, you wire me the money and I\'ll drop it in the mail. I\'ll try to let you know tomorrow.'),(29047,'612d4e5717','Yo\r\n\r\nThe guy to speak to is Michael, m.horenkamp@minispeeder.net.\r\n\r\nYou can telephone on 0049 5251-69976-13 if you want to.\r\n\r\nMention my name and company (Derek, Bonzer Gear).\r\n\r\nGood luck\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTB');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33529,'e64cf44c2f','Hey i had a couple questions for ya. I thought you might know the answers to. \r\n\r\n\r\nDo you know if its possible to wire up a hs-55 to a mr-02 board? And mount the hs-55 on to the pro-z?\r\n\r\nI think there is a way to use the front servo gearbox and a hs-55 together but the wiring is my only problem. \r\n\r\n\r\nIs there anyplace i can buy a mr-02 servo assembly seperatley that would be able to screw onto a pro-z chassis? \r\n\r\nAny help would be appreciated. \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt\r\n\r\n\r\nI am asking this because i am looking to upgrade the servo on my pr0-z to a higher grade and i do have a extra hs-55 laying around. And i know you have alot of experience.'),(32240,'d901f1e14e','burn one in a little bit?\r\n\r\nreply or give me a call....\r\n\r\n\r\nHow about those Epoch prices?  :lol:'),(32241,'c088a7a9bc','ok, so $12+2 s&amp;h.  Just want to confirm.\r\n\r\nAlso, I\'m new to zz, and was wondering if you knew anywhere on the web that sells older bodies (in particular the chevy chevelles ss)?\r\n\r\nThanks, let me know..'),(32246,'91e0c1c9b2','Hey, I got your car all ready to go. I went ahead and stacked the FETs, just cause that\'s what I\'m practicing this week. \r\n\r\nHate to bug you, but I could kinda use that cash, and I got some other cars I gotta get out. Don\'t want make multiple bus trips in this heat. So get me your address. I\'m heading to the PO on Thursday. \r\n\r\nBTW, You\'re normally one of the guys I wouldn\'t normally charge for a FET mod, but I was out of FETs at the time, and  was trying to avoid that $5 surcharge on my FET order, but I\'m all stocked up now, so if you just want to pay me for the Zip Zap+shipping, like $30, that\'s cool. Whatever\'s clever. My Paypal email, just so its handy ;), is davesmoejoe@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nthanks\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32244,'4d02b4eacf','lets just say $12 flat, $14 for some bodies seem high to me.  As far as places to get those older bodies i think your best two bets would be bitpimps in either the trade or the looking to score area,, im sure somone has something they would like to sell.  Another place is ebay,, greatest site for finding discontinued stuff although it may be pricy\r\n\r\nlet me know if that works\r\nSTG'),(36176,'5b51dcc454','Hey man, i saw that you got the FET &quot;How to&quot; up and running, looks great.  I dont know if you saw my buggy project im working on but its been taking up alot of my time and although i will try the FET mod one of these days i was wondering if i can contract one out to you for the time being?  I have a brand new SE sitting around that i need modified for the buggy but i just dont have the spair time to work on the pcb and the chassis.  Id be willing to pay of course.\r\n\r\nI need it to be able to handle 6 cells, 7.2 volts (3 zzse cells) (Let me know if that will work)  If it cant handle that then i can downsize a little...Sounds crazy i know  :? \r\n\r\nAnyways, let me know if you want the job.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG'),(32545,'2a127d3ecb','yep, same address.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\n\r\nrich');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29488,'7825368765','Ok got my head out of my ass and read the post (sorry was out most of the weekend so did not get my butt in gear. Money was just send via paypal to that Vary Strange email address??? sent a few dollars extra too!\r\nthanks so much for doing this have a great week buddy!! :-) \r\n\r\nAaron \r\nSteelwoolghandi\r\nAddress:\r\nAaron W. Olmsted\r\n1941 Sayers Road\r\nBastrop, Texas 78602'),(35188,'efd15eb7d0','Ok man not a problem, We have all the EVOs and some 1st gens. I will see what I can do for you tomorrow night.'),(29391,'ff22fcf810','Cool, here\'s my address...\r\n\r\nMat Mathey\r\n3104 SE 39th Avenue\r\nPortland, OR\r\n97202\r\n\r\nI\'ll get that Gloria in the mail tomorrow... thanks, dude!'),(29067,'a7e1920504','Heh, ya..i am a dumbass...sorry.\r\nSuggestion, why no put the dam sticky IN the section so its easyier to find or something..but ya..still my bad..'),(29068,'81037b01fd','[quote:81037b01fd=\"mod_o_matic\"]Heh, ya..i am a dumbass...sorry.\r\nSuggestion, why no put the dam sticky IN the section so its easyier to find or something..but ya..still my bad..[/quote:81037b01fd]\r\n\r\nThere\'s a whole section devoted to rules and faqs, why no READ the topics there and understand them before posting for your first time? :???:'),(29167,'662f23a3da','Hey man, i have a few so order as many as you want. Sorry i can\'t tell you where i get them, but i sell them for a good price and shipping for as many as you want would be a buck. \r\n\r\nBut i\'m only selling them to people who can charge them right, either with a peak charger or stand alone, if you don\'t know what a stand alone charger is, it\'s like what you use to charge dual cells.\r\n\r\nHere is my website. [url]http://www.freewebs.com/microupgrades/index.htm[/url]\r\ngo to the product page for batteries.  :cool:  :grin:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29074,'76b997e6c2','Hi :-) ,I just wanted to ask if you\'ve got the price....'),(36556,'4dccfb3ad6','Dave \r\n\r\nWhats up dude - just put a quick post in the Misc section about a new Wally World vehicle.  Thought you might be interested\r\n\r\nLater\r\n\r\nVik'),(36557,'60af59e655','Wow, in this post: http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7272 you say u used putty? Where?! its so neat, lol i cant notice.'),(30190,'b796059451','[quote:b796059451=\"crazydave\"]Nah, that\'s cool, I wanted you to have extra, i just threw that ptiorty mail thing in there last minute as an option.[/quote:b796059451]\r\nI figured, but I get used to dealing middle school kids, the only time they don\'t want every cent back is when they\'ve stolen it from someone elses paypal accounts :shock: \r\n\r\n[quote:b796059451]How feasible is that? [/quote:b796059451] \r\nMostly it just adds two more wires to the DC mod install, other than that its pretty much the same as far as installation goes.  Of course, its already a bit of a pain with 4 wires, going to six will make the install a bit hairy for most people.\r\n\r\nIts still really tempting to design an PCB from scratch using a 400Mhz RF chip for the TX and RX.  I could get rid of all the extra wires and stuff and just have a nice compact board that does what I want.  Unfortunately that would price it out of the market for most people.\r\n\r\nAh well, I\'ve got other projects to finish before I get started on something like that anyway.\r\n\r\nlemme know what you think of the board!\r\nDave'),(30191,'21c12b11dd','Not a prob man, I fixed it up for you. As soon as I recieve the money order I will ship out the board. It\'s all packaged up and ready as we speak. ttyl...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37229,'6565cab934','Damn it!'),(37230,'6e532cb87c','I cuaght the avatar change but missed the &quot;comback&quot; reply. Thanks to hatchi I got to read it though. :lol:'),(36552,'8990f3b06f','OK, I\'ll take the purple ones.  Thanx.  Do you still have all my info?\r\n\r\nHere it is again jsut in case;\r\n(This is my work address, pls send here)\r\n\r\nHM2 Wilson, Robert G.\r\n1550 Tomcat Blvd. Ste. 150\r\nVirginia Beach, VA\r\n23460\r\n\r\n\r\nThanx for all your help.  I\'ll get on your site and order the towers now.'),(36743,'96aa568a12','[quote:96aa568a12=\"steelwoolghandi\"]Hey man you probably know but just in case I could not send out the money today due to the Post Offices are closed for MLK day. I will send out the cash on Tuesday!\r\n\r\nthanks man!\r\n\r\nAaron[/quote:96aa568a12]\r\n\r\n\r\nI realized that the hard way, I wasted a perfectly good gallon of petrol.  DOH!!  Totally forgot about the holiday. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\nLater, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(32634,'b1c4cebeb0','dude, that is weak!!\r\n\r\nwhat commitment to still post at BP without a keyboard. :grin: \r\n\r\nI see your posts and it cracks me up, but I feel bad too.\r\nShit, I see keyboards all the time at the local second hand stores. Are you broke like me? :lol: \r\n\r\nI have some extra keyboards, too. Not sure what type of plug they have off the top of my head. \r\n\r\nDo you want me to send you one? Wait, here I am asking questions when you don\'t have a keyboard.\r\n\r\n1 or Y = YES\r\n\r\n2 or N = NO\r\n\r\n :lol: \r\n\r\nwait, what about that speak and read whatever program, where you say shit in the mic and it types it out, then copy and paste? Just a thought.\r\n\r\nMotorGong');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36703,'b317380b19','No problem, thanks... :-)'),(31043,'49c348d9c6','[quote:49c348d9c6=\"stampede_dude\"]i dont have a controller...(?) \r\n\r\ndo you have some sort of instant messaging service?if so, [size=18:49c348d9c6]lmk[/size:49c348d9c6].[/quote:49c348d9c6]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDude, I\'ve never been a part of an online forum in my life much less have a messinger service.  :grin: \r\nMy computer has been for video games up till 2 months ago. :smile: \r\nLike MSN Messenger?\r\n\r\nAnd what is lmk?'),(29078,'a9f785ddb3','[quote:a9f785ddb3=\"hue35\"] he\'d always yell at me for not having any confidence in myself, yet he couldn\'t see that he was the one who took it away in the first place... [/quote:a9f785ddb3]Yup, can definately relate to that.\r\n\r\n[quote:a9f785ddb3]He was a badass in his day... captain of the football team, eagle scout, chopped &amp; channeled a \'49 Merc when he was 14 without knowing anything about what the fuck he was doing and he was a fuckin\' wrecking machine... total fighter guy. My friends used to joke that he could crush a pool ball with his bare hands. I didn\'t like to fight, didn\'t want to play football, got kicked out of the boy scouts... I always felt he was basically ashamed of most of me... man, I could go on and on.[/quote:a9f785ddb3]Yep, same shit, my dad jammed with Bob Dylan, got in fist fights with local folk legend Bob Bethencourt, Played in Alice Cooper\'s band the Spyders for 2 weeks. He worked on cars until he lost his license. I think he felt he was living in his brother\'s shadow in that respect, as his brother had a couple cars apear in Hot Rod magazine. I could go on and on also, but the point is I always felt I could never be as cool as him. \r\n\r\nI\'m a little guy, and I\'d always get beat up. When I ran in crying, he\'d tell me get back out there and kick his ass. So I\'d go back out, \"My told me to kick your ass.\" To which I would recieve another pounding.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:a9f785ddb3]He was the most amazingly natural talent I\'ve ever seen... he could just fuckin\' [i:a9f785ddb3]do[/i:a9f785ddb3] shit. It didn\'t even matter what... if he could see the finish line, he\'d figure out how to get there right. I don\'t think he understood how rare and natural his abilities were, so he put that expectation on everyone, but especially me. So, he didn\'t even consider [i:a9f785ddb3]teaching[/i:a9f785ddb3] me anything, because nobody needed to teach him... he just did it, so why can\'t I... \"figure it out, idiot\" (nice way to build confidence in a 6 year old kid).[/quote:a9f785ddb3]That\'s almost exactly like my dad, except he like to explain stuff, and go way over a 6 yo\'s head, and be like, \"What? are you an idiot or something\"\r\n\r\n[quote:a9f785ddb3]Then there\'s the temper, his own insecurities (which he stuffed as deep inside himself as possible), and a whole other angle that\'s too complicated to get into here (an addiction of sorts)... he didn\'t have enough energy for a son, but there I was.[/quote:a9f785ddb3]That\'s me and my dad, and those are exactly the demons I have to fight every day when dealing with my kid.\r\n\r\nBy this point I\'m not sure why I\'m here, but I know for a fact it\'s to be a better father than mine was.\r\n\r\n[quote:a9f785ddb3]Anyway, a few days before he died, he and my mom and I went out to dinner. This was right after college... I had just settled into my first job and first apartment on my own. We went to my place after dinner (the first and only time he saw my place)... I didn\'t have any extra scratch in those days, so I had built a lot of my own furniture... I would bring wood, or whatever, over to his shop, make cuts and haul it back, but he had no idea why. So, when he got to my place, it hit him... he looked around and saw a shitload of his DIY problem solving skills all around him, except it all came from me... I could see it on his face, it was the first time he realized just how much alike we were. And, he was proud... it was an expression I\'d never seen before, and it made me feel great. I remember going to bed that night thinkin\', \"holy shit, we\'ve just arrived at a place I thought we\'d never reach... we\'re gonna be friends, starting right now.\" ... that was Friday night, and Monday morning I got the call.\r\n\r\nI\'m glad we got to get to the point of mutual respect... even if it was just for a second. The whole thing still fucks me up to this day, but I\'m always thankful for that last time I saw him.[/quote:a9f785ddb3]That\'s so funny, my dad saw where I was living for the first time just a week before he died. Me and my wife dig furniture out of the dumpster and refinish it. So it was a similar situation, even though we found mutual respect over a bong. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'ll tell you what. I got into RC when my dad was dying. I had mentioned my uncle was around alot too then, and he was playing super dad at the time, working 3 jobs just so his kids can get the best BMX bikes to race with, and still find time to take them to race. That made really jealous, and I got the Stampede, because that was something I had wished me and my dad did together. We had looked through the Tower Hobbies catalog together, and he helped me pick it out. (Even though I already knew what I was getting, he was on morphine by that point, I\'d humor him. :lol: ). I was really hoping I could get it before he died, and was alive when I got it, but I was about 2 hours into building when I got the call from my mom, and she called the second she found out. I just felt this overwhelming sense of presence like I never felt before, and I knew he was with me. And shit, I guess now that I think about it, he helped me build every bit I\'ve done.\r\n\r\nWell shit that\'s enough of that, I\'m thinking too much, it\'s starting to get to me. Makes my head hurt.\r\n\r\n[quote:a9f785ddb3]Man, sorry for the heavy stuff there, but it was your fault.  :lol: [/quote:a9f785ddb3]Yeah, I guess it was my fault, sorry. :lol: \r\n\r\nThat\'s cool though. It\'s great when you can post something like that, and instead of getting pity or some BS, someone can actually relate. It goo d feeling knowing someone else feels as bad as you do. :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:a9f785ddb3]If you don\'t mind me askin\', how old were you when you lost your dad? I was 23, by the way.[/quote:a9f785ddb3]I was 25 when he died. It was 9 years ago last week.\r\n\r\nSo thanks for the PM dude. I really appreciate you taking the time to relate.\r\n\r\nDave\r\n\r\nOh yeah, when my dad first went into the hospital for his liver poisoning, he was already out his mind from the toxins his liver was developing. It was at this point when my dad called my mom at 3 am, and delivered the classis line, I will never forget, and I will somehow imortalize, \"Bring me a screwdriver and a pack of Kools. Have a cab meet me at 3rd St. and Van Buren. I\'m busting out of this crazy town.\"'),(31761,'9ad377b592','Thanks alot.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32232,'ec0f552e42','Cool DT. It\'s all good.'),(31050,'71d81b0fbc','[quote:71d81b0fbc=\"blindrider3\"][quote:71d81b0fbc=\"MotorGong\"][quote:71d81b0fbc=\"blindrider3\"][quote:71d81b0fbc=\"MotorGong\"]dude, look at the picture that chaoscauser posted.\r\nthe one of his car. look at the quality of the photo, the style of\r\ncouch everything is on.....all looks like it is from the seventies.\r\nIt\'s before my time, too, but I\'ve seen old photos, seen the Seventies Show, etc.\r\n\r\nGet it?\r\n\r\n\r\n-Motor :)[/quote:71d81b0fbc]\r\n\r\nOhhhh I didn\'t even notice the homies lol[/quote:71d81b0fbc]\r\n\r\n\r\nYep hahaha\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nYes, the homies, but do you get the joke now? Did ya read the whole thread?[/quote:71d81b0fbc][/quote:71d81b0fbc]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDude, ya gotta write something when ya quote, unless I\'m missing something here..... :???:'),(30159,'6a7e1f847e','Ohh yeah, I can fit the trace for you if you like. Matter of fact I will do it right now before i package her up.'),(29743,'31294a1f21','Do you need a set of stock wheels to measure?  I can drop you a set/sample of them.  The regular stock and the wide rims for ZZ\'s.\r\n\r\nYou can get an exact measure ment that way.  In person.\r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36925,'0031a975ee','Thanks for the howdy...\r\n\r\n[quote:0031a975ee=\"crazydave\"]So that contest judging was a clisterfuck huh? I glad you spoke up. I wanted to say something in the last contest even, but before I was a mod I was one of the ones that threw a bitch, and questioned their judging in that middle of the road contest, so I just didn\'t want to be the bitch that always bitches. :lol: [/quote:0031a975ee]\r\nThanks for sayin\' that... I was starting to think I was a lone pimp with a lost cause. I got a little too worked up... OK, way too worked up, but still, I just get so fuckin\' tired of his control-freak bullshit and his selective participation on matters like that... and while he\'s ignoring some whole thing, he\'s controlling the group into moving away from it... like it\'s just gonna go away. :? \r\n\r\n[quote:0031a975ee=\"crazydave\"]And how about DT with that Big Kahuna is back shit?  :lol: \r\nApparently he\'s still trying to comprehend what you meant about passive aggressive BS. Dense ass mofo. :roll:[/quote:0031a975ee]\r\nYeah, where the hell did that even come from? It was just all of a sudden DT is in full-tilt action... everytime I read that muthafucka\'s writing, I hear it as 50% Foghorn Leghorn + 50% Mr. T... [b:0031a975ee]&quot;I say.. I say... HERE\'S HOW IT\'S GONNA BE, PIMP!!!&quot;[/b:0031a975ee] Jesus Christ already.\r\n\r\n[quote:0031a975ee=\"crazydave\"]Been digging my Xmod H2. Now that I think about it, I haven\'t charged anything else since I got it.  [/quote:0031a975ee]\r\nYeah man, I\'ve been diggin\' the looks of those... yours in particular. The silver H1 SSMT chop is badass. I\'ll have to check one out at the shack. I\'m just reluctant to open the door to a new platform. How much do you have into yours?\r\n\r\n[quote:0031a975ee=\"crazydave\"]Been bored with music. Been mostly just listening to the Reverend Horton Heat lately, because it reminds of the old school rods. Man, you gotta check out that Car Kulture Deluxe mag if you come across it. The whole mag just has that really retro, but at the same time kinda punk attitude. I\'ve been getting it at Wakmartm its bi-monthly. I always wanted to build a rat rod, and looking through this mag really makes me wish I had a place to work on a project. I want an old Model A to sand rust off of on the weekends. :-([/quote:0031a975ee] \r\nI have checked out the mag, but haven\'t bought any issues yet. There was a great episode of &quot;Rides&quot; a few weeks back that was basically a top-notch documentary on the Rat Rod scene... it\'s almost too much of a scene for me. Like, those folks just [i:0031a975ee]know[/i:0031a975ee] they\'re the coolest motherfuckers on the planet... and they are, but they don\'t have to [i:0031a975ee]know[/i:0031a975ee] it.  :lol:\r\n\r\nI\'ve been all over the map with my tunes, as usual. I\'ve been rockin\' pretty hard these days... Atomic Bitchwax, Alabama Thunderpussy, Black Label Society, Motörhead... but also goin\' back to some of the stuff that\'s just attached to my soul, like Stevie Wonder, Captain Beefheart, Zappa (I know, I know :lol: ), Miles Davis, John Coltrane, John Zorn... Stones. All over the map.\r\n\r\nWork has been about to fucking kill me dead.... the pressure is just too much. I\'m working on this brochure that was WAY the fuck over-estimated by our account execs, but the client bit. Now the pressure is on me to make this 8-page POS look like it\'s worth the 90k it\'s gonna cost, and that doesn\'t even include printing... it\'s about 3x more expensive than it should be. The folks around here who sold this nightmare don\'t really understand the problem, but they sense my stress level... they\'re scared as shit, which is where half of my stress comes from in the first place. \r\n\r\nAnd, on top of that, we got a new designer dude, and he\'s just not showin\' me the respect... not even an ounce. Day one, he\'s all bitchin\' about how this and that isn\'t how he woulda done it, telling me my ideas aren\'t gonna work out, and just general complaining... the bitch. I just put up a fuckin\' wall of fuckin\' doom around myself... blastin\' Sabbath all day out of my office, no lights on, window wide open, so it\'s about 55 degrees in here... just flat out un-fuckin-comfortable to approach me. Fuck him... I\'m the onliest mutha fucka here to help him out, and he pissed on my shoes from the git. Then, he has the fuckin\' nerve to start calling me &quot;dudems&quot;, whatever the fuck that is... I just don\'t even acknowledge that I heard it or read it in an email, but, if it happens one more time, I\'m going to come unglued. I will offer him 2 choices in how to address me... &quot;Sir&quot; or &quot;Mr. Sir&quot;... God damn, I hate newbies.  :lol:  I\'ve been telling Greg (SF) that I\'m just gonna have to go all &quot;hue35&quot; on his ass... it\'s funny \'cuz I\'m such a non-confrontational person in my day-to-day life. I only lash out at strangers who do stupid shit in public (like road rage type shit, or like the dude I threatened to beat the piss out of if he didn\'t get out of the nice old lady\'s face), or as my &quot;hue35&quot; alter-ego in the little car world. :lol:\r\n\r\nShit, I gotta git... thanks again for the PM, I\'ll talk to ya later.\r\n\r\nMat'),(30288,'803fe69d80','[quote:803fe69d80=\"clemo\"]Thanks, i have brought my trueno kit at yahoo singapore, where i live. I have saw a similar NIB at a rc forum around a month ago. But I have tried to contact the person but there was no reply. Ended up buying on yahoo. Good kit with really nice body shells.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you are interested and i shall contact me again. He is looking at SGD 50.00 (USD 30.00) \r\n\r\ncheck this site \r\nhttp://www.daddyhobby.com/forum/showthread.php?t=5044[/quote:803fe69d80]\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp!  I just got an Initial D set in the mail today!!!!\r\nAfter getting outbidded on every single one on eBay, I finally got one\r\nfrom an outside source  :D');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32195,'a4a680390f','Thanks P, it\'s great to know you\'ve got our backs! :)  Working on getting more alloys in, plus working on some custom stuff; lmk when you\'re ready and I\'ll hook you up! :)'),(31490,'16149b80a9','i saw your work on lowering and i must say AMAZING Many propz to you! But i cant figure out how to lower my Bit imj a newb to Bodywork and was woundering if you could help me by writing a tut or something..\r\n\r\ncan you lower without a dremel?'),(37843,'e74350e129','[quote:e74350e129=\"HirotoR34\"]definitely, I was thinking deans would do charging duties...I\'ll do you up a custom shell. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to add a bit o green :-o[/quote:e74350e129]\r\n\r\nWent out a few minutes ago.\r\n\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMike'),(36644,'71cf7f352a','Sorry man, as long as you like everything. That chassis was a shelf queen to me lol... \r\n\r\n\r\nMy stuff might be at the post office I have not checked the mail in a while.'),(37708,'a789801d02','no problems, glade you like it!!!!!!!!!!! :)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36646,'27bf4851ca','Dude you are awesome!! lol\r\n\r\nI noticed when i was writing out your adress at the post office, you don\'t have a typical American first and last name...\r\n\r\nWhat ethnic background are you from?'),(36647,'9a6e656184','You said you had a front steering problem, and I need a rear clip to fit a gen1 body on the evo chassis, and since you don\'t have any gen1 bodies and I have an extra evo chassis with the parts you would need, would you be willing to trade? I most likely have the part you need, just let me know, and if worst comes to worst We could work out a deal for the whole front end. Thanks!'),(37622,'9d29cea220','I\'ve got the Saleen on an Iwaver MM.  It fits perfectly.  The MM setup actually has a longer chassis.  The Saleen body is a long body compared to most other bodies.  It may be the longest body available for all I know, but the wheel wells are still in the same place as most other MM bodies.\r\n\r\nMy MR-02 has a RM setup with an NSX body and it\'s shorter.  This surprised me as I always thought the RM setup would be longer.  But, the MM setup needs more space in between the main chassis and the wheels to account for the motor to be positioned there.\r\n\r\nAs far as which ones better, not sure.  I guess it depends on how you\'re gonna race.  So far it doesn\'t seem to make much difference.  If you want the weight of the motor farther back then go with the RM.  You would think that with the weight farther back it would help with traction and also help wip the back around if you want to slide/turn or drift, but it\'s not like your massively changing the balance with this adjustment so the difference in performance is nominal.  Although, more distance between the front and rear wheels would help keep the car straight during acceleration and actually help some with consistancy in cornering, but again the difference is nominal.\r\n\r\nOne more issue; The motor position of the MM does keep more crap out of the motor.  I noticed that with a hot motor/better magnets more metal debri gets picked up.  The MM setup covers the motor a little better so the metal debri just gets stuck to the bottom of the car instead of directly to the motor.  Not a big deal if you\'re gonna be racing it on a track and not on a dirty concrete parking lot.\r\n\r\nBy the way, I gave the MR-02 and the Iwaver 02 a healthy comparison on a concrete parking lot yesturday.  They accelerate exactly the same and have exactly the same top speed.  I\'ll be giving them some more comparison evaluation today on a tile floor and focusing on handling/cornering.  I already know the MR-02 has cleaner steering, but how much is the question.'),(32607,'df391656cd','i am fine w/ $3.85');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37145,'61e4912f65','Just so ya know, Juzi\'s Cust[b:61e4912f65]u[/b:61e4912f65]mz (with the 3rd &quot;u&quot; and penismonster avatar) is me... I figured I could fuck with  that kid pretty good, but he may have already headed for the hills..  :lol: \r\n\r\nI couldn\'t tell if you were hip to it or not, so I thought I\'d make sure.  :-o'),(37146,'085865ed85','Oh, makes sense.  Sorry dude.  I thought somebody was just screwing with his avatar and name.  Makes sense.\r\n\r\nDamn, now I really want to see him come back.  \r\n\r\nAnd I also feel a little used. :-? \r\n\r\n :lol:'),(34380,'a3b652f4bf','I really am truly sorry I do not know enough about this site. I geuss I am a little over my head posting in that thread, without even checking the date, or I geuss without cheching his profile or knowing anything about him too.\r\n\r\nno jokes \r\n\r\nsorry at first I did not see your seniority to this site\r\n\r\ntrying to shape my appearence in a new way(p.s. I no I am still a clear noob to this site and i am one of your current enimies,not asking for anything speicle, but just not pure hate.)\r\n\r\npimptothemax'),(34381,'a3b652f4bf','I really am truly sorry I do not know enough about this site. I geuss I am a little over my head posting in that thread, without even checking the date, or I geuss without cheching his profile or knowing anything about him too.\r\n\r\nno jokes \r\n\r\nsorry at first I did not see your seniority to this site\r\n\r\ntrying to shape my appearence in a new way(p.s. I no I am still a clear noob to this site and i am one of your current enimies,not asking for anything speicle, but just not pure hate.)\r\n\r\npimptothemax');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34382,'7ee0a73ebc','[quote:7ee0a73ebc=\"pimptothemax\"]I really am truly sorry I do not know enough about this site. I geuss I am a little over my head posting in that thread, without even checking the date, or I geuss without cheching his profile or knowing anything about him too.\r\n\r\nno jokes \r\n\r\nsorry at first I did not see your seniority to this site\r\n\r\ntrying to shape my appearence in a new way(p.s. I no I am still a clear noob to this site and i am one of your current enimies,not asking for anything speicle, but just not pure hate.)\r\n\r\npimptothemax[/quote:7ee0a73ebc]\r\nLook, it isn\'t about enemies or hate... I wouldn\'t consider you an enemy, or someone I hate. just try not to be so eager to post... hold out until you actually have something to add. If it\'s just going to be a useless comment, then simply don\'t make the post. A lot of people, me included, just make 1 or 2 posts per day, on average... some people never post, they just read.\r\n\r\nAlso, you have to pay attention to the dates of the posts... unless you have something brilliant to add to something old, just leave it alone. There\'s a few years of posts here, so there\'s a lot for you to dig back into and learn from, just don\'t make us rehash old stuff by making a useless comment in an old post.\r\n\r\nI\'m thinkin\' the best way for you to redefine yourself here is to stay outta the way until you have something [u:7ee0a73ebc]useful[/u:7ee0a73ebc] to add. Also, if you\'re working on something, take some pictures and show us what\'s up.... BUT, hold off until it\'s really going somewhere... don\'t post up a picture of your new Bit or ZZ and tell us what you\'re going to do. Dig into the project and make it work and make it cool, then show us. Or, dig into the project, break something, search around a bit for some info, THEN make a post to ask some questions... BUT, make sure you have some photos (if applicable) so we can see what you\'re talking about, and, most importantly, let us know that you\'ve searched the forums for an answer... you can even say, \"I saw in this thread (and link to it) a similar problem, but mine is different because....\"   See what I mean?... a post like that, that proves that you worked on something, ran into a problem, searched the forum to try to find an answer, THEN made an informed post... that\'s what is gonna earn you some respect around here. BUT, it isn\'t going to happen over night... just be patient. You\'ll be happier in a few months if you take your time to ease into the community and find your place.\r\n\r\nNow, the big one... dude, you\'ve got some communication problems. You\'re never going to be accepted here if you can\'t improve on the quality of your posts, from a spelling/grammar standpoint. It desn\'t have to be perfect, but it just can\'t be a struggle to understand... the good news is, I think I can help... listen up. There are 3 things you need to do when you are putting a post together...\r\n\r\n1. Since there\'s no spell check here, write the actual post in an application that has a spell checker built in (like your email app, or MS Word)... that isn\'t gonna show you the difference between [i:7ee0a73ebc]there[/i:7ee0a73ebc], [i:7ee0a73ebc]their[/i:7ee0a73ebc] and [i:7ee0a73ebc]they\'re[/i:7ee0a73ebc], but it\'ll help a lot.\r\n\r\n2. Take your time... until you\'ve got your communication skills workin\' a little better, just slow down and think about what you\'re trying to say.\r\n\r\n3. Take more time... read the post over and make sure it reads clearly. Write some parts over, if you need to, so it reads clearly and concisely.\r\n\r\nJust take it slow &amp; steady... it\'s what pimps do.  :cool:'),(32125,'689f73daf9','[quote:689f73daf9=\"hue35\"]Hey man, if you\'ve got, or can take a higher-resolution, side-view shot of your car with something simple in the background, I could do a way better job (and would like to, I love that car!)... maybe even with you drivin\'.:???:  \r\n\r\nThe higher the resolution, the better... like, more than 1000 pixels wide. 2000 pixels wide would be great... saved as a high-quality jpeg.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35[/quote:689f73daf9]\r\n\r\n\r\nLol I cant drive it, to young, but I will try to get a better pic.  Thanks for doing it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30518,'c886ad194a','Holy fucknuts! :eek: \r\nHands down, all time best video between all the Micro RC sites - no shit.\r\n\r\nThat was fuckin awesome man.\r\nDid you do stop animation er somethin? How\'d you pull that shit off?\r\nIn-fucking-credible dude. I wouldn\'t change a thing personally.\r\nBut as far as \"CaboWabo\" and \"payaso\" texts, I could go either way.\r\nIt doesn\'t take away from the video, that\'s for sure.\r\n\r\nThat\'s so kick ass dude, I love this thing - can\'t wait until it\'s up so I can show it off to some others. Amazing job. Just think, if you had a coupl\'a monkeys like us helping you make clips, and you had the time to devote to this stuff - man the possibilities are mind boggling. Something to dream of at least.\r\n\r\nA+ shit dude.'),(29922,'65830264d0','Hey Miva,\r\n\r\nI am not sure you will get this, but I had to write to you anyway... I got to see Porcupine Tree last night, and it was an awesome show. I was thinking about you and wanted to say thanks for turning me on to that band... they\'re amazing. So, I hope all is well, and thanks again for introducing me to Porcupine Tree!\r\n\r\nhue35'),(29084,'c8356f70ba','minigiant - rarely\r\nminiquake - occasionally\r\nminizilla - occasionally\r\nrc18t - not done yet\r\nmini inferno - frequently\r\ntlt-1 - rarely \r\n\r\nHmm, would u like to sell the minizilla or quake? I have several things to trade.. Please message me back');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29086,'ba3780df48','sorry, but i\'ll probably hang on to them even if they go from the \'occasionally\' to the \'rarely\' category.  in addition to toying with these things, i tend to collect them as well.\r\n\r\nthanks for the offer though...'),(29088,'ba3780df48','sorry, but i\'ll probably hang on to them even if they go from the \'occasionally\' to the \'rarely\' category.  in addition to toying with these things, i tend to collect them as well.\r\n\r\nthanks for the offer though...'),(29089,'3d5c0b9227','k  8)'),(37820,'c3716dca47','[quote:c3716dca47=\"SuperFly\"]hey man-\r\n\r\nI\'ll take the IW04 parts. How about if you package that up and send it to me and let me know how much actual shipping was and I\'ll paypal ya $5 + shipping. Don\'t want you to use up all the loot just shipping it.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nsuperfly[/quote:c3716dca47]\r\n\r\nI\'ll have it packaged up to go out in the morning. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(37603,'a6d98ab839','[quote:a6d98ab839=\"PimpSmurf\"]Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative. [/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]No, you did not say that most Liberals.... [/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t say most liberals. I said most libertarians.\r\n\r\n[/quote=PimpSmurf]I don\'t agree with everything the libertarians (base = liberty, not liberal) believe, just 95% of it. They are pretty far right wing. Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative.[/quote]\r\n\r\nNow do you understand? Calm down and read it aloud.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"] :lol: You\'re a joke anymore to me dude.\r\nIf you can\'t even see the flaws in your posts, the contradictions, and just even general false statements you make - I can\'t help you.\r\nNobody can.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nThe only false statement was that I did not know that Bush decided to let the congress debate the issue futher. I correct myself. Other than that, you are dreaming man.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]I don\'t know what you\'re stuck on with the gay sex thing unless it\'s burned into your memory from you last gay experience or something.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nActually, I\'m talking about all the animated gifs with gay sex people were posting. Maybe you should read back and jog your marijuanna-riddled brain.  :-D \r\n\r\nJust kidding man, but looks back and see all the gay shit people posted.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]Anyways, I\'m not retreating. I own this place. You don\'t. If I don\'t want it to be a political forum, guess what? It won\'t be.\r\nI\'ve let you go on long enough spewing your bullshit. Now I\'m putting a stop to it.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nThat is fine man. At least this is a capitalist society where you actually have the right to own a forum. If the facists had control, none of us would control anything.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]If you can\'t go back to what this forum is about, I\'m affraid you\'ll just have to leave - and guess who else can make that happen? Yup, me!\r\n\r\nGo bite your pillow.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nWe went somehow from talking about conspiracy theory bullshit to a political discussion. Oh wait, I remember now!\r\n\r\n[/quote=CaboWabo]Off the topic of 9/11. I find it funny that this whole UAE buying ports thing was all approved, Bush backed it, then starts to backpeddle saying he knew nothing about the deal until it was over. And in the same breath says that &quot;we shouldn\'t worry about security&quot; even though that\'s his entire platform since we\'ve started this whole &quot;war on terrorism&quot; thing. \r\n\r\nTo me, that just shows that the government has finally gotten to the point where they can lie, directly in peoples faces, and it still floats. People still buy into it. The government knows that now and can be completely blatent about their actions. As long as they say 2 different things while doing 1 - they\'re asses are covered because there\'s enough ignorance that either story will be bought regardless. \r\n\r\nWhatever.\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nOh that\'s right. You\'re the one who opened the political discussion. Fuck, I forgot that shit. Seriously man, I had to look it up.\r\n\r\nBut more importantly, you should calm down man. This is why people aren\'t suppose to discuss religion and politics in polite company. In real life, we could probably have a decent conversation/debate. But in this medium, we both struggle to make our points but it is easy to get distracted and forgetfull. Everything is alright. hehe\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29711,'766e796d73','Hey DT, I got your package today. I have to say thanks for hook up man. I kind of feel bad I didn\'t have anything else to send with it. Let me know when your mustang makes it. Can\'t wait to see what kind of beast you make of it..'),(30106,'b935480eae','It works good, It has the traces cut for 10v or higher operation but you can solder them back if you plan on running it at lower then that. I also drilled out the holes for the power and motor wires to accept a bigger gauge wire. $20 shipped is cool. I can get you a pic of it if you want to see its condition.'),(36991,'8ba4a327a0','I HAVE A FEW SUPSENTION SPRINGS AND THE RED AWD ARMS, THOUSE GOOD, sorry bout caps, just relized and toooooo lazy to write over :)'),(36992,'40cf3be7c8','Sounds good to me...i want to make my own 4wd kit in the front without buying the radioshack ones, ttooo expensive here... I will ship the three bodies tomorrow night. \r\n\r\nAny susp or AWD stuff is perfect...hopefully you have the little pin for the axels, the one that connects the diff....let me know'),(36896,'e37a6e8a13','lol im pretty much out on XMODs stuff except i have a 350z body, white supra body, yellow skyline body, and a chassis. got anything in mind?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30162,'a0326eb3b1','Where did you pick up that truck??  I have looked every where for those things.. WalMart, Target, K Mart, etc...  Any help would be appreciated.\r\nTHANKS...........'),(32937,'8d0e0106d1','Unfortunately it\'s not here yet.  Is there anything you can do to see what happened?'),(32938,'4e685ec6fc','Yeah man, certainly,, ill check in tomorrow and see whats going on,, this is just rediculous,, Ill find out for sure and let you know.  I just moved into a new apartment and this is the second time ive had problems,, they will be fixed soon, i promise\r\n\r\nSporttracguy'),(32662,'66752f9d75','What is that? Australia? lol\r\n\r\nShipping that from the US is going to SUCK! Probably $15. Do you mind if I keep the AAA batteries? They will add a lot of weight.\r\n\r\nPaypal addy is joseph.yarbrough@gmail.com FYI.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36534,'68bc95de6c','It\'s headed your way man...\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36537,'3712b478d0','So what comes with the body? and how much would that be?\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37795,'217f298706','Not sure which one that is.  Either way, I\'ve got an IW02 for the comparison and I\'ve reached my hobby budget for a few months at least.  So, I gotta hold off on picking up any more cars for a while.  Sorry, otherwise I would love to pick one up from you.\r\n\r\nBy the way, the IW-02M has female ports coming out of the PCB cover like the Xmods have for plugging in lights and stuff.  That\'s the only real way to tell them from a regular IW-02.  If it is an IW-02M vs a regular IW-02, then advertise to the pimps.  Someone will grab it.  I think they\'ve worked on the electronics in the IW-02M to tweat the steering and get better reception, but I\'m really not sure of the specifics as it\'s all hear-say right now.  Not too many places to get them yet either.  Might be a hot item to sell if you get your hands on some.\r\n\r\nThanks for the offer though.  I\'ll keep in touch.'),(26789,'d07d0c2de5','oh thats not so good with iraq . i will try to write to cj .thanks for all the help . \r\n\r\ngoodluck  :)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22153,'fa20268eb0','http://www.homies.com - jeg mener at den bare hedder det. De kan desuden købes i mange amerikanske butikker. \r\n\r\nTomy har lavet deres egen monster-truck.\r\n\r\nTjek http://www.hlj.com for info og pris. - Ellers må du jo bare igang selv!'),(23780,'01ad2b45d4','lol my mom bought me one last week and i had to rob some shit but i got a bunch of extra crap. so what i gots is umm\r\n\r\na few extra stage 2 motors. two chassis two bodies(supra and skyline) extra body parts for the supra. two sets of electronics both fried inductors. ask cj what part# that is.  awd shit. and ill give ya a light kit.  most of the shit is booger rigged. you will need some knuckles. i suggest waiting for the gpm alloy ones to come out but you can sku them from the shaq. and some springs if i can find em. i feel bad man. im still jobless waiting for unemplyment to roll through in a few weeks. but at least in the meantime i can host some shit for ya. oh ya i got some extra wheels and shit to. and ill throw in a painted zz shell.'),(22155,'fa20268eb0','http://www.homies.com - jeg mener at den bare hedder det. De kan desuden købes i mange amerikanske butikker. \r\n\r\nTomy har lavet deres egen monster-truck.\r\n\r\nTjek http://www.hlj.com for info og pris. - Ellers må du jo bare igang selv!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26222,'49f989bdf9','[quote:49f989bdf9=\"hogjowlz\"]lol sorry dude actually i have a cuda body untouched you can have ill even throw in the challenger. i need your address again.[/quote:49f989bdf9]\r\n\r\nSend it to my work address.\r\n\r\nAttn: Bill J. Wilson\r\nMJI Photo\r\n1209 Walnut Street\r\nPhiladelphia, Pa 19107\r\n267-671-9250'),(22159,'6b0e309f6e','nej den hedder homie.tv men jeg mente om du vidste om de var i dk\r\nkan ikke lige finde den micro monster truck ,kennder du ikke nogen danske sider med det?\r\n\r\ndet der med at lave selv kender du nogen ud over den her inde'),(22160,'6b0e309f6e','nej den hedder homie.tv men jeg mente om du vidste om de var i dk\r\nkan ikke lige finde den micro monster truck ,kennder du ikke nogen danske sider med det?\r\n\r\ndet der med at lave selv kender du nogen ud over den her inde'),(22162,'fbf1916cb2','Har du ikke set min på rcinfo? \r\n\r\nNej, mener ikke de er i danmark. Kan da være du kan finde nogen i \"vending machines\"?'),(22164,'fbf1916cb2','Har du ikke set min på rcinfo? \r\n\r\nNej, mener ikke de er i danmark. Kan da være du kan finde nogen i \"vending machines\"?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22165,'b7162cdbbb','Nice, they have a red supra as well, but I doubt a black skyline.  do you only want the shells then?  No parts cars needed?  PM me fast and I\'ll find out right now the price.  Give me you wish list minus the black skyline and I will see what I can do.'),(22166,'80e1820090','jo har set din den er cool!! :cool:  .... men hvor kan jeg få en guid til at bygge en ud over her?....hvad er vending machins?'),(22168,'80e1820090','jo har set din den er cool!! :cool:  .... men hvor kan jeg få en guid til at bygge en ud over her?....hvad er vending machins?'),(23785,'1a54b62c02','ya electronics wise its good other than the range. the inductors are only 30cents a pop or so.'),(34200,'fa6a881455','I can bid on it for you..  I have no need for the parts since I been doing the 1/10 MT thing.\r\n\r\nThe thing is, my wife just went into labor, so I\'m not sure what the hell is gonna happen....lol..\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'m freakin out over here. It\'s our first kid, and all.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat\'d the other guy say?   It might be less hassle for you to go through somebody lees freaked out, but if you can\'t find anybody, Ican bid for you\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know.'),(33621,'f275519f6e','I\'ve never driven a nitro, I don\'t know if I wanto get into nitro. But here its 1:10 or nothing.\r\n\r\nIt\'s amazing what people are willing to spend money on, $350 for an RC is expensive for me but I just spent $550+ for my current mobile phone. People don\'t really compare things but I try to. So looking at my phone, $350 doesn\'t seem like much. I have NO money right now, I deal in cell phones and unlocking them from their networks. I am a full-time university student so I have no income. I just spent my last set of money investing in some equipment for the cell phones (motorola unlocker), so I can\'t buy anything. Maybe when the paper starts rolling in again from unlocking jobs at school  :-o (may even buy a new one)\r\n\r\nOn another note I was thinking about asking one of the pimps to be a \"bank\" for me. In barbados, we will never have Paypal. So I was thinking of getting a pimp to hold my money for me, not alot, so that I won\'t miss out on stuff being sold. Plus it would save me money in purchasing and posting moneyorders. I guess the banker can get like $1 for every transaction so that he gets something too. I would post it on the forum but I have no money right now to get started if someone volunteers  :-? so I\'ll wait till then to go public.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think, a Pimp City Bank  :lol: ?\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22180,'7cfb8a7bb9','Didja get the parts yet?'),(22183,'eb1c2b2c45','Arite, will find out tomorrow for ya.'),(35738,'041a443435','I have no clue as I\'ve not bought a bit shell in quite some time.. I was very sick with it, and the sight of the Lambo shell just got my whistle wet...lol\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat are they worth to you?   $15 shipped?   \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-S'),(33628,'d1001e109e','I hear ya,\r\n\r\nThat\'s why I am so skeptical/late to get into bigger RC\'s. Can you imagine working to buy a REVO for $1000+ . Yep, our wages are similar to yours but your currency is 2:1 with ours. So even the ZZMT is expensive compared to how easy yall get it. I really don\'t think I want to get another RC beside my MRS4 roller. But i\'d like one that I can just drive. I want to mod the MRS4 to race/drift. That\'s why the trucks are so appealing, but the price!!! :shock:  whoooooo. I can\'t afford to pour $2000+ in an RC but I\'d like one.\r\n\r\nHere we call it having:\r\n\"champagne mout\' and mauby pockets\"'),(36371,'0512a9694b','Hey, Just wonderin\' if you\'ve seen this body kit around Radioshack? If so, how much for 3 or under depending on what they have, shipped to Canada? This is in response to your &quot;Lookin\' to score&quot; Post. Thanks pimp!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35763,'529f34a4b2','I got about 4 hours before I gotta go to work...  Thinkin about firing up one of my nitro trucks.... :???: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-S'),(36281,'03db12b327','[quote:03db12b327=\"sessiz\"]Now that I\'m not all blurry eyed and on my way to work at 5:30 in the morning I just wanted to say thank you again. Not only did ya give me an idea on what to expect or look forward to (all I was looking for) but ya took it one step further and offered to go over what I will be presenting in my portfolio. This has earned my gratitude but good man and if I have the time to do it I will take you up on it. (hopefully any kind of interview is a month away yall know how I love to procrastinate :lol: )\r\nThen you got all gay ( :lol: ) on me and offered to print the stuff out and ship it to me. God damn it man, are you a fuckin saint or what?\r\nSeriously man I could keep on thanking ya but you hopefully get the jist of what I\'m goin on about. :-)[/quote:03db12b327]\r\n\r\nNo problem man, it\'s nice when I can do something for someone that\'s actually useful. And seriously, if you want me and hue (he does the same kind of stuff I do) to do a little pre-interview portfolio review or help putting it together, I\'d be happy to do it.\r\n\r\nOne other thing I thought about after you mentioned who the job was for and what you might be doing, is to show some kind of graphic system. Like if someone gave you (or you came up with) a picture, 3 colors, a typeface, a logo and a paragraph of copy, how would you apply it to say a 48&quot;x65&quot; window poster, an 8&quot;x10&quot; countertop display, a 8&quot;x6&quot; direct-mail postcard. Basically the idea of creating a family of designs in different formats. Keep me posted.'),(36283,'0ede2549f4','Ok, pmsl.. Btw, where do people get all those classic bodies? If they are for zipzaps or something then dont say search etc, because i want a few for my bit char-g. But where do you get \'em?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33632,'8fe46cbf84','I\'ve been trying hard to find a tutorial on how to make a brush guard and rails for the tricks but I have no luck, can you help me?'),(34746,'cde82c6d8d','[quote:cde82c6d8d=\"ph2t\"][quote:cde82c6d8d=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:cde82c6d8d=\"ph2t\"]lol, man, it\'s all good.  I know where you\'re comming from. I didn\'t mis-interpret, it\'s cool.  I know what you mean about the arguments n stuff, I tried to word my statements as carefully as I can, but sometimes it\'s like \"fuck it\", lol........[/quote:cde82c6d8d]\r\nUnderstood. Can we go smoke a bowl yet? lol[/quote:cde82c6d8d]\r\n\r\nlol, I say we meet up a hue\'s.....try out that new doohicky of his.........[/quote:cde82c6d8d]\r\nAight, I\'ll see you in like 36 years. :lol: \r\n(too bad you\'re halfway across the world)'),(34747,'b5dee89e1b','[quote:b5dee89e1b=\"CaboWabo\"]You should be all set to go.\r\nCreate an album/s and then start uploading whenever.\r\nLet me know if you have any problems.[/quote:b5dee89e1b]\r\n\r\nSweetness.'),(35753,'48b8f842f5','We\'ll figure something out.  I\'ll have to put my thinkin cap on while I\'m at work.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-S');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36811,'b18f311959','Hey man-\r\n\r\nJust saying hi, haven\'t seen ya round as much as usual. Kids can do that to ya. How is your little one? My little guy is having his first birthday in 3 weeks, can\'t believe it\'s gone by so fast. Santa brought him his first Hot Wheels set for xmas, so he\'s got the bug now. \r\n:-D \r\n\r\nBTW, I successfully modded my Nelly the other night. I was scared shitless I was going to fuck it up, but all went well. All I needed to do was change the direction the power wires entered the Nelly from the battery terminals. I\'m running a McLaren body on the Nelly chassis, and there\'s not a lot of room under there and it felt like I was going to bust out the windshield every time I mounted the body. I was having some binding issues that were affecting the rear suspension, so I made the wires come out the other side. Now I have about a nice short 4cm length leading to the Nelly instead of the full length as supplied being doubled over and wadded into the shell. Is there any danger in just wrapping a little electrical tape around the nelly vs. the shrink-tubing? I just wanted to protect the Nelly pcb and don\'t have a heat gun.\r\n\r\nBeen in full MR02 mode lately, almost more obsessively than I ever was with bits.'),(31329,'62152f90e5','ok , ill go in chat now :)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34462,'0dce18e724','You will be happy to know that your stuff is en route!  :-D \r\n\r\nI\'d say 5-7 days :-o , but possibly as long as 14-21.  :o \r\n\r\n-JNY'),(34761,'f9dbc51c62','[quote:f9dbc51c62=\"ph2t\"]finally got that photo, sorry for being such a slack cunt.   gotta email addy for me to send it to?&gt;\r\n\r\nta,\r\n\r\nMAtt.[/quote:f9dbc51c62]\r\n\r\nshoot it to greg@grymttr.com\r\n\r\nthanks!'),(28616,'71178db24a','Sure, just drop me the link so I can read along.  Is that cool with you?\r\n\r\nThanks for asking........ :-) \r\n\r\nLater.............'),(28619,'f8c4be9f87','You guys running a contest?  Last time I tried to cruise thru there it wouldn\'t let me.  I\'ll give it another try and let you know!'),(36610,'e647b2fa05','Thanks alot man, I sent you 2 bucks.'),(28622,'bb5d3767e2','Actually morfars.dk (the guys running RCinfo - the place i moderate) is talking about a future contest. \r\n\r\nDon\'t think you can enter though - he will most likely limit it to active users on the forum. However you are more than welcome to judge a contest. \r\n\r\nHehe, and IF you really want the SL/CLK/Whatever MB it is, then i\'m pretty sure you can get it at RCmart - and for a MUCH cheaper price than at Morfars(it means grandpa btw).\r\n\r\nSuperfly and Hue35 once posted some of their cars in the garage at the forum - with great succes, alot of the members got interested in 1:64 suddenly. Just tell me where you are lost and i will help you :)\r\n\r\nCheers'),(22213,'86f6e75fc9','Hey man you still around?\r\n\r\n\r\n  I was gone for a few months but still here :)\r\n\r\n  Just wondering what you been upto.\r\n\r\nL8r bro');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22214,'c381f598f4','I\'m still around ...I read up on the latest, but am workin 2 jobs for awhile, so I haven\'t been real active here.....I will be soon...I\'m moving next week and will be able to start back up with my 2nd favorite hobby soon  8-) ....holla....'),(22215,'7d4e41e103','[quote:7d4e41e103=\"kvik369\"]that\'ll work - you can keep the zip board if you want\r\nSo i\'ll paypal you $45.00(5 bucks to cover shipping) - is that right[/quote:7d4e41e103]Sounds right to me. So I guess it looks like we\'re set to go. 8-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(22217,'2f28b2bead','Hey, I figure you got your cars by now. Haven\'t heard from you. Was everything cool?\r\n\r\ndave'),(30181,'f93173326f','[quote:f93173326f=\"crazydave\"]Hey, just sent you money. I\'m just getting one for now, but I\'m sure I\'m gonna need more. You didn\'t mention shipping, but I went ahead and sent you $15. You can ship it Priorty Mail if you\'d like.\r\n[/quote:f93173326f]\r\nIt shipped this morning, but I had my wife drop it off at the post office and I forgot to mention shipping options, so she sent it regular 1st class.  Should be there Wednesday.  Shipping costs me about a buck-fiddy, so there\'s a bit left over.  I can paypal it back if you don\'t mind having them skim some fees off it, or if you\'re planning on buying another at some point I can just hang on to it and you can send the difference next time.\r\n\r\n[quote:f93173326f]\r\nThat would be great if you posted the review on your site. :-o \r\n[/quote:f93173326f]\r\nLookin\' forward to it, my site needs more content anyway.  If I weren\'t so GD lazy/busy I\'d write up some of my other stuff and get it up there.\r\n\r\n[quote:f93173326f]\r\nI just read your articles. Honestly dude, you\'re just so full of information I think you confuse a lot of people, but I always learn a lot from you and appreciate that there\'s someoene out there that explains this stuff to me.[/quote:f93173326f]\r\nI try to present as much info as I can without making it too technical.  I should probably provide some more links out to descriptions of basic stuff.  I kinda tend to forget that most people wouldn\'t know the difference between an BJT and a MOSFET if it bit \'em on the butt.  I still have to explain to people that the DC mod isn\'t a MOSFET, and they can\'t just buy one from Digikey and hook it up without programming it first.\r\n\r\nOf course, I end up writing most of that stuff at 3AM, then not proof reading when I\'m actually awake, and it comes out looking like an ADHD ferret on crack edited it.\r\n\r\n[quote:f93173326f]\r\nSo if I\'m understanding this correctly, it should perform like a dual cell car. If that is the case, I may be way overshooting my goals, but that\'s gonna be super cool. I\'m getting excited now. :-D \r\n[/quote:f93173326f]\r\nYep, its basicly a dual cell without the extra weight and space, but with some expanded control as well.  The SE had basicly 5 speeds, call \'em 18, 26, 34, 42 and 50.  if you dual cell it, you get 36, 52, 68,84  and 100.  So you basicly loose all your low-speed control.  With the DC mod you end up with something more like 15, 30, 55, 75, 100.  You get to keep the low end control, but you have access to the high end as well.\r\n\r\nSince there are only 5 forward steps it takes a pretty fine touch to really use it well though.  For the next version of the DC mod I\'d like to take the 4 or 5 reverse speeds and remap them to forward speeds.  So you\'d get one reverse gear (not often you need more than that anyway) and then 8 or 9 forward speeds, so you\'d have much better control.  You just have to adjust the throttle trim on the controller so its almost all the way back.\r\n\r\nThe other plan is to increase the PWM frequency up from 100hz to about 30,000hz or so, so you can\'t hear it buzz.  Should provide much smoother torque, which could improve handling in corners.  Without the heavy throttle pulsing it should stick to the road a little better, and it will sound much better.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I\'m babbling again, so later,\r\nDave K aka CodeSuidae'),(37613,'fac11c932e','I told you what state and county I\'m in because you asked--you can\'t do the same?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37614,'82cc0718b6','Hey man, I just received the body today.  Thanks a bunch.  I can\'t wait to see what you do with the Jeep.  I\'m a big fan of your work.'),(37615,'fac11c932e','I told you what state and county I\'m in because you asked--you can\'t do the same?'),(36231,'84cc5d9927','[quote:84cc5d9927=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:84cc5d9927=\"sg219\"][quote:84cc5d9927=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:84cc5d9927=\"sg219\"]Hiroto... :-o  :-o[/quote:84cc5d9927]\r\nCool, go edit that post. You\'re only a few minutes behind Chedder.\r\n\r\nMake sure you change &quot;Myster Winner&quot; in both spots and add the image of the car that made him win.[/quote:84cc5d9927]\r\n\r\nI can\'t edit there. :( \r\n\r\nI posted it next.\r\n\r\nYou can change it. :-o[/quote:84cc5d9927]\r\n :???: Whoops, maybe I\'ve got that fucked up.\r\nAt any rate, I\'ve edited Chedders post to include your decision.\r\nDo you mind if I delete your post after Chedders?[/quote:84cc5d9927]\r\n\r\n\r\nNope go for it.  clean it up.\r\n\r\nThanks'),(32101,'872f814a67','[quote:872f814a67=\"Finks\"]This is what I want to fit\r\n[url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/index.php?cat=10009]Suck My Bits[/url]\r\n[img:872f814a67]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10009/FinksZ.jpg[/img:872f814a67]\r\n:twisted:[size=7:872f814a67]©2005 Finks fucked your girlfriend in highschool inc[/size:872f814a67]\r\n\r\ni.e. this\r\n[url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/index.php?cat=10009 ]Suck My Bits[ /url]\r\n[img ]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10009/FinksZ.jpg[/img]\r\n:twisted:[size=7 ]©2005 Finks fucked your girlfriend in highschool inc[/size]\r\n\r\nMinus a couple of spaces I added so you could see.  Is there anything I could do, as it stands right now I can do it, just w/ out the tiny type because that uses 15 characters.[/quote:872f814a67]\r\nCheck it, it fits at 252 characters.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32129,'6bd9bdbcfe','I\'d like to buy them if you still have them'),(32130,'fafe9a2d92','Yeah, i still have them, How much are you willing to put down for them?  Im always up for an interesting trade as well\r\n\r\nSTG\r\n\r\nPS,, sorry its taken me a while to reply, my internet has been out for a few weeks'),(36311,'2dea7f5f07','Sounds good,, Thanks man\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36317,'f3b7251b04','HEy, \r\n\r\nGuess who\'s back  :cool: . I have been working on a scale model of a remote control &quot;volvo ocean racer&quot; sailing boat. Stupid me because now I also missed the end of the year blow out, while having three entries lying around  :sad: . \r\nBut YEAH , I still want them  8-) .\r\nmy adress: \r\nJoris de Iongh\r\nCipreslaan 48\r\n3053nd\r\nRotterdam, the Netherlands\r\n\r\nJust shove them into an envolop between two cards if you are going to send the coils only. Unless you send me the chassis in total. \r\nYou\'ll figure something out. Bad luck with the car accident man!\r\n\r\nTnx in advance,\r\n\r\n :)'),(32132,'4522518770','[quote:4522518770=\"hue35\"][quote:4522518770=\"blindrider3\"][quote:4522518770=\"hue35\"]Hey man, if you\'ve got, or can take a higher-resolution, side-view shot of your car with something simple in the background, I could do a way better job (and would like to, I love that car!)... maybe even with you drivin\'.:???:  \r\n\r\nThe higher the resolution, the better... like, more than 1000 pixels wide. 2000 pixels wide would be great... saved as a high-quality jpeg.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35[/quote:4522518770]\r\n\r\n\r\nLol I cant drive it, to young, but I will try to get a better pic.  Thanks for doing it.[/quote:4522518770]\r\n\r\nHoly shit dude... that\'s your car and you\'re not even old enough to drive? Make damn sure you use that thing for what it\'s good at... attracting loose chicks, yo!!  :lol: \r\n\r\nSweet ride, dude... with the combination of that car and your avatar, I figured you must be about my age (I was born in \'69).\r\n\r\nAnyway, get a high-quality pic and I\'ll take some time to do it up right.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35[/quote:4522518770]\r\n\r\n\r\nLol.  Even though I\'m 13, I got some old school tastes lol.\r\n\r\nBut next time me and my dad pick the car up, I will get some good pics.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33419,'143471ec8c','Bro i hate the way they say \"Eh\", we say it like everyone else says it, if you know what i mean. Yeah the only thing i hate, is once someone starts shit, everyone tries to jump in and shit, makes them feel \"tuff\" i guess. Thats what pissed me off about skylinekid, but w/e stay, same shit happened to me in begginin but i got last word on it so it\'s all good.'),(28107,'770839872a','Yea man I found it on a  www.srh.com on their messageboard.I couldn\'t live without taking it for my avatar lol.'),(28108,'31d9d7dc1c','Whats up bitch? How is the Northwest these days?'),(28489,'3168eed309','Hey mang, got any suggestions as to why my trim steering will not work going one way but works going the other way?\r\n\r\nI just finished the AWD mod and its now doing that?'),(28119,'136a6f60d4','Another dawg....where you from?'),(28120,'b5b53ffa2e','Whay up bird???Yeahhhh!!!!'),(28130,'8f50b824a2','people call me the space cowboy....\r\nYeah....some call me the gangster of looo\'ooove. Some people call me Maurice.....'),(23993,'0fac762881','Got it today! I apreciate the fast shippin, and the nice packaging.  :-)  Im afraid I didnt have access to anything but a box and some paper as protection.\r\n\r\nThanks again, let me know when you get yours,\r\nKanye.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22262,'b7e431d019','[quote:b7e431d019=\"steelwoolghandi\"][quote:b7e431d019=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:b7e431d019=\"steelwoolghandi\"]Cabo I understand if you dont agree with me but I do take extreme offence when Jowlz edits my posts to say something I didnt say! This is extremely wrong and childish and this is a practice that should not be tolerated! I am not personally attacking you Cabo but you should exercise some more restraint when it comes to your moderators attacking and changing members posts to make themselves look better!\r\n\r\nSteelwoolghandi[/quote:b7e431d019]I have nothing against you either man.\r\nI\'ll take your comments into consideration.[/quote:b7e431d019]\r\n\r\nCool Cabo I am not looking to have some sort of War come out of this I was just protecting a friends rep like your mod Jowlz felt he was protecting his Boys. I would appreciate if Jowlz is going to edit my post that he not put things about me personally in there as that is supposed to be the reason he was editing them in the first place? I would politely ask you to go back into the thread and delete the Derogatory edit that was made by Jowlz in the post I would thing that would be the polite thing to do and I would appreciate it. I mean if you someone is going to disagree just disagree and debate but please its poor form to attack a member personally because you disagree with him!\r\n\r\nI will refrain from posting about this subject but would appreciate if you would delete Jowlz editing of my post! \r\nThanks so much for the reply and if I can be of any service over at WeGotU or R7R please let me know.\r\n\r\nsteelwoolghandi[/quote:b7e431d019]the problem is many times I don\'t get to see the original posts before they were edited.\r\nI\'m under the impression that hogjowlz edits in personal attacks when the original post had a personal attack itself.\r\nI\'ll ask him to be sure if this is the case.\r\n\r\nbecause I\'m a nice guy (we all are really), I will go in and edit the edits.\r\njust remember how completely stupid this whole thing got (not saying it was anyones fault, we all contributed to the stupidity).... I think you know where I\'m going with this so I\'ll leave it at that.\r\n\r\nI was actually glad to see both you and azimov come here, afterall I don\'t know either of you but know you both have been around awhile.\r\nit\'s a shame that 2 locked threads and 1 live one turned out to be a thorn in everyones sides.\r\nyou should know you both are still welcomed here.'),(22223,'7010a786aa','[quote:7010a786aa=\"kvik369\"]I just sent the money (Paypal) to the email you gave me (davesmojoe@yahoo.com), but paypal said you weren\'t registered and would send you an email.  The package should be in the mail sometime Friday.\r\nThanks\r\n\r\n   Vik[/quote:7010a786aa]Also, my wife just informed me that she made her email the primary, so that may also have something to do with it. Her\'s is strollerpusher@cox.net');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22224,'7010a786aa','[quote:7010a786aa=\"kvik369\"]I just sent the money (Paypal) to the email you gave me (davesmojoe@yahoo.com), but paypal said you weren\'t registered and would send you an email.  The package should be in the mail sometime Friday.\r\nThanks\r\n\r\n   Vik[/quote:7010a786aa]Also, my wife just informed me that she made her email the primary, so that may also have something to do with it. Her\'s is strollerpusher@cox.net'),(26216,'254df79948','no problem   -   tanx\r\n\r\nvik'),(26217,'46a715a5c5','Ok, SEs done, I\'ll be shipping today.\r\n\r\nIt\'s good thing I got the new SE, because the battery in the old one is dead. One of the side effects of a dead short, I was afraid of that.\r\n\r\nThe new SE has decent steering. It don\'t jitter, but it has a mild smooth vibration. Hardly noticable, and it may have been because I had the trim cranked all the way to one side on my transmitter. I with some adjustment to your radio, I believe it can be made jitter free.\r\n\r\nDave'),(22229,'0c119058bf','[quote:0c119058bf=\"kvik369\"]should I try and cancel the first one - I think you would have to open an account under that email[/quote:0c119058bf]Yeah, I would think so. I really don\'t know what that is about. My wife also used our paypal yesterday, so it is active.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22231,'ab920686df','[quote:ab920686df=\"kvik369\"]I just sent the money (Paypal) to the email you gave me (davesmojoe@yahoo.com), but paypal said you weren\'t registered and would send you an email.  The package should be in the mail sometime Friday.\r\nThanks\r\n\r\n   Vik[/quote:ab920686df]That odd, I just checked, and my account is all good, and I didn\'t get any email. Maybe it was a typo, let me give the email again in case. It\'s davesmoejoe@yahoo.com.\r\n\r\nDave'),(32332,'5a4cbed6e2','dave\r\n\r\nHaven\'t been online for awhile - the cannonball is a hummer.  They been out for a while.  I will leave it just like it is.  Stock they kinda suck but I figured with the fets it would be a decent car.  So with the duals also it should be great.  I know the steering sucks but that is gonna be an \"slight offroad\" car with some muscleworks nobby tires so it don\'t matter as much.  \r\n\r\nHope these weren\'t too much a pain in the butt.  I appreciate it.\r\nAnd I\'ll get them when I get them. No problem\r\n\r\nTanx - Vik\r\n\r\nHarold V. Irvin\r\nPO Box 429\r\nPocono Lake, Pa 18347'),(37933,'c83a1faf6d','Both torque and high speed set-ups.  I\'ll also take orders.  For example, how ever many turns you want or even certain parts and pieces.  That will be when I get more work done to get set up.  I need to do a bunch of research and testing to get ready.  I\'m starting with the spiral armeture because I\'ve never used one and I\'ve heard some interesting things about them.  The top speed in a spiral is generally higher, but I think the torque is lower and it pulls more current getting started whitch will blow fets and boards easily if I do the wrong setup.  Torque is very important of-course, possibly more important than top speed, but I\'d like to see what would happen if I took a spiral and set it up for torque.  It should make an all around sweet motor.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33624,'303e8ae85c','Would you mind shipping me those extra chassis that you made that werent up to par with you?\r\n\r\nI could pay for the chassis and shipping or whatever you want.\r\n\r\nThough it was worth a try since there sitting around.\r\n\r\nLet me know\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(22237,'d56f065068','[quote:d56f065068=\"kvik369\"]2nd one worked[/quote:d56f065068]Ok cool. (whew) I hate complications. :lol: \r\n\r\nIt did go through.\r\n\r\nAlrighty then, I\'ll be keeping an eye for your stuff. I\'ll let you know when I get it, and when I\'m done modding.\r\n\r\nDave'),(28628,'aca1ff6a82','http://www.rcinfo.dk/forum/index.php?\r\n\r\n\"Registrér\" = Register\r\n\"Brugernavn\" = Username\r\n\r\nI guess there\'s not much more to it. \r\n\r\nI dunno what\'s morfar is cooking on regarding the contest. It\'s gonna be HUGE though. I\'ll let you pimps know.'),(28436,'b5019e11ac','Hey Man, \r\nIs everything cool with You about this deal?\r\nJust get back to me and let me know what You want to do, You already got my info, so if this deal is alright with You just give me Your info so I know where to send the MT stuff etc.\r\nThanks\r\nJDM-R34'),(22241,'c123b7d18a','[quote:c123b7d18a=\"kvik369\"]trying to make me a little crazy are ya - well it wont work - I already am[/quote:c123b7d18a]Well I wasn\'t trying to, but I have been known to drive people crazy. My wife and mother in particular. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22243,'45b7794725','Crystal City.  :lol: \r\nSounds like some magical place from the wizard of oz, I\'m sure you\'ll be very happy there. :lol: \r\n\r\nOk cool, just wanted to make sure.\r\n\r\n\r\nDave'),(22245,'c381f598f4','I\'m still around ...I read up on the latest, but am workin 2 jobs for awhile, so I haven\'t been real active here.....I will be soon...I\'m moving next week and will be able to start back up with my 2nd favorite hobby soon  8-) ....holla....'),(35019,'43c7d70b2e','Any word, big bird? I haven\'t got a response from email.\r\n\r\nWhat\'s up?\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(25262,'523a787696','Voodoo, did you get the shiat yet?'),(32448,'7f67db211b','hi man, i got the goodies last week, just forgot to tell you! :-)  thanks heaps for the cups, you\'re a legend! :smile: \r\n\r\nthanks bruvva, trent.'),(36923,'2410247ffa','Thanks dude. I will play around with that gallery thing tonight. I know absolutly nothing about php so.... kinda screwed there. and as far as mysql forget it. I barly know html. ROFLMAO. \r\n\r\nI guess I;m glad I can build what I have thus far. Its been trying at times but it looks good for a starting out page.'),(22247,'65159957d2','http://www.wegotu.com/forums/view_topic.php?id=2031&amp;forum_id=2\r\n\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=19880\r\n\r\nOnly because you asked. Posting here is pointless when the mods ( actually ONE mod) edits your post , locks threads and falsely post using your screen name.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22248,'9924f36aa8','Man, you\'re a goooooood debater.... :eek:'),(22249,'9924f36aa8','Man, you\'re a goooooood debater.... :eek:'),(22263,'5002d4255b','I appreciate that Cabo and I do like it here I am not here much because of running wegotu and being and admin at R7R but I have felt welcome here! (Well except for the little incident) and I totally understand the problems with this type of thread I never plan for something like this to go bad as I know you dont but it happens especially when the subject gets personal. Thanks for your understanding (and for being a nice guy I never doubted that) and for editing the post that is appreciated!\r\n\r\nI also want to thank you for what you said about Azimov and I we can get carried away just like everyone else when they think one of their buds is being treated unfairly but like you said let it drop and it will all go away so I am ready to move on and dont hold any grudges! \r\n\r\nThanks again \r\n\r\n\r\nSteelwoolghandi'),(32659,'87de6de604','[quote:87de6de604=\"itzlinky\"]Just wondering how much would it be total including shipping to 39540?  Packing could be whatever\'s the most cheapest and efficient method using priority mail.[/quote:87de6de604]\r\n\r\n\r\nDude, I wish I didn\'t pass up your offer. I\'m not sure if this Red_Line guy/kid is going to come through. \r\n\r\nIf he doesn\'t, you can still have it if you want.\r\n\r\n\r\n--MotorGong');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22266,'2cc2407310','[quote:2cc2407310=\"steelwoolghandi\"]I appreciate that Cabo and I do like it here I am not here much because of running wegotu and being and admin at R7R but I have felt welcome here! (Well except for the little incident) and I totally understand the problems with this type of thread I never plan for something like this to go bad as I know you dont but it happens especially when the subject gets personal. Thanks for your understanding (and for being a nice guy I never doubted that) and for editing the post that is appreciated!\r\n\r\nI also want to thank you for what you said about Azimov and I we can get carried away just like everyone else when they think one of their buds is being treated unfairly but like you said let it drop and it will all go away so I am ready to move on and dont hold any grudges! \r\n\r\nThanks again \r\n\r\n\r\nSteelwoolghandi[/quote:2cc2407310]perfect, neither do we...\r\nwe appreciate good/understanding/contributing members - it doesn\'t go un-noticed.\r\n\r\nanyways.... blah blah blah and now back to having fun! lol'),(28613,'edc7ddde7e','David Knaack\r\n850 Amelia Ave\r\nElkhorn, NE 68022\r\nUnited States\r\n\r\nis where to ship the lipoly, and FET\'s x 12');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31480,'7b59a4770a','As far as i know , there wasnt a  removable deck  when i baught it new , im not 100% sure what you mean though.As for the frequency that doesnt matter . But yes i would definatly prefer one without arms if you cant find the hummer body. Those arms are U.G.L.Y. lol , \r\nmany thanks and il pack+post it tomorrow sometime. its 4.23pm here tuesday.So by tomorrow evening it will be on its way to you. :-o \r\n\r\nthanks , \r\nJO3\r\n\r\nP.S - i need your FULL adress eg. your state/city and country.\r\nthanks , \r\nJO3 ~!'),(31481,'b912c22061','Good deal on those bodies. I\'m going hunting right now to find one! :)\r\n\r\nThe arms are ugly as sin. lol\r\n\r\nMy address is:\r\nJoseph Nicholas Yarbrough\r\n2515 Graham Rd.\r\nConway, SC 29526\r\nUSA\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n-JNY'),(22269,'61902ee76d','I don\'t think anyone has contacted you yet, sorry about that.\r\nand if they have, please let me know.\r\n\r\nanyways, congratulations on your winning bid.\r\nyou have a few payment options, you\'re choice.\r\nyou can either send cash or money order (US funds only)\r\nor\r\nyou can pay via paypal.\r\n\r\nlet me know which you prefer to do.\r\nonce payment is received, your car will be shipped.\r\n\r\nthanks for helping support bitPimps!'),(22270,'f24da81fd3','yeah i tried to contact big kahahouna but he did not reply.\r\n\r\ni got paypal\r\n\r\ncan u tell us the paypal email thing and how much it will cost?\r\n\r\ncheers man');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34156,'be4034e5b7','[quote:be4034e5b7=\"SuperFly\"]Hey man-\r\n\r\nYou mentioned an image showing alternative contact points for Nelly wires...\r\n\r\nThanks![/quote:be4034e5b7]\r\n\r\nYea, I got it somewhere.  Takes a while ot sort through all me old pics, god knows I\'ve got enough of the bloody things..... I\'ll shoot it to you asap.\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nmatt.'),(32126,'762f6c4d61','[quote:762f6c4d61=\"blindrider3\"][quote:762f6c4d61=\"hue35\"]Hey man, if you\'ve got, or can take a higher-resolution, side-view shot of your car with something simple in the background, I could do a way better job (and would like to, I love that car!)... maybe even with you drivin\'.:???:  \r\n\r\nThe higher the resolution, the better... like, more than 1000 pixels wide. 2000 pixels wide would be great... saved as a high-quality jpeg.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35[/quote:762f6c4d61]\r\n\r\n\r\nLol I cant drive it, to young, but I will try to get a better pic.  Thanks for doing it.[/quote:762f6c4d61]\r\n\r\nHoly shit dude... that\'s your car and you\'re not even old enough to drive? Make damn sure you use that thing for what it\'s good at... attracting loose chicks, yo!!  :lol: \r\n\r\nSweet ride, dude... with the combination of that car and your avatar, I figured you must be about my age (I was born in \'69).\r\n\r\nAnyway, get a high-quality pic and I\'ll take some time to do it up right.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(26446,'093158e110','[quote:093158e110=\"Sdog\"]If you are absolutely sure you want it, I will hold it for you. I know you are good for it. I don\'t need the cash right way, I just need to clear some space for some new stuff I received for Christmas. So, If you really want it, I\'ll just move it off the shelf, package it and hold it for you until the 14th.\r\n\r\nLater pimp.[/quote:093158e110]\r\n\r\n\r\nSounds like a deal then.\r\n\r\n$80 on the 14th.\r\n\r\nThanks, \r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37136,'0be367eaf2','excellent.\r\nI\'ll paypal you the total of $37.11 today or tomorrorw.\r\nclintoteri@yahoo.com\r\n\r\n[quote:0be367eaf2=\"cj\"]Hello Clint\r\n\r\nHere is what I got you down for:\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver \r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET	$7.74	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET	$0.00	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET 	$15.54	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET 	$7.74	1\r\n\r\nSub	$34.11	\r\nS&amp;H 	$3.00	\r\nTotal	$37.11	\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.59 off of GPM\'s regular\r\nprice.\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me now as\r\nsoon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com. \r\nPlease include your user name in the notes on PayPal.	\r\n\r\n\r\nThank You\r\nCJ\r\n\r\nBTW your email address on here didn\'t work.[/quote:0be367eaf2]'),(37137,'','whats up me and my friends have bought zip zaps mt and we found the supension artical and was wondering two things. One is where did u get the jeep body and have u herd about xmod. This my first time login on to the bitpimps web page so im not sure on how im gonna get this message.\r\nThanks \r\n\r\nSpanky :grin:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22272,'f24da81fd3','yeah i tried to contact big kahahouna but he did not reply.\r\n\r\ni got paypal\r\n\r\ncan u tell us the paypal email thing and how much it will cost?\r\n\r\ncheers man'),(22273,'3ab5ff7e1f','[quote:3ab5ff7e1f=\"TallduDe\"]yeah i tried to contact big kahahouna but he did not reply.\r\n\r\ni got paypal\r\n\r\ncan u tell us the paypal email thing and how much it will cost?\r\n\r\ncheers man[/quote:3ab5ff7e1f]crazydave actually handles the paypal payments so I\'m going to refer this question to him.\r\nHe\'ll contact you with information.\r\n\r\n~ CaboWabo'),(28331,'8c1017be5d','Not really sure what type of bit rims are my favorite that you may be able to do, but if You have ever seen these rims called M parallels or Contours off BMW M3\'s those 2 types of rims are pretty hot, I think that would look cool on a bit, but idk if You\'d be able to make something like that, since You don\'t have any to copy...idk\r\njust a thought\r\nThanks :cool:'),(22276,'e4022e07fc','What about Pomme and Sg...\r\n\r\nI dont even see a recent warn on Sg. He didnt do anything wrong.  \r\n\r\n__________________________\r\n\r\npomme ran out of warnings and I have my reasons for turning off sg account.\r\n\r\nCatch ya later, MysticKnight  \r\n___________________________\r\n\r\nMK- I dont mean to be rude, but Sg has no idea why he was banned. He doesnt know, and no one else but you knows.\r\n\r\nYou should atleast e-mail him or talk to him on AIM. He only had 20% warn, and that was because of a link in his sig.\r\n\r\n___________________________________________\r\n\r\nIn some cases, I don\'t want to spend the time on explaining things. This is one of those cases. Rest assured, I do have my reasons.\r\n\r\nCatch ya later, MysticKnight  \r\n\r\n____________________________\r\n\r\nThats it, I have no idea why, consider all the time he spent saying he didnt want to talk about it, and spend the time. I belive he could of just told us.\r\n\r\nTorque');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28008,'35a2ebdb48','Nope. nothing yet.'),(33114,'2437d5cc3c','[quote:2437d5cc3c=\"45tr0\"]thanks again for the heads-up dude, i just got the stuffs today! You definitely got me the jump on somma these guys.\r\n\r\nNow i gotta get a lipo charger (them things is scary! pray i don\'t blow myself up!)\r\n :shock:[/quote:2437d5cc3c]\r\n\r\n\r\n :lol:  :lol: \r\n\r\nRight On!!! Good to hear it!\r\n\r\nI\'m glad it was a sweet deal for ya. :-o'),(26210,'c724eaf736','Hey man,\r\nI wanted to ask you if I could duplicate your ZZSE Duty Cycle Mod:\r\nhttp://members.cox.net/codesuidae/DCMod.html\r\n\r\nin our Articles section:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/index.php\r\n\r\nwith all credits to you of course.\r\n\r\nspecifically, I\'d probably post it under the \"Performance Mods\" section, found here: (unless you have a better idea)\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/index.php?catId=7\r\n\r\nI\'d host the images and content, that way if your site disappears for whatever reason - we still have a copy to share with everyone.\r\n\r\nI\'ll understand completely if you\'re not interested so if that\'s your choice, no hard feelings there man.\r\n\r\nAnyways, let me know. I\'d like to be able to help share your knowledge with everyone else.\r\n\r\n- CaboWabo'),(29974,'8804ca2bea','Sorry I couldn\'t get back sooner.  I\'ve been busy with concerts and work.  Just went to 2 DMB shows!!!\r\n\r\nAnyway, I only have one of each right now, but if I come across any, I\'ll let you know.  The RS\'s just aren\'t getting many returns right now.  \r\n\r\nLater, \r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30049,'76e68f91c2','[quote:76e68f91c2=\"codesuidae\"]DC mod boards are $10 if you install \'em yourself.\r\n\r\nIt should take care of any hesitation on the start, and you may even want to switch to a slower motor or gears.  I find that a fast motor makes it pretty undrivable, just too fast, constantly rolls on corners, and does donuts when you try to accelerate.[/quote:76e68f91c2]Yeehaw! That\'s what I want to hear. :-D \r\n\r\n[quote:76e68f91c2]If you want to order one just paypal me the $10 and your address and I\'ll get one sent off.[/quote:76e68f91c2]What\'s your paypal email? I\'ll try to get that to you by monday.\r\n\r\nBTW, $10 shipped is very reasonable, if it works as good as you say, then everyone should have one. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nDave'),(22280,'8191cf9a2b','hey dave,\r\ncan you take care of this?\r\nI guess he wants to use paypal and I don\'t know all the in\'s and out\'s.\r\nI told him you actually handle the paypal stuff and that you would reply back to him.\r\ncool?\r\n[quote:8191cf9a2b=\"TallduDe\"]yeah i tried to contact big kahahouna but he did not reply.\r\n\r\ni got paypal\r\n\r\ncan u tell us the paypal email thing and how much it will cost?\r\n\r\ncheers man[/quote:8191cf9a2b]'),(22281,'49408f20c0','[quote:49408f20c0=\"CaboWabo\"]hey dave,\r\ncan you take care of this?\r\nI guess he wants to use paypal and I don\'t know all the in\'s and out\'s.\r\nI told him you actually handle the paypal stuff and that you would reply back to him.\r\ncool? [/quote:49408f20c0]No prob, but to save time in the future, they just need my email, davesmoejoe@yahoo.com \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22285,'27032dba34','I was hesitant to borrow from the bPs funds to get more FETs, even though I had cleared it through you, but it\'s a good thing I put it off. I got a guy that payed me for 4 mods today, so now I don\'t have to worry about that.  :grin: \r\n\r\nSo now I\'m all set to get back modding next week. 8-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(22289,'e0e937d8ae','[quote:e0e937d8ae=\"crazydave\"]I was hesitant to borrow from the bPs funds to get more FETs, even though I had cleared it through you, but it\'s a good thing I put it off. I got a guy that payed me for 4 mods today, so now I don\'t have to worry about that.  :grin: \r\n\r\nSo now I\'m all set to get back modding next week. 8-) \r\n\r\ndave[/quote:e0e937d8ae]excellent! lol\r\nwhew!'),(22290,'1d1c43bf5a','Hey Dude. Can I get access to the FTP for your playlists? Or can you allow http access to it for me.\r\n\r\nI have wanted quite a few of the songs off there and D/Ling from Kazaa/Emule is such a pain now-a-days.\r\n\r\nLemme know\r\n\r\nThanks Bro.\r\n\r\n :-D'),(22471,'f0f49bf24f','Thanx Dude. You rule\r\n\r\n\r\nI have kept this in my \"HTML Stash From Scott\" Won;t bug ya again for it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26551,'e51658b88f','Want me to throw in a barely used Bigfoot Monster Truck and Monster Truck Motor Upgrade kit for another $20?\r\n\r\nThis stuff is in the orifinal packaging as well.'),(29520,'1853ea9f9a','Whats up you little all kinds of RC havin\' bitch???'),(29521,'c43a9b49bd','Dude, shit\'s falling into place.\r\n\r\nMy wife already has another trip planned, so I made her feel guilty because its supposed to be my turn (even though we were sidetracked anyways  :lol: ) So she sat down and worked out a budget to save me some money for August. She\'s budgeting me like $500. I don\'t think it\'ll cost that much, so if I save some money I should get an Overland out of this, ya think? :lol: \r\n\r\nThen yesterday, I found these Accelerators cars that Hot Wheels came out with for their new series on Cartoon Network. I saw the 6-spoke wheels like on the World Race cars, so I knew there had to be a 5-spoke version, and there was, it was the very back one, and the only one left. Ironically, I found the same wheels on a standard $.75 Hot Wheels, but they were too small. That was one of the things I almost ordered last week. I was gonna get a World Race car off of ebay. :lol: \r\n\r\nIt has big and small wheels like a bit, so I think I\'m actually gonna use the big wheels, and use zip zap tires on them. I think that\'ll work out better because the lower profile will make the rear tires seem fatter, less rolling resistance, should transfer more weight to the rear, and mostly, I have a pile of Zip Zap tires, so that simplifies things.\r\n\r\nSo now I have a ZZ chassis to hack, a pair of SE batteries, KIT racer gear sets, alloys for the rear, and wheels for the front. I have a \'69 Camaro set aside for you, but my local shack just got a bunch of P&amp;P sets in out of no where, so if you want a \'68 instead, now is your chance to speak up.\r\n\r\nAll I have left is decals, but I have more than enough to start with now. To top it off, my kid was puking all day yesterday, so I called in today. Now he\'s fine, and I got the day to fuck around. part of my hang up lately, is that I spend all weekend recovering, and then Tuesday when I go back, I got plans, but one day back at work kills my mood. So I\'m hoping to have some fun today.\r\n\r\nOh yeah, and I got the killer sticky green green yesterday too. Been kinda half ass for the last month. I also made my first post at mini-zracer.com, and made a friend just up the road here in Phoenix. About a 10 minute drive.\r\n\r\nSo I feel like everything just fell together. Hopefully today turns out as I hope, and I have some fun working on your car, but for now I gotta go back to bed, it\'s not quite time to start today yet. (I couldn\'t wait, so got up for a little head start.  :lol: )\r\n\r\ndave'),(22317,'00f0d0a723','Yes, I do still have it all. I would prefer Paypal, but a money order is fine. I will send the stuff out once the money order is recieved though.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22318,'00f0d0a723','Yes, I do still have it all. I would prefer Paypal, but a money order is fine. I will send the stuff out once the money order is recieved though.'),(22319,'b0030b84b9','Ok great we wil get your money :)'),(22320,'b0030b84b9','Ok great we wil get your money :)'),(22321,'ab246bc160','[quote:ab246bc160=\"Stoli\"]Hey Dude. Can I get access to the FTP for your playlists? Or can you allow http access to it for me.\r\n\r\nI have wanted quite a few of the songs off there and D/Ling from Kazaa/Emule is such a pain now-a-days.\r\n\r\nLemme know\r\n\r\nThanks Bro.\r\n\r\n :-D[/quote:ab246bc160]it\'s easier if you just tell me which one you\'re wanting that\'s up at the moment and I send ya a link to download or something.'),(36804,'32fab24b88','hey man, I know, slack late response.  You\'ve prolyl figured out the problem now.\r\n\r\nI take it was a DNS issue?  You running an exchange box in a BIND DNS environment?\r\n\r\nhttp://www.msexchange.org/ is an excellent site for all things exchange, just search the forums there, it may help.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nMatt.'),(37107,'db9b781349','[quote:db9b781349=\"Mad_Maxx\"]Hi Cabo!\r\nI have seen something that for me is against BP policies and philosophy, the last member called &quot;Juzi\'s Mom&quot; has a website that is NOT (Ithink) related to BP.\r\ncan you check it?\r\nI think she\'s not interested in bits...should be banned!\r\nI might be wrong but..you never know.\r\nthks 4 taking te time to read.\r\nMad_Maxx[/quote:db9b781349]\r\nI\'m pretty sure &quot;Juzi\'s Mom&quot; is a current bitPimp member who registered a new name to screw with &quot;Juzi\'s Customs&quot;.\r\nThe account &quot;Juzi\'s Mom&quot; has not been activated yet, I\'m guessing it might not ever be.\r\nI\'m not too concerned, stuff like that blows over pretty quickly.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37691,'75e8599b13','Sorry man i am just overly excited to get this body...\r\n\r\nI wanted to know what color the thing was? I am thinking of body another race body for my car, maybe another murcielago lime green. \r\n\r\nI have a lime green one already i am just keeping it mint condition, and the one you give me is gonna be my racer...\r\n\r\nAnyways just let me know big guy\r\n\r\npeace'),(37644,'5c51f80911','Check for the $13 in 5-7 mins, I should be done the transaction by then.'),(34560,'93d0d2f373','[quote:93d0d2f373=\"BilboBaggins\"]I was a little surprised that nobody had answered it before me. I had been off line to two days.\r\n\r\nIf you are shipping US Mail use:\r\n\r\nBill J. Wilson\r\n4457 Tolbut Street\r\nPhiladelphia, PA 19136\r\n\r\nIf using UPS:\r\n\r\nBill J. Wilson\r\n8719 Jackson Street\r\nPhiladelphia, PA 19136\r\n\r\nUPS requires signatures in Philly and my father is retired and at home most the time. Just let me know which way it\'s coming so I can warn him (Unfortunately we share a name  :lol: ).[/quote:93d0d2f373]\r\n :lol: Right on. I\'ll be sending it US Mail in a padded envelope.\r\n\r\nYea, I posted the quiz late last night, I was thinking it would run for at least a few days before someone nailed it. I was wrong. lol\r\nGood job man.'),(37894,'b64d497811','[quote:b64d497811=\"hue35\"]Hey man, I\'m not blowin\' you off, I\'ve just been slammed like a muthafucka. Saw ya just now, so I thought I\'d at least say hey.\r\n\r\nTalk to ya more thoroughly later.[/quote:b64d497811]Cool. :-o  \r\nI assumed you were busy. That\'s pretty much been your story lately.  \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33728,'a2e7df83b2','dude fucking chill out. i was trying 2 take the nice approach by appolijizing(woopdido i know i spelt it wrong). besides, its only a web site.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\njust *CHILL OUT*\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\np.s. try not to take any offence to this.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\npimptothemax'),(22331,'4fd519ebae','Did you get the items yet?'),(22332,'e7271af8fc','Nope'),(22333,'5cdf099082','Nope'),(33454,'16b64cd3de','[quote:16b64cd3de=\"weazel\"]PayPal sent :-)[/quote:16b64cd3de]\r\n\r\nI shipped it out today about 4:30pm Priority. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nThanks and enjoy!! :driving:'),(35642,'831ed214c3','well i was just looking at your siggy and I like fps and I was wondering what game that was'),(35644,'ceaeb8de7f','[quote:ceaeb8de7f=\"Whitesupra35\"]well i was just looking at your siggy and I like fps and I was wondering what game that was[/quote:ceaeb8de7f]\r\nBattlefield 2\r\nhttp://www.ea.com/official/battlefield/battlefield2/us/home.jsp\r\n\r\nIt\'s pretty cool.'),(33923,'4e5c6a8a38','Hi,\r\n\r\nI have what you want, not a diagram, but an actual PCB w/ fets + 2 speeds. I see you want a ZZMT, so do I. you can get one for $6.25-ish after you buy the $12.49 one. So you can buy one for me as payment for the stuff, more like a trade really. Let me know.\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33924,'c32bf7d1ec','[quote:c32bf7d1ec=\"breakyaface\"]my adres is:\r\nCipreslaan 48 (street)\r\n3053nd (zipcode)\r\nRotterdam (city)\r\nthe Netherlands. \r\n\r\nAnd how can I be guarenteed that I do receive my ZZMT because I have been fucked up once with a money transfer with eBay.[/quote:c32bf7d1ec]\r\n\r\nAs long as you have Paypal, you should be OK.  Its a simple process.  Other than that, you\'ll have to trust me.  Check the \"Vouch for\" thread.  I\'ve dealt with everyone at some point in time.  All over the world.\r\n\r\nAccording to the USPS website, I get $10 USD for shipping.\r\n\r\nSo $25 USD should cover everything.\r\n\r\n12.49\r\n7% PA sales tax (I\'m in PA)\r\n10.00 shipping\r\nPaypal fees will be about $1 or so because of monetary conversions.\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know.\r\n\r\n\r\n:-)'),(33459,'07cc0e3071','Hey Cameron,\r\n\r\nGot the package you sent.\r\nDamn man!  :shock: I only sent you a couple sets of rims. And you send me what looks like the whole Mini RC section at BigLots! I really didn\'t expect anything in return other than pics of your Shelby with the rims!\r\n\r\nI feel you got the short end of the stick...  :sad:\r\nYou need anything else?\r\nI got:\r\n- Different DUB\'s\r\n- Cyclona bodies (bB, WRX, Celica, S2000; fits Bits and MicroSizers)\r\n- Mini Cooper (complete mini RC)\r\n- Motors\r\n- Cat5 wire\r\n- misc parts\r\n\r\nLet me know. I can take pics.\r\n\r\n-DriveWRX  :cool:'),(33460,'4e830916d1','Hey, no problem.  I would like to see pics of the Mini but be warned, there would be another shipment of stuff to your house.  -Cameron');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36519,'a780d497a6','[quote:a780d497a6=\"sg219\"]I\'ll be out near there the next couple of days.  I gotta see if they have them in the store.  Looks like it\'ll fill my needs.\r\n\r\nHave you used it yet or tryied it out?  \r\n\r\nHow noisey or quiet is it?\r\n\r\nWill it need a lot of maintenence?\r\n\r\nSturdy?  Not crappy plastic and loose parts?  Long lasting or will I be replacing it in a couple of months or years?\r\n\r\nYou know, the overall quality report the the big DT.\r\n\r\n :-o \r\n\r\nThanks man.[/quote:a780d497a6]\r\n\r\n-It\'s metal and looks to be very sturdy.\r\n-I\'ve turned it on and it\'s not that bad.  Silent compared to my 2hp/2gal  garage compressor.\r\n-It\'s oiless so I would think it\'s maintennance free.\r\n-Haven\'t tried it yet.  \r\n\r\nBeen reading and getting advice from over on the HotWheels boards about air brushes. \r\nThey all recommend the Badger 155! I just scored one last night on ebay, \r\ndude lives in Md right outside of DC so I\'ll  swing by and pick it up tomorrow  :smile:  \r\nIt\'s dual action so I\'ll need to practice.  I still have a new one that I got from\r\nHarbor Frieght last year (gave one away in the Tools Of Da Trade Contest).\r\nI went on this sight that teaches air brushing techniques so I may get to try it \r\nout this weekend though I doubt it. \r\n\r\nBike sShow is this weekend, the Skins play, need to tool on DarkTari so I may get to \r\nsqueeze it in there somewhere.  This Craft store around here is going outta\r\nbusiness so I waited til shit went to 50%-70%.  Picked up a large assortment of \r\nXacto blades, some web ribbon (for grills) some nice brushes, acrylic paint (for airbrush practicing), \r\nand other stuff.  I was surprised to see a NKOK Hummer reg $29.99 but $15.00 was still too much to me!'),(22337,'5df4dd30dc','Not sure whats going on with suntzu, don\'t really care, just thought I\'d say I hope this stays a WGU and Pimps matter.  I make all my mods and members leave their WGU crap at the door.\r\n\r\n\r\nWell just saying Hey and wow what a crazy bit of posts, but sometimes the controversary can lead to new members.\r\n\r\n\r\nTTYL\r\nRipper');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22340,'81b68d2b16','Did you need me on MSN? I\'m available now, I was at the gym.'),(26706,'d4c33c5eff','Thanks for the reply.\r\n\r\nDo you know if anybody backed up the important stuff from wegotu, like diagrams and important discussions about specs and stuff?  I\'ve been using google\'s cache, but that gets kinda tedious.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nred2cwm'),(27139,'8e228ac102','When ph2t asked you about the steering, I wasn\'t clear about the answer.  I unserstand that when you let go of the sttering wheel on the controller, the steering spring snaps the front wheels back to center.  But what about when you hold the steering wheel one way?  Do the front wheels stay turned until you let go of the weel?  Whith your current setup, when the steering motor is not connected to the steering gears (not in its slot), does it keep spinning when you turn the wheel in one direction, or does it spin and then stop?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nChris'),(26459,'a6672cd172','No problem.  Thanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22344,'6317d6bb14','hey man\r\n\r\nive got paypal so who do i send money to and how much is shipping??\r\n\r\ncheers man\r\n\r\n\r\n :D'),(22345,'9e55a3e9cc','Sorry Tall 1,  Was on vacation! \r\nDid [b:9e55a3e9cc]Cabo[/b:9e55a3e9cc] get intouch with you ?\r\nIf not hit [b:9e55a3e9cc]Crazy Dave [/b:9e55a3e9cc]about PayPal !'),(22346,'88f588cecb','on your foto there are paz but were do you have the foto from'),(22347,'734a657408','[quote:734a657408=\"PINGO\"]on your foto there are paz but were do you have the foto from[/quote:734a657408]I took the picture with my camera.\r\nyou can see more or choose one for your \'avatar\' by clicking on the \"Profile\" link above, and then \"Avatar Gallery\".'),(34492,'88a04ed103','it\'s quite different since thee\'s two different mosfets now.\r\n\r\nsee the doco here:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttp://www.woahnelly.com/stuff/xmods/EVOMOSFETInstallationGuide.pdf\r\n\r\ngood luck!\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:88a04ed103=\"Clint\"][quote:88a04ed103=\"ph2t\"]hey man, just wanted to let you know that the installation doco for the evo mosfet upgrade is almost done.  it will be posted shortly.\r\n\r\nif you wanted something sooner to help let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nph2t.,[/quote:88a04ed103]\r\n\r\nsweet thx. I received the package of fets from aus micro this afternoon.\r\nUnfortunatly, i wont be able to work on it until i get home this weekend, so no rush. if the install is anything like the original xmod fet upgrade, i wont have any problems.\r\n\r\nthx,\r\n-clint[/quote:88a04ed103]'),(32355,'16e215ae5e','[quote:16e215ae5e=\"mikirgra\"]Wassup DT? Has the BCG arrived yet? I would have thought it would get there today (Friday), maybe Saturday at the latest. Let me know daddy-o.\r\nLater.[/quote:16e215ae5e]\r\nNot yet Pimp !');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24281,'676226138d','Hey Pimp,\r\n\r\nWould you still be interrested in acquiring this\r\n\r\n[img:676226138d]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/thumb_bitcam3.jpg[/img:676226138d]\r\n\r\nFrom the [b:676226138d]Back Alley Auction [/b:676226138d]for your last bid of [color=green:676226138d]$53.00 [/color:676226138d]?\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=3982&amp;start=150\r\n\r\n[color=red:676226138d]Lemme Know ![/color:676226138d]'),(28538,'c9efacc147','Alright, Glad to do biz-naz with Ya man, Thanks again for everything, I\'ll deff Hit Ya up for a paint job within a month after I get a GT-500 and modify to a certain extent, but I\'ll let Ya know when the time comes. Let me know if you need any other parts, and Thanks again.\r\nKorey'),(28392,'54d8eb2587','[quote:54d8eb2587=\"JDM-R34\"]Hey I got a question about PM\'ing?\r\nUmm I sent a message to biohazard and I pressed send and all that, but it moved to my outbox and I don\'t know if It ever got sent....So I\'m not sure if he got it or not.\r\nWould there be a reason why It didn\'t sent but went to my outbox, or when it goes to outbox does that mean it will send later, or thath e hasn\'t gotten it yet?\r\nOh yeah good job on that camaro and GTR!\r\nThanks[/quote:54d8eb2587]Whenever you send a message, it first goes to your \"Outbox\" folder and sits there until it is delivered, it will then be moved to your \"Sentbox\".\r\nIt hasn\'t been sent yet because he hasn\'t logged in yet for it to be sent to him.\r\nNow, the thing to understand is this...\r\nPMs come in 2 parts really. In your profile, you have the option of being notified by email when a PM is sent to you. Most users have that turned on by default.\r\nSo, the email message has been sent to him, however he has not actually seen the PM so it is not marked as \"Sentbox\" yet.\r\nOnce he logs in again, the PM will be waiting in his \"Inbox\" and the message will move from your \"Outbox\" to the \"Sent\" folder.'),(37901,'24b7e18349','Where can I send the vid to, and how do I add the screen shot? I\'m kind of a dummy when it comes to videos and video editing');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37902,'4a24281a10','[quote:4a24281a10=\"HirotoR34\"]Where can I send the vid to, and how do I add the screen shot? I\'m kind of a dummy when it comes to videos and video editing[/quote:4a24281a10]\r\nWell it depends.\r\nHow big is the video? If it\'s 5MB or under, you can upload it directly to your bitPimps gallery.\r\nIf it\'s over 5MB and under 10MB, you could possibly mail it to me at: bitpimps@gmail.com\r\nIf  you\'re a member a Putfile, it may give you a direct link to download your video (I\'m not sure), if it does, send me that link and I\'ll download it directly.\r\nIf none of those work, we\'ll have to find another way.\r\nLet me know. I don\'t want to make you jump through hoops, so let me know what you think.'),(26369,'f236cb9d5f','[quote:f236cb9d5f=\"kvik369\"]Just letting you know that I got the cars - all is good\r\n\r\nUpdate on the 04 - its still running - popped an x-speed pro in it and it flys.  Some say the fets may fry but I\'m waiting on a couple of Nelly\'s anyway.  Of course I smacked head on full speed into the dining room table.  It still works but somethings not right with the steering servo.  Was smooth as silk before, but now it makes noise and twitches. Have to open it up when I get a chance. Leave it to me to run outside no problems and break it inside (LOL)  well anyway,  enjoy the holidays\r\n\r\nVik[/quote:f236cb9d5f]Cool, glad you got them. I think I forgot to tell you they were sent. :oops:  :lol: \r\n\r\nDon\'t feel bad, I seriously think it\'s more dangerous to run a fast car indoors.\r\n\r\nI got my 04 today. Gotta tell ya, everyone freaks about the shipping from China, but that was 8 days, during the holidays. Toyeast kicks ass, never had a problem with them.\r\n\r\nMy wife is gonna take it from me and wrap it, but I got a good  look and some pictures, and it looks really cool. I\'m getting excited for Christmas now. :-D \r\n\r\nMerry Christmas, dude. :-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(28176,'00edbaf568','im from maryland man wassup');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27425,'d210d43fe6','Sup bro. I\'m glad you got your order in. I got mine in too. It was ridiculously expensive, but I haven\'t found the AE86\'s anywhere else. I KNOW I can get you the Gloria body set cheaper than that for you. I\'ll check. The WRX shouldn\'t be any problem either.\r\n\r\nYes, there\'s a Shen Qi Wei Gloria too. I have 8 Shens and they rock!\r\nIf you have a KB Toys anywhere near you, they usually have the Shen\'s (rebadged as Rally Racers) for $10. You can\'t beat that deal. I have two of the blue/silver Glorias from there. I can probably hook you up if you can\'t find any.\r\n\r\nLater.'),(28407,'08f1ec9f6f','do you have the plasma/atomic motor? I saw you posting in ph2t\'s thread.\r\nLet me know if you got the friction problem sorted. I may buy one off you. Maybe $65 for GPM\'s and motor. just like last time.\r\n\r\n$65 seems to be the magic price lol\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(29396,'6ef657c006','Thanks man, I appreciate it, It\'s Christmas in May! lol\r\nThanks'),(34113,'a01fbd9bb1','[quote:a01fbd9bb1=\"sessiz\"]Usps site says they\'ve been delievered....Please tell me ya got the rims. I\'m also sending $5 for that body in less then an hour. I\'m sending cash, hope that\'s cool. :-)[/quote:a01fbd9bb1]\r\n\r\nGot the Rims man and they are sweet I can\'t wait to find a car (or make one) to go with them! thanks agian so much man you have been a true pimp!\r\n\r\nI left you some, I guess you call it feedback, In the appropriate thread (didnt throw ya under the bus)! I just went on and on......  :lol: \r\n\r\nI will make sure you get your bodies from the Bonzer man! I will probably send off the payment next week as yours and Dark Tari are the only ones to send money (unless CW sends some) I will go ahead next week and send paypal to Bonzer even if ya\'lls money is not here yet so I can get them on the road!\r\n\r\nthanks agian man if you need any more batteries let me know!  :shock:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22353,'0d5ebb25a0','there\'s no real easy way for me to check who voted for what.\r\nbut I get the feeling it\'s somebody trying to exact revenge or some stupid shit.\r\nsince this whole Panther thing between the 2 sites, weird things have been happening. I got threatened with legal action against some agency that supposedly represents one of the chicks sessiz used in one of the wallpapers he created.\r\nI can\'t say 100% for sure, but I think it\'s kids trying to make life hard, but they\'re not too good at it. lol\r\n\r\nI\'ve made the galleries now to where \"un-registered\" or \"anonymous\" users can\'t vote, so that should help.\r\n\r\nwe\'ll see what comes next lol\r\n[quote:0d5ebb25a0=\"Finks\"]Was checking out my gallery today and what the hell, some one gave my VW a sub 5star vote.  Checked out the top cars and noted that [img:0d5ebb25a0]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10017/thumb_prize2.jpg[/img:0d5ebb25a0] and [img:0d5ebb25a0]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10008/thumb_jota_darkblue_04.jpg[/img:0d5ebb25a0] also got dropped hard core from negative votes.  I know this is all bs and who really cares, but I think I am not reaching when I say none of these cars should be sub 5 star votes.  Can you find out if they were by the same person and if you feel it necessary, to remove the nagative stars?  If not, it\'s cool, but just check it out.  Thanks[/quote:0d5ebb25a0]'),(22365,'43436876d4','[quote:43436876d4=\"VooDooMafia\"]Nope[/quote:43436876d4]\r\n\r\nOk, let me know when you have them.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22366,'5d33b0da3f','I will dude'),(23052,'48c06adddf','dimelo dominicanpimp.... eres dominicano de verdad?   soy gringo, pero aprendi hablar español alla en la republica dominicana hace 7 años..\r\n\r\nBienvenidos, y disfruta nuestro forums.... :-) \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-payaso'),(22368,'ec4bb1b22d','[quote:ec4bb1b22d=\"ripper7777777\"]Not sure whats going on with suntzu, don\'t really care, just thought I\'d say I hope this stays a WGU and Pimps matter.  I make all my mods and members leave their WGU crap at the door.\r\n\r\n\r\nWell just saying Hey and wow what a crazy bit of posts, but sometimes the controversary can lead to new members.\r\n\r\n\r\nTTYL\r\nRipper[/quote:ec4bb1b22d]yea the whole thing is stupid. I\'m not wasting my, or anyone elses, time anymore with it. lol\r\n\r\nhows things in your neck of the woods?'),(24233,'0102c98886','can you still get these vehicles man?  i\'d love a few more 4wd bodies... there is only so many years that the Bb shell will suffice!'),(24234,'99e2939705','[quote:99e2939705=\"viperdout\"]muthang?  What\'s that mean.  I for got a \"to\" in my first sentence.  I have painted before, and it came out good, except my putty job underneath sucked 9first time I had ever bondoed).  Buh-bye, wannabe.[/quote:99e2939705]\r\n\r\ni forgot about you muthang,   can i ask you just one last question? how the fuck did you manage to type 9 in front of the word first? bondoed? for got? (thats one word tosser).      \r\n\r\n    if i dont get a reply i will know youve dissapeared, take all the little fags with you while your at it!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22359,'08e36d43aa','can you tell me:\r\ndoes this happen to you both at work and at home?\r\nwhat browser are you using when you get this issue?\r\ndo you use any other browsers?[quote:08e36d43aa=\"DarkTari\"]C-Ducb,\r\nMan I\'m steady gettin logged out.  I tried to reply and had to log in again.  I wrote my reply, submitted and had to log in again and it deleted all the shit I just wrote, pissed me off Pimp.  Please look into this issue......[/quote:08e36d43aa]'),(24447,'6e105e12eb','[quote:6e105e12eb=\"pimp master deuce\"]Thanks, man. I guess it automatically goes inactive if you change the email address... it said it needed to be reactivated via email because of the change.[/quote:6e105e12eb]huh, no shit lol\r\nmusta been one of the updates in 2.0.10 version we updated to.\r\ncool lol\r\n\r\nwell anyways, you should be all set.'),(36892,'71169b6ab6','Where can I purchase the MiniT servo\r\n\r\nBTW. Thanks for the helpful tip!'),(37831,'8326cec003','Yeah, just the 27 and 27a. The payment will show up to ssirpe@sympatico.ca\r\nfrom lordhelmetr342003@yahoo.com in the amount of $20 \r\n\r\n\r\nMy shipping addy is:\r\n\r\nJustin Long\r\n3 Crockett Rd.\r\nRaymond ME 04071');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36895,'e94218687f','Yo man, are there any other rc places in vancouver that i should know about? I live right downtown, (Homer &amp; Smithe)\r\n\r\nOr other rc people for that matter, heh'),(32782,'ddf2d1990e','That\'s cool pimpin, I had a problem with cashing the money order because it was \"out of country\" and they said \"It wasn\'t or didn\'t have a bank routing number\" or something like that. Don\'t worry about it though. Hope you enjoy it as much as I did. Later pimp!!'),(24848,'26c8b88330','[quote:26c8b88330=\"chrome\"]let me run those links by you again...\r\n\r\nhttp://www.radioshack.com/images/ProductCatalog/ProductImage/60/m60-7004.jpg\r\n\r\nhttp://www.radioshack.com/images/ProductCatalog/ProductImage/60/m60-7009.jpg\r\n\r\nhttp://www.radioshack.com/images/ProductCatalog/ProductImage/60/m60-7504.jpg\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...\r\n\r\nPS. I\'ll get the accessories soon.[/quote:26c8b88330]\r\n\r\nI\'m not following the idea with the links...I already have those items linked in the ZipZaps and ZipZaps Accessories pages'),(22363,'5a2fcc7e27','[quote:5a2fcc7e27=\"Finks\"]That\'s what I figured.  What a bunch of fucked up shit.  I hope this whole thing dies out really quick, cuz it\'s all BS from start to finish.  Is there any reason to think the thing w/ Sessiz is a legit accusation?  Well whatever.  I think I will just delete and repost my VW tomorrow if it is still nagging me.  Will see then.\r\n\r\nP.S. what I found super gay was your car went from the #2 best rated car to like number 203 w/ one neg vote... BS 4 sure.[/quote:5a2fcc7e27]yea it sure was all BS.\r\nyea I think the whole voting system is kind of gay.\r\nit tries to calculate a rating based on the # of votes VS the rating on each of those votes. which is some what misleading.\r\nlets say an image gets 1 vote and it\'s given 5 stars.\r\nnow lets say another image gets 10 votes and is given 5 stars on all votes except 2, which gave it a 1 star rating.\r\nby the systems calculations, the image with 1 vote given 5 stars would be on top, because the other image with 10 votes and gets a calculated rating of (let\'s say/guess) 4.5 stars.\r\nthe sessiz thing, yea he nabbed that chickita, so in theory - I\'m sure someone holds the copyrights to imagery of her. There\'s a huge grey line there though because it might be able to be argued that the image he created could be legitimately used because the entire image was not stolen, only a piece of the image (the chick) and since we\'re not a shop nor \"stealing\" revenue from the owners of the copyrighted image (the chick), it could be seen as \"Fair Use\". But that has to be determined on a case by case basis in the courts - so I would have to pay legal fees, court times, etc. to fight it and have a 50/50 chance of winning - the 2 images aren\'t worth it so I just deleted them - but also made it very clear that most of the claims were false and it could be argued that all claims were false.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25501,'affdf77178','i do have the xmod shit but i figure a brand new monster would be nicer to have. they really do kick ass.'),(28846,'53cdf0227d','Backdrift keep suckin dicks tryin\' to fit in i don\'t give a fuck what you say.'),(28588,'6c6d7bc656','Yea thats your fault one of your wonderful moderators edited it my post to say something I did not say.'),(23066,'1f2b383748','hola amigo'),(23090,'d9d2c01090','Hey Dave,\r\nTried PMing you from the other site but got no reply. I was just wondering if the cars arrived OK. I just wanted to make sure I don\'t have to jump onto the shipper for being late. Thanks and I hope they got there alright.\r\nAz\r\nJim Mullins'),(23091,'87d9f049cb','[quote:87d9f049cb=\"azimov\"]Hey Dave,\r\nTried PMing you from the other site but got no reply. I was just wondering if the cars arrived OK. I just wanted to make sure I don\'t have to jump onto the shipper for being late. Thanks and I hope they got there alright.\r\nAz\r\nJim Mullins[/quote:87d9f049cb]Nope, haven\'t seen them. I was starting to wonder. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(28523,'2f495d675d','Yep I was talking about any 1/64 scale diecast cars. I am sure we can work out a deal when you are ready to have your car painted. By the way I didn\'t get the package yet, I am sure it will show up tomorrow.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24141,'225fc4e2d6','[quote:225fc4e2d6=\"DarkTari\"]Hey Pimp,\r\n\r\nI picked up some for some kids on another site but they never responded.\r\nI still have a few if you\'re interrested and can get more.  They\'re all RPM I think, I\'ll check. All have the famous 2.6 that I\'ve raved so much about over the years.[/quote:225fc4e2d6]\r\n\r\nThanks DT! I don\'t remember which KITs are which (I\'m at work), but I\'m interested in the ones that have blue gears, or the ones with red gears that have front wheels that match the rear wheels and use tires (rather than hard plastic wheels). I\'m not interested in the ones that have green gears. Lemme know how many and how much. Thanks!\r\n\r\nSuperFly'),(24010,'671ca4717f','[quote:671ca4717f=\"VooDooMafia\"]If you goto that old thread is there anything there you would want for those shells?\r\n\r\n  Some of the stuff is gone but most is still there.\r\n\r\n  Any luck finding aother sub at wally world?[/quote:671ca4717f]actually, I haven\'t checked the wally world since monday so I\'ll go there tomorrow on my lunch and check again. they keep getting in these frickin huge ass plastic pieces of shit r/c\'s for 100.00 and they keep dis-appearing so I\'m guessing their making room for that crap.\r\n\r\nmaybe a pullback and the MAT body?'),(36782,'d935933de6','Right on, ill get the money to you tonight.\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37346,'0fb6e5e342','[quote:0fb6e5e342=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:0fb6e5e342=\"betty.k\"]yup, you got it! bettykay@gmail.com\r\n\r\ni\'ll keep these goods for you, i won\'t sell them to anyone else if you\'re slow paying :-o[/quote:0fb6e5e342]\r\n\r\nCool man, just sent the $ as we speak!\r\n\r\nBtw Change the shipping name that paypal gives you from Chris to Matt, the account was under my father\'s name originally.\r\n\r\nThanks for the sweet deal man, looking foward to recieving and reviving this xmod!\r\n\r\n :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:0fb6e5e342]\r\n\r\nok, so this is it?\r\n\r\nMatt Gera\r\n4303 Radcliffe Dr.\r\nPalm Harbor, FL 34685\r\nUnited States'),(35313,'93b9207435','[quote:93b9207435=\"LBRC\"][quote:93b9207435=\"Tuner1989\"]Allright ill look into it hopefully i can find a fix to the problem.[/quote:93b9207435]\r\n\r\nHope you find the problem.\r\n\r\nSlight amendment to what I said above:\r\n\r\nYou should be able to hold the front of the chassis and easily turn the wheels [u:93b9207435][b:93b9207435]slowly[/b:93b9207435] so that you do not to damage the servo gears[/u:93b9207435], full left and right with just the lightest finger pressure on one wheel.  The servo gears should make [u:93b9207435]a [b:93b9207435]clean[/b:93b9207435] and light zipping sound[/u:93b9207435] when you do this, if the servo saver is catching then something like a grain of sand is caught in the gears.[/quote:93b9207435]\r\n\r\nGood luck,\r\nCheers[/quote]\r\n\r\nCleaned out the gearbox took some trial and error but i finally got it turning smooth. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\nOn another note, do you know when it comes to the nelly deluxes specs if the 16A max current means motor wise or battery wise?\r\n\r\nSPECS:\r\nMax voltage: 12V, or 3 li-ion (10.8V) or 3 li-poly (11.1V) \r\nMax current: 16A (100A theoretical peak) \r\nTotal resistance: 0.0087 Ohms (lowest in the game) \r\nAccepts all \"hot\" 130 sized motors \r\nKeeps the brake function \r\nRuns exceptionally cool, even with low wind (&lt;30 turn) motors \r\nDimensions: 32mm Wide x 25mm Long x 5mm High'),(37358,'f7830d2700','hiya man. i just got back from the post office, your stuff should arrive in 1 - 2 weeks.\r\nshoot me a message when it arrives and if there\'s any problems or there\'s something missing don\'t hesitate to let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers, b.k.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31241,'61cc37bfe8','Ok, I\'m sorry I\'m being a pain in the ass. My back has been out the last month, and I should have waited until my head was clear but I got excited and couldn\'t wait. My mistake.\r\n\r\nApparently I did do something wrong before, though I\'m baffled as to what, I went over and over my connections, but I went ahead and tried again, and this time its working, nothing\'s shorting out, but it performs exactly as it did before.\r\n\r\nYou mentioned it may need to be reprogrammed afater being shorted. Think that happened here?\r\n\r\nSo where do we go from here? You want to take a look at it, or should I just buy another off you and start from scratch?\r\n\r\nAgain, sorry, this should have been simple. I blew it. :lol: \r\n\r\nThanks\r\ndave'),(26318,'3d4ae2359c','im curius of to what went wrong, fill me in here?'),(22385,'269e67af0b','[quote:269e67af0b=\"crazydave\"]I don\'t know if you\'ve considered integrating your coppermine gallery with the rest the site, so when you\'re logged in the boards, you\'re logged in the gallery, but my wife figured out to integrate her Invision board with her Coppermine gallery.\r\n\r\nShe said it was a bitch, but I\'m figuring if she figured it out, it should be no prob for you.\r\n\r\nJust thought I\'d give you a heads up.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:269e67af0b]I\'ve thought about it, just never made it a priority. my original thinking was that I really didn\'t want every forum member to be able to have a gallery, but I suppose that\'s what I could use usergroups for lol\r\nso yea, I might do that one day lol\r\nthanks for the heads up, props to your savvy wife :wink:'),(37378,'f8a984ff6d','Hey cj, I was wondering on the status of the order.  I\'ve seen a few GPM parts on the forums and was wondering if you were starting to ship orders.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22390,'9e55a3e9cc','Sorry Tall 1,  Was on vacation! \r\nDid [b:9e55a3e9cc]Cabo[/b:9e55a3e9cc] get intouch with you ?\r\nIf not hit [b:9e55a3e9cc]Crazy Dave [/b:9e55a3e9cc]about PayPal !'),(24668,'06256d253d','what\'s you\'re addy again so I can check it against what I have here on the shipping tag? I thought I saved it, but  I might have deleted it after i sent it out the first time.'),(25796,'9fda58789e','Ok got it sent out today.\r\n\r\nI tried to get it out Express. I even had the next cook come in a half hour early, so I could make it in time, but I just missed the bus, had to catch the next one a half hour later. I showed at the PO by 4, but by the time they called my number it was 4:10, and too late. It wouldn\'t be there until Friday whether I sent it Express or Priorty, because of the holiday. \r\n\r\nSo I sent it Priorty, and it should be there by Friday.\r\n\r\nCheck back at this thread. The PCB I posted is yours.\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=60367#60367\r\n\r\ndave'),(35451,'119e2ef6b1','Yo Pimpin I am tring to get everything together so I can hit the post office after i get off work you\'re the only Pimp i need mailing info from.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31760,'13754c0da9','[quote:13754c0da9=\"R/C Crazy1\"]I was wondering if you still had some of 1/3AAA batteries for sale. I am interested and can use Paypal to send payment. Just let me know the price for item and for shipping. Thanks in advance.[/quote:13754c0da9]\r\n\r\nyes I still have pleanty of batteries for sale. the cost is 4 batteries for $1.00 and depending on where you live the cost of shipping varies if in the US Cost for shipping is $ .65 the more you get the more shipping will be.\r\n\r\nlet me know how many you want shipping address and I will get you a total cost.\r\n\r\nmy paypal address is: airo@ev1.net \r\nthanks again\r\nAaron\r\nsteelwoolghandi'),(28949,'b7fd4347d5','Just letting you know.\r\npayaso can only read the forums right now, he can\'t post - his computer is messed up.\r\nHe got your PM and will get your keychain shipped out to you.'),(25993,'507a4e5d24','[quote:507a4e5d24=\"kvik369\"]I know what you mean about the MT\'s those guys did.  Something else.\r\nI do the charger thing with the motorworks base too except I have a variable power supply.  What about charging your SE\'s.  Any kind of standalone charger?\r\nAlso do I owe you for the SE?  Let me know\r\n\r\nBy the way, how do you add the quotes with the persons name in it to your reply?\r\n\r\nVik[/quote:507a4e5d24]I have a SE base wired to the same base as my other dual cells. The se has different poles. I forget so let me double check, but I believe the center one is ground, the drivers side that is usually ground is positive, and the passenger side is the signal to program the frequencies. Since I race by myself I don\'t worry aboutthe frequency it\'s on.\r\n\r\nIt\'s up to you if want to pay anything for the SE. I\'m just letting you know what\'s up. Honestly, my head\'s just not into trouble shooting it right now, so I figure get the new one while they still have clearance cars, then I gets me da GTO body, and if at a later date I feel I really need another SE, then I can pull out your chassis and figure out what the heck happened.\r\n\r\nMakes sense, huh? :???: \r\n :lol: \r\n\r\nTo get the persons name in the quote, just add an equals, and the persons name inside quotes, behinde the word quote in the brackets. Like this\r\n\r\nquote=\"crazydave\"\r\n\r\nput the brackets around it and it looks like this\r\n[quote:507a4e5d24=\"crazydave\"] [/quote:507a4e5d24]\r\n\r\nDave'),(22397,'775d2209e0','I\'m asking the questions to help me narrow down where the issue might be coming from.\r\nI\'m trying not to go into much detail because it\'s boring and confusing lol\r\nif you want the full extended version, let me know - otherwise I\'ll think you got by with the possibilities and remedies that follow:\r\n[list=a:775d2209e0]\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Sessions: Once visiting the Forums and logging in, you can sit idle for 1 hour (no clicking, posting, viewing pages, etc.) before being logged out. If you take over 1 hour, you are logged out.\r\nSolutions: (multiple)\r\n[list=1:775d2209e0]\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Don\'t sit idle for more than 1 hour.\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Sessions are stored in \"cookies\" that are written to your PC. The cookies are checked by the Forum to determine the session. If the cookies are being removed or fail to be written to your PC by some other software (like anti-spyware), then the Forum will certainly log you out.\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Other \"anti-spam/spyware\" tactics are likely to delete cookies or not allow cookies to be written to your PC unless the software can verify the sources legitamecy. Reasonably and respectable programs should be able to recognize bitPimps as a legitamite source.\r\n[/list:o:775d2209e0]\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Cookies: Cookies from this site are working. That means the probably cause is somewhere between the communication of your ISP and your MSN browser or the MSN browser itself. I\'m betting on the browser / computer.\r\nSolutions: (multiple)\r\n[list=1:775d2209e0]\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Use Internet Explorer as your browser. Sounds like a \'lame\' excuse, but MSN browser is just a \"dumbed\" down version of IE (Internet Explorer). I can\'t really give much support or help on that browser because I just don\'t use it.\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Make sure cookies are allowed to be written to your PC. Make sure it does not delete those cookies once you log off your PC.\r\n[*:775d2209e0] Alternatively, you can add the \"http://bitpimps.lixlink.com\" domain to your \"trusted sites\" list or \"trusted cookies\" list.\r\n[/list:o:775d2209e0]\r\n[/list:o:775d2209e0]\r\nlet me know if you still have troubles or need more explination, etc.\r\n[quote:775d2209e0=\"DarkTari\"]Well right now it happens ay home.\r\n\r\nUsing MSN\r\n\r\nI\'ll check at work this week, Thanx Pimp[/quote:775d2209e0]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22399,'be63570ae8','hi\r\n\r\ni won the auction for the camaro for 28 bucks and i was told to ask for paypal details off you so i could send the money?\r\n\r\ncould i get em and how much would shipping cost to get it to Sydney Australia?\r\n\r\ncheers man\r\n\r\n :D'),(22400,'818f6802cf','[quote:818f6802cf=\"TallduDe\"]hi\r\n\r\ni won the auction for the camaro for 28 bucks and i was told to ask for paypal details off you so i could send the money?\r\n\r\ncould i get em and how much would shipping cost to get it to Sydney Australia?\r\n\r\ncheers man\r\n\r\n :D[/quote:818f6802cf]Ahh man, I\'m sorry, CaboPMed me and told me to get you my Paypal info, and I totally forgot. Sorry, been distracted.\r\n\r\nAnyways, you can paypal me at davesmoejoe@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nIf you get me your Zip Code I can get you a shipping estimate.\r\n\r\nDave'),(25996,'fbf1147bfd','sent you another 8 bucks\r\n[quote:fbf1147bfd=\"crazydave\"]  but I believe the center one is ground, the drivers side that is usually ground is positive, and the passenger side is the signal to program the frequencies. Since I race by myself I don\'t worry aboutthe frequency it\'s on. \r\n[/quote:fbf1147bfd]\r\nCall me stupid but give me wire colors (driver side??), and freq don\'t matter to me either\r\nAnd thanks for the quote tip - later\r\nVik'),(33736,'be6149112c','[quote:be6149112c=\"sessiz\"]Whelp your rims are on their way man. The envelope and postage was cheap so I added a delivery confirmation onto it for tracking sakes.\r\n\r\nwww.usps.com\r\n#0305 2200 0001 7687 6304\r\n\r\nEnjoy them rims man and don\'t forget to floss em up on BP right quick. :-)[/quote:be6149112c]\r\n\r\nDang your to friggin fast! I was thinking you would wait untill I sent you the money? Thanks man, I did not get your cash out today as I was in Architect meeting all day (they really suck) but will get it out first thing tomorrow! thanks so much man! have a great week and I will get them on something sweet as quick as I can!!  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24916,'7902b2e113','Hey, I\'m gonna be shipping that auction car off to you tomorrow. I\'ll need your shipping info. :-) \r\n\r\nDave'),(24440,'9927999ae2','You could send the $2 to Bird and he can paypal me for you I\'ll send the parts to him and he can install them for you!'),(35247,'bdc98524ab','Hey I was told that you do Mosfet work I have 2 ZZSe 1 ZZMT and 2 Bits I\'d like do can you help?'),(35248,'954b7b62f8','[quote:954b7b62f8=\"Bithigh707\"]Hey I was told that you do Mosfet work I have 2 ZZSe 1 ZZMT and 2 Bits I\'d like do can you help?[/quote:954b7b62f8]Yeah, I can help. I haven\'t been doing FET mods, but if you want that many cars, that kinda makes it worth my while. I charge $10 a car, so you\'re looking at $50+ return shipping. (Priorty is usually like $3.80 if you can cram them cars in one of those flat rate boxes)\r\n\r\nWhat generation are the SEs? If they are earlier generation SEs, I can do the voltage bypass, and jumper the resistors, and it will be improved, but the current generation, from the \'66 Vette on, will still be much faster with just a direct FET swap.\r\n\r\nIf you send a MT, make sure you pack it well, I\'ve had people send me those on padded envelopes, and they came with bent axles, so I\'m not completely comfortable with shipping those.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSo if you\'re still interested, let me know, and I\'ll get you my shipping address. You can Paypal me at davesmoejoe@yahoo.com The sooner I get payment, the sooner I can order FETs. I only have a few on hand, but they only take 3-5 days to get here.\r\n\r\nDave'),(37727,'30e22b20a2','[quote:30e22b20a2=\"ph2t\"]not feeling paranoid or anything, lol, but could you do me a fave and wipe this thread?\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7370\r\n\r\nit would be mega kiss your arse appreciated, lol...\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:30e22b20a2]\r\nIt\'s dead. You can take off your foil hat now. :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36352,'0dc69253da','How\'s it going?  I sent you a few e-mails.  It was concerning some parts I\'ve ordered from you.  Did you get them?\r\n\r\nI ordered under the name Robert Wilson.  My e-mail is boho81@yahoo.com'),(22410,'53a42458c5','They came today dude\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  If you have anymore xmod stuff let me know\r\n\r\n  Also you getting rid of your xmod cars?'),(25246,'d3a4b5808d','Hey Pimp,\r\n\r\nDid you receive sumtin in the mail from Team DarkTari last week?\r\n\r\nLemme Know !'),(35062,'ec7cda8218','[quote:ec7cda8218=\"cj\"]My paypal is cjellis@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nThe one black/red kit with 2 XME039R would be $68.00 + $3.00 s&amp;h[/quote:ec7cda8218]\r\n\r\nSounds good cj.  Payday is the 15th, tomorrow, so you should see payment on the 17th or 18th as soon as my check clears.  Thanks again man, I appreciate it.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(34134,'0c9e8fb8b2','Have you gotten it yet? It is embedded within a piece of card-board. I also put a note in there along with the payment (MO)\r\n\r\nLet me know, it\'s been a while.\r\nMaxx'),(23435,'76d268ab9f','[quote:76d268ab9f=\"DarkTari\"]Hey Cavey,\r\n\r\nCan you throw in a few flame stencils with that order of fries please.[/quote:76d268ab9f]Yeah, I can, but you know what? My scanner is broken, and it\'s impossible for me to draw perfectly symetrical flames by hand. I\'ve since realized I don\'t need my computer, and I can just use carbon paper to transfer my pattern to tape.\r\n\r\nI can go ahead and make you like one set now, but ultimately, I\'d like to get a hold of some carbon paper first. (They only sell it at the craft store on the other side of town and my wife forgets to grab me some everytime she\'s there. Remember when you could get carbon paper where ever they sold office supplies. :lol: )\r\n\r\n[quote:76d268ab9f]Question,\r\nYou didn\'t send any with my chassis\'s that you did huh?  :???: \r\n\r\nThanx[/quote:76d268ab9f]Ok, you got me confused, you talking about flames mask? And by the chassis, you mean the RX-7 I\'m doing? \r\n\r\nIf so the RX7 is going out on monday, I\'ll knockj you out a flame mask tomorrow.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25421,'9d28753f5d','[quote:9d28753f5d=\"arch2b\"]thanks.\r\n\r\ni am making custom decals for my rcp track so i am naturally looking to use the logo\'s of the top sites and manufacturer\'s for my project.  these will be 3/4\" to 7/8\" by whatever length and applied by clear packing tape to the inside surface of rcp track rails.  if you already have some made let me know.  \r\n\r\ni just wanted to check in with everyone before making these decals available to everyone in pdf and jpeg formats for downloading (for free ofcourse).\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nraymond (arch2b)[/quote:9d28753f5d]no I don\'t have any decals made out yet.\r\n\r\nI\'m not sure the size you\'re going to want so I\'ll just send you a big version that you can size to whatever you need.\r\nI\'m sending it as a JPG file, if you prefer some other format, let me know.\r\nI\'ll be sending this to: arch2b@comcast.net\r\n\r\nlet me know if that email address is incorrect or if you need anything else.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nScott (CaboWabo)'),(23166,'0790e9234a','awwww whats wrong? don\'t feel like playing at r7r still?\r\n\r\n\r\nThat thread was just getting fun. Then you go and quit in the middle of it.\r\n :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25254,'d106d69f7e','Tell me you have recieved your wheels man.... I shipped em last week, so let me know.  Hope all is good. I shipped em to the addy of your pops.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(25218,'2c1f70acef','well i felt bad and i had that shit layin around. honestly i dont like the jeep on the monster. but the monsters fucking rock dude.\r\n\r\ni shipped it a few hours ago air mail. should take 7days or so.'),(22423,'a407426e84','[quote:a407426e84=\"VooDooMafia\"]OK so far its looking good at me getting those 4 wild char cars for $20 + shipping so thats good (will know for sure in 2 days lol)\r\n\r\n  Hey do you have anymore cars going up on the auction block? if so what you got going up?  I am trying to get an idea of whats left to go and what I need to save for lol.\r\n\r\n  Also I was just on toyeast website and was looking at the micro 1/43 scale F1 cars.\r\n\r\n  They look ok but I am thinking they might need fets? think you might be up for the challange?\r\n\r\n  Damn the way my mind is thinking you can just quit your job and do mods for a living lol.[/quote:a407426e84]Yeah, DT cut me short, he just slated me for the joint project with Cabo, but I have 2 other projects planned, mayeb we\'ll just whip those out as suprises, I don\'t know we\'ll see. :lol: \r\n\r\nYeah you know, I can always take a look at them F-1s, if for any reason I didn\'t feel comfortable I wouldn\'t touch it.\r\n\r\ndave'),(23681,'dbe9b42d32','Great! Send the Hummer to - \r\n\r\nJae Throssel\r\n2513 South Edgewater Drive\r\nFayetteville, NC 28303\r\n\r\nIll try my hardest to get it out on Monday too.\r\n\r\nThanks.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23682,'267722073c','Cool... I\'ll send it. Thanks, man.'),(25718,'a3d510d944','[quote:a3d510d944=\"viperdout\"][quote:a3d510d944=\"crazydave\"][quote:a3d510d944=\"viperdout\"]Dave:\r\n\r\nDid the parts get in yet?\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:a3d510d944]Nah, just ordered them yesterday. Don\'t worry man, I\'ll get this done as fast as possible. Promise.\r\n\r\nAnd I am sorry it\'s taken as long as it has, but you knew I wasn\'t quite prepared when you sent your truck. ;)\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:a3d510d944]\r\n\r\nDave:\r\n\r\nYep, I figured it could take a bit, since it hadn\'t been done before.  How long until the fets get in from digikey?\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:a3d510d944]Either tomorrow or Saturday, which means either way I\'ll be doing it up Sunday, and shipping on Monday.\r\n\r\nSince it\'s taking so long, I\'ll go ahead and put up the money for Priorty mail. You\'ll have it by Wednesday or Thursday.\r\n\r\n\r\nI tried for 3 days to comprehend codesuidae\'s version of the mod, and it\'s just too confusing the way he did it. So I gave in and just did it ph2t\'s way, and that was so much easier.\r\n\r\nWorks great, same power gain you\'d see from a FET modded bit. More than enough torque with Orange motor and Orange gears. I think you\'ll be happy.\r\n\r\nDave'),(36810,'b18f311959','Hey man-\r\n\r\nJust saying hi, haven\'t seen ya round as much as usual. Kids can do that to ya. How is your little one? My little guy is having his first birthday in 3 weeks, can\'t believe it\'s gone by so fast. Santa brought him his first Hot Wheels set for xmas, so he\'s got the bug now. \r\n:-D \r\n\r\nBTW, I successfully modded my Nelly the other night. I was scared shitless I was going to fuck it up, but all went well. All I needed to do was change the direction the power wires entered the Nelly from the battery terminals. I\'m running a McLaren body on the Nelly chassis, and there\'s not a lot of room under there and it felt like I was going to bust out the windshield every time I mounted the body. I was having some binding issues that were affecting the rear suspension, so I made the wires come out the other side. Now I have about a nice short 4cm length leading to the Nelly instead of the full length as supplied being doubled over and wadded into the shell. Is there any danger in just wrapping a little electrical tape around the nelly vs. the shrink-tubing? I just wanted to protect the Nelly pcb and don\'t have a heat gun.\r\n\r\nBeen in full MR02 mode lately, almost more obsessively than I ever was with bits.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35387,'d96223b11f','Hey I am going to send you my ZZMT if you can could you tri cell it for me too I am getting a li-po pack but not for a few weeks I don\'t have pay-pal so if you can send me your address I can shoot you the cASH AND zzmt AT THE SAMETIME.'),(24628,'51ca333fb6','Nothing Red plz I hate red'),(32276,'47f8ea0b42','Hi,\r\n\r\nI will be shipping out your micro rc stuff out tomorrow. I got sidetracked with a bunch of other things. Oh yeah and I made a mistake on listing up a white mini cooper set. Its not white but an off white cream color. Let me know if you want to make a switch on the colors. \r\n\r\nI have 4 different ones left including the cream/off white color cooper and I also have a pea green or some really weird color green with black hood, clear/see through cooper body and also a baby blue with white doors police cooper. Let me know which one you want. \r\n\r\nThanks again and sorry about the listing error. \r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nJDM'),(32277,'38e2cb25e6','[quote:38e2cb25e6=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hi,\r\n\r\nI will be shipping out your micro rc stuff out tomorrow. I got sidetracked with a bunch of other things. Oh yeah and I made a mistake on listing up a white mini cooper set. Its not white but an off white cream color. Let me know if you want to make a switch on the colors. \r\n\r\nI have 4 different ones left including the cream/off white color cooper and I also have a pea green or some really weird color green with black hood, clear/see through cooper body and also a baby blue with white doors police cooper. Let me know which one you want. \r\n\r\nThanks again and sorry about the listing error. \r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nJDM[/quote:38e2cb25e6]\r\n\r\nThe cream color sounds good, but I would like to swap out one color... I\'d like the pea green instead of the yellow. So, the final mini cooper list will be...\r\n\r\nred fire chief \r\nwhite/green police car \r\noff white/cream\r\npale yellow \r\npea green \r\nmint green \r\nblack \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24249,'0636506763','Sorry dude. I meant to post in the comments section and I thought the bidding was in 3$ increments not 3$ or more.\r\n\r\nMy bad. I punished myself don;t worry.\r\n\r\n:)'),(34117,'2d697e2c91','y do you hate me'),(23811,'9fd2168ddb','you got aim dude? im keeph42'),(22436,'37d36a3774','[quote:37d36a3774=\"VooDooMafia\"]Sounds good to me \r\n\r\nthanks\r\n\r\nI will get these cars and shit off as soon as I get your addy\r\n\r\nPete[/quote:37d36a3774]Oh yeah, shit I\'m always forgeting shit lately. :lol: \r\n\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd. #1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033'),(35447,'1bb5c00207','Shit If anybody owes anything it\'s me for all of the ideas i get from you Pimps wish I could buy one one Bits that the dem Greman catz do sorry if I came off the wrong way.'),(24981,'f00b4b6ae6','Ok I sent you my 20 bux and I have yet to see anything I got something from someone in Korea and I and he sent the item a week after you and I have it.Look I know that you are far but ok now I am feeling like I am being fucked aroud and that\'s not staight. So thankz for nothing it a 20.00 lesson that will never happen again.'),(22440,'734a657408','[quote:734a657408=\"PINGO\"]on your foto there are paz but were do you have the foto from[/quote:734a657408]I took the picture with my camera.\r\nyou can see more or choose one for your \'avatar\' by clicking on the \"Profile\" link above, and then \"Avatar Gallery\".');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22442,'56f6def5f7','then you have meny homies?'),(22443,'710ac474cb','[quote:710ac474cb=\"PINGO\"]then you have meny homies?[/quote:710ac474cb]yes, I\'m trying to get 1 of each. :grin:'),(22444,'710ac474cb','[quote:710ac474cb=\"PINGO\"]then you have meny homies?[/quote:710ac474cb]yes, I\'m trying to get 1 of each. :grin:'),(34129,'c4d883936c','[quote:c4d883936c=\"Chrome\"]you\'re the real deal; a fucking retard who has no idea he\'s retarded.[/quote:c4d883936c]\r\n\r\n[quote:c4d883936c=\"SHAUN\"]im not a fucking retard. Do you like my crawler project.[/quote:c4d883936c]\r\n\r\nI rest my case.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(22447,'0d084173b7','cool hehe where do you buy them'),(22448,'1786de7155','[quote:1786de7155=\"PINGO\"]cool hehe where do you buy them[/quote:1786de7155]mainly from gumball machines and www.homies.tv or trading other users in the forum.'),(22449,'1786de7155','[quote:1786de7155=\"PINGO\"]cool hehe where do you buy them[/quote:1786de7155]mainly from gumball machines and www.homies.tv or trading other users in the forum.'),(24481,'7a2b01aa4d','[quote:7a2b01aa4d=\"z-beam\"]2482.... Mullumbimby... Australia... see how much it would be :???: \r\n\r\n thanks for the effort...[/quote:7a2b01aa4d]\r\n\r\nI forgot to ask you....\r\n\r\nDo you care if I take it out of the box to save on shipping for you?\r\n\r\nDo you want a hummer or a jeep or both?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29804,'6aa1582fd2','Whats up dude?\r\n\r\nBy any chance do you have an extra ZZ SE 2005 Mustang shell laying around that you may want to sell.....preferably silver?\r\n\r\nThanks doggie.'),(28485,'d62504b877','I know right, thats why I stopped buying Thunderchargers, all of mine ended up being parts cars.'),(29469,'e6a7b4cafb','[quote:e6a7b4cafb=\"CaboWabo\"]Just making sure I got it right:\n\n\n\nJay Bailey\n\n105 Mayfield Lane\n\nWest Mifflin, PA 15122\n\n\n\n\n\nThat right?[/quote:e6a7b4cafb]\n\nYup... that\'s me!'),(29470,'19bcdfaef7','For some reason it\'s not workin.  Its the .. All files uploaded, then could not be uploaded.'),(36364,'e2d7dd524b','You should have got a PM from me. That is weird.\r\n\r\nYes, I got your payment, but was unable to get to the hobby shop today and get those items I ordered. I will be able to get them tomorrow, and will ship your stuff out tomorrow. Everything is boxed up and ready to go, but I\'m still looking through some of my boxes to make sure there isn\'t some parts laying around here. I think I\'ve got it all.\r\n\r\nAnyway, Thanks a lot man. I will send you a tracking number as soon as I get it shipped. This week we are preparing for a boat show, and I just got done driving boats to the convention center all afternoon. Fun fun.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(35021,'0fbd95b247','[quote:0fbd95b247=\"pimpsmurf\"]Any word, big bird? I haven\'t got a response from email.\r\n\r\nWhat\'s up?\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:0fbd95b247]\r\n\r\nhey man, when did ya send the email?  I must of missed it, lots of spam lately.   I finally finished a batch of deluxes this weekend.  Your 2nd one will hit the old post office later today (7:20am at the moment, sitting in my jocks at the PC, lol.....), I\'ll let you know when it has left my hands.....\r\n\r\nslacka...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24002,'7ec5a2b15d','OK I had all that stuff but no chassie, I tosses another pullback chassie in there though.'),(24003,'9c4850d5d9','cool, I shipped it this afternoon, so it\'ll be there.'),(26497,'ca5d739121','I found another 2F2F Camaro/Challenger kit I\'ll throw in...no extra cost.\r\n\r\nLata doggie'),(25159,'d308b58b61','dude sorry i didnt reply. i lost my job and my internet got cut for a little bit.\r\nI just packed up everything you got in the auction and a few extra bodies(jeep and supra) and a purple nos motor for the undue wait. a 27mhz thunder charger controller and an nkok charger are in there. i tested the car and controller just before packaging.\r\n[img:d308b58b61]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10003/tdude.jpg[/img:d308b58b61]\r\n\r\nagain I apologize for the delay and will pay a few extra bucks for express mail if I can.'),(24690,'a12b20ac6b','I got those parts to fix the range problems so now I just need to find something that will show me what to replace and have everything ready for there arrival :)'),(32951,'abc67152ba','No way. It\'s all about the alloy!  The alloy rear gearbox conducts a fantastic amount of heat off of the motor can! I\'m going to make a alluminum shim to replace the 8/9 shim that goes between the motor and rear gearbox. =)\r\n\r\nI\'m going to make a low turn motor on this silver comm arm and get another atomic can for it. I\'m aiming for around 35-40 mph, which may not even be possible, but we will see.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I finally got the spider FET boards in today. I underestimated shipping (I just got back from the Post Office, and it was $36 not counting the box and peanuts). That sucks, but it is going to be shipped today (I have to wrap the box in brown paper as per shipping regulations. =(\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22469,'a2c5fd8483','That impala is sick.........\r\n\r\nI would like to feature it in the mag when complete, if you are interested in writing up a little article covering the making of and finished ride.\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRipper'),(22470,'a2c5fd8483','That impala is sick.........\r\n\r\nI would like to feature it in the mag when complete, if you are interested in writing up a little article covering the making of and finished ride.\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRipper'),(22467,'f04b8c12ff','[code:1:f04b8c12ff]&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;html&gt;\r\n&lt;head&gt;\r\n&lt;title&gt;Untitled Document&lt;/title&gt;\r\n&lt;meta http-equiv=&quot;Content-Type&quot; content=&quot;text/html; charset=iso-8859-1&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;meta http-equiv=&quot;refresh&quot; content=&quot;15;URL=http&#58;//ca.geocities.com/stoli-boy@rogers.com/&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;/head&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;body&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;You are being re-directed to&#58; &lt;a href=&quot;http&#58;//ca.geocities.com/stoli-boy@rogers.com/&quot;&gt;http&#58;//ca.geocities.com/stoli-boy@rogers.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/body&gt;\r\n&lt;/html&gt;[/code:1:f04b8c12ff]\r\n[quote:f04b8c12ff=\"Stoli\"]Hey dude. \r\n\r\n          need a favour again. I need a redirect scropt to load on my rogers.com www site. As of Dec 31/04 its all gone. I just finished redoing Taylors shiat and renaming everything since geocities don;t support spaces/&amp;/ and \' in names of files. ( stoopid)\r\n\r\nanyways the new site addy that I want redirection to is\r\n\r\nhttp://ca.geocities.com/stoli-boy@rogers.com/\r\n\r\ncould you make it like a 15-20 second redirect with link so people can ready WHY its changing.\r\n\r\nThanx mang\r\n\r\nJ  :-)[/quote:f04b8c12ff]'),(22487,'af48224d4a','np\'s man i just felt abandoned  :-( \r\n\r\njust joking  :cool:  (btw i love these emoticcons LOL)\r\n\r\nokay heres my exact address\r\n\r\n39 Moate ave \r\nBrighton le Sands\r\nSydney NSW\r\n2216\r\nAustralia\r\n\r\nhit us back with postage and ill pay ya right away\r\n\r\ncheers\r\n :D');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22489,'e06a24883d','okay that explains it  :???: \r\n\r\nyeah cabo got in contact with me, ill hit up crazy dave now for the paypal and shipping cost\r\n\r\ncheers\r\n\r\n :D'),(37812,'84596b0399','hey man, is that fireball motor for an 1:18 or 1:10?  If its 1:18 and works well ill take i for $10\r\n\r\nSTG'),(27639,'5c9b9519eb','[quote:5c9b9519eb=\"viperdout\"]Dave:\r\n\r\nFor some reason my MT\'s only running for 30 seconds off of a charge.  What did a I manage to fry, and would charging it with my Pirahna charger fix it?  Thanks for any help, and to make it clear, it\'s my fault, and I don\'t expect any warranty, just wondering if my new Pirahna will fix the problem.\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:5c9b9519eb]Good, I\'m glad you said it\'s your fault, I always feel obligated to fix every car I\'ve ever worked on. :lol: \r\n\r\nSound to me like a fried battery. Could you have possibly overcharged it? Or, you know, NiMH don\'t like to be stored with no voltage in them. You should not run them all the way down like with a NiCd. Since the FETs are more efficient, that can be a problem, you don\'t realize the battery is almost fully drained, because it doesn\'t have as much of that lag at the end of the runtime.\r\n\r\nI would not reccomend the Pirahna charger, just for the simple reason that I\'ve seen 2 people destroy their cars by using it. Both guys claimed that the charger would go down to 500mah, but apparently either it don\'t, or both guys used the wrong setting. I don\'t know, never seen one of those chargers first hand.\r\n\r\nIf you let the battery sit for couple days, it might stabilize, and it should read 2.4v when stabilized. If that don\'t work it\'s more than likely fried, but charging at a consistant rate, until the battery is slightly warm, and discharging at a constant rate. (i.e. bulb discharger, or running your car with no load.), may train your battery to get decent runtimes again, but honestly, it\'ll probably never be the same.\r\n\r\nSo check your battery, and let me know what up. I\'ve got some batteries from clone cars laying around.\r\n\r\nDave'),(22491,'6edd07dd3a','i know this might be askin a bit much so you dont have to do it.\r\n\r\ni need a new zip zap se batt, if i give you the money could you get one with me so when you ship the auction item or you have to do is put it with the package.\r\n\r\nif you can cool if you cant its cools.\r\n\r\ncheers man\r\n :D');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22492,'61027e7050','[quote:61027e7050=\"TallduDe\"]i know this might be askin a bit much so you dont have to do it.\r\n\r\ni need a new zip zap se batt, if i give you the money could you get one with me so when you ship the auction item or you have to do is put it with the package.\r\n\r\nif you can cool if you cant its cools.\r\n\r\ncheers man\r\n :D[/quote:61027e7050]Aww man, I got 2 of those batteries and I promised 1 to VDM.  I gots ta keep one for myself. :lol:\r\n\r\nI\'m gonna get more one day, I\'ll keep you in mind. 8-) \r\n\r\nDave'),(25731,'1df1791322','[quote:1df1791322=\"viperdout\"] Have you seen the Superslick Monsters yet?  I\'m really curious about those.  \r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:1df1791322]Yeah I\'ve seen pictures of them. I thought they were dotrky looking, don\'t remember why, but hey, who knows, they just might have some modding potential.\r\n\r\nDave'),(23093,'20cfef87ed','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pimpbox/1.mp3\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pimpbox/2.mp3\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pimpbox/3.mp3\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pimpbox/4.mp3\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pimpbox/5.mp3'),(22494,'c6d90c5caf','Hey, just to let you know... my boy sg219 owed me a favor for a little wiring job I did for him so he sent out that fat tire set... So be expecting it to come with his patented \"sg stuff\" label lol..');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22495,'a89ba77648','Are you still getting the stuff?'),(26277,'96ac5d7d05','Sdog???\r\n\r\nWassappenin, man?\r\n\r\nwhat up?'),(36109,'78503dd36e','how the fuck do you know about unbelieveable r/c then? Thats the forum that hosts it :grin:'),(37124,'1be69b7c98','He kinda makes ya miss charlie huh? :lol:'),(22497,'b57231e293','[quote:b57231e293=\"Stoli\"]Thanx Dude. You rule\r\n\r\n\r\nI have kept this in my \"HTML Stash From Scott\" Won;t bug ya again for it.[/quote:b57231e293]no problem man'),(31459,'87bf49a086','What\'s the problem/error you\'re getting?\r\n\r\nIf you\'re trying to direct link to the image url, Tiny turned that off (so that people don\'t eat his bandwidth).\r\n\r\nIs that what you mean? Or is something else going on?'),(26565,'459c110cb6','Ok...so thats $100 smackers total. I\'m packing the stuff as we speak.'),(31471,'6915eb2ffb','Spiffy!'),(23845,'ca1155a54b','ill install yahoo im whadaretard'),(22510,'f6d777d6e9','LOL\r\n\r\nWell I\'m working on a list, or actually once I get the paying work done I\'m going to make a list of all the people that want to contribute then I will contact them and find out what they can contribute and then make a list of that then plan the issues, so I guess what I\'m trying to say in a retarded tired way is your now on the list.....  So far it\'s a pretty short list but I still have to spread the gospel to all the forums, except of course for that blue freakin one that we all love to hate\r\n\r\n\r\nttyl\r\nRipper');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22511,'f6d777d6e9','LOL\r\n\r\nWell I\'m working on a list, or actually once I get the paying work done I\'m going to make a list of all the people that want to contribute then I will contact them and find out what they can contribute and then make a list of that then plan the issues, so I guess what I\'m trying to say in a retarded tired way is your now on the list.....  So far it\'s a pretty short list but I still have to spread the gospel to all the forums, except of course for that blue freakin one that we all love to hate\r\n\r\n\r\nttyl\r\nRipper'),(26293,'de0cfef53f','Your wallpapers are up in the wallpapers thread man. I didn\'t use the hotties you asked for but I think the ones I used should do fine. Let me know what ya think. :-)'),(26295,'b2323c3f14','Mazda787b@gmail.com  \r\n\r\nShipping shouldn\'t be more than a few $.'),(26296,'413cc8f8e9','That\'s great. I\'ll try to send $20-25. Ill try to do that tomorrow, Ill need your name and shipping address so that I can purchase the MO.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(29026,'a806f23342','Thanks for the opportunity to sell them on your site.  I can\'t believe the response I have had on these engines. I just have a couple of questions for you about your web site.  Do you know approx. how many hits you get on your site a month?  Also are you linked on any other web sites and finally do you sell your items on EBAY. \r\n\r\n\r\nthanks Bio');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30048,'4227ab35b9','swg you can have the revevier for $5 plus $2 for shipping . you can paypal personal check or money order . or id take a bit or zz in trade for it since i dont have many cars anymore ...'),(25074,'a0b04ffdfd','yep, took it apart to get the pic in my gallery.  needless to say a pain in the ass to get it back together.  need smaller fingers i guess.  why do you ask?'),(37159,'7aa516206a','That is Exactly what I wanted. Thanx a bunch man!! :-o\r\nNephew loves it too'),(32306,'4e8b8f1588','GO FRIZZO!!!! WOOO!!!\r\n\r\ni didnt tell you, you have to pass this crazy initiation to be a pimp... im kidding, welcome to da hood! :)'),(27429,'adc14fc199','Hey, I moved your Super Slicks thread to Misc. Micro RC, because the performance shop is for modifications, and because of the larger scale we do not group Super Slicks with Bits/Zips.\r\n\r\ndave'),(25648,'82b74f7e14','I think we need a comment post for the contest.  I can see it gettin away already.......... :sad:'),(27426,'24f55efc1b','[quote:24f55efc1b=\"seeberg\"]http://anytoys.co.uk/category_info.php/category_id/57\r\n\r\nIt\'s anytoys UK, right?  I checked, and shit, I did get the last Trueno.  But not to worry.  I\'m working on a way to fix all that.[/quote:24f55efc1b]\r\n\r\nHey bro, no worries! I got my order placed on Friday, so it\'s all good. Yeah, looks like between the two of us, we cleaned them out. AE86\'s are damn near impossible to find now. About the only thing left for someone wanting one is to buy the Initial D set. I have a friend who has the Trueno Tuneup box for sale. It\'s used, and she wants $40, but I might bite.\r\n\r\nI\'ll let you know how my order with Anytoys works out. They better be cool considering how freakin much that cost us.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25372,'5f6acc11c8','Hi thanks for your reply, But do you have any idea how i can fix the tab,as i have lost the peice that snapped off?\r\n\r\nPEACE :cool:'),(25373,'7e80b316f4','can u do mosfet on my zip zap se'),(24517,'dc7a7347d9','From amn to man I am sorry what made me want that car was everthing about it i was willing to pay whatever but as I said my wife got hit by a car and well all the money we had at the time went to pay for stuff ans now the i\'ll have the cash this weekend my pimped car is gone  yea if you can hook a pimp up.'),(37224,'7ddecc7cbc','http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/index.php?showtopic=35943&amp;pid=353400&amp;st=15&amp;#entry353400'),(34983,'ea16ba21c6','Much obliged.'),(34984,'3a06c5b749','a few small things like a bumper and some foams, that\'s about it.'),(34985,'b9a736f5a4','ok I want the foams too, new and used.\r\n\r\nI thought you said that you had a 540 micro? Do you still have it? I need a rear ball differential, maybe some electronics etc.\r\n\r\nI definately want the foams along with the other stuff i mentioned in the previous PM.\r\nI think i\'m gunna ask around for some stock electronics. and maybe one of your kits.\r\n\r\nWhen i get home I\'ll send you a definitive PM.\r\nThanx a bunch\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(32734,'9b95611792','Yeah I had it from a trade we did in the past.  You should get your shipment in the next few days.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nFinks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32032,'3b4c822356','Cost of shipping and 2 bucks and its a deal! this is the upgrade kit with the red RX7 and the Green Eclipse. Freight it about $2.50 for box if you want it priority it will be $3.85 \r\n\r\nthanks bud\r\nAaron'),(36897,'6781c6d73c','Chassis?...lol....any of those are good, you choose what you will want to give away,,, I am ready to pack when you are man.'),(36900,'088a7b15c4','I found a CNC mill at the local polytechnic, so I\'ll be checking that out. I may also work in aluminium cuz it may be cheaper. I have a really bad sketch of how I want the chassis, I\'ll post it up on the forum.'),(37855,'b511e68d8c','No prob, I\'ve got plenty of micro stuff from skylinekid to keep me busy....thanks again! :-)'),(36910,'b8c02eee90','Nice, thanks!'),(26426,'3671054dd4','If you could hold off til the New Year, I would be happy to take that off your hands.\r\n\r\nSorry.\r\n\r\nI wish things could be more simple, but my ass is in a hole.  Sorta.  I usually get paid every other friday.  Well P-day falls on New Years Eve.  I\'m not sure if the checks are going to show up a day early or if I\'m going to have to wait until next week to deposit it.\r\n\r\nSenerio #1: I could get it this this weekend or early next week. But I could proabably only get you half this weekend and the other half the weekend of the 14th. (next P-day)\r\n\r\n Senerio #2: If you can hold it till the weekend of the 14th, that would be awsome!!  I\'d pay you all at once.\r\n\r\nSenerio #3: It\'s up to you pimp.  If you need the cash, [b:3671054dd4]PLEASE, seriously,[/b:3671054dd4] don\'t wait for me.  It\'s no biggie.   :cool: \r\n\r\nLet me know.   Thanks again for the offer. :-)'),(25932,'e12f295188','Xray Kit for $60 + $6.85 S+H\r\n\r\n[url]http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5938153126&amp;rd=1[/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27843,'4d65a5eb3e','my adress is \r\n\r\nmatt evink\r\n25085 cr 388\r\nGobles , Mi 49055\r\n\r\nill send the body whenever you want me to ( tomorow would work fine ) thanks .\r\n\r\nmatt'),(24603,'fc98197bff','Thanx Pimp !'),(35538,'fee706bfdf','[quote:fee706bfdf=\"crazydave\"][quote:fee706bfdf=\"hue35\"]Now I\'mm gonna go home and :cool:  &lt;--- except smokeless.  :lol:   Man, I\'m lovin\' this vaporizer... I haven\'t \"smoked\" anything since I got it, and my lungs can tell the difference.[/quote:fee706bfdf]Shit man, I think my lungs need one of them. I\'ve been afraid to look at them, because I\'m pretty shure they\'re more than the wife would allow for paraphernalia. :lol: [/quote:fee706bfdf]\r\nThey can be had for about $150 on ebay... the vaporbrothers one, which is the one SF and I have.\r\n\r\n[quote:fee706bfdf=\"crazydave\"]Well gald you like the start on the car. I was actually just sitting down to take a break on it. I\'m finishing up the chassis getting ready for paint. Just carved it out for the Super Slick motor.[/quote:fee706bfdf]\r\nOh man, a Super Slick motor... it\'s gonna haul ass. I still haven\'t put one of those in a Bit yet... I have a couple, though. I\'ve got some parts set aside for a tiny little demon for the RCP... now I just need some time.\r\n\r\n[quote:fee706bfdf=\"crazydave\"]My wife just brought a big bag of peanuts in the shells from one of those dudes on the side of the road, and they rock. :rockon:[/quote:fee706bfdf]\r\nSounds good... we don\'t have peanut vendors on the side of the road here, though I wish we did. We\'ve got \"fresh crab\" guys, but I have a hard time buying seafood from a dude on the side of the road.'),(37322,'986246db26','I was wondering if you would be a moderator on my froum. I thinkin you\'ll prolly say no because you hate me.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37323,'986246db26','I was wondering if you would be a moderator on my froum. I thinkin you\'ll prolly say no because you hate me.'),(37324,'cacb7ce261','[quote:cacb7ce261=\"SHAUN\"]I was wondering if you would be a moderator on my froum. I thinkin you\'ll prolly say no because you hate me.[/quote:cacb7ce261]\r\nI don\'t hate ya man.\r\nBut I am going to have to turn down the offer, I just don\'t have time between work, life, and bitPimps.'),(36084,'e6502f62ea','[quote:e6502f62ea]OMFG,DT!!! :shock: Why are you just ignoring the last several posts? ... yeah, welcome to the dilemma, PIMP! You just passed on participating in 6 posts worth of trying to solve the dilemma... what is it, your way or the highway? Welp, the highway is starting to look pretty fuckin\' good to me at this point. It\'s hard enough trying to work out issues in this format without the passive-aggressive bullshit.\r\n\r\nedit: Adding up the votes through Payaso\'s vote, I get the following..\r\n\r\n[b:e6502f62ea]70 points[/b:e6502f62ea]\r\n[img:e6502f62ea]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/contest_entries/11/thumb_04_steelwoolghandi_1.jpg[/img:e6502f62ea]\r\n\r\n\r\n[b:e6502f62ea]65 points[/b:e6502f62ea]\r\n[img:e6502f62ea]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/contest_entries/11/thumb_15_45tr0_1.jpg[/img:e6502f62ea][/quote:e6502f62ea]\r\n\r\n\r\n[b:e6502f62ea]55 points[/b:e6502f62ea]\r\n[img:e6502f62ea]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/contest_entries/11/thumb_18_sporttracguy_2.jpg[/img:e6502f62ea]\r\n\r\nDid you add 15 points to STG\'s blue truck because crazydave was considering changing his vote?[/quote]\r\n\r\nThat Hue is pretty High Strung  :lol:   :lol:   :lol:   :lol: \r\n\r\nI Luv It !!!!'),(34650,'b7233db13e','Sorry you\'re so busy man, just tryin\' to jump on MSN with ya to see what else ya need as far as Bits go. Ya must be talking to a lot of people.\r\n \r\nI wanted to send the package out today, but no problem. There\'s always tomorrow.\r\nSee ya');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34109,'c0323dd612','What is the stock voltage limit on a firelap 04 You can run li-pos safely right.\r\n\r\nIf i would be able to rum higher voltages would have to add resistors on the steering - and + wires correct? What value? would 10 kohm be allright?\r\n\r\nAny help would be appreciated.'),(32979,'71fd6a5aef','as of now, i dont do many electrical mods, mainly because if i mess it up, i cant buy another bit. (my parents wont let me... :evil: ) (im only 14) but then again i dont want an insanly fast bit, i cant control it and they are sometimes not fun to drive. but i am thinking of selling my 1:10 scale off-road buggy car, so i can take the extra $250 or so and by some bits/epochs. then i might FET some of the cars... :grin: what else can i do to make the car faster? :???:'),(30095,'95ec7225a2','A review would be great, I\'d like post it in the DC mod section of my website if you dont\' mind.\r\n\r\nInstallation instructions are linked on the main menu of my website, http://codesuidae.net  Look over on the right side, near the bottom of the main menu.\r\n\r\nI need to update the pictures though, the power wire should be connected to the voltage booster for a 3V supply, not to the battery, as shown.\r\n\r\nI\'ll get a couple put together and ready to go.'),(32224,'299649cd84','sorry man, I posted SOLD and forgot to tell you it\'s yours!\r\n\r\nyou must have been like, \'what the hell, it better be me he sold it to\' :lol: \r\n\r\nIf ya don\'t mind, we\'ll work out the details tomorrow.\r\nThe truth, I\'ve been up all frickin\' night and can\'t think straight \'cause I\'m so tired. No, not speed induced or anything, just havin fun.\r\n\r\nAnd thanks for fillin me in on those chase sets!! THATS the description I was looking for. Perfect!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34510,'50135422c4','[quote:50135422c4=\"crazydave\"][quote:50135422c4=\"CaboWabo\"]Glad someone caught the hint.\r\nI\'ve got 9401 posts and hate to keep increasing that over posts that I think most will ignore.\r\nIt\'s almost embarrassing, think about when I hit 10K and we\'ve only got 70+K posts all together.\r\nThat = gay.[/quote:50135422c4]Well you know, I can see where you\'re embarrassed having almost 10k post, \'cause I\'m feeling a little awkward just hitting 4k. :lol: \r\n\r\nBut the reality, in my opinion, is, at TRC we never really saw tiny, but here I think it always made people feel special that the admin always took the time to welcome everyone, and I think most people are attracted to your personality. So I wouldn\'t worry too much about your post count, you\'re the admin, its your place, you can do what ever you want. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:50135422c4]\r\nI\'ve even gone back and deleted some of my really old and super useless posts, but at this point it\'s like shooting an elephant with a spit-ball. It ain\'t makin no dents. :lol: \r\nAhh well.'),(31215,'8e3e99189a','for the things you are selling if you decide to sell the s2 engines let me know...i just want the red or blue one');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31216,'c118e2d208','[quote:c118e2d208=\"suprakid95\"]for the things you are selling if you decide to sell the s2 engines let me know...i just want the red or blue one[/quote:c118e2d208]\r\n\r\nWell, I\'m not home right now, so I dunno if I still have the motors, but when I get home (July 10th or so) I can look.'),(28652,'896fe0de74','[quote:896fe0de74=\"backdrift\"]I did not say it was a flaw in bitpimps, just someone that came here via my history...[/quote:896fe0de74]And I\'m just saying that it\'s very unlikely that someone came here via your history.\r\nAnd even if they did, they couldn\'t do anything malicious to you through bitPimps.'),(34556,'0f630b354d','[quote:0f630b354d=\"crazydave\"]Go ahead and tell me, its a cool Phat Boy, but I can live without. :lol: \r\n\r\nAhhh nevermind don\'t tell me. I\'ll hang out, and if no one gets it in a day or so, then I\'ll go ahead and throw my guess out.\r\n\r\nI just wanted to show you I knew the car. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave[/quote:0f630b354d]\r\nToo late, fuckin Bilbo nailed it already. :lol:'),(28516,'5079215a8a','Hey,\r\nYou got the MT parts yet? If not they\'ll be there today, because it only took Sat and Mon for the skyline to get to me, so the MT parts shoud be there today. \r\nThanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36217,'cb6ecec1ae','[quote:cb6ecec1ae=\"sessiz\"]I seem to remember something about you having a design company or doing bussiness in the &quot;graphic design&quot; area. If I\'m wrong disregard this pm. :lol: \r\n\r\nHere\'s where I need your help/advice. I have a chance at a job as a low level graphics &quot;guy&quot; for transworld entertainment corp. My cousin is a lead tech guy over there and he is getting me a foot in the door. (director of marketing owes him big  :lol: )\r\nWhat I need from you is a tip or two on what exactly should I put together potfolio wise to show this guy. I got a rough idea of what this cat wants to see and I feel gay as fuck typing this shit but any help from you would be much apreciated.  :-)[/quote:cb6ecec1ae]\r\n\r\nNope, you got it right, that\'s what I do.\r\n\r\nWhat kind of job is it? What kind of graphic work? Is it more of a creative position or a technical position? How soon is your interview? Do you have samples of any work other than what I\'ve seen here?\r\n\r\nI\'m happy to help a brutha out as much as possible. If you have enough time, I can help you get a portfolio together. I interview at least 20 people a year, so I see all kinds of stuff. Here\'s some portfolio things to consider right off the bat:\r\n\r\n- Not too much and not too little in content. Like more than 10 pieces and less than 20.\r\n\r\n- Be able to tell a story about each of your pieces. What was the point of the project? what were you trying to accomplish? What problems did you encounter and how did you solve them?\r\n\r\n- Include something that shows your thought process, like a sketch that led to a finished piece, or three options you generated before developing a final piece.\r\n\r\n- Start with the thing you think is your &quot;best&quot; work, and finish with the thing that is your &quot;favorite&quot; piece.\r\n\r\n- Have a sample sheet with 2 or 3 of your best things on an 8.5 x 11 sheet to clip to your resume, so they can remember who you are.\r\n\r\n- If you don\'t have a lot or any real-world work to show, invent your own. Find some ad or design that you think could be done better and do it up. Along these lines, I routinely show work in my portfolio that was rejected by clients. Sometimes we generate good designs that they don\'t pick. Doesn\'t mean it wasn\'t good. The people you show your portfolio to will never know the difference.\r\n\r\nNow I feel all gay, but if you answer some of those questions I can help you more. If you have enough time, I have a kick-ass color printer and a Fed-Ex account, I might be able to help you get it printed up in some cool little portfolio.\r\n\r\nIf you want to check out our incomplete website, you can see where I left off last summer:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.grymttr.com/flashtest/\r\n\r\nOnly the &quot;enviro&quot; and &quot;collateral&quot; sections are hooked up, but I hope to finish the rest before this summer. \r\n\r\nSuperFly'),(31122,'0006b7b78e','OK, here\'s my final list...\r\n\r\n\r\nsilver supra 45mhz $15 \r\nred enzo ferrari 40a mhz $15 \r\nskyline history set 35mhz $15\r\nferrari special set f40, testarrossa and 512bb 40b mhz $25\r\nspecial edition pennzoil skyline 27mhz $15\r\n\r\nyellow lambo/red ferrari 27c $8\r\nblack lambo/silver ferrari 27a $8\r\n\r\nDome Zero $3\r\n\r\nMini Heart Mini Cooper sets:\r\nwhite  $10\r\ndark green  $10\r\nwhite w/blue police light on roof  $10 \r\n\r\nQTY 1 200mah battery $1.50 \r\nQTY 1 160mah battery $.75 \r\nQTY 4 perfection 3.8 motor $2ea \r\nperfection heatsinks - QTY 2 black, QTY 2 gold, QTY 1 silver $.50ea \r\nQTY 3 perfection 4.2 motor $2ea\r\n\r\n\r\nI came up with a total of 152.75... \r\n\r\nThere\'s a few things in the list that are more than I\'d want to spend, but I\'m still interested in... I can weed those things out, which is no problem, but I\'ll offer you $125 (via PayPal) for this list as is, shipped to Portland, OR 97201.\r\n\r\nThanks again, \r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28968,'50fa662a93','This would be a great charger, will do all your batteries.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.aircraft-world.com/shopexd.asp?id=3001\r\n\r\nthis is another good one: (bit cheaper too)\r\n\r\nhttp://www.rcmart.com/catalog/product_info.php?cPath=421_37_53&amp;products_id=11309\r\n\r\nYou can buy those cheap li-ion/li-poly chargers that atomicwankers sell (and a plethora of othe xmod online stores) BUT the problem is that they charge at a minimum of about 500mA.  With lipo you MUST charge at 1C.  So the bummer is that you need a charger that will do 80mA for the real small lipo I gave you.  Both chargers listed above will charge at a minimum of 100mA.  This is fine.  I use the SWALLOW charger (same as the Kokam) and it works a treat on the smal mAh lipo\'s.  I\'ve now sold it to betty and I\'m getting the duratrax intellipeak one from towerhobbies.\r\n\r\nEither of those two chargers above are great for any batteries for 1:18 scale and smaller...\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nmatt.'),(28971,'612b738248','Hello!\r\n\r\nI think it would be better to order that stuff from radioshack.com.It would be easier 2 U,and its written that they\'re shipping for free over 50$ :smile: .I know it would cost 64$,I can send you money,and thats all :grin: !\r\nWhat do you think?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35568,'8cb3d7cd22','You\'re better off buying both car and truck. The truc chassis is significantly slower than the car. I just came from driving my nephew\'s EVO and I absolutely love it. It feels sooo much smoother than the Gen1. It\'s quieter, torquier, lower truning radius etc. If you want the truck, get both. Cuz the car is the one to race with. \r\n\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(36516,'88077d0e34','What exactly do you got under the hood of your subie in your thread?\r\n\r\nLooks sweet and i think it mentioned you have some sort of electronics thread. I would like to know my options further. Thank you.'),(37235,'0d9ead6fce','I\'ll see what they have in stock.  As far as returned stuff, I lucked up on that Evo, they don\'t get too much stuff back at the one by the job.\r\nI\'ll letcha know next week sometime!\r\n\r\n :cool:'),(25420,'cdaf83db80','thanks.\r\n\r\ni am making custom decals for my rcp track so i am naturally looking to use the logo\'s of the top sites and manufacturer\'s for my project.  these will be 3/4\" to 7/8\" by whatever length and applied by clear packing tape to the inside surface of rcp track rails.  if you already have some made let me know.  \r\n\r\ni just wanted to check in with everyone before making these decals available to everyone in pdf and jpeg formats for downloading (for free ofcourse).\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nraymond (arch2b)'),(25114,'6d58ebfc0f','Nah we cool I mean I got a ear infection at 36.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23978,'19a4dae508','Hey I still have not got the other xmod thats why I have not done anything yet about that nelly.\r\n\r\n  Is it cool just to get 2 nellys from you and I can just install them myself as I will need to learn this shit sometimes lol.\r\n\r\n  Let me know'),(23593,'a1fa7444f1','Sure I\'ll pick you one up.  They are $19.99 + 7.5% tax = $21.50 approx. + S&amp;H. .........um...about $25.00 U.S. sound good.\r\n\r\nLet me know which one you want and I\'ll see if they have it.  When I went and got mine, they only had a couple to choose from, the Two Skylines, Black and Yellow, and the Two RX-8\'s, Blue and Red.  But they might have gotten more.\r\n\r\nAs far as trading...I want Mini-T Alloy parts right now.  I don\'t think you have any of those lyin\' around. :???: \r\n\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com'),(37701,'9c7cae15d4','no worries, i just need a final price and a paypal address.\r\ni\'ll give you the shipping details when we\'re ready to roll (no cash this week :-( )'),(24403,'5f978322ba','Hi there Sugarfoot,\r\n\r\nCongratulations on your winning bid! lol\r\nAs I believe you have already been told, the original winner of the bid has not paid and so the next highest bid in line wins, that was you!\r\n\r\nI believe DarkTari has already talked to you about this and you have chosen to accept the winning bid?\r\nIf not and I am mistaken, please correct me.\r\n\r\nHowever, if not, you\'ll need some payment information.\r\nYou basically have 2 options available to you.\r\nYou can pay via PayPal to crazydave or you can send Cash or Money Order to myself (CaboWabo), it\'s your choice.\r\nPlease let me know which you prefer so I can get you the neccessary information.\r\n\r\nThanks for helping support the bitPimps Community, it\'s very appreciated by us all.\r\n\r\n- CaboWabo');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36522,'27991f21c3','I just got the order in for the rear gear box/towers.  I chose red, but any color is ok.  You can put the rear alloy axle in with that order to save on shipping if you want.\r\n\r\nThanx again.'),(24429,'96c09cb9aa','[quote:96c09cb9aa=\"DarkTari\"][quote:96c09cb9aa]and dont do it with a [b:96c09cb9aa]dremel [/b:96c09cb9aa] .. [/quote:96c09cb9aa]\r\n\r\nYIKES !  :???:   That Smart ![/quote:96c09cb9aa] :-D   yeah im gonna use a file and exacto blades now :) but thanx for the tip.... Got any more  :smile:'),(24430,'64f49305ed','Whatcha wanna know   :???:'),(25534,'a786331a89','If you get this....Which address was it sent to? Maine or Texas? I\'m moving back to Maine this Thursday, so I wanted to let my brother know that if it shows up, he can send it to me.'),(24402,'d8fc5b50a6','[quote:d8fc5b50a6=\"jrc6805\"]Greetings, \r\nI got a link to your site from payaso, a regular member here.\r\nHe and I are members of bannedr/c.com\r\nAnyway, I am from Belleville, IL. (I noticed you were from StLouis)\r\nI got this x-mod for my step-son who isn\'t the least bit interested. I want to sell it to buy more parts for my Savage. However, the rukes of your site state something about having 50 posts. I do not. Since I am not really into the micros, I do not frequent this forum. I just figured someone into the micros might realize a good deal rather than e-bay for such a small priced item. More trouble that it\'s worth if y\'ask me.\r\nThis x-mod has the stage two motors, and the steering /suspension upgrades. Several tires and wheels and various body parts. I have made it run a couple of times but that\'s it. I traded an old Notro Rustler for this x-mod. \r\nYour help and advice in this matter would be appreciated. I am 39 years old with no intentions of mistreating anyone in any way about this x-mod.\r\nIf you\'d rather, my e-mail is: jonrcoats@hotmail.com\r\n\r\nThanks[/quote:d8fc5b50a6]payaso vouched for ya, you sound legit to me. looks like you\'re already good to go man.\r\ngood luck :-)'),(34495,'295352ed08','[quote:295352ed08=\"Nasphere\"]Hey, I would like to see your PCB layout for the knight rider lights...\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1005&amp;postdays=0&amp;postorder=asc&amp;start=15\r\n\r\nyour pics died.\r\n\r\nAlso, how did you assemble a DC-DC converter for 5V? did you modify the existing one on the PCB?[/quote:295352ed08]\r\n\r\nsorry man, old stuff I don\'t have nay more.\r\n\r\nas for the DCDC convertor, I made it from external components.  check out dcdc charg pump convertors at onsemi.com  that\'s where I got mine froom.  agess ago....\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35165,'c5c7c2c8bf','You\'ve got $71.00 in paypal from jadill@charter.net.  Something was up with my last paycheck, as usual, and it didn\'t clear.  This is my father\'s account so if you need to email me, send mail to wvuchrome@gmail.com.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(25998,'0a2b53f3c4','Yeah, man... that wouldn\'t be a problem... some kind of little trade would be cool for sure. Let me know what you\'d be willing to part with... I\'m sure you have something that I don\'t have or something that I need.\r\n\r\nJay'),(35221,'25b4710086','I\'m sorry CJ, I interpreted on my own that the parts would be shipping sometme early December, so I sent my school address.  Since I saw your post about the shipment on Dec. 15th, I\'m going to need the parts shipped home.\r\n\r\nSean Dill\r\n301 Dominic Drive\r\nScott Depot, WV 25560\r\n\r\nIf you\'d like to refuse payment and have me send it again with the other address, that\'s fine too.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(32609,'2ed845ef50','You want a comp chair?\r\n\r\n***\"For FREE!!\" \r\n\r\nAll you have to do is mod the wheel I have onto the chair.  One wheel is broken, but I have the B/up.It shouldn\'t be hard at all. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n***Must get person high, \"for FREE\". :lol:\r\n\r\n\r\nCall me later if you want the chair.\r\n\r\nAlso....\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nChromes money, $7.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28432,'01d7eb70b7','Hey Man,\r\nThanks for bring that up, I completly forgot about the springs, but sadly I can only find one spring, but I did find the washer\'s for the rims, but still missing a nut though,\r\nMissing List: 1 spring and 1 nut for rim.\r\n\r\nIf it\'s cool with you, I throw in a regular ZZ PCB.\r\nI just need to get rid of this stuff.\r\nIf this deal is ok, what i said today and last night, and You give me Your address today, I can probably ship out by tomorrow and depending on where you live it might be there Sat, or maybe Mon/Tues.\r\nJust let me know if You have any questions, and tell me if I\'m missing anything else. \r\nJust PM me Your address, or if You don\'t want to send it through PM You can email me at: JDMR33@yahoo.com\r\nThank, have a good day'),(28433,'b5019e11ac','Hey Man, \r\nIs everything cool with You about this deal?\r\nJust get back to me and let me know what You want to do, You already got my info, so if this deal is alright with You just give me Your info so I know where to send the MT stuff etc.\r\nThanks\r\nJDM-R34'),(35167,'5edfa88402','Thanks SG, that\'s awesome man.  I\'ll have you mail it to my parent\'s house so I can get it over the break.\r\n\r\nSean Dill\r\n301 Dominic Drive\r\nScott Depot, WV 25560\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36553,'27991f21c3','I just got the order in for the rear gear box/towers.  I chose red, but any color is ok.  You can put the rear alloy axle in with that order to save on shipping if you want.\r\n\r\nThanx again.'),(36554,'a1d228c268','The key is to keep it cool.  I\'ll build you a special Spider (version 2) which is smaller than previous one and a little neater to mount.  I would look at ways you could make it cooler - small stick-on heatsink perhaps?  \r\n\r\nThe FETs will take the current etc pretty much no worries as long as they don\'t overheat.\r\n\r\nYou\'re right about the 02 being a problem for that, there\'s not much air space aroudn the FETs and no venting.\r\n\r\nI\'ll send the order with tyres today and the Spider will go in the next mail - it\'ll be a little special ;)\r\n\r\nA&gt;'),(23950,'bf96eb1704','I wish all my chassies that I have left have controllers and shit.  I tossed the rest in a trade I did awhile back.\r\n\r\n\r\nSo what was the trade you had in mind?'),(23951,'a685ae37f4','for those three bodies? Damn skippy! I\'m not really into ZZ\'s so you can have the whole thing. I was hoping that you would have a chassis with the origional wheels to sweeten the deal, but if not then that\'s cool. I somehow lost you\'re addy. \r\n\r\nMine is\r\nJustin Long\r\n3803 Palmtree Lane\r\nKilleen Texas 76549');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23470,'df81dae55c','[quote:df81dae55c=\"KaNye\"]Very interested. If you would rather discuss via email mine is jae_33@msn.com (other contacts: AIM - HomerS2042, MSN - jae_33@msn.com)[/quote:df81dae55c]We can communicate by email if you\'d like, but honestly, I\'d probably reply faster here.\r\n\r\nMy email is davesmoejoe@yahoo.com. That is my paypal address too, in case you wanted to pay by paypal. You could also include a money order with the cars if you prefer.\r\n\r\nMy address is:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd.\r\nApt.#1131\r\nPhoenix AZ 85033\r\n\r\nI should have the FETs on hand, that is other people asking about mods don\'t send their cars first, but at any rate, as long as I got the FETs on hand I usually have the cars out the following Monday.\r\n\r\nDave'),(27926,'ae0663f840','[quote:ae0663f840=\"Bird\"]plus, I think she\'s going out tonight...[/quote:ae0663f840]\r\n\r\nLet me know..... :-)\r\n\r\nRing the phone................................................. :cool:'),(33952,'2f3723afec','how many hertz is it?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33953,'7d758f1941','35MHz\r\n\r\nyou can\'t get that in america due to their frequency rules. You\'ll have to look to Japan.'),(25184,'835d12afcb','its cool man\r\n\r\ni just thought u forgot me dats all.\r\n\r\ndont worry about fast shipping save urself some cash.\r\n\r\nthanks for the extra shell\'s i always wanted the jeep! will look nice on my new monster.\r\n\r\nthanks for not forgetting me dude.\r\n\r\nthe site is still one of the best going around btw, \r\n\r\ncheers\r\n\r\n :D'),(28116,'31d9d7dc1c','Whats up bitch? How is the Northwest these days?'),(32724,'930ef0efb6','Your sub went out today.  I marked it as a gift hoping to avoid customs charges.  It went letter parcel post, so it will take 4-7 days.  Let me know when you get it.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(27292,'0b6ca1eb92','i think it still works fine. i just havn\'t got the time to sort out and resize pictures . i hope you got space, i\'m yet to upload my mini-zs and xmods :grin: thanks for looking out.\r\nbtw i was loooking at your gallery. your paint jobs are, super.'),(25185,'2c1f70acef','well i felt bad and i had that shit layin around. honestly i dont like the jeep on the monster. but the monsters fucking rock dude.\r\n\r\ni shipped it a few hours ago air mail. should take 7days or so.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34726,'8820aa5cc6','No...'),(28466,'7d6276303f','Hey Man,\r\nI could not ship out today due to the fact that I got to the post office to late, I got there around 1:30 and I know there open on saturdays, maybe they just close early, but I will be shipping out monday, and it should only take a couple days to get to You.\r\nTalk to Ya later'),(26916,'5cca7f0cbd','Dude throw that Hummer up on SGs contest at Rippers.'),(24572,'cc87b036f8','Hey man, Thanx! \r\n\r\n My Address:\r\n\r\nTeam DarkTari\r\n7815 Quill Point Drive\r\nBowie, Md. 20720\r\n\r\nThanx For Da Hook Up !\r\n\r\nHow are you getting the old wheels off the steering knuckles?'),(29344,'950c05bf7e','OK. 3 facts:\r\n\r\n1) I\'m 13.\r\n\r\n2) I have ADHD\r\n\r\n3) I have MEDICATION to treat it, and it works...but I still go crazy on forums.\r\n\r\nJust lettin you know, man ^^\r\n\r\nBy the way, where else can I get paint?'),(34353,'25b5430857',':finger:'),(29313,'6763f2bd4b','Hey man, I just sent you $96.07 via PayPal. The address should show up in the transaction through PayPal, but here it is, just in case:\r\n\r\nMat Mathey\r\n1500 SW 12th Avenue\r\nPortland, OR 97201\r\n\r\nThanks, Finks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26085,'e2d33fbfee','[quote:e2d33fbfee=\"kvik369\"]Not sure if you got my last pm\r\n\r\nsent you another 8 bucks \r\n\r\n[quote:e2d33fbfee=\"crazydave\"]\r\nbut I believe the center one is ground, the drivers side that is usually ground is positive, and the passenger side is the signal to program the frequencies. Since I race by myself I don\'t worry aboutthe frequency it\'s on. \r\n[/quote:e2d33fbfee]\r\nCall me stupid but give me wire colors (driver side??), and freq don\'t matter to me either, so what hooks up to what?\r\nAnd thanks for the quote tip - later \r\nVik[/quote:e2d33fbfee]Oh... shit, I forgot to reply. Call me dumbass.  :lol: \r\n\r\nHaven\'t got down to RS yet, can\'t find my Paypal card, and it takes a few day to tranfer funds to your bank account, but it looks like that\'s what I might have to do.\r\n\r\nI\'ve been so distracted with Christmas coming up... Ya know Playstation 2s are all gone? That kid is gonna be disappointed, but he\'ll get over it. :lol: \r\n\r\nOh and the wires, assuming they\'re all the same, blue is ground, and brown is positive on mine. The center is ground, and the one on the driver side of the car is positive. (If you\'re looking at the bottom of the charge pad, where you\'ll be soldering the wire on, and the arrow is pointing away from you, it\'s on the right.)\r\n\r\nDave'),(25600,'9d480975da','My dad  made me put it up in storage for some reason, he dosnt want me to sell it now or anything he thinks its gunna be worth to much, or wants me to keep it to reamber how old RC\'s used to be. sorry man.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28509,'af9bf4935b','Thanks Man'),(28521,'bddf2ec6b9','Are they just like hotwheels cars or rc cars, and do You know about how much they cost, well I\'ll just head over there soon, but I got to save up for the new GT500 SE, that thing is pimp too, maybe I can get you to paint that shell for me, nice gunmetal or artic silver or something, idk yet.\r\nThanks'),(28344,'df693433da','Bio,\r\n\r\nHope you don\'t mind me Pimp\'n your wares....\r\n\r\nhttp://www.rcuniverse.com/forum/m_2559287/anchors_2709523/mpage_1/key_/anchor/tm.htm#2709523'),(27807,'e41a2dab70','aim... disguise names lol\r\n\r\n :-)'),(37300,'0060ed02be','[quote:0060ed02be=\"cj\"]These were not in the first order.\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver	Black	Green\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	0	0	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.54	0	0	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME330LAN	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR LANCER) - 1PC	$5.90	0	0	1\r\nXME330MUS	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR MUSTANG) - 1PC	$3.84	0	0	1\r\nXET330FORD	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR TRUCKIN) - 1PC	$6.90	1	0	0\r\nXET330HUM	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR HUMMER) - 1PC	$5.90	1	0	0\r\n\r\nActual	$53.54	 	 	 \r\n10.00%	$5.35	 	 	 \r\nSub	$58.89			\r\nS&amp;H	$3.00			\r\nTotal	$61.89			\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.41 Off of GPM\'s regular price.\r\n\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me know as soon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com.  Please include your user name in the notes on PayPal.\r\n\r\nIf you do reply by February 11th  your request will not be ordered.[/quote:0060ed02be]\r\n\r\nJust silver and green.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be able to pay until this Saturday, after P-day clears.\r\n\r\nWhats the status of everything else?  The rest of the silver, all the green and the diffs?\r\n\r\nI need a complete set so I can start putting things together.\r\n\r\nHow much longer?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike'),(32512,'7b9dda0408','Yeah that\'s cool man.  Sorry I can\'t ship it today, but I\'m tied up in a few different things.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34062,'bc89fe2df7','No shit Sherlock.  \"Holy hell, we got us a regular detective here boys!\"  It\'s increasingly obvious you are home-schooled or cyber-schooled or whatever.  You are illiterate, dim-witted, and have an incredible lack of ability to articulate yourself.  I feel bad for you, you are going to end up working the rest of your life in a minium wage job until one day you are found hanging from your ceiling fan with a tipped over chair underneath you in your shitty little trailer.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(34122,'5e7f10aea1','Cause of stupid shit like this.   You are so fuckin thick headed it quit being funny after your first dozen posts.  I thought for real you were some smartass pretending to be a n00b.  No, you\'re the real deal; a fucking retard who has no idea he\'s retarded.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(37367,'fa930aacd3','Talked to my case officer this morning. My Visa has been approved. \r\n\r\nI\'ve got until Oct. 11 to enter :)'),(37368,'ebd12fe243','struth bloke! you must be rich. usually we only let in rich white folk, the rest we tip into the sea! :lol:  (i think our government sucks a little more than yours)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22531,'6f25e8d666','you got it.\r\nonce you login to the Galleries, you should see 3 buttons that allow you to create and manage your albums.\r\n[quote:6f25e8d666=\"chrome\"]Hey Cabo,\r\n\r\nI was wondering If I could have some space in the members gallery?\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...[/quote:6f25e8d666]'),(22532,'6f25e8d666','you got it.\r\nonce you login to the Galleries, you should see 3 buttons that allow you to create and manage your albums.\r\n[quote:6f25e8d666=\"chrome\"]Hey Cabo,\r\n\r\nI was wondering If I could have some space in the members gallery?\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...[/quote:6f25e8d666]'),(35771,'cf1492445e','I really want to, but it\'s a bit chilly outside (I know, I\'m a wuss)  and there is just no fuckin elevation in FL, so unless I pack up, and go to the track, it\'s just running back, and forth on flat land..  It\'s a pain to run for 20 min and have to clean it for an hour, or 2 :o \r\n\r\n\r\nArghh... This sucks.\r\n\r\n\r\nSavages are good trucks, but if you might want to get into racing at some point, get a truck with a lower center of gravity.'),(33638,'9ddbbacbd4','Yeah I meant a front bumper (crash bar). How will I join the bars together? to make cross members?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34305,'5ddf6d0b78','No, and if you PM me again, or so much as reply to this message and I will report you to the moderators and it will likely result in a ban.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(32543,'ea186fa3e2','Hey, bud! \r\n\r\nWhenever you\'re ready.\r\n\r\nBut first, this might not be a huge concern for you, but I noticed 3 strips of tape on one (1) side of the box. Everything looks perferct inside, including the box. \r\nI\'m sorta anal about that kind of stuff, so I thought I\'d mention it to you.\r\nNo hard feelings if ya want to back out.\r\n\r\nLemme know! \r\n\r\nAlso, I know you\'re a long time pimp or whatever, and if you want to PP me upon receiving the item, that is fine too. I\'m a super nice guy and all that, but new nonetheless. :grin:'),(34930,'cc73b2ea34','Here is my last PM to you.\r\n\r\n[quote:cc73b2ea34]No, and if you PM me again, or so much as reply to this message and I will report you to the moderators and it will likely result in a ban.\r\n[/quote:cc73b2ea34]\r\n\r\nThis is your last warning.\r\n\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(22540,'9f98c9839a','[quote:9f98c9839a=\"payaso\"]Ring me when you get home bitch so we can discuss the mod situation...lol[/quote:9f98c9839a]I will.\r\nI tried calling you yesterday twice but no answer, you must be using the same phones as me lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36098,'07cd8c4c43','Naw man, I didn\'t mean to come off all pissed off....  I was just cunfused.\r\n\r\nNo need to just send them out. I can pay you for them, but I wasn\'t sure if you were still wanting to sell them or not since I never got a reply about sending you a money order.\r\n\r\nI would have replied sooner, but I\'ve been stuck in the cab...lol\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know dude.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(27614,'8750de8830','[quote:8750de8830=\"red2cwm\"]Hey Man,\r\n\r\nThis was TOTALLY MY BAD.  I misunderstood the posting rules for \"Lookin\' to score\" so I posted in the main Z Forum.  \r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=5528\r\n\r\nAnd I totally got what I deserved.  And quite honestly I thought it was hillarious!  But I was wondering if you\'d mind deleting the post entirely after everybody\'s had a good laugh today.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nChris[/quote:8750de8830]You got it man, thread has been deleted.\r\nThanks for not flipping out. Good luck with your quest!\r\n\r\nCaboWabo'),(33669,'1de04113bd','Hey man-\r\n\r\nI figured you\'d be the guy to point me in the direction of the best value for one of those magnifying goggle things jewelers use. I just need it for working on bits, so don\'t need welding protection or anything like that. Lights might be nice, but not necessary. I don\'t wear glasses, so no clip-on stuff. Got any tips?\r\n\r\nThanks dude,\r\nSuperFly');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33693,'501da7ba11','Heh, well it was a noble and mature thing to do.   :-o'),(36803,'32fab24b88','hey man, I know, slack late response.  You\'ve prolyl figured out the problem now.\r\n\r\nI take it was a DNS issue?  You running an exchange box in a BIND DNS environment?\r\n\r\nhttp://www.msexchange.org/ is an excellent site for all things exchange, just search the forums there, it may help.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nMatt.'),(35306,'590ea6fd84','[quote:590ea6fd84=\"pimpsmurf\"]yes, although 1 of the cells of the 3 i have may have part of the flag torn, so it wouldn\'t really be useful unless you have a sonic welder. hehe.\r\n\r\nI hope I don\'t have it in a month, but you certainly get first shot at it. If the damned shop would get my digi video cam fixed I could put in on ebay.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:590ea6fd84]\r\nYeah that would be awesome. If you do decide to put it on the bay though would you consider parting out the deluxe to me :???: \r\n\r\nI might have asked you that before if i have slap me* *'),(35525,'7bc6a03d7e','[quote:7bc6a03d7e=\"pimpsmurf\"]If you want the MZM, now is the time, else I\'ll send you the stock board if you want it (and I can get the servo board to work out.)\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:7bc6a03d7e]\r\n\r\nAhh, christmas time i thought\'d i would of had money to spare but it turns out its tighter than ever. :sad: \r\n\r\n\r\nYeah i\'ll take the stock board off ya hands. I hope that servo idea works out. It should. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32654,'982bcd5547','[quote:982bcd5547=\"Red_Line\"]Hey I saw the Plasmatomic motors you made...very nice, I was wondering...if I paid you, for the parts and the labor, would you make me a motor and tell me how to install it...I\'m kind of new to X Mods, the local like small business sports store, right around the block from me, is making a track for X Mods inside the store, and he said they are gona do races and bets and other stuff just for fun, but with at least one of my X Mods, I wanna blow everyone out of the water, if not, thats fine, I was just asking, and thanks for your time man\r\n\r\n-Josh[/quote:982bcd5547]\r\n\r\nSorry dude, I just don\'t have the time.  I suggest you try out the tutorial www.woahnelly.com/plasmatomic\r\n\r\nit\'s not that hard and you\'ll lear a lot about motors in the process.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.'),(34471,'cdb14b8e80','hey man, could you hook me up with 16 N-MOSFETs and 3 of your DC mod boards? How much would all this cost?\r\n\r\nI measured the motor outputs, and would like to know what these change to after the DC mod.\r\n\r\noper. freq.\r\n103.5hz\r\n\r\nduty cycles (reverse to foreward)\r\n-44.5\r\n-38.3\r\n-32.2\r\n-26.5\r\n0\r\n26.5\r\n32.2\r\n38.3\r\n44.5\r\n53.9\r\n60.5\r\n\r\nAlso, with your DC mod, it only works for the foreward, correct?'),(33824,'044ad17f7e','i used a 40 watt solder iron.  make sure to clean the areas you are going to solder with steel wool or sandpaper and use flux.  makes a huge difference as to how easy it goes togther.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31944,'b9a2dd47da','Hey FYI I sent your package out yesterday morning, should be there in 4 days (Thursday/Friday)\r\n\r\nEnjoy'),(34031,'fe7b170795','that\'s cool, then I have 27 41 49 57 and 35 can race up to 4 bits and a ZZMT :D'),(37031,'6d700515a4','Naw bro, not interested right now, but good luck on ebay. Shit man ... i seen your track DAMNNNNNNNNN that thing is sick.'),(29476,'30e582ae2f','yeah, same drive fets.'),(23773,'be876b0358','Sent! Whats the status of the hummer?'),(23774,'8acc2cea62','Not sent... I spaced this morning, but it\'s in my bag now, so there\'s no forgetting it tomorrow. Thanks man, I\'ll let you know when it\'s in the mail.'),(33274,'42dd6f6309','hey dude, I\'ll take it all.\r\n\r\nI see you\'re asking for $6 shipped.  How about we make it $10 for all that.  So take $10 off the price of the deluxe fix and ship it all down together.\r\n\r\nhow does that sound?\r\n\r\nph2t.'),(36105,'1a29ac09d9','Money order = good as cash, and you can cash em at just about any store or bank.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37540,'4c89b58741','it ain\'t no biggie. i\'ll be glad to help. just let me know.'),(34945,'09646e0e46','thats cool is ther any threads that ever went on a bout them? wish it were a civic though. :-?'),(34233,'a894138c4d','Do you syill have the odifiers availible?  If you do I\' d give you $4 for both. :grin:'),(34234,'cfd121b648','[quote:cfd121b648=\"weazel\"]Do you syill have the odifiers availible?  If you do I\' d give you $4 for both. :grin:[/quote:cfd121b648]\r\n\r\nSure.\r\n\r\nIf you don\'t care.  I could take them out of the package, put them in zip-lok\'s and ship them priority for $4.50.\r\n\r\nWith the packaging it will likely be about the same price, but about 3-4 more days.\r\n\r\nYour choice.\r\n\r\nSG219\r\n\r\n\r\nPaypal addy:\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com'),(34165,'8d2fac4704','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/images/avatars/cf059ffd4105e2f764f66.jpg'),(32495,'1fb1e1977e','[quote:1fb1e1977e=\"Finks\"]No idea, whenever I upload a pic on my wifes computer it always gives me problems and that\'s what I was doing last night.  Even still I know the file size was around 84KB, they are the pics in the \"what\'s in your garage?\" thread.  Thanks for looking into it either way Cabo.[/quote:1fb1e1977e]\r\nNo problem dude. Try it from another machine and see if that helps.\r\nLet me know if you still have troubles.'),(36689,'2b25eed13f','[quote:2b25eed13f=\"pimpsmurf\"]about 1.3 feet squared.\r\n\r\nThat reminds me. all the parts are in a plastic bag. The chassis is at the bottom. You need to pull the bag out and carefully empty it. It is not packing material! =)\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:2b25eed13f]\r\n\r\nIs the lipo already installed on the chassis with the 1/16\'th elec\'s or do i have to install it?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25657,'a62cb3100c','[quote:a62cb3100c=\"viperdout\"]Dave:\r\n\r\nAny updates?  You get yours running?\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:a62cb3100c]Oh yeah, my been running since last night. That\'s why I was hesistant to jump into code\'s mod. I just got the damn thing working good again.\r\n\r\nAnyways, I was out running errands today and got stuck in the rain, so I stopped in RS and picked me up a spare monster. I\'m feeling alot better about tearing my car apart now, and feeling calmer about it, code\'s tutorial made sense. He\'s very detailed, 19 pages when I printed it out to read. Took me a couple hours to get through it. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'m gonna jump on this right after work tomorrow, it should work. Ph2t is working on a alternate method, we\'ll know by tomorrow if his worked, and you know if it did, his way\'s faster.  :lol: \r\n\r\nEither way I\'ll have this done tomorrow. :-) \r\n\r\nDave\r\n\r\n\r\nEDIT: Ph2ts method worked, and looks way simplier, but uses all N-channels FETs, I\'m debating ordering more N-channels, or just using the P-channels I got, to do codesuidae\'s method, which is kinda complicated. :?'),(27935,'c39892a02d','I don\'t want money, man... I just want to see them modded out nicely...\r\n\r\nAlls I need is your shipping info...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27936,'1ab65569fc','How about if I modded some and sent them to you? Gives me stuff to do.'),(32948,'09b89eab57','My Verizon email finally gets mail from BitPimps. YEAAAA.\r\n\r\nIt only took 10 days  :grin:  when they said it would take 7.'),(33218,'366e9dfabe','[quote:366e9dfabe=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:366e9dfabe=\"BilboBaggins\"][quote:366e9dfabe=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:366e9dfabe=\"BilboBaggins\"]I could use a second WRX body. Does it have the complete stock bumpers and hood?\r\n\r\nI\'ll can send down a MO if you send me an address.[/quote:366e9dfabe]\r\n\r\nYep everythings included!\r\n\r\nAdress\r\n\r\nMatt Gera\r\n4303 Radcliffe Drive\r\nPalm Harbor Fl.\r\n34685[/quote:366e9dfabe]\r\n\r\nI\'ll send out a MO tomorrow. $8.00 if I read it right.[/quote:366e9dfabe]\r\n\r\nYep 8.00 \r\n\r\nSo sounds like we have a deal  :-o[/quote:366e9dfabe]\r\n\r\nThe MO went out this afternoon and I enclosed the shipping information to me in the envelope.\r\n\r\nLet me know when you get it (US Mail I\'m thinking Wednesday-Thursday).'),(32418,'94876e6ed0','Your car\'s going out today, so watch for it. :-) \r\n\r\nI\'ll probably just send it standard postage.\r\n\r\nI gonna go ahead and just send it out, because I\'m anxious to get your reaction to these cars, and hoping you find some time to get to it. \r\n\r\nI got my Epoch, and I think these are faster with the 3.4 and green gears. My favorite driver car right now. Not happy with the Epoch. :( \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36361,'16e49611b1','Did you get my payment?'),(37417,'5e90dbf532','[url]www.imageshack.com[/url]\r\n\r\nThat\'s free web hosting.'),(29877,'56dbef5fb6','[quote:56dbef5fb6=\"micro_man\"]hi sg im looking for a xmods skyline body . what whould your price be on that and the front clip ? a supra body or 350z would also work . i have $7 left after geting a replacement xmod chassis (used car from rs ) and getin some other xmod goodies . if thats not enofe $$ its not a big deal i\'ll just find a way to get a few extra bucks .=and ill get back to you .\r\n\r\noh sorry about that civic deal we had going i ended up haveing a few doctor bills and had to take care of them , i totaly forgot about the car since i havent been on the forums much lately .[/quote:56dbef5fb6]\r\n\r\nI\'m sorry.  I don\'t have any spares of those models that you.  The only spares I have are the Silver RSX, and Black Civics, maybe a blue one too.\r\n\r\nIf you come across anyone with Supra bodies, let me know.  I\'ll take one too. :-) \r\n\r\nLet me know.\r\n\r\nMike'),(27376,'3525d3b0d0','As far as the automodellista LXX kits go, I think I got the last batch that rcmart.com had, they were 35, 40, and 45 mhz, and my 35 seems to have a short in the conrol, although it charges the car fine.  I found a UK site that might still have the TOMY Automodellista 4-in-1 pack, and the Inital D kit, but I want to make sure I can get my Gloria bodykit and Trueno pullback before I tell anyone where I found them.  But that\'s all I want for now, just bodies, and I have all the corresponding pullbacks that make up the Automodellista kit.  I\'d say I have enough cars at the moment.\r\n\r\nOh!  Hey, check this out.  Is this legit looking to you, as in Bit compatible?\r\n\r\nhttp://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5951170846&amp;rd=1\r\n\r\nI like new Mini coopers and I didn\'t even know a body existed until I saw the auction and there\'s a few of them.  I\'ll get one if you think I should ( I have a couple bucks).\r\n\r\nHit me back,\r\nAbe');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27493,'798aeccf97','yo bro,\r\ncheck this shit out:\r\n\r\nTomy Automodellista set\r\nhttp://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5953818734&amp;rd=1\r\n\r\nTomy Initial D set\r\nhttp://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5953334772&amp;rd=1\r\n\r\nI\'m outta cash so I\'m passing them up (that and I prefer 2-speed controllers and have all the corresponding bit bodies to the AM kit)\r\nLate,\r\nAbe'),(28152,'01fba88d0f','we can be friends sure. But i dont have anyone from the hood in my cantact list. I get along great with everyone on the forum.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(33109,'c87114d766','hey man! all your stuff showed up last week, but my mother in law picked up the package from the PO and i only got it today!\r\n\r\nI shoulda checked with you if they were all in one peice or not (got some batteries, wires to reinstall on that ZZ &amp; MS) and haven\'t had a chance to play with any of the lipo stuff yet, (no charger) so i\'ll reserve my judgement on it for now, but the rest is good!\r\n\r\nOnly a couple probs, maybe you can help cos i know nothing about zz\'s.  \r\n\r\nwith the SE, reverse doesn\'t work and i\'m having trouble getting it to charge right on the controller.  the lights goes red and blinks, then both the red and green come on together after about 20 seconds and i only get about 20second runtime.  Any idea what the story is there?\r\n\r\nAnd for the stock ZZMT, how long should i be expecting between charges? so far i\'m running dead after about a minute off a double charge - the batteries im using arent the best though.   :???:\r\n   \r\nand what is the story with motors?  there is an orange, a yellow, and a pink.  There were also a couple of green ends, a casing and a shaft in there, but i wouldnt have a clue how to put it back together.   which one do i use with which gears to get quicker/more torque, etc?\r\n\r\nlooking forward to getting a lipo charger, hopefully get the modded ZZMT and OG going, and once i\'ve locked the SS i\'ll get it rolling too!'),(33110,'555c5e6eb7','the smaller motors are ZipZap motors. blue/purple is the NX 34k motor, and the orange is the next to the fastest.\r\n\r\nThe fat motors: one is a stock motor and one (purple I think?) is a Tinyrc.com Formula II Motor (extremely fast on lipo power.)\r\n\r\nThe stock ZZMT has a stock ZZ motor replacing the original steering motor. steering is faster with MUCH more torque which is great for crawling around. It does sucks for battery runtime however. :(\r\n\r\nhrm. I don\'t know what is up with the SE. It was working before I shipped it. Check FETs and make sure everything is soldered well. Perhaps a wire on the duty cycle mod chip too. *shrug*\r\n\r\nI hope you enjoy that stuff. I got into my MZM and a 1:10th XXX-NT, so I don\'t have the time or patience for the little guys anymore.\r\n\r\nI just placed the final order for my MZM last night. oil dampers x4, alloy rear gearbox arm mount (not the whole gearbox. I have that. it is way too heavy), 3 alloy servo gears, 1 degree castor knuckles. hopefully that will keep her as straight as ph2t\'s old one was in the video.\r\n\r\nWoah Nelly deluxe is already on the way! =)\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25801,'2576c0ebf7','They went out this afternoon.\r\n\r\nHave fun. :cool:'),(28428,'4e0ec72ebc','I couldn\'t see the springs for the front end do you have them?'),(22552,'19e3d92698','no problem.\r\nnow you\'ve got another excuse to get another camera lol[quote:19e3d92698=\"chrome\"]Thanks for the hookup on the gallery.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...[/quote:19e3d92698]'),(34189,'4cd43072a7','Sup pimp?\r\n\r\nTime is of the essence, I cannot make ebay purchases :( so I\'m asking you for help. I really want this MRS4 roller, it\'s a real deal.\r\n\r\nCurrent bid= $50\r\nShipping= $12 US only\r\n[url=http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6004969682&amp;category=44015&amp;sspagename=rvi:1:1v_home]link[/url]\r\n\r\nI\'m trying to build my micro from the ground up, so I really need the diffs and suspension off that roller. The motor too. Are you into MRS4\'s? If you are, and you need an aftermarket chassis we can work something out. That roller carries a Motek EXO1 chassis. I have no need for it. More on that later.\r\n\r\nIf you don\'t want anything off the MRS4, can you have it sent to:\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\n4405 NW 73rd Ave\r\nSTE 716993\r\nMiami, Florida 33166-6488\r\n\r\nThat is a forwarding service (skybox) that my dad has. You will only pay shipping there, I pay shipping from there to Barbados.\r\n\r\nIf you [u:4cd43072a7]do[/u:4cd43072a7] want stuff off it, here\'s what I\'m willing to offer:\r\n\r\n-Micro steering servo\r\n-Battery\r\n-Ferrari body\r\n-Motek EXO chassis\r\n\r\nI\'ll send a stock bottom plate so that yoou mount the shock and the differentials on. Along with a MO. Also if you\'re taking stuff you can have it, but can you pay the shipping of my part to barbados. That stuff for $10-$15 shipping cost seems like a good deal. Tell me what you think.\r\n\r\nPlease don\'t go over $55, that would put me over budget.\r\nPlease let me know before you start bidding, as I\'ve asked another pimp.\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx'),(23926,'79f4105e03','ya i have 3 controllers and 3 bands.\r\n\r\nno tut on the install but its pretty simple. i think theres pics of the component tho.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22560,'3339c3a1a0','Yea I got it, had time to open it and then close it back..... things got me swamped.... Thanks to everyone again.'),(29001,'fc1ea06f03','Europe\r\nHungary\r\nDombovar\r\nTulipan str. 4\r\n7200\r\n\r\nMy name is:   Voros Gergely        \r\n\r\nI\'ll need a bank-account number,and a last name for the transfer.'),(22564,'4d2fb64414','SuperFly... hue...\r\nyou\'re both going to get the same PM because you guys come as a package deal, and it\'s easier on me lol\r\n\r\nyou 2 have help tremendously with the site, it\'s pimps like you 2 that help make this site what it is. from modding cars to posting content on the forums, you guys are top notch.\r\n\r\nwe\'ve been discussing and we want to make an offer to you 2.\r\nwe want to bring you 2 on as \"Moderators/Admins\".\r\nyou\'ll have the same priviliages/responsibilities as the rest of us Moderators.\r\nyou would not be eligable for contests anymore as you would be helping to produce them and judge them.\r\nfor the most part, the work involved is minimal.\r\nif you see something that needs editing, deleting, moving - do it.\r\nif you have some ideas for the community - discuss it in the Admins forum.\r\nhelp keep the place organized and in some sort of order.\r\nand of course keep doing what you do - mod up, paint, take pictures, post articles, do reviews, etc.\r\n\r\nso what do you guys think?\r\nwant another key to add to your key rings?'),(22565,'0d499544ec','SuperFly... hue...\r\nyou\'re both going to get the same PM because you guys come as a package deal, and it\'s easier on me lol\r\n\r\nyou 2 have help tremendously with the site, it\'s pimps like you 2 that help make this site what it is. from modding cars to posting content on the forums, you guys are top notch.\r\n\r\nwe\'ve been discussing and we want to make an offer to you 2.\r\nwe want to bring you 2 on as \"Moderators/Admins\".\r\nyou\'ll have the same priviliages/responsibilities as the rest of us Moderators.\r\nyou would not be eligable for contests anymore as you would be helping to produce them and judge them.\r\nfor the most part, the work involved is minimal.\r\nif you see something that needs editing, deleting, moving - do it.\r\nif you have some ideas for the community - discuss it in the Admins forum.\r\nhelp keep the place organized and in some sort of order.\r\nand of course keep doing what you do - mod up, paint, take pictures, post articles, do reviews, etc.\r\n\r\nso what do you guys think?\r\nwant another key to add to your key rings?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22566,'e398eb3214','OK, I have been thinking about this for a long time now.  1st off sorry for the generalized post, but there was no way for me to easily mass mail this to all of yall.\r\n\r\nBasically I always thought it would be totally kick ass if we as a web site could do a joint car mod!  And who better to own it than the guy that is responsable for the Hood?\r\n\r\nThe biggest question I had was if we were to do this, who would do what, and what car would we do?  Well with the way Jmay\'s car is going I thought that this car in a nut shell is all Hood.  So we would use this origional ride as the starting point.  As good as it is though, I know for sure us pimps can bring it to it\'s max. \r\n\r\nOK before I go on let me just say deciding who to suggest for each part was wicked tuff, and I really don\'t want to step on anyones toes.  So fuck it I am just going to say who I personally think would be best at each of the many tasks it takes to mod a bit.\r\n\r\n1st off chassis wise, I think it goes without saying that Crazy Dave could do up the electronics on this bad boy, wether thats FETs, Dual Cells or whatever.\r\n\r\nNow with all this power, you know there will be slop, so who takes care of slop, on the message boards as well as on the bits?  Hog, and his patented JB weld is all I have to say.\r\n\r\nAs for weels, well It\'s safe to say that all of us have shitloads of experiance here, but when I came to this site, Payaso was one of the first I saw to do Alloys and Dubs, so this is where that bastard fits in.\r\n\r\nNow for the body, and belife me, this was hella tuff to decide.  Well with this body you really wouldn\'t body kit it, but it will need some bad ass customization to make it from stock to all out P.I.M.P.  So yeah, Dark Tari was the pimp I had in mind there.\r\n\r\nFor the paint I just have no damn clue so there will be 2 parts, paint and then datail paint, and basically IMO it\'s a draw between these two pimps and I know they work well together.  So Hugh and Superfly, I would leave it to you guys to decides who lays the paint, and then who does the detailing.\r\n\r\nOh and to hit you two up again since you will be the last to have the car before it is in Cabo\'s hands, could one of you take some killer ass pics.  Why? well we can\'t leave out Sessiz, that fuck face with his mad poster/background skillz.\r\n\r\nSo what do I do?  Well like I said, this is about the best in each catagory, and I am not saying I am not really good at these things, but I feel each of you assigned was better, so I will finish this bitch off with an all out Pimpin controller for this mad ass ride.\r\n\r\nLooking at Jmays\' chassis I think it would work best on a ZipZap chassis and would afford CD more play space w/ electronics.  Oh also, I know there are some pimps missing here, as for our Bruce brothers I felt that would complicate shit with shipping times, and for the rest, well, if any of you can think of ways to include em, let me know.\r\n\r\nAlso, if we are all down for this, I would love for there to be a ways for us to all be able to comment on it in a forum base.  Any ideas, let me know.  OK, my hands are hurting, PM me w/ comments and to say if you are down for this.  \r\n\r\nOne last thing, when is the 2nd anniversary of Bitpimps?'),(26095,'90ba55bc71','Hi,\r\n\r\nHow much Is your front deck turbo?\r\nIs it hard to install?\r\nDo you ship to Barbados?\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23816,'86f51e79e2','Alright, it\'s in the mail!... Let me know when you get it and I\'ll do the same. \r\n\r\nThanks again,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(24505,'a325f5f88b','Make me an offer!\r\n\r\nThe standard rules of e-trade apply here in that if we agree on a price, you pay shipping.\r\nAssuming you read the post, you know that it was new at Christmas 2003, has many extra parts and the stage two upgrade for steering, suspension, and all 3 motors. Also a lithium Ion 9v controller battery.\r\n\r\nI\'ll look forward to hearing from you........\r\n\r\njrc6805'),(23924,'94335a9b2e','Are ther econtrollers and crysals with those cars? or will I need to look for some?\r\n\r\n  I just ordered the range parts so I will have them in and ready.\r\n\r\n  Is ther ea tut on fixing that?'),(23928,'b34b62fac9','OK cool\r\n\r\n  Yea I think I will get a few nellys and have CD install them and maybe try one myself.\r\n\r\n  I bet it makes them muscle cars even that more bitchen with the nelly'),(27076,'14b2d19f35','got it today.\r\n\r\n :-) \r\n\r\nThanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31545,'43cc65901e','Hmm , they would be nice , and thankyou VERY much for the offer its greatly appreciated but i dont think im up to installing them or affording a charger right now . \r\nThankyou anyway , \r\ni will post your item today ( in about an hour ) when i go into town. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nthanks , \r\n!-J03-!'),(28287,'064136d9d0','[quote:064136d9d0=\"micro_man\"]hi sg im looking to get another xmod . i cant afford $50 because of some medical bills i have to pay this month , so the most i can spend is $25 . if you have a working used xmod(or iwaver) for that much , or know someone who dose please let me know . i can prolly use pay pal agin . thank, matt .[/quote:064136d9d0]\r\n\r\nAre you looking for just the chassis or the whole deal?\r\n\r\nI can swing you a running chassis and a controller for $25+shipping(around $3 or 4 I would guess).\r\n\r\nAdd $5 for a body.  Black honda Civic.\r\n\r\nLet me know.'),(37317,'e2b8988bf5','[quote:e2b8988bf5=\"betty.k\"]sounds good to me! you can send paypal cash to: bettykay@gmail.com\r\n\r\nall goods will be packed well and shipped via airmail. shipping to the u.s. usually takes 1 - 2 weeks.\r\n(next time a merikan tries to charge you too much shipping you can say &quot;i got an xmod shipped from aus for $10! :-o )[/quote:e2b8988bf5]\r\n\r\n\r\nSounds good man! I\'ll send the doh later today. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22570,'d7ec9f4a3e','OK, I have been thinking about this for a long time now.  1st off sorry for the generalized post, but there was no way for me to easily mass mail this to all of yall.\r\n\r\nBasically I always thought it would be totally kick ass if we as a web site could do a joint car mod!  And who better to own it than the guy that is responsable for the Hood?\r\n\r\nThe biggest question I had was if we were to do this, who would do what, and what car would we do?  Well with the way Jmay\'s car is going I thought that this car in a nut shell is all Hood.  So we would use this origional ride as the starting point.  As good as it is though, I know for sure us pimps can bring it to it\'s max. \r\n\r\nOK before I go on let me just say deciding who to suggest for each part was wicked tuff, and I really don\'t want to step on anyones toes.  So fuck it I am just going to say who I personally think would be best at each of the many tasks it takes to mod a bit.\r\n\r\n1st off chassis wise, I think it goes without saying that Crazy Dave could do up the electronics on this bad boy, wether thats FETs, Dual Cells or whatever.\r\n\r\nNow with all this power, you know there will be slop, so who takes care of slop, on the message boards as well as on the bits?  Hog, and his patented JB weld is all I have to say.\r\n\r\nAs for weels, well It\'s safe to say that all of us have shitloads of experiance here, but when I came to this site, Payaso was one of the first I saw to do Alloys and Dubs, so this is where that bastard fits in.\r\n\r\nNow for the body, and belife me, this was hella tuff to decide.  Well with this body you really wouldn\'t body kit it, but it will need some bad ass customization to make it from stock to all out P.I.M.P.  So yeah, Dark Tari was the pimp I had in mind there.\r\n\r\nFor the paint I just have no damn clue so there will be 2 parts, paint and then datail paint, and basically IMO it\'s a draw between these two pimps and I know they work well together.  So Hugh and Superfly, I would leave it to you guys to decides who lays the paint, and then who does the detailing.\r\n\r\nOh and to hit you two up again since you will be the last to have the car before it is in Cabo\'s hands, could one of you take some killer ass pics.  Why? well we can\'t leave out Sessiz, that fuck face with his mad poster/background skillz.\r\n\r\nSo what do I do?  Well like I said, this is about the best in each catagory, and I am not saying I am not really good at these things, but I feel each of you assigned was better, so I will finish this bitch off with an all out Pimpin controller for this mad ass ride.\r\n\r\nLooking at Jmays\' chassis I think it would work best on a ZipZap chassis and would afford CD more play space w/ electronics.  Oh also, I know there are some pimps missing here, as for our Bruce brothers I felt that would complicate shit with shipping times, and for the rest, well, if any of you can think of ways to include em, let me know.\r\n\r\nAlso, if we are all down for this, I would love for there to be a ways for us to all be able to comment on it in a forum base.  Any ideas, let me know.  OK, my hands are hurting, PM me w/ comments and to say if you are down for this.  \r\n\r\nOne last thing, when is the 2nd anniversary of Bitpimps?'),(34203,'fbcf3feadc','There are 23 hours 22mins left. (when this was posted)\r\nI\'ll check my PM\'\'s tomorrow morning.\r\n\r\nOMG!!! your wife\'s in labour, Congrats man. I\'d be honored if you named him after me  :lol: jk. The best of luck for both of you. I\'ll pray for you both before I goto bed.\r\n\r\nI\'ll PM you in the morning and let you know if I heard finks. Keep me posted on your bundle of joy  :-o .\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36822,'e567d82cca','What else would you like, name somerthing and i\'ll see if i have it'),(36823,'7711346630','Any sort of Xmod upgrade Skyline kid...I am easy Xmod whore big guy ahha\r\n\r\nSeriously a piece that will smoothen out my drivetrain maybe, or lighten the car...\r\n\r\nOr something different or colorful....performance part w.e man...just let me know, its just a have alot of stock stuff already so I kinda want sometin different. The stuff is ready when you are.'),(37275,'bf4f8d97a3','[quote:bf4f8d97a3=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Never mind, I\'m gettin my bro to get the stuff for me, I\'ll pay him back when he comes home.[/quote:bf4f8d97a3]\r\n\r\nCool Beans  :-o'),(31899,'03300b46cc','[quote:03300b46cc=\"DarkTari\"]He\'s Baaack !\r\n\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;postid=192037#post192037[/quote:03300b46cc]\r\n\r\nI really wonder as to the IQ of these people:\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=11480&amp;perpage=15&amp;pagenumber=3\r\n\r\nHere\'s the IP from the new account:\r\n65.35.117.181'),(31446,'176b0da523','Dude, you\'re a frickin idiot, if I may say. \r\n\r\nWith your kind of posts, it really takes away from the learning process for NooBs like me.\r\n \r\n\r\nI don\'t mean this harsh-like, I just thought it wasn\'t necessary, especially when sg219 was trying to help ya.\r\n\r\nI hope this isn\'t a joke or something your playing..... :???:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28825,'63c381a755','Well when i \"got out\" of them i let everything go pretty much except my two favorites which were zips. one had clone pcb ( off freq) and dual batts, other has MS pcb ( the one with \"turbo\" button i think its called Pro ) and mosfet modded. only kept those 2 cars with minimal motors tire swaps and such no extra bodies or anything... those are the zz F+F green/black eclipse i think it is and the other is the old blue camaro. So i really aint got much to tinker with.  \r\n\r\nNice to hear from ya. Hows MD? i dont miss the hectic daily routines there at all. \r\n\r\nPeace \r\n\r\nErnie'),(35946,'cd1f0badd0','http://s6.invisionfree.com/Infernal_XMOD/index.php?showtopic=3664 try this\r\n\r\nAn easier way for this is jsut to take off the steering horn from the servo and realign it to that tiny arrow on the servo. But this way will surely center it. Oh yeah, I got the tight turns tutorial :D\r\n\r\nhttp://xmodworld.com/modules.php?name=Forums&amp;file=viewtopic&amp;t=6219 this is the messier version\r\nhttp://www.atomicmods.com/custom.aspx?id=28 this is the cleaner , harder version\r\n\r\nthey both have the same results, just the messy version is more prone to break\r\n\r\n\r\nif you need anything else, dont be afraid toPM me  :)'),(26756,'dac7fed63d','Hi yakboy,\r\n\r\nthanks for your nice comments about my track.\r\nI wanted to make it portable too, so I made it of four pieces of wood. \r\nScrewed together with 10 screws from the top.\r\nThe bridge with the mountains are removable for easier transportation.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:dac7fed63d]I think you Germans have taken to bits in a big way, I\'m impressed with some of your retailers especially bitstylaz...\r\n[/quote:dac7fed63d]\r\n\r\nYes Bits were quite good 1-2 years ago but now everyone likes a proportional car better than just digital.\r\nMany users are driving 1:24 now and the Bits are nearly dead.  :(\r\nBut new hope with the new Metl Tech Racers!\r\n\r\nI like the Epoch 1:43 racers. I have two of them and they drive great.\r\n\r\nI\'m a member of the [url]www.bit-racer.de[/url] forum.\r\nThe best german site I think with the most traffic and the best mods come from there.\r\nLike the ZipZap Monster 4x4x4, the rock crawler and many more.\r\n\r\nPlease tell me when you post some pictures of your track. \r\n\r\nBye,\r\n\r\n  Jens[/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31473,'d12010f5af','hi there , \r\nOk thats fine , if you can give me your adress il send it off tomorrow for you . Il make sure i pack it properly and pad it as they are quite delicate and i would feel really bad if it got broken in the mail.I wont bother to check your feedback as i trust you anyway.I would like the hummer body wich is the one with the spider-man graphic on it .\r\nThanks very much , \r\nJ03!'),(26717,'e2b908344e','The rims came yesterday!!  Thanks. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nI\'m gonna try and print out a few more decals tonight.  So I should be able to get your stuff out in the morning.\r\n\r\n(FYI...the decals aren\'t the best or even very good, but are definately useable for something)\r\n\r\nI haven\'t been over Bird\'s yet this week, but I will drop him off to him when I go over.  Probably tonight or tomarrow night.'),(34103,'502bb8bb40','Hey man-\r\n\r\nYou mentioned an image showing alternative contact points for Nelly wires...\r\n\r\nThanks!'),(26286,'891f1c286a','I am off this week, and will be checking shipping then.  For the crystal problem you have, simply put the Tx crystal in the Car, and you get half channels.  I raced my Mini-T like this the other day with no problems whatsoever.  Sorry, but the channels you said you can\'t use, are the ones I have (blue &amp; green).');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26287,'dc2441049e','Thanx,\r\n\r\nI know you told me that you have no horn, but if you can get one please send it. I suspect my horn is rounded. I\'ll try the thing with the crystals like you suggested. If I can afford it i\'ll try to send the money order express. Give me your email addy again I misplaced it the first time.\r\n\r\nThank you again\r\nMaxx'),(37157,'5ae21ac662','I hope this is what you\'re looking for. :-) \r\n\r\n[URL=http://img482.imageshack.us/my.php?image=img091110ljcopy1ra.jpg][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/1449/img091110ljcopy1ra.th.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]\r\n\r\n[URL=http://img482.imageshack.us/my.php?image=img091110ljdiggycopy3hh.jpg][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/2935/img091110ljdiggycopy3hh.th.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]\r\n\r\n[URL=http://imageshack.us][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/1512/v35sigcopy1pr.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]\r\n\r\n[URL=http://imageshack.us][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/6099/v35sigcopy22zf.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]'),(36543,'1872870d86','Can\'t do just the body, sorry.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36544,'5f446cd105','Mate no worries about going Nelly - ph2t and I have a gentlemans agreement of sorts - he does kick-arse turbos and I do the spiders which are same as a Nelly 1.2  :)\r\n\r\nThe Gandinis are great only hassle is they don\'t wear out quick enough ;)  Seriously though I think that\'s what makes them worth the bucks, they wear real good.\r\n\r\nI can chuck a couple of extra 7317s into you current pack if you like, BTW swap the steering fets for 7317s ;)  it\'s a great change ;)\r\n\r\nA.'),(24241,'31b20cf59a','[quote:31b20cf59a=\"dcsk8terboy89\"]Well, i am working on one of betty k\'s cars, and the damn pics arent showing up.. And since i cant visualize words for shit, i was hoping that you could change the pics that are there (the ones from rear shock) to the ones that are supposed to be there.  If you could, that would be great.\r\n\r\nDex[/quote:31b20cf59a]I\'d like to help you, but I\'m not sure what you mean?\r\ncould you please explain more?\r\n\r\nhere is a link to betty\'s \"rear shock\" tutorial specifically:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/article_postings.php?id=37&amp;catId=\r\n\r\nall the images are there.'),(28545,'397f445b7a','[quote:397f445b7a=\"biohazard\"]Not sure yet, the Celica fit the best because of the high back. If I use a truck body almost all of the rear end will be missing.  Ok so I am all ears on your suggestions.  let me know if you have any of those ZZford 150 bodies.  I just need it for a mod on my ZZMT[/quote:397f445b7a]\r\n\r\nWhat\'s your email address?\r\n\r\nDarkTari@msn.com');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34071,'4627d2f2d8','Y dont you like me'),(37920,'237972e7cc','Hey, what\'s up? You know I\'d be more than happy to paint something up for you.\r\n\r\nSo how would you want to work something like that? I\'m assuming it\'d be a little cheaper for me to pick a body up and send it to you, or did you already have a body you wanted painted?\r\n\r\nI would only ask that you cover my cost, and if after you get it you wanted to throw me something extra for my efforts, that\'s cool too. :-o \r\n\r\nOh and I guess you could bounce some ideas off me of what you\'re looking for, as far as style and color and what not.\r\n\r\nDave'),(31416,'3530ba7f78','i dont have video but i can probably get you some pics,,, here are the specs :\r\n\r\nMicrosizer pro chassis\r\n\r\n3 cells (one 1.2 volt 150 mah tomy cell and one 2.4 volt zz se cell) = 3.6 volts.\r\n\r\nSmall (soft/sticky rubber,,,they made two types) Lego tires, doubled in the back and the front is doubled but the tire is only on the outside (you will understand in the picture)\r\n\r\nsuperslick orange motor with red pinion and 3 capacitors (to help with electomagnetic interfearance)\r\n\r\norange microsizer gears and axle.\r\n\r\naluminum pop can skid plates (optional) \r\n\r\nI use a micro plug to charge the 3 cells and plug that into a modified epoch wall charger but there are many ways to charge 3 cells.\r\n\r\nsome plasic from a zz package for the rear mounting plate, \r\n\r\na paper clip,\r\n\r\nsuper glue,\r\n\r\nWD-40 straw\r\n\r\nsolid metal antenna (optional)\r\n\r\nplastic hotwheels humvee body with 1/8 in foam to mount)\r\n\r\npaint for body\r\n\r\nAnd that should about cover what you need to build it,, really, the only pricy part is the microsizer itself, most of the other stuff you probably have around the house.  on the humvee it doesnt have any springs for suspension, its all free moving and works great for rock crawling although with this much power its the fastest bit i have,, it can take my 4 cell epoch any day for speed but cant handle quite as well lol... Hope that helps,, if you go to my gallery there are a ton of pics of the suspension and you should be able to figure out how i built it from there,, if now just let me know, ill try and help you out\r\n\r\nGood luck\r\n\r\nSTG'),(23516,'ab580a79e2','Perfect. I should have them sent out by tomorrow (1 or 2 Bits and a ZZ). $10 per car plus the return shipping cost.\r\n\r\nThanks a ton.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25068,'dd2160a269','Hey....have you taken apart the front end on your MT?'),(37011,'910f7c7e7d','Cool, I may double this order soon, but don\'t commit me to that yet I have to find out if my friend has the money to pay for them before he gets the $$$ in Feb. He\'ll need at least $300. So I\'ll find out and get back to you.'),(27359,'e9501e91ad','Not much out there bit related I don\'t allready got, but yeah hit me off with the site.\r\nThat gallop clone is a piece of shit and not really worth the $10 it\'ll cost ya.  :-)'),(23382,'e35a9ed19f','Yes I am still doing fet mods for people.\r\nhave a look at microamps.com.au and then email me from ther.\r\nAll the best\r\nuA'),(34099,'befe390127','have any 1:10 electric touring cars for sale cheap? stockish? In good condition'),(36655,'b482016665','no problem. Thanks for doing this for me anyways, I am almost fucking broke except for my car money and it is almost hurting me the fact that I cant touch it.'),(35369,'a0c814dae9','Hey pimp, I wasn\'t able to find any display books at the store yesterday. My manager wasn\'t working and none of the other employees knew what I was talking about. However I will be working with the manager today and will ask him. I will talk to you later.\r\n\r\nSat');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33252,'e7ed89b42b','jesse king\r\n163 main st\r\nft. fairfield, me 04742\r\n\r\nit better be girl on girl porn! :lol:'),(26638,'2626001e2e','[quote:2626001e2e=\"PINGO\"]i dont noo...... hey happe birthday  :D  we dont have a fuck of micro rc\'s or eny of that  :sad:[/quote:2626001e2e]Do you have msn messenger. If so i can help you with stuff. I can seel you some stuuf man if you need it lol NP if you want an Xmod send me the money and ill send it to you . Cause im a good friend. If you wanna be my friend :)'),(28631,'fa872972a4','[quote:fa872972a4=\"backdrift\"]I would like to buy this website a domain name, if you would want one that is? www.bitpimps.com is open? If you would want to register it for me, i will send u the money via paypal. \r\n\r\n-BD[/quote:fa872972a4]Hey holmes.\r\nThanks for the offer man, that\'s very cool of you.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, some shitball domain register bought it until December 11, 2006.\r\nhttp://www.domainnamesales.com\r\n\r\nTheir so small time, they don\'t even have the ability to sell a domain name yet. They just buy up domain names to inflate the price and people have to pay them instead of somebody else.\r\n\r\nI\'ll continue to keep an eye on it, if it ever comes available - we can hop on it.\r\n\r\nThanks again for the offer dude, that kind of stuff is what helps make bitPimps the place to be - kick ass members.\r\n\r\n- CaboWabo'),(26650,'799a071385','Sorry Cabo it\'s back to \"previous message couldn\'t be placed etc\"\r\n\r\nIs it me do I have to do anything inFile description or width / height \'cos I\'m leaving those blank\r\n\r\nSorry for the hassle');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23200,'a07d8749d1','Hey man I am new to this board. I am by no means a Noob to RC I am currently big into xmods but would like to get my ZZ SE working, as it sits on a shelf collecting dust. Anyway I saw that you have had the best luck increasing the performance of the SE through fet mods and what not, and i was wondering if you offered any sort of install services?'),(25477,'965992b9b6','do you want me go get you a zz monster instead of the xmod parts? i figure one plus the motor and wheel kits should make us even. cool?'),(34487,'d70824b08e','hey man, just wanted to let you know that the installation doco for the evo mosfet upgrade is almost done.  it will be posted shortly.\r\n\r\nif you wanted something sooner to help let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nph2t.,'),(37058,'0d6ddf4f8b','[quote:0d6ddf4f8b=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Cool, I may double this order soon, but don\'t commit me to that yet I have to find out if my friend has the money to pay for them before he gets the $$$ in Feb. He\'ll need at least $300. So I\'ll find out and get back to you.[/quote:0d6ddf4f8b]\r\n\r\nIs that $300 USD or BBD?'),(35184,'8d16fe838c','Consider it done.\r\n\r\nBTW, Just finished a 3x2 install of 7910/7329\'s into a Hummer. It\'s doing wheelies on 4 cells on a stock motor.  :eek:  Finally picked up a small 2s 600mah lipo from polyquest. I\'ll have to give that a try later.\r\n\r\nHave a good one,\r\nClint\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote=\"ph2t\"]hey Clint, I was just wondering if you would be up for writing a quite little review for the evo msofets on the review section in the ausmicro.com shop.  you don\'t have to do it, I would appreciate it if you could though man.  No rush.\r\n\r\n\r\ncheers,');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22578,'e215d94169','Hello --\r\n\r\nI\'ve just found this site and you seem to be on top of things, so to speak.  I experience the same problem with four USCG lifeboats and three island class cutters.  One motor rusts which ultimatelyI cannot break free  NKOK always replaces the boats but it is a hassle and it discourages from installing lights, rigging, etc.\r\n\r\nMost recently the starboard motor on the island class cutter will not run in reverse.\r\n\r\nI only run the boats in a swimming pool, thoroughly dry them,keep them inside, etc.  NKOK tech support is useless unless I want another new boat.\r\n\r\nAny suggestions?  Have you had these problems?  Are they fixable?\r\nShould I gut the innards and put in a new system?\r\n\r\nI appreciate any help.\r\n\r\nIn your debt,\r\n\r\nEd'),(36957,'ea705790d1','I\'ve been racing the shit out of my min z about the last month with the dude at work. He\'s got the XMOD evo truck, and I got the X5 BMW.\r\n\r\nHe now has seen the light, and ordered a mini Z MR-02MM Scaglietti, cause he\'s addicted.  My Q is He paid $104 for the ready set. Is that a good price?\r\n\r\nMy other Q is, now that he\'s gettin a car, he\'ll have the obvious advantage over my truck. Would you recomend a certain model. Are the MR-02MM better than the 02MR chassis\r\n\r\nWas also thinkin bout goin with a used one. Worth it, or not?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-S'),(22580,'e215d94169','Hello --\r\n\r\nI\'ve just found this site and you seem to be on top of things, so to speak.  I experience the same problem with four USCG lifeboats and three island class cutters.  One motor rusts which ultimatelyI cannot break free  NKOK always replaces the boats but it is a hassle and it discourages from installing lights, rigging, etc.\r\n\r\nMost recently the starboard motor on the island class cutter will not run in reverse.\r\n\r\nI only run the boats in a swimming pool, thoroughly dry them,keep them inside, etc.  NKOK tech support is useless unless I want another new boat.\r\n\r\nAny suggestions?  Have you had these problems?  Are they fixable?\r\nShould I gut the innards and put in a new system?\r\n\r\nI appreciate any help.\r\n\r\nIn your debt,\r\n\r\nEd');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22581,'d3f6f6fcd0','well dude first of all id post this in the forum where a bunch of people can answer your questions.  thats pretty fucked up how they rust out that quick. id maybe put a little silicone sealer behind the props or some shit.'),(29216,'5939a7ccb0','its all cool man i am in the process of fixing my gaming computer so i know how it is :sad:  i was kinda wondering bout if u forgot or not :???: \r\n\r\njustin coats\r\n2748 stanton dr.\r\nsaginaw, MI 48601'),(23367,'5648de0871','[quote:5648de0871=\"kvik369\"]slight change -\r\n\r\n1 35 mhz BCG                - fet\r\n\r\n1 49 mhz Zip                  - fet\r\n\r\n1 27 mhz Nakamachi       - fet and steering wire switch\r\n(a BCG 27 mhz controller can control this - the steering is backwards though - I don\'t have the original controller but I think this is wired backwards anyway - I probably have almost every controller out there and nothing works correctly.)\r\n\r\nAnd the zip/ms and controller.  Paypaling as we speak\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n   Vik[/quote:5648de0871]Okey doke. Got your payment.\r\n\r\nIf the MS controller works but the steering is backwards, then a wire swap should fix the problem, but I was curious, doesn\'t the Nakamichi have like a \"turbo\", or a second speed? How does that work, I forget?\r\n\r\nDave'),(23930,'b41432b31a','nelly makes them way way way more fun dude. the install isnt that hard.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24164,'7f6bf9a34d','Hey, just a few questions on painting Bit bodies. Yours always seem to come out nice, are you using a air brush or rattle cans? Any other tips? \r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\nKanye.'),(24165,'67a803a2c1','I use \"Rattle Cans\"  Lately I\'ve been using Dupli-Color automotive paint.\r\nIt readily available, you can pick it up at just about any Automotive store, K-Mart, Wal-Mart, Target, etc.  about $3-$4 a can.  I don\'t like Plasti-coat, sprays too thick, you tend to lose a lil detail.  Never spray in a humid environment, heat the paint in a mug of hot water for about 5-10 minutes (not boiling) this will make the paint spray &amp; lay more smuthly.\r\n\r\nLater  :cool:'),(22589,'f552068f92','[quote:f552068f92=\"hue35\"]Hey man... I feel all honored and shit. I\'m in and I\'m sure SF is too. He\'s got a funny dilemma, so he\'s sortin\' through some shit... that fucker. I should let him fill you in, but I wanted to touch base and he\'s been swamped all day. It has to do with somethin\' he just finished up (pure sickness) in combination with the \'no contest eligibility\' facet of the new role... he\'s fuckin\' hilarious. \r\n\r\nAgain, I\'m happy as hell to be invited into the mod squad... I wouldn\'t be interested in that role anywhere but here. lol... not that I post anywhere else, unless it\'s for the sole purpose of stirring up shit. \r\n\r\nThanks Cabo[/quote:f552068f92]aight brutha - I\'ll wait until SF gets his stuff all sorted out and contacts me, then we\'ll make you guys moderators.'),(26391,'011c04d028','[quote:011c04d028=\"sg219\"]Was it hard to do?  :???:\r\n\r\nIf it wouldn\'t be too hard to explain...\r\n\r\nHow do you do it?  I\'d like to put one up for my site.  Either PM me or....\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if it would be worth putting in the thread, but I\'m sure if you did, someone would use the info.\r\n\r\nHappy Holidays, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike[/quote:011c04d028]nah it\'s not hard at all.\r\nbasically you just make your icon file, upload it and name it specifically favicon.ico and that\'s it, or you could use a header link.\r\n\r\nthis link will explain it all.\r\nhttp://msdn.microsoft.com/library/default.asp?url=/workshop/Author/dhtml/howto/ShortcutIcon.asp\r\n\r\nHappy Holidays to you too bro!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34090,'b951b749c0','[quote:b951b749c0=\"SHAUN\"]sup how ya doing im ok i finaly got to walmart and got my paint y was i in a big hurry to go to walmart the primer isnt dri yet  :?  hmmmm oh well hi[/quote:b951b749c0]\r\n\r\ncool man, HI!'),(34091,'7e6f6d8915','Kamen says you guys are \'getting tight\'. :shock: \r\n\r\nHe\'s okay, I used to talk to him alot, until be just kept pushing it one day.\r\nI\'ll share the convo with you sometime, I have it saved.'),(37665,'c7facb097f','[quote:c7facb097f=\"skylinekid\"]My paypal addy is  skylinekid91@gmail.com  \r\n\r\nAnd what color would you like the CD cases in, and thanks very much for the support :-o[/quote:c7facb097f]\r\n\r\nI\'m thinking about the colors and particular types of designs, will get back to you in a day or two. Thanks!'),(35154,'8ed682232e','Thanks man, but I got it now... I was just signing on to fix my deal. I just switched service, so I was in limbo for a few, then I slacked for a few, and here I am.  :lol:'),(31560,'523ecdf175','I got the holders today.... they are great thanks a million :grin: ... I just have to make sure I don\'t melt the fuck out of these :shock: \r\nyou are the greatest !\r\nfilelicker');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33364,'7fef8f7837','Naw i ment the way you said \"what you sayin\" as in watup, you know? They don\'t get it, yeah they flipped out but w/e shit happens, i just don\'t like that skyline kid.  :o'),(31429,'3ffc5a21c7','how much are you selling the bodies for? if you have aim messenger im me at suprakid95 or get back to me here'),(31431,'890768f85b','I went back last night, and they had buttloads of silver Vettes. So I went ahead and grabbed you one. I\'m gonna order FETs tomorrow morning, and we\'ll be all set to go.\r\n\r\n.dave'),(31432,'d58fe7aec6','i think bonzer just means a heater, electric or gas. or hang it up and get you mum\'s hair dryer onto it.\r\nthose offroaders of mine are staying with me, sorry!  :lol:'),(37085,'7da4c9d365','Word to Big Bird... Do it to it.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37086,'6f5afc92f9','[quote:6f5afc92f9=\"Maxximum Attack\"]US$300 so that he can buy 2 sets. I have to contact him and see what he can do for me. I\'m gunna have to start harassing these ppl for my money dammit  :o \r\n\r\nI\'ll keep in touch\r\nMaxx[/quote:6f5afc92f9]\r\n\r\nFor two sets it would be:\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Purple \r\nDXME100R	DELRIN REAR BALL DIFFERENTIAL - 1 COMPLETED SET	$20.15	2\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$15.47	2\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	2\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$31.07	2\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.47	2\r\nXME021	ALLOY FRONT KNUCKLE ARM - 1PR	$12.87	2\r\nXME022	ALLOY REAR KNUCKLE ARM -1 PR	$12.87	2\r\nXME028	ALLOY FRONT SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$10.27	2\r\nXME030	ALLOY REAR SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$10.27	2\r\nXME039F	ALLOY FRONT WHEEL SHAFT - 1PR	$5.07	2\r\nXME039R	ALLOY REAR Wheel SHAFT - 1PR 	$5.07	2\r\nXME039R/C	ALLOY REAR UNIVERSAL SWING SHAFT (CVD DESIGN) - 1PR	$17.94	4\r\nXME049/0	ALLOY STEERING PLATE - 1PC	$8.45	2\r\nXME055	ALLOY FRONT LOWER ARM - 1PR	$10.27	2\r\nXME056	ALLOY REAR LOWER ARM - 1PR	$10.27	2\r\nXME190R	ALLOY REAR DOG BONE (9.0MM) - 1PR	$6.50	4\r\nXME316F	ALLOY FRONT DAMPER (16MM) -1PR	$7.67	2\r\nXME316R	ALLOY REAR DAMPER (16MM) - 1PR	$7.67	2\r\nXME331R	ALLOY REAR SKID PLATE - 1PC	$4.55	2\r\nMZ002	ALLOY 2MM LOCK NUT SET  5PCS	$7.60	2\r\n\r\nSub	$241.45\r\nS&amp;H 4%	$9.66\r\nTotal(USD)	$251.11\r\n\r\nIf you get XME039R/4WD you dont need XME039F, XME039R or XME190R.  Do you want the CVD or the dog bones or both?'),(37862,'6be1365631','[quote:6be1365631=\"Sporttracguy\"]Thanks bro, the motor came a few days ago and looks great.  Ive never seen that much bubble wrap crammed into suck a tight space  :-o  lol\r\n\r\nThanks again, always a pleasure\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:6be1365631]\r\n\r\nI actually wanted to see how much I could get in there. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\nI have so much around.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHave fun. :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37288,'9349e502e8','No I don\'t. I dont realy know if I can drift better than you or not on a game-will never know till we go head to head. I was just saying that to bullshit; you were getting on my nerves with your drifting sigs. \r\n\r\nHowever, I said I could drift better than you in real life, with a real car, and a drivers liscence. I\'ve drifted a minivan(I\'m real proud of that). You\'re not even old enough to drive.'),(31802,'cbab93b3da','Yeah, you know, bad day yesterday. I was disappointed, but after a bad day at work, I came home and kinda snapped. I had a lot of pent up frustration I had to get out somewhere. :lol: \r\n\r\nAnyways...\r\n[quote:cbab93b3da=\"SuperFly\"]BTW, sorry for lagging on sending you the cash. I will get it out this week. Got hit with the 6-month car insurance bill and an unexpected dentist visit that has sucked me dry for the time being. I\'m waiting to get paid for an e-bay deal so I have some Paypal money to play with.[/quote:cbab93b3da]Cool about the cash, that\'s going toward my Iwaver, and Tower don\'t have them yet, so I\'m in no hurries. :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:cbab93b3da]How much extra to add the DC mod along with the FETS? :???:[/quote:cbab93b3da]Well code charges $10 for the DC Mod, so I guess $10. Have to order it from him though. That\'s something I should have mentioned in the review, this is not something you can just order from Digikey, he has to program it. Not sure if you realized that.\r\n\r\nAnyways, it\'ll add to the time to get your car finished, but I was planning to order another for myself anyways. \r\n\r\ndave'),(27492,'276ea9f9a1','Yo bro,\r\nIf it\'s a panther brand sold local/rebadged Shen, then those stores should have one sooner or later.  Yeah, for 25 fuckin bucks I better shit my pants, too. $11.95 is what I got the Gloria bodykit for at Toysnjoys, and if I can get shen copy (WRX too, I\'ve seen some for 6$)I can make what I\'d consider to be a ride of the month- A custom Gloria stretch limo.\r\n\r\nI like the open headlights look of the inital D sprinter, and I wonder if the AE86 tuneup kit looks the same as the pullback?  One thing\'s for damn sure, they both look way better than the stupid Radioshack kit!  I never did like most ZZ\'s.\r\n\r\nAfter these orders come in, I gotta start finding a Ferarri Testarossa body or a knockoff lying around.  I think it\'s too new for that though.  Miami Vice forever, bitch!\r\n\r\nHit me back!\r\nLate,\r\nAbe');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25758,'b36e9130a6','[quote:b36e9130a6=\"Bird\"]Cool. Thanks man, I was just wonderin\'...\r\n\r\nI guess I just wanted to hear the opinion of someone with some perspective... all of the people that \"reviewed\" them either seemed biased or like they were trying to suck up to suntzu... At least hearing about it from you I know that you\'re not just trying to sell one...\r\n\r\nThanks man...\r\n\r\n\r\nJay[/quote:b36e9130a6]Yeah, unfortunately I\'m biased now too. Biased because those mofos pissed me off, and no matter what I feel like dissing this car. When in fact I think I\'m supposed to love this car, but I just can\'t bring myself to enjoy it now. That\'s why I\'m more than willing to sacrifice it to my MT.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, Azimov offered the car to me, but it didn\'t come from him, it came from from someone in Canada. Being that the steering kinda sucks, the quality is typical clone stuff, and the throttle is only three steps. he was being misleading selling these at $35 claiming they are propo, and great. So I\'m confused, like I feel like I was starting to cause problems (i.e. the cars were not selling), so my silence was bought, but I have to ask, \"Why did they send this to me, they gotta know I\'m gonna tell everyone the truth?\"\r\n\r\nMaybe they really thought I\'d love them, not being able to FET mod a SE themselves, but while this car is clearly faster, the FETed SE will make better lap times on a tight technical track every time, because it steers better, and is proportional. That combined with only having 2 frequencies, makes this a just for fun car. I want a serious racer that has potential to progress the 1/64th hobby closer to the level of other scales. In that respect I think the SE blows the Panther away hands down, and I also think that\'s what other expected this car to be, the next level beyond a SE. That\'s the exact point that I feel people were misled. These are not the next step, they are the in between step RS kinda skipped over.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, we thought these would be all over by Christmas, and they\'re just not happenning. Which is too bad, because if they were offered at a reasonable price they would have some modding potential, such as the MT. Maybe I need to drop a positive review, entice people to buy, so people start stocking these before it\'s too late.\r\n\r\ni don\'t know :-? \r\n\r\n\r\ndave'),(23737,'46fc2b5b25','i got a little space. email them to me\r\n\r\nmyaaiko@comcast.net');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32829,'377e687c18','HEY\r\n\r\nfrizzen, i also live in indy, and i love bits. i have been trying to find somebody else for a LONG time who likes bits and lives in indy...\r\nmabye we can get toghther sometime? i own a super bit, and a third generation SE, and a messed up monster. \r\n\r\nkeher'),(31494,'16149b80a9','i saw your work on lowering and i must say AMAZING Many propz to you! But i cant figure out how to lower my Bit imj a newb to Bodywork and was woundering if you could help me by writing a tut or something..\r\n\r\ncan you lower without a dremel?'),(35371,'f7fd877111','Hey, that is good news.  I saw where you were going to add some diff\'s on the gearbox group buy.  If that\'s the case, I\'ll just get in on them then.  Thanks CJ.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(37775,'4e56e3576a','ok, i\'m all cashed up.\r\n\r\ngimme a paypal address and the final price (in usd) and i\'ll send the cash and give you a shipping address :-)'),(37287,'8bcf74b2b6','Do you have any online ps2 or pc game that you can drift on. You say your better than me but lets se who is better on a game atleast.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37362,'40971acd10','Yes I am interested, Could I get a price, and some pictures maybe.'),(37671,'723a57869c','Great fuckin info!!!\r\n\r\nThank you once again man...\r\n\r\n\r\nWell it looks like i am going to land myself an iwaver ball diff, and perhaps use the iwaver spring sets as well...\r\n\r\nI am going to look further into the oil damper, that is probably the best thing.\r\n\r\nLastly save up for some Gandini\'s....best places to buy them all is my next question big guy?'),(26889,'96cda90009','Whats up bud?\r\n\r\nYour stuff is all packed up...packing p-nutz and all. So it will go out immediately whenever you are ready.'),(24149,'45f49a9b69','[quote:45f49a9b69=\"KaNye\"]Got it today! I apreciate the fast shippin, and the nice packaging.  :-)  Im afraid I didnt have access to anything but a box and some paper as protection.\r\n\r\nThanks again, let me know when you get yours,\r\nKanye.[/quote:45f49a9b69]\r\n\r\nAlright, I got the body today... I didn\'t think it was coming UPS, which also explains the little bit of delay. It looks great, thanks for packin\' it up so nice... I can always use another Challenger.\r\n\r\nThanks again,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(22598,'f59d63e244','[quote:f59d63e244=\"SuperFly\"]Oh man, you just had to ask now! Of course I\'m honored to be considered for the position. Hue said he told you why I hadn\'t responded yet, and it\'s true. The selfish ego side of me was just waiting for the next contest to unleash my latest creations. I have some seriously badass rides finished or finishing up. My best work yet.\r\n\r\nFuck it, yeah, I\'m in. I\'ll just have to floss like normal and shoot for ride of the month. Thanks for asking me. Will I be able to ban hue?[/quote:f59d63e244] :lol:  this is gonna be good\r\n\r\nalrighty then - you guys both should be on inside soon.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22600,'76d91365b8','finks i am soo into this shit , and let me get this right, u r saying that my chevy impala will be the body that will be used here. i am way down with that, and it will need to fit a zz, which is sweet because u would want to have throttle control, so u could layback and cruise or when the need for speed is there just punch it. \r\n\r\ni am cool with it, just let me know if its going to happen...\r\n\r\njmays'),(22601,'414641723d','Good glad to know you are in.  All we need from you is to get that body done so you can cast it.  The rest of the pimps will take it from there.  Course what you will be doing will be creating the frame work that they will build on, and this ride looks to be a killer!  I have a feeling that this car will go down it Bit Pimps history, if not RC history :eek:'),(27899,'aa57c19fd0','Yo mang. \r\nI need your shipping info so I can send you some of these sticker decals. \r\n\r\nThey\'re on the white background so you\'ll have to cut them out. \r\nJust peel them off and stick. \r\nThese aren\'t the best by far, but maybe you use them - if not, no biggie.\r\n\r\nPS, your Hotmail account is bouncing emails back, it\'s full or something.\r\nUse your ISP provided email.\r\nYou could create a new folder in your inbox and create a rule to move (or delete or block or whatever) all messages from bitPimps and other places if wanted.'),(36418,'b10b6edc77','Id be interested in the evo, is it still up for grabs?\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36419,'297616a5ef','OI!  Thanx.  I just got the package today.  Mounted up those gandini foams.  Them are some good arse tires.  Loads better than stock.\r\n\r\nQuick question.  Can the spider handle the plasma-atomic well.  I just blew the 2 X 3 stack of 7317\'s I had in there.  I probably pushed it too much.  I was running it for about 1 1/2 hours steady.  I probably should have given it a break, but I couldn\'t put it down.  I\'m addicted.  The PCB looks OK still.  I was thinking about using a spider.  Will I have to give it a break between runs, so I don\'t blow it as well.  I know the resistance is much lower, but what about the heat?  I already know about using a heat sink.  That\'s something I will definately do.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, I think the MR-02 is at bit of a disadvantage with the OG fet swapping.  The 2 X 3 stack placed the fets pretty close to the batteries, which run pretty warm after some hard running.  They\'re too close to the batts and closed in.  They really need some air to cool them off.  A spider of-course can be placed away from the batts and given a heat sink.  Just wondering what you thought.\r\n\r\nOne more question.  Will I loose the break function?  Not a big deal really.  Just curious.  At the speed it\'s at now, the breaks don\'t work like they\'re made to anyhow.\r\n\r\nI\'ll probably pick one up soon anyhow.  I need to pick up some more gandini\'s and a few other things.\r\n\r\nThanx for your time.  Sorry about all the questions.'),(27994,'6664230205','Hey DT I found this on ebay and thought you might be interested. http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5956572263&amp;rd=1');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28553,'0990b70607','i have all the xmod stuff you need the ep just needs battery wires sautered on'),(35277,'f8843f5188','Hey Sess,\r\n\r\nImo be Flossin some rides in the weeks before the contest ends so get yo \"Wall Paper\" juices flowin and hook a Brutha Up  8-) \r\n\r\nThanx Pimp !'),(37747,'9df2a23e27','How much are you willing to trade? So far, you\'ve greatly impressed me.'),(35286,'ffb01678cb','I\'ll send via usps airmail to turkey for $ 15 extra to help cover inschurance.'),(35438,'1c1c4ad6b4','[quote:1c1c4ad6b4=\"Bithigh707\"]Hey I know it\'s been awhile but I had won the last car on the acution and something had happen that the car was owed to someone else and you told a pimp that i would get one from whom ever and that they would holla at me and that never happen so I was wondering what happen to my car  it fucked that i never got anything no email nothing[/quote:1c1c4ad6b4]\r\nWhat? I never told you that and that is nothing close to what happened, allow me to tell you how it went.\r\nI remember this clearly, [i:1c1c4ad6b4]you[/i:1c1c4ad6b4] were the one that had won the auction for the car... and low and behold you couldn\'t pay up. We waited and waited and got nothing but excuses from you as to why you couldn\'t pay for what [i:1c1c4ad6b4]you[/i:1c1c4ad6b4] had bid on.\r\nYou were then made aware (along with everyone else) that since you could not pay in a timely matter, the next highest bidder would get the car.\r\n[i:1c1c4ad6b4]That[/i:1c1c4ad6b4] is exactly what happened.\r\nMaybe the pills you took for the \"back pain\" you had messed with your memory? (Yea, I remember your \"broken back\" story too - see I got a great memory)\r\nYou want a car? Pay for it next time we run an auction - if you\'re the winning bidder.\r\nDon\'t be trying to play us for a free car dude, you\'re already on thin ice with me.'),(26865,'abfa404c02','Yeah, they rock. For real. As far as differences goes. I don\'t know.\r\nI got one only. Don\'t think they would differ. Mine was the monster patrol.\r\nThe steereng motor is hard wired clone motor(some cheap toy).\r\nit helps a lot, big difference. But it takes considerable amount of power.\r\nI would suggest tri-cell. It flies, sick air on jumps. Power adapter for charging is the must have. \r\nLast word, best micro rc for the buck you spend.\r\n And, no, i don\'t have one for sale.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31901,'357c4d2f0d','[quote:357c4d2f0d=\"DarkTari\"]He\'s Baaack !\r\n\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;postid=192037#post192037[/quote:357c4d2f0d]\r\n\r\nBlah, this explains it:\r\nhttp://www.freewebs.com/mototuner05/aboutme.htm\r\n\r\nOur little mosquito is only 12yrs old.  :roll: \r\n\r\nI\'ll leave it up to you how far to mess with him, he register (and re-registered) with these 2 email accounts:\r\n\r\nanthony7893@hotmail.com \r\ncrazysk8r777@yahoo.com'),(24931,'0a157a9ae4','Yea that 350z is cool if you want to part with it if so Here\'s my adderss D.wilson 1732 waters av McKinleyville Ca. 95519.'),(29674,'a730eee8ea','I was wondering how much do you sell the VW bus for?'),(27830,'d0cc9a5382','yup im intrested . ive needed tthem since the day i got the car and could never find them for a resonable price .'),(27831,'864b01c588','Cool, send me your address, and I\'ll send them out\r\n\r\nJustin Long\r\n132R Danforth St.\r\nPortland, ME 04101'),(35026,'a097ffd985','Oct 27 and Nov 8.\r\n\r\nI\'m pumped to get my MZM running. I\'m not sure if I\'m going to keep it now that I\'ve seen the light of brushless 1:18. I don\'t know. I\'ve got to see if it can handle the 1:10 supercross track now that we hardpacked it with clay. It might be alright.\r\n\r\nAnyway, thanks man. I\'m really looking forward to getting this 3rd cell mounted.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31010,'74a0759c13','i am lookin to get some lipos for my xmod since 3 of my ratshackes died out at the same time(have no idea why :-? ) so i remembered u had put iwaver guts in one and were going to put the 700s in but never did?\r\ni was wondering if u knew how well they fit. i measured it all out and it looks like it would cut it close to those front wheels. any suggestions welcome :-o \r\nthanks pimp :)'),(31011,'1019d601a7','how come after browsing around on your site for a while it shows this when i try to click on a link on your site \r\n  \r\nYahoo!  \r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n \r\n\r\nSorry, this site is temporarily unavailable!  \r\nThe web site you are trying to access has exceeded its allocated data transfer. Visit our help area for more information.\r\nAccess to this site will be restored within an hour. Please try again later.\r\nhttp://geocities.com/bettyk3332003/ \r\n\r\n  Need extra data transfer? Sign up for GeoCities Pro or Webmaster. Learn more.'),(34215,'e969d44250','Bid on it for me please, I haven\'t heard finks. \r\n\r\n[url]http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6004969682&amp;category=44015&amp;sspagename=rvi:1:1v_home[/url]\r\n\r\nThanx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36691,'d35d2c5f70','The part you need for the rear body clip, if you would do that. I have an almost complete evo chassis and im pretty sure i would have what you need to fix the front if you know what it is, let me know. Thanks!'),(36389,'fa6f6774ec','[quote:fa6f6774ec=\"arfin\"]Hey, well the money is set, if you have time the next time you go to radioshack, could you pick up 3, if they don\'t have 3, then give me what they do have. Thanks man![/quote:fa6f6774ec]\r\n\r\nThey had no TA sets. Those are probably sold out.  If I see any, I WILL pick them up for ya!'),(34032,'7b16090ceb','You know what, I\'m just gonna hook you up \'cause I\'m in a good mood.\r\nSend me your addy and I\'ll send you a chassis.'),(22611,'b82219c84e','and now ya got it. lol\r\n\r\nwe\'ve been discussing for sometime now the idea of creating another group of moderators, ones assigned to specific sections.\r\nwe wanted this new group of moderators have the powers needed to make certain sections their \'home\' so to speak, while not taking anything away from them (in the sense of contests and such).\r\n\r\nfor each person we have decided to ask to join this group, we envisioned a \"main\" or specific role they might fill as a primary task, while able to support in the other forum sections as a secondary task.\r\n\r\nAside from that, the chores are typical...\r\nmoving, editing, or deleting posts that require it. (no hogjowlz whims lol)\r\nhelp keep the forums clean and organized.\r\nprovide support for questions when you can.\r\n\r\nso with that, we came up with the \"bitPimps Wrecking Crew\".\r\nwhile this group does have moderators priviliages in specific forums, the groups members are still eligible to compete in contests.\r\nthis group as a whole has moderators priviliages over the following forums:\r\n(we might add to it as time goes by)\r\n- Modifications / Tutorials / How-To\'s\r\n- Mod Request / Wish List\r\n- Weird Science Laboratory\r\n- XMOD Crib\r\n- Mini-Z Hizzle\r\n- Miscellanious Micro R/C\'s &amp; Other Hobbies\r\n- Flossin\' In Da\' City\r\n- Custom Jobs\r\n- It Ain\'t No Bit\r\n- Tracks\r\n\r\nso what do you think?\r\nwant to see behind door #1? lol\r\nlet me know.'),(22616,'24af1488fe','hey finks i cant cast the body cause i ran out of the rtv rubber, would it be ok if we used the original, i could in a couple of weeks get some more rtv though. it really does not matter to me if i have it atleast that i know that all the best went into it for a good reason.\r\n\r\njmays');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37930,'34d9d5ff3e','[quote:34d9d5ff3e=\"steelwoolghandi\"][quote:34d9d5ff3e=\"SuperFly\"]I realize I said I would paypal you $30, but I forgot about shipping. If ya feel like you can trust me, you can package it up and mail it, and just tell me how much postage was and I\'ll paypal ya that amount. However you want to do it is cool with me.[/quote:34d9d5ff3e]\r\n\r\nI trust ya but I can send it for $4.00 if that sounds fair I will try and drum up some Crystals if I can find them and send them along. \r\n\r\nplease send your address and I will get it out monday. \r\n\r\noh and my paypal is my email airo@ev1.net \r\n\r\nthanks man hope ya like the Epoch I know I like them a ton! :grin:[/quote:34d9d5ff3e]\r\n\r\nSounds good. Are the crystals the same size as mini-z/xmod crystals? If so, don\'t worry about it, I have extras.\r\n\r\nWhat body is on it btw? Any other details?\r\n\r\nGreg Maffei\r\nGrey Matter\r\n431 NW Flanders, #203\r\nPortland, Oregon 97209'),(22618,'beb5b03eef','No worries at all J, get the stuff later, this project will take a while to finish, will be done around cristmas time with all the shipping and the reality factor.  I ONLY want a casting.  Your work on that ride needs to have the origional stay in your house, it\'s too bad ass to let go.  Anyway, I figure DT will chop up the casting pretty good, so it would be nice for you to have the origional so you can make more for other pimps and make some cash.\r\n\r\nAlso, the body work doesn\'t need to be started until the chassis is modded by Crazy Dave, HogJowlz and Payaso.  Only thing I would work on now bro is just finishing YOUR ride now, and worry about this project after 8-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37807,'cb3a1c4370','You didn\'t offend me and if you think that\'s me going nuts, well, ya aint seen nothing yet. :-)'),(36697,'cd9ba57247','[quote:cd9ba57247=\"stampede_dude\"]The part you need for the rear body clip, if you would do that. I have an almost complete evo chassis and im pretty sure i would have what you need to fix the front if you know what it is, let me know. Thanks![/quote:cd9ba57247]\r\nHaven\'t had time to open it up yet!  I\'ll letcha know when I know....'),(34366,'984800cf75','Hey, once i get mine, if i can\'t get used to the controller, maybe we can both mod them at the same time, or both think of a way. If i do this, i will be using an Epoch controller, cheapest i can find, and i have an extra.'),(35292,'9a9447a4ca','[quote:9a9447a4ca=\"sessiz\"]No problem man, just send me some clean pics of the rides if ya can. :-)[/quote:9a9447a4ca]\r\nAs clean as I can get \'em !\r\n\r\nThanx!\r\n\r\nCan you do anything with the this:\r\n[img:9a9447a4ca]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10005/ChopShop%20Trans2.jpg[/img:9a9447a4ca]'),(37898,'0c760ffe9e','Someone asked that about the original spider turbo and a bunch of aussies got all ancy and started going off with &quot;Aaron did all the R&amp;D on this himself....blah blah blah&quot;. Then when someone, I forget who, got a defective one that blew his car, the car was sent to ph2t for repair. There\'s something about that in the throw \'em under the bus thread.\r\n\r\nSo I personally think its just a another group effort aussie marketing scheme. Those guys are always looking to cut a buck... but then again, they are a penal colony, kinda makes sense. :lol:  \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34286,'f87545c67f','not sure if i was one of the ones, but figured it can\'t hurt...\r\n\r\nrichh\r\n\r\nRich Huang\r\n354 Mayo Ln\r\nBloomingdale, IL 60108\r\n\r\nthanks'),(34296,'cc04b48855','[quote:cc04b48855=\"DarkTari\"][quote:cc04b48855=\"hue35\"]I feel like my OG bit collection is just about done, but I need a coupla things... I need a Tomy Calsonic Skyline and the original silver Fairlady Z 2-speed car. If you have extras you\'d wanna part with, or run across either of these, would you mind giving me a head\'s up? \r\n\r\nthanks,\r\n\r\nhue35[/quote:cc04b48855]\r\n\r\nWill Do Hue !\r\n\r\nI\'m looking for a Fairlady myself.  I sent mine to MicroAmps and it got lost in transit along with my Audi SE and something he won off eBay. I replaced my Audi and just won another one off eBay.  The Z is one car that I have not seen out here since I lost mine. I\'ll get in the trenches and find us a couple  :-o \r\n\r\nThe guy I got my Calsonic &amp; Voltz from hasn\'t posted on eBay in a while.  I\'ll pop him an email and see what\'s up 8)[/quote:cc04b48855]\r\n\r\nThanks man... if I do find a little pile of Fairlady\'s, I\'ll grab one for you as well. Man, I was always gonna avoid the whole \"collector\" phase of this hobby, but it\'s actually where I\'ve landed... dammit! Oh well, at least I\'m close to done with my collection... I don\'t really keep the boxes of most of it, either... just the cars in perfect shape in their garage. I gotta be able to get \'em out, hold \'em up and admire \'em.  :cool: \r\n\r\n[quote:cc04b48855=\"DarkTari\"]...He also mentioned he had some other rare Bit stuff but didn\'t elaborate and that he was suppose to have been getting more.....???[/quote:cc04b48855]\r\nHmm... I wonder if he\'s got the Trueno set... :???: ... that\'s one I\'d love to get my hands on, but I figured that was pretty much impossible. If you have a chance at an extra one of those, count me in... cost would almost not be an issue on that one... well, not exactly, but you get the idea.\r\n\r\nThose gold/silver cars are interesting... I remember seeing those a long time ago. I\'m not feeling the need to have those ones, though... unless the price was right.\r\n\r\nThanks again, and I\'ll keep my eyes open for stuff you might be interested in too.\r\n\r\n-hue35'),(23837,'d284744221','That worked out nice with the other guys controller.  :-D   I hope the ZZ doesnt give you any trouble, i had to fix it before it was sent out. \r\n\r\nLet me know when there sent out. I cant wait!\r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\nKanye.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28056,'bbb6a3abbc','[quote:bbb6a3abbc=\"Mazda787b\"]Ok, well let me know what happens.  Actually, I will be strapping this into either a RC18, Xray M18T, or a Kyosho Mini777.  I am selling my Mini-T.  But I need the Rx for the XXX-T I am trading a custom Xmod Chassis for.  Infact, I originalyl created it to be used with a 280 motor (what a coincidence),  Thanks, I was going to order from BPP anyways, I just mainly do not want to order fro mRcmart, because they kill you with shipping.\r\n\r\nLet me know what hapens,\r\n\r\nMazda[/quote:bbb6a3abbc]\r\n\r\nMazda:\r\n\r\nI\'ve been ordering little things from them and their shipping no longer wants you to crawl under your bed and whimper.\r\n\r\n-Max'),(36623,'ce53cb13ac','Thanks Cabo!'),(36629,'ad1a9effe0','Hey man do you know where I can get some wheel barrings??\r\n\r\nI will get out the money on Monday!\r\n\r\nthanks again man always great to do biz with ya!  :-)'),(32117,'895d44af4b','[url]http://cgi.ebay.com/Logitech-Elite-USB-Keyboard-For-Windows-PC-Mac-New_W0QQitemZ5793017751QQcategoryZ33965QQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem[/url]\r\n\r\n[url]http://cgi.ebay.com/Mac-Apple-Design-ADB-Keyboard-Macintosh-M2980_W0QQitemZ5223900149QQcategoryZ25444QQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem[/url]\r\n\r\n[url]http://cgi.ebay.com/Logitech-Internet-Navigator-Keyboard-PC-MAC-USB-PS-2_W0QQitemZ5221078785QQcategoryZ33965QQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem[/url]\r\n\r\n[url]http://cgi.ebay.com/Apple-Mac-Macintosh-Design-Keyboard-ADB-Mouse_W0QQitemZ5223214244QQcategoryZ3666QQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem[/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37850,'1039778b9c','[quote:1039778b9c=\"Maxximum Attack\"]you never told me if the Fets from your friend were upgrade fets. And wheather I should try a stack and if it would make a difference.[/quote:1039778b9c]\r\n\r\nSorry about that bro i thought i mentioned it before.\r\n\r\nYes the ausmicro fet\'s are the best of the best, i think they are 7 amp fet\'s so doing a 3x2 stack or similar would basically give you a huge range of motor selection.\r\n\r\nCheck out ripper7racing under the mini-z section a couple of pages back Ph2t did a write up of the fets and the install onto a IW board.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(24730,'596c9aabf5','lol i knew it wasnt gunna be cheap,  im good i mainly wanted to know about the fets, thanks for the reply.'),(34808,'f74398cece','No fuckin shit man. For fucks sake the kid can\'t even spell \"what\" correctly. Unfortunatly I gotta get outta here so I\'m just gonna lock that shit down. I pray to the all mighty internet gods that he posts another bullshit thread when I\'m around. :lol:'),(32685,'51fedeaf8f','damn, you locked it right when I was replying to that! :lol: \r\n\r\nI was gonna tell him I had a \'wall\' to trade, too. :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34124,'4e76890132','Yes the original Iwaver 04 now sold as the Firlap 04 will need two steering resistors for anything over 6 volts.  The resistors should be in line with the black and red servo motor wires.  10 ohm resistors would be great.  However depending on the batteries you are planning on using you can even go as low as 3 ohms but thats a mater of experimenting to find the minimum resistance necessary to keep the steering from spazzing out for your battery setup.  I would start with 10 ohms then later if you feel you need a little stronger steering you could try lowering the value.  \r\n\r\nOr if you really need more steering power you can add an Epoch Turbo to it.  The ones I built for the Epoch where a little to big to be conveniently hidden away inside the 04 chassis but Ive been thinking that Ph2ts Bug might be a perfect fit, although I dont know if anyone has tried the Bug for the Iwaver steering yet.\r\n\r\nCheers'),(37652,'2ecf29ca0f','Sorry to hear that, man.\r\n\r\nWhen my father was still alive, he and I had trouble talking, too.\r\n\r\nI feel for you man.\r\n\r\nNext time you\'re in the area, just say so.  If you wanna grab a coffee and talk XMODS or whatever, let me know.\r\n\r\nPaul');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32540,'a161548545','Hi Chrome, thanks for that!\r\nI\'ll take the red mini if i can.\r\nWhat is your paypal address?\r\n\r\nbtw, my mailing address is \r\nMICHAEL FRAWLEY\r\nPO BOX 2010\r\nTOOWONG QLD 4066\r\nAUSTRALIA\r\n\r\nThanks again pimp!'),(32541,'b48c9fcb67','Sure thing with the red one.  Paypal addy is wvuchrome@gmail.com.  I\'ll get it out tomorrow morning.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(23236,'a07d8749d1','Hey man I am new to this board. I am by no means a Noob to RC I am currently big into xmods but would like to get my ZZ SE working, as it sits on a shelf collecting dust. Anyway I saw that you have had the best luck increasing the performance of the SE through fet mods and what not, and i was wondering if you offered any sort of install services?'),(23237,'e35a9ed19f','Yes I am still doing fet mods for people.\r\nhave a look at microamps.com.au and then email me from ther.\r\nAll the best\r\nuA'),(24674,'6eae823c78','Its all good bro\r\n\r\n\r\nIts \r\n\r\nPeter Kostecki\r\n20 Water St.\r\nThorold Ontario\r\nL2V 2K3\r\nCanada');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32736,'8c45f3a709','did you clean my mess up again????\r\n\r\nif ya did, thanks.\r\n\r\nI didn\'t see any mods on, so I PM\'d Cabo about it.\r\n\r\n(the double post in the computer screen topic)\r\n\r\nDOH! :-?  :grin:'),(32752,'32a3fb45cb','[quote:32a3fb45cb=\"weazel\"]i am fine w/ $3.85[/quote:32a3fb45cb]\r\n\r\n\r\nHey man, I sent your package via USPS just an hour ago.\r\n\r\nAnd it did come to exactly $3.85 for shipping, so cool!\r\n\r\n\r\n$3.85 +\r\n$1.50 =\r\n_______\r\n$5.35\r\n\r\nMy PayPal address is\r\n\r\ndaves@surfmk.com\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nit\'s in a box approx. 10\"-11\" square, usps priority.\r\nPM me when you receive it to make sure all is well!\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nDave'),(28529,'116369885e','[quote:116369885e]Need these bodies for a project I am working on. Just PM if you have one you want to sell or trade. \r\nthanks[/quote:116369885e]\r\nLemme check out [b:116369885e]Da Body Bag [/b:116369885e]and see what I can come up with...'),(32380,'aced288bfa',':eek: \n\nhttp://www.xmodsforum.com/ftopict-2423.html\n\n                                         \nhttp://www.undergroundxmods.com/catalog/product_info.php?cPath=42&amp;products_id=75&amp;osCsid=4755d561df66f9a269e7f1ef01f6a4aa\n\nhttp://www.undergroundxmods.com/catalog/product_info.php?cPath=42&amp;products_id=80&amp;osCsid=4755d561df66f9a269e7f1ef01f6a4aa                                                              \n\nhttp://www.undergroundxmods.com/catalog/product_info.php?cPath=42&amp;products_id=93&amp;osCsid=4755d561df66f9a269e7f1ef01f6a4aa                                                              \n\nhttp://www.undergroundxmods.com/catalog/product_info.php?cPath=42&amp;products_id=73&amp;osCsid=4755d561df66f9a269e7f1ef01f6a4aa');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23446,'d0efa5a834','[quote:d0efa5a834=\"KaNye\"]I heard you installed FETs on bits, is this true? ($10?) If so would you be willing to hook a pair of Bits or ZZs up for me? \r\n\r\nThanks pimp, \r\nKanye.[/quote:d0efa5a834]Yeah sure, $10 per car plus shipping.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested let me know, and I\'ll get you my info.\r\n\r\nDave'),(35536,'2687e6f3b3','[quote:2687e6f3b3=\"hue35\"]Now I\'mm gonna go home and :cool:  &lt;--- except smokeless.  :lol:   Man, I\'m lovin\' this vaporizer... I haven\'t \"smoked\" anything since I got it, and my lungs can tell the difference.[/quote:2687e6f3b3]Shit man, I think my lungs need one of them. I\'ve been afraid to look at them, because I\'m pretty shure they\'re more than the wife would allow for paraphernalia. :lol: \r\n\r\nWell gald you like the start on the car. I was actually just sitting down to take a break on it. I\'m finishing up the chassis getting ready for paint. Just carved it out for the Super Slick motor.\r\n\r\nMy wife just brought a big bag of peanuts in the shells from one of those dudes on the side of the road, and they rock. :rockon:\r\n\r\nDave'),(24731,'596c9aabf5','lol i knew it wasnt gunna be cheap,  im good i mainly wanted to know about the fets, thanks for the reply.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29345,'ad67a14956','[quote:ad67a14956=\"riceboi077\"]OK. 3 facts:\r\n\r\n1) I\'m 13.\r\n\r\n2) I have ADHD\r\n\r\n3) I have MEDICATION to treat it, and it works...but I still go crazy on forums.\r\n\r\nJust lettin you know, man ^^\r\n\r\nBy the way, where else can I get paint?[/quote:ad67a14956]\r\n\r\nI don\'t care what ya got, just settle down a notch. If you can take the time to explain your medical condition, then you can take the time to censor yourself a bit. Being hyper has nothing to do with you participation online.. you don\'t have to hit the submit button. Run around in circles or squeeze a ball, but don\'t clutter up this place with your spastic attacks... I feel for ya, in a social situation, but not here... again, you don\'t have to hit the submit button. \r\n\r\nJust relax, man... you\'ve got an average of 7 posts a day going right now. I have an average of about 1.75 posts per day. Not that you have to count, but just chill a little, ok? Also, don\'t start a new thread unless it\'s for a good reason... you\'ve started more new threads in the last 2 days than I\'ve started this year... again, you don\'t have to count, but just take your medication, breath and think twice or more before you go all post happy... it ain\'t gonna fly, and this is as nice as I get.\r\n\r\nStick around, have fun and participate when you\'ve got somethin\' really worth sayin\' (then think about it for a minute before you hit \'submit\'). Also, age has nothing to do with it... that\'s the beauty of the internet.. if you handle yourself a little more calm-like and hold back until you have something smart to say, nobody will care how old you are... you\'ll just be another dude here. Remember.. pimps are cool and calm. Ease in man, it\'s a lot easier that way.\r\n\r\nhue35'),(36135,'30ffe7037c','Let me know...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36137,'d3d23ceb96','Eh Timmy...\r\n\r\nWhat is a good after market motor for Xmods...very torquey, and won\'t kill my original board?'),(34727,'bcf87abf88','[quote:bcf87abf88=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:bcf87abf88=\"ph2t\"]http://shop.ausmicro.net/index.php?currency=USD&amp;cPath=25_39\r\n\r\n(can\'t help the plug, lol.............)[/quote:bcf87abf88]\r\nShutty... since when did we ever care about a link to some place else (other than in the Sale/Buy/Trade categories)?\r\nEspecially a \'pimps\' place - people gotta know the right place to get what.\r\n\r\nJust makin sure you know there\'s no worries man.\r\nThis your home too (one of em anyways lol).[/quote:bcf87abf88]\r\n\r\nshucks, feelin the love............\r\n\r\nthanks man.\r\n\r\nalso, I think we both posted in the \"competition hell\" post at the same time, so I don\'t really understand the context of your response, is it that the xcrl shit is the shitbag? lol....\r\n\r\nearly day at work and a fuck all sleep night, so I\'m slow today.'),(24297,'3acb30ae82','I need some wheels for my Acord and other cars too how much do they cost and can i even buy them from you  :???:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35031,'ca7edd502b','Hi, sorry to bother you...\r\n\r\nI was ready to buy an Evo Xmod today when my uncle interupted me and said that i should maybe save up and buy a MiniZ...Now i read a few things on both and I understand miniz got some crazy ass bodies, and with some velcro and a lil mod they might even fit on an Xmod chassis. I also realize the price of a MiniZ is more expensive than an Xmod, but i wanted to know what you thought was a better deal?\r\n\r\nIn Canada we can\'t get the Evo Chassis Xmod, but i found some online that came out to about 70 bucks Canadian, thats not bad considering the Source in Canada sells the original chassis for 69.99 plus tax...\r\n\r\nI wanted to know what you thought was a better deal. My uncle and I are hardcore Tamiya 1/10th scale racers. From this we wanted to build a race track in his basement for a smaller scale RC and I told him about Xmods and MiniZ. He feels MiniZ are better, but my gut feeling says Xmod...\r\n\r\nPerhaps you have both. So maybe yo ucan distinguish much of the difference for me...I want a competitive chassis, with some great hop ups, and speed, but yet controllable for a track, and of course some sweet bodies to go with it? Should i stick to my Xmod Fever. or give into his MiniZ persuasion....?\r\n\r\nThanks alot\r\n\r\nSam'),(24811,'d9976eb13f','Just to let ya know, I put your video in your album and changed the link on your post from rcpics.net to the file hosted here.\r\nour site seems to serve up the content quicker than rcpics.net.\r\n\r\nhere\'s the link to your video.\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/displayimage.php?album=181&amp;pos=7');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25744,'62fa25231c','[quote:62fa25231c=\"micro_man\"]thanks man ! my addy is \r\n\r\nmatt evink \r\n25085 cr388 Gobles MI\r\n49055[/quote:62fa25231c]\r\n\r\nI wanna make sure you and I have it right.\r\n\r\n\r\nMatt Evink\r\n25085 CR388\r\nGobles, MI    49055\r\n\r\nPssst....thats how you type an addy. :-) \r\n\r\nLet me know if its right.'),(24025,'609dacc046','Oh... I know that you don\'t have any chassis, the reason I was asking was because I need some more project materials.  I just moved to Texas and money is ridiculously tight right now.  My wife would kill my ass if she caught me buying new stuff.  Whatever you want to do is fine with me.'),(34736,'36f33522c0','[quote:36f33522c0=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:36f33522c0=\"ph2t\"]also, I think we both posted in the \"competition hell\" post at the same time, so I don\'t really understand the context of your response, is it that the xcrl shit is the shitbag? lol....\r\n\r\nearly day at work and a fuck all sleep night, so I\'m slow today.[/quote:36f33522c0]\r\nAbsolutely. I think we both mis-understood each other.\r\nYes - I think those dudes are jokes, I think that\'s obvious though.\r\n\r\nI guess the point I was trying to get across was that if he\'s a shitball, and you\'re not - I think that would show.\r\nTherefore, you going on the offensive, IMO, is like you bringing yourself down to his level. Something that you obviously don\'t [i:36f33522c0]need[/i:36f33522c0] to do, but I can understand why you would.\r\nTo me, and again - this is just my opinion, worrying about a shitball and taking action against it, almost cheapens you (for lack of better wording).\r\nI\'ll re-itterate though, I totally could understand where you might feel \"attacked\" and feel compelled to respond. I\'ve done it myself many times.\r\n\r\nMy comment about \"money\" wasn\'t directed soley at you or anyone. It was a generalization.\r\nI feel that when money is the ultimate motivator (not saying it is for you), it breeds the \"crook\" (for lack of a better term) in all of us.\r\nI don\'t want to see a good guy get burnt over his emotions.\r\nHell, I don\'t even know what road you were going down with your post, I just made a decision to try to be pro-active.\r\nI think ultimately it backfired, but hey - it\'s supposed to be the thought that counts right? lol\r\n\r\nAnyways, I hope that helps explain my comments and position on the whole matter.\r\nTo be honest. It really doesn\'t involve me, and overall - I\'m not losing any sleep over the entire thread. I just thought I was being helpful, but I think I worded it wrong or something and it failed to be helpful and was instead confusing.\r\n\r\nWhew. Fuck. That was a mouthful. :lol:[/quote:36f33522c0]\r\n\r\nlol, man, it\'s all good.  I know where you\'re comming from. I didn\'t mis-interpret, it\'s cool.  I know what you mean about the arguments n stuff, I tried to word my statements as carefully as I can, but sometimes it\'s like \"fuck it\", lol........'),(37797,'359f3919ac','no worries man your stuff is still here..just let me know exactly when your pronto and the stuff will be shipped!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37798,'9625d98237','[quote:9625d98237=\"Mad_Maxx\"]Hi mate!\r\nThanks for checking the shipping, it\'s a lot of $$.\r\ndid you meant 17$ with boxes?\r\nI think it should weight less without them,I\'m just interested in the bits, have none with boxes.\r\nWould you sell even a few bits?\r\n\r\nsee ya and thanks a lot,\r\n\r\nMax[/quote:9625d98237]\r\n\r\nDid some checking... it seems that for any box from an ounce up to a pound in weight is the same postage, $17.50.  So I could take them out of the packaging but it will be the same cost.  Seems like they treat anything under a pound the same.  The rate for Airmail letter is cheaper, but I don\'t think the bodies would make it in one piece in an envelope.\r\n\r\nRich'),(32673,'a2abd96621','That sounds great. It will be shipped Global Priority (4-6 day delivery. I\'ve been seeing 5 or 6 days to australia.)\r\n\r\njoseph.yarbrough@gmail.com is my paypal addy. it will be shipped tomorrow.\r\n\r\nI\'m with you on waiting forever for shipping. I bought a ultra dash motor off Ebay from a guy in singopore. What a mistake. I should have spent the extra $2.00 because it took 3 weeks to get here from s\'pore when hongkong shipping takes me 3-6 days (depending on day and time sent) for plain old speedpost (not EMS). EMS still takes 3 days, but I get a special delievery girl that brings it as soon as they get it off the truck! I live in a small town right off of a major hub on a major highway. which is killer for recieving shipments.\r\n\r\nAnyway. Thanks again,\r\n-JNY'),(35172,'3cb874bb36','Hey I bought a pcb from you that you put 13 fet\'s will it worked fine intil i let some do some modding and now it only goes backwards but i have to cars that i would like to have fets put on one is dual speed and tri cell and the other is stock would like to have it tri cell but would reallly like to see i can find lithum if they make them that small.anyway if you can or know someone that can do the work plz e-mail me at delano_wilson@hotmail.com also I am lookin for some alloies too.Oh the cars are bits');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23249,'a029ecff56','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=54904#54904'),(33926,'e05800d9ba','[quote:e05800d9ba=\"Clint\"]Hi Matt,\r\n\r\nIf you want them they are yours.\r\none is useable with a bunch of spacers under the front end. the front needs to be higher than the rear to prevent binding of the driveshaft for awd. it would work perfect without spacers on a rwd only car and then you could use a short fwd axle as a mini driveshaft.(there\'s a tut on doing this). that would give you TONS of room if you were to go proportional on a rwd only car.\r\n\r\nsee what you can do with them. send me your addy. dont worry about shipping i sure i can handle it. lol\r\n\r\n\r\noh btw, ive been really going at it with the ZZMT. i\'ll post some pics of what i did to it on monday when i get home. it is truly pimp. my coworkers \r\nthink im a fruitcake. :cool:  \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:e05800d9ba=\"Tuner1989\"]Would you mind shipping me those extra chassis that you made that werent up to par with you?\r\n\r\nI could pay for the chassis and shipping or whatever you want.\r\n\r\nThough it was worth a try since there sitting around.\r\n\r\nLet me know\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:e05800d9ba][/quote:e05800d9ba]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWow, Much appreciated clint thanks! And yeah pics of what youve been doing with that zzmt would be cool like to see what youve been up to.\r\n\r\nHaha \"my coworkers think im a fruitcake\" lol.\r\n\r\n\r\nOh and my addy\r\n\r\nMatt Gera \r\n4303 Radcliffe Dr.\r\nPalm Harbor Fl.\r\n34685\r\n\r\nThanks again clint!\r\n\r\nIm planning on using a iw 05 board and hs-55 servo. 4 cells too :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(36333,'8abbf07baf','Payment sent!\r\n\r\nCant wait to get it!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36334,'38642acb51','Thats helped me a bit, given me some ideas I haven\'t thought about.\r\n\r\nI\'ve been talking with a friend (davemud) and he\'s given me a better idea to the Iwaver board swap, to use an Epoch board, steering servo and encoder and the charging jack.  It\'s smaller, I can use my Iwaver radio and will be easier to charger.  Now all I need to figure out is how to wire it all up.\r\n\r\nAre you back home or still at your family\'s place?  I\'d love to see some more side shots, under shots and from inside chassis shots.  I\'m curious as to where you cut the car in half to make way for the suspension.  I\'m going to go for a flex plate and maybe a shock instead of your funky design, just to make it my own.\r\n\r\nThanks for all your help so far.  I\'ve had my ZZSE for quite some time, but never really got interested until now. :-o'),(36335,'f3af9f1980','Im at my girlfriends place until tomorrow, then ill be home so ill try and get you some pics\r\n\r\nSTG'),(27487,'10454e13a5','Checked there a month ago or so, and they don\'t got \'em.  They still list \'em like retards, though.  I think hobbyonsale still does that too.  I couldn\'t get a WRX bodykit or a Gloria bodykit from them, but they knocked off a big chunk of my order :grin: \r\nI already had a WRX body from this Auldey POS bit clone, but I should clean off it\'s \"Exercise Tip\" decals. It has the lamest shit I\'ve seen on a car, and the hood scoop was originally backwards, but a pearing knife and some superglue took care of that.  Stupid Auldey lack of quality!\r\n\r\nBut that is a nice pic, it\'ll look good as my \"car crap\" shortcut icon or on my desktop. I got the Gloria kit from Toysnjoys for 11.95 total.  The Sprinter cost me 25$ where I found it, and now they\'re out of stock too.  Shit happens, but if a clone company comes out with a Trueno clone, that would be fucking sweet, no?\r\n\r\nBouncin\' out,\r\nAbe');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37299,'6e3770d794','Thanks, well I took your advice and I am still going with the mr-02.\r\n\r\n2 weeks till some more hardcore racin...'),(27147,'a7da2fcbdd','[quote:a7da2fcbdd=\"stampede_dude\"]liek d00d i kno!!!!1111\r\n\r\nliek yoo can ad a bode kit!!!!!!!!!1111\r\n\r\nheh. thats the only way i know that would do it.[/quote:a7da2fcbdd]\r\n\r\nKnock this shit off Stampede_dud.\r\n\r\nType like your pimpin\' or get to gimpin\'!!!\r\n\r\nNo more of the AOL shit...EVER. :x'),(34508,'165aacfe3e','[quote:165aacfe3e=\"Nasphere\"]Soo, since you fly the mini choppers, could you tell me how to yaw?\r\n\r\nI spin slowly to one side. It starts sliding to the left, so i correct to the right, it then goes foreward. Thats when i loose it with coordination and crash... I thought ida had this down by now, but the fly times are rediculously low on the electric ones to get a decent amount of fly time in... I have a theory on my problem: I haven\'t been able to immagine myself [b:165aacfe3e]\'inside\'[/b:165aacfe3e] the copter, as they say is what you do when you are \"good\"...\r\n\r\nHere go the questions:\r\nDo you think walking around it while its hovering would help with my sense of direction?\r\n\r\nAbout you:\r\nDid you learn to fly with gas or electric? And, did you have an instuctor?[/quote:165aacfe3e] :lol: \r\nSorry dude. I guess my post was a little mis-leading.\r\nI know what I know about flying because my old room-mate flies planes and helicopters.\r\nI used to help him out and drive nitro trucks while he flew.\r\nHe tried getting me into flying, gave me all sorts of pointers and such - but I just never got into it.\r\nSo, I know just enough to get into trouble, but not enough to teach someone.\r\nSorry holmes.'),(28266,'8b3ec69467','Un fortunately no, didn\'t want to send it while we were bartering on the GPM\'s. I\'ll send it friday when i goto work. I\'m on crutches for the time being. I got hurt playing  soccer.\r\n\r\nSo friday, $65. I\'ll send it express.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34228,'04402bdaca','bid $64 at the very last minute. Highest, $65. No higher.'),(36123,'28932dae8d','Sup DT. Thanks for the reminder. I\'m working late, again, tonight. If I\'m not too spent when I get home, I\'ll dig these out, snap some pics, and holler back at ya tomorrow. Hope you had good holidays. MG'),(33085,'eea35330ef','Cool, thanks man.   That\'s smaller than I thought.   I need one now though...lol\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(28036,'735af5cfec','Ok, well let me know what happens.  Actually, I will be strapping this into either a RC18, Xray M18T, or a Kyosho Mini777.  I am selling my Mini-T.  But I need the Rx for the XXX-T I am trading a custom Xmod Chassis for.  Infact, I originalyl created it to be used with a 280 motor (what a coincidence),  Thanks, I was going to order from BPP anyways, I just mainly do not want to order fro mRcmart, because they kill you with shipping.\r\n\r\nLet me know what hapens,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(27696,'3c8eec6b0b','I have a question about using the Kyosho Perfex KT-2 with the iwaver board as you installed it in the MT.  Will it work?  I know that the iwavers and mini-z\'s are normally compatable.  But I was reading about somebody that swapped an iwaver board into an epoch and they said the thay couldn\'t use the kt-2.  So I just wanted to be sure.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27697,'342fa43a1d','i\'m pretty sure you can run an i wavr pcb with a kt2. i don\'t own one but i know that ph2t has used a kt5 (mad force) tx to run an iw02 without a problem.'),(24438,'e95e06ea18','[quote:e95e06ea18=\"DarkTari\"]I use Dupli-Color Auto paint.  You already have an airbrush, you need this\r\n\r\nhttp://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=34843[/quote:e95e06ea18]\r\n\r\n\r\n ahh sweet thanx for the link... I have a harbor freight by my house :) .. i\'ll have to go get one ...... Kool i aut to try the auto paint :)..... I got this testors kit at wall mart it was like 30 bux and i was like why not it came with 30 bottles of paint and a paint sorter rotating thingy... it is like a \'dual action\'  :smile:'),(25044,'2f48451f6c','Shit now that I have harvest my Weeeeeeeee I got the ends to buy alot o cars but thankz'),(34246,'596c74dcbd','No problem.  I\'ll get a regular picture with the paper soon.  I got off work tonight and passed out almost as soon as I got in the door.  Now it\'s midnight and I still got things to do.'),(32703,'45d0d9f4ae','[quote:45d0d9f4ae=\"sessiz\"] Unless ofcourse I catch his ass in chat. :lol:[/quote:45d0d9f4ae]\r\n\r\nshit, i forgot about CHAT! maybe I\'ll see ya there. :-) \r\n\r\nsee ya');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32810,'fc98197bff','Can I get a 1152x868 and a 1280x1024.'),(32711,'0f8c1180d7','as they say... small world.  i was born in northlake, grew up in addison. after college, i was in st. louis for about 3 years, then moved back to illinois (elmhurst, palatine, and now bloomingdale).'),(30754,'537c28d926','yup i still have the motors . $3 and change should cover it , let me know werer to ship it to . paypal addy is bhav4@juno.com'),(27699,'6804fa4c34','[quote:6804fa4c34=\"micro_man\"]ok man i had my dad paypal you around 3 pm , thanks for the motor , later . \r\n\r\nmatt[/quote:6804fa4c34]\r\n\r\nCool.  It\'ll go out in the morning. :-)'),(35264,'37c37a4af0','Ryan Eylander\r\n7701 Delridge Way SW apt. 9A\r\nSeattle, WA 98106\r\n\r\ngood stuff, i dont need the pinion gear from the motor, just the other red gear.  Ill get those gears out to you asap.\r\n\r\nThanks man, and i cant wait for that SE info\r\n\r\nSTG'),(37303,'1e9e52e8c0','I think by now i\'ve given you 1 of each, if you look at the top of them their shold be a veryy small and hard to read number. The 3 types are 1.5, 3, and 4.5. The stock one(yellow) is 0 the larger the number, the better turning radious you get, the smaller the better for straights, hope that helped :-) [/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36530,'1601ced4bc','some sort of... what? i\'m not an electronics guru, the stuff under my subie shell is stock-standard, an iwaver 01 board and a cirrus 4.4 servo. lithium-ion batteries came from batteryspace.com, motor is just a stage 2 with different endbell and magnets.\r\n\r\nnothing special, really... did you pm the wrong person?'),(31468,'3ecfa9a99a','alright. do you want 27 or 49mhz? Do you prefer a certain body style? I have some running to do tomorrow and I will be going by 2-3 radio shacks so I might be able to find the one you want. I would prefer for us to send them both at the same time. Check my ebay status (gamecocksrocks) and my feedback on undergroundxmods.com (username pimpsmurf). I\'m sure many people on undergroundxmods will tell you I\'m legit.\r\n\r\nLet me know,\r\n-JNY'),(32931,'86cb9696ba','How about a silver motor heatsink? not new, but almost. 2 small scratches that aren\'t really noticable.\r\n\r\nLet me know,\r\n-JNY'),(34661,'c46f44c40c','ok');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36768,'0425f192d8','lol i thought you said you wanted to hold on to it when i wanted it  :( . What are you looking for? I might still have some XMOD stuff left'),(34674,'8e61499a8b','[quote:8e61499a8b=\"SHAUN\"]your never on msn any more.[/quote:8e61499a8b]\r\n\r\nif you actually TALK while on MSN, I\'ll get on.'),(34675,'a91c35be20','Thanks \r\nIts all good! &lt;(oh yeah punctuation &amp; a capitol letter ) :-o'),(36865,'7bb76d7669','Aight, first depends on what type of media you want to embed into the webpage.\r\nIs it Windows Media, QuickTime, Flash, or RealMedia?\r\n\r\nFirst off, they\'ll all use the &quot;&lt;object&gt;&quot; and &quot;&lt;embed&gt;&quot; tags.\r\n&quot;&lt;param&gt;&quot; tags will be used to set variables like the source, controls, etc.\r\nHere\'s a link to a site that helps generate code for embedding different media types:\r\nhttp://cit.ucsf.edu/embedmedia/step1.php\r\n\r\nWithout knowing exactly what you\'re wanting to accomplish, I can\'t give you any code since I\'m not sure what type of media you\'re embedding, etc.\r\n\r\nThe link I gave you should pretty much handle the common formats.\r\nIf you still have troubles or questions, just shout.'),(35650,'eefc1c235c','I just got into putting body kits onto my bits and I was wondering Do you use credit card? Does it go on the outside of the bumper or under it, like where the bumper ends (incase you didnt get what i said) What do I use to keep it on? What do you use?\r\n\r\nWell if you could help me out :D\r\n\r\nThanks In Advance');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34741,'140c8ae565','You should be all set to go.\r\nCreate an album/s and then start uploading whenever.\r\nLet me know if you have any problems.'),(34748,'6993dc4d39','Hey got a question for ya.\r\n\r\nWhere did you get the powerquest 600mah lipo from?\r\nI searched all over and not one website sells them. Did you mean\r\nPoly Quest?\r\n\r\n-Clint'),(33135,'1eb6f59b6a','What a son of a bitch. I was cleaning out the shop and found your clone under a bunch of sandpaper I threw down.\r\n\r\nAint that a son of a bitch. I\'ll ship it out ASAP. I can\'t believe I forgot about that. I guess you will understand when I post fresh pics of my MZM tonight. 1 more clearcoat layer and I\'m finished! =)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37910,'5bf901bcd0','It\'s still in florida but my skybox has moved:\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\n1900 NW 97th Ave\r\nSTE 716993\r\nMiami\r\nFlorida 33172\r\n\r\nAny word on the GPM stuff for the 2nd group buy?\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx'),(35707,'57e299a30d','[quote:57e299a30d=\"MafiaS\"]GREAT MAN thanks for the quick reply!!!\r\n\r\nJust had a few more specific questions. It helps me to answer these on a one on one basis. \r\n\r\nAnyhow you mentioned your car had widetrack bearings? I purchased the radioshack bearings, but did you mean other bearings? \r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]These are different bearings that remove the wheel wobble,no need to get them, a small metal shim will fix the wobble. I just got them to make an internet purchase worthwhile.[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nOne of my biggest concerns is making this a track car. I built a track in the basement and it is amazing, I wish I could post up pics fast but my uncle made me promise to post them up when we were completely done haha.\r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]I\'m making a simple track of my own (I\'d like to buy the material today)[/color:57e299a30d]\r\nI figured I want a car that turns more smoothely. I noticed your car had some sort of steering upgrade?? How did you do it, and could you teach me?\r\n[color=red:57e299a30d][url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2371&amp;highlight=]tighter steering[/url]&lt;--click here[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nMy lovely little girlfried just baught me the suspension kit and steering kit from RS or w.e, but I won\'t get that till february 5th my birthday. \r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]Good start, suspension is important.[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nI want some light pieces, I was going to buy the Alloy stuff, but isn\'t alloy way heavier and sort of a waste? \r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]Alloy may not be important to you if you don\'t want to go very fast, maybe get some alloy locknuts[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nI have all the motor upgrades, but right now my car is bone stock except for the bearings. \r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]When your track is up and running, you can try different motors and see which one gives best drivability and speed on that track, my track will have a 40ft straight, so I built my track around my car. You have to do the opposite.[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nPS...if you are still interested in bits, I am giving away my \"WHOLE\" collection one by one, if say you are interested I would trade for some Xmod stuff.\r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]No thanx[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nOne last thing is I want a fast car, but not crazy fast, it still has to take the turns nice on the track, I am looking for a torquey car rather than a high speed car.\r\n\r\n[color=red:57e299a30d]The combination of motors, springs and tires will help you achieve this. I have an S2 motor in my car and it\'s pretty fast. Experiment.[/color:57e299a30d]\r\n\r\nGet back to me soon man...thanks![/quote:57e299a30d]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34920,'eda320b88e','hey sat, i noticed when u posted a picture of your collection in [url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=155&amp;start=225]this[/url]\r\nthread u had a little green hatchback on the right side of the table. i would like to know what chassi/body this is since i cant get over hatchs :smile:  \r\n \r\nthanks bro[/url]'),(34921,'5f055f1e7c','hey man what\'s up?\r\n\r\nThe body and chassis is from some cheap clone I got at walgreens about a year ago. I believe I have seen a few more around here. I think it supposed to a Honda Accord wagon. If I come across one here I will pick it up for you.'),(30968,'e40842cc5b','Dude, I don\'t know what happened to FileLicker. \r\nI sent him a couple Pms, havn\'t heard back as of yet.\r\n\r\nWe\'ll give him a few more days? :???:'),(36241,'0c3adfa6fa','I\'m on it !  8-)'),(36242,'74e09ad31d','i have a decent sized rcp track in the basement and i invite others to race 1:28 scale rc\'s on saturdays twice a month.  \r\n\r\ni don\'t care what kind of rc you have, ie; xmods, iwaver, mini-z, firelap....  i posted a link to our club forum on mini-zracer.'),(36243,'d418bd128d','[quote:d418bd128d=\"arch2b\"]i have a decent sized rcp track in the basement and i invite others to race 1:28 scale rc\'s on saturdays twice a month.  \r\n\r\ni don\'t care what kind of rc you have, ie; xmods, iwaver, mini-z, firelap....  i posted a link to our club forum on mini-zracer.[/quote:d418bd128d]\r\n\r\nI\'ll check it out!  I have a 1:24 Lxx Char-G that I just broke out after 2 years!  I\'m out in Bowie so I may be interrested in hangin one Saturday!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36251,'b51555c7c5','You fuckin rock. That\'s all there is to it. :-o \r\nI\'m not sure how much time I have, will find out monday. The position as far as I can tell has to do with the creative side and involves print and signage work. The company owns  FYE and coconuts music stores etc and etc. (music and video stores and what not)\r\nThanks man, extremely appreciated. :-)'),(32827,'8223c1c2b7','Thanks again man, I really like the wallpaper.'),(28562,'3f403b66a1','can you take off the covers and ship them to me?'),(31376,'c118e2d208','[quote:c118e2d208=\"suprakid95\"]for the things you are selling if you decide to sell the s2 engines let me know...i just want the red or blue one[/quote:c118e2d208]\r\n\r\nWell, I\'m not home right now, so I dunno if I still have the motors, but when I get home (July 10th or so) I can look.'),(31380,'a72317b773','Thanks i appreciate it.\r\n\r\n\r\n---matt'),(36669,'c1a93b992c','Thanks for being so understanding man. You probably won\'t want to use the front gearbox anyway however. It sucks for several reasons.\r\n\r\nThe only reason one would use the full rear gearbox is if you are running an extremely hot motor (like x2lspe, not a plasmatomic/etc), and using a low gear (9-10). Otherwise it is an overweight non-heatsinking sucker.\r\n\r\nIt would do some heatsinking if you manage to make a alloy replacement for the motor spacer (goes behind the motor when you use the tall gears), but I never got around to it.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31382,'fbb698e5b2','Oh yea, steering jitters.  The DC mod doesn\'t intentionally solve that, but I have noticed on a couple of cars I\'ve done that it goes away.  I\'m not sure why.  As near as I can tell the jitter issue is a software problem in the ZZSE MCU (it allows the servo to overshoot when the drive motor is running).  The jitter is it hunting for center.  If its a power supply issue the presence of the DC mod board might change the power supply character enough to get around the problem.  Dunno for sure though :???:'),(31419,'f421903402','Sounds good thanks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---matt'),(34975,'c5e385589b','Great, I will PM you as soon as I get the motors then send the car and bodies.  Estimated time frame one to two months, could be sooner but I doubt it.\r\n\r\nDont have any preference on colors or paint schemes, if you think it would look good try it.  If you dont mind one of the bodies might be a 1/28 or 1/24 since I have a bunch of Mini-Z test bodies too.'),(23281,'02c1715f44','Are you getting the stuff or not? Have you sent the money order or not? If you haven\'t sent it yet, then don\'t bother...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23284,'d80dae1bff','you still want that auction car?? i dont have paypal so pm crazydave and as soon as he gets the loot ill have it out the door.  leme know if theres any little merikan things that you want me to chuck in there.'),(23287,'9d954de507','[quote:9d954de507=\"VooDooMafia\"]OK dude they will go out in the morn as today is a holiday.[/quote:9d954de507]\r\n\r\nThanks man! \r\n\r\nSo about those custom decals...\r\n\r\nYou mentioned something about doing up some cars for you and your wife. What\'s her name? What kind of cars are you going to make? I\'ll make you a little sheet of custom decals so you can put your names above or below the driver\'s side window, and anything else you might want. Let me know...'),(28273,'7cda2c3002','Yo Man, good of you to offer. I\'ll be intouch.'),(28563,'43abd342ac','nope =/ \r\n\r\nyou would have to mask it all off...'),(31851,'36bfcff878','cheers mate.  \r\n\r\nyours is in the mail today.\r\n\r\nMy address is:\r\n\r\nMichael Frawley\r\nPO BOX 2010\r\nTOOWONG QLD 4066\r\nAUSTRALIA'),(37597,'e6013d9c16','[quote:e6013d9c16=\"sessiz\"]I gotta go....You win. :lol:[/quote:e6013d9c16]\r\n :lol: Fuck yea!\r\n\r\nAlright man... I do too actually.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26161,'65faeadec0','Ok Im in.'),(26639,'4c86c18ee5','hey my msn is : riisj@gbpackersfan.com ... Idont want to buy somthing i dont have monny'),(26684,'e807702a70','Sorry don\'t use messanger but you could always mail me yakboy@btopenworld.com\r\n\r\nregards\r\n\r\nYakboy'),(26696,'ae72854ceb','Hi Crazy Doc,\r\n\r\nGreat to speak to a fellow European, Great circuit by the way. I love scenery, thats what I\'m aiming for with my current circuit.\r\n\r\nI think you Germans have taken to bits in a big way, I\'m impressed with some of your retailers especially bitstylaz but they seem reluctant to ship outside germany which is a shame because the bodies look cool (my best friend lives in Austria so hopefully get them to ship there)\r\n\r\nThe Bit scene is smaller in the UK but hopefully will grow.\r\n\r\nI\'m hoping to make the race of champions circuit in pieces like my current circuit so it\'s portable, but this years track in paris looked so good I can\'t resist building it.\r\n\r\nGood to talk to you\r\n\r\nYakboy'),(31355,'b28aac6cb3','hi there ,\r\nhope im not being rude pm\'ing you , \r\nbut i thaught i would ask you if you have any bits for sale , \r\ni would like a complete one exept for motor+battery \r\ni would very much appreciate if you would sell me one .\r\n\r\nmany thanks and i hope im not being an ass hasling you , \r\njoe  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31356,'13ccef95be','actually, i don\'t have any spare ones running. sorry dude!\r\n\r\nbut if you have some chassis\' that can be repaired lemme know i\'m happy to do some soldering or whatever.'),(37116,'21c277f918','Damn you hue!!! I think I busted my spleen!!!!11! :lol: \r\n\r\n[img:21c277f918]http://home.comcast.net/~hue35/penismonsterdlx.gif[/img:21c277f918]'),(36404,'3c613c7432','[quote:3c613c7432=\"MafiaS\"]i read your Evo thread there...Could you get another one? We can\'t get EVOS here in Canada. I would trade you three Super Tomy Bit Char - G sets...(picks between Lambo or Ferrari, or anything else in my collection.)\r\n\r\nI wan\'t one really really bad DT...if you can do any little thing it would mean a big ass deal.\r\n\r\nTake care big guy!\r\n\r\nThanks[/quote:3c613c7432]\r\n\r\nIf they had more, he would\'ve given it to me!  I always check the local\r\nRS\'s in my area.  If I come across one, I\'ll letch know.\r\n\r\nNow just what do you have in yo collection that you\'re willing to part with?\r\nYou posted stuff you were selling but it didn\'t include a Lambo or Ferrari Set  :???:    You got those?'),(23893,'0e5f46aa3d','[quote:0e5f46aa3d=\"HirotoR34\"]or possible trades?[/quote:0e5f46aa3d]\r\n\r\n  Not sure what I have to get rid of but Iwill go through it when I get home from work.\r\n\r\n  Yea I think I am going to just go get her a mazda 3 or 6 not sure yet.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36208,'58e12432a3','I not only have no idea where I picked that animated .gif from but I\'m lookin for that chick myself. Definatly from a video of some kind. :???:'),(36210,'7e067d7d69','I seem to remember something about you having a design company or doing bussiness in the &quot;graphic design&quot; area. If I\'m wrong disregard this pm. :lol: \r\n\r\nHere\'s where I need your help/advice. I have a chance at a job as a low level graphics &quot;guy&quot; for transworld entertainment corp. My cousin is a lead tech guy over there and he is getting me a foot in the door. (director of marketing owes him big  :lol: )\r\nWhat I need from you is a tip or two on what exactly should I put together potfolio wise to show this guy. I got a rough idea of what this cat wants to see and I feel gay as fuck typing this shit but any help from you would be much apreciated.  :-)'),(34107,'7e6f6d8915','Kamen says you guys are \'getting tight\'. :shock: \r\n\r\nHe\'s okay, I used to talk to him alot, until be just kept pushing it one day.\r\nI\'ll share the convo with you sometime, I have it saved.'),(33338,'0980fcfbe8','Hi, I am havin security problems on my computer, so once I get them fixed I\'ll send the $$$');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25417,'8210905991','Hey man,\r\nHere\'s my email address: cabowabo@lixlink.com\r\n\r\nI\'m at work right now and won\'t be able to check the email until I get home. If you want, you can reply via these PM\'s (private messages) - I\'ll be checking this periodically through the day.'),(28627,'aca1ff6a82','http://www.rcinfo.dk/forum/index.php?\r\n\r\n\"Registrér\" = Register\r\n\"Brugernavn\" = Username\r\n\r\nI guess there\'s not much more to it. \r\n\r\nI dunno what\'s morfar is cooking on regarding the contest. It\'s gonna be HUGE though. I\'ll let you pimps know.'),(37139,'e47f42c0bc','Hi,\r\n\r\nCan you add some more decals to this for me? It\'s my new desktop background and I\'d like 2 more decals put in with the flow of the others.\r\n\r\n&quot;MAXXA&quot; in [u:e47f42c0bc]Bold Arial Black[/u:e47f42c0bc] , and\r\nA bitpimps one, like the ones everyone else has.\r\n\r\nThis is the hi-res version that I use for my backgrounds, so can you edit it and repost? \r\n\r\nCan you do 2? The second will have MAXXA replaced with Diggy\r\nDiggy is the name of my nephew, it\'s his car. \r\n\r\n[URL=http://img78.imageshack.us/my.php?image=img091110lj.jpg][img:e47f42c0bc]http://img78.imageshack.us/img78/9269/img091110lj.th.jpg[/img:e47f42c0bc][/URL]\r\n\r\nthanx man\r\nMaxx'),(24396,'82cb4ff13b','[quote:82cb4ff13b]and dont do it with a [b:82cb4ff13b]dremel [/b:82cb4ff13b] .. [/quote:82cb4ff13b]\r\n\r\nYIKES !  :???:   That Smart !');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29177,'2c2f721aae','I added you to my msn, yeah you can send money but i hear if they see it in the envelope they tear that shit up. At your own risk bro, if anything send bills no coins, but even then you never know. I\'ll take money in an envelope though.'),(24080,'0d1120d312','[quote:0d1120d312=\"VooDooMafia\"]hey bro I picked up one of them subs at wally world today, they are tiny lol[/quote:0d1120d312]no shit they are lol\r\nhave you tried it out yet?\r\nwhat do you think?'),(23343,'b890f229b1','[quote:b890f229b1=\"VooDooMafia\"]Dude I ordered one of them hook shooters from HLJ ofr the Wild char-g\'s\r\n\r\n  Now bad for $5.00 canadian shipped to my door.\r\n\r\n  I am going to try and get vids after work but its some funny shit to drive around then shoot a big hook at something.[/quote:b890f229b1]Cool man, that sounds cool.\r\n\r\nI just got my Power Brute minutes ago, I\'m getting ready to go play with it now.\r\n\r\nDave'),(31880,'5370ba0e70','[quote:5370ba0e70=\"DarkTari\"]\r\nWhat IP  :-? \r\n\r\nWould I  :screwed: \r\n\r\nDid we boot his lil azz from here too? \r\n\r\nThanx Pimp ![/quote:5370ba0e70]\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if we\'ve put the steel toes to his o-ring, I can\'t say I\'ve seen him around here though.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35625,'cf383324ae','CJ, how much do i owe you so i can paypal you it this weekend???? I got confused by the new posts thats why im asking!!!!! thanks in advance'),(35654,'26a38b04ec','Hey, I realize you can\'t accept money or w.e but what about a trade?\r\n\r\nAre you into bits and zips maybe we can work out something if you are really willing. Let me know pimp,\r\n\r\nand thanks for your time!'),(32611,'28b5eebedd','[quote:28b5eebedd=\"weazel\"]i am fine w/ $3.85[/quote:28b5eebedd]\r\n\r\nThat\'s cool, the shipping might be cheaper than that. I\'ll let you know when I send it. If it\'s more, it won\'t be much and I\'ll just cover it.\r\n\r\nSo yeah, a $1 for the motor. How much for the Lap Counter? I think I get \'em for somewhere around $0.50!!! So, that\'s cool too.\r\n\r\nSo it looks like we\'re floating around $4.50-$5.50 for items AND shipping. Is that cool?'),(37477,'e7b73d550b','I suggest you calm the fuck down.'),(33783,'f4f817f1a5','hey man just to let you know I sent the cash sorry I was a little late but to make up for it I added some stuff with the cash! Hope you like it its not much but hey its free...  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34538,'96bdc388b8','Yahya;  \r\n&#12516;&#12540;&#12498;&#12515;\r\n\r\nSessiz;\r\n&#12475;&#12476;&#12451;&#12540;&#12474;\r\n\r\nThis is Japanese Katagana.  It\'s what the Japanese would use to spell your name.  They use Katagana to write all foreign words.  Your name is foreign, so it would be written in katagana.\r\n\r\nThey have 3 other forms that make up their way of writing.  Hiragana, which is similar to Katagana, Kanji, which was imported from China and Romji, which is our romanization of their spoken language (their words written in English letters).  Your name\'s characters are referred to as Kana, not Kanji.  But a mix of Hiragana, Katagana and Kanji can be referred to as Kana.\r\n\r\nMy computer has windows xp.  It can be set to write in Japanese.  It has a windows program that it comes with.  If you are using the old school windows 2000, you can download the Japanese program.  It\'s the same program that windows xp comes with.'),(24157,'32e16d6a99','Glad you got it, you had me worried there for a bit! (Pun not intended  :lol: )\r\n\r\nPleasure trading with you,\r\nKanye.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36947,'fa402be9e0','Sean Dill\r\n406A Boreman South\r\nNorth High Street\r\nMorgantown, WV 26506\r\n\r\nWhat episodes do you have and what do I owe you for the hook up?\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(32416,'82aa0b7e92','[quote:82aa0b7e92=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:82aa0b7e92=\"BilboBaggins\"]I just filled out the page to allow me email from bitpimps.lixlink.com is there anything else to give them? I\'ve never had a problem with changing my email account before, of course I haven\'t changed it in a few years.\r\n\r\nI get DSL to give me speed and they give me email problems  :grin: .[/quote:82aa0b7e92]\r\nI\'m not sure, if you gave them everything they asked for on the form, I guess it\'s good to go. They should only need the domain really: lixlink.com\r\n\r\nI\'d say if it\'s not corrected by weeks end, you should call them or something.\r\nIf you receive emails from other forums, you might want to check to see if you\'re receiving emails from those forums and if not - do the same thing, request that Verizon allow the emails to come through.[/quote:82aa0b7e92]\r\n\r\nThanks for the info. This was the only forum I\'ve changed the email address to at this time. I only go regularly here and Ausmicro anymore.'),(24159,'b4622b6f5b','hey i was woundering..is it posable if you could change my user name to \"chickin00000\" that what it is on all the other sites..i dont now if you have a policy about that..i understand if you cant or decide not to.\r\n\r\nAdam');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24161,'8fa083d255','[quote:8fa083d255=\"lose alot\"]hey i was woundering..is it posable if you could change my user name to \"chickin00000\" that what it is on all the other sites..i dont now if you have a policy about that..i understand if you cant or decide not to.\r\n\r\nAdam[/quote:8fa083d255]sorry pimp, no can do. if you want the new name, I\'m affraid you would have to re-register.'),(34496,'8e77a1f289','It looks like I\'m all out of wrx and gloria bodies. I do have one each of the Tomy Sets left. Let me know if interested in those.\r\n\r\nFor the perfection beetle bodies, I have them available in 9 colors and I have at least 2 of each color. Colors available are black, blue, white, silver, bronze  orange, pea green, yellow, charcoal silver, &amp; red. \r\n\r\nTHanks!'),(34497,'ec19e5665e','How much do you want for the Tomy Sets?  Shipping?\r\n\r\nIs that everything or do you have any Lxx sets left?\r\n\r\nI know someone looking for the WRX set\r\n\r\nLemme Know!\r\n\r\nThanx Again Pimp!'),(23108,'7b38955a6b','I just got an email confirming the cars went out when I told you. You should have them. Please email me (jvernonm@yahoo.com) or PM me and let me know when they arrive. Thanks.\r\nAz');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35490,'7f32658526','Do not feel bad! I don\'t want you to send the package until i\'m done with your Epoch. K here\'s the thing, the epoch i was going to send you will take to long, since it\'s in parts, so i\'m gonna send you one of my stock Epochs, After I 4-cell it for you, Can\'t wait MG!'),(35841,'56de7bcd02','Yee Ye mah Canadian bra...\r\n\r\nimma add you right now, put this deal on the table big boi...\r\n\r\ncheck ya'),(37257,'41fc57abce','I found the red front diff, but no gear that whent on the driveshaft :(  I included all that i had spare for the AWD kit, hope it gonna be good. Im expecting the stuff 2 day or 2 morrow so yeah, you get ur stuff yet?????'),(37258,'9843500eef','nope not yet, thanks for the stuff man...\r\n\r\nCould i use the bevel gears from the rear to attach to that red front drive shaft gear?\r\n\r\nI have some extra\'s of those, they would be able to line up right?'),(26654,'8290a3caab','Cheers CaboWabo,\r\n\r\n\r\nIt\'s now uploaded succesfully. You can now laugh at my pants driving.\r\n\r\nBTW I really appreciate the work you do  for this site\r\n\r\nYakboy');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29058,'77f760e10b','Take a read at the forum rules.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1957\r\n\r\nYour post has been edited and locked. Consider this your first warning. :-)'),(27847,'4d65a5eb3e','my adress is \r\n\r\nmatt evink\r\n25085 cr 388\r\nGobles , Mi 49055\r\n\r\nill send the body whenever you want me to ( tomorow would work fine ) thanks .\r\n\r\nmatt'),(27848,'4f7248e411','cool, I\'ll send the wheel locks tomorrow as well. Thanx'),(27859,'d19f6130e3','Yo mang.\r\nI need your shipping info (hue\'s too if you got it) so I can send you some of these sticker decals.\r\n\r\nThey\'re on the white background so you\'ll have to cut them out.\r\nJust peel them off and stick.\r\nThese aren\'t the best by far, but maybe you use them - if not, no biggie.'),(37478,'430fc47940','Ok.  I am typing how all of you type.  Are you happy now?  I just have one quick question:  Why did you spend all of your time typing that up?  I\'m not trying to criticize you or anything or say your a slow typer, I was just wondering.'),(29213,'dbb2947b95','I\'m on a new machine here, so I can get your keychain out to you...\r\n\r\n\r\nSorry for the delay bro, but shit has been crazy like hell.\r\n\r\nShoot me your addy again, and I\'ll get it out asap.\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks man.\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27862,'0b1bcbd28c','Yo mang.\r\nI need your shipping info so I can send you some of these sticker decals.\r\n\r\nThey\'re on the white background so you\'ll have to cut them out.\r\nJust peel them off and stick.\r\nThese aren\'t the best by far, but maybe you use them - if not, no biggie.'),(22723,'97aacd7f33','Just a heads up reading your last post, but this project is kinda a supprise to the web site.  Also, Please don\'t worry about this project and just make YOUR car the way you want.  The whole idea is that we take a shell and \"pimp\" it out.  Think of it like you are making a shell for Radio Shack, and then one of the pimps buys it and says \"hey this or that would look cool\"  You see what I am saying?  Make this ride your own, and then the team will customize the casting that you make.\r\n\r\nOh and just FYI I am pretty sure we will be using a normal Zip body, Not an SE.'),(22726,'65b828c217','i got it finks!\r\n\r\nis the chassis for a reg zz have the same mounts and length of the se zz.'),(22727,'482766e35f','You don\'t have an Standard Zip Zap?  No they don\'t to answer your question.  Also you can buy one now for only $9.99 at Radio Shack.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22730,'e19d0221b1','i will get one in the morning then, also i edited the we\'s out of the last post..\r\n\r\nthanks\r\njeff'),(22731,'58e4a9a43e','Cool shit.  When looking, try to get a Jeep or a S2000, they have spring suspention t hat is kick ass for any bit  :smile:'),(25677,'48862fd545','[quote:48862fd545=\"viperdout\"]\r\n\r\nDave:\r\n\r\nHow do I tell on these transistors which leg is the gate, source, and drain?  This bot is a piece.  I\'ll do it in the morning.  I gotta pick out a blade for it too.\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:48862fd545]You gotta find out if it\'s a PNP or NPN, look to see if it has markings. Otherwise you\'d need to look at the schematics, if available. \r\n\r\nIf your one of them smart techy guys (that I guess I\'m not  :lol: ), you\'d hook up your multimeter, and find the ground, which is the drain (I prefer to call it the base, for reasons I don\'t have time to explain). Your gate will be hit with a smaller signal voltage, and the source will be your larger main voltage. But I\'m not sure how that will work for you if it is not working now. I\'m not good with that type of stuff. \r\n\r\nSorry I can\'t be more help with that.\r\nDave'),(36922,'06dc563817','[quote:06dc563817=\"Stoli\"]Also do you have any good scripts for a photo gallery. I wanna have a page come up with 8 thumbnails on the top and when you click a thumb it comes up 640x480 underneath the thumbs. each thumb you click will then appear in the window below and replace the current 640x480 image.?[/quote:06dc563817]\r\nHere\'s a very basic version of how the code would look for the gallery how you described it.\r\nMight be easier for you to copy and paste this code in an editor to make it more readable.\r\n\r\n[code:1:06dc563817]&lt;!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN&quot; &quot;http&#58;//www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;html xmlns=&quot;http&#58;//www.w3.org/1999/xhtml&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;head&gt;\r\n&lt;meta http-equiv=&quot;Content-Type&quot; content=&quot;text/html; charset=iso-8859-1&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;title&gt;Untitled Document&lt;/title&gt;\r\n&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;!--\r\n#img_viewer &#123;\r\n	position&#58;absolute;\r\n	width&#58;640px;\r\n	height&#58;480px;\r\n	z-index&#58;1;\r\n	left&#58; 300px;\r\n	top&#58; 50px;\r\n&#125;\r\n--&gt;\r\n&lt;/style&gt;\r\n&lt;script type=&quot;text/JavaScript&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;!--\r\nfunction MM_preloadImages&#40;&#41; &#123; //v3.0\r\n  var d=document; if&#40;d.images&#41;&#123; if&#40;!d.MM_p&#41; d.MM_p=new Array&#40;&#41;;\r\n    var i,j=d.MM_p.length,a=MM_preloadImages.arguments; for&#40;i=0; i&lt;a.length; i++&#41;\r\n    if &#40;a&#91;i&#93;.indexOf&#40;&quot;#&quot;&#41;!=0&#41;&#123; d.MM_p&#91;j&#93;=new Image; d.MM_p&#91;j++&#93;.src=a&#91;i&#93;;&#125;&#125;\r\n&#125;\r\n\r\nfunction MM_swapImgRestore&#40;&#41; &#123; //v3.0\r\n  var i,x,a=document.MM_sr; for&#40;i=0;a&amp;&amp;i&lt;a.length&amp;&amp;&#40;x=a&#91;i&#93;&#41;&amp;&amp;x.oSrc;i++&#41; x.src=x.oSrc;\r\n&#125;\r\n\r\nfunction MM_findObj&#40;n, d&#41; &#123; //v4.01\r\n  var p,i,x;  if&#40;!d&#41; d=document; if&#40;&#40;p=n.indexOf&#40;&quot;?&quot;&#41;&#41;&gt;0&amp;&amp;parent.frames.length&#41; &#123;\r\n    d=parent.frames&#91;n.substring&#40;p+1&#41;&#93;.document; n=n.substring&#40;0,p&#41;;&#125;\r\n  if&#40;!&#40;x=d&#91;n&#93;&#41;&amp;&amp;d.all&#41; x=d.all&#91;n&#93;; for &#40;i=0;!x&amp;&amp;i&lt;d.forms.length;i++&#41; x=d.forms&#91;i&#93;&#91;n&#93;;\r\n  for&#40;i=0;!x&amp;&amp;d.layers&amp;&amp;i&lt;d.layers.length;i++&#41; x=MM_findObj&#40;n,d.layers&#91;i&#93;.document&#41;;\r\n  if&#40;!x &amp;&amp; d.getElementById&#41; x=d.getElementById&#40;n&#41;; return x;\r\n&#125;\r\n\r\nfunction MM_swapImage&#40;&#41; &#123; //v3.0\r\n  var i,j=0,x,a=MM_swapImage.arguments; document.MM_sr=new Array; for&#40;i=0;i&lt;&#40;a.length-2&#41;;i+=3&#41;\r\n   if &#40;&#40;x=MM_findObj&#40;a&#91;i&#93;&#41;&#41;!=null&#41;&#123;document.MM_sr&#91;j++&#93;=x; if&#40;!x.oSrc&#41; x.oSrc=x.src; x.src=a&#91;i+2&#93;;&#125;\r\n&#125;\r\n//--&gt;\r\n&lt;/script&gt;\r\n&lt;/head&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;body onload=&quot;MM_preloadImages&#40;\'imageLarge1.jpg\',\'imageLarge2.jpg\',\'imageLarge3.jpg\',\'imageLarge4.jpg\'&#41;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Image #1&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; onclick=&quot;MM_swapImage&#40;\'img_large\',\'\',\'imageLarge1.jpg\',1&#41;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;imageThumb1.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; name=&quot;img_thumb1&quot; width=&quot;75&quot; height=&quot;75&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; id=&quot;img_thumb1&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\r\n	Image #2&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; onclick=&quot;MM_swapImage&#40;\'img_large\',\'\',\'imageLarge2.jpg\',1&#41;&quot; &gt;&lt;img src=&quot;imageThumb2.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; name=&quot;img_thumb2&quot; width=&quot;75&quot; height=&quot;75&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; id=&quot;img_thumb2&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\r\n	Image #3&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; onclick=&quot;MM_swapImage&#40;\'img_large\',\'\',\'imageLarge3.jpg\',1&#41;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;imageThumb3.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; name=&quot;img_thumb3&quot; width=&quot;75&quot; height=&quot;75&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; id=&quot;img_thumb3&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\r\n	Image #4&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; onclick=&quot;MM_swapImage&#40;\'img_large\',\'\',\'imageLarge4.jpg\',1&#41;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;imageThumb4.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; name=&quot;img_thumb4&quot; width=&quot;75&quot; height=&quot;75&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; id=&quot;img_thumb4&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;div id=&quot;img_viewer&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;imageDefault.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; name=&quot;img_large&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; height=&quot;480&quot; id=&quot;img_large&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/body&gt;\r\n&lt;/html&gt;\r\n[/code:1:06dc563817]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26524,'84c087cd3a','halo \r\nmein name ist Casper \r\ni am from denmark i do not speak soo good dutch i have just lerned it..\r\ni wantede to here where you have bourght your cars.? couse here in denmark i cant buy them.\r\n\r\n\r\nps. your cars are the best \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPINGO :cool:'),(24442,'524c9b1fec','Dude,\r\n\r\nI\'m a fuckin\' retard... I tried to change the email address on my account, but typed it in wrong. So, the activation email got sent to a fuckup email (hue35@earhlink.net instead of hue35@earthlink.net) address that I can\'t get to. LOL!!! Anyway, lucky I had this little bogus account so I could at least PM you. Mother fuck! Like I said I\'m a fuckin\' retard. Uh, so could you help your flunky-flunk newbie mod out of a bind here?\r\n\r\n- hue35/pimp master deuce... christ, this is fuckin\' gay.'),(23985,'612c2f8dbc','I sent the cash today dude thanks'),(26734,'fb579d9f80','[quote:fb579d9f80=\"honda_s2000\"]Well for starters i  need the zz mt , wich i think is @$25 + motor upgrade @ $6.99 + tire kit @ $6.99 if i got enough , i have approx $50  so mt = motors+tires =7+7+25=$37 so i SHOULD have enough for shipping also\r\n :eek:  :eek:  :eek: \r\nlol very happy chappy me\r\ncheers dude ,\r\n :cool:[/quote:fb579d9f80]\r\n\r\nYour close on the math.\r\n\r\nHere it is....\r\n\r\ntruck 24.99\r\ntires  6.99\r\nmotors  6.99\r\n--------------\r\ntotal 38.97\r\n  X .07  (sales tax I have to pay is 7%)\r\n---------------\r\ntax 2.73\r\n\r\n\r\n[b:fb579d9f80]Final total  $41.70 + S&amp;H[/b:fb579d9f80]\r\n\r\nI think about $53-55 should cover it.  I\'m expecting about $9 for shipping and then Paypal will charge me for accepting money and converting it.  That\'ll be about $1.50 or so.\r\n\r\nIf this is cool with you, just paypal me the cash to...\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com\r\n\r\nI could get it out to you before the end of the week, possibly.\r\n\r\n :-)'),(23424,'4f7611ad25','hey man\r\n\r\njust sent the money to crazydave\r\n\r\ndont worry about the batt, but do you know where i can get some.\r\n\r\ni asked dave andhe said he hadnt gotten any\r\n\r\ncheers');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23425,'117a6a2a77','ok. give me a few days since its the weekend. i can ship a 49mhz controller if you really need one but it would help me on shipping not to. also if you need it i have either an nkok or motorworks charger. \r\n\r\nit also has about an hour of running in it. the shell has maybe 15 minutes of running. its a simple design but its effective and you will break it if you hit things. anything else from america if its cheap and light?'),(23426,'d821fadbb3','I heard you installed FETs on bits, is this true? ($10?) If so would you be willing to hook a pair of Bits or ZZs up for me?\r\n\r\nThanks pimp,\r\nKanye.'),(23427,'28c17e1aac','sorry pimp, you musta heard wrong.\r\nthis might help ya though\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/article_postings.php?id=45&amp;catId=\r\n[quote:28c17e1aac=\"KaNye\"]I heard you installed FETs on bits, is this true? ($10?) If so would you be willing to hook a pair of Bits or ZZs up for me?\r\n\r\nThanks pimp,\r\nKanye.[/quote:28c17e1aac]'),(23430,'dfe212cc0e','yeah i need the controller and charger plz.\r\n\r\ni dont need anything else atm.\r\n\r\n\r\nthanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27304,'e7acf73025','Let me know before you go buy anything.\r\n\r\nI [i:e7acf73025]might[/i:e7acf73025] decide to sell the XXX-NT and just keep the T-Maxx.  I\'m not sure yet, but maybe.  So check with me when it comes time.\r\n\r\n[/i]'),(36115,'a1f3a354fc','Woot! Thanks man, I\'ll get the tracking number for your package soon.'),(36116,'d8903c5c68','Alright buddy!'),(35847,'3bf641d02e','What exactly am I getting in return...\r\n\r\nZipZap stuff I have a 49mhz controller, Corvette past and present body, and a yellow EVO, along with a chassis that needs work.\r\n\r\nI am not sure about the whole Super chassis, that\'s still my favorite one.'),(27590,'627d5fb1ab','[quote:627d5fb1ab=\"micro_man\"]hi sg219 my mailling info is \r\n\r\nmatthew evink\r\n25085 cr388\r\nGobles Mi 49055\r\nUSA\r\n\r\nthanks man .[/quote:627d5fb1ab]\r\n\r\n[i:627d5fb1ab]Stage 2 with gear.[/i:627d5fb1ab]  \r\n\r\nDo you mean the pinion on the motor or the bevel gear or both?\r\n\r\n$3 sound good for it?  Shipped.\r\n\r\nPaypal is.....\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com\r\n\r\nI can have it out Monday.'),(37311,'da7a054025','Of course not....I asked you...\r\n\r\nJust sold some Xmod shit, now getting ready to click away on ebay once more...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24009,'34431bdeb7','If you goto that old thread is there anything there you would want for those shells?\r\n\r\n  Some of the stuff is gone but most is still there.\r\n\r\n  Any luck finding aother sub at wally world?'),(37525,'1082a594f9','Dude, I\'m sorry about that. I\'ll change my post too. I didn\'t see the money order thing, plus I\'ve already got too many toys. I don\'t know what I was thinking.\r\n\r\nYou won\'t have a problem selling it at that price however.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37600,'f7474b6451','[quote=PimpSmurf]I don\'t agree with everything the libertarians (base = liberty, not liberal) believe, just 95% of it. They are pretty far right wing. Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative. [/quote]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t say liberals, I said libertarians. And they do indeed. There are a couple libertarian talk shows on talkradio and shortwave and they are most libertarians (about 75%) see Bush as more liberal than conservative.\r\n\r\nThe problem with all these labels is you have to define them. The problem with the LP is most members of the LP vote for republicans in states that are close. No need to have another sex-junkie in the White House.\r\n\r\nYou are seeing fault where there is non. I have not contradicted myself on this issue because it is an issue of beliefs. You are retreating, which is OK. I\'m not willing to argue a point (argue, not fight) that the other side isn\'t willing to bring ideas to the table.\r\n\r\nThanks anyway man. It was fun (except the gay sex.)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36306,'06392c57c2','[quote:06392c57c2=\"pimpsmurf\"]haha... I had orders from rcmart for parts for this thing that were twice that! lol\r\n\r\nSeriously, check me out. many have vouched for me, and I have no desire to ruin the poor reputation I have online by ripping someone off.\r\n\r\npaypal me $225 for priority shipping though. It is going to cost me $30-40 to ship, and paypal is going to suck 5% away, plus I have to fork out another $25 for the parts that are coming, so $225 is one hell of a deal man. Something to brag about no less. \r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:06392c57c2]\r\nIs 218 ok?\r\n\r\nThats all the doh i have in my account.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28204,'d6cab33880','I know you want to sell it as a set, but I will buy the black off you for $10.00 via paypal. let me know'),(36581,'96fd96b997','Do you have a matching set of rims and tires?Doesnt really matter what style, just as long as they have tires. Thanks.'),(28231,'ede99adf1c','well you did. but i\'ll live. :) \r\nmaybe its for the best. well i\'ll have to look for the GPM\'s elsewhere.'),(32690,'eb5b4fdff1',':lol: sokay :lol:'),(30925,'b5f12e174d','Yep, got \'em.  Thanks!  Looks like I\'ll be able to reproduce them both, but unfortunately I\'m on the road for work for a couple of weeks, so I won\'t have a chance to actually do anything but design work until probably july 8th or so.\r\n\r\nThanks again, when I get the prototypes done I\'ll post some pics and send you a set to test.'),(28660,'858d2d45c4','[quote:858d2d45c4=\"backdrift\"]You should update from phpBB 2.0.11.. This version is exploitable, and has happened to other websites.\r\n\r\nJust thought id tell ya; \r\n\r\n :cool:[/quote:858d2d45c4]Thanks for the heads up dude.\r\nIt\'ll happen soon.'),(28218,'c9919f5e22',':sad:  I love you man.\r\n\r\nYou\'re gunna make me poor again. ok so we gunna do some business here. I want : (in red?)\r\n\r\n1 pr front knuckles\r\nrear cups (differential use)\r\nThe rear thingys to screw the rims on\r\nLug nuts\r\n(probly a tie rod)\r\n\r\ngive me individual prices and then a total.\r\nI dont want the WRX or the motor (stuck on the PN04)\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29211,'3fc604f1d0','Yeah, I do have a store opening soon.  Right now, I am basing the R&amp;D on our new 300 motor on R7R, you cna see the progress [url=http://ripper7racing.com/forums/index.php?showforum=78]here[/URL].  Our actual website is [url]www.micromods.tk[/url].  I will get ahold of dex and have him add you.  \r\n\r\nUpon our Grand Opening, we will have li-ion, li-polymer, nicd, and nimh packs for cars ranging in bits to 1/10s.  We will have motors for the 1/2x and 1/18 vehicles.  \r\n\r\nSome other things may be comming soon.  I am working on carbon Fiber Mini-T chassis and Carbon Fiber TLT TVP.  A Carbon Fiber TVP for Mini-Zilla may come soon as well.  Something also in the works is a stick-pack conversion for the TLT Rockbuster.  The Max climber is stick-pack friendly, but the Rockbuster needs slight modifications to run stick packs.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(28220,'1c51c4c4c1','hey finks.. just curios. In your Wheel mod, which brand do you recomend?\r\nJada Toys import racers or Muscle machines Import tunerz ??\r\n\r\nI am guessing Jada, cause they look a little cooler to me :s hehe but figured id ask just incase you had some input into the matter...\r\n\r\nGood mods man, I have been lurking for the past year hehe havnt posted in ages. Good to see the mods still comin out clean! :P\r\n\r\nThanx in advance\r\n:D Swavey'),(25582,'4ce21350ef','well, I spoke too soon.  You are getting attacked now.  I still think you should take my advice though.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23442,'f21dde721d','Thats straight. I must have heard crazy daves name and forgot and thought I remembered it was you.'),(37087,'6f5afc92f9','[quote:6f5afc92f9=\"Maxximum Attack\"]US$300 so that he can buy 2 sets. I have to contact him and see what he can do for me. I\'m gunna have to start harassing these ppl for my money dammit  :o \r\n\r\nI\'ll keep in touch\r\nMaxx[/quote:6f5afc92f9]\r\n\r\nFor two sets it would be:\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Purple \r\nDXME100R	DELRIN REAR BALL DIFFERENTIAL - 1 COMPLETED SET	$20.15	2\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$15.47	2\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	2\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$31.07	2\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.47	2\r\nXME021	ALLOY FRONT KNUCKLE ARM - 1PR	$12.87	2\r\nXME022	ALLOY REAR KNUCKLE ARM -1 PR	$12.87	2\r\nXME028	ALLOY FRONT SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$10.27	2\r\nXME030	ALLOY REAR SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$10.27	2\r\nXME039F	ALLOY FRONT WHEEL SHAFT - 1PR	$5.07	2\r\nXME039R	ALLOY REAR Wheel SHAFT - 1PR 	$5.07	2\r\nXME039R/C	ALLOY REAR UNIVERSAL SWING SHAFT (CVD DESIGN) - 1PR	$17.94	4\r\nXME049/0	ALLOY STEERING PLATE - 1PC	$8.45	2\r\nXME055	ALLOY FRONT LOWER ARM - 1PR	$10.27	2\r\nXME056	ALLOY REAR LOWER ARM - 1PR	$10.27	2\r\nXME190R	ALLOY REAR DOG BONE (9.0MM) - 1PR	$6.50	4\r\nXME316F	ALLOY FRONT DAMPER (16MM) -1PR	$7.67	2\r\nXME316R	ALLOY REAR DAMPER (16MM) - 1PR	$7.67	2\r\nXME331R	ALLOY REAR SKID PLATE - 1PC	$4.55	2\r\nMZ002	ALLOY 2MM LOCK NUT SET  5PCS	$7.60	2\r\n\r\nSub	$241.45\r\nS&amp;H 4%	$9.66\r\nTotal(USD)	$251.11\r\n\r\nIf you get XME039R/4WD you dont need XME039F, XME039R or XME190R.  Do you want the CVD or the dog bones or both?'),(26470,'7d48b0c261','James Neat\r\n8424 Woodland Road\r\nMillersville MD\r\n21108\r\n\r\nfor; gpm cupjoints, center shaft and wheel nuts');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28051,'383d65f844','i want the nelly, a li pro kit, and a charger. Basically all i need to get started with lithium.\r\n\r\nI am paying with a money order \r\n\r\ncan u send me ur name and address so i can send it? ($65)\r\n\r\nI want to send half tho. I ordered some liths from performancexmods since November and haven\'t got them yet. I think they got lost in the xmas post.\r\n\r\nI\'ll send $40 is that ok?\r\nlet me know.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(24953,'7d3cf30344','thanks alot man!\r\n\r\n\r\nyour a champion.\r\n\r\n\r\ncheers'),(29973,'68edc3f6e7','after the 4th would work good for me cus i know i will have some cash then . thanks man ill write myself a note so i dont forget this time ...'),(25673,'801ec3ee56','[quote:801ec3ee56=\"viperdout\"]\r\nDave:\r\n\r\nDo it ph2t\'s way, since you have a bunch of Ns coming in.  I thought that the stockers actually sapped some power off the top, and you get a little top speed, and the fets just allow for a much greater amount of current.  Anyway, I have a stacked ZZ, and it\'s clocked speeds 2 mph better than stock.  I love it, and that\'s why I sent mine to you.  Ph2t\'s looks simpler, and doesn\'t look so un-stock (sleeper!)  Right now I\'m kinda pissed, because I think I fried a fet on this battle bot I\'m working on (it\'s this little half-circle thing, which has 3 legs, possibly gate, source, and drain.  I\'ve seen them on ZZ controllers at any rate).  So, go with ph2t\'s mod.\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:801ec3ee56]Ok, good, glad you\'ve had experience with FETs. Some people expect them to go like dual cells and stuff, I just wanted to make sure you were clear.\r\n\r\nSo yeah, you\'ll see some increase in top speed, that\'s just the motor working more effeciently.\r\n\r\nTruthfully, code\'s way makes my head hurt, and I wish I had the N-channels right here so I could just do it his way right now, but I suppose I\'ll try it. I don\'t know all the stuff those guys do, I\'m hoping by trying both mods, I\'ll get a better clue how this PCB works. Staring at schematics means nothing to me (even though I know what the symbols mean).\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:801ec3ee56]\r\nRight now I\'m kinda pissed, because I think I fried a fet on this battle bot I\'m working on (it\'s this little half-circle thing, which has 3 legs, possibly gate, source, and drain.[/quote:801ec3ee56]What you described sounds like an NPN or PNP type transistor, I used those in distortion pedals, used have all these part #s from the 60s remembered (gotta sound like Hendrix, ya know), now I can\'t remember the ones they sell at RS, I only know IRLML2502 now. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave'),(28286,'8782b35000','hi sg im looking to get another xmod . i cant afford $50 because of some medical bills i have to pay this month , so the most i can spend is $25 . if you have a working used xmod(or iwaver) for that much , or know someone who dose please let me know . i can prolly use pay pal agin . thank, matt .');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29348,'39d2a70236','Okay, good advice. I better not send my 47th PM to CaboWabo.\r\n\r\nJ/p'),(36036,'fc2c95af83','[url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6920]Two Skylines[/url]\r\n\r\nNoticed you\'re trying to keep it more organized, and just wanted to say its a great idea. :-o'),(36984,'4184fa23fe','Hey man, the mrs4 came today!  THanks a ton.  \r\n\r\nSTG'),(37873,'3c30bd9626','[quote:3c30bd9626=\"MafiaS\"]...alright \r\n\r\nWhat\'s your email I will snap a few of the bodies and send em 2morrow...cool?[/quote:3c30bd9626]\r\n\r\nTuner_1989@yahoo.com'),(28396,'4d83763dc9','I feel bad about the mosfet, how about I send you the panther or rally racer and I will also send you this this [b:4d83763dc9]body loose[/b:4d83763dc9]. Just remember the body only not the cool rims okay\r\n\r\nSo You will send me all of  the broken ZZMT stuff with painted body and I will send you one rally racer or panther with the drip body loose. let me know \r\n\r\n[img:4d83763dc9]http://www.rcmod.com/cmalbum/albums/userpics/10021/drip09.JPG[/img:4d83763dc9]'),(23666,'ead040bada','I\'d be interested in muscle cars for Zip Zaps or a Gloria, R32 or RX7 for Bits... you got any of those? Also, I\'ll take a pic of my Hummer bodies to make sure it\'s what you want... I\'ve got H1 shells.\r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33746,'dd4a67a41e','[quote:dd4a67a41e=\"crazydave\"]I just ordered the decals for P:PSII, and they\'ve got some new 1/72nd decals. Check \'em out. The top set are the ones I intended to order, should be smaller than the ones I used on my car, but check out the second sheet down. That\'s so great becaise I\'m making Gasser out one of my \'57s, and those even have the gasser markings.  :-D \r\n\r\nSo I ordered those too, along with a couple of the flames.\r\n\r\nYou like any of those names? ;) ;)\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:dd4a67a41e]\r\nI don\'t see anything... is it my shitty dial-up connection?. . . no link, I think.'),(34562,'66b19ee7fb','[quote:66b19ee7fb=\"CaboWabo\"]\r\nToo late, fuckin Bilbo nailed it already. :lol:[/quote:66b19ee7fb]Figures, there\'s always some smart ass. :-) \r\n\r\nThat\'s alright, never saw that movie anyways.  \r\n\r\nThat was a good one, Bilbo just sucks. You\'ll stump them next time... yeah right, huh. :lol: \r\n\r\nSidenote: Notice how Bilbo always lurks around, and then suddenly posts when there booty to be won, he just likes to win stuff. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(37759,'5b13e5b083','hey man, ive seen your clone monster (http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v413/frizzen/RC/First_Monster.jpg) a few times and i was wondering if you could get me some more pics of the under side and the front suspension?  Id like to try my hand at a mod like it (with my own twist of course)  Any chance you can give me some tips and problems you ran into,, maybe the materials you used.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36376,'2f322d02e6','[quote:2f322d02e6=\"pimpsmurf\"]Yeah, I was actually driving a truck pulling a boat. not nearly as fun at driving boats. haha\r\n\r\nI just found some tire foams under my bed! haha\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:2f322d02e6]\r\n\r\nLol keep up the good work!\r\n\r\nBTW this is going out priority correct? :???:'),(37714,'60dfcdbbb5','Yeah, I just got it.  Thank you.  Sorry its taking me so long, Ive had trouble finding a box and getting it to the post office.  My dad is mailing it tomorrow.'),(37705,'c7a333053f','Holy smackers i got it today, looks sweet, i might run it for a while but hope you not offended if i give it a brigther orange color with some black stripers later on...Thanks a bunch man, hope your stuff comes i nsoon...'),(36599,'cc56175806','A logical approach.\r\n\r\n1. Since the Iwaver Pot (short for Potentiometer) will not fit in the SE gears you will obviously want to leave the SEs Pot in place and use it.\r\n\r\n2. But since the Iwaver circuit board just has 2 wires and a Pot is just a variable resistor not some mystical piece of electronic wizardry it should be wired to the Iwaver circuit board just like the Iwaver pot was.\r\n\r\n   So far its a no-brainer, however:\r\n\r\n3. Since the Iwaver potentiometer and the SE potentiometers do not have the same resistance values (a guess I dont remember) and the desired steering limits are bound to be different you have to make changes in the perceived resistance value to set the limits where you want them.  There are several ways to do it I chose to put a 2.2K ohm resistor between the Center and Clockwise (C) potentiometer posts, in other words the yellow and blue Iwaver Pot wires.  Then with a few adjustments of the centering pot on the IW circuit board and the position screw of the SE I centered the steering, with the result being that the wheels stop turning just a hair shy of hitting the chassis, an electrical stop is always preferable to a mechanical one.\r\n\r\nThe photo should give you an idea what the posts on the Pot are/do.  CC is the Counter Clockwise post, and C is the Clockwise post, the down arrow is the Center post.\r\n\r\n[img:cc56175806]http://lbspd.com/v-web/gallery/albums/album49/Potentiometer.sized.jpg[/img:cc56175806]\r\n\r\nAnd here is a good link to help you understand how parallel resistors work.  \r\n[urlhttp://www.physics.uoguelph.ca/tutorials/ohm/Q.ohm.intro.parallel.html[/url] [/url]'),(37028,'93672560b1','I have Xmod stuff...what are you interested in?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31260,'d5d96bc457','hey lb i have a quick q\r\n i ordered the polyquest 1800 2 cell pack for my soon to be rc18t but i was wondering if my puny apache 1215 will charge it. the highest charge setting is 1200ma 2cell and i need to know if that charger will handle the 1800 set on 1200 but just take along time to charge? i also ordered the pcm guard for charging it if that matters :(  would save selling my xmod for not having to get a charger :lol:    and if that was the case i woulda got the 3 cell :D'),(31261,'d5d96bc457','hey lb i have a quick q\r\n i ordered the polyquest 1800 2 cell pack for my soon to be rc18t but i was wondering if my puny apache 1215 will charge it. the highest charge setting is 1200ma 2cell and i need to know if that charger will handle the 1800 set on 1200 but just take along time to charge? i also ordered the pcm guard for charging it if that matters :(  would save selling my xmod for not having to get a charger :lol:    and if that was the case i woulda got the 3 cell :D'),(31262,'ea4c1089ab','Your Apache will work great :-D , and the PCM Guard although not necessary is well worth the extra money, it will prolong the life of your pack and keep it working at peak performance :-o .\r\n\r\nSince LiPo cells unlike NiMH charge by voltage the closer the 2 cell pack gets to 8.4 volts the less current it actually draws.  If you where to graph the charge youd see that most of that time is actually spent toping off the last 10% at very low current levels.  \r\nWhat that means is that even if the pack was discharged all of the way down to 6 volts a 1800 mAh charger would at best only be about 5 minutes faster than your 1200 mAh charger.  In fact its always better to use the lowest current for the time you have available to prolong your packs life.  If Im not in any particular hurry I usually charge at 0.5 C (900 mAh for a 1800 pack).\r\n\r\nDo make sure you are getting the narrow pack (1800N)  for some reason a lot of people have been getting/ordering the standard 1800s.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31292,'05577dedea','Hey mau, when you post , try not to double post as in posting and posting again before someone else does. It\'s better if you use the Edit button. If you don\'t know what i mean just ask!  :-o'),(31293,'f1655ddc33','I tried jumpering the 3 and 4 pins. Still performs as before. I took a picture to make sure I got the right pins.\r\n\r\n[img:f1655ddc33]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/dcmod1.jpg[/img:f1655ddc33]\r\n\r\n\r\nJust let me know what\'s up whenever possible... go ahead and keep soakin\' if you have to, I know how that is. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(34482,'43da07b2c4','Whenever you can man.\r\nI\'ve got no preference on chinese or japanese, which ever looks better. As to the pronounciation I allready tried giving ya that in the previous pm, guess I failed. Here\'s another try at phoneticaly spelling my name...\r\n(YA-h-YA) The  \"YA\"  is how ya would say \"MA\" (as in mom) but not like \"maw\". The \"h\" in the middle is real soft almost silent. When saying Yahya you barely hear it pronounced. \r\nHow exactly do ya write kanji on your comp? Are you just using the keyboard\'s properties \"language\" thinger? :???: \r\nThanks again man. :-)'),(34483,'d70824b08e','hey man, just wanted to let you know that the installation doco for the evo mosfet upgrade is almost done.  it will be posted shortly.\r\n\r\nif you wanted something sooner to help let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nph2t.,');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28534,'0ec23ca9d7','Hey, \r\nJust checking to see if you got the package yet, it\'s coming in a brown padded envelope, but if you don\'t get it, have you checked like your door or front step/proch or whatever to see if you got a parcel pick-up slip, maybe the post office has it, but if you didn\'t get it today, I\'ll run over to the post office tomorrow and see what the heck is going on.\r\nKorey'),(29353,'9e3690ee19','Hey man, You sure you don\'t want anything in return, I\'d be glad to pay ya back in some way?\r\nBut here\'s my address:\r\nKorey Kiger\r\n6110 Germanton Rd.\r\nRural Hall, NC  27045\r\nThanks!'),(29355,'730319b6a8','[quote:730319b6a8=\"JDM-R34\"]Hey man, You sure you don\'t want anything in return, I\'d be glad to pay ya back in some way?\r\nBut here\'s my address:\r\nKorey Kiger\r\n6110 Germanton Rd.\r\nRural Hall, NC  27045\r\nThanks![/quote:730319b6a8]\r\n\r\nNaw always a plesure to help out a fellow modder just keep up the great work!\r\nI will try and get it out in the morning! \r\nhave a great one! :-)'),(24191,'2959bae455','damn ok, thanks anyway\r\n\r\n\r\nAdam');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34427,'db9122597e','lol dude, no worries, was just making sure. Was just worried, still havn\'t seen the package (mail has yet to come today tho)  No worries either way.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nFinks'),(31853,'96aeae6669','Your clone will be shipping on Monday. I\'ve been hella busy and freaking out over a monster truck. Later!\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(23886,'b43a8437bc','shell mostly but depending on teh whole setup I would take that aswell lol\r\n\r\n  Yea man thanks only thing with that car is I wont let the wife drive it and now she wants another new car.'),(27999,'05e779744b','Arite, so we know why you have been laying low on the mod game, but what\'s up w/ Hugh?  Is he in jail, or did he get himself a girly that likes him but hates Bits?  Fill a pimp in 8-) \r\n\r\nOh yeah and of course again, enjoy that little boy.  We are expecting our only girl at the end of May and I could imagine it\'s great to have both (course I have 2 boys and a girl OtW)'),(34628,'c33240b5c4','Hey DT, I have a chevelle body if you want her. I started to widen the wheelwells and removed all the lights and crap. I was gonna slam it down. I know you will do her justice so let me know if you want.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37785,'a890b907f5','sweet, money sent. i made it $16usd in total, hopefully that covers the shipping. any probs lemme know.\r\n\r\nmy address:\r\n\r\n39 currajong ave\r\ncamberwell 3124\r\nvictoria\r\naustralia\r\n\r\ncheers!'),(36787,'313d644e43','Recieved this the day after I posted.....\r\n\r\n[quote:313d644e43=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]If you need anybody to do a fet mod to the cars, then let me know.  I\'m sure you already have that covered, but just in case, it\'s the least I can do to support.  I would offer to paint and putty, but I know there are people here who can do that better than me.  I have a lot of extra supplies and what not.  If I know about the car that\'s chosen ahead of time, I can always send you some stuff that I may have laying around that might go good with the ride.[/quote:313d644e43]\r\n\r\nNow he stepped up BigTime!  I told him I may call on his services, was planning on going that far but with his offer, we may do a couple.\r\nMaybe after this thing gets started, one of the mods will step up, if not, no problem!  I\'m building a shop for shooting some after pics.  This is gonna be off Da Hook !  ( Haven\'t recieved any entries yet but it\'s still early)'),(34718,'9ea4b4869b','Wow every one hates me do you hate me.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34719,'8820aa5cc6','No...'),(37936,'c83a1faf6d','Both torque and high speed set-ups.  I\'ll also take orders.  For example, how ever many turns you want or even certain parts and pieces.  That will be when I get more work done to get set up.  I need to do a bunch of research and testing to get ready.  I\'m starting with the spiral armeture because I\'ve never used one and I\'ve heard some interesting things about them.  The top speed in a spiral is generally higher, but I think the torque is lower and it pulls more current getting started whitch will blow fets and boards easily if I do the wrong setup.  Torque is very important of-course, possibly more important than top speed, but I\'d like to see what would happen if I took a spiral and set it up for torque.  It should make an all around sweet motor.'),(36542,'5f446cd105','Mate no worries about going Nelly - ph2t and I have a gentlemans agreement of sorts - he does kick-arse turbos and I do the spiders which are same as a Nelly 1.2  :)\r\n\r\nThe Gandinis are great only hassle is they don\'t wear out quick enough ;)  Seriously though I think that\'s what makes them worth the bucks, they wear real good.\r\n\r\nI can chuck a couple of extra 7317s into you current pack if you like, BTW swap the steering fets for 7317s ;)  it\'s a great change ;)\r\n\r\nA.'),(35036,'1296860886','[quote:1296860886=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]I finally got some video of my fast-ass formula car.  Never posted video before.  Was wondering if you could recomend something.  Windows media player works right?  Do I have to put it in any special format?  I noticed I can\'t access all media from windows media player, that\'s why I was wondering.\r\n\r\nCan I put it in my gallery and post from there?[/quote:1296860886]\r\nYea you could export the movie as .wmv\r\nThat\'s a Windows Media Video file, everyone should be able to play it.\r\n\r\nIf your movie file is 5 MB or smaller, you can upload it to your galleries - if it\'s over that - you will have to use a free host like http://www.putfile.com\r\n\r\nCan\'t wait to see this sucker in action.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32154,'e70e1c09c2','[quote:e70e1c09c2=\"LBRC\"]Hey  :-) ,\r\n\r\nCouldnt exactly answer you question at 1-43.com but as a Pimp I thought you should have more of an answer. so what I can do is ask you if youve browsed through my photo gallery lately?\r\n\r\n[url]http://lbspd.com/v-web/gallery/album27/Spud_Power[/url][/quote:e70e1c09c2]\r\n\r\nWhat question is that?  I\'m sorta lost.\r\n\r\nSweet motor and deal.  Congrats.  \r\n\r\nNo, I never really knew you had one. :? \r\n\r\nI\'ll definately flip thru it.'),(26730,'86acf3dbe0','It\'s no big problem.  It\'s cool.  Don\'t sweat it.\r\n\r\nI had to go check my P.O. Box anyway.\r\n\r\nI\'ll check again tomarrow on some shipping rates.\r\n\r\nNow I need to know exactly what you want.\r\n\r\nZZMT?\r\nZZMT motor upgrade?\r\nZZMT tire upgrade?\r\n\r\nList them and I\'ll get you a price on the goods and the S&amp;H tomarrow.\r\n\r\n :cool:'),(27337,'48b2aeb40f','stop in for a minute');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33805,'9355c06287','nothing personal, just didn\'t want my thread to turn in to a noob beatdown. :cool:'),(33806,'e38872fada','haha it\'s certainly no problem. I appreciate the PM. I\'m sure you guys don\'t let SHAUN know  :-o \r\n\r\nWhat is up we these twats nowadays anyway? They make me feel 28, not 18!! \r\n\r\nI\'m glad I never was a n00b. I was new, but certainly no n00b lol\r\n\r\ngod, I miss the old days. When I was basically the only teenage pimp. But it makes me feel good to be the [b:e38872fada]original[/b:e38872fada] teenage bitPimp! haha\r\n\r\nanyway, thanks pimp!!\r\n~midget  8-)  &lt;--- is that copyrighted by anyone? lol'),(24024,'287c9a222e','No sure I will check the box when I get home from work.\r\n\r\n  As for the MAT well I had 2 cases of them so I ended up opening a bunch so I am sure I have more then just mine kicking around.\r\n\r\n  I will check them both when I get in.'),(27362,'dce34f4f53','I don\'t like the kit, but the body is interesting.  That UK price is like double the quote.  I just got my Sprinter pullback a minute ago and it cost me $25.75!  That is fucked up.  Stupid British unwillingness to convert to Euros!\r\nAt least I can save money by getting that Gloria body set from toysnjoys.\r\n\r\nHere\'s that site, now that I\'m not getting any more from them:\r\nhttp://anytoys.co.uk/category_info.php/category_id/57\r\n\r\nI have more sites that some guys PM\'d me.  I\'ll give them to ya when I get done pissing and recheck my BP inbox.\r\n\r\n5.99 pounds for a Pullback set me back way more than it should have, so I\'m having second thoughts about that auction now, but if BigLots or Wallgreens starts carrying them, hooowoah, I\'m getting one!  \r\n(I should make a \"hoowhoah\" MP3, it\'s not hoo hah like Al Pacino or Busta Rhymes, though.\r\n\r\nLate,\r\nAbe\r\n\r\nOh, shit, two links:\r\nhttp://www.hlj.com/scripts/hljpage.cgi?TOM20562\r\nhttp://www.hlj.com/scripts/hljpage.cgi?TOM20561\r\nNever seen them before, especially not in pullback trim.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23848,'d2108bb311','Hey K, this is BigBanidt. where can I find some alloy wheeles for my ZZ and Bits'),(24970,'227fa68d12','Hey Pimpin you still want that  AWD?'),(37768,'217f298706','Not sure which one that is.  Either way, I\'ve got an IW02 for the comparison and I\'ve reached my hobby budget for a few months at least.  So, I gotta hold off on picking up any more cars for a while.  Sorry, otherwise I would love to pick one up from you.\r\n\r\nBy the way, the IW-02M has female ports coming out of the PCB cover like the Xmods have for plugging in lights and stuff.  That\'s the only real way to tell them from a regular IW-02.  If it is an IW-02M vs a regular IW-02, then advertise to the pimps.  Someone will grab it.  I think they\'ve worked on the electronics in the IW-02M to tweat the steering and get better reception, but I\'m really not sure of the specifics as it\'s all hear-say right now.  Not too many places to get them yet either.  Might be a hot item to sell if you get your hands on some.\r\n\r\nThanks for the offer though.  I\'ll keep in touch.'),(23851,'402e766593','Sup man, good to see ya here!  :-) \r\n\r\nIm not exactly sure, I guess try a search. And if ya get nothing make a post in Lookin\' To Score asking to buy some off the other pimps.\r\n\r\nPeace.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30270,'3a44e7b746','hi swg i was wondering if you had sent the check and or bit for the reciver yet . that way i know when to expect it . thanks , \r\n\r\nmatt .'),(30037,'c9044fbfd1','ok i\'ll hold on the motors as long as you need me too .'),(25856,'885bb847ba','Could you change your avatar?  I don\'t like people copying me.\r\n\r\nThis isn\'t hate mail.\r\n\r\nWhat about this one? :blazin: \r\n\r\nIt\'s up for grabs.'),(24666,'f6abd6ef66','Sorry I didn\'t get back to you sooner. I\'ve been so busy lately that I\'m loosin  my friggen mind!  I screwed up your address and the Post office sent your package back to me. I\'m re-sending it out tomorrow (with the right address this time. I triple checked) and hopefully this time you\'ll get it. She\'s been cleaned up real nice and shines like a mofo. I didn\'t have any batteries for the remote to give you, but hey, the thought was there. I\'m sending it priority so, hopefully it\'ll be there as soon as possible. Thanx for your patience.\r\n\r\n :oops:  sometimes i\'m a real dumbass.'),(22770,'8e1e39de2f','I can send u pics of the nsx if u give me your e-mail address');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (22772,'671e3fb051','maffei@hevanet.com\r\n\r\nI\'ll put the pix up in your thread.'),(22777,'e6223a49ef','Well the whole thing got canned.  Basically it became a \"who is the best painter out there\" competition.  4 people felt like they should be the ones to paint this bad boy, so the father I am said, if you can\'t share I\'m gonna take it away.  And did just that.  Sorry bro, I know you were siked about this, but it would have broken up friendships and possibly this site.  Still can\'t wait to see what you do with this bad ass car, and you better belief when it\'s done, tons of pimps will want a casting.  Put me at the top of the list will ya :-)'),(22927,'373a054da6','Alright I\'m sending out the first round of emails, time to get the ball rolling and find some staff members.\r\n \r\nI plan to ask everyone what articles they would like to write or what they would like to contribute to the magazine.  After that we will work on a time schedule and a layout for upcoming magazines.\r\n \r\nThanks for any help or support.\r\n\r\n\r\nLater\r\nRipper'),(36953,'a33d85199f','I got the parts on Saturday.\r\n\r\nI\'m assuming thats all you have for now. :???: \r\n\r\nHow much longer for the rest?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36954,'ea705790d1','I\'ve been racing the shit out of my min z about the last month with the dude at work. He\'s got the XMOD evo truck, and I got the X5 BMW.\r\n\r\nHe now has seen the light, and ordered a mini Z MR-02MM Scaglietti, cause he\'s addicted.  My Q is He paid $104 for the ready set. Is that a good price?\r\n\r\nMy other Q is, now that he\'s gettin a car, he\'ll have the obvious advantage over my truck. Would you recomend a certain model. Are the MR-02MM better than the 02MR chassis\r\n\r\nWas also thinkin bout goin with a used one. Worth it, or not?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-S'),(24665,'546715861a','Just wondering if you got the loot yet bro.'),(31702,'d2b9004bbd','DarkTari &amp; payaso,\r\n\r\nI\'m an idot and an ass, and you can call me out publicly if you want. I was too tired to think clearly when I posted that about the Fiat bit (aka, Lupin the III BCG) the other night. My post was WAY to short on details, and it opened me up to just such a bind. I got PM\'s from both of you, and since my post didn\'t state that I would sell to the first to PM me, well, here we are. Don\'t misunderstand, I will NOT allow you to bid against each other. I would like your help on figuring this out. I know either of you will give the home it deserves. I think I paid like $32 plus shipping from Japan for it. I\'ll sell it to either of you for $30 shipped. Maybe whoever doesn\'t get mine can get one from HLJ?  :oops: \r\n\r\nSorry guys. I fubar\'d this one. I\'ll post to the forum that it\'s spoken for. Let me know what you guys think. Don\'t know if it matters to you, but here are the times on your PM\'s to me:\r\n\r\nDT: 7/16 @ 5am\r\nPY: 7/16 @ 2:45PM\r\n\r\nYou\'re the only two, thank goodness, and I wish I had two. Hoping we can work it out.\r\n\r\n :?'),(27705,'9237b2cc24','Hows it going man.  Yea I been browsing more than repling lately ... I will post up a Pic today to show you the Progress.... \r\n\r\nHows your T coming ?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (23677,'ce9ec73204','Looks perfect! So were you intersted in this ZZ body? - \r\n\r\n[img:ce9ec73204]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v84/HomerS2042/P9160009.jpg[/img:ce9ec73204][/img]'),(35183,'8d16fe838c','Consider it done.\r\n\r\nBTW, Just finished a 3x2 install of 7910/7329\'s into a Hummer. It\'s doing wheelies on 4 cells on a stock motor.  :eek:  Finally picked up a small 2s 600mah lipo from polyquest. I\'ll have to give that a try later.\r\n\r\nHave a good one,\r\nClint\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote=\"ph2t\"]hey Clint, I was just wondering if you would be up for writing a quite little review for the evo msofets on the review section in the ausmicro.com shop.  you don\'t have to do it, I would appreciate it if you could though man.  No rush.\r\n\r\n\r\ncheers,'),(24486,'a325f5f88b','Make me an offer!\r\n\r\nThe standard rules of e-trade apply here in that if we agree on a price, you pay shipping.\r\nAssuming you read the post, you know that it was new at Christmas 2003, has many extra parts and the stage two upgrade for steering, suspension, and all 3 motors. Also a lithium Ion 9v controller battery.\r\n\r\nI\'ll look forward to hearing from you........\r\n\r\njrc6805'),(26424,'7992ada494','[quote:7992ada494=\"honda_s2000\"]hi there ,\r\ni would be very gratefull if i could have a gallery of my very own ,\r\ni know im a n00b with a small post count , ( its not the number its how you post )  :???:  it would be a massive help , therefore people could see my pics , rather than me having to email them to \'em ,\r\ncheers either ways ,\r\nhs2000[/quote:7992ada494]you don\'t have to sell me on the idea, I know...\r\none problem. I don\'t see your username (honda_s2000) registered in the Galleries.\r\nI can\'t give you permissions if I don\'t know who you are.\r\ndid you register in the Gallery under a different name from the forum?\r\nif so, tell me - we\'ll get your Gallery name changed and I can then give you the proper permissions.\r\nif not and you just need to register for the Gallery, then do that with the username you use on the Forum and after I get notification of your registration, I\'ll give you the proper permissions to be able to create your own albums and upload your pictures and movies.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34151,'38e951ebb8','Aw man!\r\nI saw you posted yesterday about sending out the Payment to Bonzer earlier next week.\r\nNow you already did! :(\r\nThat\'s okay, I think SG219 got like six of \'em? I betcha I can snag one from him. :-o \r\nSeriously, no worries. You gave ample time, and I was lazy and late to the game! :grin: \r\n\r\nDude, GREAT rides you are modding and posting!!\r\n\r\nI think I\'m in over my head with my mod, I\'ll send ya some pics and see what ya think. Prolly in a couple days. \r\n\r\nAgain, your rides are killer! It scares me away at at the same time gives me inspiration!!! :lol:'),(33352,'aeba787161','[quote:aeba787161=\"MotorGong\"]Hey dude!\r\n\r\nDid you start a thread on computer tips? Something about the host file? I thought I saw one in the click yesterday, but can\'t find shit anywhere now. :wobble: \r\n\r\nI can see where it would be a good idea, then also not. Ya got some guy sayin\' that he screwed up his computer with someone\'s advice, etc. :grin: \r\n\r\nI just [i:aeba787161]thought [/i:aeba787161]I saw something, and wanted to confirm my sanity. :grin:[/quote:aeba787161]\r\nYea it was there. I diced it because I got the feeling not to many people were interested in it.\r\n\r\nHere\'s a Google search for it: http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&amp;q=hosts+file\r\n\r\nIt\'s easy peasy to do. If you need help, just give a shout.'),(31411,'f8551e113a','[quote:f8551e113a=\"Tuner1989\"]beause my local tru is at least a a hour away its easier just to get a controller that i know works.[/quote:f8551e113a]\r\n\r\nAh, ok.  So 10+shipping is what you offered?  Where am I shipping this to?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31457,'bc6d46c922','Thanks :-)'),(31910,'178efdf577','I\'ll take the GTO.  Let me know the info and I\'ll pay pal you the cash pronto.\r\n\r\nShipping address\r\n\r\nJesses King\r\n163 Main St\r\nFt Fairfield, ME 04742'),(37505,'1e47fc811e','sounds like a hot little rig! i\'ll have to do some work on my mt just so i can keep up! :lol: \r\n\r\nmcg drinkin\' beer? bloody bewdy! :-o \r\nyou\'ll get a sneak peek during the commonwealth games 8-)'),(37633,'07b10ce030','[quote:07b10ce030=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I can make the payment now, I was just making sure of my purchase. What can i use the lipo pack on? Can I charge it with the cheapo chargers that come with lith pro kits?[/quote:07b10ce030]\r\n\r\nIf your talking about the black cell phone type charger that would be a no.\r\n\r\nI reccomend this type charger to use for it.\r\n\r\nhttp://teammnm.net/product_info.php/products_id/70?osCsid=94bb28890e6f1c490de162bc4d31bc35\r\n\r\nYou can use the lipo pack on basically anything that will get a good runtime off of it. Since it has a very good discharge rate it is able to power very hot motors without pulling a muscle.'),(34760,'9aa7e66645','finally got that photo, sorry for being such a slack cunt.   gotta email addy for me to send it to?&gt;\r\n\r\nta,\r\n\r\nMAtt.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24944,'b258695d6d','Here it be Dave,\r\n\r\nRobert Estrada\r\n1312 Dougall Ave.\r\nWindsor, Ont.\r\nN8X 1R5\r\nCanada'),(24947,'1ceda28957','It\'s in the mail.'),(34387,'f80265cdf5','I\'m just going to surf Ebay in the UK and see what I can come up with'),(37818,'1edc344fbd','hey man-\r\n\r\nI\'ll take the IW04 parts. How about if you package that up and send it to me and let me know how much actual shipping was and I\'ll paypal ya $5 + shipping. Don\'t want you to use up all the loot just shipping it.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nsuperfly'),(24706,'b2341ea596','Yes you should have the right FETs, although Im assuming that some of the letters below the 4562 are not the ones you posted there should be some Greek characters including one that looks like a triangle.\r\n\r\nI am willing to sell you one of my first version circuit boards without FETs and your choice of deck light colors but it would take a couple of weeks to get the parts for it in and installing it is not a walk in the park, you would need a good soldering Iron and some skill at soldering.  You must remove the Xmod FETs and install the ribbon cable in their place, also there also a couple of other components on the Xmod circuit board that must be removed too, and I dont have a tutorial on how to do it.\r\n\r\nIt would not be cheep either the boards [u:b2341ea596]take me hours[/u:b2341ea596] to make, and the only extra one I have right now already has FETs on it.  I don\'t know how to put this delicately so I\'ll just fess up I\'ve sold 4 Xmods with the front deck circuit boards and lithium ions for over $250 each and have already been offered over $600 for the Mustang with it\'s GPM parts which is funny because It\'s not for sale even at that price.  I don\'t make my cars for profit but my time is valuable and they are unique.\r\n\r\nLBRC'),(32870,'d843d4f817','Cool.  Thanks for the info on the motor.  It wouldn\'t be my first nitro, but my experience with my savage was pretty limited due to money issues at the time.  \r\n\r\nBummer to hear about your sub, mine\'s pretty sealed up too.  Hope you get a new one out of it.  The store here is sold out.  I stopped by to get some for my cousin and her sister\'s birthday.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32530,'6eaf2621f5','[quote:6eaf2621f5]Rich Huang \r\n354 Mayo Lane \r\nBloomngdale, IL 60108 \r\n[/quote:6eaf2621f5]\r\n\r\nJust double checking to make sure this is still your current address.'),(32531,'f37ef8ca6e','Hey I saw the Plasmatomic motors you made...very nice, I was wondering...if I paid you, for the parts and the labor, would you make me a motor and tell me how to install it...I\'m kind of new to X Mods, the local like small business sports store, right around the block from me, is making a track for X Mods inside the store, and he said they are gona do races and bets and other stuff just for fun, but with at least one of my X Mods, I wanna blow everyone out of the water, if not, thats fine, I was just asking, and thanks for your time man\r\n\r\n-Josh'),(33512,'4d7eab9f61','Fuck your fast Cabo\r\n\r\nWell bad news with the alloys or w.e, i tried it on another bit and fucked up the bit/clone pretty bad...It wobbled sort of and theres no more smooth ride. But i wanted to order in some pullbacks, i was looking on the microsizers.de site and i saw they had a green Lambo pullback and i heard these bad boys could be thrown onto a bit, sounds sick to use all those parts so i\'m lovin it! \r\n\r\nO yee by the way, ive been keeping my mouth shut on the post boards for a while it looks to be paying off, but I got one other concern...\r\n\r\ni went to spray paint a purple tinted S2000 sport bit or w.e, and i masked everything pretty good i might add, but...The color did not look good at all????\r\n\r\nIt was a Tamiya Candy Blue and I\'ve used it on my other 1:10 scale bodies....you think it was because of the nasty purple tint? \r\n\r\nWhats the deal with that?'),(23938,'41968a9dee','Not sure what I have for custom stuff as my kids have killed most of them in our races lol.\r\n\r\n  I do have some stuff here but this also need to be updated as the alloys/sub and a few other things are gone.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=4291');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32695,'264e3e07d9','shit dude, this is scary.....don\'t mean to bug ya so much but......\r\n\r\ni posted that SAME fucking quote from him in the reg forums. then i go to the click, and there\'s your topic! :-D \r\n\r\nNoooooooooooo! I\'m thinking like sess! :lol:'),(27090,'76a50443e0','Hmmmmm....I was just looking at my other posts. I\'m not sure what I was thinking. I must have forgot that I already offered you the bigfoot kit in the original offer and then re-offered the bigfoot kit and added the motor uprade???\r\n\r\nMaybe I originally meant to put in one of my extra Mustang Mach 1 SE kits instead of the bigfoot.\r\n\r\nRegardless....a deal is a deal, so I\'ll paypal you some cash back. You did get the motor upgrade, which was not originally offered. So how about I paypal you 15 smackers?\r\n\r\nSorry for the confusion, it was unintentional.'),(25441,'9319308696','Hey sorry I was out of the country yes i got it and will put yours in the mail on monday.'),(35175,'3cb874bb36','Hey I bought a pcb from you that you put 13 fet\'s will it worked fine intil i let some do some modding and now it only goes backwards but i have to cars that i would like to have fets put on one is dual speed and tri cell and the other is stock would like to have it tri cell but would reallly like to see i can find lithum if they make them that small.anyway if you can or know someone that can do the work plz e-mail me at delano_wilson@hotmail.com also I am lookin for some alloies too.Oh the cars are bits');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24283,'f4b17fe016','Sure man, I totally support this site. Cash or money order? Oh ya, who do I mail the funds to.'),(22859,'6e17d1b862','still got the stuff?'),(22860,'8912ffc2ea','Yep, the only thing that has changed is I put some decals and gloss on the yellow Skyline. You can see it in the flossin\' forum.'),(22861,'dd31647901','Hello ph2t, \r\n\r\nI ask a question about nelly turbo.\r\n\r\nDid it work with iwaver. I have one mini-z mr01 and one iwaver. And i also think to buy mr-o2 or OL mini-z did it work to all. And i am from Turkey. How much does is cost to me + shipping thanks for your answers.'),(22862,'965b55c5d5','[quote:965b55c5d5=\"KuZGuN\"]Hello ph2t, \r\n\r\nI ask a question about nelly turbo.\r\n\r\nDid it work with iwaver. I have one mini-z mr01 and one iwaver. And i also think to buy mr-o2 or OL mini-z did it work to all. And i am from Turkey. How much does is cost to me + shipping thanks for your answers.[/quote:965b55c5d5]\r\n\r\nHey dude, yes nelly works with ALL iwaver, mr01, mr02, OL, monster..\r\n\r\nThere are two types of nelyl available.\r\n\r\nSee here for all information including shipping and $$.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.ausmicro.com/link.asp?TOPIC_ID=2355\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.'),(35025,'0fbd95b247','[quote:0fbd95b247=\"pimpsmurf\"]Any word, big bird? I haven\'t got a response from email.\r\n\r\nWhat\'s up?\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:0fbd95b247]\r\n\r\nhey man, when did ya send the email?  I must of missed it, lots of spam lately.   I finally finished a batch of deluxes this weekend.  Your 2nd one will hit the old post office later today (7:20am at the moment, sitting in my jocks at the PC, lol.....), I\'ll let you know when it has left my hands.....\r\n\r\nslacka...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25627,'a312db43a2','[quote:a312db43a2=\"viperdout\"]Dave:\r\n\r\nI\'m more of an xmods guy, but it sounds like for some reason, the Muscle Machine\'s fets fried open.   You mean the Ns give my monster some pull from the orange?  That\'s pretty cool.  Mine\'s gonna get mostly indoor running with the big gears, and I\'m building a track for it when I get back, and I\'ll probably use a stock motor and gear, so I can keep the track small.  \r\n\r\nWho knows with the resistor.  Hell, you could get better range!  Anyway, drive my stocker around for a bit and make yourself feel better.  \r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:a312db43a2]I\'m cool, that resistor did the trick. I think maybe it cut my range a little, but I pulled the knot out of the antenna, and now I think it balanced out. :lol: \r\n\r\nAnd yeah it got some decent pull with the orange gears on shag carpet, better than stock. My gears were still smooth, but as soon as I got the FETs in, the whine started, but not in the other direction. Then I got the other FET in, and the whine kicked in, in that direction too, so I knew it made a difference right away.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI was just reviewing my notes, and I didn\'t notice I did four for the steering. Their should be 2 P-channels in an H-bridge, so either I did part of the throttle, or something. Gotta ask ph2t about that.\r\n\r\nAt any rate ph2t will be getting his own soon, so if he can\'t come up with a quick fix with the information provided to him, then I\'ll go ahead and pay the shipping to getthis back to you, then when ever you have the answer, just send it to me, and I\'ll finish it off at no charge.\r\n\r\nThat way you can have some fun in the meantime. These things are so torquey to begin with, I really think this partial FET thing aint so bad. \r\n\r\nWe\'ll see, fingers crossed.\r\n\r\ndave'),(24750,'4bf2455971','I got the shipping price today.  It\'s $8.50.\r\n\r\nJeep=$11\r\nS&amp;H=$8.50\r\nTotal=$19.50\r\n\r\nMy PayPal if you still want it.\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you get this Jeep, I\'m gonna include something that has to get to Ph2t.  He said to send it with your stuff if you get the Jeep.  It\'ll be cheaper on shipping from you to him.  I\'m picking up the extra tab on the S&amp;H for his stuff.  Its the Nelly of mine he wants to inspect, so it\'s nothing big.  Its actin\' weird and he wants to investigate why.\r\n\r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33856,'c311ce22cb','Well, that\'s too bad about the Baja.  Although, I could still rip that PCB out and replace it with a spare 27 mhz or 45 mhz PCBs that I have waiting to be used.  It\'s up to you.  You put outstanding work into that Baja, so I don\'t mind giving it the extra effort.\r\n\r\nAs far as the ZZSE goes, I\'ve never fetted any of my ZZSE\'s.  Mostly because I don\'t care for them that much.  I could figure it out pretty easy and I have the right fets for the job, but, I would actually recomend this job to CrazyDave.  He\'s been doing fet jobs to ZZSE\'s for a long time.  He won\'t let you down.  Many people have sent their cars to him to get fetted.\r\n\r\nIf he can\'t do it for some reason, then let me know and I\'ll hook you up.'),(33857,'98968d408c','On a side note, the ZZSE have a dismal increase in performance with fet modding.  The way the electronics are set up, the weight and the low output batteries make this car kinda shitty really.  There\'s also not any room inside to make this car better.  Some people have managed to get them to a decent speed, but it was after heavy heavy modding.  An old school bit or ZZ with very little modding (maybe none, with certain set ups) would still blow it away.'),(31413,'17a8dee911','[quote:17a8dee911=\"viperdout\"][quote:17a8dee911=\"Tuner1989\"]beause my local tru is at least a a hour away its easier just to get a controller that i know works.[/quote:17a8dee911]\r\n\r\nAh, ok.  So 10+shipping is what you offered?  Where am I shipping this to?[/quote:17a8dee911]\r\n\r\n\r\nCan we do 10 shipped? I need your paypal address and it would be shipped to florida.\r\n\r\nMatt Gera\r\n4303 Radcliffe Dr.\r\nPalm Harbor Fl.\r\n34685');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24239,'67e248158c','Well, i am working on one of betty k\'s cars, and the damn pics arent showing up.. And since i cant visualize words for shit, i was hoping that you could change the pics that are there (the ones from rear shock) to the ones that are supposed to be there.  If you could, that would be great.\r\n\r\nDex'),(22888,'933aabdb61','Just a heads up, and a tease shot of my car that\'s goin on the block..\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:933aabdb61]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10004/normal_DSC03068.JPG[/img:933aabdb61]'),(34762,'f9dbc51c62','[quote:f9dbc51c62=\"ph2t\"]finally got that photo, sorry for being such a slack cunt.   gotta email addy for me to send it to?&gt;\r\n\r\nta,\r\n\r\nMAtt.[/quote:f9dbc51c62]\r\n\r\nshoot it to greg@grymttr.com\r\n\r\nthanks!'),(23939,'072db5b01b','Skyline GT2000 (new in box)?  That would be the shiz.....'),(23417,'548f638562','hey\r\n\r\ni just sent the 28 bucks into ur paypal account for the auction i won.\r\n\r\n\r\nif you need my details (i think paypal shows em) just ask\r\n\r\n\r\ncheers'),(35888,'15c09b1443','Nope, I\'m \"Chrome.\"  I\'ve got a poison purple mushroom icon, you can\'t miss me.  I\'ve added you as a friend, we\'ll have to play sometime.  I\'m getting on right now.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24817,'2c117adf32','Got your MO today in the mail, thanks pimp :-) \r\n\r\nI\'ve told crazydave to go ahead and ship the car to you.\r\nI\'m not certain if he has your shipping address or not, so he might send you a PM asking for it.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know when you receive the car so I can mark it as a done deal.\r\n\r\nThanks again holmes.'),(23416,'64326949fd','well still email u the admin to unban u. he said all is cool over there with you and sessiz and he said he just wasn\'t sure of the initial forum attack.\r\ni thik he kept one of those piks you had up and sent it to his friends email list.  :eek: \r\n\r\ni don\'t want to see that agaiin  :shock:  :sad: \r\n\r\n :grin:'),(24825,'57f67730aa','good info to know...\r\n\r\nthanks again, still learning my way around the hood.'),(27232,'fa5a4ea697','Ummm...\r\n\r\nYup I\'ll be up for a bit...\r\n\r\nYup, we can charge up some packs...\r\n\r\nYup... picked up the new Driver in the way home from work today...\r\n\r\nDidn\'t even look at it yet :-)'),(35230,'726d21c2e8','Hey Hue this bigbandit And I was wondering if you know anyone i can desn 2 bit 2 ZZSE and 1 ZZMT to to have work done I am working on some bodies but need speed to go with them what I am look for on my bit ie FET upgades and my ZZSE FET. AND 2 OR 3 cell upgrades and my ZZMT lipoly FET\'s so on or if you know anyne selling some bits already pimped out let me know you can reach me via e-mail delano_wilson@hotmail.com thankz');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35238,'03ac11de04','thanks if you know anyone the I can send 2 bits to for Fet upgrades plz let me know.'),(37291,'e990fac34c','yes, i have 1 spare 11t pinion and spur.\r\n\r\ni have a pair of rear alloy axles but only 1 alloy cup spare (the short one.)\r\n\r\nthe s03 probably could use some new brushes soon, i\'ll throw a set in if you want.\r\n\r\nhow\'s about $50us shipped for all that? (i\'ll throw in some other stuff too.)'),(37293,'3ca89cc133','These were not in the first order.\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver	Black	Green\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	0	0	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.54	0	0	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME330LAN	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR LANCER) - 1PC	$5.90	0	0	1\r\nXME330MUS	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR MUSTANG) - 1PC	$3.84	0	0	1\r\nXET330FORD	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR TRUCKIN) - 1PC	$6.90	1	0	0\r\nXET330HUM	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR HUMMER) - 1PC	$5.90	1	0	0\r\n\r\nActual	$53.54	 	 	 \r\n10.00%	$5.35	 	 	 \r\nSub	$58.89			\r\nS&amp;H	$3.00			\r\nTotal	$61.89			\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.41 Off of GPM\'s regular price.\r\n\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me know as soon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com.  Please include your user name in the notes on PayPal.\r\n\r\nIf you do reply by February 11th  your request will not be ordered.'),(36805,'faa31759d2','[quote:faa31759d2=\"ph2t\"]hey man, I know, slack late response.  You\'ve prolyl figured out the problem now.\r\n\r\nI take it was a DNS issue?  You running an exchange box in a BIND DNS environment?\r\n\r\nhttp://www.msexchange.org/ is an excellent site for all things exchange, just search the forums there, it may help.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:faa31759d2]\r\nThanks holmes. Nah, wasn\'t a DNS issue. I still have some residual issues left-over but the main part is working now. Our network is so convoluted it\'s not even funny.\r\nI\'ve been going through that site, found some helpful info, but most really didn\'t apply to my particular situation. Again, probably just because of how our network is setup.\r\nI like coding much better than network admin. lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31440,'0b4d07116d','I need your paypal address asap please im about to leave on vacation this coming sunday and hope to have the controller by then.'),(31441,'42a94c143e','Hey, how are the Digi-Q F1\'s? Are they fully propo? Fast? Do you have any videos? Thanks man.'),(35288,'fb0d833a85','My ZZSE\'s are first Gen I think And I\'ll pay pal you next friday after I cash my check i package the ZZMT good I am adding a lipoly to it too but I can do that one  of my Bits need 2 more cells added.'),(35427,'f45d7fd5fa','Love that reply post. Helped me out a greaaaaat deal. Thanks alot man. The order you told me to mod is exactly what I am going to follow. Once I get my miniZ I am going to see exactly what I should do to fix it up. And now that I know Xmods aint really that fast with FETS then it is definately going to be modded.\r\n\r\nThanks a alot!'),(34401,'d1e1c5a8fc','Lemme know on the WRX / Gloria  :cool: \r\n\r\nHow many Lxx VW Beetles are available?'),(34404,'28288ba3dd','Hey man was just joking when I said Hector did not mean it as a race thing or anything just pulled the name out of my butt! sorry if I offended you know I don\'t mean anything by it.  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (24906,'7cb44831a9','ok, im just working out about getting a paypal account up for myself.  sorry for the slow replys ive been on the road with work and finding web access in some shitholes is really hard...\r\n\r\n  18.50 sounds cool.   thanx for the effort again, i\'ll get back to you soon.'),(24907,'f202ce71ad','[quote:f202ce71ad=\"z-beam\"]ok, im just working out about getting a paypal account up for myself.  sorry for the slow replys ive been on the road with work and finding web access in some shitholes is really hard...\r\n\r\n  18.50 sounds cool.   thanx for the effort again, i\'ll get back to you soon.[/quote:f202ce71ad]\r\n\r\n\r\nJust let me know when you drop the cash my way via PayPal.  If it would be easier, send the money via mail to Ph2t and have him PayPal it to me if you want.\r\n\r\nAlso, could you do me a favor and drop Ph2t a message that we worked out a deal and that his stuff will be coming with yours.\r\n\r\nI\'ll let him know too, but I just want him to hear it from you too, so its comfirmed both ways.\r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(24910,'8b997ad877','hey etsu,\r\n\r\nLeave the chat room and then come back');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26623,'7ce1e79c33','1-That would be hard to do,but if you gave me a decent price I would probably do it. It would probably take  long time to get there also\r\n2-Im not sure. Maybe $25 USD shipped to the uk?Im not really sure. It depends on how much shipping would cost. \r\n3-It would smoke a bit with a 3.0 motor and orange gears. This car has an axle in the rear with teal MS gears, and small cone wheels, making it go even faster.My car also has a 3.4 Motor. Even If my car wasntdual celled, it would probably still beat the ms that you describe. But my car is dual celled, so it would basically smoke the bit you are talking about. \r\n4-thanks to you too!'),(37386,'dbb4c79f39','Nah, lets just go till the end of the month when you\'ve got more parts.  I\'d hate to have you ship out too many packages and run your shipping costs up.  Thanks for the update.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(37917,'8eb5a401bf','Redrustbucket posted this a coupla days ago... 4 posts down from yours.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7607'),(37922,'15e40ecdda','Thanks Hue.  Appears I was having cache issues and new content was showing.  Got it fixed and seeing it now.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37923,'f248f91d53','I\'ll take it!\r\n\r\nThanks SWG. Is there anything zz, bit or mini-z that you need? I\'ll paypal ya the $30.00, unless I have something of value you might want.'),(34543,'71f63c1eb8','Thanks for the kana and the lil lesson man. Highly apreciated. :-o'),(34475,'5975fb999a','Hey, I would like to see your PCB layout for the knight rider lights...\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1005&amp;postdays=0&amp;postorder=asc&amp;start=15\r\n\r\nyour pics died.\r\n\r\nAlso, how did you assemble a DC-DC converter for 5V? did you modify the existing one on the PCB?'),(32146,'3bbf8ca5bb','Hows things goin\'?\r\n\r\nHave you been able to get any parts made?\r\n\r\nHaven\'t seen you around in awhile. :-) \r\n\r\nSG219'),(32148,'eaa04bc5b7','Hey  :-) ,\r\n\r\nCouldnt exactly answer you question at 1-43.com but as a Pimp I thought you should have more of an answer. so what I can do is ask you if youve browsed through my photo gallery lately?\r\n\r\n[url]http://lbspd.com/v-web/gallery/album27/Spud_Power[/url]'),(36842,'bece45b4f5','What do you think?  \r\n\r\nSaw that the package was finally delivered yesterday and have discovered that I am more than a little anxious to know what you think of the 3 ZZMT motors in it (1 Yellow, 2 Orange).\r\n\r\nThey are my overall favorite motor option for my track, 18 x 10 feet w/ 2 foot lanes, unfortunately because the motors have to sit so close to the diff side ball bearing I couldnt seem to get one right milling it out of heavier stock and had to settle for the thin C stock with the aluminum axle and bearing tube.  Takes too long to make :-? .\r\n\r\nSo this kid says to me my brother put a ZZMT motor in an Epoch and its much faster so pompous ass that I am I show him a photo of an epoch motor beside a ZZMT motor and say its too small sonny go away. Well I was wrong, definitely big time wrong, ouch.\r\n\r\nI still doubt he even had a brother yet alone one who managed to fit ZZMT motor in an epoch motor case, not easy to do I tried it makes a mess, but he definitely was right about the motor, even one is technically faster just slow to get up to speed, and two LoL you get to decide that. \r\n\r\nI usually end up adding a little weight to the rear of the car for better traction and handling.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33235,'e75ff4342a','I\'m lookin\' for tires, wheels, and diffs, or anything else that my come my way.  Not really lookin\' to buy, just trade at the moment. \r\n\r\nI think I\'m getting the Hardcore green stuff.  There\'s a package deal on Ebay I\'ve been eyeing up.  $85 for all the goodies from HC.\r\n\r\nDid you have something in mind?'),(33148,'d55b69feca','Yo wassup cj i saw ur post. :grin:'),(33150,'e2a54123a8','Hey man,\r\n\r\nSorry for not getting back to you earlier....\r\n\r\nAnyways, the rims came from a DUB CITY (made by Jada Toys) diecast.\r\nYou\'ll find all kinds of DUB CITY cars at Target and Walmart.\r\nThe rims I used are from an original DUB CITY car. I\'m not sure if they make those any more. :o  \r\nBut I\'m sure there are still some out there... just gotta look. :-o \r\n\r\nBut, if you really need [u:e2a54123a8]those[/u:e2a54123a8] rims, I think I still have some.\r\nLet me know.\r\n\r\n-DriveWRX  :cool:'),(27750,'49a3dbf3e6','[quote:49a3dbf3e6=\"viperdout\"]Cabo:\r\n\r\nI am truly honored.  I just ask one thing: can I get rid of the Bitgimp title?  \r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:49a3dbf3e6]bitGimp no more, it\'s gone.  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28263,'e045cf608e','Hey Dave. I\'ve been offline for a couple of days. Yeah, I\'ll see what she has left. It might be a couple of weeks or so before I place an order. My car\'s tranny blew last Thursday, and I just got the estimate back today. :-( \r\n\r\nLet me get back to you with a list of what I can get, and I\'ll let you know. Have you ever got any of the Perfection bodies before? I ask, because you should be warned that the paint jobs are not purdy, sometimes. The JGTC bodies are probably the best Perfection bodies, at least of the one\'s I have. I got some VW Beetles and Buses that were horrible. I was gonna repaint those anyway, so no biggie.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nmikirgra\r\nmick the quick\r\nMichael Graham'),(34791,'9c574a7937','I was wondering if i could swap out one of my entries for another one?'),(37878,'dfc0196a20','Sorry about that, i wont put anything like that in it again :-)  Thanks for the heads up :-o'),(36802,'e689d2bd7f','I have alot of stock xmod knuckles...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33998,'dab85163b0','eh? its on a zzmt and the seering still works i just dont want to tear it up.'),(31412,'efe2d2b332','Ok , \r\nno problem , she is a BEAST .\r\ni was going to follow a betty k tutorial and i think i will as soon as i get some money . I have a 2week holiday right now , and if i spent most of it making one i might get somewhere.How much did it cost all together ?\r\ni like your work alot its a great creation. One more question though , \r\nhow long did she take you to build ?.\r\n\r\nwould you be able to send me a few pics , maybe even a video if possible. I would be very greatfull .\r\n\r\nmany thanks , \r\njoe \r\n\r\n\r\nalso , whats the specs ?'),(26668,'1ef1398cb9','you honestly don\'t need to make the shock, the h plate is more than enough suspension. just select the right sort of plastic, not too thick and not too flexy.'),(26675,'33db946a6e','yeah , lol , i 1 of the steering wires on it  :-( \r\nbut its ok , im still using it for a right turning oval LOL\r\nhaha ,\r\nthose rear tires , i use as a alternative to spending money on a drift kit haha\r\ncheers anyway ,\r\nmy mat is now honging up now to get rid of those bumps ,\r\nh20'),(31447,'0d7b5028e1','Aight no problem.\r\nGotta love em though.\r\nIl try that bonzermat thing sometime. :smile:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31430,'721831f7c8','Hmm , i cant really afford it right now but thankyou VERY much for the offer , i appreciate it alot .\r\nAs for the bonzermat , Got it out yesterday from moving and the removal men had bent it in half despite the big sign saying \" DO NOT BEND \" and it now has big creases .I was talking to the guy who makes em.He told me to hold it in front of a gas fire for a few seconds and they will drop out , but i dont have one wich is a bummer .\r\nI might be able to use a gas stove though , il try tomorrow morning.\r\nNot sure about swapping it for the shens , But if you have an off-road bit\r\nthat you would be willing to trade i would be happy to.They look so nice and i thaught you might have an old one from when you started making them . Im loving the newest one in your gallery ( the see through chassis one ) .But if you want the bonzermat , im sure we can sort something out .'),(26680,'7dbcbc2dbf','Hey dave,\r\n\r\nHow did you make that sweet body kit for you ZZSE audi TT?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31445,'06287af6cb','yes they are fully propo , they are hard to controll at first but once you get used to them , they are a blast , you can set the speed, accel, handling levels ( 1-10 ) on the controller according to what surface your racing on , e.g for a wood floow i would use , 7speed , 3 accel . therefore it wont wheelspin when it takes off but wont go to fast to turn.I can get a video , i have had an offer on this for a brand new zzmt also , so im not sure what you want to do   :???: \r\n\r\nthanks , \r\nJOE'),(26682,'e807702a70','Sorry don\'t use messanger but you could always mail me yakboy@btopenworld.com\r\n\r\nregards\r\n\r\nYakboy'),(26683,'ae72854ceb','Hi Crazy Doc,\r\n\r\nGreat to speak to a fellow European, Great circuit by the way. I love scenery, thats what I\'m aiming for with my current circuit.\r\n\r\nI think you Germans have taken to bits in a big way, I\'m impressed with some of your retailers especially bitstylaz but they seem reluctant to ship outside germany which is a shame because the bodies look cool (my best friend lives in Austria so hopefully get them to ship there)\r\n\r\nThe Bit scene is smaller in the UK but hopefully will grow.\r\n\r\nI\'m hoping to make the race of champions circuit in pieces like my current circuit so it\'s portable, but this years track in paris looked so good I can\'t resist building it.\r\n\r\nGood to talk to you\r\n\r\nYakboy'),(33522,'dbad779f4f','[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Been a while since we chatted music, so I thought I\'d see what\'s up.[/quote:dbad779f4f]I\'ve been musically broken for a few months or more... that video class I took was a really intense experience. It was pretty much my life for three+ months. The thing I never really thought about was the part where music is too distracting to listen to while working in video. I\'m used to listening to tunes while I work, so that was a bit of a shock... it\'s been a pretty interesting experience, though. \r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]I was really into that whole Modest Mouse/Franz Ferdinand/The Killers/The Bravery thing that is going on, but I\'m bored with that now.[/quote:dbad779f4f]\r\nModest Mouse is in my rotation a lot over the past coupla years... in that category, though, there\'s this band that has been fuckin\' ruling... Inouk. The\'ve got one LP out, No Danger, which is more amazing every time I hear it... great songs, but as an album it\'s genius. They\'re from Philadelphia, of all places.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Been mostly listening to the Transplant\'s 2005 release, \"Haunted Cities\". I really dig it. I think the punk is more punk, and the rap is more rap, but its cool hearing some solid rymes over punk beats. That Blink 182 guy is a solid drummer too, pulling off break beats and shit. Overall I think they really stepped it up over their last release, and remain a unique mix of punk and rap, that I don\'t hear anyone else doing.[/quote:dbad779f4f]Hmmm... ain\'t heard it. I\'m puttin\' it on the list, though.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]I\'m also listening to Meat Puppets II. They\'re local boys, I had heard most this stuff live back in the day, but this sounds more country sounding than I remember.[/quote:dbad779f4f]First real show I ever saw was Meat Puppets, on the Mirage tour... holy shit, they changed my life. I was a serious King Crimson fan back then, so to see a guy who clearly had listened to that stuff, but was just so much looser, was a mind fuck. Kurt Kirkwood\'s blend of Fripp-like arpeggiated lines and twang and punk was just so outta control... anyway, that shit changed me. I still listen to the shit outta that band, but only to a point. Too High to Die was the first album I didn\'t like at all, then I stopped caring about their new shit... I\'ve got all of it, from the first album through Monsters.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Another back in the day album I\'ve been listening to is The Cure, \"We Hate Rock \'N Roll\". I don\'t care what anyone says about these guys, Robert Smith was a song writing machine, knocking out poppy melodies faster than you can blink. This compilation of early performances is a bit rough, and the songs sound a bit stripped. There\'s an awkward hyperness to all the songs, but that got me thinking, if he traded in that chorus pedal for some distortion, he might even be punk.[/quote:dbad779f4f]I ain\'t got a problem with those guys. I\'ve got their second album, and still plan on getting the first. In the early days, they had a cool sound... I\'d never looked at it that way, but yeah, plug the instruments into different amps &amp; effects and change the character of the recording... they would be punk, huh?\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Back on the current side I was checking out The White Stripes, \"Get Behind Me Satan\". I love Jack, and I think he really steps up his performance on this one, but its just so formula by now that its kinda wearing thin.[/quote:dbad779f4f]I just got it, so it hasn\'t worn thin, yet... yeah, I wanna see them before it doesn\'t matter any more... it might be too late already. Check out The Black Keys, if you haven\'t.. last year\'s Rubber Factory was a masterpiece.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]I\'m listening to Super Furry Thing\'s recent one right now. Don\'t know much about them. Its alright. Really mellow, but they\'re appropriately named, because its all warm and fuzzy.[/quote:dbad779f4f]Do you mean Super Furry Animals? If you\'re talking about those guys, I\'ve got all of it, except the new one. I love that band.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Tried to get Stiff Little Fingers today, but the tracker was broke. Only heard one song by them, but I really liked it. [/quote:dbad779f4f]\r\nI\'ve got Inflammable Material... a dupe from a friend, anyway. I still haven\'t listened to it enough, but I dig it.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]So that\'s about it. Still loving System of a Down. They fucking rock. You listening to anything new? [/quote:dbad779f4f]\r\nSystem of a down... hmmm. I don\'t know what it is with those guys that just doesn\'t sit so well with me. There\'s a lot about it that I really appreciate, but the guy\'s voice is just... I don\'t know, maybe it isn\'t even that. I wanna like \'em, and I certainly don\'t dislike them... they just leave me all meh &amp; whatnot. What album would you start with? Maybe that\'s the problem... I just started in the wrong spot. I\'ve done that before.\r\n\r\nNew? Kasabian is sorta new... young guys from England. I saw them on Dave Letterman a few months ago and bought the cd the next day... haven\'t done that in awhile. It\'s that their bass player has balls, plays with distortion and is a little wreckless... my kinda playin\'. I like \'em.\r\n\r\nWhat I\'ve really been listening to, though, is D.O.A., War on 45/Bloodied But Unbowed. Can\'t get enough of it. That drummer, Chuck Biscuits, is just fuckin\' sick... like the John Bonham of punk. They just rock so hard, nothing else matters... nothing except The Wipers, that is, which is a conversation I\'ve been wanting to have with you for a while now. Greg Sage... he\'s from my town, but relocated to your town quite awhile ago. I\'ve read a lot of interviews with that guy and always think you and he may be of the same mindset. He\'s a super-cool dude, for sure. I\'ve got most of the catalog now, and I dig it all. I\'m sure you know all about The Wipers... they are something I put off forever, but finally got into about a year and a half ago... whew, I wish I would have been a little older when those dudes were playin\' in Portland.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Oh yeah, and I guess I was supposed to be visiting about now. Pssh, I\'d really rather not talk about that, its kind of a point of agitation with me by now. I will say, I\'m not giving up, but I am just gonna take a week off of work for now, get my head and body together, and catch up on a couple projects. Those projects being the guitar under my bed, and your car, and then take things from there.  [/quote:dbad779f4f]\r\nI hear ya... I feel like I\'m the subject of a Kafka story, these days. I\'m changing into something, but I don\'t quite know what. I just know that what I\'ve doing just ain\'t what I\'m supposed to be doing. The video thing might lead to something, but I\'m not too sure yet. It seems to suit my brain real well, but I still feel like it\'ll be real hard to make a transition, laterally, into a new career. Either way, I\'m taking this term off, then going back for some advanced editing courses in a few months. But yeah, life feels all volitile/fragile right now... an uncomfortable combination.\r\n\r\n[quote:dbad779f4f=\"crazydave\"]Speaking of your car, I wanted to talk about that. I\'ve been thinking about that. You know, over time visions change, and I think I lost touch of what you were seeing in the car. I have lowered it since I first built it, and with a little work, I was seeing how I could narrow the rear end slightly, and tuck the rear wheels into the body, kinda like what you do with your muscle cars, but then after reading this Car Kulture Deluxe mag, with all the old school rods and gassers, and after looking the original pic from the mod contest, I realized I had the fatter tires that came with the alloys in the rear, and the whole car was more jacked up. That really fit with the old school theme, and liked how the chassis was mor obvious. I thought maybe that\'s what you were seeing, and I was going in the wrong direction. I know you keep saying, what ever I want to do, but seriously, do you think that was part of the appeal, or had that even occurred to you as being part of it?[/quote:dbad779f4f]\r\nOriginally, I was thinking of a similar car to The Rat, maybe because that\'s where you were when we originally discussed it. Also because I really like your take on that stuff.\r\n\r\nSo, when you\'re asking, \"do you think that was part of the appeal, or had that even occurred to you as being part of it?\", are you talking about the \"more jacked up\", old school thing? If it\'s that, then yeah, maybe a little... again, I just like your take on that stuff. Honestly, I think I\'d be super happy with anything that came off of your bench. So, unless you aren\'t feelin\' the direction you\'re headin\', just keep on keepin\' on... but, if it feels like you\'re tryin\' to chase what you think I want, and you\'re not feelin\' like it\'s a car you\'d build for yourself, then maybe finish it off like [i:dbad779f4f]you\'d[/i:dbad779f4f] want it. The whole point for me is that I want a crazydave car, not a commissioned car that you built to my specs... does that help?\r\n\r\nHopefully I didn\'t miss your point, or make it more confusing.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMat');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33661,'25117a50c0','Hey dude, thanks for doing that. And yeah, im suprised that the post was as well as it was. With you being hammered and all, well thanks. \r\n\r\nIE: http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6786&amp;start=30'),(33677,'1f46c1c6f1','You\'re posting ALOT tonight, better ease up or you\'ll get flamed. You\'re not posting anything of substance and digging up some really old threads\r\n\r\n[quote:1f46c1c6f1=\"pimptothemax\"] :cool:  dammmm dude..................[/quote:1f46c1c6f1]\r\n\r\nPosted in :Full suspension EVO rally zipzap, springs all around!\r\nlast post: june 8th\r\nYour contribution with that post: nil\r\n\r\nPlease don\'t take this the wrong way but there have been some really immature noobs posting useless stuff. I\'d hate to see you get flamed and leave.\r\n\r\nJust a warning (I\'m not a Mod)\r\nMaxx'),(33664,'62021a4fc9','[quote:62021a4fc9=\"sessiz\"]So then you don\'t care about insurance or confirmation numbers and nextday and whatnot?\r\nIf this is correct, then I\'ll buy a padded envelope and send the rims out regular first class mail on tuesday. Do you want a delivery confirmation on that for tracking? \r\nNew York to Texas should only take a couple of days and with shipping and the price of the envelope you should be lookin at like around $3-$4 on top of that $15.\r\nSending a MO is cool but cash would be better, I don\'t use paypal anymore so that\'s out. :-)[/quote:62021a4fc9]\r\n\r\nNa no insurance, confirmation or crap just a padded envelope and send away I will send you $20.00 in cash if you think that will cover it? can I get your address to send the money? also do you want me to send it priority insured or do you feel safe with me just sending it? I have sent cash before and no problems. As soon as I have your address I will send you some moola! \r\nthanks again man!  :-o'),(34491,'295352ed08','[quote:295352ed08=\"Nasphere\"]Hey, I would like to see your PCB layout for the knight rider lights...\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1005&amp;postdays=0&amp;postorder=asc&amp;start=15\r\n\r\nyour pics died.\r\n\r\nAlso, how did you assemble a DC-DC converter for 5V? did you modify the existing one on the PCB?[/quote:295352ed08]\r\n\r\nsorry man, old stuff I don\'t have nay more.\r\n\r\nas for the DCDC convertor, I made it from external components.  check out dcdc charg pump convertors at onsemi.com  that\'s where I got mine froom.  agess ago....\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27312,'09ff7518b1','That ESC that I got from Hiroto came today.  You say it will go into the Bandit?\r\n\r\nHow hard of an install is it?  How long would it take?  It allready has the same plug as the batt packs that you let me borrow, so it would be a direct fit to those.'),(34289,'3ffb7fe6b2','[quote:3ffb7fe6b2=\"DarkTari\"][size=18:3ffb7fe6b2][b:3ffb7fe6b2]\r\n[color=blue:3ffb7fe6b2]DarkTari[/color:3ffb7fe6b2]\r\nGH Sims\r\n7815 Quill Point Dr.\r\nBowie, Md. 20720[/b:3ffb7fe6b2][/size:3ffb7fe6b2]\r\n\r\nHey Pimp!\r\nThanx again for doin this.  I got real busy yesterday and could look for that WRX.  I know I have a least 1 so when I pull it, I\'ll just send it on.\r\nGive my your addy just incase I don\'t already have it....... 8-)[/quote:3ffb7fe6b2]\r\n\r\nCool beans man my address:\r\nAaron W. Olmsted\r\n1941 Sayers Road\r\nBastrop, Texas 78602\r\nlet me know what you want for the body and I will get it to ya! \r\nOh and as for other bodies I cant think of any I have clone skylines coming out of my butt.......'),(37205,'6f3593baba','[quote:6f3593baba=\"spanky\"]hey when u made ur mt to flex, was the stiring a problem after u put it back together? The antenna is kinda in the way and the stiring does not want to spring back. Do u have any solutions  ???[/quote:6f3593baba]\r\n\r\nsteering wasnt a problem after the mod...but in general that steering motor is weak.\r\n\r\nyou can replace the steering motor with a stronger red zz motor.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37206,'','Hey thanks for the info. Its gonna be about another week until its completly done i did some extra mod to it as soon as im done ill post some pic. :-o'),(37207,'','Hey thanks for the info. Its gonna be about another week until its completly done i did some extra mod to it as soon as im done ill post some pic. :-o'),(34620,'a5bf7eca67','Hey man, Ive been searching and searching and i cant find any sort of a diagram to FET the zzse.  Since you seem to be well educated on the subject i figure ill go right to the source.  Do you have or know of a good tuttorial on doing an FET upgrade on the SE?\r\n\r\nAlso, Im trying to find the best place to order the FETs, any good places come to mind?\r\n\r\nThanks man\r\n\r\nSTG'),(27293,'b52f92b417','[quote:b52f92b417=\"ynad\"]i think it still works fine. i just havn\'t got the time to sort out and resize pictures . i hope you got space, i\'m yet to upload my mini-zs and xmods :grin: thanks for looking out.\r\nbtw i was loooking at your gallery. your paint jobs are, super.[/quote:b52f92b417]yea man, we should be able to accomidate ya.\r\n\r\nthanks holmes :-)'),(35087,'5ca043f16d','What I was trying to proove to these \"fanboys\" was that the xmods with a lil love are just as good as miniz cars.\r\nLemme start off with this. What do you enjoy more? Tinkering or driving. If you are like me and gather more pleasure from tearing apart and putting together then go Xmods. Otherwise buy a mini z.\r\nMy advice to you is this.... Buy an iwaver and hop it up with kyosho parts. :lol: \r\nIf the iwavers were out before the xmods were I would definatly never have gotten an xmod. I should also add that I was only into the 1/28s for a hot minute, the scale is just awkward to me. I do most of my racing/playing indoors and I just don\'t have the room. :( \r\nHence my love for bits and epochs. :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32980,'a6a879be54','http://one18th.com/GetGallery5902.htm                                                \n\n\nhttp://one18th.com/GetGallery5904.htm'),(32699,'bb16318498','shit dude, didn\'t you display all the responses though?\r\n\r\nthat\'s better I think..... :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n :-)'),(25738,'a6e7abb0a0','Drop me your addy.  I\'ll send you some.  Free :cool: \r\n\r\nI have plenty spare.\r\n\r\n\r\nSG219'),(28388,'a1510ff88b','Alright well I\'d really like to have a mosfet bit but I don\'t have 25 bucks at the moment, so can I just send You all the MT stuff I have and any other stuff You want, for a stock Panther or rally racer? I\'d give You my Hulk MT body but it had some ghetto work done to it, I over sprayed it with paint (kind of thick) and I took the arms off of it and filled in the gaps with putty and well I just didn\'t finish the project, but If You want I can strip it back down of all paint, and it\'d be clearish with putty here and there??? Whatever you want to do, I\'d just like to get rid of some of this stuff cuz I\'m sure fellow Bitpimps like You could use it and make it drivable again. Oh yeah the lights are still in tact on the Chevy body if You do want it. :cool:'),(28386,'01575ab917','The car and the mosfet are going to cost me around $25.00 with labor.  If you could come up with a truck body to throw into the deal that would be fair.  let me know and then I will make the mosfeted car and send you a picture as soon as I build it. FYI The mosfeted car will be a panther or ralley racer, which has better range than those microsizers and a quicker engine.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28387,'641031c00b','Alright well I\'d really like to have a mosfet bit but I don\'t have 25 bucks at the moment, so can I just send You all the MT stuff I have and any other stuff You want, for a stock Panther or rally racer? I\'d give You my Hulk MT body but it had some ghetto work done to it, I over sprayed it with paint (kind of thick) and I took the arms off of it and filled in the gaps with putty and well I just didn\'t finish the project, but If You want I can strip it back down of all paint, and it\'d be clearish with putty here and there??? Whatever you want to do, I\'d just like to get rid of some of this stuff cuz I\'m sure fellow Bitpimps like You could use it and make it drivable again. Oh yeah the lights are still in tact on the Chevy body if You do want it. :cool:'),(25147,'ab71d6e10e','hey man\r\n\r\nwas just wondering, does the shipping take 6 to 8 weeks?\r\n\r\n\r\ncheers'),(25148,'d308b58b61','dude sorry i didnt reply. i lost my job and my internet got cut for a little bit.\r\nI just packed up everything you got in the auction and a few extra bodies(jeep and supra) and a purple nos motor for the undue wait. a 27mhz thunder charger controller and an nkok charger are in there. i tested the car and controller just before packaging.\r\n[img:d308b58b61]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10003/tdude.jpg[/img:d308b58b61]\r\n\r\nagain I apologize for the delay and will pay a few extra bucks for express mail if I can.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30026,'06aa74b8df','to send them ill need to get a paded enlavope . those are 75 cents and shipping is $4 . hmm ill see what i can to to get the cash to ship it , ill take back pop cans or somethin . just pm me your mailling addy and i\'ll see what i can do .'),(25150,'448d64ffff','Yo Pimp,\r\n\r\nNo Problemo!  I asked you for the wheels, you didn\'t try to charge me, you sent then right away.  One good deed deserves another! \r\n\r\nThat\'s the way I roll Pimp....... :cool: \r\n\r\nHope you get good use outta them ! 8-)'),(28502,'c16b5debce','Hey CDub\r\nI was looking for the thread where You give props to people who\'ve You have done biz-naz with, I didn\'t find it anywhere, is it still on this site?\r\nThanks'),(28508,'12db5b5d4b','I will deff let Ya know, that paint job was clean and sharp, very good job, and I\'ll let Ya know if I need any resin parts made aswell, about those crazy rims, I\'m trying to pick out something still, not sure what would really set this skyline off, but it\'s going to be cool, any ideas?\r\nThanks Man'),(28522,'bddf2ec6b9','Are they just like hotwheels cars or rc cars, and do You know about how much they cost, well I\'ll just head over there soon, but I got to save up for the new GT500 SE, that thing is pimp too, maybe I can get you to paint that shell for me, nice gunmetal or artic silver or something, idk yet.\r\nThanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28383,'01575ab917','The car and the mosfet are going to cost me around $25.00 with labor.  If you could come up with a truck body to throw into the deal that would be fair.  let me know and then I will make the mosfeted car and send you a picture as soon as I build it. FYI The mosfeted car will be a panther or ralley racer, which has better range than those microsizers and a quicker engine.'),(25160,'835d12afcb','its cool man\r\n\r\ni just thought u forgot me dats all.\r\n\r\ndont worry about fast shipping save urself some cash.\r\n\r\nthanks for the extra shell\'s i always wanted the jeep! will look nice on my new monster.\r\n\r\nthanks for not forgetting me dude.\r\n\r\nthe site is still one of the best going around btw, \r\n\r\ncheers\r\n\r\n :D'),(28380,'c12472bf45','Hey, I\'ll get some better pictures tonight and show You every part I got, and I just looked and I have [i:c12472bf45]all[/i:c12472bf45] the front end parts, the [i:c12472bf45]only[/i:c12472bf45] part I do not have is 1 nut for one of the wheels, but everything else is there, it\'s just not all in 1 piece.\r\nPics will be up tonight\r\nThanks\r\nCould You please take a pic of the mosfet MS so I could see it.'),(25287,'1a6a227962','Sorry Pimp, I didn\'t see it.  \r\nJust wanted to know if it got lost in da mail or not.  I had your back Pimp, especially the wif issue, I covered that angle too.  I knew you\'d get a kick outta that shit !\r\n\r\nPimp On   :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26150,'25d81160d6','Hey Pimp,\r\n\r\nIf you need any modding tips, Just PM me, I\'ll be more than happy to help you out !   :cool:'),(36384,'06b2ef625f','Too cool! Thanks man, hope this ain\'t askin\' for too much, but is the xmod subaru still on sale/ available? Thanks!'),(36385,'381e0ef7f6','I\'ll check while I\'m there if they have any. :-o'),(29005,'0f36a5af7f','Hello BioHazard I an CJ from CJ\'s Hobbies and would like to know if you would let me stock those molded engines on my site.  Let me know what you can do for pricing.'),(28184,'e7025b88d0','OK lets do it, but at a total of $50  I don\'t think it\'s worth more.'),(37042,'c619e9d135','No dude. Their monitoring our web usage at work now, so I gotta stay on the down low. I\'m fixing my home connectivity, and I\'ll get some pics to you of my Trueno sets. You still have dibs.'),(28913,'ef0ae6a322','[quote:ef0ae6a322=\"betula66\"]If you have a problem,just tell me:\r\ne.g. if you don wanna send them to me or you don wanna tell me your bank acoount number,I understand you.\r\nBut those cars would be important 2 me,and I thought we could arrange it in 2 days. \r\n\r\nI\'d send you the money if I had your number(and the price),but I cant.\r\n\r\nSo how about it?[/quote:ef0ae6a322]\r\n\r\nYa know I was trying to do something nice and get you these but I work full time so it does take me a little time I did not get you a price Sunday becuse RS was closed like I said I went to a RS yesterday but they were out of the MT\'s I did not relize you were in such a hurry if you are maybe you should ask one of the other members they should be able to help you faster.\r\n\r\nsorry I could not get things to you fast enough Please contact another member and they will help you out!\r\nAaron\r\nsteelwoolghandi'),(27641,'c8d11b2c57','Edit:....blah, blah.....\r\n\r\nEdit #2.....It\'s 1am....blah...blah...\r\n\r\nI guess your hangin\' with Hog now. :???: \r\n\r\n :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26200,'96db71e420','[quote:96db71e420=\"DarkTari\"]Hi! I have a bunch of microsizers bodies sets NIB $2ea \r\n[b:96db71e420]Specifics ?[/b:96db71e420]\r\n\r\nPerfection Beetle bodies NIP $1ea \r\nPerfection Lambo or Ferrari bodies NIP $1ea \r\n[b:96db71e420]Cool ?[/b:96db71e420]\r\n\r\nNeed any sets? \r\n\r\nGot Perfection Lambo/Ferrari sets $10ea \r\n[b:96db71e420]Intrerrested! Colors? s/h?[/b:96db71e420]\r\n\r\nLxx Auto Modellista sets $10ea \r\nTomy BitCharG sets $15-$20 ea. \r\n\r\nAny interest in IWaver stuff? I\'ll be focusing more on Iwavers/ Mini z and selling the remainder of my New Micro RC stuff. \r\n[b:96db71e420]Is it too much trouble to send a detailed list of Micro RC stuff for sale?  Got any pics?[/b:96db71e420]\r\n\r\nLet me know if interested in anything. Happy Holidays!\r\n[b:96db71e420]Thanx Pimp!  Same to you ![/b:96db71e420][/quote:96db71e420]\r\n\r\n\r\nHere\'s a list of what I can remember off hand:\r\n\r\nmicrosizers body sets - supra, 350z, skyline, celica, I have a few other styles but its not coming to me at the moment. \r\n\r\nPerfection beetle bodies - colors - white, blue, green, black, gun metal, bronze, light green, silver, red, a few other colors but I know there were 11-12 different colors for the beetle bodies.\r\n\r\nPerfection lamborghini / Ferrari - red, white, black, silver\r\n\r\nThe Perfection Lambo/Ferrari sets comes with a different color lambo and ferrari body (either red, white, black, silver) \r\n\r\nAlso got Lxx VW Beetle sets with working headlights - $10ea. \r\n\r\nI might have a few 200mah batteries, 3.8 motors. \r\n\r\nFor the Tomy sets - silver s2000, black bB, Toyota Celica (not sure if its black or silver), Subaru WRX white, Nissan Gloria - $15ea ( i have more but cant remember)\r\n\r\nIm not sure on s&amp;h yet but if you decide to buy alot we can work something out. Did you need anything before xmas? Do you have an email address where I can send you some pics?\r\n\r\nThanks!'),(34503,'4ae96ceee9','[quote:4ae96ceee9=\"DarkTari\"]How much do you want for the Tomy Sets?  Shipping?\r\n\r\nIs that everything or do you have any Lxx sets left?\r\n\r\nI know someone looking for the WRX set\r\n\r\nLemme Know!\r\n\r\nThanx Again Pimp![/quote:4ae96ceee9]\r\n\r\n$15 each for the Tomy Sets.... Shipping for one set around $5 bucks priority mail with delivery confirmation. \r\n\r\nFor more sets etc... I gotta figure shipping depending on you what you would want etc... \r\n\r\nI may have a few Lxx sets left. I have the vw beetle sets with working lights. Also have the super perfection lambo/ferrari combo sets and maybe a few of the regular/auto modellista sets.\r\n\r\nThanks and let me know!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37547,'4185812979','FYI - I sent that Jeep body out this afternoon via regular mail I guess.  I\'m not too familiar with the services the Post office offers.  Should get to you in a couple days though.  Thanks.'),(37548,'47d9b4f3fa','FYI - I sent that Civic body out this afternoon via regular mail I guess.  I\'m not too familiar with the services the Post office offers.  Should get to you in a couple days though.  Thanks.'),(34507,'6826c2fe23','Soo, since you fly the mini choppers, could you tell me how to yaw?\r\n\r\nI spin slowly to one side. It starts sliding to the left, so i correct to the right, it then goes foreward. Thats when i loose it with coordination and crash... I thought ida had this down by now, but the fly times are rediculously low on the electric ones to get a decent amount of fly time in... I have a theory on my problem: I haven\'t been able to immagine myself [b:6826c2fe23]\'inside\'[/b:6826c2fe23] the copter, as they say is what you do when you are \"good\"...\r\n\r\nHere go the questions:\r\nDo you think walking around it while its hovering would help with my sense of direction?\r\n\r\nAbout you:\r\nDid you learn to fly with gas or electric? And, did you have an instuctor?'),(28350,'66cf4567e7','[quote:66cf4567e7]Yep, Lake Placid, NY, which is about an hour from Canada. I\'m going back up next week, so maybe I\'ll pick one up.[/quote:66cf4567e7]\r\n\r\n[b:66cf4567e7]Any Luck yet Pimp ?[/b:66cf4567e7]\r\n\r\n [img:66cf4567e7]http://www.senario.com/images/OffRoadImage.jpg[/img:66cf4567e7]\r\n\r\n[b:66cf4567e7]I keep look\'n at that pic and wanting a couple real bad now !!!!!![/b:66cf4567e7]  :innocent:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27056,'00fbe82859','Just tried to send you an email on the msn address, and got it sent back to me.\r\nAny chance you can email me to check?\r\nThings are happening.\r\nThanks,\r\nRoland (Microamps)'),(27057,'94e7f253bb','[quote:94e7f253bb=\"micro_Amps\"]Just tried to send you an email on the msn address, and got it sent back to me.\r\nAny chance you can email me to check?\r\nThings are happening.\r\nThanks,\r\nRoland (Microamps)[/quote:94e7f253bb]\r\nSure !'),(26209,'c6cb5de4a0','[quote:c6cb5de4a0=\"kvik369\"]ps - did you get the MT also ?\r\n\r\nvik[/quote:c6cb5de4a0]Yeah, I did, sorry, I thought I mentioned that. :-) \r\n\r\nDave'),(28555,'3ba9440c50','i have one, would u air brush my ipod for a trade? yes im serious. I only could get a pink one and it needs to be made over..'),(28557,'16ab797399','can you send me a picture of the i pod it and what color were you thinking of?'),(28559,'507a321f7a','hmm, black with blue flames or something?'),(28561,'3f403b66a1','can you take off the covers and ship them to me?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28566,'18e483877a','I was wondering what other zzse bodies you are selling??'),(28567,'18e483877a','I was wondering what other zzse bodies you are selling??'),(28390,'9d4024c3b0','Alright well I\'d really like to have a mosfet bit but I don\'t have 25 bucks at the moment, so can I just send You all the MT stuff I have and any other stuff You want, for a stock Panther or rally racer? I\'d give You my Hulk MT body but it had some ghetto work done to it, I over sprayed it with paint (kind of thick) and I took the arms off of it and filled in the gaps with putty and well I just didn\'t finish the project, but If You want I can strip it back down of all paint, and it\'d be clearish with putty here and there??? Whatever you want to do, I\'d just like to get rid of some of this stuff cuz I\'m sure fellow Bitpimps like You could use it and make it drivable again. Oh yeah the lights are still in tact on the Chevy body if You do want it.'),(28323,'11f1767e56','I am working on a cool truck body for the microsizers/clones and one for the ZZMT. It\'s a long process to make them, but I am working on it. What rims/ body were you looking at that you liked?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25694,'eca5e435a2','Just thought I\'d see if your still around somewhere and if you would respond.\r\n\r\n :-) \r\n\r\nStop in sometime over at BitPimps. :cool:'),(28311,'c1e9b942e0','sounds good to me , i\'ll take the whole deal the body and the car and tx . i can pay some time next week , this week my dad is to busy to go to the bank and mess with paypal . but $30  plus shipping is good , thanks i\'ll let you know when i can transfer the funds , later . \r\n\r\nmatt'),(27311,'e24463f978','I can help you with the Gloria and bB bodies. Check out www.toysnjoys.com. Shipping is a little steep since they\'re in Hawaii, but I don\'t know that you\'re going to find those on the mainland now. I\'ve never ordered from them, so I don\'t know if they\'re reliable.\r\n\r\nNow then, the AE86 pullback are even trickier. I have a source, but they are WAY overpriced. I could one or more for you, but it would be about $15 for one. Have to go overseas now for these. I wish Tomy would crank out some more, but it looks like they\'re out of the Bit bidness now.\r\n\r\nKeep an eye on eBay too. I\'ve seen AE86\'s popup now and then. Oh, another option would be to buy the Initial D set. You can get it pretty cheap here: www.toynk.com.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.'),(31806,'87875e0878','Hey 45tro,\r\n\r\nThis is what I came up with.  See how you like it.  Basically it\'s a Pimps intro to 1:64.  I have the Big Foot Zip Zap MT w/ controller, a busted up SE w/ battery and controller, a Hummer shell, SE shell, OG Zip shell, Mazda RX7 shell, Cat 5 wire, 3 pimps, front suspension kit, Hard tires, and Bit Pimps decales.  Don\'t have any \"spare\" MT parts but I hope this alternative is to your liking.  If there is shit you don\'t want or if you want more, please let me know, it won\'t hurt my feelings.  If you REALLy want a motor upgrade kit you can paypal me $15 US and I\'ll pick you up one brand new.\r\n\r\nHere is a pic\r\n[img:87875e0878]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v77/marjoke/Tradestuff.jpg[/img:87875e0878]\r\nLaters\r\nFinks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31699,'0414e87747','[quote:0414e87747=\"TeamBonzer\"]Hi\r\n\r\nNY toy fair is the biggest. Held in February each year at the Javits centre.\r\nNext year on 12-15th feb.\r\n\r\nHere is a link\r\nhttp://www.toy-tia.org/Content/NavigationMenu/TIA_Trade_Shows_and_Events/American_International_TOY_FAIR/American_International_TOY_FAIR1.htm\r\n\r\nIf you want to go you will have to get a free ticket. Need to prove that you are a toy company or shop or agent - just lie! (but you will need a business card - photoshop!)\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTB[/quote:0414e87747]\r\n\r\nSo they have all the big brands?  I\'ll ask around if the hobby shops mind if I go in their name, then I\'ll resort to photoshop.'),(29747,'f4187e7b3a','Yes, that would be great!\r\n\r\nHere\'s an address:\r\nDavid Knaack\r\n850 Amelia Ave\r\nElkhorn NE 68022\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\nDave'),(27910,'607c15a5b9','the goods have arrived.......... :-)'),(37937,'cf645525e5','Did you send the stuff yet? Just want to make sure, so I can keep an eye out for it.........');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27072,'67e497232a','[quote:67e497232a=\"midget_man1387\"]aww shiat..... I wanna... But I gotta spend some money on the girl for her 16th... So I\'ll try and spend as little as possible!! I\'ll hit you up after the 27th. Thanks!\r\n\r\n~midget[/quote:67e497232a]Alrighty then. I didn\'t know if you were really asking or just joking, so I figured I\'d just go ahead and give you the low down. :-) \r\n\r\nDave'),(25783,'db452252b9','[quote:db452252b9=\"viperdout\"]Dave:\r\n\r\nIs it done?\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:db452252b9]Hey, what\'s up?\r\n\r\nYeah it\'s done, but no I didn\'t get it out. Damn rain again, it rained all day. It\'s crazy cause it never rains here, and it\'s rained every weekend for 4 weeks now! :shock: \r\n\r\nI\'m gonna try to get it out tomorrow.\r\n\r\nI\'ll find out what next day cost.\r\n\r\ndave'),(25785,'fd869ef55e','can you please put fets on my zz se'),(25786,'cb26d35389','[quote:cb26d35389=\"Bigg\"]can you please put fets on my zz se[/quote:cb26d35389]Ok, I just got FETs in today. \r\n\r\nI charge $10+ return shipping. You can paypla me at davesmoejoe@yahoo.com, or send a money order with the car.\r\n\r\nMy address:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd. #1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\nDave'),(27942,'177922ea83','[quote:177922ea83=\"viperdout\"][quote:177922ea83=\"sg219\"]If you decide to part it out....\r\n\r\nI want first dibs on the Mamba....\r\n\r\nI\'ll take the Mamba from you for $85 shipped? Let me know if thats reasonable for a used Mamba.  If not, we\'ll talk it over.  n/p\r\n\r\nThen maybe the chassis a couple of weeks later.  (the following Payday. :) )[/quote:177922ea83]\r\n\r\nSG:\r\n\r\nSorry, someone already beat you to first dibs (actually 2 people have IMed me about the Mamba), so I\'m sorry to tell you you\'re out of luck.  To make things worse for your cause, I\'ve already gotten an offer on the thing, so it looks like it won\'t be parted out either.  I wish you luck on your quest, and if you need to go new, www.b-p-p.com has Mambas for 110, which isn\'t half bad.  I gather it\'s going into your T, so that\'ll be badass.  Sorry to be the bearer...\r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:177922ea83]\r\n\r\nNot a problem at all.  Just lookin\' out to score a deal. :-) \r\n\r\nThanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31708,'fc3abd56b0','Cool beans man.... DT does have some deep pockets...lol   I just can\'t compete with that, but he was first like the fast ass he is....lol\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll have to be a bit faster next time.     Maybe he will just forget about the whole PM thing....lol\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWish I knew some Jedi mind shit... :-D \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(31709,'16963ab6de','Hey, what\'s up.\r\n\r\nFinally got that review posted. Took me a bit, because I wanted to add some video and stuff, but I think it came out really well. I\'m happy with it.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=75262#75262\r\n\r\nDave'),(28578,'bcd52b66ef','Change in shipping address:\r\n\r\nDonna Murray\r\nc/o Helene Hershan\r\n33 Owatonna NJ\r\n07641\r\n\r\nI\'ll let donna know the details of what\'s in the package  :-)'),(25825,'1c982fdaf7','Could you shrink the sig a little.  It\'s a little big.  Like maybe half the size it is now.  Just the big pic.\r\n\r\nThanks, \r\n\r\n\r\nSG219'),(36386,'3473e2e23e','cool.....thanx! :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27535,'f901da9376','mikirgra and I found this site:\r\nhttp://anytoys.co.uk/category_info.php/category_id/57\r\n\r\nI had my reservations about taking it public before getting what I needed, but I ordered my Trueno pullback(is that pronounced \'true-eh-no\'?) from there and since it\'s fucking expensive, I\'m not ordering anymore shit from them.  They don\'t have anymore Trueno pullbacks after what he and I got from them.\r\n\r\nClean \'em out if ya like, but you gotta have DEEP pockets to do it.  I guess it would help to have a British relative that can send it to you. :???: \r\n\r\nIn the meantime, I\'ll keep my eyes on toyeast for parts and toyrus for a kit I\'m gonna get a friend of mine for his 21st b-day.  I\'d like to see more clone cars if Tomy is discontinuing everything, since there\'s still huge demand for it.\r\n\r\nHit me back,\r\nAbe'),(25830,'63459843a0','that better? or smaller?'),(25829,'43f655ccec','will do :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25831,'900c3f9112','[quote:900c3f9112=\"crusty\"]that better? or smaller?[/quote:900c3f9112]\r\n\r\n\r\nA little smaller would be cool.  About 150 pixels tall or so.   For a reference, the avatars on BP are 80x80 pixels.\r\n\r\nIt just helps to make the threads neater.   Look at Hogs sig, its about the biggest thats cool.\r\n\r\nThanks.'),(27328,'bf2d37a5e9','Thanks, and Respeck Nuckles!  The list was a mix of bodies and pullbacks.  Hobbyonsale has some to most  of them, but the really hard shit to find is that Spinter pullback, or even just a spinter body from the AE86 or Initial D kits.  I should\'ve gotten it back in 2003, when TE still had some.  If I ever find out how to make injecion molded copies of bidies, ha ha!  I\'ll have one, for free! (I know better than to try to sell something like that- copyright infringement, which is a no no.)\r\nThe reason why I wanted to find a shop that had everything is to try and fight the shipping costs that were going to get out of hand, no doubt it.  Luckily, most is still out there, so I can finish my collection.  Anyway, thanks fot the info, it\'ll help out a shitload!\r\n\r\nLate,\r\nAbe'),(37636,'ae6a0dc832','Well then I\'ll just take the iW board. \r\n\r\nYou wouldn\'t happen to have any MRS4 stuff you\'d like to get rid of, maybe some electronics or alloy? (I already have a TX)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37637,'f28c62a9cf','[quote:f28c62a9cf=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Well then I\'ll just take the iW board. \r\n\r\nYou wouldn\'t happen to have any MRS4 stuff you\'d like to get rid of, maybe some electronics or alloy? (I already have a TX)[/quote:f28c62a9cf]\r\n\r\nDamn you sure? Arrgh i was hoping to get rid of them both.\r\n\r\nNah i dont have a MRS4 mate.'),(37641,'3b5cebe04e','[quote:3b5cebe04e=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I would like it, but I don\'t want to buy a charger etc. I\'ll buy that stuff when I\'m shopping for batts.\r\n\r\nI only wanted it cuz I had the cheapo charger doing nothing. Plus I\'d need a board harness.\r\n\r\nSo just the board. I\'ll send you $13, shipping for phatboi was under a buck. That cool? \r\n\r\nHey, you got any Xmod stuff? Since I last asked?\r\n\r\nMaxx[/quote:3b5cebe04e]\r\n\r\nYeah sounds like a deal man!\r\n\r\nNah dont have much xmod stuff since last time, only thing i have thats noticebly cool is some blue alloy xmod rims from betty K. Beat up around the edges. They use mini-z tires.'),(25834,'7fde1839af','aright.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25835,'b6682b3ed7','Much better. :cool: \r\n\r\nJust right.'),(37756,'e8268b48fb','I\'m gonna have to go with a yes on that..... :-o I\'ll send it out tomorrow.....thanks man!\r\n\r\n\r\nJustin Long\r\n3 Crockett Rd.\r\nRaymond Maine 04071'),(28138,'ab60eafec9','Cracka...ass, cracka'),(25838,'5298133cc9','yeah its like 179 by 60 sumthing'),(25839,'49cdc139cc','Thats fine.   :cool:'),(28195,'efd7cba5a7','[quote:efd7cba5a7=\"stampede_dude\"]i dont know if you meant  it to be this way or not, but on the moderators poster, you spelled \'customized\' wrong. i am sorry if you meant it to be this way, but i just wanted to point this out until someone else found out.[/quote:efd7cba5a7]Doh!\r\nGood catch holmes, that ain\'t supposed to be there. lol\r\n\r\nThanks dude.'),(37803,'cfa9ac19e2','Sorry If I offended ya dude....no need to get nuts about it...I was just tryna give away some freeness.'),(36667,'ca2a7ddb5f','[quote:ca2a7ddb5f=\"stampede_dude\"]You said you had a front steering problem, and I need a rear clip to fit a gen1 body on the evo chassis, and since you don\'t have any gen1 bodies and I have an extra evo chassis with the parts you would need, would you be willing to trade? I most likely have the part you need, just let me know, and if worst comes to worst We could work out a deal for the whole front end. Thanks![/quote:ca2a7ddb5f]\r\n\r\nTrade what ?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36872,'70a111430c','I cleaned up an old post yesterday.  I feel Da Hookup will have a lot of outdated/no good posts cause it\'s all about a bargain, for a limited time, so after that the post is no good.  Is there any quick way to delete the entire post and all responses?\r\n\r\nI did one from sg219 about a TRU clerance last year (which is no good now) and had to individually delete every post.  Or do we want  a place like an archive dumpster where we can move old, outdated post to?\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp!'),(37040,'0ca642ed80','yes'),(36874,'d44cd142d8','[quote:d44cd142d8=\"pimpsmurf\"]So far I\'ve found the road radials with the kyosho hard foams, some titanium screws and stock diff parts, the gpm front gearbox, and the radio of course. damn. I screwed up a little man. These will be out ASAP.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:d44cd142d8]\r\n\r\n\r\nHey man i got your package today, wow do i have a night ahead of me lol.\r\n\r\ncouple things off the bat though, theres no MZM board in here? And the lipo protecter you talked about is nowhere to be found?\r\n\r\nHave you gotten a chance to ship out the front gearbox and radio etc. yet?'),(34365,'67148b4d37','[quote:67148b4d37=\"TeamBonzer\"]Try here http://www.sleepy-fish.com/Sagaris.htm\r\n\r\nand here\r\n\r\nhttp://www.racinggreentvr.com/models/sagaris.asp\r\n\r\nand here\r\n\r\nhttp://www.tvr-eng.co.uk/intro.html#tamext3\r\n\r\nGood luck :lol:[/quote:67148b4d37]\r\nThanx Bonzo !  8-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (25849,'3f88c2ae38','[quote:3f88c2ae38=\"Bit boy\"]Just wondering cause there was a guy on ThumperTalk.com from Oz that had the same avatar as you for a while.[/quote:3f88c2ae38]\r\n\r\nnah, not me mate.'),(33246,'25e32f5048','I need your current home addy for a special surprise.\r\n\r\nI need to get it out by Mon or Tues, so please hurry. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMike :cool:'),(25959,'4a0f084eb6','Hey, almost forgot about that poster, so before I forget again:\r\n\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd. #1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\n...and thanks. :-)'),(27296,'d31e25d56d','That other thread has links to examples of how betty.k doesn\'t need to pull that shit.  She/he didn\'t before, and there\'s proof of that on that thread.  Anyhow, thanks for the assist on that one.\r\n\r\nRespek Nuckles for the G,\r\nAbe\r\n\r\nP.S. kickass custom bits...'),(36286,'7b34136ac4','So, I won somethin eh? I figured they\'d like the Ferrari more than the mini.....but hey it\'s a mystery that I even placed with all the sick ass shit the pimps brought forth...\r\n\r\n\r\nJustin Long\r\n3 Crockett Rd\r\nRaymond ME 04071\r\n\r\n\r\nThanx SG!!!!! :-o'),(27551,'b0d6e240a9','Hi, Charger is a stand alone one &amp; a display case !!. Takes about 30 mins to charge fully. The speed is truly proportional doesn\'t seem to go in steps. As regards getting hold of one, they aren\'t avaliable yet. I was lucky &amp; got some preproduction samples and have been providing a bit of feedback to Ken at XXAPS. I know when launche alot more body styles will be avaliable &amp; I\'m hoping they produce a better controller for us racing types. I think if hey get this righ hey will be the next big thing ! :eek:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29156,'bede2ec3e4','Hey, I have a pair of AA li-ions I\'d like to donate to you guys.  Normal deal, 750mah, 3.6V.  Please send me an address where I can send these to so they can be used in a future contest.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(29157,'9bf9234875','[quote:9bf9234875=\"Mazda787b\"]Hey, I have a pair of AA li-ions I\'d like to donate to you guys.  Normal deal, 750mah, 3.6V.  Please send me an address where I can send these to so they can be used in a future contest.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMazda[/quote:9bf9234875]Cool man, thanks for donating!\r\nYou can send it to:\r\n\r\nIconMedialab\r\nATTN: Scott Lix\r\n700 Goddard Avenue\r\nSt. Louis, MO 63005\r\n\r\nWhen it comes time to use them as a prize, we\'ll make sure we let the pimps know you donated them. (remind us if we should forget, hopefully we won\'t though)\r\n\r\nThanks again holmes, that\'s a cool move.'),(32291,'97ffcf4b0d','[quote:97ffcf4b0d=\"hue35\"]=\r\n\r\nThe cream color sounds good, but I would like to swap out one color... I\'d like the pea green instead of the yellow. So, the final mini cooper list will be...\r\n\r\nred fire chief \r\nwhite/green police car \r\noff white/cream\r\npale yellow \r\npea green \r\nmint green \r\nblack \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nhue35[/quote:97ffcf4b0d]\r\n\r\n\r\nCool! No problem, I will switch the other one for you too. Will ship em all out to you tomorrow. \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJDM'),(27932,'c39892a02d','I don\'t want money, man... I just want to see them modded out nicely...\r\n\r\nAlls I need is your shipping info...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28964,'84b94f0950','thanks for the help there cabo  :rockon:'),(34330,'03d6753b80','Hey Wussup!\r\n\r\nSorry I didnt reply sooner, I still got a bunch of Microsizer bodies and Perfection bodies. Let me know if youre looking for something in particular. Thanks!\r\n\r\nJDM'),(34331,'da87e37977','[quote:da87e37977=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hey Wussup!\r\n\r\nSorry I didnt reply sooner, I still got a bunch of Microsizer bodies and Perfection bodies. Let me know if youre looking for something in particular. Thanks!\r\n\r\nJDM[/quote:da87e37977]\r\nCool  :cool: \r\n\r\nThanx!'),(26428,'751411a959','Dear Midget Pimp,   lol\r\n\r\nI checked my schedule for the rest of the week and its going to be tough for me to make it to the Post Office this week.\r\n\r\nHowever, I will get it out to you ASAP Monday.\r\n\r\nJust wanted to let you know whats up.  \r\n\r\nThanks again.\r\n\r\n\r\nMike :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\nP.S.  You never said wether you want a Jeep or a Hummer? :?:'),(34363,'0afb964c3d','[quote:0afb964c3d=\"DarkTari\"][quote:0afb964c3d=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hey Wussup!\r\n\r\nSorry I didnt reply sooner, I still got a bunch of Microsizer bodies and Perfection bodies. Let me know if youre looking for something in particular. Thanks!\r\n\r\nJDM[/quote:0afb964c3d]\r\n\r\nLooking for :\r\n\r\n[b:0afb964c3d]3 - Lambo Bodies\r\n3 - Ferrari Bodies[/b:0afb964c3d]\r\n\r\n\r\nand if you still got \'em:\r\nTomy [b:0afb964c3d]Gloria, WRX[/b:0afb964c3d]\r\nPerfection [b:0afb964c3d]VW[/b:0afb964c3d]\r\n\r\nAlso looking for a New Tomy Fairlady (lost mine)\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp![/quote:0afb964c3d]\r\n\r\n\r\nCool! I\'ll check to make sure I have them and will get back to you sometimes this weekend! Thanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34369,'4a313085ad','[quote:4a313085ad=\"pimptothemax\"]what betty said would work fine, or, if i understand your question, you could apply sodder to the wire near the plastic, if you need to, or just wrap electrical tape around it.[/quote:4a313085ad]\r\n\r\nDude, nice job stayin\' away for awhile, but you were supposed to come back NOT a dipshit. Look, fuckwit... quit bringin\' back old-ass threads, only to add your useless 2 cents... I ain\'t havin\' it.\r\n\r\nThat thread is a year and a half old, and the dude asking the question hasn\'t posted anything in clean over a year... what the fuck are you thinking? QUIT CLUTTERING THE SITE WITH USELESS SHIT, BITCH!!! \r\n\r\nIf you can\'t participate in an acceptable fashion, you will simply be banned... got it?'),(26076,'c57011861b','I need to talk to you on AIM.'),(36843,'039b4b5867','[quote:039b4b5867=\"LBRC\"]What do you think?  \r\n\r\nSaw that the package was finally delivered yesterday and have discovered that I am more than a little anxious to know what you think of the 3 ZZMT motors in it (1 Yellow, 2 Orange).\r\n\r\nThey are my overall favorite motor option for my track, 18 x 10 feet w/ 2 foot lanes, unfortunately because the motors have to sit so close to the diff side ball bearing I couldnt seem to get one right milling it out of heavier stock and had to settle for the thin C stock with the aluminum axle and bearing tube.  Takes too long to make :-? .\r\n\r\nSo this kid says to me my brother put a ZZMT motor in an Epoch and its much faster so pompous ass that I am I show him a photo of an epoch motor beside a ZZMT motor and say its too small sonny go away. Well I was wrong, definitely big time wrong, ouch.\r\n\r\nI still doubt he even had a brother yet alone one who managed to fit ZZMT motor in an epoch motor case, not easy to do I tried it makes a mess, but he definitely was right about the motor, even one is technically faster just slow to get up to speed, and two LoL you get to decide that. \r\n\r\nI usually end up adding a little weight to the rear of the car for better traction and handling.[/quote:039b4b5867]\r\n\r\nHey man yup did get the package yesterday and my wife did not tell me until late (she forgot and let me know about 11:00 pm) I jumped up and went into my toy room and I swore the light was beaming from heaven on the box!!! (Guess it was the florescent light on the white box but still a neat effect)! \r\n\r\nThe car is Friggen HOT1 the first thing I did was oooh and ahhh over the bodies (they are really nice) then pulled out the Epoch and charged it up pulled it off the second charge and bang nothing happened?? LOL then I saw the plug was loose at the top plugged it in and put it on my pine floor and it screamed across the floor! \r\n\r\nThis Epoch is wicked fast its just too much for the house I plan to take it out this weekend to a track and try it where I have some real room! I cant tell you how happy this car has gotten me I havent been this excited since I bought my first Epoch. \r\n\r\nI will take your advice and bring something to weight the back end when I get the thing up to some speed at the track I will see if I have to add weight. \r\n\r\nThat motor setup is sweet I can see how it would be more to manufacture I am impressed it looks factory made vary nice set up! \r\n\r\nOk the bodies they are vary nice I like the detail the muscle cars made my mouth drool! \r\n\r\nI need some info before I paint them? You said you wanted one of them painted some way which one and how do you want it painted? \r\n\r\nHow do you want the lights and windows done? Are you going to add decals for the lights and such or do you want me to paint them in? The windows on the epochs are a gray color do you want them left clear or tinted? Just let me know some of the details and I will start on them ASAP!\r\n\r\nThanks again I plan to write a review and post it here and Rippers!\r\n\r\nAaron   :-)'),(26101,'8c3fdf2230','Thanx for the quick reply. I understand the whole car situation. I\'ll check ph2t about the nelly. Would I eventually be able to run more than 2 cells with the nelly?\r\n\r\nThanx,I\'ll go with the nelly then.\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27303,'bc12310537','I\'m pushin for global mod now. :lol: \r\n\r\nI think I\'ll get it.\r\n\r\nYou like the letter.  It was an Email I sent.  I never thought in a million years it would have ended up in there.  \r\n\r\nThats actually how I started talking to that David Baker dude.  He just emailed me the other day about something he wants to do.'),(37686,'bb57955192','[quote:bb57955192=\"Tuner1989\"]Your package was shipped today give it the usual 1-2 weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:bb57955192]Thank you'),(37687,'be83880bc2','[quote:be83880bc2=\"Maxximum Attack\"][quote:be83880bc2=\"Tuner1989\"]Your package was shipped today give it the usual 1-2 weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:be83880bc2]Thank you[/quote:be83880bc2]\r\n\r\n\r\nNo problem man let me know when you get it. :-o'),(37715,'60dfcdbbb5','Yeah, I just got it.  Thank you.  Sorry its taking me so long, Ive had trouble finding a box and getting it to the post office.  My dad is mailing it tomorrow.'),(37716,'7887c80f44','Hey don\'t worry about it.  I\'m not in a big rush as long as I get it.\r\n\r\nThanks.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37717,'f6a2671cfe','Hey man I haven\'t received anything on these.  Are you still interested?  Have you sent a MO?  If so, let me know and I\'ll look out extra hard for it.  If not but you still want the bods, let me know your address and I\'ll send one over to you.  I think I\'m gonna keep the other, but the one I send you can have for free.  Don\'t expect me to use anything but regular mail though.  lol.  But if you already sent a MO, I\'ll send you both.'),(37180,'0be367eaf2','excellent.\r\nI\'ll paypal you the total of $37.11 today or tomorrorw.\r\nclintoteri@yahoo.com\r\n\r\n[quote:0be367eaf2=\"cj\"]Hello Clint\r\n\r\nHere is what I got you down for:\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver \r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET	$7.74	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET	$0.00	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET 	$15.54	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET 	$7.74	1\r\n\r\nSub	$34.11	\r\nS&amp;H 	$3.00	\r\nTotal	$37.11	\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.59 off of GPM\'s regular\r\nprice.\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me now as\r\nsoon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com. \r\nPlease include your user name in the notes on PayPal.	\r\n\r\n\r\nThank You\r\nCJ\r\n\r\nBTW your email address on here didn\'t work.[/quote:0be367eaf2]'),(26174,'88b30a990a','[quote:88b30a990a=\"kvik369\"]thanks for the update -\r\n\r\nGlad you found a PS2.  Was going to see if you wanted me to get one for you cause I see them all the time.  (PA, NY, NJ)  \r\n\r\nyeah the 04 is my xmas present too. -  I agree with what you said.  I\'m waiting on Nelly as we speak.  Hopefully I won\'t break too many parts but I\'m already looking at MiniZracer.com for parts ( I EXPECT something to break).  I\'m probably not going to bash it too much.  I wanted something that would ride on gravel and not spend too much or get something too big -  my the driveway is gravel.  So far so good.  But not too much time to mess with it right now.  Plus the snow is starting.  The body sucks.  You can rip it with your hands, but it should be easy to mod something to fit.  So far no electronic problems aside from figuring out how the adjustments work on the controller.  After hearing some of the other guys with a few problems,  there will probably be some Gen 1 problems but keep you fingers crossed.  Well anyways, so far its great for me.\r\n\r\nVik[/quote:88b30a990a]WEll damn, I typed a reply and my computer froze when I hit submit. Now I\'m out of time so here\'s the abbreviated version:\r\n\r\nYour situation is the same as mine, I\'m already shopping for parts because I expect it break. I don\'t plan on romping it too hard, just the gravel out front, and if I get into a header with a tree, I expect it to break, that\'s true of a RC monster truck in any scale, so I\'ll try to avoid doing that, and if I do, I\'ll get a shiny new part to replace it. \r\n\r\nNot too worried about the body, I was planning to get an Overland body, but they\'re expensive, probably wait for TE to get they\'re Overland copies in.\r\n\r\nSo I think I\'ll be happy, thnaks for the info. :-) \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26178,'7caf0b4b7d','Yes thanx I guess 6 will do. They\'re only going to be 5 xmods here so, what are the odds? right. If you know the stock frequencies just hope #6 isn\'t in the list below.\r\n\r\nBlack Civic       ??\r\nBlack Skyline   #1\r\n350Z               #5\r\nCorvette          ??\r\n\r\nAny aside from those will do. Thanx\r\nMaxx'),(37186,'1aa594a3e6','[quote:1aa594a3e6=\"LBRC\"]Just curious, hows the Epoch doing?  Any problems?  What would you change? That sort of thing.\r\n\r\nCheers\r\nPhilip.[/quote:1aa594a3e6]\r\n\r\nHey man Sorry I did not reply right away! \r\n\r\nI really like this car I have been having a lot of fun with it, I almost beat my nephew\'s X-mod he had upgraded it to a 6 cell and its fast but the Epoch was right there with it the whole way.\r\n\r\nThe big thing is you were right you have to weigh down the back we actualy took the cars to a nice skatboard park all concreat and lots of places to run the cars in fact a cool straitaway. The Epoch outferfomed the X-Mod hands down but for all out speed he had me. But for me I would rather have better handling then speed. You could have the fastest RC car in the world but if you cant turn it all you have is a fast drag car!\r\n\r\nThe stearing motor is much better then the standard Epoch motor more responsive. I think this car is a blast and have had a great time with it. I personly would not change a thing (well except the weight issue). I think putting a spring between the motor section and chassis would help keep the back a little tighter and I might not have to add any weight? the problem I am having is the back bounces to much it causes the back wheels to hit the wheel wells. I might try something to see if I can get it to work I will let you know! \r\n\r\n thanks again man!!  :-)'),(26657,'983061ebcb','hi man. sorry, i\'m not doing these conversions any more. too much work involved and i\'m lazy! just read through my tutorials and take it 1 step at a time, it looks harder than it really is.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27536,'77d4fac6a5','[quote:77d4fac6a5=\"seeberg\"]mikirgra and I found this site:\r\nhttp://anytoys.co.uk/category_info.php/category_id/57\r\n\r\nI had my reservations about taking it public before getting what I needed, but I ordered my Trueno pullback(is that pronounced \'true-eh-no\'?) from there and since it\'s fucking expensive, I\'m not ordering anymore shit from them.  They don\'t have anymore Trueno pullbacks after what he and I got from them.\r\n\r\nClean \'em out if ya like, but you gotta have DEEP pockets to do it.  I guess it would help to have a British relative that can send it to you. :???: \r\n\r\nIn the meantime, I\'ll keep my eyes on toyeast for parts and toyrus for a kit I\'m gonna get a friend of mine for his 21st b-day.  I\'d like to see more clone cars if Tomy is discontinuing everything, since there\'s still huge demand for it.\r\n\r\nHit me back,\r\nAbe[/quote:77d4fac6a5]\r\n\r\n[b:77d4fac6a5]Stock Up Pimp ![/b:77d4fac6a5]\r\n[img:77d4fac6a5]http://www2.gpmd.com/image/h/hcac1105.jpg[/img:77d4fac6a5]\r\n\r\nhttp://www2.towerhobbies.com/cgi-bin/wti0001p?&amp;I=LXCFC7&amp;P=7'),(32373,'dda418b4be','thanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32374,'0bc7cd2a4f','Thanks man, ill send those bodies out on monday\r\n\r\nSTG'),(27030,'733f104739','[quote:733f104739]i\'ll be going back either sun or mon. will grab one for you if there are any left. if they have both, which one do you want?[/quote:733f104739]\r\nHey Rich,\r\nWould you mind pick\'n up some of those for me?  I got 1 more Target in\r\nmy area to check out then I\'ll letcha know.  If you need an immediate answer, pick me up 5 of them in any order.\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp and good look\'n out  :cool:'),(34144,'602278e713','Finks\r\nJesse King\r\n163 Main St\r\nFt Fairfield, ME 04742\r\n\r\nThanks again Ghandi!'),(32488,'896b6347e0','[quote:896b6347e0=\"Finks\"]Got the package today :eek:   Damn the grin on my face when I saw those batteries!  All the goodies man, you really are a class muther fuckin act.  Thanks SWG for the great trade.  (I\'ll be giving props in the under the bus thread tomorrow after I send out the German deal)[/quote:896b6347e0]\r\n\r\nJust glad you liked it bud great deal just wish I had sent it out sooner but work is keeping me vary busy in fact dont have the time to finish my projects (especially my Ferrari project!) anyway hope you can use all the stuff! The extras were a big thanks for dealing with the German buy! If the extras come in let me know and I will Paypal you with some money for freight!\r\n\r\nThanks again have a great rest of the week!  :grin: \r\n\r\nOh did you get the Star Wars DVD I had to send it separate?  \r\n\r\nAaron\r\nSWG'),(27887,'0910d679cf','I just sent the wheel locks at noontime, so keep an eye out for em. Thanks for the Jota lid....');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27889,'04158877c2','cool thanks , have fun with the jota shell when ya get it . :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nmatt'),(27890,'04158877c2','cool thanks , have fun with the jota shell when ya get it . :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nmatt'),(31791,'0276f208f7','Well you\'re lucky , I went in to town to post it today and the post office i went to had closed down . So i\'ll have to go somewhere else and i was planning to go later on .\r\n\r\nDo you have any information as to why you cant send it ?\r\nI am willing to wait.'),(27229,'348a2a59a8','Are you gonna be up later?  I skipped bowling tonight, my back was hurtin\'. \r\n\r\nI\'m gonna crash for an hour or two, give me a call if your down tonight for a bit.  About 9pm or so.\r\n\r\nI wanna drive this Bandit I got from Payaso and you got the batteries and the charger. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nDid you get the new Driver yet?   :???:'),(27140,'6d9b3e11f6','the mechanical part of the steering is still the same, when i turn the controller left the wheels turn left and stay turned until i return the steering wheel to center. the steering is basically non propo.'),(30946,'b5f12e174d','Yep, got \'em.  Thanks!  Looks like I\'ll be able to reproduce them both, but unfortunately I\'m on the road for work for a couple of weeks, so I won\'t have a chance to actually do anything but design work until probably july 8th or so.\r\n\r\nThanks again, when I get the prototypes done I\'ll post some pics and send you a set to test.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33093,'46ece30146','Dude!  Thanks a ton for all the wicked fuckin cool shwag!  Honestly, what a freakin blessing dude.  I so appreciate it.  The Skyline pullback, and the Evo Sport addition, oh and the Nacumichighdlhgleesl Wanted all of those for so long.  Now that I have two UPSes, I can mod one out too, oh what to do what to do?  The motors too, jeeze dude, this was so perfect.  What you sent me was 100x better than a couple of extra bucks, I can\'t say it enough, perfect.  MUCH respect and thanks\r\n :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o \r\nFinks'),(32120,'200a17c1fd','[quote:200a17c1fd=\"Finks\"]Sent you the $$$$ a second ago, thanks again.[/quote:200a17c1fd]\r\n\r\nHey man will get you your stuff sent out ASAP! thanks a bunch!\r\n\r\nAaron'),(32122,'64ff35870d','Hey man, if you\'ve got, or can take a higher-resolution, side-view shot of your car with something simple in the background, I could do a way better job (and would like to, I love that car!)... maybe even with you drivin\'.:???:  \r\n\r\nThe higher the resolution, the better... like, more than 1000 pixels wide. 2000 pixels wide would be great... saved as a high-quality jpeg.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(26775,'1a4cde8b6f','I sent out the ride a little bit ago.  \r\n\r\nI included the decals, but they SUCK!!!\r\nMy printer ran out of RED ink and everything that was supposed to be red, came out yellow.  Plus a little blurry.  I figured I\'d send them anyway and let you check them out and use them to tag shit at school or something.\r\n\r\nWhen I get some new ink, I\'ll print out some more for you.  just throw them in the trash unless you can find a use for them.\r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34056,'8a96c1ad1e','[quote:8a96c1ad1e=\"Clint\"]One was lucite and the other was lexan.\r\nI bought the sheets at home depot for a couple bucks.\r\n[quote:8a96c1ad1e=\"Tuner1989\"]Btw what are the chassis\'s you made, made out of?\r\n\r\nAnd thanks again man!\r\n\r\nYour zzmt is looking relly good too nice work!\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:8a96c1ad1e][/quote:8a96c1ad1e]\r\n\r\nCool man thanks for the favor! :-) \r\n\r\nYou got my pm with my address right?\r\n\r\nThanks clint this is a big help!\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37802,'c80367f92b','Spamming shit (meaning putting up a link to something you\'re pushing/selling) aint cool round here. Maybe if you\'ve been here for awhile we\'ld be cool with you promoting your music but putting up a pic and a link to your shit on your first post aint gonna fly. If you don\'t understand I can elaborate. :-)'),(37804,'cfa9ac19e2','Sorry If I offended ya dude....no need to get nuts about it...I was just tryna give away some freeness.'),(27977,'73bdd17ce0','I\'ll give you a little/full background story first.\r\n\r\nA couple of months ago I was over Bird\'s chillin\' and he showed me his copy of RC Driver, it had an article with Jerome Bettis in it.  \r\n\r\nI then became a little pissed off that I\'m a subscriber and haven\'t recieved it yet, so I wrote RC Driver an email stating my thoughts.\r\n\r\n(They ended up publishing it 1 or 2 issues later.  I didn\'t know till I got mine in the mail.)\r\n\r\nI then got a reply from the Associate Editor, David Baker.  I went back and forth with a couple of emails and then hooked up on AIM to BS a little.  It turns out that he is originally from the Pittsburgh area.  (Washington, Pa)\r\n\r\nSo I ended up talking to him a couple more times.  I told him I used to work at Kennywood Park (local amusement park), and I still have a few connections there.  So now I\'m tenitively working with him on having an RC Expo at the park this summer, similar to the one they had at the Indy 500, this past summer.\r\n\r\nIt also turns out he lives around the DC area.  Laurel, Maryland.\r\n\r\nSo now this is how it ties into you and BP.\r\n\r\nA while back when I was talking to him, he asked me if I was into Nitros, I  didn\'t have any at the time.  This last conversation lead to me telling him I went nitro since the last time we spoke.  I shared the link to my Nitro thread on BP.  He checked it out and asked about the site.  I told him it was devoted to \"The baddest Micro RC\'s on the Planet\", &lt;&lt;&lt;quote. Along with other sections for members to discuss things. \r\n\r\nI asked him about his thoughts on 1:64th and 1:2? scales.  He asked what kind of mods can be done to 1:64th, they\'re so small.  I then [b:73bdd17ce0]told[/b:73bdd17ce0] him what kind and [b:73bdd17ce0]then showed[/b:73bdd17ce0] him yours!!!  I think you are by far the best body man on BP with alot of other that are damn good too.  \r\n\r\nI went on to tell him to check out the site.  He asked if I could pass along his contact info to you, to possibly discuss something for the magazine.\r\n\r\nBP promotion and DT in the spotlight.  I\'m going to copy and paste this PM to Cabo so he knows the story too.  (also so I don\'t have to type it again)  \r\n\r\nI\'m not sure what will come out of this, but it is definately a big step in getting the word out about micro\'s.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPimpin\' shit to some good people, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike\r\n\r\n\r\nP.S.  BTW....I also showed off Rippers Mag and his work with his TLT.  Awsome stuff happening.\r\n\r\n\r\nHis info....\r\n\r\nDavid Baker\r\nAssociate Editor\r\nRC Driver Magazine\r\n\r\n410-552-9050\r\n\r\ndavidb@rcdriver.com');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31803,'9a8e177185','Ok thats a bummer man . :-( \r\n\r\n\r\nWell let me know when you know  :-)'),(26779,'7eec9015f8','[quote:7eec9015f8=\"honda_s2000\"]yo sg ,\r\nu mind if i hold a little longer, just to do some more research and/or post an add in lookin2score to see if i can get one a bit cheaper, as i wouldlike to score a few clones over here for cheapies , racing on my track ,\r\nif that\'s ok wich i cannot see why it wouldnt be , as you have not payed for anything yet ,\r\nim gona post an add now , but if that\'s not ok , just let me know and il take it down&lt;\r\ncheers,\r\nh20 :cool:[/quote:7eec9015f8]\r\n\r\nDo whatever you gotta do.  It\'s cool.  Good communication doesn\'t bother me at all.\r\n\r\nJust let me know if and when you need anything and I\'ll be happy to help you out.'),(31051,'41788e97a1','[quote:41788e97a1=\"stampede_dude\"]i have yahoo,aol, and msn messengers, lmk means let me know, so lmk what your adress for any of those services are if you got em.[/quote:41788e97a1]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll turn on the msn messenger deal here....I\'m motorgong@hotmail.com?'),(29165,'2f31d74969','w00t..a Canadian Modder! First off, were did you get them from?!\r\nSecond, how many do you have? I would want quite a few at that price :D\r\nThanks a bunch man!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29166,'74e8487484','[quote:74e8487484=\"betula66\"]Hi :-) ,I just wanted to ask if you\'ve got the price....[/quote:74e8487484]\r\n\r\nHey, tell ya what. Fuck you. If you\'ve got nothing good to say about someone who is doing you a major favor, you just need to find someone else to help you out. Good luck  :x'),(31837,'acd04d6d36','No problem dude.... :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(33894,'0613d48089','[quote:0613d48089=\"arfin\"]Haha k just send me another message when you are, so we can own!![/quote:0613d48089]\r\n\r\n\r\nI REALLY need my own connection instead of the neighbor\'s wireless LOL\r\n\r\nAll of their cars pull up in front of their house about 10min into us playing today, and lag lag lag LOL\r\n\r\nIts fun as all hell anyway :)\r\n\r\nSee ya soon!'),(29170,'289e09dd1e','Cool..i know were you got them :P From Ebay off the dude..i don\'t really care or anything..i just want some batteies...\r\nI am going to make just one big order of like 10 batts sonner or later...once i get the money for other shit :P\r\nThanks man!\r\n\r\nWhat rate have you charged these at and how long? \r\n\r\nI am thinking 4C so about 600mAH for like 15 min to get full charge...what have you used and what run time you gotten?'),(29171,'16f5b328fa','I use them in my epoch, its a 4 cell so i charge it at 6v, the charger is 300 ma, i charge it for like 10-15 minutes, haven\'t timed what i get but i will today if i can and tell you. For 10 batts it would cost $5.00 USD and no shipping :) I take paypal and m/o.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36885,'a995d70cd9','I rule, or suck depending on how you look at it. I found the kyosho board. Sorry about that. I\'ll go ahead and include all this stuff I picked up on sale.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37725,'ff7ca5d52b','not feeling paranoid or anything, lol, but could you do me a fave and wipe this thread?\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7370\r\n\r\nit would be mega kiss your arse appreciated, lol...\r\n\r\nMatt.'),(34342,'c22fa3d499','Where can I get some still pics of that car?\r\n\r\nThanx!'),(31541,'5d4991d281','No problem man.\r\n\r\nThey are somewhat weird to install. you need a soldering iron, flux, and a soldering heatsink (clamp-looking thing.) You have to be very carefull when soldering them so that it does not get too hot.\r\n\r\nYou need a special lithium polymer charger for them. I can get them for $20 shipped (to me). If you can do better over the pond, go ahead! It would take 7 days or so for that to get here however. That is from batteryspace.com and perhaps they will ship to new zealand. I don\'t know.\r\n\r\nI got a package today, but I\'m not sure what exactly it is yet. I\'ll be checking later.\r\n\r\nLet me know,\r\n-JNY'),(32873,'15d6d94027','grrrr.  I checked w/ the post office as well and sending it via United States Postal they don\'t offer tracking at all...  If I sent it UPS or Fed Ex I would have been able to, but that would have cost easily an extra $5-$15.  Sorry about the insane delay.  Everything was written down just as you said, I just hope it gets to you soon.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32054,'8e26a3f5d2','[quote:8e26a3f5d2=\"Finks\"]Oh and what would it cost to get that Eppisode III DvD thrown in the mix?[/quote:8e26a3f5d2]\r\n\r\nNothing for the DVD will just throw it in!\r\n\r\nPaypal address: airo@ev1.net\r\n\r\nthanks man! will get it out as soon as I can!  :-) \r\nAaron\r\n\r\nSWG'),(36806,'faa31759d2','[quote:faa31759d2=\"ph2t\"]hey man, I know, slack late response.  You\'ve prolyl figured out the problem now.\r\n\r\nI take it was a DNS issue?  You running an exchange box in a BIND DNS environment?\r\n\r\nhttp://www.msexchange.org/ is an excellent site for all things exchange, just search the forums there, it may help.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:faa31759d2]\r\nThanks holmes. Nah, wasn\'t a DNS issue. I still have some residual issues left-over but the main part is working now. Our network is so convoluted it\'s not even funny.\r\nI\'ve been going through that site, found some helpful info, but most really didn\'t apply to my particular situation. Again, probably just because of how our network is setup.\r\nI like coding much better than network admin. lol'),(37907,'b1c73d58d2','[quote:b1c73d58d2=\"HirotoR34\"]It\'s about 20 :shock:  Could I use Flash to edit it? I could cut it down a bit, and add a screen shot with title. It\'s been a while since I\'ve used flash, but I have it. I think I may have Adobe Premier....I\'ll have to look for the disc.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?[/quote:b1c73d58d2]\r\nI think you shouldn\'t spend time on it unless you personally want to.\r\nDon\'t do it just because I asked.\r\n\r\nI also think Premiere would be the better choice over Flash.\r\nI don\'t know what version of Flash you have either.\r\n\r\nIdeally, you\'d create and export your video from Premiere as a .wmv\r\nMost likely, after compression, it\'d be small enough to upload to your Gallery. (I realize, right now, you can\'t upload it to the bitPimps Galleries. I am uprading everything, so you\'d just have to wait)\r\nOr at least email to bitPimps.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested further, I can help - just ask.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32728,'307f66d3f5','That would be sick man.  You always see people making the body bigger.  Not often that someone shrinks a chassis.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(36227,'fd84bb4b37','[quote:fd84bb4b37=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:fd84bb4b37=\"sg219\"]Hiroto... :-o  :-o[/quote:fd84bb4b37]\r\nCool, go edit that post. You\'re only a few minutes behind Chedder.\r\n\r\nMake sure you change &quot;Myster Winner&quot; in both spots and add the image of the car that made him win.[/quote:fd84bb4b37]\r\n\r\nI can\'t edit there. :( \r\n\r\nI posted it next.\r\n\r\nYou can change it. :-o'),(33576,'fce06c735b','Do you know How much kohm\'s the iw 04 pcb origionally puts out to the pot. Im looking for what resistior value i would solder in on a hitec hs-55 to make everything work nice and flush.\r\n\r\nThanks for all the help lbrc :-) \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(32967,'f78a11b74c','Aww shit DT thanks a ton!  I figured I wasn\'t the only one.  Don\'t worry, I\'ll give it a good home  :-o'),(32096,'c2758692da','[quote:c2758692da=\"Finks\"]Wish I could say yes, but havn\'t recieved em as of yet.  Holding my fuckin breath, let me tell you.  Trust me, the second they are in, the whole fuckin world will know. :?[/quote:c2758692da]\r\nYou know, I forgot that that Bratwurst replied after SWG emailed him.  MY Badd !   :innocent:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37743,'879afa5dec','will do,,, ill get them to you tomorrow  :-) \r\n\r\nSTG'),(37738,'15dc064fb0','Hey man, what are you looking for as far as bits and zips for that NSX?  I have a lot of maybe 15-20 bit and zip bodies, a few ready to run stock and several random motors and other stuff (new in box lap counter off the top of my head)  \r\n\r\nLet me know if there is anything you are looking for.  Ill send ya some pics if you are interested.  Ill be home tomorrow (at my girlfriends place for the weekend)\r\n\r\nSTG'),(29916,'12785038ca','Ok so your prosocker, I\'m looking at the back wheels on this Hot Wheels car I got, and thinking these are the perfect size for rear pullback tires. So I\'m gonna attempt to do your wheels all matching. I figure it\'ll be lighter weight than the alloys, so it might have some advantage.\r\n\r\nThen you know SWG\'s car he just did up from that Low Rider car? I want to do that as a early \'60s Pro Gasser, you know before they had sticky tire compound and they jacked the front ends way up to tranfer weight to the rear. My wife is at walmart right now, we\'ll see if she comes back with one of those.\r\n\r\nBoth my ZZ SE are working again, so I think I\'m planning on bring one of those when I visit. I\'m guessing you guys were still kinda waiting for me to make a tut, don\'t know if you understand all of codesuidae\'s mumbo jumbo, but I can do your guy\'s cars up when i get there, show you first hand.\r\n\r\nI remembered I planned to beat you with your own Xmod, so I\'m trying to get that to work. I almost got it. I think that wire leading to the antenna got pinched, because now it almost works perfect, for about 15 ft. I think if I replace that wire it\'ll be fine. (fingers crossed) \r\nHey, are the crystals directional? I don\'t think so, but i just want to cover my bases\r\n\r\nWhat I plan to do to it is just upgrade the FETs, and run an Iwaver Xspeed(maybe Pro, who knows). I might just run the Iwaver Xspeed , and see how long the FETs hold up, that might be fun too. :???: \r\n\r\nAnyways, I\'m bored, and I didn\'t think any of this was worth posting about, so I was just sharing with you instead. \r\n\r\nDave'),(34157,'6800837b16','[quote:6800837b16=\"JdmHatchback\"]Thanks for letting me know you got em. If you or anyone else you know needs bodies let me know. I gotta bunch of bodies. Have fun modifiying your new bodies! \r\n\r\nJDM[/quote:6800837b16]\r\n\r\nJD!\r\n\r\nWhatcha got left ?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31536,'4c4862a6ff','I tried sending to LMennuti38@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nLet me know if you get it or not.\r\n\r\nStoli'),(33789,'060bec7140','[quote:060bec7140=\"sessiz\"]Aight, that\'s cool. Thanks for the freebie man, whatever it is. :-o[/quote:060bec7140]\r\n\r\nnot singular Freebee\'s plural man plural!  :-o'),(33794,'a240fe387f','Hi,\r\n\r\nThis is Rasheed Sabir, maybe you remember me from some emails I sent to you about modding a ZZSE board (just the board). Just letting you know thatI sent off the board today with a MO in the envelope.\r\n\r\nThanx \r\nMaxx'),(28548,'49ce6da2af','MARONG1@NETZERO.COM'),(32499,'fa234b99e5','Hey, I\'d be willing to ship down your way.  I\'ve never shipped anything down under before though.  What\'s your preferred way of shipment?\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(32500,'6cbc436aa1','The packages I have to ship your subs out won\'t hold two boxes.  I can either try and find another package/box, or take the subs out of the bulky original packaging and ship them in one.  It\'s your call on that one.  I was able to get you one on 49mhz and one on 27mhz so you can use \'em together.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(35460,'46a5d8ff51','No man it doesn\'t!  :o  I meet all requirements EXCEPT my Graphic Card isn\'t compatible with the game! Sucks so hard, you made it sound so good, now Im jealous! Anyways, how you been bro?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36660,'9a6e656184','You said you had a front steering problem, and I need a rear clip to fit a gen1 body on the evo chassis, and since you don\'t have any gen1 bodies and I have an extra evo chassis with the parts you would need, would you be willing to trade? I most likely have the part you need, just let me know, and if worst comes to worst We could work out a deal for the whole front end. Thanks!'),(27358,'848843e2e9','Oh yeah, I love BitPimps!  I ain\'t leaving anytime soon, and I\'ve found a site that has the Gloria bodykit and the Trueno pullback for not much cash, but I gotta keep the info on the downlow until I can order it.  Then I\'ll go public, since all I need from that site is those bodies and maybe the Toyota Bb bodykit and some others.  They did have some rare kits in stock you might like though.  Reply, like tomorrow and I\'ll give you the address.  I just gotta order my stuff tonight and then i\'ll blab it to everybody.  I don\'t want what I\'m looking for to suddenly dissapear, you know.\r\n\r\nLate,\r\nAbe\r\n\r\nP.S.- what do you make of this aution:\r\nhttp://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5951170846&amp;rd=1\r\nI\'ll get one if you think it\'s bit compatible.  Peace.'),(28349,'b7a1909b56','No problem, anytime');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33662,'3c505e57c5','Hey dude  ,\r\nWanna try again with the zzmt ? , or shall i sell it elsewhere ? , i just had a look under my bed and remembered .  :-)'),(28256,'559085d365','Do you have any GPM rear axles + cups for sale?\r\nyour gold ones look tight but any color will do.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(34552,'c9952cbb56','[quote:c9952cbb56=\"crazydave\"]The car is an Avanti, but what damn movie!!! Goonies? Can mods play too? :-D  :lol: \r\n\r\nhttp://www.avantisource.com/[/quote:c9952cbb56]\r\nThat\'s pretty good dude. I don\'t think I woulda ever guessed the car. lol\r\nIt is an Avanti.\r\n\r\nAnyone can play, so if you want - go for it.\r\nOr, do ya want me to tell ya? (but then you can\'t play - neener neener)'),(34566,'06ea2b301d','[quote:06ea2b301d=\"CaboWabo\"] :lol: Right on. I\'ll be sending it US Mail in a padded envelope.\r\n\r\nYea, I posted the quiz late last night, I was thinking it would run for at least a few days before someone nailed it. I was wrong. lol\r\nGood job man.[/quote:06ea2b301d]\r\n\r\nI got the car right away, it was the movie I had to check up on.'),(27298,'a6de121ecb','[quote:a6de121ecb]=GP-05 Sptinter Tureno Pullback \r\n-GM-05 Nissan Gloria Bodykit \r\n-Lamborghini Murcielago pullback \r\n-DeTomaso Pantera GTS pullback \r\n-Scion xB bodykit \r\n-Mini Heart Monte Carlo Rally Mini Cooper 1275S Mark I set (other mini cooper kits used to be available at toyeast, as was most of this stuff) \r\n\r\nThe Nissan Gloria Bodykit and the the Sprinter Trueno pullback are rarer than shit, and I can\'t find them anywhere, toyeast, hobbyonsale, RCmart, none of them carry those two and I need them like sweet pountang, although not quite as much. [/quote:a6de121ecb]\r\n\r\n\r\nSeeberg,\r\n\r\nThose will be difficult to get, some impossible but I have a lot of connections.\r\n\r\nSome of these you\'ll probably have to buy the Bit Char-G......\r\nhttp://www.hlj.com/scripts/hljlist.cgi?Maker1=TOM&amp;Category=AutPas&amp;Dis=2\r\n\r\n[b:a6de121ecb]Gloria:[/b:a6de121ecb] never came as a pullback: Bit Char-G &amp; Body kit only\r\nhttp://www.hlj.com/scripts/hljpage.cgi?TOM62854\r\n\r\n[b:a6de121ecb]Lambo:[/b:a6de121ecb]PullBack I\'ll have to check\r\n\r\n[b:a6de121ecb]DeTomaso Pantera GTS pullback[/b:a6de121ecb]: Only found Bit Char-G\r\nhttp://www.hlj.com/scripts/hljpage.cgi?TOM68589\r\n\r\n[b:a6de121ecb]Scion xB bodykit[/b:a6de121ecb]: Was 1st known as a Toyota bB. \r\n http://www.hlj.com/scripts/hljpage.cgi?TOM62852\r\n\r\n[b:a6de121ecb]Mini Heart Monte Carlo Rally Mini Cooper [/b:a6de121ecb]: Only TE sold these so\r\nchances are if they\'re out, you\'ll have to track them 2nd hand. TE has nothing but left over stuff.\r\n\r\nContact [b:a6de121ecb]JdmHatchback[/b:a6de121ecb] for bodies, he has quite a few for around $3.00.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34160,'1b5888bfec','The sig always worked, but at leaste on my computer I don\'t see my Avatar anymore, just a [color=red:1b5888bfec]x[/color:1b5888bfec]'),(29324,'e26410e9d5','Just got the package today, thanks again man! :-)'),(27735,'02445c1b06','good news then abe, as far as the stretch goes your going to have to use at leat two glorias to make it happen...\r\n\r\ncheck out betty\'s bb limo for some ideas, ive seen it in the flesh and it is seemless...\r\n\r\ni personally have been doing more work on larger scale models at the moment, 1/28th scale mini-z bodies and im lovin it. the extra room alows for more freedom in the spray department but as far as details go i think i hit my peak of customization with my supra (look in the flossin\' in the city section here) and the allmighty bb monster i did (pics of this beast should be in my bitpimps gallery).\r\n\r\nso goin on 21 hey? i thought i was the youngest in the click, and im 22 (soon to 23 in april)...\r\n\r\n   cant wait to see what you do with these legendary bodies.\r\n\r\ni am doing some work on a sprinter (mini-z) at the moment for a freind, im not sure when i get some pics up from it but it should be soon... the front end is being tricked out with a radicaly designed body kit, im not sure if everybody would like the styling ive done but it is totally original in its shape (think of insectoid  and your getting the idea)...\r\n\r\n farewell and keep on modding!'),(27732,'02445c1b06','good news then abe, as far as the stretch goes your going to have to use at leat two glorias to make it happen...\r\n\r\ncheck out betty\'s bb limo for some ideas, ive seen it in the flesh and it is seemless...\r\n\r\ni personally have been doing more work on larger scale models at the moment, 1/28th scale mini-z bodies and im lovin it. the extra room alows for more freedom in the spray department but as far as details go i think i hit my peak of customization with my supra (look in the flossin\' in the city section here) and the allmighty bb monster i did (pics of this beast should be in my bitpimps gallery).\r\n\r\nso goin on 21 hey? i thought i was the youngest in the click, and im 22 (soon to 23 in april)...\r\n\r\n   cant wait to see what you do with these legendary bodies.\r\n\r\ni am doing some work on a sprinter (mini-z) at the moment for a freind, im not sure when i get some pics up from it but it should be soon... the front end is being tricked out with a radicaly designed body kit, im not sure if everybody would like the styling ive done but it is totally original in its shape (think of insectoid  and your getting the idea)...\r\n\r\n farewell and keep on modding!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27315,'5c36aa4fad','haha thanks, my party will be the biggest scam ill take there money and give them music and food for three hours, thell be happy, ill be happy.'),(27316,'0f49829f59','[quote:0f49829f59=\"stagg\"]haha thanks, my party will be the biggest scam ill take there money and give them music and food for three hours, thell be happy, ill be happy.[/quote:0f49829f59]\r\n\r\nDo what you gotta do.  I totally understand about having parties!!  \r\n\r\nI used to have parties when I got low on beer and buzz and made the party a B.Y.O.B. (Bring Your Own Buzz) then when everyone would leave, they would also leave without the Buzz that they brought to the party and I would have full fridge of free booze, a table full of free buzz and just a mess to clean up. :cool:'),(29716,'c0a81b2c50','i will give you one just send me the addy.'),(27882,'de62bae485','ok i sent the jota shell about 10 min ago pirotity mail , let me know when it arives , later . \r\n\r\n\r\nmatt'),(28353,'6d850eb978','Aw maaan,\r\n\r\nI think so, tell me exactly what GPM are you willing to send, and how many of each. you said $40 right?\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28055,'735af5cfec','Ok, well let me know what happens.  Actually, I will be strapping this into either a RC18, Xray M18T, or a Kyosho Mini777.  I am selling my Mini-T.  But I need the Rx for the XXX-T I am trading a custom Xmod Chassis for.  Infact, I originalyl created it to be used with a 280 motor (what a coincidence),  Thanks, I was going to order from BPP anyways, I just mainly do not want to order fro mRcmart, because they kill you with shipping.\r\n\r\nLet me know what hapens,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(27327,'120497dab4','Man, I know where you\'re coming from. I always feel singled out too, but I assure you no one is singling you out.\r\n\r\nSomeone, who, I do not know, had apparently thought they were doing you a favor by moving your thread where it might get more response, not paying attention to your post count. Betty was doing his job in enforceing the 50 post count rule for that forum. Obviously a lack of comunication. \r\n\r\nMaybe if you had pleaded your case behind the scenes by PMing Cabo, or even me, things wouldn\'t have blown up as they have, but what\'s done is done, and now Betty is pissed, and your pissed, and honestly, I make it policy to stay out of the way when 2 people are pissed. I tried to smooth things over the other day, but that didn\'t seem to help.\r\n\r\n\r\nSo anyways, what I\'m saying is, betty will be back today and tomorrow, and the next day, we know that. I\'m just hoping that you can be a better man, and realize a mistake was made, and move on. In other words, I hope you continue to hang out here. You\'re an entertaining character, for shure.\r\n\r\nWant me to just  delete that thread?\r\n\r\nDave'),(27488,'583c188443','Well some RS do have them in stock right now, if ZZ\'s are acceptable ?????\r\n\r\n[img:583c188443]http://www.zipzaps.com/images/showroom/Toyota_cars/1whtTRUENO.jpg[/img:583c188443]\r\n[img:583c188443]http://www.zipzaps.com/images/showroom/Toyota_cars/whtLEVIN.jpg[/img:583c188443]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28504,'3e631c5c70','Glad to see that you like my paint job, other people don\'t seem to realize the time that goes into my work. Can\'t wait to see that car with some crazy rims on it.  If you ever need something special painted up etc. let me know and I will hook you up. I also paint up xmods as well.'),(28317,'e69f09b58b','[quote:e69f09b58b=\"backdrift\"]Ok, to make a long story short when i was attaching the wires to two of the chargers they were faulty, and i placed an order with the place i get them from for more. so it will be a little while, im sorry for the inconvience and because of this im going do give u 8 chargers. \r\nonce again sorry. \r\n\r\nBackdrift[/quote:e69f09b58b]\r\n\r\nWhen will you be sending those or should I trough you under a bus?'),(28185,'dd94ee9177','Yeah, there are only 11 chassis, $5 eash'),(36076,'b4aa0d560a','Hey, know anywhere in the uk i can get really cheap (upgradeable) mini rc cars? Im english too :D'),(32557,'badcf03baf','Hey, if you\'re interested, I might be interested in trading some bit racer gears/wheels for your Supra body set and Microsizer tire set. Still got em?\r\n\r\nI\'ll check my inventory and see what I can part with.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32371,'dda418b4be','thanks'),(27824,'783321298d','I got some with snug washers. Let me know if you\'re interested.[url][/url]'),(27828,'cdbdaefc3c','[quote:cdbdaefc3c=\"HirotoR34\"]I almost forgot, You sent me a PM entitled Alloys. You know where I can get some? You said you\'d holla back later, so I figured I\'d ask you while I had teh chance....[/quote:cdbdaefc3c]\r\n\r\nWe\'ll Talk........'),(27871,'f8c6d5c849','Hey VP,\r\n\r\nIf you head up there to pickup an Nak Hummer, would you mind pick\'n up a few more. I\'m down for 3, color or frequency doesn\'t matter.  I\'m gonna suggest a group buy cause there seems to be great interrest.\r\n\r\nJust remember, if they only have 4 left, I\'m down for 3  8-) \r\nLemme know!'),(32812,'227ffcc902','Please tell me you got the package!'),(32813,'3eb5f92d3d','Still not here yet...  :( \r\nI checked with the post office, and without a shipping number or something, they haven\'t got any way to track it.\r\nAlthough if it came by ground mail, they said it could take anywhere between 4 - 6 weeks.'),(35941,'7f325eeb85','Hey sorry to bother you. I checked out your tutorial in the Xmods section on the resistor turning trick...\r\n\r\nCould you show me some pics, the pics you have on the site don\'t load up for me.\r\n\r\nRight now my xmod is running half decent, but it is starting to drive more to one side now, and my brother\'s xmod turns better left than right, how the hell do i fix this?\r\n\r\nAlso, what are some other good ways to actually improve the turning radius on my xmod?\r\n\r\nBy readin your post on xmods I am hoping you are some what of a pro lol...\r\n\r\nI need some help man, a little advice would be more than nice man.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27826,'d0cc9a5382','yup im intrested . ive needed tthem since the day i got the car and could never find them for a resonable price .'),(33049,'5ba52fa42a','you gonna be around much longer? ive got a charger i made inspired by yours that ide like to show you'),(27336,'799b1bb412','Edit:  Original post removed.\r\n\r\nForget it.\r\n\r\nIt\'s too late. :-)'),(33113,'56a6c7b57e','thanks again for the heads-up dude, i just got the stuffs today! You definitely got me the jump on somma these guys.\r\n\r\nNow i gotta get a lipo charger (them things is scary! pray i don\'t blow myself up!)\r\n :shock:'),(26835,'e055d397e2','Hey DT! What\'s up?\r\nLong time huh?\r\nMy fault. Lots happening here. I got engaged. I moved. Working on the house (painting, drywall and all that good stuff!)\r\n\r\nAnyway, as you already know, I\'m back!\r\nI really didn\'t think I\'d win anything. Surprise to me! WooHoo!\r\n\r\nMy new address:\r\n[b:e055d397e2]Vince Valderrama\r\n12519 McVickers\r\nPalos Heights, IL 60463 [/b:e055d397e2]\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n-Vince'),(26836,'0eea832943','Gotcha Pimp!\r\n\r\nYeah it\'s been a while, but you been Quite Busy! \r\n\r\nCongratulations on the Marriage 8-) \r\n\r\nYour prize will be in the mail tomorrow, you should get it by Wednesday.\r\n\r\nFunny incident:\r\n\r\nI posted a Red Skyline as 3rd place/choice prize.  I accidently sent it to Cabo in a package of Goodies for the 2nd BitPimp Anniversary. Since he did create this forum, I thought it appropriate to show my apreciation.\r\n\r\nAnyways I\'m sending you a replacement, still a Precious but a Red Subaru WRX !  \r\nWhat a coincidence  8-)\r\nEnjoy man, this was a very difficult contest to judge, the margins were very narrow.  Congrats Again Pimp');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33676,'edf2d8d857','Hi dave, \r\n\r\nYou wouldn\'t happen to have more than one ZZSE with the duty-Cycle mod? I\'d like one. If you\'re willing to sell me one, let me know. This will serve as the  heart of my ZZMT F-150. I wanto enter it in the year-end comp. I have some more stuff to add to it, and to mod it with articulation with a slight fix ;)\r\n\r\nSo let me know the price if you\'re willing to sell\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx'),(33685,'501da7ba11','Heh, well it was a noble and mature thing to do.   :-o'),(37875,'1983a9647d','I deleted the image link in your signature.\r\n\r\nIt contained an Internet worm. :-x \r\n\r\nI realize it\'s probably not your fault and didn\'t even know about it.\r\nJust watch what you link to.\r\n\r\nAnd for sure, DO NOT link to anything on danasoft.com'),(37881,'5d944ebfaa','dude,  i do appreciate your effort to help me out.\r\nand no disrespect intended but check your sig for small typo\r\n&quot;Those who would sacrifice liberty for security deserve[b:5d944ebfaa]r[/b:5d944ebfaa] neither. - Benjamin Franklin &quot;\r\nthank you Cabo Wabo. i mean it'),(37882,'11d6e53797','[quote:11d6e53797=\"ynad\"]dude,  i do appreciate your effort to help me out.\r\nand no disrespect intended but check your sig for small typo\r\n&quot;Those who would sacrifice liberty for security deserve[b:11d6e53797]r[/b:11d6e53797] neither. - Benjamin Franklin &quot;\r\nthank you Cabo Wabo. i mean it[/quote:11d6e53797]\r\nNo sweat dude, glad I could help.\r\nAnd thanks for the heads up on my sig. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35232,'364ff15bff','Man, I\'m finally on vacation. I haven\'t had any time off in 4 years. I even work holidays, because I like having the place to myself those days. This will actually be the first time in like 10 years I didn\'t go in on Thanksgiving to do prep.  :shock: \r\n\r\nIts hard as hell for me to get away from that place, I was telling you like 2 months ago I was taking a week off, and I was gonna work on your car, and now finally, I get some fucking time off. They have to hire new people, and borrow from other store, because they got to bring in 2 people to cover my ass. People keep quitting and getting fired, so I never get a vacation. Funny how they don\'t appreciate me when I\'m there.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSooo... Anyways, I guess I\'m just venting now, but besides relaxing and recovering, catching up on projects is high priorty this week, I\'m hoping to put out several projects. :-o \r\n\r\nBTW, want a Lexan body funny car, or how about a Willys coupe?\r\nhttp://www.wizzardho.com/Products14.htm\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDave'),(36688,'a46763c88c','about 1.3 feet squared.\r\n\r\nThat reminds me. all the parts are in a plastic bag. The chassis is at the bottom. You need to pull the bag out and carefully empty it. It is not packing material! =)\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36207,'139195e4f2','So i know this comes with crazy extra parts.\r\n\r\nBut what does it have installed right now?\r\n\r\nIs it in running condition?\r\n\r\nIts basically full alloy if i wanted it to be with the extras installed correct!\r\n\r\nAre you still including all your 1:28 stuff etc. for this like you said in your BST post?\r\n\r\nDid you get  the plasmatomic from ph2t in the mail?'),(36724,'1a0d31db54','[quote:1a0d31db54=\"pimpsmurf\"]It\'s hot glued through the middle of the chassis. There is an extra chassis (grey) pre-drilled for 600mah lithium ions, and a new clear chassis I was going to modify for gp1100 cells.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:1a0d31db54]\r\n\r\nIs there a running motor in the truck currently if so what is it?'),(36723,'b9685f472b','It\'s hot glued through the middle of the chassis. There is an extra chassis (grey) pre-drilled for 600mah lithium ions, and a new clear chassis I was going to modify for gp1100 cells.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36235,'fbe9310320','[quote:fbe9310320=\"pimpsmurf\"]I think there is a plasmatomic there. Seriously, I think there are like 3-5 armatures (uberdash arm, plasmatomic arm, pn s03, etc.) I believe the plasmatomic needs new brushes.\r\n\r\nThere are extra parts galore. It is in runing condition with the exception that it needs a new front gearbox, of which I am including 2 (1 clear, 1 chrome.)\r\n\r\nI could ship it UPS, but it would cost an arm and a leg. USPS priority would be easier and cheaper, and I would insure it for full value so you would be covered.\r\n\r\nIt is an awsome truck, but my 1:10 nitro is taking all my time, so I\'ve not had the time or money to do it up the way I wanted (custom alloy chassis, etc.)\r\n\r\nI just don\'t have the time for it.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:fbe9310320]\r\n\r\nDidnt you have a alloy front gearbox for it?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36238,'4fdf334810','[quote:4fdf334810=\"pimpsmurf\"]I think there is a plasmatomic there. Seriously, I think there are like 3-5 armatures (uberdash arm, plasmatomic arm, pn s03, etc.) I believe the plasmatomic needs new brushes.\r\n\r\nThere are extra parts galore. It is in runing condition with the exception that it needs a new front gearbox, of which I am including 2 (1 clear, 1 chrome.)\r\n\r\nI could ship it UPS, but it would cost an arm and a leg. USPS priority would be easier and cheaper, and I would insure it for full value so you would be covered.\r\n\r\nIt is an awsome truck, but my 1:10 nitro is taking all my time, so I\'ve not had the time or money to do it up the way I wanted (custom alloy chassis, etc.)\r\n\r\nI just don\'t have the time for it.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:4fdf334810]\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you have time can you attempt to write up a list.\r\n\r\nI just feel like i dont know what im buying at this point, hard to picture you could say.'),(36260,'aeadfc849c','[quote:aeadfc849c=\"pimpsmurf\"]Go to the old forum topic and read that. I haven\'t sold or given anything away. It is a completely pimped MZM. It has everything. \r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:aeadfc849c]\r\n\r\nCome with a lipo pack?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34428,'6b63e21169','[quote:6b63e21169=\"Finks\"]lol dude, no worries, was just making sure. Was just worried, still havn\'t seen the package (mail has yet to come today tho)  No worries either way.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nFinks[/quote:6b63e21169]\r\n\r\nCool I did not want to offend and some times I have a strange sense of humor! I hope you get your package today looks like just about everyone has gotten theirs. Let me know when it comes in so I can stop holding my breath! \r\n\r\nthanks for understanding bud!  :-) \r\n\r\nAaron'),(34986,'ea16ba21c6','Much obliged.'),(35647,'b81657e805','[quote:b81657e805=\"Mad_Maxx\"]Sorry to disturb you Boss,\r\nI wrote MAd_Maxx instead of Mad_Maxx for my album\\user name can I change it??\r\n\r\nSorry again 4 disturbing, i didn\'t know where to write you\r\n\r\nMax.[/quote:b81657e805]\r\nNo worries.\r\nYou wrote to the right place. I\'ve gone ahead and changed your name, should be all ready to go.\r\nLet me know if you have any troubles.'),(30070,'6c795acb0a','You can paypal to me at codesuidae@codesuidae.net\r\n\r\nI too think everyone should buy (at least) one  :-D \r\n\r\nI really need to get busy and redesign the board with a 0.3mm PCB and on-board resistor for non-FET installs.  Unfortunately I\'ve been busy with other things lately.  Once I do get it done I\'ll have to find some advertising so more people will be aware of it.\r\n\r\nFYI, I\'ll be out of town Tue 14 through Friday, so can\'t mail anything those days.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (26871,'b40ed77baa','Your Prize went out yesterday morning.  Please let me know when you receive it    8-)'),(33754,'cde1760506','[quote:cde1760506=\"crazydave\"][quote:cde1760506=\"hue35\"][quote:cde1760506=\"crazydave\"]I just ordered the decals for P:PSII, and they\'ve got some new 1/72nd decals. Check \'em out. The top set are the ones I intended to order, should be smaller than the ones I used on my car, but check out the second sheet down. That\'s so great becaise I\'m making Gasser out one of my \'57s, and those even have the gasser markings.  :-D \r\n\r\nSo I ordered those too, along with a couple of the flames.\r\n\r\nYou like any of those names? ;) ;)\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:cde1760506]\r\nI don\'t see anything... is it my shitty dial-up connection?. . . no link, I think.[/quote:cde1760506]Damn, I\'m such a fucking burn out sometimes, I forgot the link. :lol: \r\n\r\nAnd here I was all excited to see what you thought, guess I\'ll have wait \'til after work now. :-( \r\n\r\nAnyways, before I forget again, link: http://www.radicaldecals.com/172front.html[/quote:cde1760506]\r\nThose are cool... so, I assume you\'ve tried the 1:64 scale and they\'re too big? It seems, based on the way those fit on a T-Jet, the 1:72 might be too small. Bits are kinda between the 2, huh? I guess when I think about it, bits are so distorted it makes things like decals kinda tricky... I could see \"a little too small\" being easier to work with than \"a little too large\".\r\n\r\nThat\'s sweet they have the gas-type decals. Also, it\'s funny as hell they have the driver name \"Fast Eddie\"... for the first twelve or so years of my career, my main hard drive has been named \"Fast Eddie\", with my other volumes being \"Vinnie\" and \"Tony\"... little characters I invented my last year of college... the Vasalino brothers. They were hit-men/porn-stars.\r\n\r\nI think all those decals are sweet... the Hemi Hauler is cool, but limiting. I like the Alky Hauler ones too.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:cde1760506=\"crazydave\"]Interesting development concerning my trip. My wife informed me last night, she\'s taking a trip to Vegas soon, for a Scrapbooking convention. I got mad, said WTF, its supposed to be my turn to take a vaction, she\'s had 2 vacations since I\'ve been planning this trip to Portland. Then she informs me this morning, that I can just barely afford to go on Oct. 15th, if I want to. But now I\'m not ready, just getting to work on your car, and I never did anthing to my Xmod, or bought an Iwaver. So I\'m still not ready, but I got guilt working on my side now, so I\'m feeling more positive about it again. :-o \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:cde1760506]\r\nCool. You\'ll have to give me a ballpark idea when you can... I\'m about to start (in a month or two) a major project at my house that could screw things up from a \"having guests\" perspective. Although, if you wouldn\'t mind the disaster for a coupla days, it probably wouldn\'t matter too much. How long a trip were you thinking, by the way? Like, a Friday afternoon through Sunday afternoon/evening kind of thing?.\r\n\r\nMan, I gotta get a new car built... I just gotta. \r\n\r\nOh, I picked up on of the new SE\'s... man, right outta the box, these things go even better than I thought. I haven\'t even run a full charge through it, \'cuz my floors were too dog haired, but it seemed like the right amount of power. So, does the FET mod really help these out that much? Also, do you think the Duty Cycle mod is even worth doing on these things? I guess I can compare to Greg\'s Vette to see the difference... he hasn\'t even run that, by the way... that\'s how busy that guy\'s been. We\'re down to about once a month, which sucks. Neither of us have had the time... hopefully winter will bring on some more racing nights.\r\n\r\nI\'m gonna try to take one of my old, broken SE\'s back today, dressed up in the Vette\'s shell and packaging, to try and get another of these chassis... I figure they owe it to me. The first one shouldn\'t have sucked, ya know? I\'ll let ya know how that went. \r\n\r\n :cool:'),(34526,'d7b01fa81f','Cool.  I\'ll let you know if I find it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34539,'58cbc5a15e','hey i cut my body all i got to do isda bed and  a little body work'),(33818,'6aec412d2f','[quote:6aec412d2f=\"crazydave\"]I was thinking of shaving the side trim off the \'57, to give it more of the look of that \'55, and give me room to put the logo on the rear quarter panel like that. You think that would look wrong? Its not the most accurate body to begin with.[/quote:6aec412d2f]\r\nYeah, I think that would work... you may need to do something to tone down those rear fins, but like you said, it\'s not a very accurate body anyway. And, by the time you add decals &amp; stuff, it really won\'t matter.\r\n\r\nSweet, that\'s gonna be cool.\r\n\r\nI\'m with ya on the Nova thing. A \'65 Nova wagon is a car I\'ve always loved, wanted and would own, if I could afford to have a toy like that.'),(31266,'9ca78e30b8','thanks i am very happy that it will work :D  i figured it would work but take a while to charge but i have no problem with sitting around with my zipzaps and xmod waiting for the battery to charge :lol: i got the guard cuz with lipo u can never be too safe :-o and as for getting the narrow pack umm i dont think i did i just ordered it straight from bpp and got the mamba with it too so maybe they will figure it out. i got it while they were suposubly shipping the 20c ones too :eek:\r\n\r\nthanks for the help lb :cool:'),(33206,'fce4cdb1dc','Hey Cameron,\r\n\r\nSorry, I\'ve been busy at work and I totally forgot to send the rims, man.  :? \r\n\r\nThey\'ll be in the mail tomorrow for sure.\r\n\r\n-DriveWRX');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35360,'32f80b608b','Hey,  sorry was away a few days.\r\n\r\nI paypalled you 71$ for a silver kit, mustang clip, and an extra set of rear axles.\r\n\r\n-Cancel the extra set of rear axles\r\n-Add in the set of the front dogbones.\r\n-I still want the mustang clip. \r\n-I would like to add a silver diff for the car.\r\n\r\njust lemme know how much to paypal.\r\n\r\n-Clint\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:32f80b608b=\"cj\"][color=red:32f80b608b][size=18:32f80b608b][b:32f80b608b]For Your Eys Only[/b:32f80b608b][/size:32f80b608b][/color:32f80b608b]\r\n[size=9:32f80b608b]My cell number is 931-607-0548[/size:32f80b608b]\r\n[color=red:32f80b608b][size=18:32f80b608b][b:32f80b608b]For Your Eys Only[/b:32f80b608b][/size:32f80b608b][/color:32f80b608b][/quote:32f80b608b]'),(35361,'d6b3ccae91','[quote:d6b3ccae91=\"Clint\"]Hey,  sorry was away a few days.\r\n\r\nI paypalled you 71$ for a silver kit, mustang clip, and an extra set of rear axles.\r\n\r\n-Cancel the extra set of rear axles\r\n-Add in the set of the front dogbones.\r\n-I still want the mustang clip. \r\n-I would like to add a silver diff for the car.\r\n\r\njust lemme know how much to paypal.\r\n\r\n-Clint[/quote:d6b3ccae91]\r\n\r\nAdding the Diff and the clip you are looking at $21.00 more.'),(37599,'f7474b6451','[quote=PimpSmurf]I don\'t agree with everything the libertarians (base = liberty, not liberal) believe, just 95% of it. They are pretty far right wing. Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative. [/quote]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t say liberals, I said libertarians. And they do indeed. There are a couple libertarian talk shows on talkradio and shortwave and they are most libertarians (about 75%) see Bush as more liberal than conservative.\r\n\r\nThe problem with all these labels is you have to define them. The problem with the LP is most members of the LP vote for republicans in states that are close. No need to have another sex-junkie in the White House.\r\n\r\nYou are seeing fault where there is non. I have not contradicted myself on this issue because it is an issue of beliefs. You are retreating, which is OK. I\'m not willing to argue a point (argue, not fight) that the other side isn\'t willing to bring ideas to the table.\r\n\r\nThanks anyway man. It was fun (except the gay sex.)\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36963,'7f4c96a3a6','Yes, I know they are selling those, but they are about $10 more than what I started selling them at. :sad: \r\n\r\nThe &quot;PRO&quot; has better FET\'s installed.  They will handle the hotter motors like the SO line from PN and others.  However it will NOT handle the Ph2t Plasma-atomic motors.\r\n\r\nFor batteries, you can go all over the place.  Its best to shop around the internet to find the best deal.  Just do a search and check the forums for hints and tips.  I never really got into the whole Li-ion thing.  I\'m a Nimh junkie for 1/2x scale and a Lipo junkie for anything bigger, 1/18 and up.\r\n\r\nIf I come across anything, I\'ll drop you a message.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nlater, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(26890,'c99f91b859','Sounds good!! :cool: \r\n\r\nI\'ll probably do it sometime Saturday while the Steelers are practicing for the Super Bowl. :rockon:'),(33827,'8e2c983177','[quote:8e2c983177=\"crazydave\"][quote:8e2c983177=\"hue35\"]Oh, I picked up on of the new SE\'s... man, right outta the box, these things go even better than I thought. I haven\'t even run a full charge through it, \'cuz my floors were too dog haired, but it seemed like the right amount of power. So, does the FET mod really help these out that much? Also, do you think the Duty Cycle mod is even worth doing on these things? I guess I can compare to Greg\'s Vette to see the difference... he hasn\'t even run that, by the way... that\'s how busy that guy\'s been. We\'re down to about once a month, which sucks. Neither of us have had the time... hopefully winter will bring on some more racing nights.[/quote:8e2c983177]See I was telling you about them SEs. I\'m not too sure what the FET mod did. I got so in the habit of FET modding SEs right out of the package, I had only run it for a couple minutes, but I think it did help it pull the red gears. Don\'t think you\'d see any difference with the stock 12:1. The DC mod will double the performance of that car. Its a bit too much for some situations. If you only have one vette, you might want to keep that stock, for something more mild than the DC mod, but still acceptable. You also might want to stick it in the vette for the improved steering, but I think it\'d be of better use in a GTO/Torino/Chevelle/Ford GT/NSX that has good steering, but the crappy DC cycle. My Chevelle had perfect steering, but the GTO I got to replace it has some slight jitters, occasionally. The DC mod helped the steering enough that its close enough to perfect now. Code said that was just a side effect, and only happened on some cars, I\'m assuming the newer ones.[/quote:8e2c983177]\r\nSo, let me get this straight... if you did the duty-cycle mod to a Chevelle-era SE and to a new Vette SE, the 2 would be about the same? So, if I were to install code\'s deal, the older chassis would be the one to do, \'cuz it would realize more of the SE\'s power potential than even the new Vette chassis... and fix any steering issues as a bonus. These new vette chassis kick ass right outta the box... I\'m into seeing if they can get better, but I\'ll probably only mod one of \'em... eventually... maybe. I think, if I was anywhere close to on track above, I\'m gonna order up the duty-cycle deal from code soon.\r\n\r\n[quote:8e2c983177=\"crazydave\"][quote:8e2c983177]I\'m gonna try to take one of my old, broken SE\'s back today, dressed up in the Vette\'s shell and packaging, to try and get another of these chassis... I figure they owe it to me. The first one shouldn\'t have sucked, ya know? I\'ll let ya know how that went. [/quote:8e2c983177]Yeah, let me know how that goes. :-o[/quote:8e2c983177]\r\nIt worked... twice. And, I got to keep the old car both times... \"hey, since you\'re gonna throw it away anyway, can I just keep it for parts?\"   :-o \r\n\r\nAlso, I bought a couple more ZZMTs... $19 for 2 is a great deal for that toy. I love them as is, but I just set one of them on a shelf, right next my OG iWaiver... that will be a fun project.'),(31269,'e8268fbd78','[quote:e8268fbd78=\"kvik369\"]Hey dude \r\n\r\nWhats up? - You still modding for the public?\r\n\r\nVik[/quote:e8268fbd78]Not really, but you\'re cool to work with, so whatever you need, I\'ll do it. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nOh BTW, I had a story to tell you. Just a couple weeks ago, I fryed one of my SEs. That\'s why I went out and puchased that Vette. Then I remembered your chassis and pulled it out to see if I could fix it.\r\n\r\nTurns out it wasn\'t my fault that car died. None of the shrink tubing was shrunk on that car, and the shrink wrap on the motor capacitor had slid up and shorted the battery. So i taped it off,, pulled the battery from the car I just killed, and it works.\r\n\r\nSo I guess it pays off to step up when there\'s a problem. :-o \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31270,'77b54d42da','&gt;  and this time its working, nothing\'s shorting out, but it performs exactly as it did before\r\n\r\nFirst off, again, my apologies for the recent latency in my communications, being off on client sites and working 12 to 15 hours a day puts a serious dent in my motivation to do anything but float in the hotel pool.\r\n\r\nAnyway, it sounds like you need to do one of two things.  First, see if you have pins 3 and 4 shorted together.  If they aren\'t try shorting them, if they are, clear the short (I forget wich way is right for a later gen car).  Next would be to check the \'disable\' jumper.  Unfortunately I forget which pin that is, I\'ll have to look it up tonight and let you know.  The disable jumper turns off the upgrades the DC mod makes so that you can run stock without removing the chip.  I\'ve installed a few DC mods with switches on that so the user can just turn it off.  I doubt thats the problem, but it is possible.\r\n\r\nIf you are looking at the dc mod from the top, with the electrical connections \'down\', pins three and four will be on the bottom left.\r\n\r\nDK'),(36839,'f36f5d8d46','i was planning a draft in G10 fiberglass, and the final in cf.\r\n\r\nin america, stuff is available in english units, so cf will be in 1/16&quot; and 1/32&quot;. 1/16&quot; is about 1.58mm, good for the bottom plate. 1/32&quot; is about 0.8mm, good for the top deck.\r\n\r\ni don\'t know any walk-in stores you can get cf at... it\'s more or less a supplier material, and kinda high-class still... you can get it online though, i know www.dragonplate.com is a good source.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31282,'9ca78e30b8','thanks i am very happy that it will work :D  i figured it would work but take a while to charge but i have no problem with sitting around with my zipzaps and xmod waiting for the battery to charge :lol: i got the guard cuz with lipo u can never be too safe :-o and as for getting the narrow pack umm i dont think i did i just ordered it straight from bpp and got the mamba with it too so maybe they will figure it out. i got it while they were suposubly shipping the 20c ones too :eek:\r\n\r\nthanks for the help lb :cool:'),(33944,'f283941258','I deleted Shaun\'s thread about the Losi buggy... I meant to delete the thread, but ended up only deleting his first post. Then you and maxx posted in there, but I had already fucked it up, so I just deleted the whole thing... sorry about that.'),(31277,'9e7587b5d3','[quote:9e7587b5d3=\"kvik369\"]\r\nDid you check tower\'s site.  Listing alot of Iwaver stuff.\r\n\r\nVik[/quote:9e7587b5d3]Yeah, unfortunately I want an 02 like now. That\'s ok they\'re still $10 cheaper at MZR, but they only got a couple left. I\'m praying they still got them by friday.\r\n\r\nStill though, be cool if we see the Iwaver stuff listed in their Speed Mart sales flyers. It always makes me order stuff if I got a catalog to stare at. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(34906,'5781974755','[quote:5781974755=\"Maxximum Attack\"][url]http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6010340347&amp;rd=1&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1[/url]\r\n\r\nFor less than $60.\r\nthere is less than 3 hrs left\r\nI\'ll pay you back via MO\r\nI will also give you an american address to ship to\r\nThanx[/quote:5781974755]\r\n\r\nIt\'s up at over $66. I assume you meant you only wanted it for $60 or less?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31291,'547836fa3e','[quote:547836fa3e=\"SuperFly\"]Hey man-\r\n\r\nWhat\'s the going rate to get an SE fetted? I realize that the chances of me ordering the proper fets and finding the time to read up on it and get it done are slim to none, but I\'d like to get my hands on one. I was thinking that maybe instead of me going to RS and buying a new silver vette SE to mail to ya, I could just send ya some cash and you could grab one next time you\'re there. I\'m in no hurry at all.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re not interested, I\'m not assuming you would do this so no worries. However, if you are, let me know how much dough ya need and I\'ll get ya covered.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nSuperFly[/quote:547836fa3e]How ironic. I haven\'t been doing FETs for people. kvik PMed today and asked if I\'d do some more cars for him, and I said I would since he hooked me up in return in the past...\r\n\r\n... so I was gonna be ordering up the FETs anyways. Good timing.\r\n\r\nPrice, I just charge people $10, so the SE+tax is like $27, then shipping... call it an even $40?\r\n\r\nI grabbed the last silver Vette when I was there, but they had a bunch of blue ones. Is blue cool? If you\'d rather silver I can check online at a few other surrounding ones and see if I can find one.\r\n\r\ndave'),(29739,'bc12c51d44','I had to change the title, that misspelling got on my nerves.\r\n\r\nYou or Superfly must have said something about you guys getting together to jam or something that made me think you were still active. I get confused alot, my bad. :lol: \r\n\r\nYeah, I dig that magical pig stuff. I wish I still had the video tape of my buddy\'s band Loonacy. he used to slap and pop the fuck out of his bass, and did a lot of finger tapping too. He\'s just a big fat funny ass mexican, like your avatar with dreadlocks. He\'d be over on his side of the stage, standing in his spot, just going freaking nuts. I think you would have loved it. They were like Suicidal Tendencies meets Primus.\r\n\r\nWhen I get off my ass and put you together a CD for you, I should gather all the local shit I can. I was probably more influenced by the bands I hung out with, than anything on a label. that\'s gonna be a project though, alot of that shit is on tape, but it\'ll be good to archive them, I\'m already missing that Loonacy video, and I had a few killer demos get eaten, cause I used to play them over and over. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37668,'75e8599b13','Sorry man i am just overly excited to get this body...\r\n\r\nI wanted to know what color the thing was? I am thinking of body another race body for my car, maybe another murcielago lime green. \r\n\r\nI have a lime green one already i am just keeping it mint condition, and the one you give me is gonna be my racer...\r\n\r\nAnyways just let me know big guy\r\n\r\npeace'),(28134,'4a8dec578c','Yeah two.  I am getting a Pro chassis mailed the 18th and will see it in 7-10 buissness days. :D'),(26923,'4c63381974','It\'s a quicky week long contest, trust me, it\'s done enough, deadline is tomorrow I think.'),(34132,'2792f21c22','Allright, so my wife made me a flash Avatar.  So I uploaded it to photobucket like she normally would for hosting flash and tried both upload from a URL and upload from another site or whatever.  Not only did it not work, but it again said my signature was too long.  Now I don\'t know if you remember but it was you that got it to work like it does right now not me and I havn\'t touched it at all since then.  Think you can help me out?  Here is the link.\r\n\r\nhttp://img.photobucket.com/albums/v77/marjoke/jessesstupbitpimp.swf'),(32641,'68331bbc01','[quote:68331bbc01=\"richh\"]no, no need for tracking.  can i just send you $20?[/quote:68331bbc01]\r\n\r\n\r\nHey, you bet. Sounds good.\r\n\r\nSorry about all the PM trading....you\'re probably sayin \"just ship the damn thing already!\" :grin: \r\n\r\nYeah, give me your address and I\'ll send it out today.\r\n\r\nMy PayPal addy is.....daves@surfmk.com (verified account)\r\n\r\n---Dave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36194,'ec62d5f962','[quote:ec62d5f962=\"pimpsmurf\"]Yeah, It comes with all that that I can tell. It is literally 2 shelfs full of parts. Way too much too too list, and my camera is still in the shop. I promise that you won\'t be disapointed. There are tons of parts and spare parts. The only thing that comes to mind is the nelly. I\'ll include it, but it is fried beyond repair.\r\n\r\nThe new gearboxes and all will be here on Monday at the latest, but probably tomorrow. The chassis currently installed has a 2 cell polyquest 850mah lipo &quot;custom&quot; installed. There is a new-in-box clear chassis too, and a chassis for lithium ions if I recall. I really can\'t go though everything because it would take forever.\r\n\r\n$210 will be fine if I can ship without priority mail. It will still be insured, but will take 3-7 days (I\'m in South Carolina, btw) to get to you.\r\n\r\nLet me know man,\r\n-JNY[/quote:ec62d5f962]\r\n\r\nDamn its a deal :-o \r\n\r\nJust need to sell one of my extra cars and i should have enough doh.\r\n\r\n :eek:'),(32547,'2a127d3ecb','yep, same address.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\n\r\nrich');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32550,'69a4c79bd3','[quote:69a4c79bd3=\"Finks\"][quote:69a4c79bd3]GH Sims \r\n7815 Qyuill Point Dr. \r\nBowie, Md. 20720 \r\n[/quote:69a4c79bd3]\r\n\r\nJust double checking that this is infact your address.[/quote:69a4c79bd3]\r\n\r\n[size=18:69a4c79bd3][b:69a4c79bd3]7815 Quill Point Drive\r\nBowie, Md. 20720[/b:69a4c79bd3][/size:69a4c79bd3]\r\n\r\nWhat will be sent? As I said before the only thing missing from my order\r\nis the Van Bodies.'),(29320,'caf8f26170','[quote:caf8f26170=\"Finks\"]Awsome thanks, that\'s near perfect.  All I need now from you is your shipping info. :-)[/quote:caf8f26170]\r\n\r\nWell I sent it with the Payment but here it is again: 8-) \r\n\r\nGH Sims\r\n7815 Qyuill Point Dr.\r\nBowie, Md. 20720\r\n\r\nThanx  :cool:'),(37228,'6565cab934','Damn it!'),(26969,'cdd8c6c740','[quote:cdd8c6c740=\"HirotoR34\"]Did you send it to....\r\n\r\n132R Danforth St.\r\nPortland ME 04101 ?[/quote:cdd8c6c740]\r\n\r\nNope! I sent it where I sent your care package.....\r\n\r\nJustin Long \r\n3803 PalmTree Lane \r\nKilleen TX 76549\r\n\r\nWhen did you move ???'),(26970,'d492bd969c','[quote:d492bd969c=\"DriveWRX\"]Hey DT! What\'s up?\r\nLong time huh?\r\nMy fault. Lots happening here. I got engaged. I moved. Working on the house (painting, drywall and all that good stuff!)\r\n\r\nAnyway, as you already know, I\'m back!\r\nI really didn\'t think I\'d win anything. Surprise to me! WooHoo!\r\n\r\nMy new address:\r\n[b:d492bd969c]Vince Valderrama\r\n12519 McVickers\r\nPalos Heights, IL 60463 [/b:d492bd969c]\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n-Vince[/quote:d492bd969c]\r\n\r\nHey Vince,\r\n\r\nDid you receive your prize yet ?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28270,'1cf3ee8272','Hey bio, sorry about how my comments came out over the ram thread.  I am not angry at all that you are using this hobby to make a buck, I mean CD and Ph2t among others make cash on the side doing mods and what not for others.  My issue was that you would post work as your latest mod and then later that day it was for sale.  Also as many have noted when you started doing this it seemed that even though it was a great lay of paint that was it (and personally from a painted for resale point of view that\'s cool so that the purchaser can add the final details).  Just if you are making it just to sell, don\'t post it in flossin, just in for sale.  Far be it from me to tell you what to do actually, but just a suggestion.\r\n\r\nI loved your ultimate hummer and your Dirty MT, really great, but those were built for you and you could tell that.  Keep on pimpin out killer rides and sorry again for how I expressed my opinion.'),(37231,'6e532cb87c','I cuaght the avatar change but missed the &quot;comback&quot; reply. Thanks to hatchi I got to read it though. :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37239,'17267db555','Good job on that mrcc thing brother. Only thing that woulda made it better would have been this sentence &quot;Sessiz is awesome, barticus sucks penis monsters.&quot;  :lol:'),(27517,'4755f7fca5','Thanks man! :-)  and do they really run 30 minutes? Is tteh charger a stand alone one? how long does it take to charge? and where can I get these beauties! I really want one badly! how many , uuhh, \"steps\" is the speed? I know on the se they only have 2 speeds like fast and moderate. how much will they be american? thanks dude. Lata Playa\r\n\r\n-ibb :cool:'),(37125,'f0418b80dd','[quote:f0418b80dd=\"sessiz\"]He kinda makes ya miss charlie huh? :lol:[/quote:f0418b80dd] \r\n:lol:  exactly... I kinda hope for this shit'),(37126,'2b395332c8','Dude, you gotta find a way to add some little white jizz spurts on that avatar to go with the fleshy penis monster. :lol: \r\nAnimate a few white splooges er somefin. :-o'),(27365,'043c306d88','That\'s cool.  If I actually did something wrong there, I woulda just sucked it up and taken it.  \r\n\r\nBitPimps as a whole is second to none as far as I\'ve seen when it comes to Bit Char-G in general, except in the state of Tomy, LXX and other off brands, I don\'t know what kind of outlook to have for bits as a whole, say, by the time 2006 rolls around.  \r\nI think it depends on this: Tomy should continue their making of Super Bits or move on to a 4th generation series, like ultra mega mega bits or somesuch- that\'s the way I see it.    \r\n\r\nI\'ll keep in mind to PM you if some crazy thing happens.  I\'m working on something BIG, but I gotta keep hush-hush about it until I can make a rough prototype, but it could be a big contribution unless it\'s been done right already.\r\n\r\nCool headed moderators are best for any situation in my opionion.  Same thing in real life, a manager with a good additude is awesome compared to one with a bad attitude.\r\n\r\nTo sum it up, like someone once said here in the forums, \r\n\"it\'s all good in the hood\"!\r\nOh, and uh, keep up those sweet custom jobs- \"they is kickass for real, yo\".\r\nLate,\r\nAbe');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35943,'dded3741e4','Does the Xmod PCB handle 6 cells? Or do I need some sort of a fet?\r\n\r\nSorry if this question is really obvious or whatever. I am lookin over the Xmod discussion forum as I type to you.'),(29994,'51178dd397','if yah google ho slot cars you might be able to find better deals or maybe ebay but i got a few quick links for yah.........\r\n[url]http://www.ncphobbies.com/cgi-bin/vcat/CatalogMgr.pl?cartID=b-2753&amp;SearchField=partnumber&amp;SearchFor=LIF934&amp;template=Htx/164slotcar3.htx&amp;hdr=Thank+You+For+Shopping&amp;displayNumber=1[/url]\r\n\r\n\r\nthat is a bare chassis similar to one of mine where i ripped the rear end outta.\r\nfor axles their are things like these that you need the crown gears for\r\n[url]http://www.ncphobbies.com/cgi-bin/vcat/CatalogMgr.pl?cartID=b-2753&amp;SearchField=partnumber&amp;SearchFor=AML555&amp;template=Htx/164slotcar3.htx&amp;hdr=Thank+You+For+Shopping&amp;displayNumber=1[/url]\r\n[url]http://www.ncphobbies.com/cgi-bin/vcat/CatalogMgr.pl?cartID=b-2753&amp;SearchField=partnumber&amp;SearchFor=AML554&amp;template=Htx/164slotcar3.htx&amp;hdr=Thank+You+For+Shopping&amp;displayNumber=1[/url]\r\n\r\nthen u can get endless amounts of rims including alloy\r\n\r\ni use the rims and tires for my fast cars because they are made of silicon or foam\r\n[img:51178dd397]http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y102/Civicsr2cool/zzlipoly13.jpg[/img:51178dd397]'),(35384,'d96223b11f','Hey I am going to send you my ZZMT if you can could you tri cell it for me too I am getting a li-po pack but not for a few weeks I don\'t have pay-pal so if you can send me your address I can shoot you the cASH AND zzmt AT THE SAMETIME.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35396,'a555e3e437','[quote:a555e3e437=\"cj\"][quote:a555e3e437=\"Clint\"]Hey,  sorry was away a few days.\r\n\r\nI paypalled you 71$ for a silver kit, mustang clip, and an extra set of rear axles.\r\n\r\n-Cancel the extra set of rear axles\r\n-Add in the set of the front dogbones.\r\n-I still want the mustang clip. \r\n-I would like to add a silver diff for the car.\r\n\r\njust lemme know how much to paypal.\r\n\r\n-Clint[/quote:a555e3e437]\r\n\r\nAdding the Diff and the clip you are looking at $21.00 more.[/quote:a555e3e437]\r\n\r\nThanks..\r\n21$ sent via paypal.'),(27377,'6d95bfa923','Please DON\'T anything about that site in the UK, yet! I\'m sure it\'s the same place that I\'m preparing to order from. I\'ll have mine in today. I just don\'t want them to run out of the things that I want before I get mine in.\r\n\r\nI\'ve actually seen the Gallup cars in a mall near me. The Mini bodies look pretty darn good for being a clone and all. You can search the forums here and find out more about them.\r\n\r\nLater bro.'),(31024,'eb0ca4f41c','I\'ve seen him on the board here a bunch since, he might have forgotten!\r\n\r\nI\'m gonna PM him here, and we\'ll get it rollin\'.....\r\n\r\nNow, you want a car, right? Do you have a controller?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Motor');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29472,'f3e8ad79f3','[quote:f3e8ad79f3=\"stagg\"]For some reason it\'s not workin.  Its the .. All files uploaded, then could not be uploaded.[/quote:f3e8ad79f3]Try it now, you should be all set.\r\nLet me know if you have any more troubles.'),(37856,'b511e68d8c','No prob, I\'ve got plenty of micro stuff from skylinekid to keep me busy....thanks again! :-)'),(34766,'3f5eb902ac','It\'s a wedding man.  My sister in law is getting hitched to a Merican :grin:   I\'ll give you a ring for sure.  No idea what my scedual will be but here is my Cell # 207-551-9773  I\'ll call you when I get down there Sat, will be there from Sat-Sat so a whole friggin week.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nJesse (aka Finks)'),(32648,'d535344e6c','Sorry man. I just looked at that PM i sent ya.\r\n\r\nIt made a link or something, and looked funny. \r\n\r\n\r\nJust so there\'s no confusion, the PP addy is:\r\n\r\n\r\ndaves@surfmk.com\r\n\r\nforget the \"is.......\" or whatever in the last PM.\r\n\r\n\r\n--Dave'),(33845,'b34aef8d9e','[quote:b34aef8d9e=\"sessiz\"]Did you get the rims yet man? Cuase I got your package and shit man thanks. I now have a shit load of bats to add to my shitload of bats. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'ve checked the usps site and it\'s yet to be updated. It\'s kinda weird that this package came here so quickly. :???: \r\n\r\nShoot me a pm when ya get the rims. :-)[/quote:b34aef8d9e]\r\n\r\nWell have not gotten the rims yet so prob Monday as the mail has already run. sorry about the bat thing didnt know you had a crap load already hope you can use the bodies! \r\n\r\nI will PM you as soon as the rims come in!  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33005,'b7b1faee4a','Just received your package from the micro hookup!\r\nThanks man, sub rocks hard and the mini is awesome.\r\n\r\nCheers bro.'),(37909,'c7b633d9de','I think I\'ll give myself a quick skoolin on premiere....I\'ll get back to you soon.\r\nThanks for the advice :-o'),(27804,'4b93b0a644','I guess I\'m not allowed over anymore or something? :-( \r\n\r\nI ordered the bodies today from DBR.'),(27526,'44c0e7917b','I\'l holla atcha later   8-)'),(28916,'8b87b2f8a3','No matter when it arrives,I\'d just like you to send me your account number,and I could send you your money.It takes 3 days to the money to get there,so I wouldn\'t have this toll on me and on you either.\r\n\r\nI do thank for your help and I hope I can still count on you.'),(27407,'118786330a','I haven\'t told anyone about the UK site, and all I ordered was the Trueno pullback.  There should still be one in stock but it was so fucking expensive.  I won\'t be ordering from them anymore, since I have most everything else of value already.  Ya know, it would\'ve been 43$ if I got the Gloria bodykit with my order!\r\n\r\nI guess in the meantime I can pay attention to the cars that come through my local bimart, biglots, and wallgreens stores.  I could use another impreza WRX body, and if I run up against the Panther Gloria \"BMW M3\" clone out there, I\'m so getting that.  I\'m sure you\'ve seen it?\r\n\r\nLate,\r\nAbe'),(27408,'0be5885c4f','http://anytoys.co.uk/category_info.php/category_id/57\r\n\r\nIt\'s anytoys UK, right?  I checked, and shit, I did get the last Trueno.  But not to worry.  I\'m working on a way to fix all that.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27886,'de62bae485','ok i sent the jota shell about 10 min ago pirotity mail , let me know when it arives , later . \r\n\r\n\r\nmatt'),(35050,'0c5235fce9','Right now I have three Xmods (all Gen 1\'s) I am getting an Iwaver 02 for Christmas. Mini Z\'s are great, but kinda pricey....I haven\'t tried the New Evolution Xmods, but have heard some good (and bad) about them.'),(27844,'199a0d17f3','i jsut traded hiroto34 a bit shell for some . i wish i new you had some otherwise id have had you throw them in with the motors ... next time im looking for some ( geting another xmod next month  ) i\'ll pm you . \r\n\r\nps: the stage 2 kicks major ass !'),(27776,'98ffb19ded','I was thinking taking one body and making an extender, like in a real limo.  My sister had an ex-boyfriend that had a stretched Chrysler LHS, and it\'s the same way, but two bit chassis\'s would have to serve as one for it to work.  The motor/heatsink/gears/axle come out of the front and the suspension/steering assembly comes out the back, and both bits would run on say, 45mhz or something.  The extension could be fabricated out of scratch stryofoam (look in my thread about a caterham dreamkit and you\'ll see what I mean) and then a mold could be cast and you just superglue everything proper.  From there it\'s just choosing gears, batteries, motors, suspenion, heatsink, and nice tires.  The idea drawn out looks much better.\r\n\r\nI don\'t have any plans laid out for the sprinter at the moment.  I like how the hood comes off though :grin: \r\nWell, keep in touch.  Gotta go, the buzz from my bro\'s bud is killing me.\r\nSmoke on,\r\nAbe  :cool:'),(33136,'a0761bee73','I\'m hoping your allright.\r\n\r\n :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35833,'faf43f0f44','[quote:faf43f0f44=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Can you move this to the dumpster?\r\nI renamed it so that it can go there and simmer for a while.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=83743#83743\r\n\r\nA couple of pimps have the game  :-o \r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx[/quote:faf43f0f44]\r\n\r\nno problem. done.'),(36082,'57eeaddc88','Very nice track. :D. Did you try the setup yet on it? Oh yeah, I was looking through your pictures of Microsizers and I saw the Orange Beast Skyline. I was wondering what rims those were. http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7031 they are real nice haha. Could I have them?  :grin:'),(35835,'e74a310eb7','Sweet..just let me know right now my stuff is all over the map, but i will start putting aside some things you like...\r\n\r\nkeep me posted bud'),(37674,'29b7635bd4','How much do you want for the two 27mhz chassis?'),(37676,'445bc75d49','Just the chassis no controllers?\r\n\r\nnot sure what is reasonable thats why i left the offers open, just hoping to be happy for what i let the loose for.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36686,'b4eb0f7b35','The red steering rod makes the turning better right? A little sharper correct?'),(36140,'22f11ff9c8','http://www.atomicmods.com/ProductInfo.aspx?productid=10142 this one, I loved this motor. Add a red gear and you\'ll be really happy haha. Atomicmods also ships internationally.'),(35854,'977840428d','So we gotta deal as follows:\r\n\r\nbearings/carbon fiber drive shaft/alloy front and rear shafts\r\n\r\nfor the \r\n\r\nSkyline body, Perfection chassis and controller, the Ferrari F50 body, the Countach body\r\n\r\nWhen you are ready I will give you my shippin info...'),(27501,'ac080681c1','The metl Tech cars run for 30 mins on one charge. The steering &amp; speed is truly proportional (about 21 steps) .Team Bonzer has a little vid of the steering on www.bonzergear.com . They are fast. Maybe not as fast as a bit with a 4.2 motor but they are alot more controlable around corners. My only quibble is the controller which I don\'t like much. If they could make a more standard controller (not that difficult to do) then these things would be perfect.\r\n\r\nI have a vid in my gallery (yakboys gallery) of me racing one of the BMW\'s (very badly), The controller is hindering me a bit with correcting mistakes as you can see (I can get around my course easily with bits).\r\n\r\nIf you want specific photo\'s let me know but bonzer has good pics on his site'),(28892,'a666fd5c49','49mhz please. Thanks very much.\r\n\r\nSimon');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27762,'0a7449d1a8','Didn\'t go Nitro ....yet..  :wink:   I have two T\'s now from the spare parts of the other one and 4 epochs.  I got that sweet deal : 3 cars (2 full kits and 1 standalone) and $25 worth of parts for $100. My car is actually on another website I have not been able to upload any pics.  the website is [url]http://www.ultimaterc.com/gallery/d...e.php?pos=-1727[/url]\r\n\r\nAll the specs are there .\r\n\r\nTake care man.'),(30786,'0aab46e360','ok swg i should be able to send the reciver tomorow , if i cant i\'ll let you know but it should get sent tomorow . sory for the wait its been a busy week .'),(27764,'c61dcf858c','Don\'t forget to call me if you get time to play a little.:cool: \r\n\r\nI gotta get out of this house sometime.  :driving:\r\n\r\nI broke the damn pull start on the XXX today. :-( \r\n\r\nGotta figure out how to fix it. :???:\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit:  Since you didn\'t get this yet.  I ordered the \'02 and \'04.  I asked if he has a Merc around for ya.\r\n\r\nI also contacted Dogdude about the bodies.  Waiting on reply. :-)'),(37729,'f02e3835a3','[quote:f02e3835a3=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:f02e3835a3=\"ph2t\"]not feeling paranoid or anything, lol, but could you do me a fave and wipe this thread?\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7370\r\n\r\nit would be mega kiss your arse appreciated, lol...\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:f02e3835a3]\r\nIt\'s dead. You can take off your foil hat now. :lol:[/quote:f02e3835a3]\r\n\r\nlol, as you can see, I have MANY uses for foil.........\r\n\r\nthanks mate....');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35444,'e7e88da852','[quote:e7e88da852=\"Bithigh707\"]Yo Cuzz I am not tring to play anybody for a car I can bye all I remember getting a PM stating one thing I am not trippin like that and sorry if you think I am tring to run game I\'ve been thru to much and to old for that shit and I had the cash to pay for that car[/quote:e7e88da852]\r\nAlright, I\'ll take your word for it (that you\'re not trying to play anyone for a car).\r\nBut honestly, do you remember why that car went back on the auction block?\r\nI do, so do all the moderators. It wasn\'t because we wanted to give it to someone else or something. Simply it was because we did not receive any money for that car from you.\r\nYou can partially confirm this by looking in the \"bitPimps Auction Block\". I believe the 6th post down is the post where the car went back on the auction block.\r\nWe didn\'t mention the exact reason to the rest of the forum members because we didn\'t want it to sound like we were \"calling anyone out\".\r\nBut the fact remains, that car went back on the auction block because it was never paid for.\r\n\r\nI imagine you probably spoke to DarkTari (I\'m guessing here, could be wrong) at the time, as he made that particular ride.\r\nI\'m not sure what exact words he used to explain it to you, but you definitely were made aware that the car was going back on the auction block.\r\n\r\nI guess the point I\'m trying to make is this.\r\nbitPimps doesn\'t owe you anything. You never paid for a car, therefore we never sent you a car.\r\nI\'m sure the Auction Block will open back up at some point, at that time you are free to bid on whatever. If you win, and pay, you get the car - simple.'),(27761,'8e09f8da14','[quote:8e09f8da14=\"codesuidae\"]Cool, looks good.\r\n\r\nGo ahead and do the MOSFET one too if you like.  When I wrote it I intentionally did not give a \'recipe\' style description, in an effort to get people to really read and understand the material before attempting the mod themselves.  Its a little harder to understand, but serves to discourage people without the necessary skills screwing up their cars.[/quote:8e09f8da14]I hear ya man. I really liked how you broke up your article and gave clear directions and explination. Writing tutorials is an art. I gather with your technical background, documentation is a large part of your job.\r\nThanks for putting stuff like that together to help the rest of us.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31820,'77dda6dea6','DT &amp; P,\r\n\r\nSending this to both of you...\r\n\r\nMan, you\'re both telling me the same thing: \"If he still wants it, let him have it, and I\'ll try to find another one. If he doesn\'t want it, then I still want it...\" Something like that anyway. Can you two \"talk\" to each other and figure it out? Otherwise, I\'m going to have to do something really dumb like \"pick a number...\"\r\n\r\nMan, I messed this up.'),(31821,'79d12c669b','LMAO...... It happens man.  I\'ll send him a PM and see what\'s up.\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks dude.\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(27514,'3f105fcd32','What up? Did you get your audi yet? I ended up moving back to Maine, and called my brother in Texas. He said I got one package, but didn\'t say what it was. If you\'re still in it, send me a pm.'),(27520,'b0d6e240a9','Hi, Charger is a stand alone one &amp; a display case !!. Takes about 30 mins to charge fully. The speed is truly proportional doesn\'t seem to go in steps. As regards getting hold of one, they aren\'t avaliable yet. I was lucky &amp; got some preproduction samples and have been providing a bit of feedback to Ken at XXAPS. I know when launche alot more body styles will be avaliable &amp; I\'m hoping they produce a better controller for us racing types. I think if hey get this righ hey will be the next big thing ! :eek:'),(27523,'c562e3aace','[b:c562e3aace]Nah, I\'m good. I found the Trueno pullback at a [b]British site[/b:c562e3aace], and got the last one. It should be here in a week. [/b]\r\n\r\nWhat\'s the site ?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30358,'48bd5453ba','Where did you get your JMK camera / transmitter / receiver?  About how much did it cost?\r\n\r\nIt looks cool.  Is the picture quality and transmission range ok?'),(29160,'f0d6e0bb03','Cool, I can get them shipped out tomorrow.  \r\n\r\nHey, no problem.  It\'s the least I can do for having you guys put up with me.  I am cleaning out my R/C stuff right now, so anything un-opened that I think you guys would get use out of, I will send you a PM and ship them on out.\r\n\r\nThanks alot,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(28524,'2f495d675d','Yep I was talking about any 1/64 scale diecast cars. I am sure we can work out a deal when you are ready to have your car painted. By the way I didn\'t get the package yet, I am sure it will show up tomorrow.'),(29448,'4a5b5af742','[quote:4a5b5af742=\"ezenterprises\"]Well , minus the shit that doesnt work right or whatever.... can you order me 1 of each in blue( 2wd and 4wd )..... I can send you a down payment, and then buy stuff like every week till ive bought it all from you. Just let me know when u get the blue stuff in... Thanks.[/quote:4a5b5af742]\r\n\r\nI can place the order this week you are looking at about $162.88 + $4.00 S&amp;h.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com.  It could take 3 weeks or more to get you the first parts.  I woun\'t know what they can send me first untill I place the order.'),(27927,'9aa4e4a38d','yeah, cool. i\'d like some. thank you.\r\nD. Yenin \r\n8201 4 ave. apt.1F\r\nBrooklyn, N.Y. 11209');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27969,'6b857efc2c','Will do- hey, check out the thread I made on Goodwill.  Some interesting shit\'s been coming through there lately.\r\nLate,\r\nAbe'),(28912,'4387990b13','If you have a problem,just tell me:\r\ne.g. if you don wanna send them to me or you don wanna tell me your bank acoount number,I understand you.\r\nBut those cars would be important 2 me,and I thought we could arrange it in 2 days. \r\n\r\nI\'d send you the money if I had your number(and the price),but I cant.\r\n\r\nSo how about it?'),(28865,'5c3381c0f8','Spaten Optimator bitch....'),(30393,'e4904711ea','Hey man, that looks like it\'s going to be a real nice looking shell. I\'d like to propose a little trade... I\'m a graphic designer/photographer, and if you send me a small handfull of those, I\'ll take some really nice photographs of them for use on your web site. Check out my gallery to see my photography style... if you like what you see, then let\'s do it. I\'ll make that thing look like a million bucks, and it\'ll only cost ya a small quantity of bodies and a little shipping.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(29702,'47134b097d','I\'ve been reading up on Los Lonely Boys. Here\'s an article from there home town paper that\'s pretty gushy, but has lots of background info.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.austinchronicle.com/issues/dispatch/2003-08-01/music_feature.html\r\n\r\nThey are actually self taught and don\'t read any music. Obviously being brothers that growing up jamming together has everything to do with the way they naturally vibe together. After hearing some of their studio tracks, I decided they\'re not really my type, but it was a pleasure to watch them jam live. They are incredibly talented, and it\'s great the way the three of them can sing harmonies while playing.\r\n\r\nYou just reminded me I need to go check out Guster. I really liked them. They were kinda strange, I like that.\r\n\r\nIf you get a chance, check out the new Gorrillaz, Demon Days. I\'m really liking it, though it is kinda up and down.\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31836,'074203567e','Ok Steve, DT says you guys worked it out, and it\'s his. Sorry dude. I tell you what, I got some other bits I\'m going to unload pretty soon. I\'ll give you first crack at em. Unfortunately, I don\'t have any more of the Lupin III sets. I think I got a Trueno pullback or two. Well, I\'ve got like six, but I\'m only going to hang on to a few of them. I might have a couple of Gloria bodies too. Anyway, I\'ll hit you back in a week or so.\r\n\r\nThanks for being cool.'),(35342,'6b0d6593c3','Wazzup!!\r\n\r\nYeah man, I just started working for RS a few weeks ago. I will try to find out about the display guide. My manager knows I am into the zaps would most likely hook me up with one if we have some laying around. I will see what I can do tomorrow when I get there.\r\n\r\nLater Pimp!!!'),(28861,'d4921110b4','So if I understand you,you wanna give micro rc\'s as a gift?\r\n\r\nI don\'t understand the money-stuff, will you give me a bank-account number,and so I can send you the money? \r\n\r\n(In Hungary the Paypal doesn\'t work,this is why I need a bank-account number,where to send the money.)\r\n\r\nI was advised to not to send money to someone unknown,but I\'d really like those cars. What makes sure I\'m not gonna be fooled?\r\n\r\nJust tell me how much it costs and will decide.'),(28862,'0ef735a715','Well if you want I can send you my eBay name I have a lot of feedback and am an honest seller! http://cgi3.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewUserPage&amp;userid=steelwoolghandi\r\n\r\nAlso you aske me about the ZZMT\'s I was just going to send you some cars free even pay the shipping (ya a gift) does that sound like someone dishonest? If you dont wish to send me the money for the ZZMT\'s thats fine I will still send you some Micro RC\'s as a gift free of charge as I think you would mod them well!\r\n\r\ntalk with ya later');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28858,'2b44474362','Hi well I was just going to send you some extra RC cars I have I dont have any extra ZZMT If you send me a money order I can get you 2 of them with the motor kits and tire kits and I will pick up the freight cost. and I will still send you some extra micro RC cars as I have some sitting around and I am not doing anything with them. \r\n\r\nIf you wish for me to buy the ZZMT I will just charge you what it cost to get them as I dont wish to make any money off the deal. I like to encourage people to mod RC\'s and you look to have some real tallent I cant wait to see what you do with more RC cars!\r\n\r\nLet me know what you want me to do and I will send an address to send the money for the ZZMT\'s and send them to you. and since I am paying for the cost of freight I will probable send parcel post as its cheaper but it can take sometimes 6 weeks to get to you. (not always but sometimes). \r\n\r\ntake care,\r\nAaron\r\nsteelwoolghandi (from Texas)\r\n\r\nOh and if you get a chance I am an admin at http://ripper7racing.com/forums/index.php?act=idx\r\ncome over and take a look we are pals with bitpimps'),(28525,'b816d188be','WHAT? dude it should have been there by now,  what was this the 3rd day?\r\nAlright I\'ll see if I can track it and let ya know.\r\nEDIT: alright it is insured, and I have the receipt so if You don\'t get it tomorrow I\'ll contact the post office and see if they are sending it to the right address and all that, etc, but Yea it should come tomorrw.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28533,'0ec23ca9d7','Hey, \r\nJust checking to see if you got the package yet, it\'s coming in a brown padded envelope, but if you don\'t get it, have you checked like your door or front step/proch or whatever to see if you got a parcel pick-up slip, maybe the post office has it, but if you didn\'t get it today, I\'ll run over to the post office tomorrow and see what the heck is going on.\r\nKorey'),(32742,'eecc57bf74','[quote:eecc57bf74=\"sessiz\"]Yeah, just call me mommy. :-)[/quote:eecc57bf74]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n :-x  :lol:'),(27995,'d2ac113cf2','[quote:d2ac113cf2=\"blindrider3\"]Hey DT I found this on ebay and thought you might be interested. http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5956572263&amp;rd=1[/quote:d2ac113cf2]\r\n\r\nOh yeah, I saw it when it first hit the block.  One of our fellow Pimps is goin for it so I\'ll get the next one.  I out bidded for the last oneso I told him I won\'t bid on the next.  But after this one, the floor\'s open! 8-)'),(27996,'f07ab2e5ad','[quote:f07ab2e5ad=\"blindrider3\"]Hey DT I found this on ebay and thought you might be interested. http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=2565&amp;item=5956572263&amp;rd=1[/quote:f07ab2e5ad]\r\n\r\nPS.\r\n\r\nThanx for look\'n out  :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28001,'44ff53962c','got the wheel locks , thanks. they look and work great . got a qestion though what brand are they ,or are they just standard 2mm alloy nuts ? it donest realy matter but id like to know for when i finish my xmod and post the specs . have you goten the jota shell yet ? i cant wait to see what you do with it . \r\n\r\nmatt'),(28029,'9b54c49815','Hey,  I saw that you are selling your Mamba Xmod.  I am VERY interested in the Mini-X reciever, as well as the Mamba 6800 Combo.  How much you want for each one, and how much for both together?  \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(28030,'57abac052c','[quote:57abac052c=\"Mazda787b\"]Hey,  I saw that you are selling your Mamba Xmod.  I am VERY interested in the Mini-X reciever, as well as the Mamba 6800 Combo.  How much you want for each one, and how much for both together?  \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMazda[/quote:57abac052c]\r\n\r\nMazda:\r\n\r\nThere\'s a deal pending for the whole car, so I\'m not going to part it out.  RCMart has the receiver and www.b-p-p.com has a 6800/ESC combo for 110.  You dropping one in a Mini-T?  Once I sell some the stuf I\'m getting in trade I\'m going with an 8000 and a 3s li-po pack into my RC18T that\'s STILL on backorder at Tower for almost a month when they claimed it\'d be a week. :x \r\n\r\n-Max'),(28013,'6a001e505d','No problem I\'m always here to help a fello pimp out :grin:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28026,'9b54c49815','Hey,  I saw that you are selling your Mamba Xmod.  I am VERY interested in the Mini-X reciever, as well as the Mamba 6800 Combo.  How much you want for each one, and how much for both together?  \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMazda'),(28062,'d25cca1a7b','My dad already said no to the paypal idea. That\'s why i use moneyorders.\r\n\r\nI\'ve even ordered from Tower hobbies with them. So It\'s completely up to you. I can send it express if you want. I already know that you can get someone else to buy the stuff using paypal so it your choice.\r\n\r\nIf you\'ll let me use the MO i\'ll need your name and address so that no one but YOU can cash it.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(28493,'92a3a7aa10','FYI Here is the confirmation number from usps 03043490000019673533'),(28494,'751419b866','jump in the chat'),(28065,'fb555abf02','Great!  Thanks for the heads up!\r\n\r\n\r\n-Mazda'),(28164,'13b03239b0','[quote:13b03239b0=\"hue35\"]Heh... I actually haven\'t finish that car yet. It\'s the same shot as before (faked decals and color), only I blacked out the windows, too... ya know, somethin\' special for the big contest.\r\n\r\nI stopped by BitPims yesterday for the first time in at least a few weeks (probly more)... I read Cabo\'s post about the rcmod dude\'s proposition. It rubbed me wrong, so I figured I piss on his contest with a faked entry that would stir up some shit. Beat the admin?... who the fuck is he? I\'ll beat \'im with a ratchet![/quote:13b03239b0]You fucker. (get it?) \r\n\r\nNo but really though, you fucker, I fell for that shit. :lol: \r\n\r\nYeah, RCMOd has always irritated the fuck out of me, it pained me to register there to win that last contest, but I really wanted that Calsonic Skyline. I need a 45mhz bit controller. :lol: \r\n\r\nNow that POS better send me my shit soon or I\'m gonna flame the shit out of their forums. It\'s already been over 2 weeks, then I heard how they took 7 months to send betty.k his prize last year, and I was like fuck, it would have just been easier to snag a bit off of ebay.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:13b03239b0]As far as the music tradin\' is concerned, I\'ve got some mp3\'s (stuff I\'ve downloaded), but all of my cds are ripped as AAC (mp4) files... can you play those? I\'ve been listening to some NOFX lately... it was the last torrent I nabbed... I\'m pretty sure it\'s a fairly complete discography. COOL SHIT! A bit the same song to song, but when I\'m in that mood, it\'s perfect. I\'d love to hear the spinoff band... plus, I\'m all for complete discographies in the mp3 format... makes for a great archive and sampler. That way I can hear it all and buy my favorite nugget or two, if I dig it enough. Sometimes, the compressed version is enough. I managed to grab about 40-50GB of stuff via torrents... almost all of that stuff is mp3, plus I have a ton of progressive rock from a buddy that\'s all mp3 format. So, if you can\'t play the AAC\'s, then I still have a ton of stuff you might be interested in.[/quote:13b03239b0]I don\'t know about the mp4s. I know I have music jukeboxes that support it. (I\'m pretty sure Quicktime Pro does if anything), but I doubt I can play those on my DVD player. I\'ll have to experiment to see if I can convert them.\r\n\r\nThat\'s my thing lately, MP3 CDs. When we got the PS2, I hijacked the DVD player and hooked it up in the bedroom. I always had all my shit archived in mp3 CDs, but never listened to them. Now it great, because I throw one in my DVD player, and I\'m rocking all night, and the next day too. Those one I snagged the torrents of, are great, like like you said, they are wonderfully organized, complete with cover art and everything. Now if companies would offer discographies, organized like that, and available for download at a reasonable price, I actually pay for that shit. Personally, I think what they\'re charging to download an album from legitimate places is too much. I mean what the hell, there\'s no packing material involved, no shipping involved, much smaller staffing at the retailers, so you know they\'re gouging you for bigger profits.\r\n\r\nAnyways, sorry, I get pissed about the state of music now days. Overpriced mass produced BS is what most of it is.\r\n\r\nI\'m not really a big fan of NOFX. I think they are the band that started the trend with that same constant freakin beat through the whole album, gets on my nerves, but they do have some funny songs, and I dig their ska songs. I think they\'re also one of the bands that helped bring about the little ska punk thing we had going on in the 90s.\r\n\r\nI guess MFatGGs is kinda similar, same constant beats, with the occasional ska song thrown in, but listening to the them tear through Somewhere Over The Rainbow, Rocket Man, Nothing Compares 2 U, Puff the Magic Dragon, The Boxer, Country Roads, Fire and Rain, Cheers Theme, Me and Julio, Don\'t Cry For me Argentina, and just about any other song you can imagine, that should not be punk, is just mind numbing. It\'s seems so wrong, but when you hear it, you say how can something so right be wrong?\r\n\r\nCool album is Ruin Johnnies Bar Mitfa (sp?). It sounds as if, or they give the illusion that they are playing a Bar Mitfa, and besides the traditional songs, they do some of their worst (best?) covers yet. Stairway to heaven anyone?\r\n\r\nI\'ll have to hook you up with that.\r\n\r\nDave'),(28142,'96a8239153','ok i\'ll send all $65 maybe monday i\'ll send it express.\r\nI\'ll send the shipping address in the envelope\r\n\r\nNice doing business with you (i hope).\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28143,'df0e4122fd','Hopefully I will still be here when you get back. I ain\'t smokin\', but I\'m drinkin and want to kick it in chat or some shit.'),(28455,'6d355c35d7','You know that\'s why I love you man, we hate the same shit. :lol: \r\n\r\nYeah I\'ll tell ya, he strikes me as being a bit ignorant, and he irks me at times too. Frustrates me that one of own mods don\'t even know how to post in the right forum half the time.\r\n\r\nHere\'s what really got me irked. I\'ve done about a half dozen FET mods for him, and asked for nothing, because he\'s a fellow pimp. Well most people are so appreciative for only charging $10 a mod, they send me more money, Bit Char-Gs, and all kinds of other cool stuff. What does DT hook me up with? Some bodies that he botched, and I brought back from the dead, beetle body set, perfection 3.0 and a 3.0 Lucifer rotor. yay.\r\n...and at the very same time he was posting his collection of unopened stuff. It was like I really didn\'t expect anything, because I didn\'t ask for anything, but when he said was gonna hook me up, I thought he was gonna hook me up! God knows he could\'ve.\r\n\r\nThen when we\'re doing those auctions he was having me do FET mods in exchange for the Precious chassis, even after I stated that I would rather use the Charg-N-Go\'s I can get at Walgreens. All the damn Precious chassis had jacked up rear ends, and out of the 6 I got in exchange for 6 FET mods, only 3 were usable enough to auction off.\r\n\r\nSo I\'m feeling like the guy kinda owes me, then he just starts sending everyone else free shit. When me and sessiz bitched how broke we were (and I actually started it), he sent Sessiz 3 MS speed sets, and a couple Precious cars. I only know that because because sessiz was pimp enough to think of me, and he sent me 2 of the speed sets. Since he was so cool, I\'m sending one back FET modded and painted.\r\n\r\n\r\n... and what he pulled on you was BS. Me and everyone else was pushing for your prize, that was a cool ass prize, but DT resisted, why? because he knew it was cool and he had to run the show. I had a feeling that was part of the reason you backed away too.\r\n\r\nAnd as far as the ebay auctions, read seeberg\'s thread about his holy grail thingy, you\'ll see hiroto and others were backing down to DT. He\'s greedy I tell you. Superfly called you the hoarder, but I think it\'s really DT.\r\n\r\nOh and one more little bitch before I\'m done, you realize that DT emails RS and everyone else about bitPimps, trying to promote us. There\'s 2 things about that. Do we really want this mofo to represent us? And why else do you think that companies steal our ideas. Like how Toyeast ripped my Cali beetle, 1/64th Homies, and RS integrated the voltage bypass into newer PCBs. Yeah they\'re watching us, and DT is leading the way. \r\n\r\nSo anyways, please, please don\'t leave me alone with him, I got Hiroto teaming with Finks on one side, DT on the other, I need someone here to always say what I wanted to say. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave'),(28459,'fce4465912','Cool, cool. \r\n\r\nI totally noticed the hits to his gallery, and here what you\'re saying about him promoting himself, and not us so much. As far as the companies go, yeah, it is flattering they pay attention. I\'m just saying, alot of these companies get a 1001 emails from dipshits, so you can imagine how he\'s making us look. At least that\'s the way I\'m seeing it.\r\n\r\nYeah, my address:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd. #1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\nhey shoot me yours too, i want to send you a couple MP3 cds. Have you heard Dillinger Escape Plan? Interested in 700mb of punkabilly and a Man or Astroman album?\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (28464,'7d6276303f','Hey Man,\r\nI could not ship out today due to the fact that I got to the post office to late, I got there around 1:30 and I know there open on saturdays, maybe they just close early, but I will be shipping out monday, and it should only take a couple days to get to You.\r\nTalk to Ya later'),(28467,'50f4c69cd6','No problem on shipping it out Monday, I was able to ship yours out today they told me you should receive it Tuesday'),(28468,'50f4c69cd6','No problem on shipping it out Monday, I was able to ship yours out today they told me you should receive it Tuesday'),(28469,'2a4fb96282','Alright so shipping to each other is around three days, so if I ship out Mon morning it should get to you Weds or thurs, Thanks though for shipping out today, which car did You end up sending, the 49 or 27 mhz?\r\nThanks'),(28470,'2a4fb96282','Alright so shipping to each other is around three days, so if I ship out Mon morning it should get to you Weds or thurs, Thanks though for shipping out today, which car did You end up sending, the 49 or 27 mhz?\r\nThanks'),(28471,'92ecc93f07','I had to send you he 27 because something was wrong with the 49. both of the cars were brand new too. I have had a couple of new cars not work.  You would think after they have made a couple of million of these cars the would get it right.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27565,'a0c1ed39ea','Well, can you give me the e-mail address to Ken? I have some questions to ask him. Very important stuff. I already asked some other duded but he just sent me \"theyre not available yet.\" And that was it. Thanks man. Later\r\n\r\n-ibb :eek:'),(27566,'47e7aa389d','It\'s ken@xxaps.com.'),(27569,'825516de9a','Fucking shit.  Thanks!  Is that towerhobbies site really selling that shit for that cheap?  \'Cause I might just get one of everything they have if that\'s the case.\r\n\r\nDamn, I wish I had more cash so I\'d have some serious shit ordered by the time you read this.  I\'m sure I can wait a week.  You scored the motherfucking jackpock.  If there\'s anything you need, just holla down my way.  Respek Nuckles!\r\n\r\nLate,\r\nAbe'),(27570,'7dabf88d12','[quote:7dabf88d12=\"seeberg\"]Fucking shit.  Thanks!  [b:7dabf88d12]Is that towerhobbies site really selling that shit for that cheap?[/b:7dabf88d12]  \'Cause I might just get one of everything they have if that\'s the case.\r\n\r\nDamn, I wish I had more cash so I\'d have some serious shit ordered by the time you read this.  I\'m sure I can wait a week.  You scored the motherfucking jackpock.  If there\'s anything you need, just holla down my way.  Respek Nuckles!\r\n\r\nLate,\r\nAbe[/quote:7dabf88d12]\r\n\r\n[quote:7dabf88d12]Is that towerhobbies site really selling that shit for that cheap?[/quote:7dabf88d12]\r\nOh yeah!,  They\'re clearing out all the 1:64 shit, they only carried Hobbico products so it\'s da real deal man!\r\n\r\nNo Problem Pimp !  You missed this one, it was posted back in October:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=4774\r\n\r\nWhen I 1st read the post, same day I ordered 9 for around $25.00 incl shipping, then I ordered 9 more plus a whole lotta other shit.  \r\nTRU is clearing out Body, Hop-Up &amp; Tune-Up and Maintenance kits for .89  so check them out.  Look in the 70% clearance basket'),(27571,'8024f24dce','[quote:8024f24dce]In the meantime, I\'ll keep my eyes on toyeast for parts and toyrus for a kit. [b:8024f24dce]I\'m gonna get a friend of mine for his 21st b-day[/b:8024f24dce].[/quote:8024f24dce]\r\n\r\nNow you can order a couple Speed Sets from Tower and spend $5.00 !!!!\r\nIf you do that and need a Tx for it, let me know, I have a shit load of 49hz, I\'ll send you however many you want.  8-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35942,'7cf5e32ee0','Is there anything you could trade for the body?'),(28007,'44ff53962c','got the wheel locks , thanks. they look and work great . got a qestion though what brand are they ,or are they just standard 2mm alloy nuts ? it donest realy matter but id like to know for when i finish my xmod and post the specs . have you goten the jota shell yet ? i cant wait to see what you do with it . \r\n\r\nmatt'),(27916,'13df5282c3','Later?\r\n\r\ncall me, i\'ll bring that shit over.\r\n\r\nor your ass can come get it. :???:'),(29755,'a84950498c','Your giving them out free? \r\nI can give you my addy, but I\'d prefer thru Email if thats okay with you.\r\nIf not, I\'ll just send it through here.'),(29756,'f98b0c4e54','you can email me at this email, your addy,\r\nsuperpieboy@yahoo.com\r\ni will have to cast one for you, i have the mold ready, so just give me a couple of days to get it out.\r\n\r\njeff mays'),(29162,'37f74556ec','Hey mod, you were asking for batteries, i live in Canada to. I have lots of them and am selling that at .50 cents a piece. But i just sent 4 to Aantoin from rcmod and platinumrc to test them for me with a peak charger. If they are truly 150 mah like they say they are then i can sell you some if you want. But they only get a good charge with a peak charger, or stand alone charger, like the one that works on 4 aa batts or ac adapter.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27575,'7fed77e38a','Yo!\r\nAs far as getting my bro his kit, it\'s gonna be a Toyota Bb kit(27 or 49, it\'s not an issue), but I want the clear body so I\'ll take it and give him a different way more badass body in its place.  He\'s also getting the Tomy 3.0 motor(I actually like them when uisng a slimmer motor insert space.  LXX and others use my 4.2 pros and 3.4 NX, etc.) a perfection top tension heatsink, a light kit, a microsizers hopup kit, and a 200mah battery.  Toyeast has the perfection parts, and they\'re cheap due to low shipping weight.  I\'m gonna ween him off of XMODS.\r\n\r\nI might need some 2-speed transmitters for 27 mhz.  (one for my Phantom car, one for my nephew since he needs a better control than Panther makes.)  I\'ll wait on those since you gotta have 50 posts for semi-legit status at BP, so I\'ll hold off for now-that, and I gotta wait to get paid.  I don\'t wanna end up like that bitch that got owned for trying to trade a GBA for an Epoch :grin:  You guys should bring back the news article of it or make it a sticky in the forums.  It was funnier than shit, but not as funny as \"p-p-p-powerbook\".\r\n\r\nI\'m amazed that thread that brought towerhobbies into the spotlight was so old; you\'d think they\'re outta bit parts by now.   I might get an extra 49 with everything becuse I need to fix my shitty LXX 49 controller, and maybe I can swap out the custom upgrades too.  I\'ll have to see what I need when I bring in the green.\r\n\r\nOh!  What\'s TRU, is that ToysRus?\r\n\r\nHit me back,\r\nAbe'),(27576,'818b93a869','[quote:818b93a869]Oh! What\'s TRU, is that [b:818b93a869]T[/b:818b93a869]oys-[b:818b93a869]R[/b:818b93a869]-[b:818b93a869]U[/b:818b93a869]s? [/quote:818b93a869]\r\nYep!\r\n\r\nSorry, I only have single speed Tx\'s\r\nAt $2.49 each, I would pick up more than a couple 8-) \r\nYou do know that they don\'t have a Tx ?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27579,'d57f564b19','On the speed kits?  Sure.  Oh, I mean, I need to buy some controllers.  It\'s not a big issue though; my 27 works fine but the thing had it\'s charger removed at the factory.  Perfection\'s fault.  I\'ve been to the TRU before, I got my little sister a kit for Christmas and she\'s going to customize her clear Celica body.  I\'ll get her more stuff when I\'m in the giving mood.\r\n\r\nBouncin\' out,\r\nAbe'),(27580,'47e7aa389d','It\'s ken@xxaps.com.'),(27617,'84a26b48d1','yo mutha! i seen the guys laid the smack down on your request in the click. stay cool, i hope you didnt take it to heart... im a regular b-boy even if im white and 22, and right now a little tanked on some fine australian beer and a little jack. ive met betty.k in person and he really is a nice guy. its just his online persona is just a little hardcore...\r\n\r\n i got a spare cooper if your interested, but the sprinter and the glorias are staying in the collection! i supose i could sell you one painted up gloria, but its rear window has been filled up and sanded back to get rid of the ugly holes these bit bodies usually come with...\r\n\r\npm me back or make your way over to the regular site of mine ausmicro and pm me there for a quicker response...and while your there check out my gallerty, its full of more recent work of mine...\r\n\r\npeace out brother!'),(37418,'979e3f66b8','Who is the girl in your avatar?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32569,'eb759d6a47','Just wondering how much would it be total including shipping to 39540?  Packing could be whatever\'s the most cheapest and efficient method using priority mail.'),(29748,'f4187e7b3a','Yes, that would be great!\r\n\r\nHere\'s an address:\r\nDavid Knaack\r\n850 Amelia Ave\r\nElkhorn NE 68022\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\nDave'),(27628,'2b864302cb','My bad about the post in the wrong area.  When I read about the 50 post min, I thought that was for all posts in \"Lookin\' to score.\"  Not just for ppl posting an item.'),(27629,'c802218d48','[quote:c802218d48=\"red2cwm\"]My bad about the post in the wrong area.  When I read about the 50 post min, I thought that was for all posts in \"Lookin\' to score.\"  Not just for ppl posting an item.[/quote:c802218d48]\r\n\r\nIt is a rule.  Yes.\r\n\r\nHowever, you still can\'t post things like that in the open forum.  That is what the other sections are to be used for.\r\n\r\nIf you are looking for something, you are \"Looking to score\".  Therefore you need to post it in the appropiate section.\r\n\r\nYou posted in the disscusion section.\r\n\r\nThanks for understanding.\r\n\r\nSG219'),(27630,'cc83ddb378','[quote:cc83ddb378=\"red2cwm\"]My bad about the post in the wrong area.  When I read about the 50 post min, I thought that was for all posts in \"Lookin\' to score.\"  Not just for ppl posting an item.[/quote:cc83ddb378]\r\n\r\nOne more thing.\r\n\r\nI\'m glad your cool about it.  That goes soooo far you don\'t understand.\r\n\r\nWe like to keep a clean and organized house here, thats all.\r\n\r\nOnce again, please stick around and have a few laughs with us.\r\n\r\nSG219');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27631,'acb51696d9','Another white boy huh, I\'m 21 in two months(Yeah, I\'m gettin tore back for my b-day) and look like the bastard son of Henry Rollins from Black Flag...\r\nAnyway, as far as the bodies/crap goes, I found a couple of shops that had the gloria and the sprinter and cleaned them out.  I still have no cooper though; is yours the old Rover style or the new BMW style?  Of course, to stay in the rules I\'ll wait till 50 posts to buy from the forums.\r\n\r\nI\'ll check out your gallery fa\'sho.  I wonder if I should enlist some help building my \"Ride of the Month\" idea- a lowrider Gloria stretch limo, heh heh.\r\n\r\nYou\'re in Austrailia, huh?  What do you think of the Holden Monaro, I call it the Aussie Corvette, and it rocks that they have it here in the States as a GTO.  I have relatives in New Zealand and Austrailia, but they\'re all pricks.\r\n\r\nAnd about the whole betty.k thing, sessiz got the word out that I was looking for an hobby shop that sells the shit I needed and not people who\'d sell it to me.  Also, DarkTari found the fucking motherload, and I\'m in contact with mikirgra cause we found this British site that had the Trueno pullback before we cleaned \'em out.\r\n\r\nHit me back,\r\nAbe'),(37675,'29b7635bd4','How much do you want for the two 27mhz chassis?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27938,'36a0f26824','If you decide to part it out....\r\n\r\nI want first dibs on the Mamba....\r\n\r\nI\'ll take the Mamba from you for $85 shipped? Let me know if thats reasonable for a used Mamba.  If not, we\'ll talk it over.  n/p\r\n\r\nThen maybe the chassis a couple of weeks later.  (the following Payday. :) )'),(35537,'2687e6f3b3','[quote:2687e6f3b3=\"hue35\"]Now I\'mm gonna go home and :cool:  &lt;--- except smokeless.  :lol:   Man, I\'m lovin\' this vaporizer... I haven\'t \"smoked\" anything since I got it, and my lungs can tell the difference.[/quote:2687e6f3b3]Shit man, I think my lungs need one of them. I\'ve been afraid to look at them, because I\'m pretty shure they\'re more than the wife would allow for paraphernalia. :lol: \r\n\r\nWell gald you like the start on the car. I was actually just sitting down to take a break on it. I\'m finishing up the chassis getting ready for paint. Just carved it out for the Super Slick motor.\r\n\r\nMy wife just brought a big bag of peanuts in the shells from one of those dudes on the side of the road, and they rock. :rockon:\r\n\r\nDave'),(31250,'7e59f66fc3','Hi TB, how exactly does entering the competition work? Id doesn\'t ask for email, or name. But it opened up my Outlook Express and i think emailed it to you. So do you know who wins by email? Thanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27644,'d329a8200a','What\'s up dude?\r\n\r\nHaven\'t seen you around in awhile. :???: \r\n\r\nGot any pics of you Mini-T with the aluminum chassis and stuff yet?'),(27802,'f0a9602171','I\'d take all of what you\'re offerin. Just give me a price, and I can paypal it too you or send you loot in the mail. whatever works.'),(28867,'998674c11e','Hi!\r\nDo you still feel like helping me?'),(28868,'c619e64956','[quote:c619e64956=\"betula66\"]Hi!\r\nDo you still feel like helping me?[/quote:c619e64956]\r\n\r\nSure, what do you need? I can get you anything Radio Shack has (any Zip Zap stuff, ZZSE, ZZMT. Also, a store near me has Microsizer Auto Modellista sets for $15. Tell me what you want, I\'ll figure out how much it will cost and how much shipping will be. You can paypal me the money and I\'ll get it and mail it. \r\n\r\nI guess you\'ll just have to trust me, but you can check with betty.k and ph2t, as I\'ve done this for them as well since they\'re in Australia.\r\n\r\nLet me know what you\'d like.'),(37752,'ffc80c5e93','It\'s fairly stock, but I think I put bearings, awd kit, and a few other things in it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37753,'99e79a0920','cool, so you interested in the trade???\r\n :-)'),(27729,'2a2c27084a','I finally got around to putting your tutorial up:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/article_postings.php?id=48&amp;catId=7\r\n\r\nCheck it out, let me know if there\'s anything you\'d like me to add, edit, delete, etc.\r\nI tried to follow your format for easier reading and such.\r\n\r\nNow that I\'m PMing you, might as well ask you about putting up your ZZSE Mosfet Mod. Would you mind if I added that to our articles as well, just as I did the Duty Cycle Mod?\r\nAs with the Duty Cycle Mod, I would totally understand if you would rather not - no hard feelings.\r\n\r\n- Cabo'),(27730,'c7b6f15a8b','I hope you don\'t mind, I went ahead and added your tutorial to our Articles:\r\n(full credits to you of course)\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/article_postings.php?id=47&amp;catId=8\r\n\r\nIf that\'s not okay with you, please let me know - that is fine and no hard feelings. I would take it down if you asked.\r\n\r\nAnyways, I thought it was a cool little mod and would like to help spread the word about it.\r\nLet me know what you think and if you\'d like me to do anything with it.\r\n\r\n- CaboWabo'),(27731,'acb51696d9','Another white boy huh, I\'m 21 in two months(Yeah, I\'m gettin tore back for my b-day) and look like the bastard son of Henry Rollins from Black Flag...\r\nAnyway, as far as the bodies/crap goes, I found a couple of shops that had the gloria and the sprinter and cleaned them out.  I still have no cooper though; is yours the old Rover style or the new BMW style?  Of course, to stay in the rules I\'ll wait till 50 posts to buy from the forums.\r\n\r\nI\'ll check out your gallery fa\'sho.  I wonder if I should enlist some help building my \"Ride of the Month\" idea- a lowrider Gloria stretch limo, heh heh.\r\n\r\nYou\'re in Austrailia, huh?  What do you think of the Holden Monaro, I call it the Aussie Corvette, and it rocks that they have it here in the States as a GTO.  I have relatives in New Zealand and Austrailia, but they\'re all pricks.\r\n\r\nAnd about the whole betty.k thing, sessiz got the word out that I was looking for an hobby shop that sells the shit I needed and not people who\'d sell it to me.  Also, DarkTari found the fucking motherload, and I\'m in contact with mikirgra cause we found this British site that had the Trueno pullback before we cleaned \'em out.\r\n\r\nHit me back,\r\nAbe');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (27662,'4cdc92198a','[quote:4cdc92198a=\"viperdout\"]Dave:\r\n\r\nWell, that answers my question, as I store it with no charge (same reason my regular fetted ZZ has the same problem too).  Right now, it\'s cheaper for me to go li-po than to replace the ni-mh (or at least now I have an excuse :lol: ).  The charger I have supposedly can charge 1-8 ni-cad or ni-mh, and can charge as low as 100ma: http://www2.towerhobbies.com/cgi-bin/wti0001p?&amp;I=LXCLD5&amp;P=ML\r\n\r\nLuckily, I have an Apache S2500 lith charger for my brushless xmod, so I guess that\'s how I\'ll charge it.  One last question: my MT isn\'t drawing an amp or more, right?  I can\'t see how that tiny-ass motor could, but since I don\'t have a multimeter (I\'m a cheap bum who uses my school\'s multimeters) at hand, just curious.  Hell, you might\'ve worked on the fastest stock electonics MT!  \r\n\r\n-Max[/quote:4cdc92198a]I got a cheap ass multi-meter, it doesn\'t read above 200mA, or below 5amps. It\'s odd. So anyways, I\'m not sure what it draws, but you know, the highest current drain it when the motor is dead stalled. Doubt it\'s much, but it could be as much as 1 amp I\'m sure.\r\n\r\nDave'),(37002,'21b97cdc02','Holy shit! Dude, that chassis is a fucking thing of beauty... a work of art... a masterpiece. My jaw is on the floor. God damn, man. I can\'t wait to see this thing done (I can and will, but Jesus that\'s nuts). \r\n\r\nWhew.\r\n\r\nI\'m not sure I more to say at this point... just wow... it\'s sick.\r\n\r\nAnd now for some emoticons...  :-o  :eek:  :-D  :D  :eek:   :-o  :shock:  :shock:    :eek: ...... :shock:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33363,'8f6eea2c0a','I\'m from T. Ontario.....and im guessin the americans hate the way i talk cuz i try to put some enthusiam in my bits lol'),(37530,'be996d3119','[quote:be996d3119=\"betty.k\"]holy crap! that could explain it! :lol: \r\n\r\nmakes me wonder if that\'s why the steering was weak for me!\r\n\r\ni used to run it on a 1:10 scale track so the shorter travel, slower responding steering didn\'t matter so much.\r\n\r\nif i was to try for more throw with the servo i\'d get a resistor with a value around 5kohm (4.7kohm is more common, it\'s good enough). you want to solder it between the 2 servo pot wires. you can do that on the pot or on the pcb. whenever i\'ve done it i\'ve used a surface mount resistor and soldered it on the pcb, across the 2 servo pot tabs.\r\n\r\nwhat this does is electronically fool the servo into moving more than it thinks it is.\r\nyou\'ll probably find it\'s too much throw and will need to adjust the steering sensitivity accordingly.\r\n\r\nonce you swap out the motor and add the resistor i think we might have it worked out.\r\ni\'d personally swap the motor first and see how it reacts before adding the resistor when you add the mr01 pcb. the kyosho pcb has a much stronger steering curcuit.\r\n\r\nkeep me posted :-)[/quote:be996d3119]\r\n\r\n\r\nCool, i\'ll give it a try and let you know how it goes. :-o \r\n\r\nI\'ll keep ya posted on the project, i guess i\'m off to the shack to pick up some parts.'),(32194,'e8292e4aba','[quote:e8292e4aba=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hi,\r\n\r\nOk, I have one set of the roofs for the mini coopers. There are 5 different ones. I also have a few sets of spare tire sets for the mini coopers as well. \r\n\r\nTalk to you later,\r\nJDM[/quote:e8292e4aba]\r\n\r\nCool, so would you take $75 (shipped) for the following list, plus the Mini Heart roofs and tires...\r\n\r\nTomy BCG sets: \r\n\r\nSpeed racer mach V 45mhz \r\nLupin the third 35mhz \r\n\r\n\r\nMini Heart sets: \r\n\r\nred fire chief \r\nwhite/green police car \r\nwhite \r\npale yellow \r\nyellow \r\nmint green \r\nblack \r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know,\r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33470,'c314c8f2d7','Yo whats up Cabo!\r\nI know its probably stupid to even bring this up... And I may not be the best person to mention it. But I been readin the forums for a good long time (since tinyRC days...) and I gotta say lately the attitude of a few members hasnt really impressed me....\r\n\r\nFor a random example. SG seems to have an amazing ability to read anyones thread and take it negatively and retort back. His replies seem downright rude a lot of the time...\r\n\r\nI dont know could really be done, but I just worry that \"future pimps\" will get stand off-ish on postin here if they fear for getting their heads ripped off for askin somethin... And I know thats not somethin you could want...\r\n\r\nI am pm\'in you about this just as a heads up... I beenm here a long time, and I dont want things to get outs control  :(  Sory if Im outa line, hehe but I love BitPimps just to much  :-o \r\n\r\nPeace out man! hit me back\r\n:D Swavey'),(29267,'23d67dd82b','Sorry for the tardiness of my reply, I have had a shitty week.  I shipped it today, should arrive in 2-3 days.  You cna track it at [url]www.USPS.com[/url] with the number 0304 1560 0004 2125 3558\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\nMazda');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29268,'0a3f616890','[quote:0a3f616890=\"Mazda787b\"]Sorry for the tardiness of my reply, I have had a shitty week.  I shipped it today, should arrive in 2-3 days.  You cna track it at [url]www.USPS.com[/url] with the number 0304 1560 0004 2125 3558\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\nMazda[/quote:0a3f616890]No sweat dude, there\'s no rush, I was out of town anyways.\r\n\r\nI\'ll let ya know when it comes.\r\nThanks again holmes!'),(32809,'fc98197bff','Can I get a 1152x868 and a 1280x1024.'),(35412,'06e4c6f753','Hmm, well I see what your saying, but I don\'t understand any of this. I was thinking of getting lithium ion batteries I heard they boost the performance nicely, as for FETS and Plasmatomic engines and stuff, I think once I purchase either a MiniZ (most likely getting an MR-02) or an Xmod i will try these upgrades.\r\n\r\nBy the way you know any good and cheap sites or something to buy MiniZ or Xmods. See I would buy an Xmod but they are too fuckin xpensive in Canada.'),(28693,'865db39e57','Well, I was wondering if you had a PSP, because in a link, I saw your name, adn then I saw a PSP animation. I was wondering if you have one? Later :-) \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-rcd :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36280,'3d4ae2359c','Now that I\'m not all blurry eyed and on my way to work at 5:30 in the morning I just wanted to say thank you again. Not only did ya give me an idea on what to expect or look forward to (all I was looking for) but ya took it one step further and offered to go over what I will be presenting in my portfolio. This has earned my gratitude but good man and if I have the time to do it I will take you up on it. (hopefully any kind of interview is a month away yall know how I love to procrastinate :lol: )\r\nThen you got all gay ( :lol: ) on me and offered to print the stuff out and ship it to me. God damn it man, are you a fuckin saint or what?\r\nSeriously man I could keep on thanking ya but you hopefully get the jist of what I\'m goin on about. :-)'),(34655,'cf88b3cf7e','Thanks man, cant wait for the write up.  \r\n\r\nSTG'),(37853,'1fce917324','What\'s up, sorry i havent got back to you, ive been driving across cities for a few days back and forth playin soccer, and the tourny is finally over for me to relax.\r\n\r\nAnyhow i checked my emails today and my uncle confirmed he recieved the money, so hopefully tomorrow, or for sure monday your stuff will be shipped...\r\n\r\nHope that\'s cool and take care!'),(37783,'a890b907f5','sweet, money sent. i made it $16usd in total, hopefully that covers the shipping. any probs lemme know.\r\n\r\nmy address:\r\n\r\n39 currajong ave\r\ncamberwell 3124\r\nvictoria\r\naustralia\r\n\r\ncheers!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30886,'bf109b5657','[quote:bf109b5657=\"backdrift\"]Cj : Ive sent you PM\'s, we are threatening the source for the chargers to give a refund, or we take them to court. Or they just ship the damn things.[/quote:bf109b5657]\r\n\r\nWhat did I send you for the chargers?'),(30415,'67ba3c85a7','Hmmm let think about it and get back with you. I would say the cost of the parts + a little for me to build it. Let me finish the Skyline and I will let you know.'),(33757,'0d1120d312','[quote:0d1120d312=\"DarkTari\"]Send me your addy Pimp ![/quote:0d1120d312]\r\n\r\nHere ya go \r\nAaron W. Olmsted\r\n1941 Sayers Road \r\nBastrop Texas 78602\r\n\r\nI also put my address in the thread (last post) including price and freight.\r\nthanks man!  :-)'),(33029,'a7218b5834','Its all good dude.  I spoke to the other Aussie guys, and they reckon it can take an assload of time sometimes, so i\'ll wait it out another fortnight or so.  We can sort somethin im sure.  I\'m not riding you man, I know sending mail to the asshole of the world is a pain, and you\'ve been checking in and stuff, so please don\'t think im trying to be pushy or nothin.  Just getting peeved with australia post.  Apparently any shipment of international mail can land in any australian capital city, so it could be sitting in fucking perth for all i know.  Thats like me sending a parcel to my sister in NY and having it arive in LA. Then they kick it around customs for a while, then send it ground shipping from whichever place they decide to land the shipment.'),(34637,'02456631a2','[quote:02456631a2=\"arfin\"]Whaaaa? A package? For me? LOL, it\'s funny because today i found all the parts for the Epoch i was gonna send you! Luckily i had a few new parts that i needed, i just spent 1 hour sanding the baby down, because it had previous solder burns on the side, and i did my best to make her look good again.\r\n\r\nCan\'t wait to finish her up! Yo, sucks what happened to Sat4ife though, but i think i got him to think i want to give/sell him an epoch! This is what was said, maybe you can help explain:\r\n\r\n\"... if you need any help with r/c related shit especially epoch (my main r/c) don\'t hesitate to ask\"\r\n\r\n\"... yeah i\'ll hit you up on an epoch here soon\" The ... represent the quote i left out, but what does that sound like to you?[/quote:02456631a2]\r\n\r\n\r\nhmmm, maybe he\'s saying he wants to buy one from ya. Maybe not FROM you but perhaps you give him a connection to get one. Or maybe it was a typo on his part. :???: idk\r\n\r\n\r\nCOOL!!!! right on man!!! I\'m glad you found the shizz!!!! \r\nI almost got your package all together!!\r\nI need to know what kind of bodies/cars do you like again? Or are you like me, and its whatever! :)\r\n\r\nYou said you have a 35mhz car and controller?\r\n\r\nI do remember the charging port thing you need.\r\n\r\nI\'m off today, so perhaps we\'ll talk.\r\n\r\n--Dave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36877,'3eaae68be3','[quote:3eaae68be3=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:3eaae68be3=\"DarkTari\"]I cleaned up an old post yesterday.  I feel Da Hookup will have a lot of outdated/no good posts cause it\'s all about a bargain, for a limited time, so after that the post is no good.  Is there any quick way to delete the entire post and all responses?\r\n\r\nI did one from sg219 about a TRU clerance last year (which is no good now) and had to individually delete every post.  Or do we want  a place like an archive dumpster where we can move old, outdated post to?\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp![/quote:3eaae68be3]\r\nI say just lock them up so people know they\'re dead, but it\'s still there arhived.\r\n\r\nIf you want to delete an entire topic and all responses, just go into the topic, scroll to the bottom of the page.\r\nOn the left side, there should be a red button with an X (next to the yellow button with an arrow).\r\nHit that and you\'ll be able to delete the entire topic and all responses.[/quote:3eaae68be3]\r\n\r\n :-o'),(31474,'c3f6c4abf8','Is 27mhz ok? That is the only frequency for the hummer body I\'ve seen. Also, I don\'t know if I will be able to find a hummer because those are sort of old. I will look around for one, but if I can\'t find a hummer, would you prefer one of the bodies without the arms on the side (like the hulk body), or one with the arms? I\'ll find one and ship it out tomorrow. I\'m really not sure how to go about shipping this, so I might just let my UPS Store handle it. hehe\r\n\r\nI\'m looking forward to that DigiQ. It looks really cool, and I\'m hoping that I can put a 3.6V 145mAh lipo cell in it and really burn some rubber. :)\r\n\r\nBTW, I saw the removable front spoiler, does it have the other pieces? (The removable rear deck?). Doesn\'t really matter, I was just wondering.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n-JNY\r\n\r\nJoseph Nicholas Yarbrough\r\n2515 Graham Rd.\r\nConway, SC 29526\r\n\r\njoseph.yarbrough@gmail.com');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31099,'9dd76247de','Hey max, I just recieved your MO in the mail today. I will get the v1 send out first thing tomorrow morning.'),(36150,'bea8423c16','[quote:bea8423c16=\"DarkTari\"]Dave,\r\nIf I get a lead on some, for a good price, would you be interrested?\r\n\r\n[img:bea8423c16]http://capsule.rc.online.fr/images_v2/forum/oatures/Dsc00350.jpg[/img:bea8423c16][/quote:bea8423c16]Yeah, I want one. :-) \r\n\r\nDave'),(37863,'25ffdc991c','Hey Betty.k\r\n\r\nAwhile ago I read a post and you said you got your S-2000\'s offroading rims from a hotwheels car. I hope that is correct. Now my question is which hotwheels model did you get it from? Im trying to make my own offroad bit with the same rims. Thanks in advance.\r\n\r\nYou can contact me at sky_seraph@hotmail.com\r\n\r\n\r\nP.S: your offroad bits are awsome lol. Everyday I end up looking at one of your bits.\r\n\r\n\r\n-RyanL'),(32092,'0cad89bb8a','[quote:0cad89bb8a=\"Finks\"]Any chance I could get 1 more line allowed on my sig?  When I do what I am trying to do it states that it is too long, but if I don\'t hit return it allows me, just doesn\'t look right w/ the text next to my pic.  If you can thanks[/quote:0cad89bb8a]You can have up to 255 characters.\r\nYour current sig is around 176 characters.\r\nI just updated your profile and was able to add a return after the text and before the pic. Is that what you were trying to do?\r\nBasically, you have 255 characters of space to play with so you\'ll have to make it fit within that limit.'),(34274,'e84606754c','PayPal sent');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34275,'8cc79c4cff','I feel like my OG bit collection is just about done, but I need a coupla things... I need a Tomy Calsonic Skyline and the original silver Fairlady Z 2-speed car. If you have extras you\'d wanna part with, or run across either of these, would you mind giving me a head\'s up? \r\n\r\nthanks,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(31285,'c6e1141e75','Arfin, got your entry ok - yes the form sends me an email (low tech solution).\r\n\r\nYour in the draw, you will be notified by email if you win.\r\n\r\nGood luck.\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTB'),(35233,'987eed5e8d','[quote:987eed5e8d=\"crazydave\"]Man, I\'m finally on vacation. I haven\'t had any time off in 4 years. I even work holidays, because I like having the place to myself those days. This will actually be the first time in like 10 years I didn\'t go in on Thanksgiving to do prep.  :shock: \r\n\r\nIts hard as hell for me to get away from that place, I was telling you like 2 months ago I was taking a week off, and I was gonna work on your car, and now finally, I get some fucking time off. They have to hire new people, and borrow from other store, because they got to bring in 2 people to cover my ass. People keep quitting and getting fired, so I never get a vacation. Funny how they don\'t appreciate me when I\'m there.[/quote:987eed5e8d]\r\n\r\nRight on, man... that\'s what I need. My vacation time has been seriously fucked with this year... I have had a week off scheduled and denied at the last minute, three times in a row over the last 2 months. I was actually supposed to be on vacation right now, too... through the Thanksgiving week. It sucks and I\'m bitter for it. What it has meant is that my home improvement projects have been put on hold and my girl movin\' in is tied to those projects. Sore subject theses days for me, but it\'s actually nothin\' compared to your situation... 4 years? Dude, congratulations on some time off. You seriously need it and deserve it.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:987eed5e8d=\"crazydave\"]Sooo... Anyways, I guess I\'m just venting now, but besides relaxing and recovering, catching up on projects is high priorty this week, I\'m hoping to put out several projects. :-o \r\n\r\nBTW, want a Lexan body funny car, or how about a Willys coupe?\r\nhttp://www.wizzardho.com/Products14.htm\r\n\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:987eed5e8d]\r\n\r\nWell, considering how much you put out when you\'re busy as hell, I think I\'m a little scared to see what this week brings.  :shock:  You\'re gonna have a good time.\r\n\r\nI\'ve been looking for a place that sells lexan HO and actually has pictures of all the bodies, not just a list... I don\'t think it exists. That car (who built that... Hachi?) that showed up recently really inspired me to make a super bit that\'s built to drive on the RCP track... something scary fast that actually drives well. My OG dual cell car kicks ass on that track. I can get a nice lookin\' lap that would probably hold its own with a stock xmod, or OG iWaiver 01... anyway, maybe I\'ll have to bite the bullet on a few of those that sound good, just to make sure I come up with one I like.\r\n\r\nHave a good week, dude... you deserve the shit out of this.\r\n\r\nMat'),(29930,'2df559ebc1','[quote:2df559ebc1=\"hue35\"]\r\nThat sounds sweet, dude. That got me thinkin\'...\r\nI\'ve been watching weird movies lately... you ever seen Two-Lane Blacktop, with James Taylor? If you haven\'t, you should check it out... super-interesting film. It\'s just got a cool vibe about it... very zen like. Very little dialog... basically a dude and his mechanic just lookin\' for their next race.\r\n\r\nAlso, Funnycar Summer... 70\'s documentary that follows Jim Dunn for a summer of drag racin\'... it was cool to see a dude who was all about the racin\', and gave the \"big dollar\" operations a run for their money. [/quote:2df559ebc1]Don\'t think I\'ve seen that first one, but I vaguely remember seeing Funnycar Summer when I was a little kid watching it with my dad. I dig movies like that, where you finding those at?\r\n\r\nOh and the wife didn\'t find any Lowrider cars but she did bring home a Guitar World with System of a Down, New York Dolls, and and article on the new underground metal. It\'s a decent read, if you feel like reading.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:2df559ebc1]Man, I hate the way that fuckin\' contest thread went down... mostly I\'m pissed that I let my frustration get the best of me. DT gets me so fuckin\' mad sometimes with his authoritative bullshit... fuck. That was bad timing with your modem... it woulda been cool if you had brought your level head a day sooner... fuckin\' computer gear. [/quote:2df559ebc1]Aww man, it\'s a good thing my modem went down, if I came back monday night and saw DT cussing and swearing the post after mine, I would have blew. Then as soon as cabo took his side, he\'s all ready to address that package out to Finks, WTF is that? Fact is I didn\'t have time to really reply, \'cause my wife had 3 days of catching up to do too, and she gets a hella a lot more emails. By Friday I had time to think about what I wanted to say, but I was to late. Sucks I really didn\'t get a chance to get my say, but oh well, it was shit a for a contest anyways.\r\n\r\nI was tranfering the chassis to a microsizer one yesterday, as I had intended to do weeks ago, and I was squeezing the wheels onto the axle with the teal gear, pushed too hard, and the axle popped through, and right into the tip of my finger, went in about an 1/8 inch. Fucking hurts like hell. This is the same car that I nearly sliced my finger off with, I\'m convinced its jinxed and I can\'t wait to make it go the hell away. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'m goin\' through one of those \"I suck\" phases... I really gotta get some of these cars done. I\'ve got a Ferrari I\'ve been workin\' on for 2 months, but nobody\'s gonna give a fuck, \'cuz SWG just revived the \"Miva\" project... that dude goes like lightning. I wish I could let go of the details like that... I\'ve ripped the back end of this car apart 3 times now. The fuck of it is, the first version was probably just fine... it hasn\'t improved that much. \r\n\r\n[quote:2df559ebc1]I\'m also working on another one that I was gonna have done for the truck contest, but it just didn\'t happen... actually, I\'m gonna give you a sneak peek...\r\n\r\nthese pictures are from the end of fucking March!... god damn I slow.\r\n[/quote:2df559ebc1]So is that truck one them little grave diggers? Or is that the Rev up? That\'s cool anyways, I like how you\'re integrating the chassis. just needs a grill, and maybe some bumpers. You got a grill for it? \r\n\r\nThat Ferrari should be cool too, sucks that SWG is beating you to it, but that guy is a monster right now. Where the hell did that come from, and thank  god he\'s posting it here. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'m doing a quicky right now, hopefully I\'ll get some pics tonight.\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31155,'842d2ba07c','Sweet, dude... thanks for the speedy delivery. I may need another fix (God, I need to stop), but yeah dude, I\'ll absolutely let \'em all know where I got the hookup. I\'ll shoot you a PM when the stuff gets here.\r\n\r\nThanks again,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(35429,'d318f8bac5','Hey MG, i\'m downloadin\' the demo right now, so when i get back from work it sould be done, and we can play! Take care, i\'ll be on later.'),(30945,'2a4a10836e','Hey man, sorry for the delay, I\'ve been out in Washington bringing a grocery store live on the managment and register software I write, and it was a total cluster.  The store manager is retiring next month, so he didn\'t really give a crap if it worked or not, and the area manager was too busy to test anything, so there were all kinds of problems.  I spent about 4 days running 14 hours a day fixing their stupid problems.\r\n\r\nAfterward I wasn\'t inclined to get on the computer (but I did go out for a $70 steak and wine dinner on the company :) )\r\n\r\nAnyway, apologies for not getting back to you on the car.  It looks like you\'ve got the right power connections, but I think you probably have a short somewhere, that would explain it getting hot.  Maybe a solder bridge near the voltage booster?\r\n\r\nYou also might need to double check your connections at the resistor pad where the input and output wires for the DC mod connect.  You should have one wire connected to each side of the pad (the DC mod basicly takes the place of the resistor), and be sure you don\'t have a short there.  The pads aren\'t made for connecting wires, so it can be easy to short the wires to other traces on the PCB.\r\n\r\nYou might also need to double check the connections on the mod board, the pads are pretty close together, so its easy to short things out there.\r\n\r\nIf you want me to take a look at your first board just lemme know, if the MCU isn\'t blown its usually possible to bring \'em back to life.\r\n\r\nI\'m flying out at like 6am tomorrow morning, but I\'ll try to get on the computer at night so I can answer any questions.  This week should be much easier than last week, so I\'ll be on more often.\r\n\r\nlater\r\nDK'),(36239,'132b0356bd','[quote:132b0356bd=\"DarkTari\"]Cool !  I\'ll keep you informed.\r\n\r\n[/quote:132b0356bd]I\'m not into the Metl-Tech cars. You know how I am about die cast, and that controller is horrible.\r\n\r\nI am curious about those Canadian cars.\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7191\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7243\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35236,'bdc98524ab','Hey I was told that you do Mosfet work I have 2 ZZSe 1 ZZMT and 2 Bits I\'d like do can you help?'),(31383,'ce6173f30e','[quote:ce6173f30e=\"codesuidae\"]Oh yea, steering jitters.  The DC mod doesn\'t intentionally solve that, but I have noticed on a couple of cars I\'ve done that it goes away.  I\'m not sure why.  As near as I can tell the jitter issue is a software problem in the ZZSE MCU (it allows the servo to overshoot when the drive motor is running).  The jitter is it hunting for center.  If its a power supply issue the presence of the DC mod board might change the power supply character enough to get around the problem.  Dunno for sure though :???:[/quote:ce6173f30e]Well from what you just told me, here\'s my 2 cents...\r\n\r\nThe Torino, Chevelle, and GTO, had almost fixed steering. It mostly worked right but would occasionally jitter, but Cabo\'s Torino that I played with jittered. In this GTO that I have the DC mod in, it originally was jitter free, but when I rebuilt it, it started jittering. I believe because the servo pot had to be adjusted crooked. So it would be my guess that it some kind of power management isue, and the DC mod, being more efficient, is giving just enough power back to the steering.\r\n\r\nThat my theory anyways. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\nThanks again. :-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(31423,'c0a6669f60','I got your box today...... thanks a ton ! I can\'t wait to strip the car down to fix mine.\r\nyour the best  :) \r\n\r\nmarc');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31424,'5f8f4e217c','hey man, do you want me to pick up a couple of the metallic super shens for ya? they\'re $15aud each and they sell em at my local toyshop.\r\nlemme know if you\'re interested or i would be willing to send you 2 for the bonzermat.'),(35683,'b7546a4d42','Hey Hunny,\r\nJust wondering if you will be home for dinner. I got something good cooking up for ya.\r\nLove,\r\nFellow gansta'),(35684,'b7546a4d42','Hey Hunny,\r\nJust wondering if you will be home for dinner. I got something good cooking up for ya.\r\nLove,\r\nFellow gansta'),(35685,'e8107a3c64','[quote:e8107a3c64=\"Bryce\"]Hey Hunny,\r\nJust wondering if you will be home for dinner. I got something good cooking up for ya.\r\nLove,\r\nFellow gansta[/quote:e8107a3c64]\r\nI\'m here and ready to eat - but you better have an appetite as well, because I\'m serving a full course meal.\r\nWhat do you have to say besides stupid shit?\r\nDon\'t waste my time, either come with an apology, insults, or something. I don\'t need to waste my time with bullshit.\r\n\r\nI\'m open for business - so say whatever you got to say - just make sure you say something. This \"hunny\" and \"dinner\" shit is lame as all fuck.\r\n\r\nLove,\r\nYour Poppa'),(31649,'7a4f6ad2e3','No problem. Let me know if they tell you about when it will arrive.\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36975,'564ed0f142','[quote:564ed0f142=\"pimpsmurf\"]I\'m not sure about the screws. There were some screws in the package I sent you today.\r\n\r\nI\'m also not sure about the brakes. My half 8 controller allowed it to do brakes. Did it have brakes in reverse? Then the motor is reversed. I don\'t remember man.\r\n\r\nThe ESC supports brakes though, and kyosho TX\'s are standard. They don\'t have the brakes, etc built into the TX like the iwavers.\r\n\r\nYour package went out USPS Priority today, so expect it in 2-3 days. Sorry about the screw up. Is palm harbor near New Port Richey? I lived in NPR, Ybor, Clearwater, St. Pete, and S. Tampa a couple years ago... bounced around a lot. =)\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:564ed0f142]\r\n\r\nSomewhat i\'m about 30 min from tampa and raymond james.\r\n\r\nYeah it has brakes going from reverse to foward but that couldnt be the motor wires. Hmm i dont know.\r\n\r\nThanks man!'),(35260,'2ba1a5aec4','Hey man, i put up a picture of those gears i have, let me know if thats what you are looking for and we can make a trade.  Also, did you ever get that FET tut. made for the zzse?\r\n\r\nthanks\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31324,'bda73d7452','I was wondering if you have a extra ssmt controller i know you did the i waver conversion. I can pay 10$ shipping if you do have it it would be appreciated thanks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37118,'08b5dbe893','[quote:08b5dbe893=\"sessiz\"]Damn you hue!!! I think I busted my spleen!!!!11! :lol: \r\n\r\n[img:08b5dbe893]http://home.comcast.net/~hue35/penismonsterdlx.gif[/img:08b5dbe893][/quote:08b5dbe893]\r\n\r\nDude, you stole my thunder... just hold on, I\'m in testing mode.'),(37119,'f142a7fa05','I figured as much man...sorry. :-('),(37645,'7dda132adb','[quote:7dda132adb=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Check for the $13 in 5-7 mins, I should be done the transaction by then.[/quote:7dda132adb]\r\n\r\nCool, will do man, i\'ll get your package to the post office this week. :-o'),(37646,'ab2586c646','money sent'),(37750,'b6b8e8c4b1','All of it man, i dont need them and looks like you dont need the NSX :-) \r\n\r\nBTW: could you please tell me what mods the NSX has?'),(37764,'cc84483d11','Thanks man.  :-o   I remember those some of biohazards shots but i was having a hard time finding pics.  Im sure they are saved somewhere on my computer  :???:   Those two pics you loaded in your library are two that i havent seen before.  I think the only ones that i saw were when he modified it further and gave it a flex plate and a spring for a full suspension.  \r\n\r\nIf you have any other pics that would be great.  I think i can manage a new design based on the idea :???:   Its a good place to jump from anyways\r\n\r\nThanks again man\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36661,'ca2a7ddb5f','[quote:ca2a7ddb5f=\"stampede_dude\"]You said you had a front steering problem, and I need a rear clip to fit a gen1 body on the evo chassis, and since you don\'t have any gen1 bodies and I have an extra evo chassis with the parts you would need, would you be willing to trade? I most likely have the part you need, just let me know, and if worst comes to worst We could work out a deal for the whole front end. Thanks![/quote:ca2a7ddb5f]\r\n\r\nTrade what ?'),(36876,'3eaae68be3','[quote:3eaae68be3=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:3eaae68be3=\"DarkTari\"]I cleaned up an old post yesterday.  I feel Da Hookup will have a lot of outdated/no good posts cause it\'s all about a bargain, for a limited time, so after that the post is no good.  Is there any quick way to delete the entire post and all responses?\r\n\r\nI did one from sg219 about a TRU clerance last year (which is no good now) and had to individually delete every post.  Or do we want  a place like an archive dumpster where we can move old, outdated post to?\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp![/quote:3eaae68be3]\r\nI say just lock them up so people know they\'re dead, but it\'s still there arhived.\r\n\r\nIf you want to delete an entire topic and all responses, just go into the topic, scroll to the bottom of the page.\r\nOn the left side, there should be a red button with an X (next to the yellow button with an arrow).\r\nHit that and you\'ll be able to delete the entire topic and all responses.[/quote:3eaae68be3]\r\n\r\n :-o'),(34751,'ab46b73ffc','[quote:ab46b73ffc=\"Clint\"]Hey got a question for ya.\r\n\r\nWhere did you get the powerquest 600mah lipo from?\r\nI searched all over and not one website sells them. Did you mean\r\nPoly Quest?\r\n\r\n-Clint[/quote:ab46b73ffc]\r\n\r\nDoh! :o \r\n\r\nSorry about that, yes i meant polyquest.\r\n\r\nIts a great lipo pack for the dimensions of the evo chassis.\r\n\r\nCheck out \r\n\r\nwww.zagi.com \r\n\r\nThey have reasonable shipping etc.\r\n\r\nSorry about that, and btw great job on the tut.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37351,'49ddeb725f','[quote:49ddeb725f=\"SHAUN\"]Would you be a moderater on my forum. I\'m thinkin your gonna say no cause i dont think ya like me.[/quote:49ddeb725f]\r\n\r\nOK.  I\'ve contacted you few times already and you have yet to reply.\r\n\r\nHow do you expect to run a forum if you don\'t let people sign-up or even reply to any questions or problems. :o \r\n\r\nThats allright, you just keep signing in and out of BP and ignoring PMs.   :-x \r\n\r\n\r\nI tried.  You didn\'t. :thebird:'),(34241,'08c90f35f1','Thanks :)'),(34242,'e0eb65236b','Wow, your zzmt is looking really good, Why have you stayed away from pimps all these months lol. did you get a body mounted on the other zzmt you were working on?\r\n\r\nYouve defietley got some skills lbrc has some competition.\r\n\r\nOh and did you get a chance to ship those ex. chassis out.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37900,'24b7e18349','Where can I send the vid to, and how do I add the screen shot? I\'m kind of a dummy when it comes to videos and video editing'),(35365,'ff1a8cf278','[quote:ff1a8cf278=\"chrome\"]Hey CJ I\'m just getting in from my week long vacation.\r\n\r\nI\'m a little lost on the GPM deal, I think I follow you, but I\'m not 100% sure.  Dropping the clip to make up the cost of the increase sounds fine.  I want a complete car kit with dog bones and axles for AWD minus the front clip.  If you need anymore dough, that\'s fine.  Just drop me another PM and I\'ll have it to you as soon as I can get to the computer.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...[/quote:ff1a8cf278]\r\n\r\nHeres the good news i need $0.00 to cover your current order for an AWD car.  Unless you want to add the new Rear Diff for $16.00.  If you do let me know what of the two colors of parts you want that to be?\r\n\r\n[img:ff1a8cf278]http://www.cjshobbies.net/Images/11_18_050002.jpg[/img:ff1a8cf278]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32199,'86a217e52a','[quote:86a217e52a=\"mikirgra\"]Yo DT, shipped out the bit on my lunch break. I packed it up really tight. Sent parcel post. Should by there by end of the week. Damn you got a good deal! Keep you\'re eyes peeled, cuz I might have to sell off a lot of my other bits. I have some really cool sets, but I have two or more of a lot of them. I\'m going to sell my dups off cuz I just don\'t have the time for them, and I need to the $. C\'est la vie. Later.[/quote:86a217e52a]\r\nSorry to hear that Pimp!  Lemme know what you got, if I don\'t have it already we can deal.  I\'ll look out for it.  One TRU didn\'t have it.  I\'ll check at one more this week, if they don\'t have it I\'ll just PayPal you the 30 BigUns.\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp  :cool:'),(34555,'0d3db31168','[quote:0d3db31168=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:0d3db31168=\"crazydave\"]The car is an Avanti, but what damn movie!!! Goonies? Can mods play too? :-D  :lol: \r\n\r\nhttp://www.avantisource.com/[/quote:0d3db31168]\r\nThat\'s pretty good dude. I don\'t think I woulda ever guessed the car. lol\r\nIt is an Avanti.\r\n\r\nAnyone can play, so if you want - go for it.\r\nOr, do ya want me to tell ya? (but then you can\'t play - neener neener)[/quote:0d3db31168]Go ahead and tell me, its a cool Phat Boy, but I can live without. :lol: \r\n\r\nAhhh nevermind don\'t tell me. I\'ll hang out, and if no one gets it in a day or so, then I\'ll go ahead and throw my guess out.\r\n\r\nI just wanted to show you I knew the car. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave'),(30047,'a569874306','DC mod boards are $10 if you install \'em yourself.\r\n\r\nIt should take care of any hesitation on the start, and you may even want to switch to a slower motor or gears.  I find that a fast motor makes it pretty undrivable, just too fast, constantly rolls on corners, and does donuts when you try to accelerate.\r\n\r\nIf you want to order one just paypal me the $10 and your address and I\'ll get one sent off.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33092,'5050432922','[quote:5050432922=\"crazydave\"]... in hell that you\'d pull your Calsonic out of the box to examine it?\r\n\r\n\r\nBeen meaning to PM you about this for a while. The reason I\'m asking, is because I believe the RCMod calsonic I have is a fake.\r\n\r\nThe wheels have stepped edges like a Precious car. The gears are grindy and noisy as hell like the crappiest of clones. The tires are hard like a Cannonball\'s. It is a Tomy chassis, but not the best handling. I have my doubts if it is a Tomy body, because the wing cracked so easily, with in 5 minutes of having it out of the box. The box showed no signs of being previously opened, which makes this all very odd.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:5050432922]\r\nNo Problem Pimp. I\'ll try to get to it tonight,  At work right now, fuckin oncall  :mad:'),(30050,'e798182805','[quote:e798182805=\"micro_man\"]swg you can have the revevier for $5 plus $2 for shipping . you can paypal personal check or money order . or id take a bit or zz in trade for it since i dont have many cars anymore ...[/quote:e798182805]\r\n\r\npm me your address and I will send you some money if I can round up a Bit I will send you one of those to for the receiver. (I have some extra so will send you one with extra bodies). Thanks for the deal. \r\nI will send my address with the money and car so once received you can send out the Receiver.\r\n\r\nthanks man! :-) \r\n\r\nAaron \r\n\r\nsteelwoolghandi'),(35265,'cd573f3943','Its in the mail\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36834,'e75a630d88','[quote:e75a630d88=\"CaboWabo\"][quote:e75a630d88=\"Da Big Kahuna\"]Recieved this the day after I posted.....\r\n\r\n[quote:e75a630d88=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]If you need anybody to do a fet mod to the cars, then let me know.  I\'m sure you already have that covered, but just in case, it\'s the least I can do to support.  I would offer to paint and putty, but I know there are people here who can do that better than me.  I have a lot of extra supplies and what not.  If I know about the car that\'s chosen ahead of time, I can always send you some stuff that I may have laying around that might go good with the ride.[/quote:e75a630d88]\r\n\r\nNow he stepped up BigTime!  I told him I may call on his services, was planning on going that far but with his offer, we may do a couple.\r\nMaybe after this thing gets started, one of the mods will step up, if not, no problem!  I\'m building a shop for shooting some after pics.  This is gonna be off Da Hook !  ( Haven\'t recieved any entries yet but it\'s still early)[/quote:e75a630d88]\r\nThat kicks ass, I love it when the members step up like that.\r\nCool man, run with it - I\'m sure more interests will get perked soon, especially after the 1st one goes out.[/quote:e75a630d88]\r\n\r\n[b:e75a630d88]WORD [/b:e75a630d88]  :cool:'),(31669,'9a244bc373','count me in one 2 of those shells when you get them in let me know');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34348,'d98b286d22','yeah. no problemo, but they will have to go out on monday because I have a race tomorrow. :(\r\n\r\nI\'ll see if I have any other bit stuff around. I think I have a bit clone here. Might be useful. I\'ll see if that will fit in the envelope. :)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(29948,'55336753f3','[quote:55336753f3=\"hue35\"] There might be a cool way to deal with those reversed wheels... some kind of inserts or something.[/quote:55336753f3]Hmmm, you just got me thinking, you know how those touring cars have the covers on their BBS wheels to direct the air into the brakes...\r\n\r\n\r\nBTW, just discovered your thread on the bP theme song... Second version? i missed the first. :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'m gonna check that out after my shower... I\'ll be back.\r\n\r\nDave'),(35548,'96ddd05970','[quote:96ddd05970=\"sg219\"]Totally forgot that it came.  Been a little busy with some stuff.\r\n\r\nI like the cover you made. :-o \r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nI\'ll check it out soon.  Gotta find some buds. :search:[/quote:96ddd05970]\r\n\r\nI hear ya on the \"busy\" front... Jesus Christ. \r\n\r\nCool, I\'m glad it got there... hopefully there\'s some stuff there you\'ll dig. \r\n\r\nHope you found some buds by now.  :cool:'),(30316,'890e7b55f4','Hope you don\'t mind I\'m pming ya here, I know you don\'t know me that well.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6215');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29763,'acbf362959','No sweat dude, I thought it time you don some bitPimps shit.\r\n[quote:acbf362959=\"HirotoR34\"]I just got em in the mail and I must say these are sweet! I haven\'t had much time for micros right now, but come next winter I\'ve got some ideas so these will grace some of my future mods. I\'ll keep on postin when I can. Thanks again.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHiroto[/quote:acbf362959]'),(37448,'a0ed9c9b04','[quote:a0ed9c9b04=\"betty.k\"]the steering is a little sluggish, i put it down to the weakness of the iwaver steering curcuit.\r\nyou\'ll notice all those servos have the motors swapped out, from memory the bpnsx still has a stock servo motor. try using a stock (red) zz motor instead.\r\n\r\nanother reason for the sluggishness is the front springs press hard on the knuckles making them harder to turn, press on the front shocks then twiddle the steering. you\'ll probably find it a bit snappier. this means when it\'s on the ground and running the steering works better due to the suspension sag.\r\n\r\ni\'m pretty sure there\'s no broken parts, it\'s just the combination of the suspension, weak curcuit and weak motor. softer springs and a better servo motor is what i\'d try :-o \r\n\r\nany other problems or questions, just gimme a yell :-)[/quote:a0ed9c9b04]\r\n\r\nThis one has a upgraded steering motor from the looks of it a yellow one.\r\n\r\nI mean its not steering at all man, i\'m puzzled as hell here.'),(31108,'9ca7cc9112','Congratulations stampede you officially get warned. Keep it up dumbass.  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34500,'0a4fcbed99','Glad someone caught the hint.\r\nI\'ve got 9401 posts and hate to keep increasing that over posts that I think most will ignore.\r\nIt\'s almost embarrassing, think about when I hit 10K and we\'ve only got 70+K posts all together.\r\nThat = gay.'),(34654,'384b4fe2d2','[quote:384b4fe2d2=\"Sporttracguy\"]Hey man, Ive been searching and searching and i cant find any sort of a diagram to FET the zzse.  Since you seem to be well educated on the subject i figure ill go right to the source.  Do you have or know of a good tuttorial on doing an FET upgrade on the SE?\r\n\r\nAlso, Im trying to find the best place to order the FETs, any good places come to mind?\r\n\r\nThanks man\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:384b4fe2d2]I\'ve held off on doing a SE tutorial, because codesuidae has already done one, its at codesuidae.net but I think the way its arranged can be very confusing, and I\'m afraid anyone that follows that step by step might have some issues. \r\n\r\nYou know what? The info on FETs here is all spread out, and kinda confusing too. Give me until this weekend, I\'m gonna try to put together some kind of all inclusive article on FET mods.\r\n\r\nI get my FETs at digikey.com. They are cheap there, but theres a $5 surcharge on orders under $25. $5 is 10 FETs, so I always order 55 FETs, puts my order just over $25 before shipping. The #s are IRLML2502 for the N-channels, and IRLML6401 for the P-channels.\r\n\r\nDave'),(35364,'1680a44616','Hey CJ I\'m just getting in from my week long vacation.\r\n\r\nI\'m a little lost on the GPM deal, I think I follow you, but I\'m not 100% sure.  Dropping the clip to make up the cost of the increase sounds fine.  I want a complete car kit with dog bones and axles for AWD minus the front clip.  If you need anymore dough, that\'s fine.  Just drop me another PM and I\'ll have it to you as soon as I can get to the computer.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31398,'4dc063eb9a','beause my local tru is at least a a hour away its easier just to get a controller that i know works.'),(31400,'408ab28229','Sorry man, she really insnt up for trade or sale.  At the moment she is the best bit i have and im not really ready to give her up at the moment.  If you would like i could give you some instructions on how to make one yourself, they arent as hard as you would think.  Id make a few more but i dont have any SE batteries or microsizer chassis lol\r\n\r\nSorry,, Glad you like my work though\r\n\r\nSporttracguy'),(33190,'e1607db386','Great, glad to hear that they made it.\r\n\r\nSo far Ive been pretty happy with the diff mod results.  Have modified about 10 and only screwed up once, ouch bad shaft grove.\r\n\r\nI use a 5/32 bit with a guide tip to enlarge the bearing hole, it also doesnt hurt to enlarge the shaft hole slightly since the bearing will now hold the wheel mount gear.  The hardest part of the whole thing, and the only part I screwed up on is cutting and placing the E-clip grove.  Am looking to replace the E-clip with a push on fastener they are round and press on so you only need a slight indent in the shaft, instead of cutting a grove, buy pushing them on backward only the inside tines contact the bearing inner race. Will let you know if they work.\r\n\r\nIf you can keep a secret, just for starts Max has ball bearings (5 ), a coreless servo motor, 4 different battery packs all of which can be changed in less than 30 seconds, a turbo of course, a battery indicator light, and a couple of surprises that you will unfortunately have to wait for.  Matt may have told you that I have been building cars for Apexs new owner but kicker is where he is sending the Max test car and why.'),(37534,'27d75272eb','I\'m having a little trouble figuring out what to do with my servo wires. The Gen1 has 3 wires and the iWaver has 2 I think. How did you wire up your board? Pics would help.\r\n\r\nHow do I tell the difference between 01 and 02 boards?\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37939,'c403ac96d2','O yes! I got around to sending it out....and you are definately gonna wanna keep an eye out for your surprise this time my friend! \r\n\r\nthat\'s all im gonna say! \r\n\r\nTake it easy!'),(34911,'4f1f3bf2b5','jump in the chat urgent!'),(34940,'eab230bcd8','Aaron,\r\n\r\n10 would be more than enough.  I would like to send you 6 to 8 + a couple of spares for you or incase of accidents with the car, and then the rest at a later date since the guy who made them for us will be making some thicker versions.\r\n\r\nBest guess is that I will have motors within a month.  Cant wait to see what you think of the car, since youre planning on getting a lithium charger I will make sure to throw in a 340 mAh LiPo pack too.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nPhilip'),(29976,'93531e4159','[quote:93531e4159=\"codesuidae\"]An Xmod rim would be great, I\'ve had a couple of people ask me about doing some of those.\r\n\r\nI can\'t think of anything else, I\'ve got most of the zip size stuff, so thats not a problem.\r\n\r\nWhen I get them working right I\'ll send you a set or two of zip size rims if ya like, maybe you can come up with a good way to mount them.[/quote:93531e4159]\r\n\r\nI\'m sending out those parts in the morning.  I was a little busy for a few days. \r\n\r\nRock concerts and work. :-D \r\n\r\nMike'),(34501,'4ae96ceee9','[quote:4ae96ceee9=\"DarkTari\"]How much do you want for the Tomy Sets?  Shipping?\r\n\r\nIs that everything or do you have any Lxx sets left?\r\n\r\nI know someone looking for the WRX set\r\n\r\nLemme Know!\r\n\r\nThanx Again Pimp![/quote:4ae96ceee9]\r\n\r\n$15 each for the Tomy Sets.... Shipping for one set around $5 bucks priority mail with delivery confirmation. \r\n\r\nFor more sets etc... I gotta figure shipping depending on you what you would want etc... \r\n\r\nI may have a few Lxx sets left. I have the vw beetle sets with working lights. Also have the super perfection lambo/ferrari combo sets and maybe a few of the regular/auto modellista sets.\r\n\r\nThanks and let me know!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35418,'e1c3b863cb','No problem, always up to help out a pimp.  The red gear came today!  Thanks, now i just need to make some new mounts and install it.\r\n\r\nKeep me posted on that SE tuttorial\r\n\r\nTHanks\r\n\r\nSTG'),(35421,'d00b2d130a','Hello DarkTari,\r\n\r\nYou replied to a post of mine on microrccenter regarding VW Bus. \r\n\r\nDo you know where I can get a body for a Bit?'),(35687,'3fd7bafac5','Ok.\r\nEnough of this shit,  i don\'t want to just have arguing, i want to have a serious chat here.\r\nI understand that you are tired of n00b\'s and shit coming in, asking stupid questions. Mine wern\'t stupid questions, I was just asking some decent questions for info, help, and to update on my upcoming project.\r\nI am wondering if you knowe of the name you guys have given your self, for being \"flamable\" towards n00bs, etc. You guys are know to be netherless rude and obnoxious. Why? I don\'t know. I always though these forums people have created were to spread idea,s tips, information, and HELP ONE ANOTHER. I don\'t see much of this, just threats, foul language, etc.\r\nMind you i disagree with PG forums, that bann you for saying \"shit\" , but the degree that I have witnessed from SOME of your members, admins, moderators, and what other people have told me about this forum.\r\n You have a great forum, very knowledgable people here, great mind, projects, creation.\r\nNow if I came in without proper punctuation( I try my best), asking completley gay question, I would be expected to be treated fairly(flamed a bit, told to use punctuation, and directed towards a rules page or something)\r\nEVEN though, I have punctuation, some good questions, and intense interest in these forum. I still was flamed, threatened to be stabbed with a pen(lol..) etc.\r\nI\'m hoping you guys could do something to resolve your beat/flame the new bitches theme, for something more civilized. Maybe you could get a better name, draw more interest, and have more good members in the end.\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nBryce'),(36501,'345d3b5d36','Nope not yet, did you recieve yours? You should get it on friday or the following monday. Sorry I cant provide you with the tracking addy, lost my reciept somewhere.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37566,'de47d0c902','I just heard back from the guy, and it\'s off so anything that\'s &quot;ON HOLD&quot; is available.  I can\'t update the post from work because our proxy blocks off that link.  Go ahead and take your picks, let me know and I\'ll try to send it off tomorrow.'),(37659,'11f42ac284','Try this;  Soft suspension in the front and hard suspension in the back.  \r\n\r\nYou see, when you slow down, for example before cornering, the weight of the car is transfered to the front, puting more weight on the front wheels.  This can create over-steer.  Over steer is when you try to turn and it turns more than you want or spins out.  With more weight on the front wheels, you have more friction/traction on the front wheels.  Softer springs should help that as it will give with added pressure instead of puting more weight on the front wheels.  You can\'t stop all the weight transfer though.\r\n\r\nYou\'ll notice during acceleration you loose a little steering until you get up to speed.  That\'s because the weight is transfered to the back of the car, therefore taking weight off the front wheels.  With less weight you get less traction/friction.  So, you should get more under steer during acceleration.  Hard springs in the back will put more pressure on the back wheels. This helps to take advantage of the torque.  Softer springs will give and you\'ll loose some traction.  Also, hard spring in the back keep some of the weight from transfering back so the front wheels don\'t loose so much traction during acceleration.\r\n\r\nAlso, you can adjust the steering power on the transmitter.  This helps the steering give a little instead of jerking the car.  I have my Kyosho adjusted somewhere between 80~90% power and continue to adjust it depending on terrain.\r\n\r\nIf you still have oversteer with this setup, then try throwing on some soft tires in the back and hard/slick tires in the front.  You may end up with understeer, but you can get use to it and learn to race with it as opposed to over steer which makes you spin out.\r\n\r\nThe other thing that I have and I love is a rear oil shock for my Kyosho.  That thing is cool as hell.  When I hit a bump the car doesn\'t bounce as much so I don\'t loose so much traction.  This doesn\'t completely relate to balancing the damper system except you can get different oils to make the suspension stiffer or softer as well as you can still use springs with the oil shock to stiffen the suspension.  So it makes the rear suspension more adjustable.\r\n\r\nA ball diff can also help.  I have an Iwaver ball diff and it works very well.  You can adjust those as well to help with cornering.  Tighten them for more torque or loosen them for better cornering.  My Atomic ball diff is crap.\r\n\r\nLastly, tires.........  Tire wear like you\'ve noticed plays a part, but not as big of a part as people think.  Tire quality on the other hand is a different story all together.  My answer to that is Gandini foams, at least in the back.  If the tires you have are working good on the track, then you probably don\'t need them.  But, if you want to make this car faster via fets, hot motor and/or lithiums, the Kyosho and Iwaver line of tires wont cut it.  They don\'t have enough traction.\r\n\r\nUltimately this is all theory.  Track time is going to be the end all.  You should go with the theory, but be prepared to adjust.  There are many things that affect balance and steering as you can tell.  You may find that on the surface that you are driving on you only need medium springs in the front instead of soft.  OR etc., etc., etc......\r\n\r\nHope this helps and I\'m jealous.  I currently need a racing partner.  I\'ve been utilizing my wife and a few other people to run comparisons.  It gets the job done, but they\'re not seasoned racers by far.\r\n\r\n :-)'),(34530,'ddd5e7acd3','no man, I am sorry but I have non of those. But thanks for sending it to me  :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34531,'d91656ab14','Yeah, I hear you on that one. (just enough to get into trouble)\r\n\r\nI found out that when I\'m a little more daring, like going up fast, jet it foreward, I seem to do a LOT better, but then when I go in for a slow landing, I crash... lol, I\'m getting enough air time in now so i should get pretty good soon. It\'s just really difficult to rotate a 90 and keep it straight...\r\n\r\nGot more questions:\r\nWhat model of heli are you flying in the video you made?\r\nHow long are the run/charge times?'),(32568,'eb759d6a47','Just wondering how much would it be total including shipping to 39540?  Packing could be whatever\'s the most cheapest and efficient method using priority mail.'),(32598,'06d338fa3e','I just got home.....\r\n\r\nMike Smalley Jr.\r\n3918 Inland Ave.\r\nWest Mifflin, Pa  15122\r\n\r\nThere you go.\r\n\r\nThanks, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(31527,'8ca63c656d','Cool man, glad I can help you out.'),(31528,'ac2dee6794','Giggity Giggity (Quagmire)\r\n\r\nI found you a 27 mhz spiderman Hummer! :)\r\n\r\nAs a side note, I thought to myself, \"Myself, he can\'t buy these there so he probably can\'t buy the motor upgrade either.\" I desided that you would probably want that, so I\'m sending you the motor &amp; gearing upgrades with it. If you want, I have like 6 kokam 145mAh lithium polymers coming sometime this week. I can wait until they get here, and send you one of those too. They only cost me like $3.45US, so it is no big deal! hehe\r\n\r\nYou would have to get a charger, which can be cheap ($10US) or expensifve ($200US) depending on what you want. What do you think?  :???: \r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35662,'2440dc3899','Hey man, I\'m interested in a couple of those... how much for 2 shipped to Portland, OR 97202?'),(34515,'d090220555','Those 3-spokes are from an old school bit racer.  Only one or two body sets had them and it didn\'t come with a track.  They were sold seperately.  They are pretty bitchin and I\'ve been looking for those off and on for a while, but I can\'t find them.\r\n\r\nI\'ll keep an eye out for the M1.  I got it at my LHS.  It may have been an AFX HO slot car, but don\'t quote me on the brand.  If I see it, would you like me to pick one up for you?  We could do a trade or something.'),(32270,'d0e4afd233','no rush, just let me know...\r\n\r\n\r\nrich'),(34084,'244cf3a1f4','sorry  :sad:  i wont do it again im a  :?'),(34085,'503e94c7c2','[quote:503e94c7c2=\"SHAUN\"]sorry  :sad:[/quote:503e94c7c2]\r\nDon\'t be sorry, just quit being an idiot... settle down already.\r\n\r\n[quote:503e94c7c2=\"SHAUN\"]im a  :?[/quote:503e94c7c2]\r\nYeah, no shit.'),(30027,'35cbe8b97b','Naw i don\'t want you to send it until you recieve the cash because that ain\'t fair at all. I\'ll send you my addy when i get the 4.00. At least Canadians have cheaper shipping to U.S (one of the only things we have) because i have sent 20 ZZ batteries in a padded envelope for $1.70!\r\n\r\nThanks for the offer bro, but i\'ll send you cash first.  :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32160,'486bad9c02','I assume you\'ll be selling these then? :???:\r\n\r\nIt interests me.  :grin:'),(29531,'f1a55cd571','[quote:f1a55cd571=\"hue35\"]\r\n\r\nGod damn, man... it did all come together! SF just found a new green connection too... $70 less for a considerably better oz., so that\'s cool. And it\'s super cool you got a dude to run some mini-z scale shit with... when you meetin\' that dude? Is he an overland/mini-z Monster guy, or an MR-02 guy?[/quote:f1a55cd571]Well it\'s not totally  like that. He seems to be a kid that ask too many questions, but he is about 10 minutes up the road. He list a bunch of mini-z and couple 1/10th scales in his sig line. \r\nhttp://mini-zracer.com/forums/showthread.php?t=18286\r\n\r\n[quote:f1a55cd571]You planning on bringin\' an xmod to run with the mini-z 02\'s? The one thing you might think about is the body on those xmods... the xmod bodies were a little too sharp and heavy, so they beat the shit outta the track, and we quit running \'em... if you can do it, a mini-z body or some kind of lexan body would be way better for the track.[/quote:f1a55cd571]Well i I\'ve determined Xmods have no chance of beating Mini-Z\'s without being heavily modded to the point where I don\'t want to bother. i have a better chance of beating you guys with my 04, and that really don\'t make sense.\r\n\r\nSo I figured one of you guys must have an extra Mini-Z. Who knows I might just get an Iwaver by then. I was gonna bring my 04 either way.\r\n\r\nI also got 4 bits set up to race you guys, my original 35mhz bit, pink endbell 3.8, stock gears, a 35mhz bit also a Skyline, the Hiroto one, with teal gears and 2.6. A 45mhz car with a 4.2 and teal gears, and a 45mhz bit with stock gears, and a Tomy 3.0. All are FET modded. That way I got you guys covered for long and short tracks, and in 2 frequencies, in case one frequency doen\'t work out. I think that should cover me.  :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:f1a55cd571]edit: your quote from arch2b\'s post\r\n\r\n[quote:f1a55cd571=\"crazydave\"]Nice set up too. I would dig on road cars much more if I had a nice track like that to race on.[/quote:f1a55cd571]\r\nThat\'s the same track we have, by the way... his might be a little bigger, but it\'s hard to tell.[/quote:f1a55cd571]Yeah, I figured your track was like that, but really I was just trying to make him feel cool, so maybe he\'d come back more often. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\ndave\r\n\r\nedit: forgot to say, I realized to day, the pentip i got for the alloys are not gonna work, and I need a new set of dremel bits, BUT  I am really ff\'in baked, so all is well. :good:'),(35153,'c703aa9b0f','[quote:c703aa9b0f] &lt;--- need a new place to host my .gif... oh, and all my old pics. D\'oh![/quote:c703aa9b0f]If you want, I can set you up an account on my ISP. I get 10mb storage for every email, and 6 emails. I barely use 2.\r\n\r\nIf so, pick a username, it\'ll be the extension in your address.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35158,'15b59e49e5','[quote:15b59e49e5=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Hello Cabo,\r\n                 I put the videos up as MPEG videos.  It works on my computer, but I don\'t know if it\'s working on anybnody elses computer.  Nobody has responded to the videos (3~4days).  I think people have just been busy recently, but I was wondering if they came out ok or is it just shitty quality?  I couldn\'t figure out how to change the file to Windows Media.\r\n\r\nThey\'re at the bottom.\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6984&amp;start=15[/url]\r\n\r\nSorry for the \"I\'m a retard on the computer\" question, but honestly, I\'m a retard on the computer.  Just kidding :lol: .  No seriously though :-? .[/quote:15b59e49e5]\r\nNo worries man.\r\nYea they work, I watched them, just haven\'t had time to honestly reply.\r\nThe video quality was a little poor, it was hard to see the car with the camera moving and stuff.\r\nI\'m guessing the car was moving too quick for the camera to focus on it while both car and camera are moving - but I still got the idea.\r\nThat fooker huals ass. Can\'t believe it didn\'t explode when you nailed the pole or whatever that was. lol\r\nLike I said, I\'ve been super busy lately so I haven\'t really paid much attention on the boards lately to see how busy they\'ve been. I\'m not even sure I\'ve posted a reply to anything in the past few days. lol\r\n\r\nAnyways, you car is impressive as hell.\r\nMaybe try to get some better footage and post them up too?'),(35652,'92fe167e19','hey man-\r\n\r\nSo what kind of extra bit stuff ya got laying around? I have a 1st gen red supra xmod collecting dust. I also have pretty much every upgrade as well as all the extra parts minus one set of wheels from the wheel set. It has been well driven, but all indoors by an adult (me).\r\n\r\nI wasn\'t really thinking about selling or trading it, but I thought I\'d check and see what you wanted to trade for. Don\'t be offended if I decline, just checking.  :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34439,'6c4054058f','Just came in the mail!  Awsome thanks again'),(37584,'5395e86bc9','Thanks again Hachi...i think i might just pick up an iwaver to tool around with!'),(37415,'7e6b31afae','Hi-\r\nWhat website do you use for storing pictures to post on this site.\r\n                                                                             -99skyline\r\nP.S.\r\nThank you for help and information.'),(36185,'7116063a89','Look, dumbfuck, don\'t think it\'s as easy as a new user ID. You just need to fuckin\' settle down.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\n\r\nhue35\r\n\r\nModerator/dumbass american'),(36186,'18071f8a33','Sorry dude, i just got wound up, us english are pretty stupid too, we are ignorrant and get annoyed easily Which you obviously already knew..!) :l New start?'),(36187,'18071f8a33','Sorry dude, i just got wound up, us english are pretty stupid too, we are ignorrant and get annoyed easily Which you obviously already knew..!) :l New start?'),(36198,'119724e880','Ok, thanks very much. Im glad were cool  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36199,'119724e880','Ok, thanks very much. Im glad were cool  :-)'),(34679,'1f2dfe2387','&gt; OK, I got it. So, uh... how do I use it? LOL... seriously, though, I think I\'ll need to understand what the different buttons do, since the don\'t say. \r\n\r\nThere are two buttons IIRC, one is to reverse the polarity, and one is to check the polarity (because reverse charging may not be the fun you have in mind! =)\r\n\r\nIf you connect the battery without plugging it into the wall, and press the check polarity button (on the left?) it will either be green or not. Green means it is correct to charge. Remember not to have it plugged in when you are checking polarity. You can press the reverse polarity button, or just switch it around if you are backwards.\r\n\r\nI believe plugging it in starts the charge.\r\n\r\n&gt;I\'ll take a pic and label the parts in question... that cool? Also, those connectors.. you weren\'t thinking those were the right size for a bit, were you? I used them on a zipzap, and a clone. I just cut off most of the connector and used them as really small connectors.\r\n\r\n&gt;If so, explain just a bit how you use those, they seem bigger than I was thinking. \r\n\r\nI used them on a zipzap, and a clone. I just cut off most of the connector and used them as really small connectors.\r\n\r\n&gt;Sorry for the dumb questions, but I\'ve never used these batts before, and it seems like there are some definite \"don\'ts\" in the Lipo world. \r\n\r\nBEWARE! =)\r\n\r\n&gt;I\'ll try to get a pic together with my questions in the next day or so. \r\n\r\nSure, but it has been a while since I used it. I\'ll help in any way I can. The instructions were on the box it came in, which went in the \"special file\" at the end of my desk.  :-D \r\n\r\n-JNY'),(32285,'abd47a44dd','Happy Birthday Miget :)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37561,'6b2a9adc91','no thanks, some other stuff arose :('),(37562,'c50c3fa57b','I\'m updating the list because someone asked me to hold a bunch of bodies.  I\'ll mark them on the main thread.  But anything on the list is open for negotiation.  I also have some red, blue and a couple yellow ZZ motors.  \r\nI\'m gonna follow up with him to see if he\'s gonna get them or not.\r\n\r\nCome to think of it, he has me holding a lot of bodies so I\'ll message him now.  Let me know if anything he has on hold is something you\'re interested in.  I do have multiples of some of them and was gonna hold it for myself.'),(37563,'6e0f485670','What ever is left is fine, just let me know'),(37568,'5a52641091','sup man?\r\n\r\nJust letting you know, you\'re posting alot. And they\'re all useless posts. I\'m not getting on your back or anything, but post count means nothing here. Plus the pimps don\'t like it when useless stuff is posted. Also your digging up oldish threads and posting stuff like &quot;sweet ride&quot;. Doesn\'t fly here.\r\n\r\nAgain, I\'m not getting on you, just giving you a heads up for how things are done here. \r\n\r\n\r\nKeep cool\r\nMaxx'),(32172,'5ed4e94fd1','[quote:5ed4e94fd1=\"LBRC\"]The original Spud cost too much, but I am working on affordable motors, several in fact. After seeing the message I contacted Mike and we have had several lengthy discussions, he seems to love micro cars as much as we do and is definitely dedicated to the Epoch.  \r\n\r\nNot sure who will be selling the motors yet but that doesnt matter as long as they are available and as soon as possible.  \r\n\r\nHe has a lot planed for the Epoch but nothing that will happen overnight.  Right now roomers seem the be a big problem, especially with the various internet forums/stores and such, there is a good deal of ill will toward the old management (not limited to the internet) and a great deal of misunderstanding on how the whole manufacturing and distribution system works.  For example Tiny is right the Epochs never went out of production, only the North American distributor went tits up, now that Mike has the rights back it will take a while to get things going, and any changes will take even longer and unfortunately they also cost, so it all boils down to time and money but in the long run if his plans work I think you will be happy.  [b:5ed4e94fd1]At least he seems to understand that hop-ups and aftermarket parts are a must, and that the Epoch will need to change and evolve to stay competitive.[/b:5ed4e94fd1][/quote:5ed4e94fd1]\r\n\r\nSounds like there is some actual work and ideas that are coming around to make things better for the Epoch.\r\n\r\nI hope things get off to a great start and that we\'ll see some results sooner, rather than later.  Thats what people need to see in order to make all of the past either go away or become more of a distant memory.\r\n\r\nKeep me updated.  I really do like my Epochs and would love to see some of the ideas and suggestions that are out there get followed thru with.\r\n\r\nJust gotta tackle the pricing now. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36298,'1795a90e1b','[quote:1795a90e1b=\"pimpsmurf\"]&gt; Does it come with a controller to use the 1:16 elec\'s with.\r\nIt comes with the MZM controller, which works with the 1:16 electronics\r\n\r\n&gt; How did you make the servo work?\r\nThe 1:16 electronics are kyosho-brand. I just wired it up.\r\n\r\n&gt;Did you get those parts in today?\r\nTomorrow or Monday.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:1795a90e1b]\r\n\r\nAllright sounds like a deal, how can i pass it up.\r\n\r\nI\'ll send you paypal tonight 215 If you can ship it priority insured.\r\n\r\nAnd just to let you know this is the most money ive ever trusted anyone with ever so dont let me down pimp! :-o'),(32935,'a0968cf741','Hey buddy you were saying you wish you could have gotten one of the 57 chevy bodies? Do you want one? if so I have an extra one I would be willing to part with for a buddy! just send your address and I will get it out to you! Kind of a hey its 2:00 AM and I wana supprise ya!  :eek: \r\n\r\nPM me back if you want it and its yours! its the clear body so you will have to paint it and such but its free so ya cant bitch to bad!  :lol: \r\n\r\ntake care man!\r\nAaron \r\nSWG'),(32930,'59bfe19f0c','No worries mate.  :-o \r\n\r\nI forgot to mention that one of  [url=http://www.tinyrc.com/shop/product.php?pid=499]these[/url] in installed in one of the chassis. It\'s the bit-size (purple I think) motor. I hear it is pretty nice.  :cool: \r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32974,'a9e17948e9','[quote:a9e17948e9=\"Finks\"]OK as I alluded to in the thread I of course am pissed as hell about the group buy and thought I would vent that frustration more constructively.  \r\n\r\nMy proposal is to hold a contest  for everyone, even those not involved in the group buy to write the best email to Michael and his Mini Speeder crew.  All letters will be posted here and then all will be mailed to this fuckwad.  \r\n\r\nAlso as we like to do here in the Hood, hopefully the contest could be advertised at other sites so that the whole community knows about this Douche.  \r\n\r\nOh and as for a prize for the winner, I got ya covered.  I have the Custom Porsche that I wanted to donate to the hopefully revitalization of the auction block.  You know, the one that looks like my RotM Porsche?  \r\n\r\nAnyhow, let me know if I am going overboard or if this is something that the hood would support.  Thanks\r\n\r\nFinks[/quote:a9e17948e9]\r\nWelp, right now I\'m drunk so unfortunately for you, you\'re going to get a somewhat cheesey response.\r\nWell... not so much cheesey as a \"hey, let me respond to this later\" thang.\r\n\r\nLet me just say, I know you gotta be pissed, I\'d be - anyone would.\r\nYou took the brunt of the hit, that\'s bullshit.\r\nThat Michael dude is an asshole. That\'s no way to run a business, especially with someone how just placed a $500 order.\r\n\r\nI\'m not sure where this left off.\r\nLast I heard you said you were waiting for shit from Michael - he could send it to you or your mother-in-law.\r\nTime went by and you sent shit out to us.\r\n\r\nSo, are you certain that nothing else is coming?\r\nHe\'s not communicating anymore? Nothing is being done to correct his error?\r\n\r\nMost likely, if that is the case, we can probably put something together - no problem. But I want to make sure before we fry somebody, we\'re in the right to do so.\r\n\r\nAnyways, like I said, I\'m fuckered up right now so I\'ll have more clear thoughts on this later.'),(32178,'2408010d48','Sup Dave?\r\n\r\nI thought it was wrong for sg219 to approach it like that, so I deleted the whole deal. \r\n\r\nYou don\'t have to defend youself here, and I\'ll see to that.   You\'ve always been super cool, and it\'s only fair you be treated the same.\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll be in the market for some epoch stuff you can count on it.  Just have to calm down on the Maxx, and the Revo parts....lol.\r\n\r\nThose alloy wheels look great too. Will they be available?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29536,'8efc5ee31f','[quote:8efc5ee31f=\"hue35\"][quote:8efc5ee31f=\"crazydave\"]edit: forgot to say, I realized to day, the pentip i got for the alloys are not gonna work, and I need a new set of dremel bits, BUT  I am really ff\'in baked, so all is well. :good:[/quote:8efc5ee31f]\r\n :lol:  I\'m not followin\' ya on the pen tip thing, but I\'ll be followin\' your lead on being really ff\'in baked in about an hour (even though it\'s exactly 4:20 right now).\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMat[/quote:8efc5ee31f] http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1782\r\n;)\r\n\r\nFuck I\'m stoned. :lol: \r\n\r\ndave'),(29658,'b5cc48202f','Hey,\r\n\r\nI was wondering how did you contact Jmays to buy one of his VW shells?\r\n\r\nI searched through his profile, but no email address..'),(29659,'b5047241f4','PM is the only way, he has been MIA now for 2 months.... :-?'),(34644,'9c81ac794a','Yeah no trade, just sending some shit to eachother  :-o , yeah man, this ain\'t gonna be no stock epoch either ;) :D'),(31811,'745a5f1cce','The SE is a parts car, not fixable at all.  Hook me up w/ something (anything really, but I do dig odd shells) and I\'ll throw in a working SE chassis to boot.\r\n\r\nto paypal me the money you have to have the account linked to your bank account or a credit card and enter my email address (which is Finks1@gmail.com)  It\'s fairly simple.   Once I get the money I\'ll pick up the upgrade kit.  Let me know about the working SE.\r\n\r\nP.S. Oh and don\'t feel shy about offering me something for it, I have shit loads of em.  I used to work at RS and even after I quit the guys there would sell me the \"broken\" ones for like $2 a piece. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31072,'10b8ec1770','cool!!!!!!\r\nyeah, i had to think for 20 sec on that one...... :lol:'),(30778,'3250713b58','I will give you $7.00 for the kit, do you have paypal?'),(31952,'dc8b075eba','I know its you.\r\n\r\nEveryone told me its you.\r\n\r\n\r\nSo dont even lie.'),(31953,'8a89f7d0f0','[quote:8a89f7d0f0=\"blindrider3\"]I know its you.\r\n\r\nEveryone told me its you.\r\n\r\n\r\nSo dont even lie.[/quote:8a89f7d0f0]\r\n\r\n\r\nIt was cool that you explained to me what was going on with that.\r\nWhen I went there yesterday, I couldn\'t even understand most of the posts.\r\n\r\nAnyway, listen, we could go \'round and \'round with this, but I see no reason. Who is \'everybody\' that told you? I don\'t think people know me very well as of yet.\r\nI went to go see where the pics were linked to, but all was gone. And you said it was linked to motorgong? hmmmmm\r\nHave ya found out anything else yet?\r\n\r\nAgain, I have nothing against you.'),(36983,'cad31646f6','[quote:cad31646f6=\"payaso\"]Cool, that\'s kinda what I was thinkin, but what do you mean by &quot;tubby&quot;?\r\n\r\nDid you mean the body, or chassis, cause he wanted it cause of the MM chassis over the RM one.\r\n\r\n\r\nthanks for the insight.  He also ordered the 911 Carrera body to go with it, that fucker..[/quote:cad31646f6]\r\nThat body is considerably bigger and bulkier than the McClaren, so I figured it would drive kinda tubby by comparison. I agree that the MM is the way to go, but that and the M3 are the last 2 I\'d choose, simply due to body size.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34857,'9c321cdf8e','http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/1970-Super-Sport-468-Lingenfelter-4-speed_W0QQitemZ4587346877QQcategoryZ6172QQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem\r\n\r\nThere ya go.'),(37074,'29db99bad2','Im going up to Canada this weekend, how far is whre u live from Cambridge, ON???? Matbe we could race or sumthing, MAYBE* :-)'),(36164,'6143422264','yep the drag gear'),(34517,'762e4a72be','[quote:762e4a72be=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Those 3-spokes are from an old school bit racer.  Only one or two body sets had them and it didn\'t come with a track.  They were sold seperately.  They are pretty bitchin and I\'ve been looking for those off and on for a while, but I can\'t find them.\r\n\r\nI\'ll keep an eye out for the M1.  I got it at my LHS.  It may have been an AFX HO slot car, but don\'t quote me on the brand.  If I see it, would you like me to pick one up for you?  We could do a trade or something.[/quote:762e4a72be]\r\n\r\nYeah man, that\'d be sweet... thanks. I got plenty of OG bit stuff to trade.'),(30392,'e4904711ea','Hey man, that looks like it\'s going to be a real nice looking shell. I\'d like to propose a little trade... I\'m a graphic designer/photographer, and if you send me a small handfull of those, I\'ll take some really nice photographs of them for use on your web site. Check out my gallery to see my photography style... if you like what you see, then let\'s do it. I\'ll make that thing look like a million bucks, and it\'ll only cost ya a small quantity of bodies and a little shipping.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37582,'b8ee2eed6e','I am currently running some comparisons with the Iwaver 02 and the MR-02.  The speed is pretty equal, but the handling is a little in the MR-02\'s favor.  There are a lot of little problems that I fixed on the Iwaver.  I\'ve nick-named it the epoxy machine because there is more epoxy in it holding things together than I care for.  Not the end of the world though.  I put the same hot motor in and 3 X 2 stack of 7317 fets.  I haven\'t modified the firelap 2.0 yet, but I will probably get that done this weekend.  If the firelap can keep up with the MR-02 then that would make it a steel for &lt;$50.  I\'ve already noticed the steering doesn\'t seem as nice on the firelap as the MR-02, but I\'m curious if some fets wont fix that.\r\n\r\nWill know more soon.'),(35956,'e7700ea13b','O MAN THANKS ALOT!!!\r\n\r\n\r\nThose look great, once I get some sleep i am going to try em out, I gotta get a hold of those resistors! \r\n\r\nI think i am also going to solder two extra cells. You think the 6 cells will help the speed keep up with an MR-02? I want it more torquier...\r\n\r\nThis is what i got planned out.\r\n\r\n- medium drive shaft\r\n- awd\r\n- bearings\r\n- 6 cells 1000 mah 1.2v\r\n- white drift motor\r\n- CF drive shaft, once I get one in lol\r\n- Tie rod mod\r\n- steering resistor mod\r\n\r\nAnything else..remember it is a short track, has two nice straights the rest is gradual curvers, perfect for top speed turning!'),(37899,'b64d497811','[quote:b64d497811=\"hue35\"]Hey man, I\'m not blowin\' you off, I\'ve just been slammed like a muthafucka. Saw ya just now, so I thought I\'d at least say hey.\r\n\r\nTalk to ya more thoroughly later.[/quote:b64d497811]Cool. :-o  \r\nI assumed you were busy. That\'s pretty much been your story lately.  \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29943,'f1a0303539','Ok, I\'ll stop starting new subjects right about now, but fuckin finks man. I can\'t believe how that fucker can always manage to say the one thing that is gonna piss me off. Every fucking time. Fuck I hate him.\r\n\r\nDid you see this?\r\n[quote:f1a0303539]Holy hell! I can\'t belive I placed. Personally this was one of the most jaw dropping contests to date. I mean not only did people drop some KILLER body mods and paint, but fuck, like 50% of the entries had scratch built or totally custom chassis! Of course congrats to SWG and Sport, but mad props to the others because I have a feeling 1st and 2nd place took thier positions pretty solidly, but 3rd must have been highly contested. [/quote:f1a0303539]At least he alluded to sucking, but christ did he really think it was that good? Ok then, here let me scrap my jaw up. No really. Yeah fifty percent, what\'s that like 5? :roll:\r\n\r\ndave'),(29995,'7d4cb72909','Thanks man.  I ended up just going to the hobby store and picking up a cheap HO scale car.  I only needed it for the rear gearing configuration.  The plan is to make some micro U joints (in process) and make a mini dune buggy style bit,, its very tiny to its taking some time,, Thanks again\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36347,'a62a0e1fdc','most of the time i use the zipzap package for the plastic so a good set of scissors works well and to touch up i use my dremel drill with a sanding bit or something\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36250,'cb6ecec1ae','[quote:cb6ecec1ae=\"sessiz\"]I seem to remember something about you having a design company or doing bussiness in the &quot;graphic design&quot; area. If I\'m wrong disregard this pm. :lol: \r\n\r\nHere\'s where I need your help/advice. I have a chance at a job as a low level graphics &quot;guy&quot; for transworld entertainment corp. My cousin is a lead tech guy over there and he is getting me a foot in the door. (director of marketing owes him big  :lol: )\r\nWhat I need from you is a tip or two on what exactly should I put together potfolio wise to show this guy. I got a rough idea of what this cat wants to see and I feel gay as fuck typing this shit but any help from you would be much apreciated.  :-)[/quote:cb6ecec1ae]\r\n\r\nNope, you got it right, that\'s what I do.\r\n\r\nWhat kind of job is it? What kind of graphic work? Is it more of a creative position or a technical position? How soon is your interview? Do you have samples of any work other than what I\'ve seen here?\r\n\r\nI\'m happy to help a brutha out as much as possible. If you have enough time, I can help you get a portfolio together. I interview at least 20 people a year, so I see all kinds of stuff. Here\'s some portfolio things to consider right off the bat:\r\n\r\n- Not too much and not too little in content. Like more than 10 pieces and less than 20.\r\n\r\n- Be able to tell a story about each of your pieces. What was the point of the project? what were you trying to accomplish? What problems did you encounter and how did you solve them?\r\n\r\n- Include something that shows your thought process, like a sketch that led to a finished piece, or three options you generated before developing a final piece.\r\n\r\n- Start with the thing you think is your &quot;best&quot; work, and finish with the thing that is your &quot;favorite&quot; piece.\r\n\r\n- Have a sample sheet with 2 or 3 of your best things on an 8.5 x 11 sheet to clip to your resume, so they can remember who you are.\r\n\r\n- If you don\'t have a lot or any real-world work to show, invent your own. Find some ad or design that you think could be done better and do it up. Along these lines, I routinely show work in my portfolio that was rejected by clients. Sometimes we generate good designs that they don\'t pick. Doesn\'t mean it wasn\'t good. The people you show your portfolio to will never know the difference.\r\n\r\nNow I feel all gay, but if you answer some of those questions I can help you more. If you have enough time, I have a kick-ass color printer and a Fed-Ex account, I might be able to help you get it printed up in some cool little portfolio.\r\n\r\nIf you want to check out our incomplete website, you can see where I left off last summer:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.grymttr.com/flashtest/\r\n\r\nOnly the &quot;enviro&quot; and &quot;collateral&quot; sections are hooked up, but I hope to finish the rest before this summer. \r\n\r\nSuperFly'),(36512,'dcd6fc3ad7','Thats cool, a little body work is a simple thing to fix anyways.  I was just wondering if i could take it off your hands,, i only need the evo body.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36514,'ca77ee0537','[quote:ca77ee0537=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Well, you sent me a gen 1 alloy front axle/joint cups.  I ordered a rear alloy axle.  \r\n\r\nAlso, The alloy rear lower arms cause binding in the rear axle.  Do I need to get the rear alloy towers to get them to fit right?\r\n\r\nSorry, this is kinda short and sweet.  My e-mails went into more detail.  \r\n\r\nI know GPM made the rear lower arms so I of-course don\'t hold any blame on you for that.  I just wondered if you had any essay on them.\r\n\r\nThe wrong axle is all your fault though. :grin:  But, I appreciate your service and you\'ve always been good to me in the past.  I could actually order the rear axle again and you could charge me for a front.  This would equal out the cost at least.\r\n\r\nThanx for your time.\r\n\r\nHachi[/quote:ca77ee0537]\r\n\r\nI have the rear axle cups in Purple, Pink, Bronze,or gold.  Which color do you prefer?\r\n\r\nGetting the rear gearboxes will help also because RS didn\'t mold the plastic one the same for every car.  If you want the Rear gearboxes just order that from the site and let me know what color rear cup you want.  Don\'t worry about the front cups you can keep them.'),(30000,'fe39259e71','yeah the cheap ho\'s are the way to go since ur only using the rears. also the connectors that get power from the track have some springs under um that are perfect and non magnetic  for bits and such.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29670,'bad825c6f5','[quote:bad825c6f5=\"ezenterprises\"]i went over the list and wanted to send you an actual order..... Wife complainin so keepin order small for now........hopefully in future will finish. Would like everything Blue. THANKS\r\n\r\nXM021\r\nXM039F\r\nXM039F/4WD\r\nXM039R\r\nXM041\r\nXM041F/4WD\r\nMZ002\r\nSend me a paypal bill to X_FUNSTUFF_X@yahoo.com when i need to pay.[/quote:bad825c6f5]\r\n\r\nPlaced the order and am waiting for the confirmation from them.'),(34485,'8e77a1f289','It looks like I\'m all out of wrx and gloria bodies. I do have one each of the Tomy Sets left. Let me know if interested in those.\r\n\r\nFor the perfection beetle bodies, I have them available in 9 colors and I have at least 2 of each color. Colors available are black, blue, white, silver, bronze  orange, pea green, yellow, charcoal silver, &amp; red. \r\n\r\nTHanks!'),(30096,'21edba2c18','Hey, just sent you money. I\'m just getting one for now, but I\'m sure I\'m gonna need more. You didn\'t mention shipping, but I went ahead and sent you $15. You can ship it Priorty Mail if you\'d like.\r\n\r\nThat would be great if you posted the review on your site. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\nI just read your articles. Honestly dude, you\'re just so full of information I think you confuse a lot of people, but I always learn a lot from you and appreciate that there\'s someoene out there that explains this stuff to me. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo if I\'m understanding this correctly, it should perform like a dual cell car. If that is the case, I may be way overshooting my goals, but that\'s gonna be super cool. I\'m getting excited now. :-D \r\n\r\ndave'),(30110,'e5a0e8392e','[img:e5a0e8392e]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10076/HPIM0175.JPG[/img:e5a0e8392e]\r\n\r\nI forgot to mention that  part of a trace come off during a uninstall. Its no biggy and I will show you what you need to do when you install it. I also trimmed away part of the board so you can swap crystals easy.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30113,'24ad581b52','Almost forgot,\r\n\r\nJarrod Edwards\r\n1978 Kings Chapel Rd \r\nAPT#74\r\nPerry, GA 31069'),(37754,'99e79a0920','cool, so you interested in the trade???\r\n :-)'),(36711,'150791de69','Hey I\'ll check out what you got then get back to ya. Sorry for the delay, I have been travelin\' around a bit and just got back in. I\'ll speak to ya inna short time.\r\nThanks!\r\nShirazz'),(35515,'c5a4369ba3','Finally, I got a start. I really didn\'t want to do the wheels if I wasn\'t feeling it, \'cause you know, they gotta be round and stuff, and that\'s really hard. That was my hang up. So I finally just did it, I finally got the hard parts out of the way, and I\'m extremely happy with the results. Better than mine.\r\n\r\nHere your wheels, Tomy pullback rears, and ZZ fronts:\r\n[img:c5a4369ba3]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/psII1.jpg[/img:c5a4369ba3]\r\n\r\nI gotta go back and clean up that bevel on the fronts, didn\'t have any fine grit sand paper around, but I went ahead and painted in the silver ring to give you an idea.\r\n\r\n\r\n...and here\'s the beginnings of your chassis. You this part is tricky cause its gotta be square. It\'s Zip Zap based. I Figured they\'re only a couple bucks more than clones when on clearance, and that gives a solid platform.\r\n[img:c5a4369ba3]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/psII3.jpg[/img:c5a4369ba3]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'m not flossin\' this until I\'m done, so you\'re gonna get the progress shots, cause you know I gotta show someone. :lol:\r\n\r\ndave'),(31750,'8c0891c4e6','Have you shipped this yet? If not, please don\'t send it. I\'m not able to send you one of these for some reason. It was returned to me today. I don\'t know what happened, but I have a number here to call for more information. If you have shipped it, don\'t worry. I will be glad to send it back at my expense, forward it to another buyer if you prefer, or send you this ZZMT as soon as I clear this up.\r\n\r\nI am sorry for the problem. This really sucks ass, and I don\'t want it to affect my reputation. Especially since I have not been posting here for very long.\r\n\r\nSorry again,\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31764,'8caa214183','Hey, superfly, what\'s happening?\r\n\r\nI posted this review of the DC Mod, and I put a lot of time into it, and now nobody has seemed to notice it, and I\'m pissed. So I\'m on a little promotional spree right now.\r\n\r\nI\'m hitting you up to check it out, because the video has the Silver Vette in it, and I thought you\'d be interest to see how it performs, since I got one sitting here for you.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6427\r\n\r\nThank you for your time. :-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(33761,'8ff28f3ba2','[quote:8ff28f3ba2=\"hue35\"]Those are cool... so, I assume you\'ve tried the 1:64 scale and they\'re too big? It seems, based on the way those fit on a T-Jet, the 1:72 might be too small. Bits are kinda between the 2, huh? I guess when I think about it, bits are so distorted it makes things like decals kinda tricky... I could see \"a little too small\" being easier to work with than \"a little too large\".[/quote:8ff28f3ba2]I debated over 1/64th or 1/72nd when I ordered for my prostocker. I ended up going with the 1/64th and they were larger than I pictured. I had wanted them clustered behind the front wheel. I meant to get both this time, but they had a lot more in the T-jet section. They just had the one before. So I went all nuts and blew my wad right there. I had just ordered a superslicks after Superfly mentioned they were cheap. So that cut into my budget. I haven\'t even looked at the 1/64th section to see of they have anything new. I gonna have to do that. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo yeah, I\'m figuring smaller will give me more flexibility. Especially on a bit, its hard enough on a Zip Zap, I figure they\'d be harder to cram on  a bit. I\'m gonna scan a picture for you, the car my gasser is gonna be based off of.\r\n\r\n[quote:8ff28f3ba2]Cool. You\'ll have to give me a ballpark idea when you can... I\'m about to start (in a month or two) a major project at my house that could screw things up from a \"having guests\" perspective. Although, if you wouldn\'t mind the disaster for a coupla days, it probably wouldn\'t matter too much. How long a trip were you thinking, by the way? Like, a Friday afternoon through Sunday afternoon/evening kind of thing?.[/quote:8ff28f3ba2]Yeah, its gonna have to be like that now, because I\'m taking my week off of work ASAP. :lol: \r\n\r\nDisaster my ass, gotta soft spot for me to lay on, I\'ll sleep there. As long as we can get to the gueetars. 8) \r\n\r\nI figure after the 1st of the year is a good plan. Get the holiday BS out of the way, let my wife take her trip so I can hold that over her head. Ask santa for an Iwaver for Christmas, and we\'re in business. :-o \r\n[quote:8ff28f3ba2]Man, I gotta get a new car built... I just gotta. [/quote:8ff28f3ba2]Well yeah, you always gotta do that. Me too. :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:8ff28f3ba2]Oh, I picked up on of the new SE\'s... man, right outta the box, these things go even better than I thought. I haven\'t even run a full charge through it, \'cuz my floors were too dog haired, but it seemed like the right amount of power. So, does the FET mod really help these out that much? Also, do you think the Duty Cycle mod is even worth doing on these things? I guess I can compare to Greg\'s Vette to see the difference... he hasn\'t even run that, by the way... that\'s how busy that guy\'s been. We\'re down to about once a month, which sucks. Neither of us have had the time... hopefully winter will bring on some more racing nights.[/quote:8ff28f3ba2]See I was telling you about them SEs. I\'m not too sure what the FET mod did. I got so in the habit of FET modding SEs right out of the package, I had only run it for a couple minutes, but I think it did help it pull the red gears. Don\'t think you\'d see any difference with the stock 12:1. The DC mod will double the performance of that car. Its a bit too much for some situations. If you only have one vette, you might want to keep that stock, for something more mild than the DC mod, but still acceptable. You also might want to stick it in the vette for the improved steering, but I think it\'d be of better use in a GTO/Torino/Chevelle/Ford GT/NSX that has good steering, but the crappy DC cycle. My Chevelle had perfect steering, but the GTO I got to replace it has some slight jitters, occasionally. The DC mod helped the steering enough that its close enough to perfect now. Code said that was just a side effect, and only happened on some cars, I\'m assuming the newer ones.\r\n\r\nSuperfly needs to try that car out, I\'ve been waiting. :lol: \r\nYou\'ll have to compare to his, and let me know if the FET seem to make a big difference.\r\n\r\n[quote:8ff28f3ba2]I\'m gonna try to take one of my old, broken SE\'s back today, dressed up in the Vette\'s shell and packaging, to try and get another of these chassis... I figure they owe it to me. The first one shouldn\'t have sucked, ya know? I\'ll let ya know how that went. [/quote:8ff28f3ba2]Yeah, let me know how that goes. :-o \r\n\r\nDave'),(36978,'1055ecc7c1','[quote:1055ecc7c1=\"payaso\"]I\'ve been racing the shit out of my min z about the last month with the dude at work. He\'s got the XMOD evo truck, and I got the X5 BMW.\r\n\r\nHe now has seen the light, and ordered a mini Z MR-02MM Scaglietti, cause he\'s addicted.  My Q is He paid $104 for the ready set. Is that a good price?\r\n\r\nMy other Q is, now that he\'s gettin a car, he\'ll have the obvious advantage over my truck. Would you recomend a certain model. Are the MR-02MM better than the 02MR chassis\r\n\r\nWas also thinkin bout goin with a used one. Worth it, or not?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-S[/quote:1055ecc7c1]\r\n\r\n$104 is a killer deal on a new ready set... that Scaglietti ia going to be a little on the tubby side, so I\'d keep that in mind. If I were you, I\'d get one of the MM cars... the Enzo, the McClaren, the BMW M3 or the Lamborghini Murcielago (I\'m pretty sure this is MM)... I have the McClaren F1, and I\'d get it again in a heartbeat. It\'s really compact, super low, and doesn\'t have much overhang in the front or back (the Enzo has a long front)... it\'s the body that\'s closest to runnin\' a bare chassis. \r\n\r\nIf you can find a used one in nice condition, grab it. Just make sure you see clear pictures. And, if there\'s a FET upgrade or a turbo, I\'d make sure to get close-ups of that stuff... if it isn\'t a clean install, I\'d avoid it. The good news is that iWaiver PCBs for that car are on the market now for about $30 (a little less), so even if somethin\' went haywire, you could get it runnin\' fairly cheap.\r\n\r\nI\'d probably get a new one, since the dude you\'re runnin\' with has a new one. Then y\'all can upgrade them as a matched pair along the way, which makes the racing better... it\'s cool when SF and I start out with a stock pair, then upgrade each a little at a time... it makes for a cool evolution.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37122,'524405791c','[quote:524405791c=\"sessiz\"]I figured as much man...sorry. :-([/quote:524405791c]\r\nIt\'s cool... sorry I was short with ya, but it was just about GO time!\r\n\r\nOK, now, have at it... I deleted your post, but if you could put it up again, that\'d be perfect... or somethin\' like it, anyway.\r\n\r\nMan, this shit is almost the all-time funniest shit ever... god damn, just when you think we\'re out of dumb fucks....\r\n\r\n :lol:'),(37123,'1be69b7c98','He kinda makes ya miss charlie huh? :lol:'),(37697,'059d2cdf6e','so how\'s $10 + shipping grab ya?'),(37140,'61e4912f65','Just so ya know, Juzi\'s Cust[b:61e4912f65]u[/b:61e4912f65]mz (with the 3rd &quot;u&quot; and penismonster avatar) is me... I figured I could fuck with  that kid pretty good, but he may have already headed for the hills..  :lol: \r\n\r\nI couldn\'t tell if you were hip to it or not, so I thought I\'d make sure.  :-o'),(33981,'44302019eb','[quote:44302019eb=\"arfin\"]Yeah it aint my place, so i\'ll stay out.[/quote:44302019eb]\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n[quote:44302019eb=\"arfin\"]So lets just forget about this, and be cool.  :-o[/quote:44302019eb]\r\n :-o \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nhue35');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33996,'fea5e75efe','what are you talking about? You removed the spring? Did you cut it or did you pry it out? When you just pried it out there is no problem, glue it back in the good way around. If you damaged a single wire in the spring then you are most likely fucked.'),(37405,'8b2449b497','Bird has two sets he\'s willing to trade.  I\'m going over there tonight to pick them up.\r\n\r\nHe was wondering about some of the decals like you sent me.  He\'s not picky.  He said to be creative when trading.  (catch my drift?) :wink: \r\n\r\nI\'ll send them out sometime in the next couple of days. :-o'),(31797,'b3955af485','Yo DT, you out there???\r\n\r\nFrom: mikirgra \r\nTo: DarkTari \r\nPosted: Mon Jul 18, 2005 1:23 pm \r\nSubject: Lupin the III BCG  \r\nDarkTari &amp; payaso, \r\n\r\nI\'m an idot and an ass, and you can call me out publicly if you want. I was too tired to think clearly when I posted that about the Fiat bit (aka, Lupin the III BCG) the other night. My post was WAY to short on details, and it opened me up to just such a bind. I got PM\'s from both of you, and since my post didn\'t state that I would sell to the first to PM me, well, here we are. Don\'t misunderstand, I will NOT allow you to bid against each other. I would like your help on figuring this out. I know either of you will give the home it deserves. I think I paid like $32 plus shipping from Japan for it. I\'ll sell it to either of you for $30 shipped. Maybe whoever doesn\'t get mine can get one from HLJ?  \r\n\r\nSorry guys. I fubar\'d this one. I\'ll post to the forum that it\'s spoken for. Let me know what you guys think. Don\'t know if it matters to you, but here are the times on your PM\'s to me: \r\n\r\nDT: 7/16 @ 5am \r\nPY: 7/16 @ 2:45PM \r\n\r\nYou\'re the only two, thank goodness, and I wish I had two. Hoping we can work it out.'),(29731,'d7829313cf','[quote:d7829313cf=\"hue35\"]\r\n\r\n[quote:d7829313cf=\"crazydave\"]But I figure fuck it, I enjoy it, and it gives me a creative outlet. I actually have gained a much greater understanding of electronics from bits. [/quote:d7829313cf]\r\nI\'ve learned a ton as well... the thing I realize about Bits, having recently taken a chunk of time away from them, is that they (via bitPimps) actually help to give me confidence. My job has sucked so much of my confidence and spirit away, it\'s really important for me to do something that gets a little of that back... there\'s nothin\' like getting to the finish line of a project that\'s goin\' well. When it\'s all done and I\'m photographing it and making a post in \'flossin\'... it\'s been awhile for me, and I really miss that shit. I got a few of those coming up soon, and I\'m really looking forward to it. [/quote:d7829313cf]Exactly. Damn, its crazy talking with you. You know what\'s up.\r\n\r\n \r\n[quote:d7829313cf][quote:d7829313cf=\"crazydave\"]...You gots yourself a band, and and shit, I\'m jealous. :lol: [/quote:d7829313cf]\r\nMan, I haven\'t been in a band for quite awhile now... like, 2 years. I miss it.  :sad: I\'ll find something... maybe, I don\'t know. I actually want to do more little recordings and try to acquire some of them song-writing skills we were talking about. I also want to get back to my drums... ah fuck, too many things, I tells ya... too many fuckin\' things.[/quote:d7829313cf]Shit man, that\'s funny. When I first met you and Superfly, I was jealous of you guys, long time friends racing bits, [i:d7829313cf]had[/i:d7829313cf];) a band, as far as I as I understand, you guys are graphic artist. That sounded like my dream to me. Then now you\'re all bitching about your job, I find out you haven\'t actually had the band for a couple years. :roll:\r\n\r\nIt\'s cool man, I still look up to you even you don\'t have a band. :lol: \r\n\r\nSeriously, I\'m not good with the compliments, but you\'re pretty fuckin smart and all that shit too.\r\n\r\n...and at least you\'ve had the band experience, I\'ve always just been the guy that hung out with the band.  :lol:  \r\n\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29749,'c9af0342be','I\'ll put them out Wendsday after the holiday.  \r\n\r\nPost office is closed Monday and I work Tuesday.\r\n\r\nWhat else are you trying to replicate?  Do you need other parts for measurement?  I have alot of extra stuff that I would be willing to donate to you to learn and practice with.  Xmods, ZZ\'s, Bit\'s....I have a shitload of Xmod rims.\r\n\r\nGlad to help out in anyway possible.\r\n\r\nJust hook a pimp up down the road. :wink:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(29752,'30f0941cb1','An Xmod rim would be great, I\'ve had a couple of people ask me about doing some of those.\r\n\r\nI can\'t think of anything else, I\'ve got most of the zip size stuff, so thats not a problem.\r\n\r\nWhen I get them working right I\'ll send you a set or two of zip size rims if ya like, maybe you can come up with a good way to mount them.'),(29753,'c1f4881169','Cool.\r\n\r\nI\'ll send you a couple of Xmod rims too.\r\n\r\nMike'),(29770,'da0cf22858','[quote:da0cf22858=\"jmays\"]hi there crazydave, were on earth did you ever find that vw beetle body, i have to get one of those for my collection.\r\n\r\nthanks\r\njeff mays[/quote:da0cf22858]Radio Shacks gots da Herbies.  :-) \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37903,'4a24281a10','[quote:4a24281a10=\"HirotoR34\"]Where can I send the vid to, and how do I add the screen shot? I\'m kind of a dummy when it comes to videos and video editing[/quote:4a24281a10]\r\nWell it depends.\r\nHow big is the video? If it\'s 5MB or under, you can upload it directly to your bitPimps gallery.\r\nIf it\'s over 5MB and under 10MB, you could possibly mail it to me at: bitpimps@gmail.com\r\nIf  you\'re a member a Putfile, it may give you a direct link to download your video (I\'m not sure), if it does, send me that link and I\'ll download it directly.\r\nIf none of those work, we\'ll have to find another way.\r\nLet me know. I don\'t want to make you jump through hoops, so let me know what you think.'),(37829,'5fefe839bb','[quote:5fefe839bb=\"Sporttracguy\"]Sounds great, ill have the money to you by the end of the day  :-o \r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:5fefe839bb]\r\n\r\nWent out today.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(37709,'7e203ec029','Poor subie :-(   Imma fix her up, just another project to do :?  No i gots 3, the \'05 stang, a civic i foung in the bottom of my scrap box ( looks like shit, gon be hard to fix), and now my subie, i got some big plans for her :-o  And my top secret (dont tell no one) wide body 350Z :-D  Imma be posting some pics of all but the secret Z today or tommorow. And thanks for the Ferrari Bit, i love it :smile:  :-)  8-)  :)  :cool:  :smoking:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36651,'8df3d85b4e','Hey i just checked the mail !!!\r\n\r\nWooo the stuff came in! \r\n\r\nI just quickly went through it don\'t have much time to play today. I gotta study for my exam, but 2morrow when i get back from school it is game time! \r\n\r\nThanks for all the extras, I saw the steering rods...are those better than the stock ones? The red one looks pretty cool. \r\n\r\nI like the mustang, wow, you piant that? \r\n\r\nI am still not sure which of the body parts go where, but once I get my hands on it it should be fun. I am going to repaint the subie after some sanding..mm can\'t wait! I might repaint the mustang too, not sure! \r\n\r\nThanks a ton, and thank you for the extra\'s you have outdone yourself man! Number one pimp to me right now man...props gallore!'),(36652,'c02aee5229','Got the stuff just now...thanks alot for the parts.\r\n\r\nI could not believe how much lighter the shaft was...o man! lol I thought it was fake at first ahah! It should make a huge differences. Thanks for the other alum parts man. \r\n\r\nBTW are those Radioshack bearings? I needed a set too, thanks!'),(37758,'f4b97c4010','I\'ll send mine out tommorow or tuesday, my addy is:\r\n\r\nOskar Kohanec\r\n111-405 N.Briggs Ave\r\nSarasota FL  34231\r\nUSA\r\nEarth\r\nMilky Way\r\nLocal Group\r\nSpiral Galixy\r\nUniverse');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36737,'674efb063f','give me 1 used xmod part...could be anything...i payed like 20 canadian for all the bodies....you have any spare knuckles, or cheaper aluminum parts...\r\n\r\nor do you strickly want to buy it off people?'),(29941,'3a93c55763','[quote:3a93c55763=\"hue35\"]\r\nI thought the scale was pretty much the same?... I\'m pretty sure, because of the adjustable wheelbase of the xmod, it will fit a mini-z body. I know betty.k used that porsche iWaiver on his xmod... he mounted it with velcro, I think. I know I\'ve seen lexan bodies that were the correct scale... they may have been for them big-ass slot cars. I\'ll look further into that.[/quote:3a93c55763]Yeah, see betty is reversing his wheels to fill out the iwaver body, and I guess that helps with handling too, but I\'m not totally into that reversed wheel look. I know I\'m being picky, but I just hate when things obviously look like they don\'t belong. he did get some alloys recently that were extra wide, but I have a feeling that\'s gonne be the pricier route. The slot cars bodies are just too big. They are 1/25th scale like a model car, you can kinda get a way with that on a monster truck, like my 04, but that\'s just not gonna work on an xmod. \r\n\r\nWell anyways, i got time, I\'ll keep looking into this, maybe there\'s someone on one the forums out there making bodies.\r\n\r\ndave'),(29825,'465b829d8f','i dunno bout size but i think it is ho scale? i know nothing bout them soooo. they are the same length as zips but little thinner and i use their rims for my zips that need tons of traction.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (29826,'51c25477fd','ok cool,, i figured it was HO but i really dont know much about those things... I want it for the gear setup,, im in the process of making some mini U joints and im building a full indipendant rear suspension (I hope) and the gear setup is perfect,,,\r\n\r\nThanks again\r\nSporttracguy'),(35574,'e5c6a17e2c','Hey, thanks for the advice, but I think I\'ll be fine, I am gonna be using this in my rather small living room, and from what I\'ve read around, the speed and torque is due to the motor and gearing it comes with. Anyways too late, I already got the Hummer. Can\'t play until Cheistmas though.\r\n\r\nI\'m sure with my Iwaver Xspeed pro, and a 12 tooth pinion it be plenty fast for me, but I want to get bearings before I try that set up, don\'t wan\'t to fry the FETs right away, though I do plan on stacking them with some IRF7316s. :-o \r\n\r\nDave'),(37755,'e8268b48fb','I\'m gonna have to go with a yes on that..... :-o I\'ll send it out tomorrow.....thanks man!\r\n\r\n\r\nJustin Long\r\n3 Crockett Rd.\r\nRaymond Maine 04071'),(35111,'cdf525b981','Hey man, well i want to bid on this http://cgi.ebay.com/Micro-RC-Collection-Bit-Char-g-Microsizer-Many-Parts_W0QQitemZ6011299770QQcategoryZ44025QQssPageNameZWDVWQQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem\r\n\r\nBUT, he forgot to let Canadians bid on it, so Ebay won\'t let me. So, i\'m just sending the hook up to my homie.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33898,'95cbb0c1b5','dude, that was SO RAD!!!\r\n\r\nI had the sniper rifle, and you said \'ill cover you\' and you just wiped out like 4 dudes in 15 sec down that one thoroughfare!! LOLOL\r\njust awesome!\r\n\r\n\r\nyeah,m here\'s the deal, the connection is good, but goes out like once every 5 or 10 minutes when everyone is parked in front outside:(\r\n\r\nill try to play though'),(31879,'894fab590c','[quote:894fab590c=\"pimpsmurf\"]Your clone will be shipping on Monday. I\'ve been hella busy and freaking out over a monster truck. Later!\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:894fab590c]\r\n\r\nLol its cool, Its free, I can wait, lol, take your time, and ship it whenever you can. Thanks again.'),(30364,'8793dda43e','Welp, I feel pretty stupid right about now. Not so much because I messed up, but because I didn\'t PM you and clarify first, before jumping the gun.\r\n\r\nYou had mentioned that the v+ should be hooked to the voltage booster for a 3v volt power supply. Honestly, I don\'t know what one looks like. I had removed the resistor, hooked up the input and output as you had shown, but then I just assumed where the 3v converter was. I thought I was on to something with this little black box, it was 2.65 on one end and  3v on the other, so I hooked the v+ to the 3v side where the white arrow is in the pic below.\r\n[img:8793dda43e]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/sepcbad.jpg[/img:8793dda43e]\r\n\r\n\r\nSo did I screw up? Was that the wrong place to put it? Cause after I got done the car was completely dead. I removed the DC mod, and restored it as it was originally, and it was still dead, but at that point I noticed that black box got hot. So I replaced it with one off another SE board, and now my car runs non stop with full power from the battery.\r\n\r\nSo what have I done? I know the car is screwed, but if I did hook it up wrong do you think I killed the DC mod also? \r\n\r\nAnd if by some freakish chance that I just happened to guess right, is there a chance that was something went wrong with the DC mod? (Assuming everything else was hooked up right, which I had my wife double check for me. )\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAgain, I feel really silly about all this, but I really thought I had it figured out. I guess I wasn\'t as smart as I thought. :lol:  \r\n\r\ndave'),(31014,'020eb85c19','the alloys i have i bought second hand, they\'re supposedly bbs racing rims (part no: wt 4345). they\'re 10mm round and 7mm wide.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31015,'7885bdf1e7','[quote:7885bdf1e7]Why exactly am I getting a ticket? \r\n\r\n\r\nIt happened in the 70\'s. Let it go.[/quote:7885bdf1e7]\r\n\r\nWhat the hell does that mean lol'),(31016,'d7e0069136','dude, look at the picture that chaoscauser posted.\r\nthe one of his car. look at the quality of the photo, the style of\r\ncouch everything is on.....all looks like it is from the seventies.\r\nIt\'s before my time, too, but I\'ve seen old photos, seen the Seventies Show, etc.\r\n\r\nGet it?\r\n\r\n\r\n-Motor :)'),(35663,'6d061419cb','On the DL....\r\n\r\n$50.00 total including Priority. ($3.85)\r\n\r\n\r\nYour the first person to PM me about these, instead of going straight to Ebay.  \r\n\r\n :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\nPaypal addy...\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com'),(37866,'d66f4d69c8','The Skyline is black, with yellow side add ons or w.e, im not sure if its the whole body upgrade but there is quite a bit.\r\n\r\nit\'s condition, if your picky like me you\'d wanna touch it up with your own personality, but its not that bad at all, could actually make it look really good.\r\n\r\n350 sick is copper as you know, and its condition has been run before, not that bad...\r\n\r\nshow me an offer and its yours man!'),(37836,'d0b4b36918','Hey man just wanted to check if Bird and you got the stuff I sent? I never heard and just wanted to check.\r\n\r\ngot the lights man working on hooking things up! if I could ever get a little time off from working all the time.\r\n\r\noh kamen emailed me says he wants to buy some stuff from you and is personal check ok?  :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37837,'74d22a1381','[quote:74d22a1381=\"steelwoolghandi\"]Hey man just wanted to check if Bird and you got the stuff I sent? I never heard and just wanted to check.\r\n\r\ngot the lights man working on hooking things up! if I could ever get a little time off from working all the time.\r\n\r\noh kamen emailed me says he wants to buy some stuff from you and is personal check ok?  :lol:[/quote:74d22a1381]\r\n\r\nTotally forgot to drop you a PM.  The stuff came and I gave it all to Bird.  He said thanks.\r\n\r\n\r\nRemember this, its a hobby.  No need to rush on a project. :-o \r\n\r\nKamen. :o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLater, \r\n\r\nMike'),(37838,'c3102883bb','Hiya sg!\r\n\r\nJust wanted to know...any news for my ZZSE?\r\n\r\nThanks ,\r\n\r\nM_M'),(37840,'fd77c7e24f','[quote:fd77c7e24f=\"HirotoR34\"]definitely, I was thinking deans would do charging duties...I\'ll do you up a custom shell. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to add a bit o green :-o[/quote:fd77c7e24f]\r\n\r\nI\'ll get them out ASAP. :-)'),(35667,'024a3aa75d','Y have you not been on msn. I was just wonderin If you were mad at me or somethin.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32605,'ed4311a20b','Oh dude, that sucks so bad you lost that car. Man, I would have been pissed about that. You do some great work. Hope micro-amps didn\'t take it hard.\r\n\r\nGlad you got the car. The Ned Flanders lookin dude at my local PO said it should get there in 3-5 days, so I was startin to sweat it a little. My paypal id is graham@gte.net. Hope you like that car. It\'s pretty funky, ain\'t it?'),(32561,'799c9d9b81','[quote:799c9d9b81=\"SuperFly\"]Hey, if you\'re interested, I might be interested in trading some bit racer gears/wheels for your Supra body set and Microsizer tire set. Still got em?\r\n\r\nI\'ll check my inventory and see what I can part with.[/quote:799c9d9b81]\r\n\r\n\r\nHey man!! \r\n\r\nYes, they are still available.\r\n\r\nWay cool, thanks! Ya know, if you like the Tomy HARD tires, I have a whole bunch of those out of the package too. I use hard tires at times, but for some reason I have about 8 extra sets. I can throw in how ever many you want for free. \r\nAlso, ya probably know about these, but I have a couple NIB SenFa tires. They are \'soft\', softer than the soft Tomy tires, but the tire pattern is that of a medium tomy tire. Shit, does that make sense? :grin: I can throw a set of those in too.\r\n\r\nThat would be way cool to get Bit Racer axles. Whatever else ya might want, I can throw something else in. I think this stuff is alot more readily available than the Bit Racer axles, making the Bit Racer axles more valuable it seems.\r\n\r\nHue also showed slight interest in a couple Accord Bodies about 2 months ago or so. He mentioned you might be interested too. We exchanged a couple PMs, but then I didn\'t hear from him.\r\nI think it was the crappy photos I linked him to not realizing he has dialup, or he just kinda freaked out cause here\'s me new on the scene PMing him sayin \"Free for Cool Northwest Musicians\". :lol: \r\n\r\nEither way don\'t tell him, he\'ll hunt me down then, I know it. :lol:  \r\n\r\n\r\nGet back to me after you check out whatcha got!!!!\r\n\r\n--Dave'),(37127,'2b395332c8','Dude, you gotta find a way to add some little white jizz spurts on that avatar to go with the fleshy penis monster. :lol: \r\nAnimate a few white splooges er somefin. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36252,'b51555c7c5','You fuckin rock. That\'s all there is to it. :-o \r\nI\'m not sure how much time I have, will find out monday. The position as far as I can tell has to do with the creative side and involves print and signage work. The company owns  FYE and coconuts music stores etc and etc. (music and video stores and what not)\r\nThanks man, extremely appreciated. :-)'),(31539,'adafa75dc8','how thanks alot, ill think about joining and i prob will...'),(33948,'5f8ff9ce6a','[quote:5f8ff9ce6a=\"crazydave\"]Did you delete SHUAN too? :-D[/quote:5f8ff9ce6a]\r\nWho knows anymore... man, the noobs are killing me these days. Too many all at once. I\'m just gonna delete \'em all &amp; let gawd sort \'em out.'),(32333,'40df28cfa8','[quote:40df28cfa8=\"kvik369\"]Hope these weren\'t too much a pain in the butt.  I appreciate it.[/quote:40df28cfa8]Its no problem. I don\'t mind doing the work at all. I just sometimes have trouble finding the moment to get to them, then I feel bad.  :lol: \r\n\r\ndave'),(31034,'95f32d343c','Cool, I just got a hold of Filelicker. \r\n\r\nI thought somebody needed the propo-controller also. Was it you? Or did you need just the car? FL\'s gettin back to me also .....\r\n\r\nI have:\r\n1 yellow/white Skyline I.D.2\r\n1 silver Skyline I.D.4');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31315,'c862777817','Well, if you want i can just do the Headlights for you, or if you sent me the bit i can do any mod you wanted, then send it back. The headlights run of a separate coin battery.\r\n\r\nThe only problem is i have no switches left, if you have one i can tell you how to wire it in.  :-o  We can arrange something, i know a nice way to make underglow but would actually have to have the bit, to make it.\r\n\r\nWe can arrange something.  :-o'),(31257,'b182600d9a','Dunno much about this stuff so you can help me test it out.\r\nI think I got ya in the right group. We\'ll have to play around and see.\r\nLet me know if you find something interesting.\r\n\r\nPublisher Email: lmennuti38@yahoo.com\r\nUsername: Namuna\r\nPassword: l1nc0ln$'),(29901,'5b3be8fc00','hey mate, thanks again for this!!!!\r\n\r\nI want\r\n\r\n2 sets of these buggers:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.minizstore.com/minizDetail.asp?minizPN=581\r\n\r\n2 set of these buggers as well:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.minizstore.com/minizDetail.asp?minizPN=583\r\n\r\nThat will do me for now.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you wants the cash first and I\'ll paysluts ya asap.\r\n\r\n5 weeks to go before miniph2t arrives, lol............ :? \r\n\r\n :cool: \r\n\r\nMatt.'),(33823,'3f4d217620','Hey, I have a question for you.  When you made the wheelie bar out of the copper rod, you soldered it together right?  Did you use a soldering iron, or some kind of torch?  Thanks in advance.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36028,'67d2716fa2','C-Dub,\r\n\r\nMan what has happened here?  Voting used to be so easy, pick your choices, add up the points and pick your winners!  Goddamn, it seems like every contest it gets more difficult!  Shit \"USED\" to run so smuth with these, now it\'s a fuckin bunch of complaining and wishwashing back and forth!  This shit ain\'t fun no more and every contest it becomes less fun!  All started with trying to give one entrant 2 prizes which I wasn\'t gonna stand for, that shit was just fuckin rediculous!  We never had no shit like that happen in the past! So what if you voted for a car that didn\'t make the cut, points are all that count period!  Man I just don\'t know anymore.\r\nI voted for Hirotos Ferrari, it didn\'t make the cut but I\'m not changing my vote to something I don\'t like as much just to go with what everybody else likes! Fuck Dat! It just doesn\'t make the cut!\r\n\r\nI think YOU know what I\'m saying without saying it :???:'),(36617,'ac322cdc41','Just recieved my stuff today, what about yours?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36618,'487560cea0','Nope, did not recieve anything yet, I have to check during the day 2morrow...how is the stuff?'),(37694,'0880855300','Its a orange fade to green, you\'ll see, im guessing u havent got it yet :-)'),(36620,'530dabd781','O you got all your stuff?\r\n\r\nPHew! \r\n\r\nNo I did not check it out today, i worked all day. I will probably check the mail 2morrow or something...Hopefully it all came in...\r\n\r\nEnjoy the stuff?'),(31746,'23886bee84','[quote:23886bee84=\"Jeep\"]There was a pic of a superslick - gold benz (with another benz) that was lowered, can you please explain how you lowered it? If pics are possible it\'d be awesome but it\'d be cool if you could just explain too. Thanks.[/quote:23886bee84]Here, I had to find it, is a thread where I showed how I lower Super Slicks,\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=4843&amp;highlight=super+slick\r\n\r\ndave'),(37893,'bc28697c93','Hey man, I\'m not blowin\' you off, I\'ve just been slammed like a muthafucka. Saw ya just now, so I thought I\'d at least say hey.\r\n\r\nTalk to ya more thoroughly later.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32179,'b603c65a6f','I didn\'t like the tone sg was using, so I deleted it.    I don\'t thing Dave should have to defend himself here. He\'s never been anything but cool to me/us..\r\n\r\n\r\nFeel free to start another.   I\'ve made a post in the mod forum saying the same thing.\r\n\r\n\r\nSorry for the hassle man...\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Steve'),(32182,'5a9de2d029','not a problem.  thanks for the heads up.  \r\n\r\nthis guy has been posting the same garbage on all the epoch forums.  he obviously has little experience with product sales and pricing :-( \r\n\r\ni even pm\'d ripper to ask what was up as he\'s a assit. mod over on ripper7 forum.  \r\n\r\nsome people... you give them what they want and they do nothing but sh&amp;^ on you for doing it.\r\n\r\ni\'ll start another thead later but with a differnet subject as i would like to avoid the pricing issues of another forum here in your place.  just bad business and not very respectful.  my apologies for starting a mess.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nraymond'),(37865,'00e5135627','Hey what\'s up? Just another one of my, &quot;Hey, let\'s bug hue, see what he\'s up to.&quot; PMs.\r\n\r\n\r\nI hate my new computer, it pisses me off at least twice a week, but it does burn CDs really fast, like 2 minutes. I\'m used to 20. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo i\'m gonna be burning you some music, probably make you some MP3 cds because there just so much shit I\'ve meant to send you.\r\n\r\nJust recently ben listening to The Subways. They are kinda garage-y, really fluffy kinda pop, sometimes really heavy. I dig them, but they wear kinda thin on repeat listenings. Artic Monkeys, this is my second time through this album as I type this. I\'m loving it. Kinda hard to decribe, modern punk, winda poppy, hints of funk, occasional little bits that remind me of The Jazz Butcher. Interesting. Matchbook Romance, they\'re hard for me catagorize. Going by their single &quot;Monsters&quot;, you\'d place them in the Fallout Boy category, but the overall album has more of a heavy metal style to them to me anyways, but the funny thing is the metal head at work hated them, told me he didn\'t care for punk, so I\'m over here listening to it over and over trying to hear where he hears the punk. The best I can figure is the beat, but this guy like Green day and Blink 182, so I\'m not getting it. I think it sounds metal. :lol: \r\nAnyways, I got off track on that band, but speaking of Fallout Boy, saw them on SNL, I thought, &quot;That was kinda cool.&quot; So I downloaded all three of their albums... it all sound the same, kinda boring after awhile. :lol: \r\nGot the Black Sabbath Black Box set DLed. The complete 70-78 Sabbath if you\'re interested. :-o \r\n\r\nRight after I got my computer Torrentspy apparently became a pay site or something. I figured what the hell, I\'ll pitch them $18 if it makes them happy and I can keep DLing the way I have been. I forgot to click a box, and accidently paid an extra $14.99 for their software, but oh well, I think I\'ve DLed hundreds of $$$ of music since then. Funny thing is when you search from their software it searches mininova.org, and I was billed by Supernova.org, I\'m guessing they own Torrentspy too. At anyrate if anyone ask, I thought I was DLing music legally, being as I paid for it and all. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHate to say it, but, after playing with my new Losi mini LST, all my smaller cars just seem like cheap POS. :lol: \r\nI still love my bits, but if you want to get serious, you shoud look into 1/18th scale, and the nearby racing scene. The step up in quality is really that noticable, and I\'m looking forward to gwtting out to race occasionally. I\'ll still be playing with little cars though, that\'s part of my plan. I\'m gonna save my pennies until I can afford a charger that will do LiPos too. Easier to rationalize that when I have the Losi, than just for a few ZZ SEs. Then when I upgrade the servos, I\'ll have a pair of servos to tear down for projects. I realized a while ago that the reason why people like LBRC kick ass at that shit is because they are into the bigger cars, and have access to shit.\r\n\r\nSo that where I\'m at. Things are pretty good here. I got work straightened out, wife\'s being cool, kid\'s goofy as ever, bud\'s stoney, no complaints.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30224,'a7686fce64','[quote:a7686fce64]Hi gurus....been abit late on the band wagon. have purchase 3 sets of bits, gloria (USD 8.00), auto modellista (USd 24.00) of course the Trueno tune up kit (USD 24.00) it really is quite a steal for all these under USD 60.00 \r\n\r\nSaw a toy collector selling it for USD 50.00 [/quote:a7686fce64]\r\n\r\nGood 1st post Pimp and Welcome to Da Hood  :cool: \r\n\r\nQuestion:  Where can I find this set you mentioned?  Website?\r\n\r\nThanx:\r\n\r\nVisit my gallery.......'),(29934,'a118347b07','[quote:a118347b07=\"hue35\"]\r\nOh yeah... I wanted to mention again about the xmods and our track... those heavy-ass xmod bodies with their sharp-ass body kits tear up the RCP track. So, if you can, a lexan body or a mini-z body mounted on that thing would be awesome... it\'d also shave a ton of weight.[/quote:a118347b07]Actually, I\'d would love to do that, problem is with the slight difference in scale, got any suggestions? I haven\'t really looked into that yet.\r\n\r\nWithout the batteries, I swear the body weighs as much as the chassis with the motor, probably would be lighter than the body with the motor out. :lol: \r\n\r\nBTW, I was just replying to your last post (Yeah, I know, wifey stole the \'puter), now we gotta play tag team PMs. That\'s ok, it\'ll be fun. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(30647,'cb78bf8300','Just haven\'t seen you around in awhile and wanted to see how things were goin\'. :-) \r\n\r\nGot and before and after pics of the Vespa?\r\n\r\nI\'d really love an Impala.  hint, hint.\r\n\r\nStop past a little more often.  Its great to have you around. :-o \r\n\r\nLater, \r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32056,'03d98f3ee1','Finks,\r\n\r\nHave you shipped the goodies yet  :eek:'),(34055,'782696f504','One was lucite and the other was lexan.\r\nI bought the sheets at home depot for a couple bucks.\r\n[quote:782696f504=\"Tuner1989\"]Btw what are the chassis\'s you made, made out of?\r\n\r\nAnd thanks again man!\r\n\r\nYour zzmt is looking relly good too nice work!\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:782696f504]'),(34416,'f2f3641642','Dude. I totally forgot about this. It has been hecktic this week(end), but it *will* be shipped today.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37062,'ff7799f994','[quote:ff7799f994=\"hue35\"]\r\n\r\nGod damn!... I\'m still stunned by how fuckin\' cool this thing is. Shit, man... people are gonna shit when they see this car flossed up.\r\n\r\nedit: AND, it hasn\'t EVEN sunk in yet that this car will be in my hands, when all is said and done. God damn.[/quote:ff7799f994] :lol: You almost sound like someone that just got Overhauled.\r\n\r\nCool.  :-o \r\n\r\nYep, its yours. :-o \r\n\r\nOh yeah, and people are really gonna shit when I make another vid, showing the 2 cars, then right when they line up as if they are about to race... another &quot;to be continued&quot;. I\'ll do the last vid when/if I ever fly out to see you.  :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:ff7799f994]edit 2: have you heard The Ribeye Brothers? If not, I\'ve got a couple of discs to send ya... right up your alley, I\'d bet... fun stuff. They\'re another spinoff of Monster Magnet, just the polar opposite of the other spinoff (Atomic Bitchwax).[/quote:ff7799f994]I loved Monster Magnet when they came out. That first vid of theirs looked like an old Sabbath video. Then on like the 3rd or 4th album they cheesed out. He even said he was tired of the lack of response from the audience, and decided if this is what you want then I\'m gonna go over the top with all of it, and went all 666 and shit. \r\n\r\nAnyways Monster Magnet rant aside (I actually edited that back :lol: ), that sounds way cool. I have a pile a crap I want to send you, but my CD-R is down. Oh well, its almost tax time, and (fingers crossed) we should be getting a new computer real soon.\r\n\r\nDave'),(32309,'983c607733','Hey, what\'sappinin :-) \r\n\r\nMy wife threw that envelope away, I need your address so I can get these out.\r\n\r\nI wanted to get out yesterday, but my next chance will be on monday, so hopefully you get this before then.\r\n\r\n\r\nSorry this is taking longer than it should, I\'d really like to just get this wrapped up. \r\nThanks\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32310,'380af970e1','Hey, whats\'up?  :-) [size=8:380af970e1]©sessiz[/size:380af970e1]\r\n\r\n\r\nDude didn\'t get me his address in time yesterday. My next chance to get out will be monday, so your car will go out 2nd day priorty one way or the other on monday.\r\n\r\n\r\nMeantime, hue\'s asking about FET modding a SE Chevelle in exchange for an Iwaver body. I don\'t know if you guys like to surprise each other with your new little toys, so I\'m stalling him. I\'d kinda like for him to be evenly matched with us, when I come out to race with you guys. \r\n\r\nSo would you mind if I go ahead and tell him about the Vette, so we can work out our deal, or should I hold off until you get your car?\r\n\r\nI need the Iwaver body to get my Xmod ready for your RCP track. Hue says Xmod bodies snag it.\r\n\r\ndave'),(31080,'1fb8ea97f1','OK, I\'m close.... \r\n\r\nOne more thing, then I\'ll give you my final list of what I want...\r\n\r\nhow many of each of these do you have...\r\n\r\n200mah battery $1.50 \r\n160mah battery $.75 \r\nperfection 3.8 motor $2ea \r\nperfection heatsinks - black, gold, silver $.50ea \r\nperfection 4.2 motor $2ea \r\n\r\nThanks for putting the list together, that was nice and tidy... makes things easy.\r\n\r\nhue35'),(32257,'9a9ee3c19e','Got it. Thanks dude, you da man.  :-o[size=7:9a9ee3c19e]©crazydave[/size:9a9ee3c19e]\r\n\r\n\r\nDave\r\n[quote:9a9ee3c19e=\"SuperFly\"][quote:9a9ee3c19e=\"crazydave\"]Hey, I got your car all ready to go. I went ahead and stacked the FETs, just cause that\'s what I\'m practicing this week. \r\n\r\nHate to bug you, but I could kinda use that cash, and I got some other cars I gotta get out. Don\'t want make multiple bus trips in this heat. So get me your address. I\'m heading to the PO on Thursday. \r\n\r\nBTW, You\'re normally one of the guys I wouldn\'t normally charge for a FET mod, but I was out of FETs at the time, and  was trying to avoid that $5 surcharge on my FET order, but I\'m all stocked up now, so if you just want to pay me for the Zip Zap+shipping, like $30, that\'s cool. Whatever\'s clever. My Paypal email, just so its handy ;), is davesmoejoe@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nthanks\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:9a9ee3c19e]\r\n\r\ngotcha. check your mail. thanks!\r\n\r\nGreg Maffei\r\nGrey Matter\r\n431 NW Flanders, #203\r\nPortland, Oregon 97209[/quote:9a9ee3c19e]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31337,'418affda8b','Whats up!\r\nI don\'t think my original pm sent since my sent folder was empty , but on to the reason for my pm..... the battery holder I melted is the drivers side one.. and thanks much for the offer of parts.... where in the pittsburgh area are you..... we have been looking at house in the area but don\'t want to live in p-burgh cause the roads are really bad { potholes , severely steep  hills and hills with curves with rivers and no guardrails}.\r\ncan you recommend a low cost neighborhood?If you need anything bit or clone or zz related let me know .\r\n\r\nthanks\r\nmarc{filelicker}'),(36197,'a853bd38b3','JustJustin wrote:\r\nSorry dude, i just got wound up, us english are pretty stupid too, we are ignorrant and get annoyed easily Which you obviously already knew..!) :l New start?\r\n\r\n\r\nIt\'s cool... yeah, a new start would be smart. I\'d stick with your original user ID, and I\'ll delete the &quot;dumbass American&quot; flame in that thread. In general, it\'s a good idea to hang around a while before you start creating &quot;joke&quot; or other useless threads. We don\'t know your sense of humor yet, and you don\'t know ours. \r\n\r\nCool? \r\n\r\nhue35 \r\n\r\nedit: I\'ve deleted the fucked up parts of that thread, and locked it down. Now, stop usin\' the JustJustin ID and continue with the Juzi ID.'),(31124,'c4402bd2b9','hey man\r\n\r\ni would like to get 4 batts off ya.\r\n\r\ni live in sydney australia would that be a problem???\r\n\r\ni have paypal could this happen still?\r\n\r\ncheers');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36564,'0397776a11','[quote:0397776a11=\"pimpsmurf\"]I believe I have everything else in there. I am going to clean up the workshop tonight and sort everything. It\'s possible there is something else left behind, but I\'ll be sure to include it.\r\n\r\nI\'m really very sorry about the mistake man. That sucks. I hope you have another TX for the mean time (any AM 27 is cool)\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:0397776a11]\r\ni might have one somewhere\r\nThanks man!\r\n\r\nHopefully you\'ll find some more MZM goodies when you clean your shop out lol.'),(30081,'d5e17dd415','[quote:d5e17dd415=\"micro_man\"]well i somehow just killed my 3rd an prolly last xmod i\'ll ever get . im sick of them breakin all the time . im just gona fix up my mini t i guess . thanks for all your help with the car , and the stage 2 motor and shocks .\r\ni guess i wont be needing that supra body i hope you didnt get it yet man , if ya did i\'ll still pay for it since i said i would . later . matt .[/quote:d5e17dd415]\r\n\r\nNope, I didn\'t get the chance to pick it up yet.\r\n\r\nNo problems.... :-)'),(36942,'3a261fea51','By any chance did you make a tutorial to get a server running? I thought I saw your name in a tutorial and just interested...thanks.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30184,'be0c37da71','[quote:be0c37da71=\"codesuidae\"]\r\nIt shipped this morning, but I had my wife drop it off at the post office and I forgot to mention shipping options, so she sent it regular 1st class.  Should be there Wednesday.  Shipping costs me about a buck-fiddy, so there\'s a bit left over.  I can paypal it back if you don\'t mind having them skim some fees off it, or if you\'re planning on buying another at some point I can just hang on to it and you can send the difference next time.[/quote:be0c37da71]Nah, that\'s cool, I wanted you to have extra, i just threw that ptiorty mail thing in there last minute as an option.\r\n\r\n[quote:be0c37da71] For the next version of the DC mod I\'d like to take the 4 or 5 reverse speeds and remap them to forward speeds.  So you\'d get one reverse gear (not often you need more than that anyway) and then 8 or 9 forward speeds, so you\'d have much better control.  You just have to adjust the throttle trim on the controller so its almost all the way back.[/quote:be0c37da71]How feasible is that? That would be perfect. You only need reverse for backing out of tight spaces. If you can do that, go for it, I\'d want one. :-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(37113,'9852434ec0','[quote:9852434ec0=\"mikirgra\"]No dude. Their monitoring our web usage at work now, so I gotta stay on the down low. I\'m fixing my home connectivity, and I\'ll get some pics to you of my Trueno sets. You still have dibs.[/quote:9852434ec0]\r\n\r\n :-o   :-o   :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36336,'f3af9f1980','Im at my girlfriends place until tomorrow, then ill be home so ill try and get you some pics\r\n\r\nSTG'),(37887,'a67b56d8b5','Sweet, stuff came in not bad time...hope you like it, thought you could do more with it any how! \r\n\r\nBesides i believe you should get what you pay for man! lol\r\n\r\nTake er\' easy..'),(36339,'3aad10ceac','I thought I gave you a link for those fets.  Here it is though;\r\n[url]http://shop.ausmicro.net/product_info.php?cPath=21_24&amp;products_id=31[/url]\r\n\r\nThese are the best fets for a gen1 xmod, mini-z or iwaver.  You may be able to locate them on digikey for cheaper, but supporting Ausmicro will support more fet research.  Ausmicro and PH2T are the reason anybody knows how to put fets in a Xmod EVO.  They also found the best mosfet for gen1 xmods, mini-z\'s and iwaver\'s.  Other places like atomic mods are still using the old fets that aren\'t as efficient.  Ph2T also developed the best external turbo, the &quot;Nelly Deluxe&quot;.  And Aaron at Ausmicro has also developed an outstanding external turbo, the &quot;spider&quot;.  Ph2T gets a cut of the fet profets and together they continue R&amp;D on mosfet technologies.  Aaron is getting ready to put out a new external turbo that is better than the &quot;spider&quot;.  Most of the other external turbos out there are just copies of PH2T\'s earlier fet boards.  Anyhow, I\'m done tuting my horn.  Pick them up from Ausmicro if you can.  But I wont hold it against you if you don\'t.'),(32275,'7506a9ef32','$12 it is. I\'ll pay within the next couple of days.\r\n\r\nThanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32278,'7506a9ef32','$12 it is. I\'ll pay within the next couple of days.\r\n\r\nThanks'),(32279,'8861a20c60','sounds good, ill ship them as soon as i get the $$$\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36460,'b10b6edc77','Id be interested in the evo, is it still up for grabs?\r\n\r\nSTG'),(35940,'d7f9c41b09','What\'s up Skylinekid..\r\n\r\nJust chilled out today and started running the Xmods with my brother..somethings did\'nt turn out too good and I wanted to ask you a quicky mayn.\r\n\r\n***\r\n\r\nWhen my brother first got his Xmod he put it together and started driving around the basement. His car took a nasty wide turn and while he was turning right, his left tire struck the side of an object and his car became motionless.\r\n\r\nI then saw this and picked the car up to notice the wheels had locked towards the right. Like something was jammed. So I told him not to worry and opened up the front section of his mod. \r\n\r\nOnce i popped the hood I just pushed the wheels back into the center and sorta loosned up the servo, suddenly the wheels turned back and forth and it was almost all good to go.\r\n\r\nNow just one more problem...\r\n\r\nBack on the track his car went, and..OH NO! His car pulls majorly to one side, and turns sharper left than right!? \r\n\r\nNow is there a way to fix this, because I am noticing my Xmod starting to pull to the right too...\r\n\r\nHow can I straighten out these cars?'),(36470,'1eed82a92f','one more shot that sould show you how i did all of the pivots with the tubes.  it pivots up and down as well as left and right.\r\n\r\n[img:1eed82a92f]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10078/suspension-in-progress-evo.jpg[/img:1eed82a92f]\r\n\r\nstg');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36815,'46834f03da','Right on man!  I cant wait\r\n\r\nSTG'),(37611,'ca029316d6','[quote:ca029316d6=\"lekker\"]how do i go about putting up my pics and get special permision to do so . thnx , very cool site .[/quote:ca029316d6]\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1177\r\n\r\nScroll down to the bottom of the first post.\r\nYou\'ll see &quot;How Do I Post Images?&quot;'),(37874,'3c30bd9626','[quote:3c30bd9626=\"MafiaS\"]...alright \r\n\r\nWhat\'s your email I will snap a few of the bodies and send em 2morrow...cool?[/quote:3c30bd9626]\r\n\r\nTuner_1989@yahoo.com'),(37605,'20b217baac','This is exactly why you won\'t see any &quot;hot topic&quot; debates on this forum about:\r\nGod\r\nAbortion\r\nMACs vs PCs\r\nPolitics\r\n\r\nLast warning.\r\nYou just can\'t seem to get it through that bible thumping thick skull can you?\r\nDo not PM me any more about politics.\r\nI\'m done discussing anything with you.'),(36740,'47323fc48c','Hey man you probably know but just in case I could not send out the money today due to the Post Offices are closed for MLK day. I will send out the cash on Tuesday!\r\n\r\nthanks man!\r\n\r\nAaron');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37594,'f069b240a1','Thanks Cabo, i wll give it a try later on tonight, or this weekend!'),(32405,'e06988770a','Thanks player!  Crazy ass initiation?  I gotta go make like a goat turn tricks or something?  they seemed to kinda like my first post.\r\n\r\nStay up.'),(37441,'740bfe5d83','Well, its closing the regular work week over here in the states so i took a few minutes to test out the BP xmod.\r\n\r\nHooked it up, turned on tx then turned on the car, alright no sudden movements looking good.\r\n\r\nPress throttle houston we have liftoff!\r\n\r\nThen i go to steer the wheels and the buggers just dont want to move, and when they do move its loud as hell, and half ass steering and returning. (Sluggish you could say)\r\n\r\nI guess i\'ll take the elec\'s out and look for any loose steering wires, maybe broken gears of somesort?'),(37268,'2b53146186','Never mind, I\'m gettin my bro to get the stuff for me, I\'ll pay him back when he comes home.'),(37575,'70ddb07751','Ok.  That sounds good. I\'m expecting to recieve a Yellow Honda Civic from clxfiles soon so that will be the body I customize.  I don\'t want to screw up right away so I\'m just going to ask you this:  Do you lower the body before you paint it or after?\r\n\r\nThanks for being so nice about this and all of your help so far.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37281,'8bcf74b2b6','Do you have any online ps2 or pc game that you can drift on. You say your better than me but lets se who is better on a game atleast.'),(30282,'c4d0dda466','Thanks, i have brought my trueno kit at yahoo singapore, where i live. I have saw a similar NIB at a rc forum around a month ago. But I have tried to contact the person but there was no reply. Ended up buying on yahoo. Good kit with really nice body shells.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you are interested and i shall contact me again. He is looking at SGD 50.00 (USD 30.00) \r\n\r\ncheck this site \r\nhttp://www.daddyhobby.com/forum/showthread.php?t=5044'),(30283,'d244618a3f','[quote:d244618a3f=\"clemo\"]Thanks, i have brought my trueno kit at yahoo singapore, where i live. I have saw a similar NIB at a rc forum around a month ago. But I have tried to contact the person but there was no reply. Ended up buying on yahoo. Good kit with really nice body shells.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you are interested and i shall contact me again. He is looking at SGD 50.00 (USD 30.00) \r\n\r\ncheck this site \r\nhttp://www.daddyhobby.com/forum/showthread.php?t=5044[/quote:d244618a3f]\r\n\r\nI\'m very interested in a few!'),(31985,'944437eb3e','thanks for the heads up.\r\nwow, the post over there sounds quick!  \r\naustralia post said yours would be about 10 days, so you should expect it next tuesdayish. \r\nThanks for a great trade.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31020,'ba6a475574','[quote:ba6a475574=\"blindrider3\"][quote:ba6a475574=\"MotorGong\"]dude, look at the picture that chaoscauser posted.\r\nthe one of his car. look at the quality of the photo, the style of\r\ncouch everything is on.....all looks like it is from the seventies.\r\nIt\'s before my time, too, but I\'ve seen old photos, seen the Seventies Show, etc.\r\n\r\nGet it?\r\n\r\n\r\n-Motor :)[/quote:ba6a475574]\r\n\r\nOhhhh I didn\'t even notice the homies lol[/quote:ba6a475574]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nYes, the homies, but do you get the joke now? Did ya read the whole thread?'),(37297,'9b7880c889','I got it in the mail yeaterday, thanks for the extra rimms and stuff :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o'),(36302,'0d8ca16dac','sometime after saturday, either saturday, or monday, i sent it last saturday and they said 7-10 days...so pretty soon than man!'),(37305,'1e9e52e8c0','I think by now i\'ve given you 1 of each, if you look at the top of them their shold be a veryy small and hard to read number. The 3 types are 1.5, 3, and 4.5. The stock one(yellow) is 0 the larger the number, the better turning radious you get, the smaller the better for straights, hope that helped :-) [/url]'),(36313,'9d9131fdd1','Beauty!!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33341,'e47fc92f3e','Awsome, thank god!\r\n\r\nAs far as the SE...  Hrmmm, it worked when I test drove it, I honestly couldn\'t tell you, I am in no way a tech guru.  You say it only says that it\'s charging for the first couple of seconds, maybe the battery, or the charger.  This is a question for  the pimps.  Ask and you shall recieve.'),(34152,'caaec5504d','[quote:caaec5504d=\"MotorGong\"]Aw man!\r\nI saw you posted yesterday about sending out the Payment to Bonzer earlier next week.\r\nNow you already did! :(\r\nThat\'s okay, I think SG219 got like six of \'em? I betcha I can snag one from him. :-o \r\nSeriously, no worries. You gave ample time, and I was lazy and late to the game! :grin: \r\n\r\nDude, GREAT rides you are modding and posting!!\r\n\r\nI think I\'m in over my head with my mod, I\'ll send ya some pics and see what ya think. Prolly in a couple days. \r\n\r\nAgain, your rides are killer! It scares me away at at the same time gives me inspiration!!! :lol:[/quote:caaec5504d]\r\n\r\nMotor I bought 3 bodies for myself so if you want one I will give one up I really did not need three but felt somone (humm like you) would get in late and want one!  :lol: \r\n\r\nI would love to see some pics of your ride! I am on MSN Messanger if you want to send them that way name: Steelwoolghandi \r\n\r\nthanks for the comments man its appreciated it took me several years to get to the point of modding that I am doing now, now I want to just get better!\r\n\r\nThanks again let me know about he TVR shell and if you want it!  :-) \r\nSWG\r\nAaron'),(36394,'9465afef36','yeppers w/ insurance\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37830,'ad81360c09','That\'s fine just make sure you send it to \r\n\r\nsstirpe@sympatico.ca\r\n\r\nSoon as I get noticed the stuff will be shipped \r\n\r\nYou just wanted the two 27mhz chassis right? the 27, and the 27a chassis?\r\n\r\nsend me your addy and I could try for it to be sent wednesday or thursday....\r\n\r\ntake it easy pimp'),(37404,'425cfad327','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7241&amp;start=30\r\n\r\nHey in the above thread you talk about using blue builders foam. Could you tell me the actual product name if you remember. I am in Toronto (Canada) and I am trying to find some. I went to home depot and they don\'t have anything like that (well anything that I or the staff could help me find.)\r\n\r\nTIA'),(35295,'cdf77aa97c','If you have that whole lot in a month or so im on it!\r\nAnd it has the deluxe in the lot too right?'),(36985,'3f9f00a428','Coolio dude.... Thanks. Now it\'s vapor time.  My driving skillz are so honed, that i\'ll be whippin him with my truck...\r\n\r\nYou know I just pwn all...lol :-)'),(32474,'81217b9333','Hi Man,\r\nNo sign of the package yet.   :( \r\nI\'m checking the post box today, so hopefully they will be there.\r\nDid you send them tracked? I checked with Aus post, and they said that it probably would have made it here within 4-5 days, but that customs can take a while.\r\nGlad you like the bus and I\'m glad to hear the truck was okay - i\'m always a bit dubious on clones.\r\nI guess I just play the waiting game!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32475,'0666ff9788','Hi Man!\r\n\r\nAnother fellow brisbane pimp here.  \r\nI\'ve seen some of your posts around the place, just wanted to see if you were still around the traps, or Have you gotten out of micros?\r\nWould be nice to find someone local to race sometime :D\r\n\r\nAnyhoo, have a good one!\r\n\r\nMik.'),(32476,'d549f01660','I personally think the woman at the counter didn\'t realize I was sending it to Aus when she quoted me length of time.  Hopfully it will arrive in the same time frame yours did I would figure.  As far as tracking #, honestly I can\'t recall.  Waiting for shit to ship internationally has been oh so fun for me latly, but don\'t worry about the package, it will arrive, lets just hope it\'s in the next day or two :???:'),(33887,'7413d4fa73','I currently only have 4 bodies: a blue beetle and a transparent beetle which I am currently modding, a handmade ford F250 model which only needs to be painted and detail and a clone supra/porsche? model. And they are all bits. So I might not be able to help you but maybe we can work something out.'),(32989,'9d6ff6be90','With the curved rear above the load deck, thought you were going for more of a 60\'s hearse.  If you\'re going black on black, I\'ll aim for Metallic grey with black vinyl top then.  I\'ll probably do Superior or Miller Meteor landau irons, but that\'ll be decided for sure when doing paint detailing.\r\n\r\nHere\'s an in work teaser I\'m probably not gonna show off too much http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v413/frizzen/RC/Coach_2.jpg\r\n\r\nSorry to bother you about it, you just do really amazing scratch built models and I can\'t wait to see how it turns out, and I didn\'t want us to release nearly identical cars around the same time.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36274,'f895d15266','[quote:f895d15266=\"Juzi\'s Customz\"]Ok, sorry again. But i have been searching. I wanted to find out how to get putty, and i looked at every single post/thread but couldnt find out how, and the thread i asked about it got locked.. Urrm? Im not going to make another therad \'cos i know il get flamed like fuck. So whats the deal \'io on that? In other words, can you open it up? ;) Or, give me a straight answer.. Anyway, sorry again. Btw, lovcin your cars![/quote:f895d15266]\r\n\r\nI\'m thinkin\' if you can\'t figure out how to find putty, you might be fucked. &quot;Go to a hobby store&quot; is the answer to that... or, search google for &quot;modelling putty&quot;. Again, I don\'t get how anyone can\'t figure out how to get putty... that\'s like not being able to figure out how to get glue. I don\'t think you tried very hard at all, and I think that until you figure out how to answer these &quot;how do I wipe my own ass?&quot; kinds of questions, you should probably just do a lot of reading and VERY LITTLE posting, if any.'),(34087,'ff2d6a4a49','Thanks so much:\r\n\r\nJoris de Iongh\r\nCipreslaan 48\r\n3053 ND Rotterdam\r\nthe Netherlands');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34088,'8ed7a0e31f','sup how ya doing im ok i finaly got to walmart and got my paint y was i in a big hurry to go to walmart the primer isnt dri yet  :?  hmmmm oh well hi'),(34089,'8ed7a0e31f','sup how ya doing im ok i finaly got to walmart and got my paint y was i in a big hurry to go to walmart the primer isnt dri yet  :?  hmmmm oh well hi'),(34646,'e4f075bd91','[quote:e4f075bd91=\"arfin\"]Yeah no trade, just sending some shit to eachother  :-o , yeah man, this ain\'t gonna be no stock epoch either ;) :D[/quote:e4f075bd91]\r\n\r\nKILLER!!!!! Do you have time for messenger?'),(32614,'7f22635919','Thats great! :)'),(32615,'2fd70b155d','[quote:2fd70b155d=\"weazel\"]Thats great! :)[/quote:2fd70b155d]\r\n\r\n\r\nCool. How do you want to pay? I have Paypal, or whatever you want.\r\n\r\nGive me your address and I\'ll send it out today/tomorrow.'),(32642,'465042a519','Hey, dude! How are ya doing?\r\n\r\nIf you can, yell me as soon as possible if you want the upgrades. \r\nI think I\'d be willing to wait, but see what your brother says about my post to you in the Fo\'Sale section. :grin: \r\n\r\n\r\n---MotorGong'),(36993,'bafd91d9ed','Got the inspiration, spent my whole weekend fiddleing with this:\r\n\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_1.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_2.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\nYep, that one\'s yours, biotch. :-o \r\n\r\nI still need to FET mod it, a few details like wrapping some strips around the wheels, to hold the tires on, spin the right front wheel with the dremel to loosen it up a bit,  it pitches the axle out of the car in reverse... but its freaking together, and just about ready to kick butt. The hard shit is done, its all downhill from here. :-o \r\n\r\nI also plan to get another SS motor set, mine has red KIT gears, and orange SS motor now, I plan to run the red SS motor, with my red gears, and yours with the purple motor, and these blue gears. If that works out like it does in SSs, then we should be fairly evenly matched, with a slightly different acceleration curve. Should make for more interesting racing than two indentical setup cars.\r\n\r\nOh yeah, and does this look familiar?\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_3.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\nIts like its the same, but different. :???: \r\n\r\nPretty sure this is your body, but I haven\'t decided on the colors. Pep Boys ditched the Plasti Coat, and blew my plans to play with some candy blue on top of black and silver graphics. Walmart ditched the Testors stuff for some House of Kolor paintes, which I\'m excited to check out, but they just threw them in the locked cabinet in a big ol\' pile. Hopefully they\'ll have that\'ll straightened out this weekend, and I can pick some cool custom colors.\r\n\r\n... and I know you like to see how the wheels sit in the wheel wells...\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_4.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37184,'b69692a5b8','Hey man thanks for the offer but I need the front and back lights not the underglow lights. I found some on eBay for about $15.00 with shipping so thats not too bad? \r\n\r\nthanks for the offer though man!  :-)'),(37185,'92beee7e6a','No problem...I was going to get rid of em anyways so before I did I thought I would let you know. \r\n\r\nHow do you like your Iwaver? I am still waiting for my mr-02 to come in, but I told my brother to pick one up, I hope they are a good deal and provide some tight competition between us !'),(37630,'2b716c89f8','Do you think you will be able to make the payment today?'),(37631,'9365b1b968','I can make the payment now, I was just making sure of my purchase. What can i use the lipo pack on? Can I charge it with the cheapo chargers that come with lith pro kits?'),(32649,'56b6b1c403','Not sure I ever gave my address. I\'m not sure of anything really. So just in case.\r\n\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd #1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\ndave'),(34535,'c37cb72cf2','Wassup mang? :)\r\n\r\nJust seeing what\'s goin\' on and how\'s everything.\r\nGOtta go to work, but just logged on and saw you on.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34537,'58cbc5a15e','hey i cut my body all i got to do isda bed and  a little body work'),(30624,'086cee71f0','Hey nope i have them, but he and CJ are selling them to, and i don\'t want to post i have them anymore because it will seem like i\'m trying to take away the business they are starting. But yeah i have the same ones he does.'),(32630,'86468011bc','Thnx :grin:'),(32624,'ee38d89821','I need the pinion'),(32625,'032d1391b3','[quote:032d1391b3=\"weazel\"]I need the pinion[/quote:032d1391b3]\r\n\r\nOkay, that\'s an extra $7.50.  :lol: \r\n\r\nj/k.....you got it, I\'ll throw one in for you.'),(31094,'0cfb23e3dc','Wow glad you said something I did not know I made COTM? \r\nI am glad you like the car I built (someday I might have to make a mold of it)?\r\n\r\nI appreciate the VW truck I am really looking forward to it! I will definatly post some pic\'s when its painted and finished up!\r\n\r\nhave a great week I will PM ya when I get it in.\r\n\r\nAaron \r\n\r\nsteelwoolghandi'),(32640,'c4bd37f1e0','no, no need for tracking.  can i just send you $20?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31130,'1dd6279b59','[quote:1dd6279b59=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hi,\r\n\r\nCool, what were the other things that you were interested in? I\'d prefer to sell everything at once. So let me know what other stuff and we\'ll work something out.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJDM[/quote:1dd6279b59]\r\n\r\nOh, I left those things in the list... I just meant that\'s why my offer was lower than your asking price. \r\n\r\nAnyway,  I\'m already spending more than I wanted to spend, but make me a killer deal on that whole first list (all your bit stuff) that I can\'t refuse, and I\'ll see what I can do... I\'ve done crazier things.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(31132,'f4c45c5190','[quote:f4c45c5190=\"TallduDe\"]hey man\r\n\r\ni would like to get 4 batts off ya.\r\n\r\ni live in sydney australia would that be a problem???\r\n\r\ni have paypal could this happen still?\r\n\r\ncheers[/quote:f4c45c5190]\r\n\r\nI can send you batteries but the freight will be more then the cost of the batteries (freight is about $4.75 aprox) I do have paypal and can ship to you but like I said the cost of freight for four Batteries is high. the cost of the batteries for 4 is $1.00. \r\n\r\nlet me know if you still would like to purchase them?\r\nthanks \r\nAaron \r\nsteelwoolghandi'),(34978,'8d45acfe36','I\'m still trying to find a way to do a ball-bearing mod that does\'nt require the use of 10$ a pop imported german bearings. After I saw your bearing mod in the \"ZZSE bearings\" thread, I thought it might fit the bill. Any tips?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32430,'fbf1916cb2','Dude?  Have you still not recived the package?  Let me know when you do arite?  I can\'t remmeber if I told you already, but I got the bus and Fire engine a couple of days ago,  they are so nice, I love em both.  Thanks a ton and here\'s to hoping you get yours ASAP.'),(30526,'b81933a4e6','Copyright should be fine.\r\nI can for sure host this, and it\'ll live in the bitPimps Theatre, under bitPimps Entertainment Productions:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/index.php?cat=5\r\n\r\nI\'ll send you the link as soon as it\'s up, I\'ll probably rename the file to bitpimps_2005.mov (but wait till I send you the direct link to make sure).\r\n\r\nThis baby needs a new thread. You can update the old thread, just make a new post in the old thread giving the link to the new thread. I got a feeling this mutha is gonna generate some chatter and will warrant it\'s own thread, shit, 2 really. lol\r\nAlso, you might mention in your new thread that it might better for some pimps with slower connections to download the movie and play it on their machine.\r\n\r\nVideo/animation job would be cool. The animation part seems like it might be a little harder to excel in and a more cut throat industry - I dunno for sure though - I\'ve only had limited exposure to the video side.\r\nOne of my current bosses is leaving our company and dedicating more of his time to one of his other companies, just so happens to be audio/video technology. That market is going to do nothing but boom for a long time, with all the new technologies and consumer products coming out almost daily. Seems like a sure shot if know what you\'re doing and have a solid plan.\r\n\r\nAnyways, you should be proud - you nailed this one man.'),(37521,'f7c4a3fb12','Im sorry to be such a pain in the ass, but im not to familiar with the MRS4 so would it come with the ESC, RTR or does it still need some stuff to be RTR? thanks ahead :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30530,'1ade4fe743','[quote:1ade4fe743=\"hue35\"]I\'m at least gonna do more animation work for fun and as an artistic outlet.[/quote:1ade4fe743]\r\nIMO, that\'s the best reason to start. If you\'re having fun, it don\'t really seem like work - then before ya know it, you da man.\r\n\r\n[quote:1ade4fe743=\"hue35\"]Yeah, I\'m just in job burn-out mode these days...[/quote:1ade4fe743]\r\nGod, I hear ya there.'),(34821,'36fd88b329','[quote:36fd88b329=\"DarkTari\"]I contacted dude for an update, received the following:\r\n\r\n[quote:36fd88b329]\r\n[b:36fd88b329]My 18 month son had surgury on OCT 25 they nicked his bowel and had to go back ing three days later he\'s still in the hospital please let everyone know they will get there items i will try to ship them monday usps express mail\r\n\r\nthanks chad conus[/b:36fd88b329][/quote:36fd88b329][/quote:36fd88b329]\r\n\r\nWow, that explains a lot! Hope things are ok, and I won\'t sweat it.'),(34822,'354f364096','Sorry for the delay,  here\'s what i found so far.  These items are all new.\r\n\r\nHPI Micro RS4 Kits\r\nViper\r\nSkyline\r\n\r\nMRS4 Bodies\r\nHPI NSX\r\nHPI Vette\r\nHPI Viper\r\nHPI Dodge Stratus\r\nProline GMC Sierra\r\nProline Dodge Dakota\r\n\r\nHPI Hopups\r\nDogbones x 2\r\n150mm Belt x 2\r\nTitanium Antenna\r\nDual Link Tie Rod Set\r\nBall Diff Set\r\nLed Light Set\r\n\r\nMisc Hopups\r\nGH Alum Pulley (Silver)\r\nGH Alum 300 Motor Mount (Purple)\r\nGPM? Alum Pulley (Silver)\r\nGPM Front Spring Damper (Purple)\r\nGPM 1pc Rear Oil Damper (Purple)\r\nGPM X-shock Set (Purple)\r\n\r\nI know I have more bodies than that so I think I\'m still missing a box of stuff.  I also some more used stuff that\'s already on cars.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (30536,'90130828d5','Hey Greg, thanks heaps huckleberry! lol...\r\n\r\nCan ya ship it to my work address?\r\n\r\nMatt Marcos\r\nTrinity Grammar School\r\n60 Wellington Street\r\nKEW   VIC   3101\r\nAUSTRALIA\r\n\r\nLet me know the total and I\'ll paysluts ya asap.\r\n\r\nthanks mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.'),(35840,'82664f73e1','Watup mafias, add me to msn lets talk business. kewarkis@hotmail.com I\'m in Hamilton.'),(33027,'d205f782a5','Hmmm....  This is fuckin gay.  Well, don\'t worry, I am being fucked by intercontenental shipping a lot latly.....  If it\'s ok with you give it another week, if you don\'t get it by next tues PM me and I\'ll see what I can do.  I have assloads of SEs, and I should be able to throw together another stock MT.  As for the extras... well I don\'t know.  \r\n\r\nThis sucks'),(33853,'63421fecbf','Congrats.  I didn\'t think anybody would get that.  Are you Phillippino?\r\n\r\nHere\'s your gold star.\r\n\r\n[img:63421fecbf]http://i2.ebayimg.com/03/i/04/e0/9e/79_2.JPG[/img:63421fecbf]'),(36008,'911e0532dc','Hey DT, do they have the Trans Am body kits? If so, could you get me a few, and i\'d throw in some extra cash for you. Thanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35843,'a91b4338a0','Arfin, I added you...incase you don\'t catch me online tell me what you want here in the pm.'),(33775,'73a6774836','[quote:73a6774836=\"Fordman212\"]Hey thanks.  How long u been a member here?[/quote:73a6774836]\r\n\r\nFor a while. Lookup my name under the search option.\r\n\r\nUsually chat isn\'t live unless there is some people in there. \r\nThat doesnt happen every day, but when it does its awesome. You just missed a session.\r\nI\'ll let ya know next time it comes around, and it\'s active.\r\n\r\nMotorGong'),(37814,'e798666b66','[quote:e798666b66=\"Sporttracguy\"]hey man, is that fireball motor for an 1:18 or 1:10?  If its 1:18 and works well ill take i for $10\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:e798666b66]\r\n\r\nIts for 1/18th.  It was in my M18 when I got it.\r\n\r\n$12 shipped cool?  I can ship it out tomorrow.\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com .........is my Paypal'),(34201,'9572394f70','HEY DUDE!!!!!\r\nHow\'s it goin\'?\r\n\r\nI left ya a funny suprise message at E-Bay!  :lol:'),(36073,'924f128ae5','That\'s cool just let me know...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36074,'b4aa0d560a','Hey, know anywhere in the uk i can get really cheap (upgradeable) mini rc cars? Im english too :D'),(37890,'c7263fc678','Do you think you could part with one of your plasmatomics?\r\nI would order the parts to make one myself but i need one by tuesday next week, and overseas shipping can take a long time.'),(36422,'b2def3748f','[quote:b2def3748f=\"MafiaS\"]I got the chassis and controller for the 27mhz super tomy bit...ABC\r\n\r\n\r\nBut I am going to get my hands on the other\'s if people were interested in them. I would trade them for a sweet Xmod Evo or something...Everything else is in my collection post in the fo sale section.\r\n\r\nI got three speed sets available as well. And I believe the Ferrari BB body, and Testarossa.[/quote:b2def3748f]\r\n\r\nWhen I said Ferrari or Lambo I meant these:\r\n\r\n[img:b2def3748f]http://i16.ebayimg.com/03/i/05/bf/33/e7_2.JPG[/img:b2def3748f]'),(35890,'7aa1a6001b','Honestly i still do not quite understand the whole mod...\r\n\r\nHow is it performed? How did you do it?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34863,'9462a43cd1','Here she be:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/article_postings.php?id=52&amp;catId=3\r\n\r\nLet me know if you want something changed man.\r\nThanks for lettin us put this bad-boy up. :-o'),(34864,'477a0b7804','Wow you really hate me.'),(34865,'d41f2397f2','16h 44mins to go.\r\nItem: 1-18th scale micro rs4 w/ extras RTR\r\nCurrent price: $45\r\n\r\nI\'d like to only pay $46 but you can goto $50\r\n\r\nI cannot join ebay cuz I\'m from barbados and I have no credit card. Barbados is not an authorised Paypal country, so I can\'t join paypal either. I\'d like to know if you can bid on my behalf, I will repay you by MO when you win the auction. I also have an American address to use, so don\'t worry if the seller doesn\'t ship overseas.\r\n\r\n[url=http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6010340347&amp;rd=1&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1][b:d41f2397f2]link[/b:d41f2397f2][/url]\r\n\r\nI\'m buying this to beat around, but I\'m currently building a very fast MRS4. But the lack of [u:d41f2397f2]anything[/u:d41f2397f2] to drive is urking me :(.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you\'ll be bidding\r\nThanx man\r\nMaxx'),(37607,'5443835dd1','Fine. BTW, I\'m not a bible-thumper... I don\'t know what gave you that idea.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32947,'ebc5dbdf56','[quote:ebc5dbdf56=\"hogjowlz\"]lol sorry dude actually i have a cuda body untouched you can have ill even throw in the challenger. i need your address again.[/quote:ebc5dbdf56]\r\n\r\nHmmm.\r\n\r\nHow long since I won the contest?  :???: \r\n\r\nThe address to send it to is:\r\n\r\nBill Wilson\r\nComet Camera &amp; Video Repair\r\n1209 Walnut Street\r\nPhiladelphia, PA 19107'),(30586,'b12f220639','Hey man, can you send me a list of what you got? I might be interested in some of those bodies.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nhue35'),(37663,'a836c5d501','My paypal addy is  skylinekid91@gmail.com  \r\n\r\nAnd what color would you like the CD cases in, and thanks very much for the support :-o'),(36594,'049e4562b3','ahha you scared me man....i woulda sent the lambo by its self haha'),(33578,'b3849ecd52','[quote:b3849ecd52=\"arfin\"]Hey i sent the set yesterday, and some LED\'s in case you ever need them. PM me when you get them please  :-o[/quote:b3849ecd52]\r\n\r\nNo prblem.\r\n\r\nThanks, \r\n\r\nMike'),(30733,'3b312e1eec','Hey do you still have those motors? I don\'t have $4.00, i have $3.46 is that ok? I can assure you shipping won\'t be more then a Dollar if you live in America. Thanks alot bro!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37022,'390da766c0','Naw bro not really, well how much for it? Shipped to me.'),(35110,'365698f0ed','HAHA, that e-mail was HARSHHHHHHHH, how you doin\' bro?'),(36332,'58678a01cf','[quote:58678a01cf=\"pimpsmurf\"]Yeah, the 1:16 can handle pretty much any 130 size motor. Probably could handle a 10 turn silver magnet wire. lol\r\n\r\n$218 is ok. paypal joseph.yarbrough@gmail.com and I\'ll ship her out tomorrow!\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:58678a01cf]\r\n\r\n\r\nCash sent!\r\n\r\nCant wait to get this lot!\r\n\r\nSo i take it you got those parts in today?\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks again man!'),(32657,'7de623bfc8','[quote:7de623bfc8=\"45tr0\"]thx for the heads up man,\r\n\r\ni just woke up down here, so first thing i did was PM the brother[/quote:7de623bfc8]\r\n\r\n\r\ncool, hope it works out for ya! :-)'),(32226,'1fa51bc3a7','[url]http://ripper7racing.com/forums/index.php?showtopic=4103&amp;view=findpost&amp;p=41374[/url]\r\n\r\n[url]http://ripper7racing.com/forums/index.php?showtopic=4103&amp;view=findpost&amp;p=41496[/url]'),(31142,'7245d67319','Cool, more stuff! I\'ll send you the money right now, man... thanks again, and yeah, I\'ll spread the word.\r\n\r\nHere\'s the shipping info.\r\n\r\nMat Mathey\r\n1500 SW 12th Avenue\r\nPortland, OR\r\n97201');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31156,'925a7f79db','It should be there around tuesday of next week. Monday is the 4th of July and mail won\'t be running. [url=http://www.atomicmods.com/tutorials/V1_Installation/V-1%20Install.htm]Here is the how-to[/url] for the V1 board. It isn\'t really hard to install just the jumper wire can be tricky. I used a little dab of superglue to hold it into place for soldering.'),(34395,'196614a462','[quote:196614a462=\"DarkTari\"][quote:196614a462=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hey Wussup!\r\n\r\nSorry I didnt reply sooner, I still got a bunch of Microsizer bodies and Perfection bodies. Let me know if youre looking for something in particular. Thanks!\r\n\r\nJDM[/quote:196614a462]\r\n\r\nLooking for :\r\n\r\n[b:196614a462]3 - Lambo Bodies\r\n3 - Ferrari Bodies[/b:196614a462]\r\n\r\n\r\nand if you still got \'em:\r\nTomy [b:196614a462]Gloria, WRX[/b:196614a462]\r\nPerfection [b:196614a462]VW[/b:196614a462]\r\n\r\nAlso looking for a New Tomy Fairlady (lost mine)\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp![/quote:196614a462]\r\n\r\nHey,\r\n\r\nI still have quite a few of the perfection lambo and ferrari bodies. I have them in 5-6 different colors. I also have these available in the sets too if interested. \r\n\r\nI have the Perfection VW Beetle bodies or sets in quite a few colors as well. For the Tomy Fairlady, the only thing that I most likely have is the Pullback. As for the Tomy WRX and Gloria, I still need to check on those as I packed alot of my stuff in storage. \r\n\r\nThanks!\r\nJDM'),(32903,'1ea2e1045f','Ouch indeed. UPS wanted $125 to ship it. No bullshit. Fuck them.\r\n\r\nI did the math, and counting the box, peanuts, shipping, and paypal fees I am only getting $30 for that stuff. lol.\r\n\r\nI\'m going to send it the USPS (the fast way) today, and if you feel like sending me another $10US sometime, that would be pimp. If not, it\'s cool. I have to get it out of the house anyway. lol.\r\n\r\n\"Pimp! Pimp! Hurray!\" --Snoop Doggie Dogg\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36444,'7f5339ce00','No, but it will definately ship tomorrow. Everything is rounded up and ready to go.  :-o \r\n\r\nHot damn,\r\n-JNY'),(36085,'de174aaad2','Just wondering if you have that crazy mini-z monster lot o stuff still for sale?'),(36097,'26cee431a7','Posted it today, your stuff should come from between 7-10 days!'),(36102,'be9fddfe88','[quote:be9fddfe88=\"pimpsmurf\"]Yeah, but it has 1:16 electronics installed. How much were you thinking about spending? I have 2 more front gearboxes (1 clear, 1 chrome), and some kyosho plastic rims coming for it, and was planning on using a Novak Micro ESC, with a micro reciever on it. The range on the half-8 electronics I have in it now is awsome.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:be9fddfe88]\r\n\r\nI have about 200 to spend\r\n\r\n\r\nIf thats in your price range can you give me a list of everything with the truck and whats installed?'),(36550,'a435acac92','I\'ve made a boo boo. I knew I was going to miss something. I left out the TX in a drunken frenzy, but I will send it out ASAP. I\'m sorry about that man.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37375,'2744fd586d','And you know this !............MAN!  :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37377,'','hey did u no that u could take the rear end of another mt and glue it to the rear end of another and make it 6 wheel drive.    what did u use for the rear end of the hummer 6 wheel?'),(37931,'d15a0ca8ec','yah those crystals will work in them.\r\n\r\nthe body is the Evo Rally Body if that is ok?\r\n\r\nI will see if I can dig up another body to send with it for ya.\r\n\r\nwill get it out Monday\r\n\r\nthanks man I know you will just love this car!\r\n\r\nSWG'),(32757,'53da159213','paypsl sent'),(35249,'0113a88a84','You know, since I first made my first fast bit, I wanted lexan bodies. I\'ve been planning something like what Hachi has done for long time now. My only hang up was the same as you, no pics! So now I\'m figuring, I know what a funny car basically looks like, and some of those others sound apealing as drag cars also, so that makes it worth while to order, then at $2.50 a piece its not such a risk to throw in the Porshe GT car, which I\'m afraid is just a wedge shaped car like most the others. \r\n\r\nI\'m hoping the funny cars are longer so I can stretch the chassis more. A funny car with like 3 SE cells (or 6 little ones depending how you look at it), and a lexan body would be too sick, maybe not even feasable, so I gotta try it. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(37598,'e6013d9c16','[quote:e6013d9c16=\"sessiz\"]I gotta go....You win. :lol:[/quote:e6013d9c16]\r\n :lol: Fuck yea!\r\n\r\nAlright man... I do too actually.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37376,'2744fd586d','And you know this !............MAN!  :-o'),(36247,'dd5131cd97','we just happen to be racing tomorrow!  \r\n\r\nwe typically get together every other week.'),(36248,'194eee7d7b','[quote:194eee7d7b=\"arch2b\"]we just happen to be racing tomorrow!  \r\n\r\nwe typically get together every other week.[/quote:194eee7d7b]\r\nThanx for the invite unfortunately can\'t do it tomorrow.\r\n\r\nSend me your Email &amp; Home addresses.\r\n\r\nThanx!'),(31629,'fbcd6d1473','Ok, just sent you the cash.  I\'m sending out the biffs on monday.  allow the usual 7 - 10 days.  Here\'s an installation doco I put together for you that should help.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.woahnelly.com/stuff/biff/Biff_Installation_Guide.pdf\r\n\r\nThanks again for the foams, they\'re pretty good!  I was worried that they\'ll tear up like the GPM\'s but they don\'t, they seem to be working well.   Needed to glue the buggers though, I\'m so used to the gandini foams that are pre glued it\'s not funny! lol...\r\n\r\ncheers mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.\r\n\r\n(no, the mrs hasn\'t popped yet, dam slacka kid is already 5 days overdue)\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:fbcd6d1473=\"SuperFly\"]Hey man-\r\n\r\nI shipped your stuff out last wednesday on the 4-7 day parcel post. \r\n\r\nSo ya got $15 worth of tires that cost $5 to ship to me, and then another $3.50 for me to ship to you. The minimum shipping from that joint is $5, and I piggybacked your same order for me so it didn\'t increase the shipping price, but just make it an even $23 and we\'ll call it good.\r\n\r\nBy the way, I realize you\'re a busy guy, and when your little creature busts out you\'ll have even less time, but I have to ask about something...\r\n\r\nI pre-paid ya $30 for 2 biffs (isn\'t that what they were called? the outboard FET turbo for bits) back when I bought the Nellies. Curious if I might ever see those.\r\n\r\nTake care,\r\nGreg[/quote:fbcd6d1473]'),(33445,'bee7507afb','[quote:bee7507afb=\"crazydave\"][quote:bee7507afb=\"DarkTari\"]\r\nNo Problem Pimp. I\'ll try to get to it tonight,  At work right now, fuckin oncall  :mad:[/quote:bee7507afb]Thnaks dude, though, I\'m not totally sure its neccesary at this point. I\'m kinda more confused upon further examination.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSee here\'s the crappy wheels,\r\n[img:bee7507afb]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/cal1.jpg[/img:bee7507afb]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThen I just noticed the steering adjuster is narrow and tall like a tHunder Charger one, but is says Tomy 2001, etc.\r\n[img:bee7507afb]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/cal2.jpg[/img:bee7507afb]\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter looking at the tape again, I noticed it was retaped, or at least taped twice. So I figured, \"it was tampered with\" \r\n[img:bee7507afb]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/cal3.jpg[/img:bee7507afb]\r\n\r\nThen I notice the picture behind the tape, and the car in the pic has stepped wheels. Here again on the other end.\r\n\r\n[img:bee7507afb]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/cal4.jpg[/img:bee7507afb]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSo what do you think? An early or oddball run? Possible fake? I don\'t know anymore.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:bee7507afb]\r\n\r\nDamn Dave !!!!  I fuckin totally forgot, just went thru this (been offline for a few days) and puuled this message.  I\'ll look tonight and get back atcha!  :-?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35646,'c4bcd2a63b','Sorry to disturb you Boss,\r\nI wrote MAd_Maxx instead of Mad_Maxx for my album\\user name can I change it??\r\n\r\nSorry again 4 disturbing, i didn\'t know where to write you\r\n\r\nMax.'),(34988,'7afc6170d0','Hey dude,\r\nI seem to remember you saying somefin about making a DVD with the bitPimps movie you did on there.\r\nI\'d like to get the source file to make a DVD myself - think you could that mutha to me somehow?\r\nAlso, just out of curiousity, what size is the source file? Like is it sized for the web at 640 x 480 or for TV at 720 x 480?\r\n\r\nOh... and while I\'m PM\'ing ya.\r\nI\'ve noticed your emails from bitPimps are bouncing back, from loosing your ISP, if you don\'t have a useable email address yet, I can send you a gmail invite if you want, you could use that for your online activities or whatever. Just let me know.'),(37374,'f3a2d07719','[quote:f3a2d07719=\"DarkTari\"]Yo Pimp!  You\'re our Admin, that\'s why I put &quot;Us Mods&quot; in quotes.  You have enough on your plate so we\'ll take care of it, those that step up that is .  I sure hope we don\'t have a lotta fuckin conflict with this.  I think it ran rather smuth last year and I don\'t want to fuck with the process......\r\nIf It Ain\'t Broke.... :???:[/quote:f3a2d07719]\r\nYea I hear ya.\r\nI\'ve got a controller I\'ve been wanting to paint in bitPimps colors, basically just to finish off the rattle cans. lol\r\nSo I might be able to help out a little here and there.\r\n\r\nKinda funny, I get the feeling the guys almost disappear when we post stuff like that.\r\nI don\'t know why. It\'s not like we force them to do anything one way or the other.\r\nIt\'s okay if someone doesn\'t want to participate - just say so instead of hiding until it\'s all over ya know? :lol: \r\n\r\nAh well. I\'m not worried. We\'ll get through it one way or another.'),(35535,'313b87c5f2','[quote:313b87c5f2=\"crazydave\"]Finally, I got a start. I really didn\'t want to do the wheels if I wasn\'t feeling it, \'cause you know, they gotta be round and stuff, and that\'s really hard. That was my hang up. So I finally just did it, I finally got the hard parts out of the way, and I\'m extremely happy with the results. Better than mine.\r\n\r\nHere your wheels, Tomy pullback rears, and ZZ fronts:\r\n[img:313b87c5f2]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/psII1.jpg[/img:313b87c5f2]\r\n\r\nI gotta go back and clean up that bevel on the fronts, didn\'t have any fine grit sand paper around, but I went ahead and painted in the silver ring to give you an idea.\r\n\r\n\r\n...and here\'s the beginnings of your chassis. You this part is tricky cause its gotta be square. It\'s Zip Zap based. I Figured they\'re only a couple bucks more than clones when on clearance, and that gives a solid platform.\r\n[img:313b87c5f2]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/psII3.jpg[/img:313b87c5f2]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'m not flossin\' this until I\'m done, so you\'re gonna get the progress shots, cause you know I gotta show someone. :lol:\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:313b87c5f2]\r\n\r\nSorry for the delayed response, work has been kicking my ass... actually life in general has been kicking my ass. \r\n\r\nAnyway, shit dude... this thing is lookin\' sweet already. I really dig the way the chassis looks so far. It\'s cool you\'re startin\' with a ZZ... the quality of ZZ chassis, especially the steering components, is pretty much the best of the old-school stuff. The bulk is the only thing that keeps me away... it\'s a lot of work to carve away all that bulk. I really dig the way you just stripped away the whole bulky mid section.\r\n\r\nThe wheels look badass. I know how it is to have one little thing hold a whole thing up... I\'m the master at that shit, which is why I don\'t finish very many cars.\r\n\r\nSweet!\r\n\r\nIt\'s cool to get a sneak peek, man... thanks.\r\n\r\n\r\nNow I\'mm gonna go home and :cool:  &lt;--- except smokeless.  :lol:   Man, I\'m lovin\' this vaporizer... I haven\'t \"smoked\" anything since I got it, and my lungs can tell the difference.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34972,'a2f307dee5','[quote:a2f307dee5=\"codesuidae\"]If you want to specify your own mapping its no trouble to drop the new values into the table and recompile.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be back in town until next week, but after that I can set up the boards for you.\r\n\r\ncs[/quote:a2f307dee5]\r\n\r\nI like your duty cycle numbers, those would work. But $10 is quite a bit... Maybe I\'ll have to settle on 1 or 2 boards. But it\'s cool, hold the rush, I\'m in no hurry.\r\n\r\nAbout the frequency change. I would say, make it a little lower, unless you plan to include a MOSFET driver for the FET modded cars. The FETs without a driver should run ok at &lt;1khz, but for the higher numbers a MOSFET driver would be optimal. Unless you have some secret plan in the works.'),(32247,'74d6ab0c83','Hey, what\'s up?\r\n\r\nThese stacked FETs are taking longer than I planned, but I just have one MT left. I\'ll be able to get that one done after work tomorrow, no prob, then I\'ll get these out on Thursday, gotta leave work early that day anyways, so I got me a plan.\r\n\r\nI got your address around, but can you shoot it to me again, just so I have it handy.\r\n\r\n\r\nHonestly, when you said you were sending a Cannonball, I wondered why you\'d want one of those POS FETed, but I\'ve never seen one of these long chassis Bensu clones, heard of them, but never seen one. So was this branded a Cannonball? It is typical of a Cannonball, just long.\r\n\r\nSo anyways, I got a little sidetracked with that one on Sunday. It has a spot in the chassis obviously for holding a dual cell pack. I just happened to have a dual cell pack from a Microspeed stunt car on my desk. So I threw it in. Man, with the stacked FETs, dual cells, 10-tooth pinion, it is screaming. These motors are great dual cell motors too. Steering is still wide to one side, nothing you can do about that, its because of the sloppily wound steering coils. If for some reason its too fast for you, you can clip the dual cell right out and slip single cell back in.\r\n\r\nJust giving you an update, to let you know I\'m about to wrap this up. :-) \r\n\r\nDave'),(32248,'8673b62efb','Sorry dude, had to work late. REAL LATE!\r\n\r\nI hope you weren\'t in a BIG HURRY for the set, or you\'d be pissed by now :grin: \r\n\r\n\r\nDefinately tomorrow if your around?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34123,'238323350e','im not a fucking retard. Do you like my crawler project.'),(36924,'d02fc497be','I\'m bored and thought I\'d give a howdy. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nSo that contest judging was a clisterfuck huh? I glad you spoke up. I wanted to say something in the last contest even, but before I was a mod I was one of the ones that threw a bitch, and questioned their judging in that middle of the road contest, so I just didn\'t want to be the bitch that always bitches. :lol: \r\n\r\nAnd how about DT with that Big Kahuna is back shit?  :lol: \r\nApparently he\'s still trying to comprehend what you meant about passive aggressive BS. Dense ass mofo. :roll:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBeen digging my Xmod H2. Now that I think about it, I haven\'t charged anything else since I got it. \r\n\r\nBeen bored with music. Been mostly just listening to the Reverend Horton Heat lately, because it reminds of the old school rods. Man, you gotta check out that Car Kulture Deluxe mag if you come across it. The whole mag just has that really retro, but at the same time kinda punk attitude. I\'ve been getting it at Wakmartm its bi-monthly. I always wanted to build a rat rod, and looking through this mag really makes me wish I had a place to work on a project. I want an old Model A to sand rust off of on the weekends. :-('),(37436,'1d14cbc539','sorry dude, i forgot to get back to you!\r\nyeah, it made it here safe and sound, 2 weeks to the day after you sent it. quickest shipping yet from the states!\r\nBy that point, the blowout thread had gone a bit cold so i didn\'t bother postin there, but i shoulda messaged you back.  \r\nSorry man, slackage on my behalf.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34494,'e00913e3cd','got it thx!\r\n\r\nnow i need to wind a new motor, i gave away all my 130\'s when i went brushless.   :-( \r\n\r\n[quote:e00913e3cd=\"ph2t\"]it\'s quite different since thee\'s two different mosfets now.\r\n\r\nsee the doco here:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttp://www.woahnelly.com/stuff/xmods/EVOMOSFETInstallationGuide.pdf\r\n\r\ngood luck!\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:e00913e3cd=\"Clint\"][quote:e00913e3cd=\"ph2t\"]hey man, just wanted to let you know that the installation doco for the evo mosfet upgrade is almost done.  it will be posted shortly.\r\n\r\nif you wanted something sooner to help let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nph2t.,[/quote:e00913e3cd]\r\n\r\nsweet thx. I received the package of fets from aus micro this afternoon.\r\nUnfortunatly, i wont be able to work on it until i get home this weekend, so no rush. if the install is anything like the original xmod fet upgrade, i wont have any problems.\r\n\r\nthx,\r\n-clint[/quote:e00913e3cd][/quote:e00913e3cd]'),(37495,'9150972a7f','[quote:9150972a7f=\"betty.k\"]hmmm, i\'m stumped! it was definately working when i had it, slow steering but working.\r\nsounds like there could be some binding in the steering somewhere. check it over and as a last resort pull the servo apart and check it out.\r\ni\'d try a different servo motor too.\r\n\r\nsee how you go with that and lemme know if it works. :-o[/quote:9150972a7f]\r\n\r\nWelp, after a breather or 2 i decided to give it another go.\r\n\r\nTook a stock xmod servo and wired it up to the ep and walla! Shit captain it\'s working :-o \r\n\r\nBut that left the question in my mind, why isnt the other servo working. Upon curiousity and inspection i pulled the old servo apart once again, this time paying close attention to the servo motor, took the servo motor out, then i tried to spin the shaft. The shaft came out! Holy hell no wonder why it wasnt steering.\r\n\r\n\r\nAny ways, do you have any suggestions on how to make the steering radius bigger with a stock xmod servo and MR-01 board, (The iw board is going somewhere else at the moment)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35394,'6489d0c99e','Is it possible for me to get a  alluminum(right?) diff for the EVO truck?If so tell me how much and what other parts i need for it, thanks...'),(35395,'c507c62da4','[quote:c507c62da4=\"blindrider3\"]Is it possible for me to get a  alluminum(right?) diff for the EVO truck?If so tell me how much and what other parts i need for it, thanks...[/quote:c507c62da4]\r\n\r\nYes you can get a Ball diff for it.  I won\'t be placing an order until after the 1st of the year when I start a Group Buy on them. \r\n\r\n[img:c507c62da4]http://www.cjshobbies.net/Images/11_18_050009.jpg[/img:c507c62da4]\r\n\r\nBTW: if you have IE as your browser check the spelling link in my sig.  \r\n\r\nits aluminum'),(33060,'d771af0a19','Great pics\r\n\r\nhttp://s6.invisionfree.com/Infernal_XMOD/index.php?showtopic=6779\r\n\r\n\r\nPrintout of the skus for all the new stuff i made\r\n\r\n http://s6.invisionfree.com/Infernal_XMOD/index.php?showtopic=6730\r\n\r\nAtomic mods review of the new chassis\r\n\r\nhttp://www.atomicmods.com/projects/Evo%20Xmod/Evo_Xmod.htm\r\n\r\n\r\nUnder this general discussion there is alot of informative topics and pics of the new xmods \r\n\r\nhttp://s6.invisionfree.com/Infernal_XMOD/index.php?showforum=4\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHope this helped :-) \r\n\r\n---Matt'),(35263,'920b587402','[quote:920b587402=\"Sporttracguy\"]Hey man, i put up a picture of those gears i have, let me know if thats what you are looking for and we can make a trade.  Also, did you ever get that FET tut. made for the zzse?\r\n\r\nthanks\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:920b587402]Yep those are the gears. :-o \r\n\r\nHere\'s my address:\r\nDavid Harrington\r\n7002 W Indian School Rd. apt 1131\r\nPhoenix, AZ 85033\r\n\r\nGet me your address and I\'ll get that red gear w/ the pinion, out ASAP.\r\n\r\n\r\nNah, no tutorial yet. Haven\'t had a clear enough head lately to really sit down and think about writing a tutorial, but I am on vacation this week. No promises, but maybe I\'ll whip something up.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35645,'c4bcd2a63b','Sorry to disturb you Boss,\r\nI wrote MAd_Maxx instead of Mad_Maxx for my album\\user name can I change it??\r\n\r\nSorry again 4 disturbing, i didn\'t know where to write you\r\n\r\nMax.'),(32381,'8f5bf52c7b','Now thats the shit.\r\n\r\nI hate to buy somewhere other than CJ, but I might just have to do so. :-? \r\n\r\nI can\'t find a short CF driveshaft. :???:  \r\n\r\nI\'m off to a house/pool party with some sororirty chics or something.  I\'m not sure, I\'ll find out when I get there. :drinkin:  :greenblob: \r\n\r\nLater :-)'),(33476,'3ef4a737cf','[quote:3ef4a737cf=\"crazydave\"][quote:3ef4a737cf=\"DarkTari\"]\r\n\r\nDamn Dave !!!!  I fuckin totally forgot, just went thru this (been offline for a few days) and puuled this message.  I\'ll look tonight and get back atcha!  :-?[/quote:3ef4a737cf]How ironic, I just got an email from someone else today, that i thought forgot about me. :lol: \r\n\r\nSeriously though, I just figured you blew it off after I realized it matches the pictures on the box. Nothing left to say.\r\n\r\nStill though, I guess I was curious what you thought. I\'ve never seen a Tomy bit with wheels like this. Its kinda odd to me. :???: \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:3ef4a737cf]\r\n\r\nMines is exactly the same way. The chrome on the wheels are kinda crappy, not like the other Tomy\'s which I looked at on another set.  Maybe they where all made like this  :-?'),(33480,'b0b50f6989','hey, got a Q... have you ever worked with a PIC16C56 microcontroller?\r\n\r\nWent to my local elec. surplus store, they have a bin of scrapped battery chargers that for some reason failed tests or whatever... So naturally i bought the entire bin for 50¢ a piece. TL494\'s, LM393\'s, high amp trannies, inductors, red/green dual color LEDs, some switch IC\'s, and ONE micro-controller to rule them all. Anyways, to get to the point, I would like to know what they can do and how well they perform it... Obviously, they can\'t perform \'EVERYTHING\' because of the various other IC\'s there... Yes, I do have the datasheet, 1.3mb, waaaay too long for me to \"read\" or even \"skim\" for that matter, so please please please help me out if you can!\r\n\r\nThanks in advance!\r\n\r\nPS:\r\nIf you get a chance and don\'t mind another forum, check out\r\nhttp://forum.4hv.org/\r\nNot to be pawning you or anything, but thats the lair of genious to which you belong... You could lend quite the helping hand with your microcontroller programming \'skillz\'.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33484,'0d8b1383d6','Thanks man, I have one I might be able to let go of. I will let you know here in a few days. I am in the middle of moving so my internet will be down after today for a week at least. If you are still in need of one by then I will hook you up. Later Pimp!!!'),(33614,'7190acb06f','I just read the thing about the tempo... No, i have a 99 f-150 flareside.  4.6l Triton v8.  Mark 3 conversion package.  Flowmasters with 45\'s comming out the back, ill send you a link to my picturetrail gallery since i know u wont believe me.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.picturetrail.com/gallery/view?username=xcubanoloco2x&amp;x=0&amp;y=0'),(33922,'a8d89a9eaf','my adres is:\r\nCipreslaan 48 (street)\r\n3053nd (zipcode)\r\nRotterdam (city)\r\nthe Netherlands. \r\n\r\nAnd how can I be guarenteed that I do receive my ZZMT because I have been fucked up once with a money transfer with eBay.'),(33489,'43af60c293','Got them today :-D'),(33490,'d557f5d27d','Mike Smalley Jr.\r\n3918 Inland Ave.\r\nWest Mifflin, Pa  15122\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike\r\n\r\n :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32134,'2eae0c8512','I think you said in the post 6 bucks each plus shipping?  They are in new condition right? \r\n\r\nI don\'t have much to trade, just some bodies I don\'t use.\r\n\r\nLet me know, thanks. I\'ll pay by PayPal'),(32135,'b8f16b0355','yeah, they are brand new, with the lights. That price sounds perfect, if you want you can send the money through paypal,, my address is sporttracguy@hotmail.com\r\n\r\nSTG'),(32140,'2d26c24fab','[quote:2d26c24fab=\"mikirgra\"]Yo DT, been totally swamped at work. Haven\'t made it to PO yet. Have it boxed and ready. Will try to send out Saturday. I\'ll let you know Monday. Hang in with me.[/quote:2d26c24fab]\r\n\r\nNo hurry Pimp, I\'m not goin anywhere  :-o \r\nI\'ll check on the WRX tomorrow while I\'m out !'),(32156,'09f5239d97','Oh sorry -\r\n\r\n[quote:09f5239d97]Its that all of a sudden there is a sudden interest in Epochs.[/quote:09f5239d97]\r\n\r\nNot the photo you have to scroll down to the comments under the photo for why the sudden intrest.\r\n\r\nCheers'),(37559,'9e8cdf92c6','Are we still on for those bodies?  Let me know because I have someone interested in a couple things you requested.  Let me know how you wanna send the money.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37560,'9e8cdf92c6','Are we still on for those bodies?  Let me know because I have someone interested in a couple things you requested.  Let me know how you wanna send the money.'),(32158,'7355db3bf5','Yes, I read that.  \r\n\r\nCongrats on the deal. 8) \r\n\r\nA motor, a turbo,  and other mods all around the same time.  Good shit!!! :-o'),(32183,'d6e05de8cd','No no no... Don\'t get me wrong... You did nothing wrong arch.   It was sg that turned it south bound.\r\n\r\nWe\'ve never even thought about having an issue with trc/minizracer, and posting about new things.    We like being kept in the loop, so please feel free to update as you like. :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n-S'),(32190,'0c7ec69d25','yeah dude, that sounds cool.\r\n\r\nI think it\'s around $5.00 for shipping, maybe less, for a USPS box.\r\nI definately recommend a box. I\'ll check the web site and get back to ya later today!\r\n\r\nI won the E-Bay auction for $35.00 incl shipping, and got a whole bunch of extras with it. I already have a set, so if I sell it for $20, its like payin\' $15 for the extras, which sounds good.\r\n\r\n\r\n-Dave'),(36940,'3f0a92070e','[quote:3f0a92070e=\"hue35\"]\r\nYeah, where the hell did that even come from? It was just all of a sudden DT is in full-tilt action... everytime I read that muthafucka\'s writing, I hear it as 50% Foghorn Leghorn + 50% Mr. T... [b:3f0a92070e]&quot;I say.. I say... HERE\'S HOW IT\'S GONNA BE, PIMP!!!&quot;[/b:3f0a92070e] Jesus Christ already.[/quote:3f0a92070e] :lol: :lol: That\'s funny as shit. \r\n\r\nI just got a crazy idea. Ya know, you had that killer ass prize package put together... What if just out of no where you\'re alternate ego popped up out if no where and ran his own contest. Might cause some controversy, would at least give DT a taste of his own medicine. Hell, you\'d probably be able to get Cabo behind it, and have Chedderspreader announce it. Maybe with it being all MS stuff, it coulf be an OG Bit themed contest.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know, just something that happened to pop into my head. :???: \r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e][quote:3f0a92070e=\"crazydave\"]Been digging my Xmod H2. Now that I think about it, I haven\'t charged anything else since I got it.  [/quote:3f0a92070e]\r\nYeah man, I\'ve been diggin\' the looks of those... yours in particular. The silver H1 SSMT chop is badass. I\'ll have to check one out at the shack. I\'m just reluctant to open the door to a new platform. How much do you have into yours?[/quote:3f0a92070e]Oh shit, you just opened a can of something. :lol: \r\nLet\'s see\r\n$60 car\r\n$17 motor\r\n$20 bearings\r\n$16 offroad set\r\n$16 second offroad set after I screwed the first dyed job :lol: \r\n$16 AWD\r\n\r\nSo that\'s what? $145? Son of a bitch, I could of had a Mini-t. :lol: \r\n\r\nThat\'s ok, I dig how the Xmod is more true to scale, and its plenty for indoors. :-o \r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e][quote=&quot;crazydave&quot;]There was a great episode of &quot;Rides&quot; a few weeks back that was basically a top-notch documentary on the Rat Rod scene... it\'s almost too much of a scene for me. Like, those folks just [i:3f0a92070e]know[/i:3f0a92070e] they\'re the coolest motherfuckers on the planet... and they are, but they don\'t have to [i:3f0a92070e]know[/i:3f0a92070e] it.  :lol:[/quote:3f0a92070e]I wish I caught that episode, I\'ll have to keep an eye out.\r\n\r\nI hear ya about those guys being just a bit too cool. I could see myself, even if I built my dream rat rod, I\'d probably be ripped for using a 350 and not a flat head, or using a fiberglass body panels, when I couldn\'t find or afford steel ones. Its like you can\'t just jump into that scene half assed. :-( \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e]Work has been about to fucking kill me dead.... the pressure is just too much. I\'m working on this brochure that was WAY the fuck over-estimated by our account execs, but the client bit. Now the pressure is on me to make this 8-page POS look like it\'s worth the 90k it\'s gonna cost, and that doesn\'t even include printing... it\'s about 3x more expensive than it should be. The folks around here who sold this nightmare don\'t really understand the problem, but they sense my stress level... they\'re scared as shit, which is where half of my stress comes from in the first place. [/quote:3f0a92070e]I can totally ralate, but on a much smaller level. When I was doing banner ads, the customers were only paying $30. I know people doing work of my quality charge much more, so I wasn\'t too stressed, but I had a hard time even rationaling making it worth $30 to them. Then my buddy dropped a $200 logo design in my lap, and I just had to make it worth $200. I don\'t really know what  $200 logo looks like. I think I kinda dropped the ball on that one, because my buddy had to tweak it to their taste... but a 90k catalog! :shock: I feel your stress.\r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e]And, on top of that, we got a new designer dude,..[/quote:3f0a92070e]I\'ve been dealing with this POS for over a year now, shows up a half an hour late, making me late to pick up my kid from school. On top of my job, I do 90% of his job for him, just so the whole night crew don\'t get screwed, then he spends an hour a day just to bitch that I do nothing. So fuck that, I want all crazydave on his ass this last week, stopped doing his job, and he\'s about an inch from getting fired.\r\n\r\nGo hue35 on his ass dude, I\'m telling ya, I ready to kill all the dipshits.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36941,'3a261fea51','By any chance did you make a tutorial to get a server running? I thought I saw your name in a tutorial and just interested...thanks.'),(37586,'ac65089bda','Cabo I would like to submit one of my own songs I have created. I wanted you to review it and give me the ok to perhaps put it on the bitPimps radio. I would like others to get a taste of my music. \r\n\r\n    I will propose music that comes from an underground house style of music. If this is cool please pm me back and we could figure out how to get the song to you. I have many, but would like to send em out one by one and get some critique on them. \r\n\r\ni figure bitpimps is a good chance to get some opinions on my stuff considering i am taking a Disk Jockey course and it has become one of my other hobbies.\r\n\r\nThanks for your time...'),(32889,'3b9a1ee61f','On your website I saw you had batteries.  How many mah are these?'),(32890,'62b31bd372','Hi, when i bought them, the guy said 150 MAH, i have no way of testing this, but after you charge/discharge process they run good. Also, if you are interested i might be selling a box with 150 inside. I sold one last week and it sold for $40.\r\n\r\nI sell them 10 for $7 shipped.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34390,'5e4e2b7c8f','Thanks for the tips and information, I\'ll start working on it. 8-)'),(34391,'07e4a0992c','[quote:07e4a0992c=\"pimptothemax\"]Thanks for the tips and information, I\'ll start working on it. 8-)[/quote:07e4a0992c] :-o'),(34396,'cdb14b8e80','hey man, could you hook me up with 16 N-MOSFETs and 3 of your DC mod boards? How much would all this cost?\r\n\r\nI measured the motor outputs, and would like to know what these change to after the DC mod.\r\n\r\noper. freq.\r\n103.5hz\r\n\r\nduty cycles (reverse to foreward)\r\n-44.5\r\n-38.3\r\n-32.2\r\n-26.5\r\n0\r\n26.5\r\n32.2\r\n38.3\r\n44.5\r\n53.9\r\n60.5\r\n\r\nAlso, with your DC mod, it only works for the foreward, correct?'),(32964,'7db3e4c051','Man I wanted that New Shen, I been lookin at it all week, was wait\'n on it.  I\'m not gonna block you flow though man........... :-?'),(37914,'0efbfb9533','Can do.  It will be a few months before I really get into production mode, but if I produce one that kicks ass before then, then I\'ll send it to you for free if you give it a review.  In fact, the first one I want to work on will be a spiral armeture.  With a spiral armeture, fat comm and winding for torque with some good neo mags and a bb case it should have some interesting performance.  That may be exactly what you want.  Wont know until I make it though.  I\'ll keep everybody posted.\r\n\r\nI don\'t mind giving a few out for free at first so I can get some reviews on my motors from other people besides myself.  If I really want to sell these motors and make a few ducks off it, then I need to get some good advertisement.\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to send one out to you first.'),(36785,'c7ce954133','[quote:c7ce954133=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]If you need anybody to do a fet mod to the cars, then let me know.  I\'m sure you already have that covered, but just in case, it\'s the least I can do to support.  I would offer to paint and putty, but I know there are people here who can do that better than me.  I have a lot of extra supplies and what not.  If I know about the car that\'s chosen ahead of time, I can always send you some stuff that I may have laying around that might go good with the ride.[/quote:c7ce954133]\r\n\r\nHachi !\r\n\r\nPimp I really appreciate your offer and I may call on your services in that respect.  I wasn\'t planning on going that far but with your offer, we may can do a couple FET\'s for the lucky Pimp\'s who\'s name is picked.\r\nI\'ll be intouch!  :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36789,'692324074e','Anytime,\r\n             I can get them in and out as fast as you need.  Just give me a heads up first.  I\'ve already got the fets on hand and I\'ve had plenty of practice doing them in bits.  I\'m not to savy on fet swapping with ZipZaps, but I could always replace the pcb with a bit/clone pcb and give it a controller that I know would have longer range.  I\'ve got literally boxes of controllers that I\'ll never use.\r\n\r\nMy address;\r\nRobert Wilson\r\n1230 North Tomcat Court\r\nVirginia Beach, Va\r\n23454'),(34490,'88a04ed103','it\'s quite different since thee\'s two different mosfets now.\r\n\r\nsee the doco here:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttp://www.woahnelly.com/stuff/xmods/EVOMOSFETInstallationGuide.pdf\r\n\r\ngood luck!\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:88a04ed103=\"Clint\"][quote:88a04ed103=\"ph2t\"]hey man, just wanted to let you know that the installation doco for the evo mosfet upgrade is almost done.  it will be posted shortly.\r\n\r\nif you wanted something sooner to help let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nph2t.,[/quote:88a04ed103]\r\n\r\nsweet thx. I received the package of fets from aus micro this afternoon.\r\nUnfortunatly, i wont be able to work on it until i get home this weekend, so no rush. if the install is anything like the original xmod fet upgrade, i wont have any problems.\r\n\r\nthx,\r\n-clint[/quote:88a04ed103]'),(36791,'9b33bc27a5','[quote:9b33bc27a5=\"Da Big Kahuna\"]Recieved this the day after I posted.....\r\n\r\n[quote:9b33bc27a5=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]If you need anybody to do a fet mod to the cars, then let me know.  I\'m sure you already have that covered, but just in case, it\'s the least I can do to support.  I would offer to paint and putty, but I know there are people here who can do that better than me.  I have a lot of extra supplies and what not.  If I know about the car that\'s chosen ahead of time, I can always send you some stuff that I may have laying around that might go good with the ride.[/quote:9b33bc27a5]\r\n\r\nNow he stepped up BigTime!  I told him I may call on his services, was planning on going that far but with his offer, we may do a couple.\r\nMaybe after this thing gets started, one of the mods will step up, if not, no problem!  I\'m building a shop for shooting some after pics.  This is gonna be off Da Hook !  ( Haven\'t recieved any entries yet but it\'s still early)[/quote:9b33bc27a5]\r\nThat kicks ass, I love it when the members step up like that.\r\nCool man, run with it - I\'m sure more interests will get perked soon, especially after the 1st one goes out.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37593,'f069b240a1','Thanks Cabo, i wll give it a try later on tonight, or this weekend!'),(34976,'a5718a545c','no problem on the size 1/43 or 1/24 is cool if you want more then one 1/24 scale body painted throw it in. The time frame is cool to It might take me a little time to paint all those bodies too so bear with me. \r\n\r\nthanks again looking forward to it!\r\n\r\nAaron'),(37008,'21b97cdc02','Holy shit! Dude, that chassis is a fucking thing of beauty... a work of art... a masterpiece. My jaw is on the floor. God damn, man. I can\'t wait to see this thing done (I can and will, but Jesus that\'s nuts). \r\n\r\nWhew.\r\n\r\nI\'m not sure I more to say at this point... just wow... it\'s sick.\r\n\r\nAnd now for some emoticons...  :-o  :eek:  :-D  :D  :eek:   :-o  :shock:  :shock:    :eek: ...... :shock:'),(37624,'b3aee7e951','Great info Thank You!\r\n\r\nWell,\r\n\r\nLast night my uncle and I took the mr-02s to the track once again! \r\n\r\nHe\'s got the mr02 RM, and I have the MM. Like you said the MM is much longer and we just noticed this last night. It seems my MM on the shortest setting is just as long if not a touch longer than my the RM longest setting.\r\n\r\nAfter doing a few laps I noticed some things, and it is bothering me because it has because some a nag on the track.\r\n\r\nFirstly my tires obviously are not worn in just yet. They are very circular, and do not have the worn in patch for track contact. While we were racing on a few turns I found that my mr-02 would actually pull a 360.\r\n\r\nI found this rather odd concidering my track has very good grip on it (although it is not an RCP material or what ever). \r\n\r\nKeep in mind I was running my mm murcielago chassis and wheels with the mclaren body. \r\n\r\nNow I could be wrong but I figured if i tried to slap on some tires with more wearness the car would handle alot better. I threw on the older set and yes it did indeed handle slightly better. But yet there were still some turns I could not take a high enough speed. The RM on the turns was able to take the turns at about half throttle (stock) While my MM would have no throttle power on turns and just need to be &quot;felt out&quot;.\r\n\r\nThe RM was running on an 8tooth pinion, as compared to my 6tooth pinion (both stock mr-02s)\r\n\r\nSo then I figured perhaps it is the torque and throttle power. My throttle may be too torky for my own good. But I also kept in mind that the track had to have a very specific suspension set up. \r\n\r\nThe question I wanted to ask is this. \r\n\r\nOur track is very flat. It is quite similiar if not exactly the same conditions as concrete. Should I put the rear springs to a harder setting, or Softer setting? and should I consider the front springs to a harder or softer?\r\n\r\nWhat are your best tips for suspension? or a damper system that could be avialable? I am interested to see the difference because my uncles car does not spin like this. He has lowered it, and added a few spacers here and there to fix a few things, but he wants me to try and spot this one out myself (competitive edge haha)\r\n\r\nThanks for your time Hachi!'),(36664,'766a0f681f','[quote:766a0f681f=\"pimpsmurf\"]So far I\'ve found the road radials with the kyosho hard foams, some titanium screws and stock diff parts, the gpm front gearbox, and the radio of course. damn. I screwed up a little man. These will be out ASAP.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:766a0f681f]\r\n\r\nDamn, the gpm front gearbox wasnt in the 1st package?\r\n\r\nGlad you found it!\r\n\r\nLet me know when you ship the stuff out, and if you find anything else.\r\n\r\nI\'ll let you know when i get your origional package should be on tues.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34302,'af6933d093','so could you like , like me instead hate me  :grin:'),(34303,'af6933d093','so could you like , like me instead hate me  :grin:'),(34304,'5ddf6d0b78','No, and if you PM me again, or so much as reply to this message and I will report you to the moderators and it will likely result in a ban.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(34470,'f82e59e2c0','Whats up?\r\n\r\nI need to ask you for another shopping favor, especially since you came through last time with the memory stick.\r\n\r\nMy sister wants an Ipod.\r\n\r\nI\'d like to stay around $150-$225 or lower.  So it doesn\'t have to be a huge memory Ipod.  She wants a pink one, but I told her to worry about price first and then choice of colors.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike'),(37700,'9c7cae15d4','no worries, i just need a final price and a paypal address.\r\ni\'ll give you the shipping details when we\'re ready to roll (no cash this week :-( )'),(36050,'2dc7453b32','That\'s cool, I am always here lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34333,'476ac74650','[quote:476ac74650=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hey Wussup!\r\n\r\nSorry I didnt reply sooner, I still got a bunch of Microsizer bodies and Perfection bodies. Let me know if youre looking for something in particular. Thanks!\r\n\r\nJDM[/quote:476ac74650]\r\n\r\nLooking for :\r\n\r\n[b:476ac74650]3 - Lambo Bodies\r\n3 - Ferrari Bodies[/b:476ac74650]\r\n\r\n\r\nand if you still got \'em:\r\nTomy [b:476ac74650]Gloria, WRX[/b:476ac74650]\r\nPerfection [b:476ac74650]VW[/b:476ac74650]\r\n\r\nAlso looking for a New Tomy Fairlady (lost mine)\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp!'),(34323,'e9bec1fe7e','Eh Arfin, What kind of Epochs are availalbe to us Canadians.\r\n\r\nIs there anything better out there I should be looking for. MY dilemma is propo steering. I love the bits but i just wish they could turn better, I\'ve been designing a sweet track for a while 12inch lanes, which means great for bits alotta room, but even nicer for propo Epochs, tight competitive one on one battles. I just hope these things are worth the money, and if there are \"clones\" to choose from. Let me know man.\r\n\r\nPeace'),(34324,'0f35528c74','I was readin up on some ol posts of yours about Epoch. Lately i\'ve been checkin em out. \r\n\r\nFirst off what part of Canada you from and where can I get a hold of these suckers?\r\n\r\nSeconly any clones around or no?\r\n\r\nTry and get back to me man, thanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34467,'dade5c24cf','[b:dade5c24cf]This IS in the Fo\' Sale section.  Post a price or its gone.[/b:dade5c24cf]\r\n\r\nFuck, just once would someone read the fuckin\' rules.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:dade5c24cf]http://www.klln.fm/klln/images/Assorted/GENERIC/read_rules_anim.gif[/img:dade5c24cf]\r\n\r\n[img:dade5c24cf]http://db.bbc.co.uk/southyorkshire/competitions/images/lead_rules.jpg[/img:dade5c24cf]'),(35017,'6a367eaa5e','your bearing tutorial:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7045'),(35018,'6a367eaa5e','your bearing tutorial:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7045'),(37055,'436a96b48f','[quote:436a96b48f=\"crazydave\"]Got the inspiration, spent my whole weekend fiddleing with this:\r\n\r\n[img:436a96b48f]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_1.jpg[/img:436a96b48f]\r\n\r\n[img:436a96b48f]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_2.jpg[/img:436a96b48f]\r\n\r\nYep, that one\'s yours, biotch. :-o \r\n\r\nI still need to FET mod it, a few details like wrapping some strips around the wheels, to hold the tires on, spin the right front wheel with the dremel to loosen it up a bit,  it pitches the axle out of the car in reverse... but its freaking together, and just about ready to kick butt. The hard shit is done, its all downhill from here. :-o \r\n\r\nI also plan to get another SS motor set, mine has red KIT gears, and orange SS motor now, I plan to run the red SS motor, with my red gears, and yours with the purple motor, and these blue gears. If that works out like it does in SSs, then we should be fairly evenly matched, with a slightly different acceleration curve. Should make for more interesting racing than two indentical setup cars.\r\n\r\nOh yeah, and does this look familiar?\r\n[img:436a96b48f]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_3.jpg[/img:436a96b48f]\r\n\r\nIts like its the same, but different. :???: \r\n\r\nPretty sure this is your body, but I haven\'t decided on the colors. Pep Boys ditched the Plasti Coat, and blew my plans to play with some candy blue on top of black and silver graphics. Walmart ditched the Testors stuff for some House of Kolor paintes, which I\'m excited to check out, but they just threw them in the locked cabinet in a big ol\' pile. Hopefully they\'ll have that\'ll straightened out this weekend, and I can pick some cool custom colors.\r\n\r\n... and I know you like to see how the wheels sit in the wheel wells...\r\n[img:436a96b48f]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_4.jpg[/img:436a96b48f]\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:436a96b48f]\r\n\r\nGod damn!... I\'m still stunned by how fuckin\' cool this thing is. Shit, man... people are gonna shit when they see this car flossed up.\r\n\r\nedit: AND, it hasn\'t EVEN sunk in yet that this car will be in my hands, when all is said and done. God damn.\r\n\r\n\r\nedit 2: have you heard The Ribeye Brothers? If not, I\'ve got a couple of discs to send ya... right up your alley, I\'d bet... fun stuff. They\'re another spinoff of Monster Magnet, just the polar opposite of the other spinoff (Atomic Bitchwax).'),(33597,'0ca4bfdaf1','Sup dude, sorry for the slow reply, lately I\'ve been as busy as the proverbial one-legged man in an ass-kicking contest.\r\n\r\nSweet score on the chargers, but the PIC16C56 is one-time programmable unfortunately.  There are some variations on the 56 chip, you can see them here:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.microchip.com/ParamChartSearch/chart.aspx?branchID=1002&amp;mid=10&amp;lang=en&amp;pageId=74\r\n\r\nBut if its a regular 16C56 it probably won\'t do you much good.\r\n\r\nI\'m checking out HV Community now, just wish I had more time to spend on all these cool projects, there simply aren\'t enough hours in the day!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37793,'5d602e1995','my real name is trent but i get mail as betty too. whichever you want to use is fine with me.\r\nyou could even address it to &quot;the dickhead&quot;, should make it ok! :lol: \r\n\r\nthanks man, no rush for anything. i\'ll let you know when it arrives :-o'),(31298,'194afe10e4','hey thanks! i didnt know i can do that!!!'),(34939,'6e68c46ee5','[quote:6e68c46ee5=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I want that car  :sad: .\r\nInch up to $70 that is my definate maximum.\r\n\r\nThank you\r\nMaxx[/quote:6e68c46ee5]\r\n\r\neh, it\'s clear up over $102.'),(34942,'2282f4d892','What else have you found? You\'re my main source for parts now. eBay is definately off my list now. \r\nSo let me know whatch\' got  :-o \r\n\r\nMaxx'),(31300,'13aadc2a9a','[quote:13aadc2a9a=\"SuperFly\"]\r\n\r\nI\'m pretty hot for the silver one, but there\'s no need to run all over town. Like I said, I\'m in no hurry, and I\'m sure they\'ll restock your local RS sometime soon. I guess include me when you order FETs, and grab a silver vette next time ya see one. What\'s yer Paypal addy? Thanks a ton, I really appreciate it.[/quote:13aadc2a9a]Cool, we\'ll make sure we get you a silver one. Don\'t worry, I wont be running all over town. I\'ll just keep checking online. I got 3 stores within a mile and a half.\r\n\r\nOh and the paypal email is davesmoejoe@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nDave'),(31303,'9c102c8ed4','[quote:9c102c8ed4=\"crazydave\"]\r\n[img:9c102c8ed4]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/dcmod1.jpg[/img:9c102c8ed4]\r\n[/quote:9c102c8ed4]\r\n\r\nIt looks like you\'ve got the two pins at the lower right side of the image jumpered?  Those are pins 1 and 2.  3 and 4 are the two on the lower right.\r\n\r\nSee that dot on the top of the chip?  That marks pin 1.  The pins are numbered from there, going down that side of the chip, then across and back up the other side.  So as the chip is oriented in that picture the pins would be numbered:\r\n\r\n8 7 6 5\r\n (chip)\r\n1 2 3 4\r\n\r\nConnecting 1 and 2 like that won\'t hurt anything, but you\'ll want to disconnect it before continuing.\r\n\r\nDK');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31304,'3df4593ec0','[quote:3df4593ec0=\"codesuidae\"]\r\nIt looks like you\'ve got the two pins at the [b:3df4593ec0]lower right[/b:3df4593ec0] side of the image jumpered?  Those are pins 1 and 2.  3 and 4 are the two on the [b:3df4593ec0]lower right[/b:3df4593ec0].[/quote:3df4593ec0]Are you messing with me?  :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:3df4593ec0]See that dot on the top of the chip?  That marks pin 1.  The pins are numbered from there, going down that side of the chip, then across and back up the other side.  So as the chip is oriented in that picture the pins would be numbered:\r\n\r\n8 7 6 5\r\n (chip)\r\n1 2 3 4\r\n\r\nConnecting 1 and 2 like that won\'t hurt anything, but you\'ll want to disconnect it before continuing.[/quote:3df4593ec0]Ok I see where I went wrong, when you said electrical connections down, I thought you ment the +/- on the bottom corner, like the pic on the website, but I understand what you were saying now. \r\n\r\nOk, cool beans, I\'m gonna give it another go after work tonight. Thanks for taking the time to work with me. :-) \r\n\r\ndave'),(33265,'12e5655dc7','I totally forgot to put something in you package.\r\n\r\nIt was a Love note from Sezzis.  He said he loves you and thanks you for doing the group buy.\r\n\r\nXOXOXOXOXO :-)  :oops:  :bowdown: \r\n\r\nI thought I put it in the box, but instead I put the mailing label. :? \r\n\r\nI don\'t want Sezzis hatin\' on me.\r\n\r\n\r\nlater, \r\n\r\nmike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33752,'e11f42fea3','[quote:e11f42fea3=\"hue35\"][quote:e11f42fea3=\"crazydave\"]I just ordered the decals for P:PSII, and they\'ve got some new 1/72nd decals. Check \'em out. The top set are the ones I intended to order, should be smaller than the ones I used on my car, but check out the second sheet down. That\'s so great becaise I\'m making Gasser out one of my \'57s, and those even have the gasser markings.  :-D \r\n\r\nSo I ordered those too, along with a couple of the flames.\r\n\r\nYou like any of those names? ;) ;)\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:e11f42fea3]\r\nI don\'t see anything... is it my shitty dial-up connection?. . . no link, I think.[/quote:e11f42fea3]Damn, I\'m such a fucking burn out sometimes, I forgot the link. :lol: \r\n\r\nAnd here I was all excited to see what you thought, guess I\'ll have wait \'til after work now. :-( \r\n\r\nAnyways, before I forget again, link: http://www.radicaldecals.com/172front.html\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nInteresting development concerning my trip. My wife informed me last night, she\'s taking a trip to Vegas soon, for a Scrapbooking convention. I got mad, said WTF, its supposed to be my turn to take a vaction, she\'s had 2 vacations since I\'ve been planning this trip to Portland. Then she informs me this morning, that I can just barely afford to go on Oct. 15th, if I want to. But now I\'m not ready, just getting to work on your car, and I never did anthing to my Xmod, or bought an Iwaver. So I\'m still not ready, but I got guilt working on my side now, so I\'m feeling more positive about it again. :-o \r\n\r\nDave'),(31587,'1b26422822','Hi:\r\n\r\nI just noticed that you mentioned there was a toy fair in NYC, and I was curious as to where it\'s located and usually what time of the year it occurs.  Does it have bigger R/Cs also?  Thanks for any help.\r\n\r\n-Max\r\n\r\nP.S.- Love the mat, and it might be a neat idea to make an offroad/rally course for the zip zap monsters and lifted bits.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36027,'8b48256a52','How ever many i can get for 20 shipped to Canada  :-o . But, i\'m buying an xmod lot (if all goes well) so this will have to wait a week or two. So i\'ll just get back to you then! Thanks pimp!'),(34220,'b27cbc6846','[quote:b27cbc6846=\"arfin\"]MG WHERE YOU BEEN HOMIE, lol i been on msn for a while looking for you.![/quote:b27cbc6846]\r\n\r\nHey dude!!\r\n\r\nJust workin\', had to work this weekend, and now i just got up. :) Late night.'),(34638,'272f2690d6','[quote:272f2690d6=\"arfin\"]Hey, long time no see, man i\'m so excited this week, seen those new Microz topic? They look amazing, AND THEY ARE IN CANADA! Also my Metl-tech racer is comin\' in this week, BUT i\'m kinda pissed about that because TeamBonzer, in his review posted about how good it was, THEN all of a sudden tells me it lags, LIKE WTF![/quote:272f2690d6]\r\n\r\nDid you get this METL TECH yet?'),(36265,'e6926478df','[quote:e6926478df=\"Juzi\'s Customz\"]1. Dont ask other people to mae shit for you..\r\n2. I might actually try that once i get the right kind of truck body..  :shock:[/quote:e6926478df]\r\n\r\n1. Unless there\'s a good reason, and I mean damn good, don\'t make posts in old-ass threads. It brings those posts to the top and clutters up all the current posts. You\'re gonna piss a lot of people off real quick if you keep this up... it\'s a personal peeve of mine, and this is as nice as I get.\r\n\r\nYour post wasn\'t even close to anything I\'d consider a decent reason, which bring me to the next thing... \r\n\r\n2. Don\'t make posts about shit that you &quot;might&quot; do. Nobody fuckin\' cares. Really. Not at all. Nobody even cares about what you &quot;will&quot; do. A good rule of thumb is, if you\'re not adding something of value, don\'t make a post.\r\n\r\n3. You\'re in NO fuckin\' position to be telling anyone what they should or shouldn\'t do... ESPECIALLY in an old thread like this. This shit was handled several months and rehashing it is not only totally inappropriate, but it just ISN\'T YOUR FUCKING PLACE.\r\n\r\n4. I get that you\'re all excited to fit in here, so I\'ll do you a favor and tell you... you\'re going about this all wrong, and you\'re startin\' to piss some people off. So, just settle down a notch... right now, time and patience are your best friend. THE WORST possible thing a &quot;newbie&quot; can do is start making a shitload of useless posts... it\'ll be the end of you, real quick like.\r\n\r\nAnother good rule of thumb... right now you\'re profile if showing that you\'re making about 6.75 posts per day on average, which is actually more like 8, since I\'ve deleted several of your useless posts. I, a moderator here, make 1.8 posts per day on average. You\'ll have a lot of posts soon enough, so just chill. Posting like a spaz is only gonna make things worse for you.\r\n\r\n5. Search for some answers before you ask question... this takes time and you\'ll have to do a bunch of reading. The cool thing about that is, you\'re here learning and you\'re not posting anything... that\'s good for everyone at this point in time.\r\n\r\nHere\'s a great example of what I\'m talkin\' about... in the &quot;decal&quot; thread..\r\n[quote:e6926478df=\"Juzi\'s Customz\"]How do you actually apply them?[/quote:e6926478df]\r\nThis shit pisses me off, but I know some others that will tear you apart for this. I\'m gonna do you the favor of deleting this miserable post, and give you even more advice... that\'s an answer you can easily find on your own, so just fuckin\' do that. You could easily go to Google and search for &quot;applying decals&quot; or &quot;water slide decals&quot;... you could also do that search here.\r\n\r\n\r\nAlright, I\'m gonna leave it at these 5 points for now... there\'s more than enough information there to help on your way to becoming a pimp. Read them a few times and let them sink in and it might happen sooner than later. If you find that your posts are disappearing, you\'ll know your not doing very well, and it might be time to re-read this PM.\r\n\r\nFinally, this is not the way things are often handled around here. Normally, I\'d have left your &quot;dumbass american&quot; comment in place, you\'d have been smacked the fuck down and you wouldn\'t want to stay... it\'d just suck too bad for ya. Every once in a blue moon, someone gets a lcuky break and gets some tips on how to get along around here... you\'re getting the deluxe version of this, and you\'d better understand that it\'s just about over. \r\n\r\nGood luck,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(33261,'b7aa61b659','Ummm you PMed me for it........');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33262,'244f230fbd','I did?\r\n\r\n :? \r\n\r\nWow, I must have been really high. :cool:'),(33263,'f3d58f2734','jesse king\r\n163 main st\r\nft. fairfield, me 04742'),(32447,'81217b9333','Hi Man,\r\nNo sign of the package yet.   :( \r\nI\'m checking the post box today, so hopefully they will be there.\r\nDid you send them tracked? I checked with Aus post, and they said that it probably would have made it here within 4-5 days, but that customs can take a while.\r\nGlad you like the bus and I\'m glad to hear the truck was okay - i\'m always a bit dubious on clones.\r\nI guess I just play the waiting game!'),(32450,'1fcaa7030b','could you delete my post in lookin to score\r\n\r\nnew here and posted w/o 50 posts\r\n\r\nsorry'),(31319,'e515deeb56','[quote:e515deeb56=\"crazydave\"][quote:e515deeb56=\"codesuidae\"]\r\n\r\nIt looks like you\'ve got the two pins at the [b:e515deeb56]lower right[/b:e515deeb56] side of the image jumpered?  Those are pins 1 and 2.  3 and 4 are the two on the [b:e515deeb56]lower right[/b:e515deeb56].[/quote:e515deeb56]Are you messing with me?  :lol: [/quote:e515deeb56]\r\n\r\nWell, you know, theres the right, then the [i:e515deeb56]other[/i:e515deeb56] right.  :???: \r\n\r\nI really ought to write a good step-by-step for this.  With pictures.'),(31321,'0f44896f87','Man it\'s the same here in Canada! But i do have a Zip Zap, do you know what those are? I can fully mod that thing, as in Tri-Cell INTERNAL, dual motors, what ever you ask for. If no ZipZaps, i\'ll try and get a Clone/Bit and mod it, then send it to you.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36382,'a09add10d8','Hey, well the money is set, if you have time the next time you go to radioshack, could you pick up 3, if they don\'t have 3, then give me what they do have. Thanks man!'),(36383,'fa6f6774ec','[quote:fa6f6774ec=\"arfin\"]Hey, well the money is set, if you have time the next time you go to radioshack, could you pick up 3, if they don\'t have 3, then give me what they do have. Thanks man![/quote:fa6f6774ec]\r\n\r\nThey had no TA sets. Those are probably sold out.  If I see any, I WILL pick them up for ya!'),(33369,'2735d60aa9','yeah, but i have to install it first\r\n\r\nlol'),(31341,'4cf0544904','Hi there , I purchased a bonzermat from you at christmas , and i really liked it . I recently moved house , and dispite the sign on the package\r\n \" DO NOT FOLD\"\r\nthe removal people still managed to fold it in half , now i have big creases that are like creater shapes in my mat .I would really appreciate if you could give me any help possible on getting rid of them.\r\n\r\nmany thanks , \r\nJoe :cool:'),(31353,'b6d924099d','Got it just now ..... its all good..... and yeah, my controller looks like refugee from a garbage dump...the regular zz\'s are slow... thats why there are so many speed mods for them ...you rock ,thanks for the extrta love!\r\nmarc');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37316,'0060ed02be','[quote:0060ed02be=\"cj\"]These were not in the first order.\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver	Black	Green\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	0	0	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.54	0	0	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME330LAN	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR LANCER) - 1PC	$5.90	0	0	1\r\nXME330MUS	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR MUSTANG) - 1PC	$3.84	0	0	1\r\nXET330FORD	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR TRUCKIN) - 1PC	$6.90	1	0	0\r\nXET330HUM	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR HUMMER) - 1PC	$5.90	1	0	0\r\n\r\nActual	$53.54	 	 	 \r\n10.00%	$5.35	 	 	 \r\nSub	$58.89			\r\nS&amp;H	$3.00			\r\nTotal	$61.89			\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.41 Off of GPM\'s regular price.\r\n\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me know as soon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com.  Please include your user name in the notes on PayPal.\r\n\r\nIf you do reply by February 11th  your request will not be ordered.[/quote:0060ed02be]\r\n\r\nJust silver and green.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be able to pay until this Saturday, after P-day clears.\r\n\r\nWhats the status of everything else?  The rest of the silver, all the green and the diffs?\r\n\r\nI need a complete set so I can start putting things together.\r\n\r\nHow much longer?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike'),(37001,'bafd91d9ed','Got the inspiration, spent my whole weekend fiddleing with this:\r\n\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_1.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_2.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\nYep, that one\'s yours, biotch. :-o \r\n\r\nI still need to FET mod it, a few details like wrapping some strips around the wheels, to hold the tires on, spin the right front wheel with the dremel to loosen it up a bit,  it pitches the axle out of the car in reverse... but its freaking together, and just about ready to kick butt. The hard shit is done, its all downhill from here. :-o \r\n\r\nI also plan to get another SS motor set, mine has red KIT gears, and orange SS motor now, I plan to run the red SS motor, with my red gears, and yours with the purple motor, and these blue gears. If that works out like it does in SSs, then we should be fairly evenly matched, with a slightly different acceleration curve. Should make for more interesting racing than two indentical setup cars.\r\n\r\nOh yeah, and does this look familiar?\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_3.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\nIts like its the same, but different. :???: \r\n\r\nPretty sure this is your body, but I haven\'t decided on the colors. Pep Boys ditched the Plasti Coat, and blew my plans to play with some candy blue on top of black and silver graphics. Walmart ditched the Testors stuff for some House of Kolor paintes, which I\'m excited to check out, but they just threw them in the locked cabinet in a big ol\' pile. Hopefully they\'ll have that\'ll straightened out this weekend, and I can pick some cool custom colors.\r\n\r\n... and I know you like to see how the wheels sit in the wheel wells...\r\n[img:bafd91d9ed]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10007/ps2_4.jpg[/img:bafd91d9ed]\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36670,'dc30a70ee2','[quote:dc30a70ee2=\"pimpsmurf\"]Thanks for being so understanding man. You probably won\'t want to use the front gearbox anyway however. It sucks for several reasons.\r\n\r\nThe only reason one would use the full rear gearbox is if you are running an extremely hot motor (like x2lspe, not a plasmatomic/etc), and using a low gear (9-10). Otherwise it is an overweight non-heatsinking sucker.\r\n\r\nIt would do some heatsinking if you manage to make a alloy replacement for the motor spacer (goes behind the motor when you use the tall gears), but I never got around to it.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:dc30a70ee2]\r\n\r\nNo problem man, i might run the full rear gearbox but i\'ll have to see whats in the package, i plan on running a plasmatomic with the 1/16\'th electrics, and if theres enough parts to build a second rolling chassis then i\'ll run a deluxe too since i have one just laying around on my workbench.'),(31368,'4d80e7adb4','Excellent!  Glad you\'ve got it going! \r\n\r\nI haven\'t really got past the basic plans for the 9 step version.  I\'m not looking forward to doing installs for people, since it will require a couple more wires.  Doing the installs is a bit tedious.  On the other hand it would be fun to do :)  One of the stopping points is just that I have to rebuild my software almost completely because I want to increase the PWM frequency from its current 100Hz to something like 100kHz.  This will eliminate all the buzzing and smooth out the torque.  It should be quieter and may aid in driveability.\r\n\r\nI\'ll also have to do a new PCB design to allow for the extra wires required for the 9 step version.  The new PCB design will be a little bigger and will include a couple of resistors so the DC mod can be installed on cars without the fet mod without requiring external resistors.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I\'m looking forward to seeing your writeup.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35799,'8b4d282271','[quote:8b4d282271=\"MafiaS\"]Let me know, I could get them easily here![/quote:8b4d282271]What are they going for?\r\n\r\nEither way, I\'m broke now. Can I keep you in mind when I have cash in a month or two?\r\n\r\ndave'),(35930,'ccbc835a27','I can\'t, but I\'ll try! :lol: \r\n\r\nThanks man, I\'m very interested in trying out this project.  Just one more question, would you consider it to be a hard project for a first project?  I haven\'t found anything willing to try that isn\'t too hard, nor do I have the time to make up a design (school, work, sleep, food....), so I am willing to try your idea.'),(31956,'eba38f566e','[quote:eba38f566e=\"MotorGong\"][quote:eba38f566e=\"blindrider3\"]I know its you.\r\n\r\nEveryone told me its you.\r\n\r\n\r\nSo dont even lie.[/quote:eba38f566e]\r\n\r\n\r\nIt was cool that you explained to me what was going on with that.\r\nWhen I went there yesterday, I couldn\'t even understand most of the posts.\r\n\r\nAnyway, listen, we could go \'round and \'round with this, but I see no reason. Who is \'everybody\' that told you? I don\'t think people know me very well as of yet.\r\nI went to go see where the pics were linked to, but all was gone. And you said it was linked to motorgong? hmmmmm\r\nHave ya found out anything else yet?\r\n\r\nAgain, I have nothing against you.[/quote:eba38f566e]\r\n\r\n\r\nOh well.\r\n\r\nNow they are making a forum dedicated to how gay I am..\r\n\r\n\r\nMan their fags\r\n\r\nThey have like no lives. Their pissed cause I deleted a shitty forum, wow.'),(31957,'56b28a4e23','crappy, man.\r\n\r\nserious, dude. \r\n\r\nI have 1 window open right now.\r\nI\'m new to computers.\r\n\r\nI could see someone new like me screwing around like that and doing something dumb like linking to photobucket :grin: \r\n\r\nBut someone is screwin with me just the same.\r\nIf ya need to know anything, I can try and find out.\r\n\r\nwhat the hell is \'Nakkah\' anyway? :-?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (31958,'aa91d1f781','Yo DT, sounds good. I\'ll bring the bit with me to work tomorrow and ship it out. Later.'),(36563,'8ad1283b58','I believe I have everything else in there. I am going to clean up the workshop tonight and sort everything. It\'s possible there is something else left behind, but I\'ll be sure to include it.\r\n\r\nI\'m really very sorry about the mistake man. That sucks. I hope you have another TX for the mean time (any AM 27 is cool)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36565,'baf47ae657','Hey man, ive been doing some searching on the site and i cant seem to find the answer im looking for.  Im installing an iwaver pcb in my zzse buggy but im a little confused about what to do with the steering POT.  Do i use the existing zzse pot or do i use the iwaver pot???  ALso, ive been reading that i need to install 10k ohm resistors on the pot (whatever pot i end up using)  Do   What wires do i need to solder these to?  The iwaver pot only has two wires but the se has three so im a little confused on the issue.\r\n\r\nAny help would be great\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36160,'bcbe5411e0','[quote:bcbe5411e0=\"pimpsmurf\"]Well, you would get everything I have for it including the H8 electronics that are currently installed and the parts that are coming for it.\r\n\r\nThere is a brand new stocker diff (I like it with thick grease better than the BB diffs), new clear chassis, new clear front gearbox and chrome gearbox. The alloy/titanium parts. oil shocks, etc, etc. Custom front bumper, titanium-shaft GPM BB diff, kyosho shock mounts. Too much to list. Buttloads of parts and whatnot. Over $1000 in it. I have all sorts of tuner parts here and there.\r\n\r\nI\'ll include the old kyosho board if you want, but it needs a turbo.board to work in anything.\r\n\r\nI\'ll take $225 including USPS Priority w/ $200 in insurance &amp; paypal fees.\r\n\r\npaypal joseph.yarbrough@gmail.com if you want it.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n-JNY[/quote:bcbe5411e0]\r\n\r\nso it still has all thos aluminum parts etc. that you listed before?\r\n\r\nMan thats one hell of a deal, and motors too and what not correct?\r\n\r\nI got a deluxe just sitting on my bench so i could put that board to use too :eek: \r\n\r\nIf i paypal you could you give me a full list of everything included or maybe just a huge pic before i seal the deal.\r\n\r\nAlso you you be able to do 210? most i have');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37340,'948e8e70e4','[quote:948e8e70e4=\"betty.k\"]yup, you got it! bettykay@gmail.com\r\n\r\ni\'ll keep these goods for you, i won\'t sell them to anyone else if you\'re slow paying :-o[/quote:948e8e70e4]\r\n\r\nCool man, just sent the $ as we speak!\r\n\r\nBtw Change the shipping name that paypal gives you from Chris to Matt, the account was under my father\'s name originally.\r\n\r\nThanks for the sweet deal man, looking foward to recieving and reviving this xmod!\r\n\r\n :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(36221,'6a3b475d0f','I think there is a plasmatomic there. Seriously, I think there are like 3-5 armatures (uberdash arm, plasmatomic arm, pn s03, etc.) I believe the plasmatomic needs new brushes.\r\n\r\nThere are extra parts galore. It is in runing condition with the exception that it needs a new front gearbox, of which I am including 2 (1 clear, 1 chrome.)\r\n\r\nI could ship it UPS, but it would cost an arm and a leg. USPS priority would be easier and cheaper, and I would insure it for full value so you would be covered.\r\n\r\nIt is an awsome truck, but my 1:10 nitro is taking all my time, so I\'ve not had the time or money to do it up the way I wanted (custom alloy chassis, etc.)\r\n\r\nI just don\'t have the time for it.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37154,'5ae21ac662','I hope this is what you\'re looking for. :-) \r\n\r\n[URL=http://img482.imageshack.us/my.php?image=img091110ljcopy1ra.jpg][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/1449/img091110ljcopy1ra.th.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]\r\n\r\n[URL=http://img482.imageshack.us/my.php?image=img091110ljdiggycopy3hh.jpg][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/2935/img091110ljdiggycopy3hh.th.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]\r\n\r\n[URL=http://imageshack.us][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/1512/v35sigcopy1pr.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]\r\n\r\n[URL=http://imageshack.us][img:5ae21ac662]http://img482.imageshack.us/img482/6099/v35sigcopy22zf.jpg[/img:5ae21ac662][/URL]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36663,'3542ca49cc','So far I\'ve found the road radials with the kyosho hard foams, some titanium screws and stock diff parts, the gpm front gearbox, and the radio of course. damn. I screwed up a little man. These will be out ASAP.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36397,'6f843b2072','[quote:6f843b2072=\"pimpsmurf\"]yeppers w/ insurance\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:6f843b2072]\r\n\r\n\r\nCool let me know when you ship it out man!\r\n\r\nI\'m full of anxiety i cant wait! :eek:'),(33195,'7141bcbb30','I could use a second WRX body. Does it have the complete stock bumpers and hood?\r\n\r\nI\'ll can send down a MO if you send me an address.'),(37712,'74a2be13fa','lol no problems\r\n\r\nonce again a clean deal with skylinekid! that makes like what? 5?'),(37924,'38542dd6df','I realize I said I would paypal you $30, but I forgot about shipping. If ya feel like you can trust me, you can package it up and mail it, and just tell me how much postage was and I\'ll paypal ya that amount. However you want to do it is cool with me.'),(34901,'97c1883c51','thanx anyhow guy  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36175,'8b60f54c46','It comes with everything on this list here except the deluxe\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6918\r\n\r\nDid you get the plasmatomic in the mail?\r\n\r\n\r\nAnnnd the stuff installed and listed in the before pm?\r\n\r\nIf so I\'ll take it! :eek: \r\n\r\nJust give me a few days, im expecting some paypal payments soon.'),(37897,'ab6245197d','[quote:ab6245197d=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]I wouldn\'t mind helping you out, but I have just enough for one in each test car right now.  I\'ve got to keep one in each car to do the comparison essay I\'ve been working on.  Also the parts for each are starting to get scarse.  If I let one go, there\'s no garauntee that I\'ll get another anytime soon at a decent price.\r\n\r\nSorry to be a taco, but if it helps any, after I finish the next two cars reviews I\'m going to take a break from all the comparisons and go into motor construction.  I\'ll be making hand wounds, plasma-atomics and other types of motors and selling them.  There just isn\'t enough people that do that.  I know, that doesn\'t really help you out now.\r\n\r\nHave you looked into an Uberdash?  Also, an Anima modified motor or &quot;Fatboy HC&quot; as they call it at Atomic mods is also a good second.[/quote:ab6245197d]\r\n\r\nYeah problem with the uberdash is it\'s plastic comm.\r\n\r\nSo you will be hand winding motors? :???: \r\n\r\nMight you be interested in making me one, i could test it out and do a full review if your serious about it. I would pay you of course.\r\nReason why i ask is i could use a nice top speed motor for my lipoly MZM, with a sideplate of torque too of course.'),(33004,'49a8cd90ea','Hey Finks,\r\n\r\nJust letting you know I still havent got the parcel.  \r\nIt sucks, I got all excited cos there was a slip in the box to pick up a parcel, but it was the mini and sub Chrome sent me less than 2 weeks ago.  :? \r\nThanks again for helping out man, but after 6 weeks im beginning to wonder if some customs officer isn\'t enjoying some office-bashing with my MT.  Australia post said the only way to check it\'s progress is from the America end, but if they have told you they can\'t help, then I guess i may never know where it ended up.\r\nI\'ll keep you posted if I get anything, but right now i\'m not holding my breath.  :(');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32906,'ffaff945f7','[quote:ffaff945f7=\"Sporttracguy\"]yeah man, $10 sounds good to me for the bearings and the blue subaru body.  I also have stuff to trade if you are interested, mostly bit bodies and what not but i figure you are trying to get rid of that sort of thing lol,, just let me know and ill send the money\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nSTG[/quote:ffaff945f7]\r\n\r\n\r\nHey man!!!\r\n\r\nIt\'s been kida of hectic on this end, and I thought maybe I dropped the ball here. I forgot where we left off---did you still want the bearings and body? \r\nLet me know , and sorry if I kinda stalled the whole deal here.\r\n\r\nMotorGong\r\n--Dave'),(36295,'7e0e040703','&gt; Does it come with a controller to use the 1:16 elec\'s with.\r\nIt comes with the MZM controller, which works with the 1:16 electronics\r\n\r\n&gt; How did you make the servo work?\r\nThe 1:16 electronics are kyosho-brand. I just wired it up.\r\n\r\n&gt;Did you get those parts in today?\r\nTomorrow or Monday.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(32975,'8efc0f68da','Hey man, sorry to bug you.  I was moving shit around and found one of the custom bodies I was working on a long time ago (started building it back on TinyRC), decided to search to see if anybody had done one yet on Pimps. \r\n\r\nNoticed you\'ve got one in work and Last Ride should be beautiful when done, but your last update was in May.  Wondered if you were gonna do anymore updates, or if it\'s been put on hold, killed, or what?\r\n\r\nMy body relies on composites rather than styrene, and should fit an unaltered ZZ chassis.  Mine is going to be a 1980\'s Cadillac Funeral Coach (haven\'t chosen it\'s coachbuilder yet), based *very* loosely off a Majorette Caprice police car.   What paint scheme were you planning, I don\'t want to be accused of copying.  I was probably gonna go Black on Black, Black on Blue, or Black on White/Cream.  I had considered going Hearse Hotrod with it, but yours seems to have taken that title, so I\'ll just try to go with elegant and stately instead.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (32976,'9c76da02a5','Yah still in the works mine is based on an 80\'s model hearse and its going to be black on black just have a lot of iron\'s in the fire so havent finished it up yet! I am still working on it off and on just have not posted any updates (guess I should do that soon!). \r\n\r\nI would like to see what you have planned sounds real cool give me a buzz if you need anything!  :grin: \r\n\r\nSWG'),(36812,'9eeb6ce5a1','[quote:9eeb6ce5a1=\"Sporttracguy\"]Right on, ill get the money to you tonight.\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:9eeb6ce5a1]\r\n\r\nIt hot the PO about 9am this morning. :-o \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike'),(36813,'22e0ed4101','[quote:22e0ed4101=\"SuperFly\"]Hey man-\r\n\r\nJust saying hi, haven\'t seen ya round as much as usual. Kids can do that to ya. How is your little one? My little guy is having his first birthday in 3 weeks, can\'t believe it\'s gone by so fast. Santa brought him his first Hot Wheels set for xmas, so he\'s got the bug now. \r\n:-D \r\n\r\nBTW, I successfully modded my Nelly the other night. I was scared shitless I was going to fuck it up, but all went well. All I needed to do was change the direction the power wires entered the Nelly from the battery terminals. I\'m running a McLaren body on the Nelly chassis, and there\'s not a lot of room under there and it felt like I was going to bust out the windshield every time I mounted the body. I was having some binding issues that were affecting the rear suspension, so I made the wires come out the other side. Now I have about a nice short 4cm length leading to the Nelly instead of the full length as supplied being doubled over and wadded into the shell. Is there any danger in just wrapping a little electrical tape around the nelly vs. the shrink-tubing? I just wanted to protect the Nelly pcb and don\'t have a heat gun.\r\n\r\nBeen in full MR02 mode lately, almost more obsessively than I ever was with bits.[/quote:22e0ed4101]\r\n\r\nlol, good stuff!  Yeah, marrisa is %110 my attention and fucken loving it.  she\'s going wel, just started solids.  So it\'s poo left right and centre!\r\n\r\nI\'ve been busy whoreing on the xmod forums.  Sorta to an obssesive level, lol...  Pushing nelly\'s trhough my site shop and doing al sorts of crazy things in the 1:28 world.\r\n\r\nI hear ya on the mr02.  I\'mjust about to goto betty\'s for an extended lunch/race/bake meet. lol.  Gotta love the holidays when no-ones in at work!\r\n\r\nThe tape will be fine.  SHouldn\'t have any issues there.  I now use 28AWG silicon wire on my nellys for the very reason you pointed out.  It works well and takes the current no probs.  It\'s funny with all the xmod kiddies go &quot;but man, you\'re not using 18awg superflex, mega huge wire&quot;.  Yeah, just shows how a little bit of info can be screwed so royally on forums with kids on it.\r\n\r\nI also have the ma-010, you may want to look into it for your RCP track.  EMU knows a shitload about z\'s and he says that the ma-010 even in stock form totally owns the RCP tracks.\r\n\r\nbetty and I are concrete whores so my ma-010 needs a lot of suping up to make it even remotely effective.  One good thing is that they\'re improved the electronics so you can run hot motors no probs.  The hottest I\'ve run ins the pn Anima and it works a treat.\r\n\r\ncheers and avagoodone mate.\r\n\r\nMAtt.'),(35324,'ff5749d04a','Sup Pimp !\r\n\r\nI didn\'t know you worked for RS, what a coinkidink !\r\n\r\nWanted to ask a favor, Is there any way you can get hold of a ZipZap store display guide?\r\n\r\n[img:ff5749d04a]http://i12.ebayimg.com/03/i/05/82/f7/7d_12.JPG[/img:ff5749d04a]\r\n[img:ff5749d04a]http://i21.ebayimg.com/01/i/05/7c/bf/07_12.JPG[/img:ff5749d04a]\r\n\r\nI\'ll pay/trade you for one if possible.\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp  :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35955,'968b634d4b','Thanks for your time. \r\n\r\nSorry to keep buggin you, I read up on the steering mod for the original chassis could i purchase those resistors at a local RS or something?\r\n\r\nthe 4.7 ohms are best correcT?'),(33345,'d929b50690','I wanted to know how the hell you made that thing? can u give me a lil step my step please?'),(34237,'81282db8db','I dont care about packages.  Is it ok if I send the $ tomarrow?'),(34238,'66044446b5','Thats cool with me. :-o \r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com'),(36673,'acea2cad77','The 1:16 electronics are sort of top heavy because of how I could mount them. I would definately suggest the nelly deluxe, but the nelly will own. Also, I had included some silver magnet wire which will turn one of those armatures I included into an insane motor. They are freaking nuts. a 21 turn silver motor will make an extreme top-speed machine...\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36406,'78d0652773','Did you get a chance to ship it out?'),(37934,'cf645525e5','Did you send the stuff yet? Just want to make sure, so I can keep an eye out for it.........');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36204,'f28a140570','Yes!\r\n\r\nJust sold some of my last rc stuff!\r\n\r\nI should have payment ready tomorrow!\r\n\r\nStart packing it up pimp knowing its going to a good loving home :-o \r\n\r\n\r\nBTW would you be able to ship UPS Ground?'),(36205,'36910ce06a','Hey man where did you get that picture in you Avatar that chick is sweet! is there a full video? I hope I hope I hope!!  :-o'),(36211,'37859ff144','[quote:37859ff144=\"sessiz\"]I not only have no idea where I picked that animated .gif from but I\'m lookin for that chick myself. Definatly from a video of some kind. :???:[/quote:37859ff144]\r\n\r\nMan if you find it I wana copy! thats one hot Gif! thanks for sharing!'),(36214,'74e09ad31d','i have a decent sized rcp track in the basement and i invite others to race 1:28 scale rc\'s on saturdays twice a month.  \r\n\r\ni don\'t care what kind of rc you have, ie; xmods, iwaver, mini-z, firelap....  i posted a link to our club forum on mini-zracer.'),(37348,'74ae8351e8','[quote:74ae8351e8=\"betty.k\"][quote:74ae8351e8=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:74ae8351e8=\"betty.k\"]yup, you got it! bettykay@gmail.com\r\n\r\ni\'ll keep these goods for you, i won\'t sell them to anyone else if you\'re slow paying :-o[/quote:74ae8351e8]\r\n\r\nCool man, just sent the $ as we speak!\r\n\r\nBtw Change the shipping name that paypal gives you from Chris to Matt, the account was under my father\'s name originally.\r\n\r\nThanks for the sweet deal man, looking foward to recieving and reviving this xmod!\r\n\r\n :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:74ae8351e8]\r\n\r\nok, so this is it?\r\n\r\nMatt Gera\r\n4303 Radcliffe Dr.\r\nPalm Harbor, FL 34685\r\nUnited States[/quote:74ae8351e8]\r\n\r\nYup you got it man! :-o \r\n\r\nThanks again\r\n\r\n---Matt');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36256,'9f55c99bf4','Go to the old forum topic and read that. I haven\'t sold or given anything away. It is a completely pimped MZM. It has everything. \r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36955,'a33d85199f','I got the parts on Saturday.\r\n\r\nI\'m assuming thats all you have for now. :???: \r\n\r\nHow much longer for the rest?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(36956,'f201e6be7c','[quote:f201e6be7c=\"sg219\"]I got the parts on Saturday.\r\n\r\nI\'m assuming thats all you have for now. :???: \r\n\r\nHow much longer for the rest?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\n\r\nMike[/quote:f201e6be7c]\r\n\r\nCool \r\n\r\nFind some .5mm shims for the rear Knuckles before you start putting it together.  The GPM Knuckles are 1MM deeper than stock so the stock/Ball bearings leave too much play.  Since they did that also your wheels will set about a mm further out.\r\n\r\nI\'ll know more what I am getting later this week.\r\n\r\nI did get an email form GPM this morning.  I\'ll be posing the updated price list with Gearboxes in the Group buy.'),(33443,'482f425c79','Got the bodies a couple dayz ago....Thanx\r\n\r\nAlthough one of the Mini Van packages had a clear Civic body  :???: \r\n\r\nWhat happened ?  Now I got 5 of them  :lol: \r\n\r\nDon\'t worry though, I got enough shit around here for it not to even matter!  (Then why am I bringin it up ?)  :? \r\n\r\nPeace Out');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33598,'5b523145ef','This ain\'t my normal style, but your response to my earlier ribbin\' proved to me that you can take a little shit and be cool, so I figured stop by and give some advice.\r\n\r\n[quote:5b523145ef=\"Fordman212\"]FUCK this place.  You\'re all a bunch of pricks who think you\'re the shit just because you\'re respected on a micro-rc-car site.  Its a god damn internet forum for crying out loud, you act like its some big important thing where everything has to be perfect.  peace out.[/quote:5b523145ef]\r\nI just read SG\'s post you\'re replying to here... just have a bit of patience, man. It\'ll be cool. What he\'s trying to say is that you should have just waited until you\'ve got the pics, then make your post... it is sort of useless to say, \"I did this and that and I\'ll post up some pics later\".\r\n\r\nGettin\' pissed is only gonna make it worse. If you\'re serious about splittin\', then see ya later. If you wanna stick around, just chill, take your time and get a good feel of what\'s what... if you think about it, your thread would have been just fine if you had all your shit together. As it was, it was just kind of an empty post... SG was right, now you just gotta let that shit roll off... be cool and that shit goes away quick.\r\n\r\nAs for the \"we\'re a bunch of pricks... yadda yadda...\", This place is just as we want it, and it\'s certainly not for everyone. And nobody gives a fuck who comes or goes, \'cuz we\'re happy as we are. However, it\'s always cool to have a cool new pimp around... \r\n\r\nEither way dude, but if ya let this initial round of shit roll off your back and participate in a useful way, you\'ll fit in just fine... it\'s a good place to be, if you\'re into micro RC cars.\r\n\r\nlater,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(34914,'0d31d08465','[quote:0d31d08465=\"Maxximum Attack\"]jump in the chat urgent![/quote:0d31d08465]\r\n\r\nOkay, where you at?  :grin:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34935,'bdfb043167','[quote:bdfb043167=\"Maxximum Attack\"]thanx anyhow guy  :-)[/quote:bdfb043167]\r\n\r\nLemme know in the future if you need anything. I asked my wife\r\nto check out that auction(i wanted to see what it was). She said it \r\nwas up near 100$.  :eek: \r\n\r\nAre you specifically looking for an hpi? Local shop here has the\r\nxray m18 for 75$, but you still need the electronics.'),(33934,'77f3d2a44f','i never stuck anything up my ass domb shit im not gay like u i can get some u just have to pretend bizatch'),(33068,'e741263a75','holy crap, just realized i never replied to your ealier pm.  sorry about that.  anyway, the tri-celled zzmt i made was pretty easy to do.  it had great  speed, but from your posts, it sounds like you\'re looking for more of an off roader than a speed demon.  anyway, i have a duratrax piranha peak charger that i used to charger the tricell.  i wired up a zzmt controller with pigtails that i could connect to the duratrax.'),(33094,'68d9c8aefc','[quote:68d9c8aefc=\"Finks\"]Dude!  Thanks a ton for all the wicked fuckin cool shwag!  Honestly, what a freakin blessing dude.  I so appreciate it.  The Skyline pullback, and the Evo Sport addition, oh and the Nacumichighdlhgleesl Wanted all of those for so long.  Now that I have two UPSes, I can mod one out too, oh what to do what to do?  The motors too, jeeze dude, this was so perfect.  What you sent me was 100x better than a couple of extra bucks, I can\'t say it enough, perfect.  MUCH respect and thanks\r\n :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o \r\nFinks[/quote:68d9c8aefc]\r\n\r\nNo Problem Pimp!  I appreciate the hard work you did to pull that group\r\nbuy together (you got bigger balls than me!)\r\n\r\nEnjoy  8-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36465,'91d6c69db3','[quote:91d6c69db3=\"MafiaS\"]yes sir i could get em....imma talk to my guy and let him know for how much sound good?[/quote:91d6c69db3]\r\n\r\nLet me clearify my position!\r\n\r\nI\'m only interested in Special Edition, Limited Edition and Rare [u:91d6c69db3]Tomy[/u:91d6c69db3] Bit Char-G cars.\r\nCheck with Yo Guy and lemme know !'),(34815,'948825ccc4','[quote:948825ccc4=\"45tr0\"][quote:948825ccc4=\"Nasphere\"]:-? \r\n[quote:948825ccc4]Processor: Mac OS X-compatible processor that is a model G3 or higher.\r\nOperating system: Mac OS X version 10.3 or later.[/quote:948825ccc4]\r\nlol, i have OS9... My mac wont run OSX...[/quote:948825ccc4]\r\n\r\nTry here.\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.microsoft.com/mac/downloads.aspx?pid=download&amp;location=/mac/download/misc/msn_messenger2.xml&amp;secid=35&amp;ssid=1&amp;flgnosysreq=False[/url]\r\n[quote:948825ccc4]\r\nProcessor: Macintosh PowerPC.\r\nOperating system:* Mac OS 9.2.2. or above [/quote:948825ccc4][/quote:948825ccc4]\r\nThanks dude..'),(35132,'2e5d3b2c4c','[quote:2e5d3b2c4c=\"arfin\"]Hey man, well i want to bid on this http://cgi.ebay.com/Micro-RC-Collection-Bit-Char-g-Microsizer-Many-Parts_W0QQitemZ6011299770QQcategoryZ44025QQssPageNameZWDVWQQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem\r\n\r\nBUT, he forgot to let Canadians bid on it, so Ebay won\'t let me. So, i\'m just sending the hook up to my homie.[/quote:2e5d3b2c4c]\r\n\r\nHey dude!\r\nThanks! Actually, I have lots! That\'s why I\'m sending you some stuffs! LOL\r\nYeah, sorry, I haven\'t been on for a while. Talk to you soon hopefully!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33118,'e2fe03815c','[quote:e2fe03815c=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I saw Cabo, in a tut, wire the battery box directly to the charging post on the controller, by-passing all the circuitry and timers etc. So the controller keeps charging untill you break the loop by removing the car. This was a BCG dual cell tut BTW.\r\n\r\nWill this also work for a Tricell?\r\n\r\nMaxx[/quote:e2fe03815c]\r\n\r\nit might, but without any way of regulating the charger output, the batteries may not last more than a few cycles.  too much juice for too long equals toasted batts.'),(33130,'bf13e6d590','ok, I\'m at dan_lacap@hotmail.com in case you\'re missing my paypal account. With the money, I\'m gonna bid on one on Ebay.  Thanks for your quick responses!!!  I hope it shows up.\r\n\r\nThanks again'),(33123,'a464ae73fd','It looks like they\'re lost. Any luck with you?  Let me know...'),(33124,'0a49182d2c','Yeah, its not looking good man,, USPS says im pretty much out of luck so i think im going to have to just send you back your cash and if they show up ill let you know,, i figure they will end up back at my place one of these days,,,, Im really sorry about all of this\r\n\r\nSTG'),(33126,'f00a26055c','that may work, just make sure the batts don\'t get too warm.  also not to sure how many charges you\'ll get out of the aaa\'s in the controller.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35760,'9ec20cf591','Ok so it\'s the...\r\n\r\n- Subie Body\r\n- Mustang body and kit\r\n- stage 2 motor\r\n- as for stock parts if you could, throw in wheels or somtin, but i really need a steering rod, either a yellow or red one, I want to try the steering mod but I don\'t have any extra\'s.\r\n\r\nand in return it\'s the...\r\n\r\n- custom rally painted mitsu\r\n- Diablo\r\n- 27 mhz controller\r\n- 49 mhz controller\r\n- both 3.0 motors, 1 is sorta fishy, but i will give it to ya ne ways. \r\n\r\n\r\nI think that\'s cool, but if you don\'t just let me know...ps if you really don\'t want the Civic body i will take it ahah...\r\n\r\nMy shipping info is:\r\n\r\n26 George Gale Road\r\nWoodbridge, Ontario.\r\nL4H 2S6\r\nCanada\r\n\r\nLet me know yours, and how would you like to do this?'),(37431,'a4703d7887','[quote:a4703d7887=\"sg219\"]Went out today. :-o[/quote:a4703d7887]\r\n\r\nI will get out some stuff to you (I will try) tomorrow I have been knee deep in work and traveling but will get it out As soon as I can. Thanks man and thank bird for me!!  :-)'),(37432,'b5aa6c9c9b','[quote:b5aa6c9c9b=\"steelwoolghandi\"][quote:b5aa6c9c9b=\"sg219\"]Went out today. :-o[/quote:b5aa6c9c9b]\r\n\r\nI will get out some stuff to you (I will try) tomorrow I have been knee deep in work and traveling but will get it out As soon as I can. Thanks man and thank bird for me!!  :-)[/quote:b5aa6c9c9b]\r\n\r\nWhenever.  It\'s cool. :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36546,'4f6a47aef5','I\'ll take the 7317\'s.  They\'re good fets.  I went ahead and picked up a Spider.  I was trying to stay on a budget, but the Spider was calling me.  I really want to try and keep the MR02 as stock as possible.  The Nelly Deluxe needs a lithium setup.  I\'ll save the Nelly for another project and try out the Spider first.\r\n\r\nThink that Spider can handle the plasma-atomic with neo mags and an alloy 10 tooth pinion?  Should I give it a break in between runs?  Could it ultimately be fried if pushed too hard for too long?  Soryy for all the questions.'),(36061,'d68d7c968c','Yup, hope you get the parts fast! Drivetrain parts are the best haha.'),(35815,'f6296ed4ec','Alright, I like your bearings, shaft, and the alloy stuff you just showed me\r\n\r\nYou still want the body, controller and chassis?'),(33446,'23b1082305','Ye I prolly wanna buy some duel cell batteries and some clear and painted bodies I wanna start up a collection.......\r\n\r\nThe F1 will prolly be for bits, but the thing is im tryin to shave down bit chassis make em really light....or just design my chassis out of aluminum or something light and shape it myself so its flatter not really a bathtub sort of look......just picture a 1/8th scale F1 chassis brought down to a 1/64th scale......close to the look of most F1 slot cars just the chip is the trouble right....'),(33440,'23b1082305','Ye I prolly wanna buy some duel cell batteries and some clear and painted bodies I wanna start up a collection.......\r\n\r\nThe F1 will prolly be for bits, but the thing is im tryin to shave down bit chassis make em really light....or just design my chassis out of aluminum or something light and shape it myself so its flatter not really a bathtub sort of look......just picture a 1/8th scale F1 chassis brought down to a 1/64th scale......close to the look of most F1 slot cars just the chip is the trouble right....');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33140,'7a433de844','I just saw your beautiful FD, and I was wondering where you got the rims for it from?  They would look awesome on my ZZSE Shelby!'),(37649,'22a5f11aad','[quote:22a5f11aad=\"Maxximum Attack\"]money sent[/quote:22a5f11aad]\r\n\r\nCool :smile: \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt\r\n\r\n\r\nHope all goes well with the install man! :-o'),(33146,'e2a54123a8','Hey man,\r\n\r\nSorry for not getting back to you earlier....\r\n\r\nAnyways, the rims came from a DUB CITY (made by Jada Toys) diecast.\r\nYou\'ll find all kinds of DUB CITY cars at Target and Walmart.\r\nThe rims I used are from an original DUB CITY car. I\'m not sure if they make those any more. :o  \r\nBut I\'m sure there are still some out there... just gotta look. :-o \r\n\r\nBut, if you really need [u:e2a54123a8]those[/u:e2a54123a8] rims, I think I still have some.\r\nLet me know.\r\n\r\n-DriveWRX  :cool:'),(33151,'038d34f6c5','It\'d really help if you could send a set of those my way, how are the tires on them?  Will Zip tires fit?  I bought a Big Time Muscle car today, but the tires were like friggin\' plastic. :o  I got a few things laying around, I have some skater clones, Micro Speed body and track sets, and some Racing Champions F&amp;F diecast &amp; keychains.  Just give me a holler as to what you need and i\'ll dig it up for ya.  Thanks! :-) -Cameron'),(33152,'c246aa757e','Hey cabo, \r\n\r\nI\'m having problems getting my user gallery to work.  I can upload a file, enter information for it, then get a \"The Previous File Could Not Be Placed.   All files placed successfully\" error.   I dunno if I\'m just a stupid newb, or if I need to seek higher authority to unlock it.  Do I need to like go on quests for the moderators, or post a pic that makes even Sessiz feel sick, or like be over 50 posts, or something?      Um, help?\r\n\r\nfrizzen-');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33153,'2d14d3ec72','[quote:2d14d3ec72=\"frizzen\"]Hey cabo, \r\n\r\nI\'m having problems getting my user gallery to work.  I can upload a file, enter information for it, then get a \"The Previous File Could Not Be Placed.   All files placed successfully\" error.   I dunno if I\'m just a stupid newb, or if I need to seek higher authority to unlock it.  Do I need to like go on quests for the moderators, or post a pic that makes even Sessiz feel sick, or like be over 50 posts, or something?      Um, help?\r\n\r\nfrizzen-[/quote:2d14d3ec72]\r\nTry it now. You should be good to go. Let me know if not.\r\n\r\nI waived the normal fee of a jar of goats blood and a pair of mosquito testicles. :-)'),(33162,'038d34f6c5','It\'d really help if you could send a set of those my way, how are the tires on them?  Will Zip tires fit?  I bought a Big Time Muscle car today, but the tires were like friggin\' plastic. :o  I got a few things laying around, I have some skater clones, Micro Speed body and track sets, and some Racing Champions F&amp;F diecast &amp; keychains.  Just give me a holler as to what you need and i\'ll dig it up for ya.  Thanks! :-) -Cameron'),(33163,'41c237df88','Hey Cameron,\r\n\r\nI saw the pic of your Shelby...Nice!  8-) \r\n\r\nThe DUBs came in two different sizes. I used the small ones on my FD.\r\nI think you need the larger size for your Stang to look right.\r\n\r\n[img:41c237df88]https://home.comcast.net/~DriveWRX/Wheels.jpg[/img:41c237df88]\r\n\r\nThe DUBs have a soft plastic tire. They\'re OK. Some grip but nowhere near Bit or ZZ tires.\r\nYou can put Bit or ZZ tires on DUBs but you\'ll need to modify the DUBs first. Look at the pictures and you\'ll see that stock Bit wheels have a midrib that hold the tire on. DUBs don\'t have this, so you\'ll need to make your own. I superglued styrene plastic strip stock (available at your local hobby shop, they\'ll know what that is. Look by the train section) to make midribs on DUBs.\r\n\r\n[img:41c237df88]https://home.comcast.net/~DriveWRX/WheelMod.jpg[/img:41c237df88]\r\n\r\nHope this makes sense.  :-o \r\n\r\nSend me your address and I\'ll send you a DUB small set and a DUB big set. You\'ll have to modify the DUBs yourself though...\r\nI\'m also going to assume you know how to mount the wheels to the axels and spindles. If not, do a search on the forums, you\'ll find all the info there.\r\n\r\n-DriveWRX (Vince)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33164,'41c237df88','Hey Cameron,\r\n\r\nI saw the pic of your Shelby...Nice!  8-) \r\n\r\nThe DUBs came in two different sizes. I used the small ones on my FD.\r\nI think you need the larger size for your Stang to look right.\r\n\r\n[img:41c237df88]https://home.comcast.net/~DriveWRX/Wheels.jpg[/img:41c237df88]\r\n\r\nThe DUBs have a soft plastic tire. They\'re OK. Some grip but nowhere near Bit or ZZ tires.\r\nYou can put Bit or ZZ tires on DUBs but you\'ll need to modify the DUBs first. Look at the pictures and you\'ll see that stock Bit wheels have a midrib that hold the tire on. DUBs don\'t have this, so you\'ll need to make your own. I superglued styrene plastic strip stock (available at your local hobby shop, they\'ll know what that is. Look by the train section) to make midribs on DUBs.\r\n\r\n[img:41c237df88]https://home.comcast.net/~DriveWRX/WheelMod.jpg[/img:41c237df88]\r\n\r\nHope this makes sense.  :-o \r\n\r\nSend me your address and I\'ll send you a DUB small set and a DUB big set. You\'ll have to modify the DUBs yourself though...\r\nI\'m also going to assume you know how to mount the wheels to the axels and spindles. If not, do a search on the forums, you\'ll find all the info there.\r\n\r\n-DriveWRX (Vince)'),(33165,'d657b556dd','Yup, I already read up on the tutorials...thanks for the tip on the midrib though!  Thanks for the comments on the Shelby, she\'s mostly stock right now but i\'m working on changing that.  Right now i\'m halfway through installing a 2.8 steering motor.  Here\'s my addy, make sure you put your return address on it, ya dig? :-o \r\n\r\nCameron VanDerHorst\r\n10102 Prouty Road\r\nConcord, OH 44077');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36509,'aee3dcb801','Yup the rear driveshafts were Alloy.'),(36510,'4578a26f9a','kk thanks just wanted to know!'),(34955,'3b321dd792','[quote:3b321dd792=\"Clint\"]I\'m pretty sure i\'ve seen them at the hobby shop.. Packaged under the Great Planes brand. you could most likely order them online as well.[/quote:3b321dd792]\r\n\r\nThanks clint! :-)'),(33167,'d657b556dd','Yup, I already read up on the tutorials...thanks for the tip on the midrib though!  Thanks for the comments on the Shelby, she\'s mostly stock right now but i\'m working on changing that.  Right now i\'m halfway through installing a 2.8 steering motor.  Here\'s my addy, make sure you put your return address on it, ya dig? :-o \r\n\r\nCameron VanDerHorst\r\n10102 Prouty Road\r\nConcord, OH 44077'),(33964,'1fa3785fe7','[quote:1fa3785fe7=\"arfin\"]No, i wasn\'t calling YOU the hypocrite, i was calling SKYLINE KID a hypocrite. He keeps shit talking newbs, dissing them about all types of shit, when he had these same problems recently.\r\n\r\nWhen i said i was sayin\' the same thing as you, i was talking about the \"pud on pud\" action, if that quote still exists, i coudn\'t find it i was asking why all the newbs are dissing eachother.[/quote:1fa3785fe7]\r\n\r\nAlright then... it wasn\'t clear at all that that\'s where you were coming from. But, I shoulda given you the benefit of the doubt before I flew off the handle. Man, it\'s been so damn nuts around here lately, I guess I have an itchy trigger finger. I\'m glad I misunderstood, \'cuz like I said, you seemed to quickly get past your rough start and have been a good guy to have around... that\'s why I was so pissed. Like, in the midst of all this recent noob bullshit, guys like you are gonna start causing trouble? Cool, well, sorry I flew off the handle... someone probably deserved it, but it wasn\'t you :lol: .    And thanks for bein\' cool about it... you coulda gone off in the other direction, but you stayed cool like a true pimp... my cool has been blown since about last week sometime... whatever day SHAUN signed up.  :shock: \r\n\r\nThat said, it\'s best to just stay outta that shit altogether, \'cuz obviously it just gets confusing with everyone goin\' off on everyone these days... I\'ve had too many PMs with noobs just straight-up not gettin\' it. \r\n\r\nAgain, sorry for the short fuse and thanks for bein\' cool.\r\n\r\nlater,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(36781,'3194502d92','No worries,\r\n                It sounds like the diff.  I\'ve never had a problem with mine, but I\'ve heard of other people having problems.  The red on works better from what I\'ve read.  I\'ve taken mine apart.  It\'s not too complex.  It\'s definately not as bad as taking apart a ball diff.  \r\n\r\nAlso, are you using any after-market products on the rear drive train?  I tried some aluminum rear lower arms that caused binding in the rear axle.  I had to get the rear gear box to go with the arms to fix it.  Rat-shack\'s rear lower arms are all made with different measurements on their screw holes on the arms, so swapping out rear lower arms can cause binding sometimes.  \r\n\r\nlastly, try taking the whole rear drive train apart to see if there is any hair wraped around anything.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33709,'a72c8648a2','Can a ZZSE board take 3-cells w/o a FET mod? I\'ve searched and all I\'ve seen were FET posts and topics\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx'),(33712,'40475654ba','Salaams,\r\n\r\nI hope Allah makes Ramadan easy on you and accepts your deeds and du\'ah. \r\nAhmeen\r\n\r\nWa salaam :-o \r\nMaxx\r\n\r\nPS: I\'ve started fasting today.'),(33175,'7c063291d9','hi man! ph2t just dropped in an e clip and bb for my epoch that you sent. thanks a bunch for the hookup! :-) \r\ni got to hear about \"max\". sounds good, i\'m interested to see how it all goes together.\r\n\r\ncheers, b.k. :-)'),(35178,'6c4634624e','[quote:6c4634624e=\"arfin\"]Serious! Is the bf2 Demo mulitplayer? Yeah, my computer SHOULD be able to run it, It will be sick if we do, maybe the clan can be BitPimps LOL. Next time i see you on Msn, or pm\'s i\'ll tell you about the MetlTech.[/quote:6c4634624e]\r\n\r\nCool, sounds good!!!\r\nDude, read the Battlefield 2 thread at BP! That\'s all I\'ve been talking about for the past 2 weeks LOL!! \r\nCheck out the demo!'),(33939,'4de582d729','Btw what are the chassis\'s you made, made out of?\r\n\r\nAnd thanks again man!\r\n\r\nYour zzmt is looking relly good too nice work!\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35173,'3be8456856','[quote:3be8456856=\"arfin\"]O, that E-mail that Superfly posted up here and at craiglist or somthing. Anyways, i got the metl tech! It\'s pretty sweet.[/quote:3be8456856]\r\n\r\nYeah, sorry man, I remembered that e-mail from craigslist after I sent that to you LOL!!!\r\nCool, the Metl-Tech is cool? I can\'t wait to hear about it. I\'m sure I\'ll talk to you soon.\r\n\r\nHey, can your computer run BF2 Demo?\r\nYou know how we hook up on MOHAA? Well, we can easily hook up in BF2 and make our own squad and everything. So if someone dies, they can respawn at the squadleaders position. We can do secret missions together or be snipers together or whatever.\r\n\r\n--Dave'),(35693,'71a0ab40f9','[quote:71a0ab40f9]It seems to be a mechanical problem, because when i pick it up, it does fine. I bought it returned, but it didnt seem to do this at the start, and once she gets going she doesnt stutter as much but about once every 2 or 3 feet when at full speed. I dont really want to replace the electronics, but I don\'t know of any electronic interference that could be happening, I am using the stock motor. Thanks for your help.[/quote:71a0ab40f9]\r\n\r\nI am going to sleep pretty soon but ill open a chat window and if you dont mind, we can discuss the problem there.'),(33908,'fe41219d2e','[quote:fe41219d2e=\"SuperFly\"]I finally got around to digitizing those Stones bootlegs. Do you have an easy way for me to transfer them to you? I can burn CD\'s and mail them, but if you\'ve got some space I can upload to, I can send em tonight. There\'s about 8 albums worth of material.[/quote:fe41219d2e]\r\nUnfortunately, we\'re gonna have to go the CD route. The FTP is setup rather strictly so I wouldn\'t be able to open a connection to you or vice versa.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37647,'7dda132adb','[quote:7dda132adb=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Check for the $13 in 5-7 mins, I should be done the transaction by then.[/quote:7dda132adb]\r\n\r\nCool, will do man, i\'ll get your package to the post office this week. :-o'),(33182,'ab34126eff','Still no package.\r\n\r\nCan you send the money?'),(33183,'106752fb80','it was $12'),(36933,'603b7ca6b8','[quote:603b7ca6b8=\"Stoli\"]Thanks dude. I will play around with that gallery thing tonight. I know absolutly nothing about php so.... kinda screwed there. and as far as mysql forget it. I barly know html. ROFLMAO. \r\n\r\nI guess I;m glad I can build what I have thus far. Its been trying at times but it looks good for a starting out page.[/quote:603b7ca6b8]\r\nWelp, some of those PHP/MySQL galleries are self-installers.\r\nYou basically upload everything, hit an install script, it installs, and then you configure the rest via a web administration/configuration screen.\r\nIt\'s pretty simple really.\r\nGive it a go dude - what do you have to lose?'),(34796,'fc8c059ed9','[quote:fc8c059ed9=\"HirotoR34\"]Never mind....I just wanted to throw in an MT seeing as how all my entries are bits. I just finished a kick ass MT and thought it would fit in well, but I\'ll just wait for the next one. No big deal, just thought I\'d ask...... :-o[/quote:fc8c059ed9]\r\nWell, that\'d make life easier on everyone so cool. :-o \r\nSorry, but thems the rules.\r\nFor sure keep it for the next contest, you know we\'ll have more. This just gives you more time to fuck everyone else up with your innovation and skill.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37876,'1983a9647d','I deleted the image link in your signature.\r\n\r\nIt contained an Internet worm. :-x \r\n\r\nI realize it\'s probably not your fault and didn\'t even know about it.\r\nJust watch what you link to.\r\n\r\nAnd for sure, DO NOT link to anything on danasoft.com'),(37357,'f7830d2700','hiya man. i just got back from the post office, your stuff should arrive in 1 - 2 weeks.\r\nshoot me a message when it arrives and if there\'s any problems or there\'s something missing don\'t hesitate to let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers, b.k.'),(33253,'2a48b36c73','[quote:2a48b36c73=\"Finks\"]jesse king\r\n163 main st\r\nft. fairfield, me 04742\r\n\r\nit better be girl on girl porn! :lol:[/quote:2a48b36c73]\r\n\r\nHow\'d you know I needed your addy? :???:'),(33254,'67b2ade23c','[quote:67b2ade23c=\"Tuner1989\"]Crap i almost forgot. The subaru body has the rear bumper posts are shaved on the inside so a fith cell could fit everything looks fine. you just wouldnt be able to change bumpers easily. Its all packed and ready to go i hope this is ok if not pm me and ill ship back your money order[/quote:67b2ade23c]\r\n\r\nThat shouldn\'t be a problem, I was planning on using it as is and my current body will be painted.'),(34558,'7e4e540af7','I was a little surprised that nobody had answered it before me. I had been off line to two days.\r\n\r\nIf you are shipping US Mail use:\r\n\r\nBill J. Wilson\r\n4457 Tolbut Street\r\nPhiladelphia, PA 19136\r\n\r\nIf using UPS:\r\n\r\nBill J. Wilson\r\n8719 Jackson Street\r\nPhiladelphia, PA 19136\r\n\r\nUPS requires signatures in Philly and my father is retired and at home most the time. Just let me know which way it\'s coming so I can warn him (Unfortunately we share a name  :lol: ).');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33269,'685fd03437','I got your envelope today, thanks!  I put a box o\' goodies together for you.  I\'ll ship it out tomorrow when I get some packing tape.  Thanks again!  -Cameron'),(33284,'8a1d203927','DT wats goin on i wanted to quickly ask u man.....i dunno if u can do this for me but i love porsches the Carrera is my all time favorite car, specially the GT versian man......but ne ways can u teach me how u made that car? show me a lil tutorial or something step by step to make my own? i would fuckin truly appreciate it man honestly.........let me knoww'),(33285,'0df9cd2f15','[quote:0df9cd2f15=\"SicilianRacer9\"]DT wats goin on i wanted to quickly ask u man.....i dunno if u can do this for me but i love porsches the Carrera is my all time favorite car, specially the GT versian man......but ne ways can u teach me how u made that car? show me a lil tutorial or something step by step to make my own? i would fuckin truly appreciate it man honestly.........let me knoww[/quote:0df9cd2f15]\r\nSorry Man, you may have the wrong Pimp!  I don\'t have a Posted Porsche in my stable.  Super Fly did a few slammin Porsches, Finks did one also but I think thats it.  Look thru the Galleries............ 8-)'),(33290,'47529508ea','I really need some rim lugs. Metal if ya got em but if not send me price for alllllllllllllllll the plastic ones ya got. Rat shack wants $8.00 for 15?? WTF is that all about. Mine keep bustin ever since i put the stage 3 motor and 4x4 in it. every 3rd drift on the hardwood floor the back right one keeps bustin no matter how loose/tight I put it. \r\n\r\nAnyways enough sob story. How many you got.\r\nAlso looking for different bodies that will fix on the RSX Chassis. Banged up or whatevere I don;t care.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33294,'063b23fd60','thats no prob dude paypals aight. Can you just hol em for me. I;m kinda broke this pay. its rent and car payment paycheck? \r\n\r\nFo sho I\'ll take 1 set though?\r\n\r\nthanks dude.\r\n\r\nJ'),(35300,'996120fab5','I can work with that no problem man. By clean what I mean is the background. Less shit goin on behind the car the easier for me to cut it out. :-)'),(33418,'3f9e25830c','Ya...what you sayin must be a Canadian thing \"eh\"....lol ye we talk like that in Toronto and these people are lucky there\'s a fuckin computer screen infront of me and now thier actual faces the thing i hate is everyone thinks there a tough guy on the computer and can write wat eva the fuck they want...what ever man'),(37915,'d89fa965a7','[quote:d89fa965a7=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Can do.  It will be a few months before I really get into production mode, but if I produce one that kicks ass before then, then I\'ll send it to you for free if you give it a review.  In fact, the first one I want to work on will be a spiral armeture.  With a spiral armeture, fat comm and winding for torque with some good neo mags and a bb case it should have some interesting performance.  That may be exactly what you want.  Wont know until I make it though.  I\'ll keep everybody posted.\r\n\r\nI don\'t mind giving a few out for free at first so I can get some reviews on my motors from other people besides myself.  If I really want to sell these motors and make a few ducks off it, then I need to get some good advertisement.\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to send one out to you first.[/quote:d89fa965a7]\r\n\r\nSounds promising, i would be more than happy to do a full write up etc. I also have a speedchecker i could test it out on.\r\n\r\nSo are these mainly going to be torque motors or top speed?\r\n\r\nMaybe make the winds for top speed 25 or so, then slap some neo\'s in there to make the torque jump.\r\n\r\nJust throwing out ideas.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(33881,'36e5f81f17','[quote:36e5f81f17=\"arfin\"]You know i never felt \"hung over\" before, about a year ago i drank a mickey to my head of straight JD, and still felt good the next day!!! Was a little wobbley, but it was all good, i have stories to tell from that night DAM. Well our time zones are way off, so i don\'t know when 9:15 is, could you tell me in minutes? It\'s 11:41 over here.[/quote:36e5f81f17]\r\n\r\n\r\nShit, we\'re 3 hours apart? damn, yeah, it\'s 8:47 right now lol\r\n\r\nso i guess that would be about 12:15pm to you. just sittin having coffee, talkin to the GF before she leaves for the whole day...Sunday is her busy day with riding lessons and all');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33302,'685fd03437','I got your envelope today, thanks!  I put a box o\' goodies together for you.  I\'ll ship it out tomorrow when I get some packing tape.  Thanks again!  -Cameron'),(35488,'d76cbfcc46','[quote:d76cbfcc46=\"arfin\"]No man it doesn\'t!  :o  I meet all requirements EXCEPT my Graphic Card isn\'t compatible with the game! Sucks so hard, you made it sound so good, now Im jealous! Anyways, how you been bro?[/quote:d76cbfcc46]\r\n\r\n :( \r\nawww man, that sucks!! You were the first person I thought of when I first played the game.\r\n\r\nI\'ve been alright. Almost caught up with my finances and what not.\r\nSorry I STILL haven\'t sent that package yet! :( \r\nI feel bad. Hang in there, and we\'ll get that charger working in no time! :-o'),(34078,'80cb359fff','Yes you can enter. Read the rules on the 1st page of the contest, don\'t ask such noob questions.\r\n\r\nNow, you first have to learn how to resize your pics to 600mpx wide or less then you have to find a site to host the picture, you\'re using putfile so that\'s ok, then, read this carefully:\r\n\r\nOnce the picture is hosted on putfile (and is the right size), right-click the picture and goto properties. There you will see Address(URL) copy that url and paste it between image tags ([img]     [/img] &lt;---image tags).\r\n\r\nSo when posting your picture it should look like this:\r\n\r\n[img]h*tp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/images/logo/bitpimps.gif[/img] \r\nput \'t\' in place of \'*\' and the picture will be visible like below.\r\n[img:80cb359fff]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/images/logo/bitpimps.gif[/img:80cb359fff] \r\n\r\nAfter you\'ve finished typing your post, PREVIEW IT before clicking SUBMIT, so that you know for sure if the picture will show.\r\n\r\nReply and let me know what you do and do not understand\r\n\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(33309,'c7559c3b1b','Hi,\r\n\r\nI know you bought some modded ZZSE\'s from pimpsmurf...are you willing to part with one? DC+Fet mod?\r\n\r\nLook at this thread [url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6718&amp;highlight=]click me[/url] . I canadd on stuff I guess for one of those modded SE\'s\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37408,'bfcfcc6089','[quote:bfcfcc6089=\"blackranger3d\"]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7241&amp;start=30\r\n\r\nHey in the above thread you talk about using blue builders foam. Could you tell me the actual product name if you remember. I am in Toronto (Canada) and I am trying to find some. I went to home depot and they don\'t have anything like that (well anything that I or the staff could help me find.)\r\n\r\nTIA[/quote:bfcfcc6089]\r\n\r\nwell dont know the true name its insulation foam they put it behind walls like behind siding (outside walls) I got mine at Home Depot in the lumber section. The foam sometimes comes in pink and green but main color is blue. I think its called Celotex or close to that. Hope that helps let me know if you need more help.\r\n\r\nSWG'),(33313,'912739dda0','Hey man.\r\n\r\nsorry, I only got the one ZZSE off Pimpsmurf, (the rest was ZZMT\'s and a lipo zip) I\'m still trying to fix the SE too, cos there is something wrong with it.  it won\'t hold a charge, reverse doesn\'t work and i think the duty cycle mod is the problem.\r\nBest of luck dude!'),(33314,'616265c7d0','Thanx anyway dude. any MT parts lying around that I can get a charging port of the controller?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34092,'b951b749c0','[quote:b951b749c0=\"SHAUN\"]sup how ya doing im ok i finaly got to walmart and got my paint y was i in a big hurry to go to walmart the primer isnt dri yet  :?  hmmmm oh well hi[/quote:b951b749c0]\r\n\r\ncool man, HI!'),(33328,'2d68aa632a','Hi, my zip is 80207'),(33329,'334425a9a2','[quote:334425a9a2=\"weazel\"]Hi, my zip is 80207[/quote:334425a9a2]\r\n\r\nPriority.....$9.00\r\n\r\nReg Mail.....$7.00\r\n\r\nFor 5 Kit racers\r\n\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com is my Paypal.'),(33331,'a4cfcca2c4','Guess what just showed up in the mo\'fuckin post!?\r\n\r\nAll present and accounted for - the box looks like it got kicked from the states, not flown, but its all here.\r\n\r\nThanks man.  Phew.  9 weeks - i was worried there for a while!\r\n\r\nOh, btw, I can\'t get the ZZSE to charge right - i turn on the controller, turn the car to OFF and put it on.  The light blinks red for about 15 seconds, then goes yellow (red &amp; green together).  Turn it on to try and run it, and no good. Any thoughts on what I\'m doin wrong?  (i\'ve checked it on all six selections on the controller too - no luck)\r\n\r\nBut jeez, just so glad it all got here safe!'),(33332,'e47fc92f3e','Awsome, thank god!\r\n\r\nAs far as the SE...  Hrmmm, it worked when I test drove it, I honestly couldn\'t tell you, I am in no way a tech guru.  You say it only says that it\'s charging for the first couple of seconds, maybe the battery, or the charger.  This is a question for  the pimps.  Ask and you shall recieve.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33381,'3f9e25830c','Ya...what you sayin must be a Canadian thing \"eh\"....lol ye we talk like that in Toronto and these people are lucky there\'s a fuckin computer screen infront of me and now thier actual faces the thing i hate is everyone thinks there a tough guy on the computer and can write wat eva the fuck they want...what ever man'),(33545,'e181add8ba','To connect any servo to a Mini-Z CB you have to remove the servos internal circuit board then wire the motor and potentiometer directly to the Mini-Zs circuit board, you also may have to use a parallel resistor to match the potentiometers resistance.\r\n\r\nThe MR-02 servo case is part of the chassis so the only way I know of to use the MR-02 servo is to make a custom case.'),(33915,'6a3371d463','As far as this baja bit goes, no i dont plan on selling it.  I may however make  another one later on down the line though.  Im glad you like it.\r\n\r\nSorry,\r\n\r\nSTG'),(33559,'d9bce9ec77','Cabo I need a favor...\r\n\r\nI just got in a Microsizer Ferrari set 40mhz\r\n\r\nWell i ran into some problems. At first while I was driving the motor was throwing it around. Then it hit the wall a few times and it just stopped completely, followed by some interupted gesture. Ex, when you put it in forward motion it continued even when I let go of the botton and this happened with reverese as well. \r\n\r\nSo I went to see if it was the charger and the red 45 second light would not shut off when it was completely charged, this happend from the minute i opened the box. So i thought it was a battery fault, and it kept overcharging. I opened the chassis and the silver conductors at the bottom of the chassis were a \"greenish\" coloration.\r\n\r\nI figured if i scratched this off and then resolder the battery back on it would actually function properly again.\r\n\r\nBut in the meantime I actually took apart some wires i am not to sure which ways they must be put back in. And how to get this car back up and going...\r\n\r\nCabo if you have any pictures, or suggestions, or any tips please contact me as soon as possible because I really dont know how to do this by myself as a beginner...\r\n\r\nThanks Alot\r\n\r\nSicilianRacer9\r\n\r\nLooking forward to your response!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33560,'bb4e73e185','[quote:bb4e73e185=\"SicilianRacer9\"]Cabo I need a favor...\r\n\r\nI just got in a Microsizer Ferrari set 40mhz\r\n\r\nWell i ran into some problems. At first while I was driving the motor was throwing it around. Then it hit the wall a few times and it just stopped completely, followed by some interupted gesture. Ex, when you put it in forward motion it continued even when I let go of the botton and this happened with reverese as well. \r\n\r\nSo I went to see if it was the charger and the red 45 second light would not shut off when it was completely charged, this happend from the minute i opened the box. So i thought it was a battery fault, and it kept overcharging. I opened the chassis and the silver conductors at the bottom of the chassis were a \"greenish\" coloration.\r\n\r\nI figured if i scratched this off and then resolder the battery back on it would actually function properly again.\r\n\r\nBut in the meantime I actually took apart some wires i am not to sure which ways they must be put back in. And how to get this car back up and going...\r\n\r\nCabo if you have any pictures, or suggestions, or any tips please contact me as soon as possible because I really dont know how to do this by myself as a beginner...\r\n\r\nThanks Alot\r\n\r\nSicilianRacer9\r\n\r\nLooking forward to your response![/quote:bb4e73e185]\r\nYou need to be searching for these answers in the forums, or at least asking this stuff in the forums. I really don\'t have time to play \"Micro Support Service\" to everyone as I\'m sure you know.\r\n\r\nAnyways, it sounds like this just started once you hit a wall.\r\nCheck to make sure your motor is seated properly and the heat sink is clipped in properly.\r\nNext make sure you have fresh batteries.\r\nNext make sure you have a fully charged car.\r\nIf you still have troubles, you\'ll have to start digging a little more.'),(36523,'eb1d811a5c','Whats the word bigbird?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37640,'441c5faead','I would like it, but I don\'t want to buy a charger etc. I\'ll buy that stuff when I\'m shopping for batts.\r\n\r\nI only wanted it cuz I had the cheapo charger doing nothing. Plus I\'d need a board harness.\r\n\r\nSo just the board. I\'ll send you $13, shipping for phatboi was under a buck. That cool? \r\n\r\nHey, you got any Xmod stuff? Since I last asked?\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(37102,'5f6d792f29','[quote:5f6d792f29=\"Maxximum Attack\"]XME039R/4WD\r\n\r\nIf this is all I need for the 4WD, weed out the unnecessary parts that it replaces. \r\n\r\nIf I get the 2nd set in blue would it change the price? If not, gimmie the 2nd set in blue. [b:5f6d792f29]Don\'t commit me to the 2nd set yet I still haven\'t contacted my guy yet.[/b:5f6d792f29] I will do so this evening when I think he got home from work[/quote:5f6d792f29]\r\n\r\nColor really doesn\'t matter.  You could get your car parts every color they offer and pricing would be the same.  They only problem with color is that certain colors tend to take longer to get here.\r\n\r\nI plan to submit this order in 1 week.  Let me know soon how many you need.'),(33582,'27e8add558','The Iwaver CB uses a 5,000 ohm potentiometer.  You will need a multimeter to check the resistance value of the potentiometer of your servo.  I have a HS-55 that has a 5,000 ohm potentiometer, if yours is the same you won\'t need a parallel resistor.  \r\n\r\nAlthough you can use resistors to adjust the steering throw, parallel will reduce the potentiometers resistance, or two on each side in series will increase the resistance.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33583,'73eaca8fd0','[quote:73eaca8fd0=\"LBRC\"]The Iwaver CB uses a 5,000 ohm potentiometer.  You will need a multimeter to check the resistance value of the potentiometer of your servo.  I have a HS-55 that has a 5,000 ohm potentiometer, if yours is the same you won\'t need a parallel resistor.  \r\n\r\nAlthough you can use resistors to adjust the steering throw, parallel will reduce the potentiometers resistance, or two on each side in series will increase the resistance.[/quote:73eaca8fd0]\r\n\r\nVery helpful thanks lbrc :-o \r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(34931,'b6f07d50d1','Let me know how many bodies you feel you would need me to paint for that and I will do it I can paint at least 10 or more but I want to be fair. I was planing on getting a Li-poly charger so this will just be an excuse to go ahead and do it! \r\n\r\nlet me know what you think would be fair oh and I will provide an Honest and detailed review no problem. \r\n\r\nthanks for the opertunity man!\r\nAaron \r\n :-)'),(34519,'21fa8a0957','Hey there\r\n\r\nI haven\'t sent out your chassis yet, I\'ve been broke paying for tuition. But I should be able to send it out next week around thur/fri.\r\n\r\nBTW, dou you have any of the 8-spoke bit wheels, the smaller ones. I would like some for an Initial D car I will be working on soon. If not, then dont worry about it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33602,'28caecb21d','Well, instead of wasting my time and his, all he had to do was click the \"back\" button, and get on with his life.'),(33603,'e46ec7a7a4','Like I said, either way... it can get rough around here, but once you\'ve earned a little respect, it\'s smooth sailin\'. A lot of new dudes have a hard time and go away. Occasionally, they have a hard time, stick it out and enjoy the hell outta their stay.\r\n\r\nIf you went back into that thread, made a new post, acknowledged that you should have waited to post until you had pics and that you get that now, I bet shit would be different for you fairly quickly.\r\n\r\nWhatever though... just tryin\' to help ya out.\r\n\r\nhue35'),(35501,'3d879a0b86','Oh that\'s so wicked.  Bit size?   How much do you need to have for it?\r\n\r\nI\'m:   \r\nJeremy Boyle\r\n1325 N Dukane Way\r\nIndianapolis, IN  46214'),(33607,'df6c6316c6','Ill give it a shot.  But after that, If one more dipshit pisses me off, well, its been great talkin to ya.. We\'ll see what happens.'),(33615,'1f5e2cc728','[quote:1f5e2cc728=\"Fordman212\"]I just read the thing about the tempo... No, i have a 99 f-150 flareside.  4.6l Triton v8.  Mark 3 conversion package.  Flowmasters with 45\'s comming out the back, ill send you a link to my picturetrail gallery since i know u wont believe me.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.picturetrail.com/gallery/view?username=xcubanoloco2x&amp;x=0&amp;y=0[/quote:1f5e2cc728]\r\n\r\nI woulda believed you man, but whatever... nice truck. \r\n\r\nI guess the advice I gave earlier kinda went the wrong way, eh? Well, all I can say is it seems like MafiaS is the guy who actually took the advice... if you read his shit, from the start of his SicilianRacer9 posts (where he was a fuckhead), to his do-over as MafiaS, you\'ll see he has turned shit around pretty damn well. It\'s a good example of what I was talking about.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33680,'7834ceedb4','[quote:7834ceedb4=\"backdrift\"]Hey dude, thanks for doing that. And yeah, im suprised that the post was as well as it was. With you being hammered and all, well thanks. \r\n\r\nIE: http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6786&amp;start=30[/quote:7834ceedb4]No prob, I suppose. I was just drunk, I love to fight when I\'m drunk. I would have threw my beer in his face if he was here, but he\'s not, so I typed, alot. :lol: \r\n\r\nThat was the first time I tried doing Hogjowlz style edits. I prefer to let the idiot\'s post stand on its own merit, but I have to admit that was fun. It was like a edit fest, because someone was even editing some of my edits. Dude had no chance of getting a post through. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave'),(36216,'7e067d7d69','I seem to remember something about you having a design company or doing bussiness in the &quot;graphic design&quot; area. If I\'m wrong disregard this pm. :lol: \r\n\r\nHere\'s where I need your help/advice. I have a chance at a job as a low level graphics &quot;guy&quot; for transworld entertainment corp. My cousin is a lead tech guy over there and he is getting me a foot in the door. (director of marketing owes him big  :lol: )\r\nWhat I need from you is a tip or two on what exactly should I put together potfolio wise to show this guy. I got a rough idea of what this cat wants to see and I feel gay as fuck typing this shit but any help from you would be much apreciated.  :-)'),(33679,'25117a50c0','Hey dude, thanks for doing that. And yeah, im suprised that the post was as well as it was. With you being hammered and all, well thanks. \r\n\r\nIE: http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6786&amp;start=30');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33643,'f6f14c309f','Yea, So silicanracer and mafia are the same person?  Who knew.  Thanks for the comment on my truck'),(35096,'0101704670','Almost forgot.. Can you add in an extra set of car rear dogbones to my order?\r\n\r\nXME039R ------$6.50--------21----35%----$4.23 (11/11 @ 9:45am)'),(37695,'c7a333053f','Holy smackers i got it today, looks sweet, i might run it for a while but hope you not offended if i give it a brigther orange color with some black stripers later on...Thanks a bunch man, hope your stuff comes i nsoon...'),(33651,'1c5889aec3','Yah man I would like them! I can send you a money order or Paypal just let me know what you would like! Regular shipping is cool and a padded envelope would be best just to add the added protection!\r\nthanks a ton man and no probs on the wait I was not in a big hurry!\r\n\r\nthanks agian \r\nOh address to get the total shipping\r\nAaron W. Olmsted\r\n1941 Sayers Road\r\nBastrop, TX 78602 \r\n\r\n :-)'),(33652,'2b66323d00','I have 3 requests:\r\n\r\nI need to know if you have anymore of those resin lights etc and can have a set? What\'s the price?\r\n\r\nHow do you make those crash bars that you have on your micros?\r\n\r\nYour articulation mod seems easily done, cuz you have alot. How do you do it so easy? I\'ve seen the diets thread on the german site Can I have a quick walkthrough? No pictures needed. Just a quick tut.\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35699,'a4cd8d324d','[quote:a4cd8d324d=\"MafiaS\"]Your WRX in the videos you have shown in your thread...is that a GEN1 xmod? \r\n\r\nI wanted to know this because I just purchased my first Xmod, and it is a Gen1, and I wanted to know what I should do for upgrades, how I could possible make it faster, or where I could get lighter, perhaps faster hop up parts. Could you let me know please.\r\n\r\nKick ass vid by the way man![/quote:a4cd8d324d]Thanx man\r\n\r\nAnd yes it\'s a Gen1. It\'s the last Gen1. My car isn\'t the fastest, it can be faster but I like it. \r\n\r\nHere is my setup:\r\n\r\nShimmed blue motor/white bevel \r\nAWD \r\nWide/RS bearings \r\nBent tierod, \r\nsteering slop removed with Bic pen ink tube (makes tierod wider, tighter turns) \r\nHard springs all round \r\nStage 2 motor advanced \r\nNeo magnets \r\nRear LSD (tight)\r\n\r\nThese pics show how to combine the blue stage 2 motor with the stock bevel gear. This gives the blue motor great acceleration and keeps it\'s top speed almost the same.\r\n\r\n[img:a4cd8d324d]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10097/IMG_0743.JPG[/img:a4cd8d324d]\r\n\r\nAbove shows where to put the stock yellow bushing in order for the pinion and bevel gear to work. You shim ONLY that side and not both.\r\n\r\n[img:a4cd8d324d]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10097/IMG_0744.JPG[/img:a4cd8d324d]\r\n\r\nThis is a VERY fun car just using RS upgrades. You can check eBay for aftermarket upgrades. Or www.customxmodsparts.com they have lots. Like CF driveshafts, Li-ion (i\'m never buying those again). Also you can get cosmetic upgrades. Check them out. If you want speed check ph2t, his nelly turbo is a must have for speed deamons (that covers FETs), he also has li-ion and li-poly batteries that are great to use.\r\n\r\nLi-ions make your car wicked fast but you can burn the FETs. So if you have the nelly turbo you will have no problems.\r\n\r\nI guess I can ramble on, so ask more specific questions and I\'ll help you out.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(35117,'20989ce43c','you seriously need a place to host a .gif? I can help you out.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33657,'0ca4bfdaf1','Sup dude, sorry for the slow reply, lately I\'ve been as busy as the proverbial one-legged man in an ass-kicking contest.\r\n\r\nSweet score on the chargers, but the PIC16C56 is one-time programmable unfortunately.  There are some variations on the 56 chip, you can see them here:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.microchip.com/ParamChartSearch/chart.aspx?branchID=1002&amp;mid=10&amp;lang=en&amp;pageId=74\r\n\r\nBut if its a regular 16C56 it probably won\'t do you much good.\r\n\r\nI\'m checking out HV Community now, just wish I had more time to spend on all these cool projects, there simply aren\'t enough hours in the day!'),(36215,'6ef4bab9ec','Will do. :-)'),(33660,'cd48e621c4','[quote:cd48e621c4=\"arfin\"]Hey i sent the set yesterday, and some LED\'s in case you ever need them. PM me when you get them please  :-o[/quote:cd48e621c4]\r\n\r\nGot\'em today.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nSG :-)'),(33763,'cf81c414c6','would this work?\r\n\r\nI am thinking about buying an x-mod evo soon when they are released. I will probably buy the turbo*bug* with a plasma-atomic moter setup that i wil be build based from your tutorial.\r\n\r\n\r\nI reailized things like the fact that the bug is *meant* for the Epoch Indoor Racer.\r\n\r\nso all-in-all would this work?      \r\n\r\n (only asking [color=blue:cf81c414c6]*not to bug you*[/color:cf81c414c6] because you are the creator of this set up and i dont wanna\' risk blowing mony on a setup that wont work)\r\n\r\nThanks alot,\r\n\r\npimptothemax');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33765,'7d0f5ae480','shaun\'s in chat man!!!!!!! I\'m there.....'),(34221,'b27cbc6846','[quote:b27cbc6846=\"arfin\"]MG WHERE YOU BEEN HOMIE, lol i been on msn for a while looking for you.![/quote:b27cbc6846]\r\n\r\nHey dude!!\r\n\r\nJust workin\', had to work this weekend, and now i just got up. :) Late night.'),(33767,'00031c8147','Hey, wassup dude? \r\n\r\nLooks like yer having a little trouble here. \r\nBut no biggie, it should pass.\r\nThe best thing to do is to join in BitPimps Chat. You really can get to know the guys here quick, and grammer isn\'t a high priority in chat.\r\nThe button is at the top of your forum screen.\r\nI\'ve met lots of cool people there!!\r\nEverybody seems more \'laid-back\' in chat.\r\n\r\nSee ya there!!!\r\n\r\nMotorGong'),(33768,'ee784de7b4','Hey, wassup dude? \r\n\r\nLooks like yer having a little trouble here. \r\nBut no biggie, it should pass.\r\nThe best thing to do is to join in BitPimps Chat. You really can get to know the guys here quick, and grammer isn\'t a high priority in chat.\r\nThe button is at the top of your forum screen.\r\nI\'ve met lots of cool people there!!\r\nEverybody seems more \'laid-back\' in chat.\r\n\r\nSee ya there!!!\r\n\r\nMotorGong'),(34612,'c4e776f520','[quote:c4e776f520=\"arfin\"]Shit, you must be busy, haven\'t seen you in a while. LMAO at the vader thing, i was thinking pussy, and he guessed \"sex thing\" ![/quote:c4e776f520]\r\n\r\nLOL, yeah.\r\n\r\nYeah man, just plain ass busy catching up with some bills and stuff. This \'real\' job stuff sucks. LOL\r\n\r\nI havn\'t even sent your package yet, but will probably Wednesday.\r\n\r\n--Dave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33772,'d8cc3af4c4','Hey thanks.  How long u been a member here?'),(33776,'771af6c033','[quote:771af6c033=\"arfin\"]Yo watup MG! You goin on msn?  :cool:[/quote:771af6c033]\r\n\r\nNo, but now I will .LOL\r\n\r\nSee ya there in 10 min'),(33779,'095bde7686','K, thanks man, whats ur name? im josh.'),(33784,'a1bb8c84b0','Hey what up? I have a quick question, where did you get the tires for your MT?  The street looking tires, they look pretty badass.  Peace'),(33787,'9355c06287','nothing personal, just didn\'t want my thread to turn in to a noob beatdown. :cool:'),(33792,'a8e1f4b325','I have one Microsizer front end that I can send you, I will not remove the coils from the steering box.\r\n\r\nYes there is kite sailing/surfing in Barbados. It\'s great here, good for normal surfing too. White sand beaches etc. Google us and you\'ll see what we have to offer.\r\n\r\nGive me your mailing address so I can send out the stuff.'),(33801,'5e80cbc800','GREAT, do you wind/kite surf too? I do it a lot here in the Netherlands. A lot colder but the wind can be good sometimes. \r\n\r\nMy adress is:\r\n\r\nName: Joris de Iongh\r\nStreet: Cipreslaan 48\r\nZipcode: 3053nd\r\nCity: Rotterdam\r\nCountry: the Netherlands.\r\n\r\nIf you have other scrap parts lying around tell me, I might be interested in old batteries axles gears old wheels models etc.\r\n\r\naloha Joris');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33802,'5051f4b25c','Great, I\'ll keep an eye out for it!\r\nI\'ll let you know when it arrives.'),(33803,'a1bb8c84b0','Hey what up? I have a quick question, where did you get the tires for your MT?  The street looking tires, they look pretty badass.  Peace'),(33909,'882007c672','Hey man, I just deleted your post in the \"help!!!!!\" thread \'cuz it pissed me off and there\'s no need to add more chaos to the site right now... I could have gone off on ya in the locked thread, but I thought I\'d share my thinking in a PM instead... because I feel like being a nice guy.\r\n\r\nSo, let me get this straight... you\'re pissed at me because we were saying the same thing, which is why you called me a hypocrite?\r\n\r\nFor the record, bitch, we\'re not saying the same thing at all... I\'m doing my job, and you\'re outta fuckin\' line. Get it? The reason I get to set a noob straight (any fucking way I please, I might add) is because I\'m a fucking moderator here... you, last I checked, are not. So, especially when a thread is already a god-damned cluster fuck, the last thing we need is some little fuck (you), who\'s barely outta the noob stage himself, telling other noobs what\'s what... that\'s the moderators\' job and we sure as fuck don\'t need help from you... it just ain\'t your place, so stay the fuck out of it. In fact, that\'s the shit that\'s pissing us off more than just about anything else these days, and it just ain\'t gonna be tolerated anymore. So when I, or any other moderator here, shuts you down for steppin\' outta line, you\'d better show some respect or shut the fuck up. You\'ve been just fine for quite awhile (and we\'re glad to have ya... seriously), so don\'t fuck yourself over now. So, next time you wanna step in my face when I\'m doing my job, I\'ll call ya out in the forums, and I\'ll have all the other moderators behind me... your welcome will be expired, and it\'ll be a painful exit.\r\n\r\nhue35'),(33809,'98948133bb','Ghat gear and motor set up would work best for climbing hills with my zip zap monster truck.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33826,'e720bbdd96','[quote:e720bbdd96=\"Sporttracguy\"]Right on man, THanks\r\n\r\nRyan Eylander\r\n7701 Delridge Wasy SW apt 9A\r\nSeattle, WA 98106\r\n\r\nThanks again,\r\n\r\nRyan[/quote:e720bbdd96]\r\nJust so I make sure I got this correct, is that supposed to be \"Delridge Way\"?'),(33829,'7e8fbcdfe7','I love your work on the Baja.  In fact, I love it so much I can\'t stand to think that you\'ve got two cells, a SS motor and no fets.  I\'m tellin you, that car needs fets!  If you want, I can put them in for you.  You just gotta get it to me.  I\'ll put the fets in for free and mail it back out to you.  I\'m good with fets.\r\n\r\nYou see, the fets will give you a massive jump in torque.  You can throw on 3:1 K.I.T. gears and turn all that extra torque into speed.  For that car, I might recomend 4:1 K.I.T. gears.  It would keep some of the torque and still make it fast as hell.  I\'d have to see how much it weighs to recomend the perfect gearing.  \r\n\r\nAnyways, I have a ton of K.I.T. gears.  I can mail those back with the car.  I would rather you put them on.  Mechanical stuff seems to be your specialty.  I can do it, but it looks like you could do it better.  But as far as the fets go, that\'s easy for me.\r\n\r\nAnyhow, if you want to send it out, I\'m at;\r\nBob Wilson\r\n1230 North Tomcat Court\r\nVirginia Beach, VA\r\n23454\r\n\r\nAs long as it\'s still a regular Tomy Microsizer/BitCharge PCB I don\'t need the controller.  Just the car.  I have a million controllers.'),(33830,'2f3263a8d2','[quote:2f3263a8d2=\"hue35\"]\r\nSo, let me get this straight... if you did the duty-cycle mod to a Chevelle-era SE and to a new Vette SE, the 2 would be about the same? So, if I were to install code\'s deal, the older chassis would be the one to do, \'cuz it would realize more of the SE\'s power potential than even the new Vette chassis... and fix any steering issues as a bonus. These new vette chassis kick ass right outta the box... I\'m into seeing if they can get better, but I\'ll probably only mod one of \'em... eventually... maybe. I think, if I was anywhere close to on track above, I\'m gonna order up the duty-cycle deal from code soon.[/quote:2f3263a8d2]Yep, I think you got it. Since I haven\'t tried one in the Vette, I can\'t say for sure, but in theory, it should be exactly the same, since the only difference in performance between the Vette and GTO is the GTO\'s crappy duty cycle. There\'s no guarantee on the steering. It helped mine, Code says that happens sometime, he don\'t know why.\r\n\r\nI know I have to order another, because my old SE without it is useless now. :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:2f3263a8d2=\"crazydave\"][quote:2f3263a8d2]I\'m gonna try to take one of my old, broken SE\'s back today, dressed up in the Vette\'s shell and packaging, to try and get another of these chassis... I figure they owe it to me. The first one shouldn\'t have sucked, ya know? I\'ll let ya know how that went. [/quote:2f3263a8d2]Yeah, let me know how that goes. :-o[/quote:2f3263a8d2]\r\nIt worked... twice. And, I got to keep the old car both times... \"hey, since you\'re gonna throw it away anyway, can I just keep it for parts?\"   :-o [/quote]That\'s cool. I\'m jealous, I wish I had the balls to try it. What did you tell them was wrong with it?\r\n\r\n[quote:2f3263a8d2]Also, I bought a couple more ZZMTs... $19 for 2 is a great deal for that toy. I love them as is, but I just set one of them on a shelf, right next my OG iWaiver... that will be a fun project.[/quote:2f3263a8d2]I know I should be cashing in on that, need an extra MT to mod, but they pissed me off that day with that $2.50 shit and when I went back the clearance cars were gone. Still gotta check the one in the mall, but it hasn\'t been a priorty. I really want a proportional MT, but I don\'t know, I get all excited about gassers and stuff, then I\'m off in another direction.\r\n\r\n\r\nSuper Furry Animals kinda grew on me. Really dig the song \"Ohio Heat\".\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33831,'044ad17f7e','i used a 40 watt solder iron.  make sure to clean the areas you are going to solder with steel wool or sandpaper and use flux.  makes a huge difference as to how easy it goes togther.'),(33832,'b36d32d62f','Will do, thanks man.'),(34532,'eaff4c680f','[quote:eaff4c680f=\"Nasphere\"]Yeah, I hear you on that one. (just enough to get into trouble)\r\n\r\nI found out that when I\'m a little more daring, like going up fast, jet it foreward, I seem to do a LOT better, but then when I go in for a slow landing, I crash... lol, I\'m getting enough air time in now so i should get pretty good soon. It\'s just really difficult to rotate a 90 and keep it straight...\r\n\r\nGot more questions:\r\nWhat model of heli are you flying in the video you made?\r\nHow long are the run/charge times?[/quote:eaff4c680f]\r\nThat was my old room-mate flying in the video, I was filming.\r\nIf I remember correctly, it was the E-flite.\r\nhttp://h1070250.hobbyshopnow.com/products/description.asp?prod=EFLH1100\r\n\r\nTypically, landing and hovering are the 2 things you would want to practice most. It requires the most control.\r\n\r\nRun and charge times vary on what model you have.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if you ever saw this or not, but this is some serious control:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/displayimage.php?album=16&amp;pos=28\r\n\r\nEvery now and then some dudes will come up to the hobby shop and put on a demo doing exactly what you see in that video, it\'s amazing.'),(33834,'b36d32d62f','Will do, thanks man.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35051,'5665bbca0e','Thanks alot...The reason I am asking is because I love the upgrades and price of Xmods, but I hear the racing quality is better on a Iwaver and Mini Z, this attracts me because we are building a track in the basement and i wanted something very competitive...\r\n\r\nI thought about it, if i found a great deal on an Xmod EVO, or someone sold me a good Original xmod i would take it, customize it and make it a good competitor. But I am probably going to buy 4. 1 EVO, 1 Original, 1 Iwaver, and 1 MiniZ because with the track set up I would like different cars to compete with. Considering many of my friends are into it now, and my uncle especially. We dedicate at least 1 day a \"hop up RC day\" so this could get very edgy in the competition.\r\n\r\nThanks for your time man!'),(33849,'b87151f6ab','I would love a dead/stipped chassis with coils in it :D'),(33850,'e9104a01b1','Well then maybe we can work out a trade.'),(33851,'afa204effc','Well then maybe we can work out a trade. Maybe a ZZ body or something. Currently looking for KT\'s FD RX7, the yellow one.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (33860,'452d8e2819','how was the wedding? hope ya had fun!!!!!!!!!!!!!!'),(34182,'08d90dbf75','Hi sessiz, thanks for the compliment.\r\n\r\nIf you dont mind me asking, where upstate are you? i\'m currently in Delmar.\r\n\r\nHappen to know any good hobby shops around here?  Was down in the poughkeepsie/fishkill area for a few years and then just recently moved up here.'),(34183,'5a2dae96bb','I\'m actually in albany and unfortuantly there\'s not much in the line of hobby shops round here man. There\'s a hobbytown on central ave in the old builders square plaza. Hobbytown are a bunch of rapists though. There\'s a mini z track/hobby shop in clifton country mall and there\'s a lil shop that caters to mainly nitro buggys on 9w.\r\nI noticed the albany NY and was almost floored that there\'s someone else round here thats into the micro rc. In The nearly 4 years I\'ve been into this shit you\'re the second guy I\'ve come across.\r\nYou\'ve done one hell of a job on that crawler man, inspiring. :-)'),(35657,'0795cc3cd0','No problem.  I\'m assuming you were looking at my AE86.  That\'s just plastic packaging that I got off of something I bought in a store.  I used 5 Minute apoxy to glue it on.  The rest of it is a wing from a celica and tamiya epoxy putty.\r\n\r\n[img:0795cc3cd0]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10049/18.JPG[/img:0795cc3cd0]\r\n\r\nThe fog lights are small shiny nails that I cut down with my dremel and the grill is from a facet filter.\r\n\r\nBasically, I keep my eyes out all the time for possible aplications, but I also get tons of ideas from here too.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34259,'fe0e678c05','whoa dude. stay safe.'),(34260,'596d2a7513','[quote:596d2a7513=\"Clint\"]whoa dude. stay safe.[/quote:596d2a7513]\r\n\r\nThanks man, hopefully it will let up.'),(34206,'710fde78d1','[quote:710fde78d1=\"MotorGong\"]Hey, thanks again for hookin\' me/us up with this guy!\r\nHis site is pretty cool, I\'m sure you know about it already.\r\n\r\n[url]http://customcarperformance.com/dks2005/dks2005.htm[/url]\r\n\r\nI am hyped up about purchasing those motors. Even the lower RPM ones.\r\nHave you run these motors yourself, and are there any you [i:710fde78d1]don\'t [/i:710fde78d1]recommend?\r\n\r\n-Dave[/quote:710fde78d1]\r\n\r\nSup MG, I only got a couple of the DarkSide Motors from him, haven\'t used them yet. Don\'t know about the other motors but they all have a great reputation. Choose what you\'re looking for and I\'m sure you won\'t be disappointed..\r\nI did buy [i:710fde78d1]Extreme Motors[/i:710fde78d1] remaining lot of motors &amp; batteries. (1st &amp; 2nd editions)These are \"Extremely\" good motors, the only one I\'ve run so far from that lots is the \"1.6 Circuit Rotor\".  Great for track running!  :-o \r\nI have so much shit hoarded, it\'s unbelievable  :shock: \r\nHe was giving us Pimps a really good deal on his clearance when I first contacted him.  A few Pimps contacted him and got great deals, I think better than he\'s offering now.  Good Luck !'),(34249,'b29ff16ec6','[quote:b29ff16ec6=\"Tuner1989\"]Wow, your zzmt is looking really good, Why have you stayed away from pimps all these months lol. did you get a body mounted on the other zzmt you were working on?\r\n[/quote:b29ff16ec6]\r\n\r\nHi Matt.\r\nhaha, member since July 2003 and no posts. lol\r\nI got caught up in xmodworld. ugh. \r\n\r\nBeen busy at work, so I havent had a chance to work on a body. It needs\r\nsomething \"special\". \r\n\r\n[quote:b29ff16ec6=\"Tuner1989\"]\r\nYouve defietley got some skills lbrc has some competition.\r\n[/quote:b29ff16ec6]\r\n\r\nwow. thx, lol. LBRC and Diets are true pimps.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:b29ff16ec6=\"Tuner1989\"]\r\nOh and did you get a chance to ship those ex. chassis out.\r\n---Matt[/quote:b29ff16ec6]\r\n\r\nyup, I found a 3rd chassis i did, so i shipped you all 3. Threw them in an envelope with some bubble wrap, nothing fancy. if you can do anything with them i\'d be impressed!\r\n\r\nWhen i do make a fully working chassis, I\'ll send u one of those as well.\r\n\r\nlater,\r\nClint');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34250,'af9a743ede','[quote:af9a743ede=\"Clint\"][quote:af9a743ede=\"Tuner1989\"]Wow, your zzmt is looking really good, Why have you stayed away from pimps all these months lol. did you get a body mounted on the other zzmt you were working on?\r\n[/quote:af9a743ede]\r\n\r\nHi Matt.\r\nhaha, member since July 2003 and no posts. lol\r\nI got caught up in xmodworld. ugh. \r\n\r\nBeen busy at work, so I havent had a chance to work on a body. It needs\r\nsomething \"special\". \r\n\r\n[quote:af9a743ede=\"Tuner1989\"]\r\nYouve defietley got some skills lbrc has some competition.\r\n[/quote:af9a743ede]\r\n\r\nwow. thx, lol. LBRC and Diets are true pimps.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:af9a743ede=\"Tuner1989\"]\r\nOh and did you get a chance to ship those ex. chassis out.\r\n---Matt[/quote:af9a743ede]\r\n\r\nyup, I found a 3rd chassis i did, so i shipped you all 3. Threw them in an envelope with some bubble wrap, nothing fancy. if you can do anything with them i\'d be impressed!\r\n\r\nWhen i do make a fully working chassis, I\'ll send u one of those as well.\r\n\r\nlater,\r\nClint[/quote:af9a743ede]\r\n\r\n2003  :-?   lol\r\nYeah xmodworld has gone down the drain, overrun with way too many newbs and online argumenters.\r\n\r\nWow thanks man That would be awesome when you make a full working one. Much appreciated. I\'m hoping I can start to get the feel for how my setup will be with the electrics i have on a pan type chassis. And get the hs-55 all setup.\r\n\r\nJust looked at the news Hurricane wilma is a category five :shock: \r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37673,'45a7f69d4b','I picked up my gandinis from Ausmicro.  I didn\'t do a tremendous amount of looking, so you might find them somewhere else.  I also went ahead and got the other parts from them as well since I was already getting like $45 worth of tires at the time.  But, if you let him know that you\'re a regular at Bit-Pimps he\'ll throw in extra stuff.  I probably got an extra $30 of extras that he just threw in with the order.  Don\'t know if he\'ll do that every time but he may.  It also might help if you tell him I sent you.  Tell him you know me by name &quot;Bob Wilson&quot; as well as my username.  The other sources I\'ve been using are Toyeast, Hobby link Japan and RCMart.  All of those are in Asia, so you\'ll be spending a little extra on the shipping.  \r\n\r\nThis place seemed pretty cool.  I used him once.  Good dealer and decent prices. [url]http://www.microracers24.com/en-us/button.html[/url]  He ships quickly too.  It looks like an overseas site, but he has a distributor in the States.\r\n\r\nIf you find Gandinis somewhere else for much cheaper let me know.\r\n\r\nAs far as the Iwaver ball diff, you shouldn\'t be spending any more than $20 for one.  If they have it for a good price and you\'re OK with the shipping, then I say go for it.  You may want to reference the &quot;Vouch for a pimp, or throw him under the bus&quot; section of this forum in the contests/polls/surveys area.   [url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewforum.php?f=27[/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36402,'474f689168','Long gone mate :)\r\n\r\nBut trust me there\'ll be a surprise heading your way sooner or later ;)\r\n\r\nA.'),(34578,'25956bbdb2','damn sessiz made me say that he like breaks into my acount and shit.\r\nHe can go fuck his mom.'),(34579,'acec11b388','LOL hey dude it\'s all fun and games. Just don\'t take the crap to heart and try to get back into everyones good graces and it will be ok. We just like to weed out the weak links here. The main thing here is about the hobby. It\'s not for beginners here but if you are just read the useful stuff and then try to be creative. Other wise you shouldn\'t post. After you have a little street cred the older members will lighten up and make you apart of the click. Thats all I can say man, just don\'t take it to heart and go around blasting them. sessiz is a moderator and has the ability to change posts. He isn\'t hacking anything. Just don\'t give him a reason to fuck with you.'),(34580,'e54f06ce8d','Hey Sat,\r\n\r\nYou probably don\'t notice me much on the forums, because i haven\'t posted a big project yet, but i just wanted to send you a message to let you know i care! If you need any R/C related shit, (especially epoch) since that is my main R/C don\'t hesitate to ask!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36372,'72c8009467','I will look in a couple of RS\'s tomarrow.  I\'m off work and be going past a couple.  \r\n\r\n :-o'),(37027,'554f4e4bdf','o i thought you were selling it'),(34623,'272f2690d6','[quote:272f2690d6=\"arfin\"]Hey, long time no see, man i\'m so excited this week, seen those new Microz topic? They look amazing, AND THEY ARE IN CANADA! Also my Metl-tech racer is comin\' in this week, BUT i\'m kinda pissed about that because TeamBonzer, in his review posted about how good it was, THEN all of a sudden tells me it lags, LIKE WTF![/quote:272f2690d6]\r\n\r\nDid you get this METL TECH yet?'),(34587,'c4e776f520','[quote:c4e776f520=\"arfin\"]Shit, you must be busy, haven\'t seen you in a while. LMAO at the vader thing, i was thinking pussy, and he guessed \"sex thing\" ![/quote:c4e776f520]\r\n\r\nLOL, yeah.\r\n\r\nYeah man, just plain ass busy catching up with some bills and stuff. This \'real\' job stuff sucks. LOL\r\n\r\nI havn\'t even sent your package yet, but will probably Wednesday.\r\n\r\n--Dave'),(35931,'e6b96444e8','If you can, let me know when your going to post. That way all the winners can go up at one time.\r\n\r\nI sorta would like to pick someone that doesn\'t place. \r\n\r\nProbably Hiroto\'s ride. :???: \r\n\r\n\r\nLater');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34596,'1b2cbe8a90','[quote:1b2cbe8a90=\"Nasphere\"]hey man, could you hook me up with 16 N-MOSFETs and 3 of your DC mod boards? How much would all this cost?\r\n[/quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\n\r\nHey, sorry its taken so long to get back to you, I\'ve been on vacation and away from the computer.  Just had some free time to check email and whatnot.\r\n\r\nDC mod boards are $10 each and the mosfets are about 40 cents each, so about $38 shipped.  Thats assuming I\'ve got that many FETs on hand, I haven\'t counted recently, but I\'m pretty sure I\'ve got them if you still need \'em.\r\n\r\n[quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\nI measured the motor outputs, and would like to know what these change to after the DC mod.\r\n\r\noper. freq.\r\n103.5hz\r\n[/quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\n\r\nIn the current version of the DC mod, the frequency is unchanged.  Version 2 bumps the frequency up to several kilohertz, so its more like a hobby ESC.  Version 2 is in early prototype stage though, I haven\'t been able to put it all together yet.\r\n\r\n[quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\nduty cycles (reverse to foreward)\r\n-44.5\r\n-38.3\r\n-32.2\r\n-26.5\r\n0\r\n26.5\r\n32.2\r\n38.3\r\n44.5\r\n53.9\r\n60.5\r\n\r\nAlso, with your DC mod, it only works for the foreward, correct?[/quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\n\r\nYep, forward only.  Thats another feature I\'m hoping I might be able to put into version 2, remapping of some of the reverse steps into forward steps so that there is more control of the extra power.  Again, still on the drawing board.\r\n\r\nThe actual rates on the forward duty cycles I\'d have to go look up the conversion table in the sourcecode, which I don\'t have handy.  From memory its something like 15, 25, 38, 50, 75, 100.  I pushed it down a little at the bottom end, and way up at the top end.  If you want to specify your own mapping its no trouble to drop the new values into the table and recompile.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be back in town until next week, but after that I can set up the boards for you.\r\n\r\ncs'),(35577,'b5e5377012','Hey llama,\r\n\r\nI got a question about your 180mAh batts.  I\'m assuming that they\'re Kan\'s from a flight pack.  How long are they?  I\'m also assuming that they\'re the same width as the standard bit batts.  I just need to know the length since I may try to jam them into an epoch.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nChris');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34615,'1b2cbe8a90','[quote:1b2cbe8a90=\"Nasphere\"]hey man, could you hook me up with 16 N-MOSFETs and 3 of your DC mod boards? How much would all this cost?\r\n[/quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\n\r\nHey, sorry its taken so long to get back to you, I\'ve been on vacation and away from the computer.  Just had some free time to check email and whatnot.\r\n\r\nDC mod boards are $10 each and the mosfets are about 40 cents each, so about $38 shipped.  Thats assuming I\'ve got that many FETs on hand, I haven\'t counted recently, but I\'m pretty sure I\'ve got them if you still need \'em.\r\n\r\n[quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\nI measured the motor outputs, and would like to know what these change to after the DC mod.\r\n\r\noper. freq.\r\n103.5hz\r\n[/quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\n\r\nIn the current version of the DC mod, the frequency is unchanged.  Version 2 bumps the frequency up to several kilohertz, so its more like a hobby ESC.  Version 2 is in early prototype stage though, I haven\'t been able to put it all together yet.\r\n\r\n[quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\nduty cycles (reverse to foreward)\r\n-44.5\r\n-38.3\r\n-32.2\r\n-26.5\r\n0\r\n26.5\r\n32.2\r\n38.3\r\n44.5\r\n53.9\r\n60.5\r\n\r\nAlso, with your DC mod, it only works for the foreward, correct?[/quote:1b2cbe8a90]\r\n\r\nYep, forward only.  Thats another feature I\'m hoping I might be able to put into version 2, remapping of some of the reverse steps into forward steps so that there is more control of the extra power.  Again, still on the drawing board.\r\n\r\nThe actual rates on the forward duty cycles I\'d have to go look up the conversion table in the sourcecode, which I don\'t have handy.  From memory its something like 15, 25, 38, 50, 75, 100.  I pushed it down a little at the bottom end, and way up at the top end.  If you want to specify your own mapping its no trouble to drop the new values into the table and recompile.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be back in town until next week, but after that I can set up the boards for you.\r\n\r\ncs'),(34616,'a2f307dee5','[quote:a2f307dee5=\"codesuidae\"]If you want to specify your own mapping its no trouble to drop the new values into the table and recompile.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be back in town until next week, but after that I can set up the boards for you.\r\n\r\ncs[/quote:a2f307dee5]\r\n\r\nI like your duty cycle numbers, those would work. But $10 is quite a bit... Maybe I\'ll have to settle on 1 or 2 boards. But it\'s cool, hold the rush, I\'m in no hurry.\r\n\r\nAbout the frequency change. I would say, make it a little lower, unless you plan to include a MOSFET driver for the FET modded cars. The FETs without a driver should run ok at &lt;1khz, but for the higher numbers a MOSFET driver would be optimal. Unless you have some secret plan in the works.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34618,'88ce5c11f6','Hey Dude,    \r\n                I need your fully address to some Sammy a B-Day card. 16 Crystal Lake Drive Saint Peters MO 63 ?'),(34622,'02456631a2','[quote:02456631a2=\"arfin\"]Whaaaa? A package? For me? LOL, it\'s funny because today i found all the parts for the Epoch i was gonna send you! Luckily i had a few new parts that i needed, i just spent 1 hour sanding the baby down, because it had previous solder burns on the side, and i did my best to make her look good again.\r\n\r\nCan\'t wait to finish her up! Yo, sucks what happened to Sat4ife though, but i think i got him to think i want to give/sell him an epoch! This is what was said, maybe you can help explain:\r\n\r\n\"... if you need any help with r/c related shit especially epoch (my main r/c) don\'t hesitate to ask\"\r\n\r\n\"... yeah i\'ll hit you up on an epoch here soon\" The ... represent the quote i left out, but what does that sound like to you?[/quote:02456631a2]\r\n\r\n\r\nhmmm, maybe he\'s saying he wants to buy one from ya. Maybe not FROM you but perhaps you give him a connection to get one. Or maybe it was a typo on his part. :???: idk\r\n\r\n\r\nCOOL!!!! right on man!!! I\'m glad you found the shizz!!!! \r\nI almost got your package all together!!\r\nI need to know what kind of bodies/cars do you like again? Or are you like me, and its whatever! :)\r\n\r\nYou said you have a 35mhz car and controller?\r\n\r\nI do remember the charging port thing you need.\r\n\r\nI\'m off today, so perhaps we\'ll talk.\r\n\r\n--Dave'),(36408,'7f5339ce00','No, but it will definately ship tomorrow. Everything is rounded up and ready to go.  :-o \r\n\r\nHot damn,\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37699,'1bb99ee956','sounds good to me\r\n\r\nthe stuff is yours i am just hookin up with my uncle right now to get the go ahead for you pimps to send the money to his paypal because i dont have my own.\r\n\r\nWhen he gets back to me i will post up the pm right away...\r\n\r\ncool?'),(37190,'16bb2827eb','Well I like my Iwaver real well! I had an older Mini-Z and I think that I like my IWaver much more! Its on the workbench right now as I am trying to build that Back to the Future body for it!  :grin:'),(37187,'1aa594a3e6','[quote:1aa594a3e6=\"LBRC\"]Just curious, hows the Epoch doing?  Any problems?  What would you change? That sort of thing.\r\n\r\nCheers\r\nPhilip.[/quote:1aa594a3e6]\r\n\r\nHey man Sorry I did not reply right away! \r\n\r\nI really like this car I have been having a lot of fun with it, I almost beat my nephew\'s X-mod he had upgraded it to a 6 cell and its fast but the Epoch was right there with it the whole way.\r\n\r\nThe big thing is you were right you have to weigh down the back we actualy took the cars to a nice skatboard park all concreat and lots of places to run the cars in fact a cool straitaway. The Epoch outferfomed the X-Mod hands down but for all out speed he had me. But for me I would rather have better handling then speed. You could have the fastest RC car in the world but if you cant turn it all you have is a fast drag car!\r\n\r\nThe stearing motor is much better then the standard Epoch motor more responsive. I think this car is a blast and have had a great time with it. I personly would not change a thing (well except the weight issue). I think putting a spring between the motor section and chassis would help keep the back a little tighter and I might not have to add any weight? the problem I am having is the back bounces to much it causes the back wheels to hit the wheel wells. I might try something to see if I can get it to work I will let you know! \r\n\r\n thanks again man!!  :-)'),(34625,'25bddbcc1c','[quote:25bddbcc1c=\"JdmHatchback\"][quote:25bddbcc1c=\"DarkTari\"]How much do you want for the Tomy Sets?  Shipping?\r\n\r\nIs that everything or do you have any Lxx sets left?\r\n\r\nI know someone looking for the WRX set\r\n\r\nLemme Know!\r\n\r\nThanx Again Pimp![/quote:25bddbcc1c]\r\n\r\n$15 each for the Tomy Sets.... Shipping for one set around $5 bucks priority mail with delivery confirmation. \r\n\r\nFor more sets etc... I gotta figure shipping depending on you what you would want etc... \r\n\r\nI may have a few Lxx sets left. I have the vw beetle sets with working lights. Also have the super perfection lambo/ferrari combo sets and maybe a few of the regular/auto modellista sets.\r\n\r\nThanks and let me know![/quote:25bddbcc1c]\r\n\r\nI want the following:\r\n2- Lxx VW Sets\r\n2- Lxx Super Sets: Ferrari/Lambo\r\n1- Tomy Gloria\r\n\r\nLet me know which Lxx AM sets you have, and bodies.\r\nThanx!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37371,'9a3e0d4d66','Yo Pimp!  You\'re our Admin, that\'s why I put &quot;Us Mods&quot; in quotes.  You have enough on your plate so we\'ll take care of it, those that step up that is .  I sure hope we don\'t have a lotta fuckin conflict with this.  I think it ran rather smuth last year and I don\'t want to fuck with the process......\r\nIf It Ain\'t Broke.... :???:'),(35343,'99312d8edb','[quote:99312d8edb=\"sat4life27\"]Wazzup!!\r\n\r\nYeah man, I just started working for RS a few weeks ago. I will try to find out about the display guide. My manager knows I am into the zaps would most likely hook me up with one if we have some laying around. I will see what I can do tomorrow when I get there.\r\n\r\nLater Pimp!!![/quote:99312d8edb]\r\n\r\n :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  Thanx !'),(35346,'dc07b6e933','[color=red:dc07b6e933][size=18:dc07b6e933][b:dc07b6e933]For Your Eys Only[/b:dc07b6e933][/size:dc07b6e933][/color:dc07b6e933]\r\n[size=9:dc07b6e933]My cell number is 931-607-0548[/size:dc07b6e933]\r\n[color=red:dc07b6e933][size=18:dc07b6e933][b:dc07b6e933]For Your Eys Only[/b:dc07b6e933][/size:dc07b6e933][/color:dc07b6e933]'),(34627,'c33240b5c4','Hey DT, I have a chevelle body if you want her. I started to widen the wheelwells and removed all the lights and crap. I was gonna slam it down. I know you will do her justice so let me know if you want.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34929,'8695c0d6b4','Hey  SWG,\r\n\r\nIt will be a month or so since Im waiting for gears and my turn at a motor production run then shipping from China via HK (only way I could afford them). But Im making up several aluminum mounts in advance, also working on a solder-less motor connector for the aluminum mount so that the motors can be swapped out.\r\n\r\nAny way so how many bodies would you be willing to paint for a turbo chassis with Kan 180 replaceable battery and a BB aluminum motor mount, of course youd have to post and honest review, whether you liked it or hated it.  BTW do you have a lithium charger.'),(34641,'71b181c82f','[quote:71b181c82f=\"arfin\"]OMG NO! it\'s such a buz kill, i come home expecting it to be there, AND NO! It better be here tomorrow, and it better be worth it! Btw, maybe you should wait till i finish the epoch before you send out the package, because it\'s not really fair for you. It\'s up to you. It\'s gonna be cool for both of us to get something new![/quote:71b181c82f]\r\n\r\nAhhh shit mang, no worries. I think it\'s all fair and whatnot.\r\n\r\nNo \'trade\' here involved, really. I just have a bunch of Bit stuff, and this stuff is kinda rare where you live.\r\n\r\nAnd, I think you\'ll like these \'toynk\' 3.8 motors, I\'ll have to send one of those to you also!\r\n\r\n--Dave'),(34645,'e4f075bd91','[quote:e4f075bd91=\"arfin\"]Yeah no trade, just sending some shit to eachother  :-o , yeah man, this ain\'t gonna be no stock epoch either ;) :D[/quote:e4f075bd91]\r\n\r\nKILLER!!!!! Do you have time for messenger?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37245,'6ed29b6dc8','[quote:6ed29b6dc8=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Hey DT, I need some stuff from Radioshack. If you\'re up to it of course.\r\n\r\nAll from Radioshack, all in-store only:\r\n\r\n[b:6ed29b6dc8]XMODS® Custom RC Command Logic Lights[/b:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n[img:6ed29b6dc8]http://rsk.imageg.net/graphics/product_images/pRS1C-2266576t98.jpg[/img:6ed29b6dc8] I want 4 of these.  $5.99 each  [b:6ed29b6dc8]60-8509[/b:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n\r\n[b:6ed29b6dc8]XMODS® Custom RC Body Kit for Silver Toyota® SUPRA® [/b:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n[img:6ed29b6dc8]http://rsk.imageg.net/graphics/product_images/pRS1C-2160618t98.jpg[/img:6ed29b6dc8] one of these. $9.97 each  [b:6ed29b6dc8]60-8546[/b:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n\r\n[b:6ed29b6dc8]XMODS® Custom RC Body Kit for 2004 Ford® Mustang® [/b:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n[img:6ed29b6dc8]http://rsk.imageg.net/graphics/product_images/pRS1C-2265436t98.jpg[/img:6ed29b6dc8] one of these $9.97 each  [b:6ed29b6dc8]60-8535[/b:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n\r\nThat stuff and all the returned Xmod EVO cars you can get for free or $10  bucks(or less).\r\n\r\nJust tell me how much it all came to and what you got and I\'ll paypal you the cash  :-o \r\n\r\nMaxx[/quote:6ed29b6dc8]\r\n\r\nStopped by today, they do have the lights! None of the body kits you wanted, they did have the Supra in red, Red 68 Camaro, Copper Nissan Z, Blue 68 Mustang  &amp; Silver Vettefor $6.95.  I\'ll check out another one tomorrow!'),(36860,'3cf51e2a85','Sick...keep me posted');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34667,'8c71410a0d','I\'ll lend you my smile if you promise to only use him here and on my site.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.cjshobbies.net/phpBB2/images/smiles/eek1.gif\r\n\r\n[img:8c71410a0d]http://www.cjshobbies.net/phpBB2/images/smiles/eek1.gif[/img:8c71410a0d]'),(34671,'8e61499a8b','[quote:8e61499a8b=\"SHAUN\"]your never on msn any more.[/quote:8e61499a8b]\r\n\r\nif you actually TALK while on MSN, I\'ll get on.'),(37606,'20b217baac','This is exactly why you won\'t see any &quot;hot topic&quot; debates on this forum about:\r\nGod\r\nAbortion\r\nMACs vs PCs\r\nPolitics\r\n\r\nLast warning.\r\nYou just can\'t seem to get it through that bible thumping thick skull can you?\r\nDo not PM me any more about politics.\r\nI\'m done discussing anything with you.'),(37619,'a19a9e1e1f','nah man, no need to pm.\r\n\r\ni\'m glad you pointed out my error, we\'re all about correct information here at bp\'s :-) \r\n\r\nkeep up the good work :-o'),(37728,'30e22b20a2','[quote:30e22b20a2=\"ph2t\"]not feeling paranoid or anything, lol, but could you do me a fave and wipe this thread?\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7370\r\n\r\nit would be mega kiss your arse appreciated, lol...\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:30e22b20a2]\r\nIt\'s dead. You can take off your foil hat now. :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36353,'6a8b140a3f','Hey, :-) \r\n\r\nSorry to take so long but sometimes time just runs away.  \r\n\r\nAnyway are you still interested, if so I have one with a motor combo that I think you would appreciate, the only bad thing is that when word gets out about how well the motor combo in it works Im going to owe some kid a MRCC an apology.   Do you have a particular body preference?  Let me know if you are and if the address is still correct and I can have it in the mail today.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nPhilip (LBRC)'),(34709,'82c6384b2f','Yeah Man, no problem\r\n\r\nWhatcha doing here next week?  Work related?\r\nLet me know your schedule next week.  My son has\r\nTae Kwon Do practice Mon, Wed, Thu and Jujisu on Wed.  \r\nso schedules pretty tight but I\'ll fitcha in there somewhere.\r\n\r\nHome: 301-464-9628\r\nCell:    301-802-7638\r\nWork:  703-305-7398\r\n\r\nHolla !  8-)'),(34731,'cf1d9098a8','[quote:cf1d9098a8=\"CaboWabo\"]Hey Clint,\r\n\r\nWould you mind if I duplicated your tutorial (http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6991) in our Articles section?\r\nFull credits to you of course.\r\n\r\nIf not, that\'s fine - no hard feelings (ya fucker lol)\r\nBut seriously, it\'s fine if you\'d rather not.\r\n\r\nLemme know.[/quote:cf1d9098a8]\r\n\r\n\r\nSure thing. Do what you need to do to.\r\nI also have full res pics of each one. Just remove the /thumb/ directory from each url to access them. The smaller pics seemed clear enough, \r\nso I didnt bother linking.'),(34732,'04d355f56e','[quote:04d355f56e=\"Clint\"]Sure thing. Do what you need to do to.\r\nI also have full res pics of each one. Just remove the /thumb/ directory from each url to access them. The smaller pics seemed clear enough, \r\nso I didnt bother linking.[/quote:04d355f56e]\r\nCool.\r\nNo, I think you\'re right - the smaller pics should be fine.\r\nNice to have the option though should it be needed.\r\nI\'ll let you know when it\'s up.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36875,'1d69512641','[quote:1d69512641=\"DarkTari\"]I cleaned up an old post yesterday.  I feel Da Hookup will have a lot of outdated/no good posts cause it\'s all about a bargain, for a limited time, so after that the post is no good.  Is there any quick way to delete the entire post and all responses?\r\n\r\nI did one from sg219 about a TRU clerance last year (which is no good now) and had to individually delete every post.  Or do we want  a place like an archive dumpster where we can move old, outdated post to?\r\n\r\nThanx Pimp![/quote:1d69512641]\r\nI say just lock them up so people know they\'re dead, but it\'s still there arhived.\r\n\r\nIf you want to delete an entire topic and all responses, just go into the topic, scroll to the bottom of the page.\r\nOn the left side, there should be a red button with an X (next to the yellow button with an arrow).\r\nHit that and you\'ll be able to delete the entire topic and all responses.'),(37883,'11d6e53797','[quote:11d6e53797=\"ynad\"]dude,  i do appreciate your effort to help me out.\r\nand no disrespect intended but check your sig for small typo\r\n&quot;Those who would sacrifice liberty for security deserve[b:11d6e53797]r[/b:11d6e53797] neither. - Benjamin Franklin &quot;\r\nthank you Cabo Wabo. i mean it[/quote:11d6e53797]\r\nNo sweat dude, glad I could help.\r\nAnd thanks for the heads up on my sig. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36632,'bde5843677','[quote:bde5843677=\"stampede_dude\"]Do you have an extra XMOD Evo Car Rear Body Clip? to use for a gen1 corvette body? I can send you some more $ if you do, LMK...since you cant ship monday, its MLK day  :-)[/quote:bde5843677]\r\n\r\nDOH!!\r\n\r\nOK. Tuesday. :-o \r\n\r\nSorry, no clips.'),(36262,'194eee7d7b','[quote:194eee7d7b=\"arch2b\"]we just happen to be racing tomorrow!  \r\n\r\nwe typically get together every other week.[/quote:194eee7d7b]\r\nThanx for the invite unfortunately can\'t do it tomorrow.\r\n\r\nSend me your Email &amp; Home addresses.\r\n\r\nThanx!'),(36314,'a1e1e39cc8','Congratulations Pimp!  Great work once again!\r\n\r\nI got yo info, I\'ll get it out to you 1st thing Monday.  :-o'),(36316,'3f119c48fc','Hey! Where the hell did you go?\r\nI still have the dead chassi for you. I was in a car accident with a freind before I could send them, and helped her pay for damages. \r\n\r\nI seem to have lost your address, and you have been MIA for a while. Let me know if you still want them, and I can send them out in about a week or so.'),(36829,'fa0c3ac8a8','[quote:fa0c3ac8a8=\"ph2t\"]I inhereited the worse fucken network known to man when I started here.  Now it\'s good.  Took me a year to get shit sorted....\r\n\r\nfucken dumbarse admins........[/quote:fa0c3ac8a8]\r\nI dunno, I think this network is in the running for &quot;worste fucken network&quot;. lol\r\nWe\'ve still got a Win NT box running some shit. :eek: \r\nI\'m affraid to even reboot the fucker.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37057,'ff7799f994','[quote:ff7799f994=\"hue35\"]\r\n\r\nGod damn!... I\'m still stunned by how fuckin\' cool this thing is. Shit, man... people are gonna shit when they see this car flossed up.\r\n\r\nedit: AND, it hasn\'t EVEN sunk in yet that this car will be in my hands, when all is said and done. God damn.[/quote:ff7799f994] :lol: You almost sound like someone that just got Overhauled.\r\n\r\nCool.  :-o \r\n\r\nYep, its yours. :-o \r\n\r\nOh yeah, and people are really gonna shit when I make another vid, showing the 2 cars, then right when they line up as if they are about to race... another &quot;to be continued&quot;. I\'ll do the last vid when/if I ever fly out to see you.  :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:ff7799f994]edit 2: have you heard The Ribeye Brothers? If not, I\'ve got a couple of discs to send ya... right up your alley, I\'d bet... fun stuff. They\'re another spinoff of Monster Magnet, just the polar opposite of the other spinoff (Atomic Bitchwax).[/quote:ff7799f994]I loved Monster Magnet when they came out. That first vid of theirs looked like an old Sabbath video. Then on like the 3rd or 4th album they cheesed out. He even said he was tired of the lack of response from the audience, and decided if this is what you want then I\'m gonna go over the top with all of it, and went all 666 and shit. \r\n\r\nAnyways Monster Magnet rant aside (I actually edited that back :lol: ), that sounds way cool. I have a pile a crap I want to send you, but my CD-R is down. Oh well, its almost tax time, and (fingers crossed) we should be getting a new computer real soon.\r\n\r\nDave'),(34752,'4cc2ba07a1','[quote:4cc2ba07a1=\"Finks\"]When you say clear the Cache memory, is that going to tools the internet options then delete cookies and clearing the history?  God, I knew this at one time......[/quote:4cc2ba07a1]\r\nYea you got it.\r\nYou can just clear the history if ya want.\r\nIf you clear cookies, probably most of your \"logins\" won\'t be saved.\r\nSo for example you\'d have to re-login to bitPimps next time you visited.\r\n\r\n* Also, after \"Tools &gt; Internet Options &gt; Delete Files\" you should close your browser and open it up again.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37626,'a599e67864','Please ship to the following address and not the address of the paypal account.\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\nBannister Land\r\nMartindales Road\r\nSt.Michael BB11115\r\nBARBADOS\r\n\r\nwhat is your paypal addy'),(37627,'7e65c78b4f','[quote:7e65c78b4f=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Please ship to the following address and not the address of the paypal account.\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\nBannister Land\r\nMartindales Road\r\nSt.Michael BB11115\r\nBARBADOS\r\n\r\nwhat is your paypal addy[/quote:7e65c78b4f]\r\n\r\nCool, i gotcha, BTW You sure that you got evo fets? I\'m pretty sure he was selling his 7317 fets he got off ausmicro?\r\n\r\n\r\nPaypal Addy:\r\n\r\nkgera1@tampabay.rr.com'),(37638,'f28c62a9cf','[quote:f28c62a9cf=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Well then I\'ll just take the iW board. \r\n\r\nYou wouldn\'t happen to have any MRS4 stuff you\'d like to get rid of, maybe some electronics or alloy? (I already have a TX)[/quote:f28c62a9cf]\r\n\r\nDamn you sure? Arrgh i was hoping to get rid of them both.\r\n\r\nNah i dont have a MRS4 mate.'),(37639,'441c5faead','I would like it, but I don\'t want to buy a charger etc. I\'ll buy that stuff when I\'m shopping for batts.\r\n\r\nI only wanted it cuz I had the cheapo charger doing nothing. Plus I\'d need a board harness.\r\n\r\nSo just the board. I\'ll send you $13, shipping for phatboi was under a buck. That cool? \r\n\r\nHey, you got any Xmod stuff? Since I last asked?\r\n\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36369,'97e22704f0','Yeah, I was actually driving a truck pulling a boat. not nearly as fun at driving boats. haha\r\n\r\nI just found some tire foams under my bed! haha\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(34758,'b82cb4e1df','[quote:b82cb4e1df]OK, so I assume TE is test, and SW is switch or swap... reverse polarity. \r\n\r\nWhen I put the leads to a batt and press TE, it barely flashes green for a split second. Then, when I change the \"SW\" detting, it does nothing... so, the brief flash of green (really brief) means it\'s connected properly?... OK, wait... I just connected it to one of the other batteries and it really lit up green and stayed on. Does that mean the other batt (the brief flash one) has absolutely no charge, or that it\'s defective? \r\n\r\nAlso, do you know what the PW light is for? \r\n\r\nFinally, I assume that once I connect this thing and plug it in, it knows when to shut down? \r\n[/quote:b82cb4e1df]\r\n\r\nYes. Test and Switch. You have to hold the test button to test. If you want to find out what it does when it detects reverse polarity, just switch it around and you will see.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know why the light would go out if you held it down. Perhaps it detects low voltage, but I doubt it. Best thing to do it charge them up and be sure to watch them charge. you definately want to make sure they charge propperly.\r\n\r\nIt will turn off automatically. If you test charge, and watch it charge, you will see how it works. It really isn\'t rocket science, but be sure to unplug the cell if it starts to swell up. That is the first sign that the cells have gone bad. Those cells have been sitting around for a couple months, and I really can\'t attest to their quality. If you have a problem with any of the cells, I don\'t have a problem giving you a partial refund if you like. *shrug* I just didn\'t need the charger so I was trying to give it away to someone who would use it, not really make any money.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(34765,'c61953159a','[quote:c61953159a=\"Tuner1989\"][quote:c61953159a=\"Clint\"]Hey got a question for ya.\r\n\r\nWhere did you get the powerquest 600mah lipo from?\r\nI searched all over and not one website sells them. Did you mean\r\nPoly Quest?\r\n\r\n-Clint[/quote:c61953159a]\r\n\r\nDoh! :o \r\n\r\nSorry about that, yes i meant polyquest.\r\n\r\nIts a great lipo pack for the dimensions of the evo chassis.\r\n\r\nCheck out \r\n\r\nwww.zagi.com \r\n\r\nThey have reasonable shipping etc.\r\n\r\nSorry about that, and btw great job on the tut.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:c61953159a]\r\n\r\nOrdered. Thx.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34767,'1cbe18ebf7','[quote:1cbe18ebf7=\"Finks\"]It\'s a wedding man.  My sister in law is getting hitched to a Merican :grin:   I\'ll give you a ring for sure.  No idea what my scedual will be but here is my Cell # 207-551-9773  I\'ll call you when I get down there Sat, will be there from Sat-Sat so a whole friggin week.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nJesse (aka Finks)[/quote:1cbe18ebf7]\r\n\r\nCall my Cell.  If I\'m on the bike, I\'ll call you when we lunch break at [color=orange:1cbe18ebf7]Hooters.[/color:1cbe18ebf7]  I\'ll be working out at 09:00, riding da motorcyle at Noon and I\'ll be gone most of the day.  Saturday is suppose to be the best! Mid 70\'s, no rain, just perfect.  Rain late Sunday.  I\'ll see what your schedule looks like........\r\n\r\nGlenn'),(34769,'0b30001215','don\'t leave yet, jump in the chat. (04/11/2005)\r\nPlease'),(34772,'f7523f8a77','Ok here is what I want:\r\n[color=red:f7523f8a77]-------------------------PARTS-------------------------------[/color:f7523f8a77]\r\nDrivetrain:\r\n-Steel Universals\r\n-Alloy knuckles (purple?)\r\n-Rear Ball differential\r\n\r\nEssentially I\'d like 2 fully assembled front ends with\r\n-one-way diff w/ metal cups (for drifter)\r\n-front ball diff w/ metal cups (for racer)\r\nIf not, the drop-in diffs would do. Just wanted to cut out the swapping hassle.\r\n\r\n-VCS shock and mounts\r\n-front springs (different stiffnesses)\r\n-deans connector for liths to ESC (drifter)\r\n-140mm belt\r\n\r\n[b:f7523f8a77]Price: $60 shipped (to US) for everything above this line[/b:f7523f8a77]\r\n\r\nyes/no?\r\n[color=red:f7523f8a77]--------------------------CARS-----------------------------------[/color:f7523f8a77]\r\nYou say that you have kits, but I\'d really like something RTR and stock. If you only have kits, but also have all the stock electronics in another place, combine them and I\'ll take them. So that\'s:\r\n\r\n-(1) RTR-ish Kit 140mm (I want to use an impreza body)\r\nIf you have an RX-7/skyline/supra kit that would be sweet\r\n\r\nIf you don\'t have stock electronics (with stock Tx), never mind.\r\n\r\n[b:f7523f8a77]Price: $100 shipped for everything above this line[/b:f7523f8a77]\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know what you think\r\nMaxx'),(34774,'4d05c63ba6','Hey DT, how you doing man? Remember this thread:\r\n\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6183[/url]\r\n\r\nI have two of those sets, open box, never run, collecting dust. I need money right now, so I need to sell these. I bought one set from Bithed a long time ago, and the other came from JDMHatchback a few months ago. \r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in one or both of these, holler at your boy. I can give you more details, and probably even pics this weekend.\r\n\r\nI\'d like to see you have these if you want them. Not offering to anybody else for now. Just let me know if you\'re interested, and then I\'ll offer you a great deal. \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMichael Graham');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34775,'931548fc9c','[quote:931548fc9c=\"mikirgra\"]Hey DT, how you doing man? [b:931548fc9c]Remember this thread[/b:931548fc9c]:\r\n\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6183[/url]\r\n\r\nI have two of those sets, open box, never run, collecting dust. I need money right now, so I need to sell these. I bought one set from Bithed a long time ago, and the other came from JDMHatchback a few months ago. \r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in one or both of these, holler at your boy. I can give you more details, and probably even pics this weekend.\r\n\r\nI\'d like to see you have these if you want them. Not offering to anybody else for now. Just let me know if you\'re interested, and then I\'ll offer you a great deal. \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMichael Graham[/quote:931548fc9c]\r\n[quote:931548fc9c=\"mikirgra\"]Hey DT, how you doing man? [b:931548fc9c]Remember this thread[/b:931548fc9c]:\r\n\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6183[/url]\r\n\r\nI have two of those sets, open box, never run, collecting dust. I need money right now, so I need to sell these. I bought one set from Bithed a long time ago, and the other came from JDMHatchback a few months ago. \r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in one or both of these, holler at your boy. I can give you more details, and probably even pics this weekend.\r\n\r\nI\'d like to see you have these if you want them. Not offering to anybody else for now. Just let me know if you\'re interested, and then I\'ll offer you a great deal. \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMichael Graham[/quote:931548fc9c]\r\n\r\n[b:931548fc9c]DO I !!!!!!![/b:931548fc9c] :eek: \r\n\r\nBoth Are SOLD !!!!!!!  Get me details..... :D \r\nI just missed out on one about two weeks ago cause I \"forgot\"  :mad: \r\nIt went for $17.26 w/ a Digi-Q and Pull Back plus some gear sets!\r\nBut I\'m over that now....with this PM, I\'m REALLY over it now!  :smile: \r\nJD never told me he had this set.  I\'m getting some sets from him here real soon.\r\n\r\nHey Thanx for offering it to me first Pimp!  :-o'),(34776,'d2a9c77a92','Hey Pimp,\r\n\r\nI got Lupin set from ya too !\r\n\r\nWhat else do you have back in the BatCave I may be interested in?  :lol: \r\n\r\nThanx AGain Pimp !');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36330,'0e4c788f04','[quote:0e4c788f04=\"steelwoolghandi\"][quote:0e4c788f04=\"DarkTari\"]Congratulations Pimp!  Great work once again!\r\n\r\nI got yo info, I\'ll get it out to you 1st thing Monday.  :-o[/quote:0e4c788f04]\r\n\r\nthanks a ton man the contest was great I appreciate the work ya\'ll went to, to put it on! \r\n\r\nthat was a hard choice glad I was not the one to try and make it!\r\n\r\nthanks again man!  :-)[/quote:0e4c788f04]\r\n\r\nHarder than you could ever imagine  :-? \r\nCongrats again Pimp!'),(35688,'3fd7bafac5','Ok.\r\nEnough of this shit,  i don\'t want to just have arguing, i want to have a serious chat here.\r\nI understand that you are tired of n00b\'s and shit coming in, asking stupid questions. Mine wern\'t stupid questions, I was just asking some decent questions for info, help, and to update on my upcoming project.\r\nI am wondering if you knowe of the name you guys have given your self, for being \"flamable\" towards n00bs, etc. You guys are know to be netherless rude and obnoxious. Why? I don\'t know. I always though these forums people have created were to spread idea,s tips, information, and HELP ONE ANOTHER. I don\'t see much of this, just threats, foul language, etc.\r\nMind you i disagree with PG forums, that bann you for saying \"shit\" , but the degree that I have witnessed from SOME of your members, admins, moderators, and what other people have told me about this forum.\r\n You have a great forum, very knowledgable people here, great mind, projects, creation.\r\nNow if I came in without proper punctuation( I try my best), asking completley gay question, I would be expected to be treated fairly(flamed a bit, told to use punctuation, and directed towards a rules page or something)\r\nEVEN though, I have punctuation, some good questions, and intense interest in these forum. I still was flamed, threatened to be stabbed with a pen(lol..) etc.\r\nI\'m hoping you guys could do something to resolve your beat/flame the new bitches theme, for something more civilized. Maybe you could get a better name, draw more interest, and have more good members in the end.\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nBryce'),(34781,'87e80a00b8','The Trueno sets are yours. Yep, you bought the Lupin set from me too. That was another set I had bought from Bithed. JD probably didn\'t tell you about the Trueno set because she (the JD I deal with is female, but I think she likes to be a little private about that) was holding it for me, FOREVER. She\'s really really cool. My all time fav to deal with.\r\n\r\nLook DT, I got more stuff that I will have to unload soon, but most of it is dups, and you probably already have it. Regardless, I\'m a fan, so I will give you first shot at those items too once I get around to sorting my crap and deciding what I can and can\'t live w/o.\r\n\r\nI gotta start my commute home, but I\'ll get back with you on Monday if not sooner about the Trueno sets.\r\n\r\nThanks man.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34782,'aa87f018e8','Cool Pimp !\r\n\r\nI\'ve got a lot of Dups so lemme know whatcha got!\r\n\r\nAppreciate it Pimp!  Be Safe.......'),(34789,'e90a267cfc','Sorry, but i had to buy a replacement came gear for my 4G63. I have a few bucks left over right now, but the PO is closed. But come Monday and I should send them off.\r\n\r\nNo worries, I\'m listening to AFI. :smile:'),(34792,'d868ce96ec','[quote:d868ce96ec=\"HirotoR34\"]I was wondering if i could swap out one of my entries for another one?[/quote:d868ce96ec]\r\nYou\'re putting me in a bind man. lol\r\nNormally, to just a \"user\", I\'d say no.\r\nCould you imagine if I had to do this for every member? I\'d lose my job because my time would be spent exchanging photos, updating shit, etc.\r\nBut for pimps like you, I like to try to accomidate.\r\n\r\nKeep it on the down low.\r\nDon\'t annouce your change, just make the change (edit links etc.)\r\nIf you promise to go back and edit your post, the post with the ride you plan on replacing. I\'ll do it this time. Please try not to do it again.\r\nAnd you have to let me know which ride to replace and get me the photos of the new ride you\'re replacing it with so I can upload them to the galleries.'),(36927,'91483f278a','[quote:91483f278a=\"DarkTari\"]Man I knew Namuna would like this post but God Damn!  Chicken Nuggets !!!!  :lol: \r\nHe\'s gonna blow this mutha UP !!!!  Watch....[/quote:91483f278a] :lol: \r\nI know dude, I saw Chicken Nuggets and just about spit on my monitor laughing.\r\nHe sure likes those odd-ball deals. lol');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36928,'2410247ffa','Thanks dude. I will play around with that gallery thing tonight. I know absolutly nothing about php so.... kinda screwed there. and as far as mysql forget it. I barly know html. ROFLMAO. \r\n\r\nI guess I;m glad I can build what I have thus far. Its been trying at times but it looks good for a starting out page.'),(36307,'5991771a9d','[quote:5991771a9d=\"Sporttracguy\"]This was a complete suprise,  i never thought the baja truck would get me very far  :eek: \r\n\r\nHere is my info\r\n\r\nRyan Eylander\r\n7701 Delridge Way SW apt. 9A\r\nSeattle, WA 98106\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG[/quote:5991771a9d]\r\nCongratulations Pimp!  This was the most difficult contest yet.  Man we\r\nwere like a cannibal boardroom!\r\nI got yo info, I\'ll get it out to you 1st thing Monday.  :-o'),(34804,'602f6bddc2','never mind the kits. I\'m getting a free Xmod, do I\'ll just drift that in my free time. \r\nAny progress on the finding the parts?'),(37826,'131e88a43f','I\'m gonna pay pal you the $20 for the chassis tonight. Is that ok?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37852,'69b32ab789','[quote:69b32ab789=\"JdmHatchback\"]Hey Darktari!\r\n\r\nHope everythings doing good. I just remembered that I needed to send you pics of what I have left. Are you still interested in anything? \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJDM[/quote:69b32ab789]\r\n\r\nAh, Yeah !\r\n\r\nDarkTari@msn.com'),(36245,'dd5131cd97','we just happen to be racing tomorrow!  \r\n\r\nwe typically get together every other week.'),(34811,'9687ea3f0f','I contacted dude for an update, received the following:\r\n\r\n[quote:9687ea3f0f]\r\n[b:9687ea3f0f]My 18 month son had surgury on OCT 25 they nicked his bowel and had to go back ing three days later he\'s still in the hospital please let everyone know they will get there items i will try to ship them monday usps express mail\r\n\r\nthanks chad conus[/b:9687ea3f0f][/quote:9687ea3f0f]'),(34812,'8376e9454e','I contacted dude for an update, received the following:\r\n\r\n[quote:8376e9454e]\r\n[b:8376e9454e]My 18 month son had surgury on OCT 25 they nicked his bowel and had to go back ing three days later he\'s still in the hospital please let everyone know they will get there items i will try to ship them monday usps express mail\r\n\r\nthanks chad conus[/b:8376e9454e][/quote:8376e9454e]'),(34813,'c7a2ef60be','I contacted dude for an update, received the following:\r\n\r\n[quote:c7a2ef60be]\r\n[b:c7a2ef60be]My 18 month son had surgury on OCT 25 they nicked his bowel and had to go back ing three days later he\'s still in the hospital please let everyone know they will get there items i will try to ship them monday usps express mail\r\n\r\nthanks chad conus[/b:c7a2ef60be][/quote:c7a2ef60be]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34818,'948825ccc4','[quote:948825ccc4=\"45tr0\"][quote:948825ccc4=\"Nasphere\"]:-? \r\n[quote:948825ccc4]Processor: Mac OS X-compatible processor that is a model G3 or higher.\r\nOperating system: Mac OS X version 10.3 or later.[/quote:948825ccc4]\r\nlol, i have OS9... My mac wont run OSX...[/quote:948825ccc4]\r\n\r\nTry here.\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.microsoft.com/mac/downloads.aspx?pid=download&amp;location=/mac/download/misc/msn_messenger2.xml&amp;secid=35&amp;ssid=1&amp;flgnosysreq=False[/url]\r\n[quote:948825ccc4]\r\nProcessor: Macintosh PowerPC.\r\nOperating system:* Mac OS 9.2.2. or above [/quote:948825ccc4][/quote:948825ccc4]\r\nThanks dude..'),(34817,'b2ca0122ae',':-o \r\n\r\nhey thanks for the update.  was starting to get a little nervous.'),(34823,'704ff7cf81','[quote:704ff7cf81=\"richh\"]Sorry for the delay,  here\'s what i found so far.  These items are all new. [color=red:704ff7cf81]I want...[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\n\r\nHPI Micro RS4 Kits\r\nViper\r\nSkyline\r\n\r\nMRS4 Bodies\r\nHPI NSX [color=red:704ff7cf81]This (unpainted right?)[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\nHPI Vette\r\nHPI Viper\r\nHPI Dodge Stratus\r\nProline GMC Sierra\r\nProline Dodge Dakota\r\n\r\nHPI Hopups\r\nDogbones x 2 [color=red:704ff7cf81]This[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\n150mm Belt x 2\r\nTitanium Antenna\r\nDual Link Tie Rod Set [color=red:704ff7cf81]This[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\nBall Diff Set [color=red:704ff7cf81]This[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\nLed Light Set\r\n\r\nMisc Hopups\r\nGH Alum Pulley (Silver)\r\nGH Alum 300 Motor Mount (Purple)\r\nGPM? Alum Pulley (Silver)\r\nGPM Front Spring Damper (Purple) [color=red:704ff7cf81]This (does it have replacement springs too?)[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\nGPM 1pc Rear Oil Damper (Purple) [color=red:704ff7cf81]This[/color:704ff7cf81]\r\nGPM X-shock Set (Purple)\r\n\r\nI know I have more bodies than that so I think I\'m still missing a box of stuff.  I also some more used stuff that\'s already on cars.[/quote:704ff7cf81]\r\n\r\nPut that stuff asside, and I\'ll see what else I want from the remaining box(es)'),(37256,'41fc57abce','I found the red front diff, but no gear that whent on the driveshaft :(  I included all that i had spare for the AWD kit, hope it gonna be good. Im expecting the stuff 2 day or 2 morrow so yeah, you get ur stuff yet?????');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36505,'2889173d2f','Alrighty, did you use Air Mail? I used Air Mail so the earliest date it should arrive would be Friday.'),(36506,'1003468991','I used airmail also...\r\n\r\n\r\nI had sent something via airmail to Newzealan, and he had already recieved my package, that is why i asked you incase you recieve the stuff.\r\n\r\nThe parts you sent me...were they Aluminum?'),(34835,'e072d5aeb5','Hey Mang, You got a copy/get a copy of Adobe Premier Elements.'),(34839,'d7ebe10ad0','[quote:d7ebe10ad0=\"cj\"][quote:d7ebe10ad0=\"sg219\"][quote:d7ebe10ad0=\"cj\"]Just got some XM018 motor heatsinks.  I have 1 Green just for you and if you want it I didn\'t get gold but I did get Champagne which is a light gold.[/quote:d7ebe10ad0]\r\n\r\nI\'ll take them. :-o \r\n\r\nHow much?[/quote:d7ebe10ad0]\r\n\r\n$14.99 ea plus $2.00 s&amp;h for a total PayPal of $31.98 to cjellis@yahoo.com[/quote:d7ebe10ad0]\r\n\r\nWhoa... :shock: \r\n\r\nI didn\'t think they were $15 bucks each.  Um, are you in a hurry to get rid of these?  Could you wait till my next P-day, Nov 18th?\r\n\r\nIf not, I\'ll just take the Green one now. :-o \r\n\r\nThen if you still have the other later, I\'ll take it.\r\n\r\nThanks, \r\n\r\nMike'),(34841,'d264673acd','My dad put our nova on ebay, theres tons of pics there.  I\'d rather not put the ebay auction on the forums, I dont know why, but if your interested I\'ll hook ya up with the link, cause that Stubby Nova pic ya did was fuckin\' sweet.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34842,'59965e429e','Sure man, shoot me the link... I\'m busy like a mutha right now, but I\'d love to see more pics of that car. I\'ll eventually get around to stubbifyin\' one (or some) of \'em, and I\'ll send \'em to ya when I do.\r\n\r\nMy dad had a mint 1969 (my birth year) Camaro Z28 (orange with black rally stripes) when I was 12 through 15... it was always gonna be my car, but he had to sell it when I was 15. It was a major bummer... I\'m hopin\' your story is less of a bummer, but if it\'s the same, just know there\'s at least one pimp that understands.\r\n\r\nlater,\r\n\r\nhue35'),(34846,'4a78114829','Sounds good.  Thanks.\r\n\r\nAre you going half upfront and half when they get here on the EVO parts, or all at once, or something else? :???:'),(37722,'f79508d385','That\'s cool pimp. If you want I will keep em aside for you? \r\n\r\nLet me know when you send the dough, and give me your mailing address when you are ready.\r\n\r\nTake care pimp'),(36793,'2d9ff93acb','Got your money out today also I added something to the letter so be carfull when you open it.\r\n\r\nthanks man!  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34851,'2420f8979a','hey sup havent talk to you in a while do you not like me.'),(34852,'e9a07ad8f8','I don\'t really have regular conversations with anyone on BP, so don\'t feel bad. I don\'t normally go in the chat either, it\'s just that, that day I needed to have a convo with Zeineth.\r\n\r\nSo what\'s up man? How\'s the home-schoolin\' coming? I hope your tutor is teaching you the right things lol. I\'ve gone into \"lurking mode\" here on BP since I have school work to concentrate on right now. But, look out for 2  more entries in the competition from me. I\'d like to post a really good looking one for my 500th post. So keep a look out and keep a lid on it. Don\'t ask what they are cuz I\'m not tellin. I\'ll ask ppl questions about what i really need to know through the PM\'s so no one will know. Of course, this is [u:e9a07ad8f8]after[/u:e9a07ad8f8] I\'ve serched. :-o \r\n\r\nI\'m trying to get some MRS4 stuff to get my micro running. That\'s where most of my money is going right now. Plus I have to buy some ZZ stuff to sell for Xmas. \r\n\r\nAnyhow, I\'m done spilling my guts.\r\nLater,\r\nMaxx'),(34869,'eda320b88e','hey sat, i noticed when u posted a picture of your collection in [url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=155&amp;start=225]this[/url]\r\nthread u had a little green hatchback on the right side of the table. i would like to know what chassi/body this is since i cant get over hatchs :smile:  \r\n \r\nthanks bro[/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34870,'477a0b7804','Wow you really hate me.'),(34871,'cc73b2ea34','Here is my last PM to you.\r\n\r\n[quote:cc73b2ea34]No, and if you PM me again, or so much as reply to this message and I will report you to the moderators and it will likely result in a ban.\r\n[/quote:cc73b2ea34]\r\n\r\nThis is your last warning.\r\n\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(37643,'5c51f80911','Check for the $13 in 5-7 mins, I should be done the transaction by then.'),(36380,'9465afef36','yeppers w/ insurance\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37884,'f68808361b','hiya brudda! stuff arrived today just as good as it left you :-o \r\nthanks a bunch for the extras, you\'re a legend! :cool:'),(34879,'88d6f72561','[quote:88d6f72561=\"mikirgra\"]Hang in there with me man. Been real busy at work, and the wife is sick at home, so I\'m playing Mr. Mom too. If I get a few minutes after I get the boys down tonight, I\'ll get the trueno sets out of my closet and get you some more details.\r\n\r\nYour patience will pay.  :grin:[/quote:88d6f72561]\r\n\r\nThanx Again Pimp!\r\n\r\nNo Rush, Take yo time  :cool:'),(34880,'9176ba8198','hey man, could you move this thread to miscleaneous RC?\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7018\r\n\r\n\r\nlol, i wasn\'t sure where it should go until after i started it...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (34881,'f77b041f88','i need a purchase. Please reply'),(36497,'71fe3f4147','I picked up this one!  It should be in the advertisement too !\r\n\r\n[img:71fe3f4147]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10005/DSC02851.JPG[/img:71fe3f4147]'),(36498,'a4a7602fd2','I\'ll be out near there the next couple of days.  I gotta see if they have them in the store.  Looks like it\'ll fill my needs.\r\n\r\nHave you used it yet or tryied it out?  \r\n\r\nHow noisey or quiet is it?\r\n\r\nWill it need a lot of maintenence?\r\n\r\nSturdy?  Not crappy plastic and loose parts?  Long lasting or will I be replacing it in a couple of months or years?\r\n\r\nYou know, the overall quality report the the big DT.\r\n\r\n :-o \r\n\r\nThanks man.'),(34888,'c3231fd9c4','I need a purchase'),(34891,'46bff1fa14','[quote:46bff1fa14=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I need a purchase[/quote:46bff1fa14]\r\n\r\nHey, Whats up?\r\n\r\nI do, but I wont be home for a while. I commute to work and dont come\r\nhome until a week or two(or when i get sick of it).'),(34892,'13d3527880','Can you ship it to another US address? 3 Hours left.\r\nI\'ll send you a MO when you win.\r\nI just need you to bid as late as possible on [url=http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6010340347&amp;rd=1&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1][b:13d3527880]THIS[/b:13d3527880][/url] so that I can get it as cheap as possible and less than $60.\r\n\r\nThat cool? All you need to do is pay for it, unless, by \"not home\" you mean that you will not have any internet access  :???: \r\n\r\nLet me know\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37928,'54ca36b0b0','[quote:54ca36b0b0=\"SuperFly\"]I realize I said I would paypal you $30, but I forgot about shipping. If ya feel like you can trust me, you can package it up and mail it, and just tell me how much postage was and I\'ll paypal ya that amount. However you want to do it is cool with me.[/quote:54ca36b0b0]\r\n\r\nI trust ya but I can send it for $4.00 if that sounds fair I will try and drum up some Crystals if I can find them and send them along. \r\n\r\nplease send your address and I will get it out monday. \r\n\r\noh and my paypal is my email airo@ev1.net \r\n\r\nthanks man hope ya like the Epoch I know I like them a ton! :grin:'),(37219,'8c8c125766','Here you go.  \r\nBoho81@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nor rgwilson@mar.navy.med.mil'),(37220,'17002da939','[quote:17002da939=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Here you go.  \r\nBoho81@yahoo.com &lt;-----[b:17002da939]sent here[/b:17002da939]\r\n\r\nor rgwilson@mar.navy.med.mil[/quote:17002da939]Just forward that to baratacus. Remove all evidence that it was forwarded (subject etc)'),(35072,'0b71e5d186','[quote:0b71e5d186=\"hue35\"]Sorry for the delay, I had some friends in town this weekend. OK, so the software I used on that vid has a master file that uses the clips and pics as resources, so there ends up not being a final, single source file. So, the easiest thing to do would be for me to make a down and dirty DVD (simple menus and stuff), then you could rip that into whatever you want.\r\n\r\nDoes that sound like it would work for you?\r\n\r\nI could probably format it into a single file also... what file type would you prefer, and I\'ll give it a try? I\'ve had troubles outta that program before, so I can\'t promise that route. Either way, it\'ll have to end up on a disk and be mailed... it\'s about a 4 or 500 MB file.[/quote:0b71e5d186]\r\nNo worries dude, hope ya had fun!\r\n\r\nA compiled version of the clip would probably work better for me (i.e. not the storyboard from the program you\'re using)\r\nAVI, MPEG, MOV are all file types I could use if you have it.\r\nIf not, no biggie.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37592,'57978c4709','[quote:57978c4709=\"MafiaS\"]Cabo I would like to submit one of my own songs I have created. I wanted you to review it and give me the ok to perhaps put it on the bitPimps radio. I would like others to get a taste of my music. \r\n\r\n    I will propose music that comes from an underground house style of music. If this is cool please pm me back and we could figure out how to get the song to you. I have many, but would like to send em out one by one and get some critique on them. \r\n\r\ni figure bitpimps is a good chance to get some opinions on my stuff considering i am taking a Disk Jockey course and it has become one of my other hobbies.\r\n\r\nThanks for your time...[/quote:57978c4709]\r\nThere\'s places to upload your own music.\r\nCan\'t remember where right now, would have to look.\r\nBut I know some of the other pimps on here have done that in the past.\r\nThat way everyone can check it out and critique it if you\'d like.\r\n\r\nOr...\r\n\r\nMail a song to bitpimps@gmail.com (make sure it doesn\'t contain a virus or I\'ll have to end you lol)\r\nI\'ll check it out. :-o'),(37601,'516e644ab1','[quote:516e644ab1=\"pimpsmurf\"][quote=PimpSmurf]I don\'t agree with everything the libertarians (base = liberty, not liberal) believe, just 95% of it. They are pretty far right wing. Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative. [/quote:516e644ab1]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t say liberals, I said libertarians. And they do indeed. There are a couple libertarian talk shows on talkradio and shortwave and they are most libertarians (about 75%) see Bush as more liberal than conservative.\r\n\r\nThe problem with all these labels is you have to define them. The problem with the LP is most members of the LP vote for republicans in states that are close. No need to have another sex-junkie in the White House.\r\n\r\nYou are seeing fault where there is non. I have not contradicted myself on this issue because it is an issue of beliefs. You are retreating, which is OK. I\'m not willing to argue a point (argue, not fight) that the other side isn\'t willing to bring ideas to the table.\r\n\r\nThanks anyway man. It was fun (except the gay sex.)\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote]\r\n :lol: You\'re a joke anymore to me dude.\r\nIf you can\'t even see the flaws in your posts, the contradictions, and just even general false statements you make - I can\'t help you.\r\nNobody can.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know what you\'re stuck on with the gay sex thing unless it\'s burned into your memory from you last gay experience or something.\r\n\r\nAnyways, I\'m not retreating. I own this place. You don\'t.\r\nIf I don\'t want it to be a political forum, guess what? It won\'t be.\r\nI\'ve let you go on long enough spewing your bullshit. Now I\'m putting a stop to it.\r\n\r\nIf you can\'t go back to what this forum is about, I\'m affraid you\'ll just have to leave - and guess who else can make that happen? Yup, me!\r\n\r\nGo bite your pillow.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35076,'df50dddf5b','[quote:df50dddf5b=\"hue35\"][quote:df50dddf5b=\"CaboWabo\"]A compiled version of the clip would probably work better for me (i.e. not the storyboard from the program you\'re using)\r\nAVI, MPEG, MOV are all file types I could use if you have it.\r\nIf not, no biggie.[/quote:df50dddf5b]\r\nGot ya... I may not be able to do that from the app I used, but I\'ll try it. Can you rip &amp; copy DVD\'s? What I was getting at is, that may be the only option... a normal video DVD, then you could extract from that, if you\'re set up that way. Like, I copy about 3-6 vids a week from netflix, so I\'m all set up for that shit... stealin\' is what the kids are callin\' it. Crazy kids.[/quote:df50dddf5b]\r\nI hear ya, but what file format is that when you rip the DVD?\r\nI think typcially they are ISO files right?\r\nI can\'t import an ISO into a video editing program so I\'m looking for any possible file formats.\r\nYou could re-export the video as .mov, just not at 320 x 240 for the web and that\'d probably do fine - if you can that is - I don\'t know. Maybe the source files were recorded at 320 x 240 and therefore increasing dimension would just pixelate it.\r\nIf it\'s at all hassle, don\'t do it. I don\'t want to waste your time. It was just something I wanted to try to play with, but it\'s not that big of a deal.'),(35086,'5f4e08f209','What kind of condition is the MR-01 in?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36531,'c703949b14','no sweat, i\'ll pass it on :-)'),(36532,'68bc95de6c','It\'s headed your way man...\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(35099,'1893242760','[quote:1893242760=\"cj\"][quote:1893242760]OK. Made up my mind. \r\n\r\nHere\'s my list. \r\n\r\nSilver Please. \r\nFor an Evo Mustang. \r\n\r\nEverything, except: \r\nXME330LAN-ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR LANCER) - 1PC[/quote:1893242760]\r\n\r\nMy paypal is cjellis@yahoo.com\r\n\r\nTotaL $63.00 + $3.00 s&amp;h.[/quote:1893242760]\r\n\r\nsweet deal!!! \r\n\r\nI get paid tuesday night, so I will paypal you on the 16th (wednesday).\r\n\r\nThx.'),(35100,'0101704670','Almost forgot.. Can you add in an extra set of car rear dogbones to my order?\r\n\r\nXME039R ------$6.50--------21----35%----$4.23 (11/11 @ 9:45am)'),(35101,'049f7200b4','[quote:049f7200b4=\"Clint\"]Almost forgot.. Can you add in an extra set of car rear dogbones to my order?\r\n\r\nXME039R ------$6.50--------21----35%----$4.23 (11/11 @ 9:45am)[/quote:049f7200b4]\r\n\r\nSure just paypal me $71.00 total.'),(35102,'abf0174f68','Hi, what do you think of the deal?\r\nI\'d like to have this stuff b4 Xmas. \r\nI definately want the skyline kit, but I may not want the dogbones. I\'m getting a set from someone else. When you reply, quote me so I know what I said I wanted cuz the list may change.\r\n\r\nLet me know\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37577,'df12a7045a','[quote:df12a7045a=\"99skyline\"]Ok.  That sounds good. I\'m expecting to recieve a Yellow Honda Civic from clxfiles soon so that will be the body I customize.  I don\'t want to screw up right away so I\'m just going to ask you this:  Do you lower the body before you paint it or after?\r\n\r\nThanks for being so nice about this and all of your help so far.[/quote:df12a7045a]good question, you lower before you paint, this way if the car get\'s scratched while you\'re doing your lowering, it won\'t ruin your nice paintjob.\r\n\r\nThere is more than one way to lower so you got some work ahead of you, to find the way that\'s easiest for you.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(37578,'4a877306d1','Thanks.  That should should save a lot of time and effort, lol.'),(37579,'4a877306d1','Thanks.  That should should save a lot of time and effort, lol.'),(37867,'d66f4d69c8','The Skyline is black, with yellow side add ons or w.e, im not sure if its the whole body upgrade but there is quite a bit.\r\n\r\nit\'s condition, if your picky like me you\'d wanna touch it up with your own personality, but its not that bad at all, could actually make it look really good.\r\n\r\n350 sick is copper as you know, and its condition has been run before, not that bad...\r\n\r\nshow me an offer and its yours man!'),(37628,'7e65c78b4f','[quote:7e65c78b4f=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Please ship to the following address and not the address of the paypal account.\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\nBannister Land\r\nMartindales Road\r\nSt.Michael BB11115\r\nBARBADOS\r\n\r\nwhat is your paypal addy[/quote:7e65c78b4f]\r\n\r\nCool, i gotcha, BTW You sure that you got evo fets? I\'m pretty sure he was selling his 7317 fets he got off ausmicro?\r\n\r\n\r\nPaypal Addy:\r\n\r\nkgera1@tampabay.rr.com');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37007,'a594e3b791','[quote:a594e3b791=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Remove the items in bold,I would rather an 11T but that\'s not offered. Can I use the gears from the stage 2 kit with this alloy? Your update post was confusing. If I can please remove [b:a594e3b791][DXME1224T DELRIN MAIN GEAR (12T/24T) - 2PCS SET $3.50 $3.50 1][/b:a594e3b791] also.\r\nI want all the items in purple. \r\nI didn\'t really want to commit to this so early, but hey :-? [u:a594e3b791]I\'m in[/u:a594e3b791]. Please note that it would be VERY hard for me to ADD more money to this order. So if prices start going up, start dropping the &quot;non-essentials&quot; one-by-one. \r\n\r\nWith the bolded stuff removed I think it brings my total to:\r\n\r\nSub     $136.04\r\nTotal    $141.48\r\n\r\nDouble check that figure for me.[/quote:a594e3b791]\r\n\r\nThis is what I got now:\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Purple \r\nDXME100R	DELRIN REAR BALL DIFFERENTIAL - 1 COMPLETED SET	$10.08	1\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$7.74	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.54	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$7.74	1\r\nXME021	ALLOY FRONT KNUCKLE ARM - 1PR	$6.44	1\r\nXME022	ALLOY REAR KNUCKLE ARM -1 PR	$6.44	1\r\nXME028	ALLOY FRONT SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$7.90	1\r\nXME030	ALLOY REAR SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$5.14	1\r\nXME039F	ALLOY FRONT WHEEL SHAFT - 1PR	$2.54	1\r\nXME039R	ALLOY REAR Wheel SHAFT - 1PR 	$2.54	1\r\nXME039R/C	ALLOY REAR UNIVERSAL SWING SHAFT (CVD DESIGN) - 1PR	$13.80	2\r\nXME039R/4WD	ALLOY REAR Wheel SHAFT FOR 4WD - 1PR 	$2.54	1\r\nXME049/0	ALLOY STEERING PLATE - 1PC	$4.23	1\r\nXME055	ALLOY FRONT LOWER ARM - 1PR	$5.14	1\r\nXME056	ALLOY REAR LOWER ARM - 1PR	$5.14	1\r\nXME190R	ALLOY REAR DOG BONE (9.0MM) - 1PR	$3.25	2\r\nXME316F	ALLOY FRONT DAMPER (16MM) -1PR	$3.84	1\r\nXME316R	ALLOY REAR DAMPER (16MM) - 1PR	$3.84	1\r\nXME331R	ALLOY REAR SKID PLATE - 1PC	$2.28	1\r\nMZ002	ALLOY 2MM LOCK NUT SET  5PCS	$3.80	1\r\n\r\nSub	$131.87	\r\nS&amp;H 4%	$5.27	\r\nTotal	$137.14	\r\n\r\nThe stock gears should work with the Delrin Diffs.  You may want to examine the Stock gears though and make sure they are smooth and free of any defects.  \r\n\r\nRight now if you lock in this price before the 30th you will get the parts at these prices.  I plan on placing this order Feb 1st if O have enough payments.  \r\n\r\nThe way GPM works for me.   I place the order, GPM tells me how much including shipping, I send them that amount and in less than a month if the parts were in stock I get them.\r\n\r\nMy paypal is cjellis@yahoo.com'),(35112,'2e5d3b2c4c','[quote:2e5d3b2c4c=\"arfin\"]Hey man, well i want to bid on this http://cgi.ebay.com/Micro-RC-Collection-Bit-Char-g-Microsizer-Many-Parts_W0QQitemZ6011299770QQcategoryZ44025QQssPageNameZWDVWQQrdZ1QQcmdZViewItem\r\n\r\nBUT, he forgot to let Canadians bid on it, so Ebay won\'t let me. So, i\'m just sending the hook up to my homie.[/quote:2e5d3b2c4c]\r\n\r\nHey dude!\r\nThanks! Actually, I have lots! That\'s why I\'m sending you some stuffs! LOL\r\nYeah, sorry, I haven\'t been on for a while. Talk to you soon hopefully!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37719,'f8831e87bc','Can\'t afford the remotes right now. If you still have them next week, then no problem. I\'ll send the $22 for the chassis tomorrow.....thanks :)'),(36769,'190dbc5df1','What xmod stuff you have? Sorry for being selective but i really don\'t know what I want. What I want is to get rid of as much Bitstuff possible lol! \r\n\r\nLet me know what you got...\r\n\r\nPs...I think there is something wrong with my diff. One wheel spins to its full potential and the other hardly spins when i accelerate while holding the chassis. What could be the problem...and do you think I should throw the AWD set diff in the rear?\r\n\r\nps...give me a list of your xmod stuff ahah'),(35996,'0d51ad3c31','http://i20.photobucket.com/albums/b238/MafiaSam99/FirstBitPics014.jpg\r\n\r\nI am super-interested in the 57 chevy body and the red car in the right of this pic. I would also like a controller and a chassis. I am going to go sometime this week and see if i can score you a returned xmod and/or some parts.'),(37679,'f8a8bf70fa','I\'d give you twenty shipped......How much do you want for the controllers?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35712,'194548faad','I can\'t buy the material today :( The insurance company has to check my dad\'s car.\r\n\r\nSo maybe I\'ll put up pics and a vid on the weekend.\r\n\r\nThis is the other steering mod I forgot to add, this may not be needed tho\r\n[url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=5011&amp;highlight=slop]Knuckle slop fix[/url] I used the ink tube from a cheap bic pen, this weakens the knuckle but gives the steering more throw. You can just use heatshrink.\r\n\r\nOh, and GPM knuckles are important too. When the bottom screw starts dropping out, you\'ll wish you had replaced it with some alloy. I don\'t have that problem, I\'m currenly running the blue springs upfront, these keep me jacked up off the ground. But I may switch to softer springs in my drift quest.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(35131,'4b30e4addc','hey Clint, I was just wondering if you would be up for writing a quite little review for the evo msofets on the review section in the ausmicro.com shop.  you don\'t have to do it, I would appreciate it if you could though man.  No rush.\r\n\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.'),(35139,'dc47282374','i think $70 is kinda low for all this stuff (remember it\'s all new).  while it would be nice to get some cash for this stuff that\'s just sitting in boxes, i don\'t want to take that big a hit for it.  i\'ve got two kids that may be able to make use of it in a few years.\r\n \r\n\r\n[quote:dc47282374=\"Maxximum Attack\"]This is the final list of what I want according to what you say you have.\r\n\r\nSkyline kit\r\nDogbones x 2 \r\nDual Link Tie Rod Set \r\nBall Diff Set\r\nGPM Front Spring Damper (Purple) \r\nGPM 1pc Rear Oil Damper (Purple) \r\nAll the foams, rims and rubber tires you have.\r\n\r\n$70 shipped (US) to take all that old stuff off your hands. \r\n\r\nMaxx[/quote:dc47282374]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35141,'18f393929f','[quote:18f393929f=\"hue35\"]Dude, send me your address and I\'ll mail you a clean dupe from my Atomic Bitchwax disc. Their first disc kicks all kinds of ass... you\'ll dig it. I\'m trying to download the Desert Sessions suff (1-10) right now. Stoner rock rules... duh. :-o \r\n\r\nI\'ll also dupe you the best of the Kyuss records, Blues for the Red Sun. \r\n\r\nHave you heard any Alabama Thunderpussy? They also kick ass... a little more scary, in a trailer park meth kinda way, but they rock... it\'s southern and greasy.\r\n\r\nlater...\r\n\r\nedit: Oh yeah, have you heard any Fu Manchu? They\'re like the kings of stoner rock, in an LA kind of way... like a hard hittin\', rawk version of the chili peppers. No funk, just chunk.\r\n\r\nanother edit: (I wrote this last night, then thought I\'d listen to some of that Desert Sessions stuff before I sent it) Anyway, the Kyuss, Monster Magnet and Atomic Bitchwax stuff is probably a little less sprawling and a bit harder... another band that came to mind was Masters of Reality. They\'re also real cool. \r\n\r\nif you want i can just load up a disc or two with AAC files (mp4). The iTunes app will play those, but I don\'t know what else. If you have/use iTunes player, the AAC\'s are considerably better sounding when comparing at the same bit rate. All my stuff is ripped as 192 kbps AAC\'s.[/quote:18f393929f]\r\n\r\n\r\nMike Smalley Jr.\r\n3918 Inland Ave.\r\nWest Mifflin, Pa  15122\r\n\r\nI use iTunes most of the time.  The only other time I use anything else is when iTunes won\'t play it. :-o \r\n\r\nNever heard of any of those other bands. (Fu Man Chu does ring a bell)  I live a sheltered music life.  I usually find stuff after its been around awhile.  Usually thru friends.  Always late, unless I see them at a big festival tour, or something.\r\n\r\n :rockon: \r\n\r\nLet me know if you get all the sessions.  I think I said there are 12, there\'s only 10.  My mistake.'),(35142,'0d4edbc510','It\'s no problem, that\'s all in negotiating.\r\n\r\nOk here\'s the final list, so you can reply with your name and addy so I can send the MO to you.\r\n\r\nList:\r\nSkyline kit\r\nBall diff\r\n\r\nCan I get those for $70? I\'d like to quickly make this deal before the Xmas rush (if it hasn\'t started).\r\nIf the above stuff is cool, pm me your addy.\r\n\r\nThanx guy\r\nMaxx');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36783,'680be9419e','Here you go!  Congrats.  Now I gotta change my sig.\r\n\r\n[img:680be9419e]http://www.operationgoldstar.org/images/star.gif[/img:680be9419e]'),(35148,'a51036b06c','I have a corupted file or two on my version too. :-( \r\n\r\nWhere did you get it?  Torrent or P2P?  I might have gotten the same thing.  I got mine from Mini-Nova I think.  The link I put up is on TorrentSpy.  \r\n\r\nWhats the odds of it being a different or the same torrent? :???:  Might try it.\r\n\r\nI tried Ziping it to send to Chrome and it won\'t do it because of the coruption.  I\'m sending him a data disc.\r\n \r\n\r\nThere are a couple of the Sessions songs that made it onto a couple of QOTSA discs.'),(36780,'8a2ccf1d9f','Sounds good thanks for the tips man...\r\n\r\nI am off to school now when I get back i will check the msg for an update.\r\n\r\nTake care'),(35226,'d318f8bac5','Hey MG, i\'m downloadin\' the demo right now, so when i get back from work it sould be done, and we can play! Take care, i\'ll be on later.'),(36549,'a435acac92','I\'ve made a boo boo. I knew I was going to miss something. I left out the TX in a drunken frenzy, but I will send it out ASAP. I\'m sorry about that man.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37442,'d355eba1af','the steering is a little sluggish, i put it down to the weakness of the iwaver steering curcuit.\r\nyou\'ll notice all those servos have the motors swapped out, from memory the bpnsx still has a stock servo motor. try using a stock (red) zz motor instead.\r\n\r\nanother reason for the sluggishness is the front springs press hard on the knuckles making them harder to turn, press on the front shocks then twiddle the steering. you\'ll probably find it a bit snappier. this means when it\'s on the ground and running the steering works better due to the suspension sag.\r\n\r\ni\'m pretty sure there\'s no broken parts, it\'s just the combination of the suspension, weak curcuit and weak motor. softer springs and a better servo motor is what i\'d try :-o \r\n\r\nany other problems or questions, just gimme a yell :-)'),(37035,'f934edf178','well what i really need is the front clip of the skyline'),(36434,'61368b6b7b','Yeah, you can still add either a FET stack or a turbo like Spider or Nelly onto the Pro board later on.\r\n\r\nWhat kind of track do you run on?  In a club?  With friends?  A Lap counter?  RCP?  LMK and I can better help you.\r\n\r\nThanks');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36435,'3a99d09dc2','Check my post in the Track section\r\n\r\nSo..We\'re making a Track...\r\n\r\nThat is the one!!!\r\n\r\nMy buddy who is just about to buy an Iwaver would like to know...\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n&quot;if i can install a novak esc and a novak receiver for micro cars in place of the one it has, and if i can replace the standard iwaver servo with a Hitec HS-81&quot;'),(37723,'14f9f0b9bc','Just let me know, and what ever your offer is that\'s cool...'),(37724,'f6a2671cfe','Hey man I haven\'t received anything on these.  Are you still interested?  Have you sent a MO?  If so, let me know and I\'ll look out extra hard for it.  If not but you still want the bods, let me know your address and I\'ll send one over to you.  I think I\'m gonna keep the other, but the one I send you can have for free.  Don\'t expect me to use anything but regular mail though.  lol.  But if you already sent a MO, I\'ll send you both.'),(35217,'77239ebf67','Just got home and checked your reply. \r\n\r\nThanks alot man, see what you can do any little thing is better than a shitty deal from some store here.\r\n\r\nAny ways its sleep time for me. \r\n\r\nLater...');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35219,'b279b48b04','.........This transaction has taken too long. I\'m buying an xmod when they go on sale. Plus I\'m buying a number of them to sell here on the island.\r\n\r\nSorry for the inconvenience, should\'ve struck while the iron was still hot\r\nNo hard feelings? Cuz I may want your foams very early in the new year.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(35224,'565da6d02f','Okay, that\'s fine.\r\n\r\nI will be at the below address from around December 12th to Janurary 9.  Other than those dates, I will be at the address I gave you with my paypal payment.  Thanks again man.\r\n\r\nSean Dill\r\n301 Dominic Drive\r\nScott Depot WV 25560 \r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(37851,'1039778b9c','[quote:1039778b9c=\"Maxximum Attack\"]you never told me if the Fets from your friend were upgrade fets. And wheather I should try a stack and if it would make a difference.[/quote:1039778b9c]\r\n\r\nSorry about that bro i thought i mentioned it before.\r\n\r\nYes the ausmicro fet\'s are the best of the best, i think they are 7 amp fet\'s so doing a 3x2 stack or similar would basically give you a huge range of motor selection.\r\n\r\nCheck out ripper7racing under the mini-z section a couple of pages back Ph2t did a write up of the fets and the install onto a IW board.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37885,'f68808361b','hiya brudda! stuff arrived today just as good as it left you :-o \r\nthanks a bunch for the extras, you\'re a legend! :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37462,'682c250224','hmmm, i\'m stumped! it was definately working when i had it, slow steering but working.\r\nsounds like there could be some binding in the steering somewhere. check it over and as a last resort pull the servo apart and check it out.\r\ni\'d try a different servo motor too.\r\n\r\nsee how you go with that and lemme know if it works. :-o'),(35215,'25b4710086','I\'m sorry CJ, I interpreted on my own that the parts would be shipping sometme early December, so I sent my school address.  Since I saw your post about the shipment on Dec. 15th, I\'m going to need the parts shipped home.\r\n\r\nSean Dill\r\n301 Dominic Drive\r\nScott Depot, WV 25560\r\n\r\nIf you\'d like to refuse payment and have me send it again with the other address, that\'s fine too.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(37499,'de45723866','holy crap! that could explain it! :lol: \r\n\r\nmakes me wonder if that\'s why the steering was weak for me!\r\n\r\ni used to run it on a 1:10 scale track so the shorter travel, slower responding steering didn\'t matter so much.\r\n\r\nif i was to try for more throw with the servo i\'d get a resistor with a value around 5kohm (4.7kohm is more common, it\'s good enough). you want to solder it between the 2 servo pot wires. you can do that on the pot or on the pcb. whenever i\'ve done it i\'ve used a surface mount resistor and soldered it on the pcb, across the 2 servo pot tabs.\r\n\r\nwhat this does is electronically fool the servo into moving more than it thinks it is.\r\nyou\'ll probably find it\'s too much throw and will need to adjust the steering sensitivity accordingly.\r\n\r\nonce you swap out the motor and add the resistor i think we might have it worked out.\r\ni\'d personally swap the motor first and see how it reacts before adding the resistor when you add the mr01 pcb. the kyosho pcb has a much stronger steering curcuit.\r\n\r\nkeep me posted :-)'),(36088,'3bb49d5082','I forgot. The nelly deluxe got fried. I wasn\'t sure if you knew that.\r\n\r\nMake me an offer if you still want it. It will include the new parts that will be here in a few days.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35399,'b93d4f54fa','Here is the list of EVO parts. \r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	PRICE	Cost	Silver	Green\r\nDXME009T	DELRIN MOTOR GEAR (9T) - 1PC	$1.90	$2.47	1	1\r\nDXME100R	DELRIN REAR BALL DIFFERENTIAL - 1 COMPLETED SET	15.50   	$0.00		0\r\nDXME1224T	DELRIN MAIN GEAR (12T/24T) - 2PCS SET	3.50   	$0.00		\r\nXME018A	ALLOY MOTOR HEAT SINK - 1PC	3.50   	$4.55	1	1\r\nXME021	ALLOY FRONT KNUCKLE ARM - 1PR	9.90   	$6.44		1\r\nXME022	ALLOY REAR KNUCKLE ARM -1 PR	9.90   	$6.44		1\r\nXME028	ALLOY FRONT SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	7.50   	$4.88		1\r\nXME030	ALLOY REAR SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	7.50   	$4.88		1\r\nXME032	ALLOY MAIN GEAR PROTECTOR - 1PC	3.90   	$2.54		1\r\nXME039F	ALLOY FRONT WHEEL SHAFT - 1PR	3.90   	$5.07	1	1\r\nXME039R	ALLOY REAR Wheel SHAFT - 1PR 	3.90   	$5.07	1	1\r\nXME047	ALLOY PROTECTOR FOR FRONT STEERING PLATE - 1PC 	3.90   	$2.54		1\r\nXME049/0	ALLOY STEERING PLATE - 1PC	6.50   	$4.23		1\r\nXME055	ALLOY FRONT LOWER ARM - 1PR	6.90   	$4.49		1\r\nXME056	ALLOY REAR LOWER ARM - 1PR	6.90   	$4.49		1\r\nXME190R	ALLOY REAR DOG BONE (9.0MM) - 1PR	2.50   	$3.25		2\r\nXME303	ALLOY BATTERY HEAT SINK MOUNT - 1PC	7.90   	$10.27	1	1\r\nXME316F	ALLOY FRONT DAMPER (16MM) -1PR	5.90   	$3.84		1\r\nXME316R	ALLOY REAR DAMPER (16MM) - 1PR	5.90   	$3.84		1\r\nXME330LAN	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR LANCER) - 1PC	5.90   	$0.00		0\r\nXME330MUS	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR MUSTANG) - 1PC	5.90   	$0.00		0\r\nXME331R	ALLOY REAR SKID PLATE - 1PC	3.50   	$2.28		1\r\nDXET009T	DELRIN MOTOR GEAR (9T) - 1PC	$1.90	$0.00	0	\r\nDXET100R	DELRIN REAR BALL DIFFERENTIAL - 1 COMPLETED SET	14.50   	$0.00	 	\r\nDXET1224T	DELRIN MAIN GEAR (12T/24T) - 2PCS SET	3.50   	$0.00		\r\nXET018A	ALLOY MOTOR HEAT SINK - 1PC	$3.50	$0.00	0	\r\nXET021	ALLOY FRONT KNUCKLE ARM - 1PR	$9.90	$6.44	1	\r\nXET022	ALLOY REAR KNUCKLE ARM -1 PR	$9.90	$6.44	1	\r\nXET028	ALLOY FRONT SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$7.50	$7.50	1	\r\nXET030	ALLOY REAR SHOCK TOWER - 1PC	$7.50	$7.50	1	\r\nXET032	ALLOY MAIN GEAR PROTECTOR - 1PC	$4.50	$2.93	1	\r\nXET039F	ALLOY FRONT WHEEL SHAFT - 1PR	$3.90	$0.00	 	\r\nXET039R	ALLOY REAR Wheel SHAFT - 1PR 	$3.90	$0.00	 	\r\nXET047	ALLOY PROTECTOR FOR FRONT STEERING PLATE - 1PC	$3.90	$2.54	1	\r\nXET049	ALLOY STEERING PLATE - 1PC	$6.50	$0.00	0	\r\nXET055	ALLOY FRONT LOWER ARM - 1PR	$6.90	$4.49	1	\r\nXET056	ALLOY REAR LOWER ARM - 1PR	$6.90	$4.49	1	\r\nXET114R	ALLOY REAR DOG BONE (14MM) - 1PR	2.90   	$3.77	2	\r\nXET303	ALLOY BATTERY HEAT SINK MOUNT - 1PC	$7.50	$0.00	0	\r\nXET322F	ALLOY FRONT DAMPER (22MM) -1PR	$5.90	$3.84	1	\r\nXET322R	ALLOY REAR DAMPER (22MM) - 1PR	$5.90	$3.84	1	\r\nXET330FORD	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR TRUCKIN) - 1PC	$6.90	$0.00	0	\r\nXET330HUM	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR HUMMER) - 1PC	$5.90	$0.00	0	\r\nXET331F	ALLOY FRONT SKID PLATE - 1PC	$3.90	$2.54	1	\r\n		Sub	$137.79		\r\n		Rouund	$138.00		\r\n\r\nYou will notice that you have 2 pairs of each Dog bone and just one each axles.  Also the front clips have been removed. They will be added to the Gear box GB.  Also so I will not have to ask you for any more money the Steering arm for the truck has been removed.  With some changes to prices Some truck people pulled out so Steering plate and shock towers are not at 35% any more.  :sad: \r\n\r\nThe ORG parts are on the way to you with a surprise.  Let me know if the Gold front arms work and are made right.\r\n\r\nSince I am taking some peoples DIFF orders on this if you want to add diffs let me know.  They run $15 each.'),(35860,'822e8c0ae4','MAN I GOT BAD NEWSSSSS!!!!!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nJust playin...I sent the stuff this morning, 7-10 days its yours my friend. \r\n\r\nTake good care of them tell me when you send your stuff k?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35861,'8e9bd3d089','Hey dude, those are some real cheap pullbacks I\'ve had forever (got those during preschool for some fund rasing thing they were doing, and to put that in perspective I got an Associate\'s degree 2 years ago).  Fully plastic except for the axles, springs, and pivots.  Just under 1.5 Bit Char-G long.  From the quality I\'d guess China or Taiwan.  No brand stamps anywhere, and if they had stickers on the bottom they\'re LONG gone.\r\n\r\nI\'ll try and see if I can find anything similar that can be ordered.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nfrizzen'),(35696,'a7722b62f8','I have to ask... You mentioned something about the brushless CD motors a while ago.\r\n\r\nWould you have an idea where to buy the neo mags needed for a project like that? I have accrued a large collection of brushless motors. I\'ve re-wound several of those stators for practice. But now comes the completion time.. I need some flat neo magnets to fit. Any ideas?'),(37554,'c8526f9a96','Well, my dad lives in White Plains.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36847,'e0f6d6653a','Glad to here you like the Epoch.\r\n\r\nNo preference what so ever on the painting, I can make decals for the lights or you can paint them whatever you think will look the best.\r\n\r\nAll I meant was that you can keep any of the bodies you like except for the 1/2x Willies coupe, I need it for a little roadster project, and that out of all of them it was the one I was hoping would turn out clean.\r\n\r\nCheers\r\nPhilip'),(35366,'e1b6110f5e','Hey Hachi\r\n\r\nI hear you just started into the 1:28 scale.\r\n\r\nI did some research but I am still confused of which I should buy. An Xmod or Mini Z. I was looking at a MR-02 Mini Z or MR-015, and an Xmod Evolution chassis. \r\n\r\nIf you get a chance could you give me a little review of the two...or as a beginner tell me what might be a good route to follow!\r\n\r\nThanks'),(35374,'c8280eedaa','Thanks   :cool: \r\n\r\nSomething new to work too.   :rockon:  \r\n\r\nHaven\'t been getting much new music lately.  Been sorta bored, except for a few new tunes.\r\n\r\n...and I keep grabbing the same old cd\'s from the collection. :-?  :lol:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(35243,'23bba3e99d','[quote:23bba3e99d=\"mikirgra\"]The Trueno sets are yours. Yep, you bought the Lupin set from me too. That was another set I had bought from Bithed. JD probably didn\'t tell you about the Trueno set because she (the JD I deal with is female, but I think she likes to be a little private about that) was holding it for me, FOREVER. She\'s really really cool. My all time fav to deal with.\r\n\r\nLook DT, [b:23bba3e99d]I got more stuff that I will have to unload soon[/b:23bba3e99d], but most of it is dups, and you probably already have it. Regardless, I\'m a fan, so I will give you first shot at those items too once I get around to sorting my crap and deciding what I can and can\'t live w/o.\r\n\r\nI gotta start my commute home, but I\'ll get back with you on Monday if not sooner about the Trueno sets.\r\n\r\nThanks man.[/quote:23bba3e99d]\r\n\r\n[size=24:23bba3e99d][b:23bba3e99d]Don\'t Forget A Pimp [/b:23bba3e99d][/size:23bba3e99d] :cool:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36455,'1f134fd27f','give me yo email address and I\'ll forward the email they sent, still have it!'),(36456,'09d413b5a2','[quote:09d413b5a2=\"DarkTari\"]give me yo email address and I\'ll forward the email they sent, still have it![/quote:09d413b5a2]\r\n\r\n\r\nsg219@sg219.com'),(37411,'3aa7c5b57a','[quote:3aa7c5b57a=\"steelwoolghandi\"][quote:3aa7c5b57a=\"sg219\"]Bird has two sets he\'s willing to trade.  I\'m going over there tonight to pick them up.\r\n\r\nHe was wondering about some of the decals like you sent me.  He\'s not picky.  He said to be creative when trading.  (catch my drift?) :wink: \r\n\r\nI\'ll send them out sometime in the next couple of days. :-o[/quote:3aa7c5b57a]\r\n\r\n\r\nwill do man do you want me to send my creativity to you or to bird? just let me know. I am on the road right now (selling) but when I get back will send some creativity out!\r\n\r\nthanks man!\r\n\r\nAaron[/quote:3aa7c5b57a]\r\n\r\nYou can send it to me.  \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\n\r\nMike Smalley Jr.\r\n3918 Inland Ave.\r\nWest Mifflin, Pa 15122'),(35246,'0113a88a84','You know, since I first made my first fast bit, I wanted lexan bodies. I\'ve been planning something like what Hachi has done for long time now. My only hang up was the same as you, no pics! So now I\'m figuring, I know what a funny car basically looks like, and some of those others sound apealing as drag cars also, so that makes it worth while to order, then at $2.50 a piece its not such a risk to throw in the Porshe GT car, which I\'m afraid is just a wedge shaped car like most the others. \r\n\r\nI\'m hoping the funny cars are longer so I can stretch the chassis more. A funny car with like 3 SE cells (or 6 little ones depending how you look at it), and a lexan body would be too sick, maybe not even feasable, so I gotta try it. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36905,'6cd0d900a8','Man I knew Namuna would like this post but God Damn!  Chicken Nuggets !!!!  :lol: \r\nHe\'s gonna blow this mutha UP !!!!  Watch....'),(37590,'ac65089bda','Cabo I would like to submit one of my own songs I have created. I wanted you to review it and give me the ok to perhaps put it on the bitPimps radio. I would like others to get a taste of my music. \r\n\r\n    I will propose music that comes from an underground house style of music. If this is cool please pm me back and we could figure out how to get the song to you. I have many, but would like to send em out one by one and get some critique on them. \r\n\r\ni figure bitpimps is a good chance to get some opinions on my stuff considering i am taking a Disk Jockey course and it has become one of my other hobbies.\r\n\r\nThanks for your time...'),(36907,'938d17f4a7','hey mang, could ya gimmie a call tonight and give me a hand with iframes stuff. \r\n\r\nBasically I want to have images on the left and when you click the images on the left an embedded media player on the right plays the video without opening a new page etc.\r\n\r\nAlso do you have any good scripts for a photo gallery. I wanna have a page come up with 8 thumbnails on the top and when you click a thumb it comes up 640x480 underneath the thumbs. each thumb you click will then appear in the window below and replace the current 640x480 image.?\r\n\r\nMake sense? I tried the iframes thingy and between Daniel and I we cann get it to work right. Same wiuth some of the photo viewers we have tried. I got one to work but not very well. I have tried programs like magic gallery but cannot find a crack for the program and all images are watermarked. I found a work around for the watermark but it will take forever to resize and copy and paste 200+ images.\r\n\r\nThanks mang! YOU RULE!'),(35256,'1159875af8','No chance I\'ll forget you man. Just haven\'t had a chance yet. Sorry about that. Don\'t worry though. I still got \'em, and I\'m still gonna sell them to you. The long weekend ahead might be my best chance to get them out of the closet, take some pics, and finalize this deal with you. We\'ll git er done, fer sure. Later.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35257,'040ffa9eda','yeah, sorry about dragging my feet.  i\'m always kinda wary/hesitant about selling stuff on the boards (been burned a few times).  not knowing you too well and the out of country shipping didn\'t help things either.  i probably shouldn\'t have mentioned the things in the first place.'),(35258,'67feac1f7c','Not to worry, you can ask crazydave. He would vouch for me  :-o . yeah and I know about getting burned (backdrift). It\'s no problem tho, i took that money that i was using to build a new micro , and invested it into 8 Xmods. I\'m gunna sell them here for US$88. I love Xmas  :smile:  :smile: \r\nThey haven\'t reached here yet, I\'m probly the only person that has one. but I\'ll change that. The neighbourhood kids will flock at such a good price  :-o . Selling the bodykits separate, one set (mild/wild) for 12bucks.\r\n\r\nIf i get everything sold, I will make $500+ profit  :smile: \r\nOff 8 cars!!!!!!!!!!!!\r\n\r\nI\'ll holla at you when I want the skyline kit again :-) I\'m almost sure I\'ll still want it in the new year. for now, I\'m broke. My dad has gone to the states with all my money :lol: \r\n\r\nMaxx'),(37632,'9365b1b968','I can make the payment now, I was just making sure of my purchase. What can i use the lipo pack on? Can I charge it with the cheapo chargers that come with lith pro kits?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35826,'c5f0f13b31','[quote:c5f0f13b31]Alright, I like your bearings, shaft, and the alloy stuff you just showed me \r\n\r\nYou still want the body, controller and chassis?[/quote:c5f0f13b31]\r\n\r\nOk include your bearings, your shaft, the alloy stuff please\r\n\r\nand in return\r\n\r\nSkyline Body, [b:c5f0f13b31]controller[/b:c5f0f13b31], and [u:c5f0f13b31][b:c5f0f13b31]2 [/b:c5f0f13b31][/u:c5f0f13b31][i:c5f0f13b31][b:c5f0f13b31]working chassis[/b:c5f0f13b31][/i:c5f0f13b31]?\r\n\r\nGood deal?'),(36944,'4772ce04c5','Nah, that wasn\'t me man.'),(36945,'e857d5e99d','whats your address?'),(36946,'fa402be9e0','Sean Dill\r\n406A Boreman South\r\nNorth High Street\r\nMorgantown, WV 26506\r\n\r\nWhat episodes do you have and what do I owe you for the hook up?\r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...'),(35465,'aa84ecdff9','Now you got a Test body...Pretty soon you earn a Test body team..lol The thing about 1/10th scale is that the tamiya bodies we love are like 50 bucks canadian, hpi is about 40 canadian...plus a can of tamiya paint, masking.......becomes tedious when u get all these dings here and there so we just let them sit hoping they look just as good as when they run on the road !'),(37147,'085865ed85','Oh, makes sense.  Sorry dude.  I thought somebody was just screwing with his avatar and name.  Makes sense.\r\n\r\nDamn, now I really want to see him come back.  \r\n\r\nAnd I also feel a little used. :-? \r\n\r\n :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37148,'d67160487b','[quote:d67160487b=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]And I also feel a little used. :-? \r\n\r\n :lol:[/quote:d67160487b]\r\n\r\nSorry dude... I think I may have gone a little too subtle, but if he comes back it\'ll be worth it. :-o'),(35475,'a974cae482','Your a master eh! I guess that\'s alot of the fun in RC. By the way would you be able to customize a Diablo for me? I got a yellow one but I want something different. Maybe some putty work, I don\'t have the skill yet, or small enough hands for that matter to try. But this was if your not busy or had no other projects in mind with regards to body work. Would you wanna work something out? \r\n\r\nIf you can\'t thats cool no worries. But what putty do you use? and when you paint over a bit thats already been painted. (example a yellow Diablo from the starter kit) do you just paint over it? Spray over? or Primer? whats a good tip?'),(35689,'8f6acae399','[quote:8f6acae399=\"Bryce\"]Ok.\r\nEnough of this shit,  i don\'t want to just have arguing, i want to have a serious chat here.\r\nI understand that you are tired of n00b\'s and shit coming in, asking stupid questions. Mine wern\'t stupid questions, I was just asking some decent questions for info, help, and to update on my upcoming project.\r\nI am wondering if you knowe of the name you guys have given your self, for being \"flamable\" towards n00bs, etc. You guys are know to be netherless rude and obnoxious. Why? I don\'t know. I always though these forums people have created were to spread idea,s tips, information, and HELP ONE ANOTHER. I don\'t see much of this, just threats, foul language, etc.\r\nMind you i disagree with PG forums, that bann you for saying \"shit\" , but the degree that I have witnessed from SOME of your members, admins, moderators, and what other people have told me about this forum.\r\n You have a great forum, very knowledgable people here, great mind, projects, creation.\r\nNow if I came in without proper punctuation( I try my best), asking completley gay question, I would be expected to be treated fairly(flamed a bit, told to use punctuation, and directed towards a rules page or something)\r\nEVEN though, I have punctuation, some good questions, and intense interest in these forum. I still was flamed, threatened to be stabbed with a pen(lol..) etc.\r\nI\'m hoping you guys could do something to resolve your beat/flame the new bitches theme, for something more civilized. Maybe you could get a better name, draw more interest, and have more good members in the end.\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nBryce[/quote:8f6acae399]\r\nI can admit that at times, our members can be rather harsh - but that\'s the way it\'s been since day 1. And as you can plainly see - that hasn\'t hurt us at all.\r\nThe bitPimps website has become a premeire micro r/c community.\r\nWe get new members pretty much daily, clearly, not all of them get run off.\r\n\r\nPersonally, yes, I thought your questions, spelling, puncuation, etc. were fine (as I\'m willing to bet others did as well). But that wasn\'t what got your ass in a sling here. It was your demanding attitude and your admitted laziness when it comes to searching for your answer.\r\n\r\nIf you felt you were treated un-fairly, you should\'ve contacted one of us via a PM on our website. Not visit another website and try to bad-mouth us.\r\n\r\nThe way we choose to run the website is really none of your business. You may not fully agree with how things work here, that\'s fine - that\'s your opinion. But if you would like to be a member of our community - we expect our members to obey the very few rules we do have.'),(37151,'83b2b1ff3e','No worries.  I shoulda noticed the post count on three at least.  It\'s all in good humor.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37152,'','whats up me and my friends have bought zip zaps mt and we found the supension artical and was wondering two things. One is where did u get the jeep body and have u herd about xmod. This my first time login on to the bitpimps web page so im not sure on how im gonna get this message.\r\nThanks \r\n\r\nSpanky :grin:'),(37155,'706d5be3b0','SWG I got the light kit that glows at the bottom of the car is that the one you need...i think it is like the &quot;glow masta kit&quot;'),(35479,'1de1cbf26e','Wow! Thank you so much. I understand you are busy so I don\'t expect you to rush. It is just I have alot of extra bodies around and I don\'t really touch the ones pre painted. So what exactly should I send to you?'),(37202,'22a4bc4b84','Yeah, that\'s me dude.  Hachi-Roku is Japanese for 86.  It\'s their nickname for the AE86 Trueno in Japan.  My &quot;Hachi-Ryoku&quot; username got banned over there forever and a day ago.'),(37203,'22a5260275','[quote:22a5260275=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Yeah, that\'s me dude.  Hachi-Roku is Japanese for 86.  It\'s their nickname for the AE86 Trueno in Japan.  My &quot;Hachi-Ryoku&quot; username got banned over there forever and a day ago.[/quote:22a5260275]\r\n\r\n\r\ngotcha, :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35483,'4d0e8d103c','Alright than. Diablo will be sent as soon as I get a chance. It will most likley be microsizer chassis. I would have sent you an empty Super Bit Char G chassis with no electronics just the frame or w.e but I might have to give that away unless you would rather work on that one?\r\n\r\nI\'m going to try and send it out by either today, tomorrow or Sunday. \r\n\r\nThanks again!'),(35489,'7f32658526','Do not feel bad! I don\'t want you to send the package until i\'m done with your Epoch. K here\'s the thing, the epoch i was going to send you will take to long, since it\'s in parts, so i\'m gonna send you one of my stock Epochs, After I 4-cell it for you, Can\'t wait MG!'),(35491,'7e57722b99','You been lookin for one of these?  I got an extra you can have, just send me yo address!\r\nI sent betty one a while ago along with some other shit cause I know he loves to make off-road bits. The body is the green one right under his Jeep (which I also sent him)\r\n[img:7e57722b99]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10012/wizzle1.JPG[/img:7e57722b99]'),(35528,'d5ef01722d','Hi mate!\r\n\r\nYou\'d think i woulda learnt by now, right?  I was testing my ford coupe out, rolled it and broke another funkin steering wire!\r\n\r\nI\'ve tried repairing the wire, and when that didn\'t work, i took it out and tried soldering in  a new one.  Still no luck.  \r\n\r\nI was wondering if i could ask you could take a look at it for me?  I\'ve got a spare zipzap lap timer i\'d be willing to trade you in return - i think i remember you said somewhere you\'d like to get your hands on one and i\'ve never used the thing.  If not i\'d also be willing to pay for your services.  :-o\r\n\r\nI was gonna cut my losses - but its the first car i\'ve really gone all out on and i\'ve already invested a lot of work into this bastard - to sacrifice it over a steering wire seems sad.  \r\n\r\ni don\'t think i\'ve fried the PCB - forward and reverse still work - i just can\'t get the steering repair to work. im sure my 20w iron isnt helping situations\r\n\r\nI know its a busy and shitty time of year tho, so i can understand if you don\'t have the time to spare.  At this point i don\'t care if i make the deadline for the blowout - i\'d just love to be able to get this thing going again at some point.\r\n\r\nThanks again mate, don\'t mean to be a PITA.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\n\r\nMik aka 45tr0');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35530,'04597b515d','I was out using the snowblower tonight, my dad walks back with the mail and says \"hey, what\'d you get from a DarkTari Racing?\"  Wow, it\'s here already!   \r\n\r\nThen I got in here and opened it up,  :eek:  God damn, when you give a hook up, you REALLY give a hookup!!!   A new in box chassis, a Lan Evo, a tuneup set, a a 3.0 Bitracer motor, a body I can\'t quite identify that\'s skyline-ish (help?), and the jeepy body I asked about.  Many thanks, and I definately owe you VERY big man.  If there\'s something you ever need, let me know.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if you want this pimping handout kept on the downlow or if it\'ll be cool to talk about on board.'),(35531,'4963e52f2b','[quote:4963e52f2b=\"frizzen\"]I was out using the snowblower tonight, my dad walks back with the mail and says \"hey, what\'d you get from a DarkTari Racing?\"  Wow, it\'s here already!   \r\n\r\nThen I got in here and opened it up,  :eek:  God damn, when you give a hook up, you REALLY give a hookup!!!   A new in box chassis, a Lan Evo, a tuneup set, a a 3.0 Bitracer motor, a body I can\'t quite identify that\'s skyline-ish (help?), and the jeepy body I asked about.  Many thanks, and I definately owe you VERY big man.  If there\'s something you ever need, let me know.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if you want this pimping handout kept on the downlow or if it\'ll be cool to talk about on board.[/quote:4963e52f2b]\r\n\r\nNo Problem Pimp !  You can take it to Da Boards if you want, It\'s All Good  :cool: \r\n\r\nThe Body you can\'t identify is another Micro Speed body.  I find those bodies look real nice with a lil modding. They take some modding to fit bit chassis......\r\nCut &amp; filed the old rear wing and fitted a larger one, did a full ground effects kit and lowered:\r\n[img:4963e52f2b]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10005/MidBlu.jpg[/img:4963e52f2b]'),(37678,'445bc75d49','Just the chassis no controllers?\r\n\r\nnot sure what is reasonable thats why i left the offers open, just hoping to be happy for what i let the loose for.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37849,'bda757953f','you never told me if the Fets from your friend were upgrade fets. And wheather I should try a stack and if it would make a difference.'),(37223,'9a1eb1d3de','Sent!'),(35894,'d59a88be0b','Thanks please let me know on the tutorial update...\r\n\r\nand also when you ship the stuff! \r\n\r\nWhat can I do to my original Xmod to keep up with a stock MR-02...\r\n\r\nI don\'t want to dump all kinds of money into the chassis but just enough to suprise all those MR-02 users.'),(36320,'ddccc18d04','well that just blew my mind!\r\n\r\nI\'ve been trippin around at a dance festival all weekend, covered in mud and higher than Edmund Hilary, and i come home to find a placing waiting for me in the blowout!  What a trip!\r\n\r\nI never woulda thunk it.\r\n\r\nThanks for having us all around Cabo - this is one fine place you\'ve got here.  Its my home on them internets. \r\n\r\nAnyways, anough of my drug induced warm-n-fuzzball sentiment! Now to collect my shiat!\r\n\r\nMy postal address is:\r\n\r\nMichael Frawley \r\nPO BOX 2010\r\nTOOWONG QLD 4066\r\nAUSTRALIA\r\n\r\nThanks again for making this whole she-bang possible cabo.  you rock!'),(37777,'9910ae6fba','PH2T,\r\n\r\nYou know me from xmodrc(91LudeSiT). I had a little incendent with my \r\nMZM, I managed to burn a stack of 4x2 7389s. However I burned them \r\nright, LOL, all the legs were gone and they melted the chassis.  To the \r\npoint, I wanna put an evo nelly in it and was wondering if you could \r\nstill get them with the motor block so you dont have to bust out the \r\nsoldering iron to change the motor. Oh and I hope your back is feeling \r\nbetter!\r\n\r\nRegards\r\nAlex');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37677,'04d0bbcb6b','I don\'t remember if I told you or not but that deal with Skylinekid fell through so most everything in my list is available except the Jeep body and the yellow Civic.  Oh yeah, someone wanted me to hold the 2 yellow SE RX-7s.  He wants to do an Initial-D thing. \r\n\r\nSo whatever you want on my list.  Send me your address also so I can send them off t you.\r\n\r\nThanks'),(35717,'a7722b62f8','I have to ask... You mentioned something about the brushless CD motors a while ago.\r\n\r\nWould you have an idea where to buy the neo mags needed for a project like that? I have accrued a large collection of brushless motors. I\'ve re-wound several of those stators for practice. But now comes the completion time.. I need some flat neo magnets to fit. Any ideas?'),(35718,'23d88b6917','Not really.  The only thing I could really think to do is take them apart and look for neo magnets.  Or try a parts/component distributor like digi-key.  \r\n\r\nOther than that, you could try looking for more info on small scale indoor flyer forums.  The idea originally started with them.  They\'re using them in their little foam airplanes.  I\'ve seen these planes used for tooling around inside an indoor basketball court and also on foam dog-fighting planes.  They\'re cheap foam airplanes with a ribbon trailing from the end.  The idea is to cut the opponents ribbon off with your prop.  The motor was ripped off old computer hard drive.  That way, if you accidently get your ass cut to shreds, then you were only out a few bucks.  Most of the time you could be put back together with glue and any broken wires would just get soldered.\r\n\r\nHope this info helps.'),(37241,'9df2262355','I was thinking about something down those lines, but this is gonna make him say &quot;?????????, wha????&quot;.  It will take him a few seconds to put it all together.  He might not even be able to put it all together.  That would really kill me.\r\n\r\nIt\'s like an intellectual kick in the junk.  I couldn\'t resist.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37242,'b188e2eb57',':-o'),(37672,'45a7f69d4b','I picked up my gandinis from Ausmicro.  I didn\'t do a tremendous amount of looking, so you might find them somewhere else.  I also went ahead and got the other parts from them as well since I was already getting like $45 worth of tires at the time.  But, if you let him know that you\'re a regular at Bit-Pimps he\'ll throw in extra stuff.  I probably got an extra $30 of extras that he just threw in with the order.  Don\'t know if he\'ll do that every time but he may.  It also might help if you tell him I sent you.  Tell him you know me by name &quot;Bob Wilson&quot; as well as my username.  The other sources I\'ve been using are Toyeast, Hobby link Japan and RCMart.  All of those are in Asia, so you\'ll be spending a little extra on the shipping.  \r\n\r\nThis place seemed pretty cool.  I used him once.  Good dealer and decent prices. [url]http://www.microracers24.com/en-us/button.html[/url]  He ships quickly too.  It looks like an overseas site, but he has a distributor in the States.\r\n\r\nIf you find Gandinis somewhere else for much cheaper let me know.\r\n\r\nAs far as the Iwaver ball diff, you shouldn\'t be spending any more than $20 for one.  If they have it for a good price and you\'re OK with the shipping, then I say go for it.  You may want to reference the &quot;Vouch for a pimp, or throw him under the bus&quot; section of this forum in the contests/polls/surveys area.   [url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewforum.php?f=27[/url]'),(36659,'b72b8e4666','When you bought those 103 capacitors off ebay from the link in ph2t\'s thread.\r\n\r\nDid it come with all 3 pictured or ??\r\n\r\nAlso which ones would i use?\r\n\r\nI assume the blue one from ph2t\'s motor pictures.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35881,'c28acfbeb0','Hey,\r\n\r\nWas it you that I was just racing on Mariokart?\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(35887,'e80a502406','57 Chevy pink/purple with silver stripe \r\n\r\nI want this and I have pay pal...how much? Just interested for now...thanks'),(37036,'f934edf178','well what i really need is the front clip of the skyline'),(37037,'d89bb1e415','I see...Are all the clips for the original xmods different?'),(35728,'8b72cd8eb9','[quote:8b72cd8eb9=\"DarkTari\"][quote:8b72cd8eb9=\"JdmHatchback\"][quote:8b72cd8eb9=\"DarkTari\"]Hi! I have a bunch of microsizers bodies sets NIB $2ea \r\n[b:8b72cd8eb9]Specifics ?[/b:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\nPerfection Beetle bodies NIP $1ea \r\nPerfection Lambo or Ferrari bodies NIP $1ea \r\n[b:8b72cd8eb9]Cool ?[/b:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\nNeed any sets? \r\n\r\nGot Perfection Lambo/Ferrari sets $10ea \r\n[b:8b72cd8eb9]Intrerrested! Colors? s/h?[/b:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\nLxx Auto Modellista sets $10ea \r\nTomy BitCharG sets $15-$20 ea. \r\n\r\nAny interest in IWaver stuff? I\'ll be focusing more on Iwavers/ Mini z and selling the remainder of my New Micro RC stuff. \r\n[b:8b72cd8eb9]Is it too much trouble to send a detailed list of Micro RC stuff for sale?  Got any pics?[/b:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\nLet me know if interested in anything. Happy Holidays!\r\n[b:8b72cd8eb9]Thanx Pimp!  Same to you ![/b:8b72cd8eb9][/quote:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\n\r\nHere\'s a list of what I can remember off hand:\r\n\r\nmicrosizers body sets - supra, 350z, skyline, celica, I have a few other styles but its not coming to me at the moment. \r\n\r\nPerfection beetle bodies - colors - white, blue, green, black, gun metal, bronze, light green, silver, red, a few other colors but I know there were 11-12 different colors for the beetle bodies.\r\n\r\nPerfection lamborghini / Ferrari - red, white, black, silver\r\n\r\nThe Perfection Lambo/Ferrari sets comes with a different color lambo and ferrari body (either red, white, black, silver) \r\n\r\nAlso got Lxx VW Beetle sets with working headlights - $10ea. \r\n\r\nI might have a few 200mah batteries, 3.8 motors. \r\n\r\nFor the Tomy sets - silver s2000, black bB, Toyota Celica (not sure if its black or silver), Subaru WRX white, Nissan Gloria - $15ea ( i have more but cant remember)\r\n\r\nIm not sure on s&amp;h yet but if you decide to buy alot we can work something out. Did you need anything before xmas? Do you have an email address where I can send you some pics?\r\n\r\nThanks![/quote:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\nXmas has me tied up, still interrested!  Do you have any rare Bits?\r\n\r\nSend all Pics to :   DarkTari@msn.com\r\n\r\nThanx Again  :-)[/quote:8b72cd8eb9]\r\n\r\nNo problem, hope you had a great xmas. I\'ll get pics out to you within the next few days or after new years at the latest. Happy New Year!\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJdm'),(37591,'57978c4709','[quote:57978c4709=\"MafiaS\"]Cabo I would like to submit one of my own songs I have created. I wanted you to review it and give me the ok to perhaps put it on the bitPimps radio. I would like others to get a taste of my music. \r\n\r\n    I will propose music that comes from an underground house style of music. If this is cool please pm me back and we could figure out how to get the song to you. I have many, but would like to send em out one by one and get some critique on them. \r\n\r\ni figure bitpimps is a good chance to get some opinions on my stuff considering i am taking a Disk Jockey course and it has become one of my other hobbies.\r\n\r\nThanks for your time...[/quote:57978c4709]\r\nThere\'s places to upload your own music.\r\nCan\'t remember where right now, would have to look.\r\nBut I know some of the other pimps on here have done that in the past.\r\nThat way everyone can check it out and critique it if you\'d like.\r\n\r\nOr...\r\n\r\nMail a song to bitpimps@gmail.com (make sure it doesn\'t contain a virus or I\'ll have to end you lol)\r\nI\'ll check it out. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35851,'eeafdc6f6d','I\'d like:\r\n· 57 Chevy pink/purple with silver stripe\r\n\r\nAnd if the deals fall through:\r\n· Red Ferrari 512BB\r\n· Yellow Lamborghini Murcielago \r\n\r\nWhat sort of Xmod stuff are you looking for? I\'ve got 8 or 9 of the beasts, extra bodies (Red Supra, Yellow Skyline, Mustang, Camaro, maybe others), some alloy, a 6-cell, a ki-po kit I never put in, etc. Not sure what you\'ve got or what you\'re after.'),(36633,'11afae55fa','Its pretty good, the bodies are very nice. The chassis was kinda strange cause i was expecting a Super Perfection chassis but its all good, just a minor mixup.'),(36634,'6241f1fb67','That\'s the only perfection chassis O had my main man sorry big guy.......i hope you still like your stuff..I really enjoyed doin bizz wit ya.'),(36065,'76703479ec','lol that track is very nice. Way better than the foam one at my local track. How did you add all the rock textures and such?'),(36180,'5e5f965c3a','Yeah, It comes with all that that I can tell. It is literally 2 shelfs full of parts. Way too much too too list, and my camera is still in the shop. I promise that you won\'t be disapointed. There are tons of parts and spare parts. The only thing that comes to mind is the nelly. I\'ll include it, but it is fried beyond repair.\r\n\r\nThe new gearboxes and all will be here on Monday at the latest, but probably tomorrow. The chassis currently installed has a 2 cell polyquest 850mah lipo &quot;custom&quot; installed. There is a new-in-box clear chassis too, and a chassis for lithium ions if I recall. I really can\'t go though everything because it would take forever.\r\n\r\n$210 will be fine if I can ship without priority mail. It will still be insured, but will take 3-7 days (I\'m in South Carolina, btw) to get to you.\r\n\r\nLet me know man,\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35855,'977840428d','So we gotta deal as follows:\r\n\r\nbearings/carbon fiber drive shaft/alloy front and rear shafts\r\n\r\nfor the \r\n\r\nSkyline body, Perfection chassis and controller, the Ferrari F50 body, the Countach body\r\n\r\nWhen you are ready I will give you my shippin info...'),(36057,'24982a113d','Nope, today. I sent it via airmail.'),(36058,'37316750e4','Fastt perfect....Via Canada POST Airmail, for you 2morrow! \r\n\r\nTake er easy!'),(35809,'2534f449c5','Hmm I really want the bearings and the CF drive shaft...I need ligther parts. You have anything that might help the drive train?'),(36062,'dd633ee93a','Thanks alot man! Im out we will talk 2morrow...\r\n\r\nbtw i painted the track gonna get some pics soon...just thought i would let you know ahha later!'),(36066,'42e50f1e41','We used a paint that is used for front steps, it has some sticky rubbery stuff in it. We painted it grey first and then painted the outsides with a darker color and blended the outside with the two colors it give it the road appeal.'),(36015,'e2034f09ca','Hey, did you mail my order yet? I didn\'t get a chance today to order it cause I had basketball practice and by the time I got to it, it was closed. I\'ll try to get there earlier tomorrow and ship it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36018,'77c891786d','Oooo very nice track. This one will be kinda tricky. I\'d say Red suspension springs in the front, Blue in the rear, AWD, and use a Stage 2 Drag motor. The straightaways do change a lot of things, but a Drag motor is very fast and I see more turns than straightaways. The Tight turns would really help here since the steering radius is a bit wide. Just do a test run with different motors and pick your preference. You should post this on the bitpimps forum and get more feedback too heh. There are tons of more experienced drivers than me  :grin:'),(36039,'38a147a670','No prob man. White is one of my favorite too :D the torque is just too fun.\r\n\r\nWanna both send the packages tomorrow? I\'m definately gonna do it tomorrow, first thing I do afterschool :D. It might take me a few hours to get home though, since I do plan on going to a recreation center afterwards for some basketball practice.'),(36040,'7b65fccb51','I went buy today, and I baught the box to fit it in...\r\n\r\nand some packaging\r\n\r\nI am sending it tomorrow...can\'t wait to recieve this stuff!!!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35795,'ef9d3bfbe6','[quote:ef9d3bfbe6]I might have some extra modding stuff availible. I think I still have a full Skyline chassis with AWD, tight turns, bearings, and suspension with rear alloy parts. Ill check my XMOD parts to see if I have any spares, but I kinda doubt it since I gave a lot of stuff for my friend since he wanted to build new cars out of scratch. \r\n\r\nBTW, is the perfection chassis the clear one with 2 speed?[/quote:ef9d3bfbe6]\r\n\r\nIf you want to get rid of that Xmod I have no problems swappin it with ya. The perfection chassis is a white one. I recieved it from a friend brand new and I tried it on my track along the straight away to record it\'s speed on my lap timer, and kept it on my shelf ever since. I barely got it about 2 weeks ago not even. \r\n\r\nThe Skyline body is custom painted, it was one of my original mods, I loved it and used it for all my drag races along my track!!! Reminded me of Need For speed.\r\n\r\nYou could have both the skyline body and perfection chassis if you are willing to trade. IF there is anything else you liked from the collection just let me know. Get back to me soon.'),(36643,'6127964e19','hahaha no prob, i can understand the mistake since it was a PRECIOUS chassis. did you recieve your stuff yet? it should be coming soon =) dunno how yours got here quicker than mines');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35910,'31c2065f25','Great news...\r\n\r\nps. My current Xmod is\r\n\r\n- RWD\r\n- Radioshack bearings\r\n- Stage 2 Drift motor (White)\r\n\r\nI am gonna slap in the AWD soon, but as for the stage two motor which do you recommend?'),(36884,'c52540f96a','hey I havent  forgot to get back to ya, lemme just figure out my situation and what I need. i\'ll get back to ya tomorrow and thanks brutha!'),(36886,'7507f0011c','[quote:7507f0011c=\"pimpsmurf\"]I rule, or suck depending on how you look at it. I found the kyosho board. Sorry about that. I\'ll go ahead and include all this stuff I picked up on sale.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:7507f0011c]\r\n\r\nCool thanks man.'),(37707,'7e203ec029','Poor subie :-(   Imma fix her up, just another project to do :?  No i gots 3, the \'05 stang, a civic i foung in the bottom of my scrap box ( looks like shit, gon be hard to fix), and now my subie, i got some big plans for her :-o  And my top secret (dont tell no one) wide body 350Z :-D  Imma be posting some pics of all but the secret Z today or tommorow. And thanks for the Ferrari Bit, i love it :smile:  :-)  8-)  :)  :cool:  :smoking:'),(37832,'d0b4b36918','Hey man just wanted to check if Bird and you got the stuff I sent? I never heard and just wanted to check.\r\n\r\ngot the lights man working on hooking things up! if I could ever get a little time off from working all the time.\r\n\r\noh kamen emailed me says he wants to buy some stuff from you and is personal check ok?  :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36092,'1543bd5930','never been there :-)'),(35804,'6cfa338f1c','If you could, give me a list of your stuff.\r\n\r\nI want the carbon fibre chassis, but if it fucks up the alignment it might not be worth it. As for buying stuff I think it is better to just do the swaps. We take care of our own postage here at BP. Give eachother\'s addys and send em out, and once we recieve em we notify. It\'s ok we don\'t all come experienced right away with mailing stuff. I am still getting in the hand of it. \r\n\r\nSend me a list and we could organize a deal, I want to get rid of my stuff as soon as possible and get the xmod stuff quick too because I am building a huge track in the basement for them and racing begins soon ahah...let me know bud..'),(35969,'29770a3273','haha I have both of those bodies!!! \r\n\r\nIt\'s ok though, someone from the bitsale is actually sending me a skyline body that I am going to paint up nice. \r\n\r\nand my lil wifey baught me an NSX kit the other day...that would fit right?'),(37571,'82a619c698','Oh, ok. I know about the post count thingy. I just wanted to be more involved.  I\'ll slow it down.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36779,'d683100fae','lol ill come up with a xmod list tomorrow, im about to sleep soon. the problem with your AWD is that the differential is slipping. The stock one and the AWD one is kinda shit so you should open them up and super glue the gears inside. This will place ALL the power from the motor to the wheels and will increase acceleration and speed. Check if its the gear differental first. If its the ball bearing one, i suggest you tighten it as mucha s you could and place it up front. That was my favorite setup for AWD, with locked rear differential and ball diff in the front. Great handling and great power :)'),(36859,'0f8dfce8e5','Yup, just havent had time to log on. I\'ll give you a list of whatever parts i can find tomorrow.'),(35975,'f2d3a730bc','Wait, doesnt the medium shaft fit the RSX? \r\n\r\nI should show you a pic of the track...Would give you a better idea of the racing...what is your email addy?'),(37583,'b8ee2eed6e','I am currently running some comparisons with the Iwaver 02 and the MR-02.  The speed is pretty equal, but the handling is a little in the MR-02\'s favor.  There are a lot of little problems that I fixed on the Iwaver.  I\'ve nick-named it the epoxy machine because there is more epoxy in it holding things together than I care for.  Not the end of the world though.  I put the same hot motor in and 3 X 2 stack of 7317 fets.  I haven\'t modified the firelap 2.0 yet, but I will probably get that done this weekend.  If the firelap can keep up with the MR-02 then that would make it a steel for &lt;$50.  I\'ve already noticed the steering doesn\'t seem as nice on the firelap as the MR-02, but I\'m curious if some fets wont fix that.\r\n\r\nWill know more soon.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37091,'25889706dd','Yeah 45mins, i dunno but if my dad agrees i might be able to come 2 race ya or sumthing, might, i dont think he\'ll let me though :sad:'),(37092,'42104a5d55','lol that would be cool...your lucky you live in florida man, you can race all year around lol'),(35985,'57bf0f3cf1','Hey thanks for the reply...I found a servo fix though where you take apart the servo to fix it yourself!'),(37183,'b69692a5b8','Hey man thanks for the offer but I need the front and back lights not the underglow lights. I found some on eBay for about $15.00 with shipping so thats not too bad? \r\n\r\nthanks for the offer though man!  :-)'),(36488,'1c25540ab8','If you need anybody to do a fet mod to the cars, then let me know.  I\'m sure you already have that covered, but just in case, it\'s the least I can do to support.  I would offer to paint and putty, but I know there are people here who can do that better than me.  I have a lot of extra supplies and what not.  If I know about the car that\'s chosen ahead of time, I can always send you some stuff that I may have laying around that might go good with the ride.'),(37098,'b05330c444','lol, u have a track and i dont =(');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35990,'58947c39f4','http://s6.invisionfree.com/Infernal_XMOD/index.php?showtopic=3664\r\n\r\nFuck I just ran into a huge problem with my servo.....fuck!'),(37653,'b3aee7e951','Great info Thank You!\r\n\r\nWell,\r\n\r\nLast night my uncle and I took the mr-02s to the track once again! \r\n\r\nHe\'s got the mr02 RM, and I have the MM. Like you said the MM is much longer and we just noticed this last night. It seems my MM on the shortest setting is just as long if not a touch longer than my the RM longest setting.\r\n\r\nAfter doing a few laps I noticed some things, and it is bothering me because it has because some a nag on the track.\r\n\r\nFirstly my tires obviously are not worn in just yet. They are very circular, and do not have the worn in patch for track contact. While we were racing on a few turns I found that my mr-02 would actually pull a 360.\r\n\r\nI found this rather odd concidering my track has very good grip on it (although it is not an RCP material or what ever). \r\n\r\nKeep in mind I was running my mm murcielago chassis and wheels with the mclaren body. \r\n\r\nNow I could be wrong but I figured if i tried to slap on some tires with more wearness the car would handle alot better. I threw on the older set and yes it did indeed handle slightly better. But yet there were still some turns I could not take a high enough speed. The RM on the turns was able to take the turns at about half throttle (stock) While my MM would have no throttle power on turns and just need to be &quot;felt out&quot;.\r\n\r\nThe RM was running on an 8tooth pinion, as compared to my 6tooth pinion (both stock mr-02s)\r\n\r\nSo then I figured perhaps it is the torque and throttle power. My throttle may be too torky for my own good. But I also kept in mind that the track had to have a very specific suspension set up. \r\n\r\nThe question I wanted to ask is this. \r\n\r\nOur track is very flat. It is quite similiar if not exactly the same conditions as concrete. Should I put the rear springs to a harder setting, or Softer setting? and should I consider the front springs to a harder or softer?\r\n\r\nWhat are your best tips for suspension? or a damper system that could be avialable? I am interested to see the difference because my uncles car does not spin like this. He has lowered it, and added a few spacers here and there to fix a few things, but he wants me to try and spot this one out myself (competitive edge haha)\r\n\r\nThanks for your time Hachi!'),(37295,'9b7880c889','I got it in the mail yeaterday, thanks for the extra rimms and stuff :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o  :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (35997,'d3468d11c9','Well man, I wish I could help you but I no longer have pictures or the xmod. Im glad someone could help you, I sold my gen one a pretty long time ago because i got tired of fooling with it. If you need any parts I can probably get them ultra cheap at my radio shack, and even be a really good deal for you even with canadian shipping prices. I hope I can help!'),(35998,'6f7de5a22e','Could you get teh Carbon fibre pieces at Radioscack for cheap?'),(36019,'6de415d01e','Well I so far love the White motor, but it seems to spurt nicely on the track. \r\n\r\nI think I will post up the pics of the track on the site\r\n\r\nthanks'),(36130,'3f119c48fc','Hey! Where the hell did you go?\r\nI still have the dead chassi for you. I was in a car accident with a freind before I could send them, and helped her pay for damages. \r\n\r\nI seem to have lost your address, and you have been MIA for a while. Let me know if you still want them, and I can send them out in about a week or so.'),(36038,'d09051420f','[quote:d09051420f=\"Zenith\"][url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=6920]Two Skylines[/url]\r\n\r\nNoticed you\'re trying to keep it more organized, and just wanted to say its a great idea. :-o[/quote:d09051420f]\r\nThanks for the heads up pimp. :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36042,'de6cd692f9','ahh I see..\r\n\r\nWell, the pink body, a chassis and controller is all cool\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know what I can get from you in return!'),(37069,'7fd85428ef','[quote:7fd85428ef=\"pimpsmurf\"]Did you get my package?\r\n\r\nBtw, I think you can reverse the throttle with a mod on the KT-5 TX. I think you reverse the wires on the pot/whatever the trigger is hooked to. It\'s sketchy, but the kid that told me this tends to know what he is talking about. I don\'t know for certain. =(\r\n\r\nDid you get the 2nd package? It should have already been there. If I didn\'t tell you, make sure to be careful taking it appart. There are titanium screws and such in there (and gpm screws I think), so do it on a flat surface.\r\n\r\nI\'m sick, so I\'m going to bed. later on.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:7fd85428ef]\r\n\r\nYeah i got your package bro thanks!\r\n\r\nYeah i was thinking about opening up the controller and messing around thanks for the tip!\r\n\r\nI\'ll shoot ya some pics of the MZM later this week its coming along quite well.\r\n\r\n\r\nTalk to ya later pimp.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37935,'d15a0ca8ec','yah those crystals will work in them.\r\n\r\nthe body is the Evo Rally Body if that is ok?\r\n\r\nI will see if I can dig up another body to send with it for ya.\r\n\r\nwill get it out Monday\r\n\r\nthanks man I know you will just love this car!\r\n\r\nSWG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37938,'c403ac96d2','O yes! I got around to sending it out....and you are definately gonna wanna keep an eye out for your surprise this time my friend! \r\n\r\nthat\'s all im gonna say! \r\n\r\nTake it easy!'),(36974,'91e897112a','I\'m not sure about the screws. There were some screws in the package I sent you today.\r\n\r\nI\'m also not sure about the brakes. My half 8 controller allowed it to do brakes. Did it have brakes in reverse? Then the motor is reversed. I don\'t remember man.\r\n\r\nThe ESC supports brakes though, and kyosho TX\'s are standard. They don\'t have the brakes, etc built into the TX like the iwavers.\r\n\r\nYour package went out USPS Priority today, so expect it in 2-3 days. Sorry about the screw up. Is palm harbor near New Port Richey? I lived in NPR, Ybor, Clearwater, St. Pete, and S. Tampa a couple years ago... bounced around a lot. =)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36161,'c52eb8f907','Sup Pimp!\r\n\r\nI grew up in NE DC !  Club huh !  What\'s that about ?'),(37041,'06a3478047','http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6030644541&amp;rd=1&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1 \r\n\r\n :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37792,'5d602e1995','my real name is trent but i get mail as betty too. whichever you want to use is fine with me.\r\nyou could even address it to &quot;the dickhead&quot;, should make it ok! :lol: \r\n\r\nthanks man, no rush for anything. i\'ll let you know when it arrives :-o'),(36800,'c637c18f8c',':D Ty :P'),(37911,'901ed9dca2','[quote:901ed9dca2=\"Maxximum Attack\"]It\'s still in florida but my skybox has moved:\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\n1900 NW 97th Ave\r\nSTE 716993\r\nMiami\r\nFlorida 33172\r\n\r\nAny word on the GPM stuff for the 2nd group buy?\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx[/quote:901ed9dca2]\r\n\r\nNot yet!\r\n\r\nI\'ll let everyone know when I do find out.'),(37233,'4b1d2babad','Hey DT, I need some stuff from Radioshack. If you\'re up to it of course.\r\n\r\nAll from Radioshack, all in-store only:\r\n\r\n[b:4b1d2babad]XMODS® Custom RC Command Logic Lights[/b:4b1d2babad]\r\n[img:4b1d2babad]http://rsk.imageg.net/graphics/product_images/pRS1C-2266576t98.jpg[/img:4b1d2babad] I want 4 of these.  $5.99 each  [b:4b1d2babad]60-8509[/b:4b1d2babad]\r\n\r\n[b:4b1d2babad]XMODS® Custom RC Body Kit for Silver Toyota® SUPRA® [/b:4b1d2babad]\r\n[img:4b1d2babad]http://rsk.imageg.net/graphics/product_images/pRS1C-2160618t98.jpg[/img:4b1d2babad] one of these. $9.97 each  [b:4b1d2babad]60-8546[/b:4b1d2babad]\r\n\r\n[b:4b1d2babad]XMODS® Custom RC Body Kit for 2004 Ford® Mustang® [/b:4b1d2babad]\r\n[img:4b1d2babad]http://rsk.imageg.net/graphics/product_images/pRS1C-2265436t98.jpg[/img:4b1d2babad] one of these $9.97 each  [b:4b1d2babad]60-8535[/b:4b1d2babad]\r\n\r\nThat stuff and all the returned Xmod EVO cars you can get for free or $10  bucks(or less).\r\n\r\nJust tell me how much it all came to and what you got and I\'ll paypal you the cash  :-o \r\n\r\nMaxx'),(36491,'8c1e094d06','[quote:8c1e094d06=\"MafiaS\"]Have you recieved your rim set yet?[/quote:8c1e094d06]\r\n\r\nNope just waiting, and waiting, and waiting............  :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37794,'657a5515e0','Sorry I haven\'t got back to you. I\'m waiting for the money to be deposited in my paypal acct. It usually takes about 3 days. Thanks for your patience pimp! :)'),(37003,'47a6068140','Yes, it is the motor wires. Reverse the motor wires, and reverse the throttle channel on the TX and everything will be kosher.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37004,'02186f3e86','[quote:02186f3e86=\"pimpsmurf\"]Yes, it is the motor wires. Reverse the motor wires, and reverse the throttle channel on the TX and everything will be kosher.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:02186f3e86]\r\n\r\nThats the problem i cant reverse the throttle channel with a kyosho kt-5 controller'),(37330,'d31942f639','[quote:d31942f639=\"betty.k\"]sounds good to me! you can send paypal cash to: bettykay@gmail.com\r\n\r\nall goods will be packed well and shipped via airmail. shipping to the u.s. usually takes 1 - 2 weeks.\r\n(next time a merikan tries to charge you too much shipping you can say &quot;i got an xmod shipped from aus for $10! :-o )[/quote:d31942f639]\r\n\r\nBefore i send the cash let me double check the address its\r\n\r\nbettykay@gmail.com \r\n\r\n\r\nCorrect?'),(37336,'11775309b9','http://www.1-2-free-forums.com/mf/?mforum=rcworld  the site as soon As we get people were going to go to a real site , its not done yet still gotta get banner and color.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37860,'b2c31db030','Thanks bro, the motor came a few days ago and looks great.  Ive never seen that much bubble wrap crammed into suck a tight space  :-o  lol\r\n\r\nThanks again, always a pleasure\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36201,'83f44a113f','All i could use is some photos and some ideas from your project.  Mainly on what you cut, and how you formed the rear suspension, I was thinking a flex-plate ala mini-z style.  Then the front suspension I\'m stuck, I\'m going to need ideas on that.  Send me photos through my e-mail, it should be in my profile.'),(36203,'83f44a113f','All i could use is some photos and some ideas from your project.  Mainly on what you cut, and how you formed the rear suspension, I was thinking a flex-plate ala mini-z style.  Then the front suspension I\'m stuck, I\'m going to need ideas on that.  Send me photos through my e-mail, it should be in my profile.'),(37153,'fe85401d41','Your MO came the other day.  \r\n\r\nI had a small problem trying to cash it.  My bank wanted to charge me $20!!  Jackasses.\r\n\r\nI then went to the Post Office and they cashed it without a problem, for free. :-o\r\n\r\n\r\nAnyway, I\'ll get your stuff out monday or tuesday morning.\r\n\r\n\r\nLater, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike'),(37020,'9608325a41','Gotcha. I never thought of that man. I don\'t know if the kyosho TX I sent you does reversing either. I don\'t think that it does. =(\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37021,'06a3478047','http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=6030644541&amp;rd=1&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1 \r\n\r\n :lol:'),(37397,'b48bbe8532','here\'s me:\r\n\r\ntrent heffer\r\n39 currajong ave\r\ncamberwell 3124\r\nvictoria\r\naustralia\r\n\r\nthanks heaps for doing this for me, i can\'t wait to rattle da bass bins!\r\ngive my thanks to de selektah :-o'),(37361,'0e2a2696ad','[quote:0e2a2696ad=\"betty.k\"]hiya man. i just got back from the post office, your stuff should arrive in 1 - 2 weeks.\r\nshoot me a message when it arrives and if there\'s any problems or there\'s something missing don\'t hesitate to let me know.\r\n\r\ncheers, b.k.[/quote:0e2a2696ad]\r\n\r\nCool man, will do.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(36254,'0bfb55f47e','yeah, but it requires shims. I didn\'t like it\'s weight up front. I prefer plastic up there. =)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36263,'351b4267a6','Read my previous emails. It comes with a chassis with an attached custom polyquest 2 cell 850mah lipo.\r\n\r\nIt has a 2 cell lipo indicator. The light goes out when the pack needs charging.\r\n\r\nIt has enough spare parts to build another chassis I\'ll bet.\r\n\r\nEven a new bearing set in the packaging. You won\'t get it and be like &quot;ahh, shit. I can\'t use this. This sucks. I thought it has this or that! Because it really has everything. Over $1000 in parts. You would need a turbo if you wanted to use the old electronics, but 1:16 scale novak electronics are better. I\'m even including the 5v regulator w/ Heatsink I build custom for 1:16 scale electronics (so you could run 3 cell lipo without blowing the stock servo motor)\r\n\r\nThis thing is badass, and the only reason I am selling it is because I have no time for it, and I don\'t have $500 to finish it the way I wanted (custom alloy chassis for gp1100 cells, custom alloy gearbox for mamba brushless motor, custom body to mount on the new, longer chassis, etc, etc.\r\n\r\nIf I\'m going to do a custom, I\'ve decided I\'ll do it from the ground up. haha. Like I said. You won\'t be disapointed. If I can manage to get a friend\'s camera, I\'ll take some pictures of the piles of stuff that will come with it. If you want it, when would you be able to pay me, and what shipping do you want? UPS would cost mucho money because I would have to ship it through the &quot;UPS Store&quot; which takes a cut.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36267,'2994ec76be','Just checking how my package situation is?\r\n\r\nI was hoping to get in the pieces for this weekend, is it all cool or no?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36268,'d4394d0f6d','Ok, sorry again. But i have been searching. I wanted to find out how to get putty, and i looked at every single post/thread but couldnt find out how, and the thread i asked about it got locked.. Urrm? Im not going to make another therad \'cos i know il get flamed like fuck. So whats the deal \'io on that? In other words, can you open it up? ;) Or, give me a straight answer.. Anyway, sorry again. Btw, lovcin your cars!'),(36277,'3d4ae2359c','Now that I\'m not all blurry eyed and on my way to work at 5:30 in the morning I just wanted to say thank you again. Not only did ya give me an idea on what to expect or look forward to (all I was looking for) but ya took it one step further and offered to go over what I will be presenting in my portfolio. This has earned my gratitude but good man and if I have the time to do it I will take you up on it. (hopefully any kind of interview is a month away yall know how I love to procrastinate :lol: )\r\nThen you got all gay ( :lol: ) on me and offered to print the stuff out and ship it to me. God damn it man, are you a fuckin saint or what?\r\nSeriously man I could keep on thanking ya but you hopefully get the jist of what I\'m goin on about. :-)'),(36270,'676beadd8a','Where did you get your pieces and parts for the tight turn mod?\r\n\r\nHachi I want to make my Gen1 competitive. I have my miniZ mr-02 mm on order right now it should make it\'s way home in the next few days or so. But my Gen1 xmod is just so cool, and it reminds me how it looks like a 1/10th scale touring RC. \r\n\r\nI want to make my Gen1 quick. I need a sorta good track car, See my track in the post, those pictures should give you an idea of the racing.\r\n\r\nAnyhow right now my set up is simple, RS bearings, stage 2 white motor...and RWD ..haha...\r\n\r\nI wanna hop this up without dishing out a terrible amount of money. I have no clue what to do with fets, or where to solder them...\r\n\r\nAnyhow are there any tips you can give me?\r\n\r\nthanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36272,'2c7d872e56','Sure.  There\'s some very good tutorials that do an awesome job of explaining it all.  I\'ll recomend the irf7317 fets instead of the fets on the Atomic mods site.  You\'ll need at least 6 of them for one car.  I would also get some for the mini-z.  I just fet modded one and it\'s bonkers fast.\r\n\r\nThe tutorials are here;\r\n[url]http://www.atomicmods.com/custom.aspx?id=15[/url]\r\n\r\nAnd the fets I\'ll recomend are here;\r\n[url]http://shop.ausmicro.net/product_info.php?cPath=25_39&amp;products_id=31[/url]\r\n\r\nThe resistors should be easy to find.  You should hunt down 2 x 4.7k ohm, 1/8 watt resistors.  I found them here;\r\n[url]http://www.digikey.com/[/url]\r\n\r\nAlso, a plasma-atomic motor is the best motor I would recomend.  It takes a little work, but it\'s well worth it.  The info om that is here;\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=5665\r\n\r\nI would recomend keeping the Gen1 Xmod RWD.  The AWD kit makes it a bit slower and it\'s already a bit slow compared to just about every other 1:28 scale car.  You\'ll see what I\'m talking about when you get that Mini-z.  The AWD kit for the Gen 1 Xmod also creates more drag in the drive system witch will increase you chance of blowing fets if you use a hot motor like the plasma-atomic.  You must replace the fets to use the plasma-atomic motor or any other hot motor.  IMO the rat-shack stage 2 motors are ok, but it doesn\'t even compare to the plasma-atomic.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.'),(36266,'d4394d0f6d','Ok, sorry again. But i have been searching. I wanted to find out how to get putty, and i looked at every single post/thread but couldnt find out how, and the thread i asked about it got locked.. Urrm? Im not going to make another therad \'cos i know il get flamed like fuck. So whats the deal \'io on that? In other words, can you open it up? ;) Or, give me a straight answer.. Anyway, sorry again. Btw, lovcin your cars!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37588,'627f228204','If you want to save some money then wait until I get the Firelap 2.0 modded and running.  So far stock it\'s pretty much the same thing as the Iwaver 02.  The chassis, tires and springs are exactly the same.  It even says &quot;This is Iwaver&quot; on the bottom.  The PCB is different, but it seems to operate pretty much the same.  It has the same steering strength and after I get the fets and hot motor installed it will probably run very similar.  I\'m still waiting on parts for the Plasma-atomic motor and the ball differential which should be here within the next five days or so.  I already have the fets and will probably get them installed Saturday.\r\n\r\nJust remind me about Wed. or so.  Otherwise the Iwaver 02 is a safe bet.  Just stay away from the Porsche Concept body.  I had that originally.  It was crap.  Didn\'t fit on the chassis correctly, the tires rubbed on the body in the front and the back.  And when you hit a bump the lip on the front of the car grabs the ground and ends up cracking off eventually.  One side was higher than the other too.  I had to rip off the body clips and epoxy them back in the right place after dremmeling a little.'),(36275,'a68e8f70c4','Thanks a bunch...\r\n\r\nSo i guess it is on the hunt for fets for me ! Than I pick up a plasmatomic...I guess that is enough power for a short track and competitive play.\r\n\r\nThanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36276,'0ede2549f4','Ok, pmsl.. Btw, where do people get all those classic bodies? If they are for zipzaps or something then dont say search etc, because i want a few for my bit char-g. But where do you get \'em?'),(37459,'a0ed9c9b04','[quote:a0ed9c9b04=\"betty.k\"]the steering is a little sluggish, i put it down to the weakness of the iwaver steering curcuit.\r\nyou\'ll notice all those servos have the motors swapped out, from memory the bpnsx still has a stock servo motor. try using a stock (red) zz motor instead.\r\n\r\nanother reason for the sluggishness is the front springs press hard on the knuckles making them harder to turn, press on the front shocks then twiddle the steering. you\'ll probably find it a bit snappier. this means when it\'s on the ground and running the steering works better due to the suspension sag.\r\n\r\ni\'m pretty sure there\'s no broken parts, it\'s just the combination of the suspension, weak curcuit and weak motor. softer springs and a better servo motor is what i\'d try :-o \r\n\r\nany other problems or questions, just gimme a yell :-)[/quote:a0ed9c9b04]\r\n\r\nThis one has a upgraded steering motor from the looks of it a yellow one.\r\n\r\nI mean its not steering at all man, i\'m puzzled as hell here.'),(37625,'a599e67864','Please ship to the following address and not the address of the paypal account.\r\n\r\nRasheed Sabir\r\nBannister Land\r\nMartindales Road\r\nSt.Michael BB11115\r\nBARBADOS\r\n\r\nwhat is your paypal addy');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36293,'2511b7f946','You need shims for it. I used tin foil, and it worked great. It\'s not the hassle of shiming that stopped me, it was the weight issue.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37494,'fbcbcd6d19','[quote:fbcbcd6d19=\"betty.k\"]hmmm, i\'m stumped! it was definately working when i had it, slow steering but working.\r\nsounds like there could be some binding in the steering somewhere. check it over and as a last resort pull the servo apart and check it out.\r\ni\'d try a different servo motor too.\r\n\r\nsee how you go with that and lemme know if it works. :-o[/quote:fbcbcd6d19]\r\n\r\nJust did all that, nothing. :?'),(36300,'437413894b','haha... I had orders from rcmart for parts for this thing that were twice that! lol\r\n\r\nSeriously, check me out. many have vouched for me, and I have no desire to ruin the poor reputation I have online by ripping someone off.\r\n\r\npaypal me $225 for priority shipping though. It is going to cost me $30-40 to ship, and paypal is going to suck 5% away, plus I have to fork out another $25 for the parts that are coming, so $225 is one hell of a deal man. Something to brag about no less. \r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37604,'a6d98ab839','[quote:a6d98ab839=\"PimpSmurf\"]Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative. [/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]No, you did not say that most Liberals.... [/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t say most liberals. I said most libertarians.\r\n\r\n[/quote=PimpSmurf]I don\'t agree with everything the libertarians (base = liberty, not liberal) believe, just 95% of it. They are pretty far right wing. Most consider Bush a liberal, not a conservative.[/quote]\r\n\r\nNow do you understand? Calm down and read it aloud.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"] :lol: You\'re a joke anymore to me dude.\r\nIf you can\'t even see the flaws in your posts, the contradictions, and just even general false statements you make - I can\'t help you.\r\nNobody can.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nThe only false statement was that I did not know that Bush decided to let the congress debate the issue futher. I correct myself. Other than that, you are dreaming man.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]I don\'t know what you\'re stuck on with the gay sex thing unless it\'s burned into your memory from you last gay experience or something.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nActually, I\'m talking about all the animated gifs with gay sex people were posting. Maybe you should read back and jog your marijuanna-riddled brain.  :-D \r\n\r\nJust kidding man, but looks back and see all the gay shit people posted.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]Anyways, I\'m not retreating. I own this place. You don\'t. If I don\'t want it to be a political forum, guess what? It won\'t be.\r\nI\'ve let you go on long enough spewing your bullshit. Now I\'m putting a stop to it.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nThat is fine man. At least this is a capitalist society where you actually have the right to own a forum. If the facists had control, none of us would control anything.\r\n\r\n[quote:a6d98ab839=\"CaboWabo\"]If you can\'t go back to what this forum is about, I\'m affraid you\'ll just have to leave - and guess who else can make that happen? Yup, me!\r\n\r\nGo bite your pillow.[/quote:a6d98ab839]\r\n\r\nWe went somehow from talking about conspiracy theory bullshit to a political discussion. Oh wait, I remember now!\r\n\r\n[/quote=CaboWabo]Off the topic of 9/11. I find it funny that this whole UAE buying ports thing was all approved, Bush backed it, then starts to backpeddle saying he knew nothing about the deal until it was over. And in the same breath says that &quot;we shouldn\'t worry about security&quot; even though that\'s his entire platform since we\'ve started this whole &quot;war on terrorism&quot; thing. \r\n\r\nTo me, that just shows that the government has finally gotten to the point where they can lie, directly in peoples faces, and it still floats. People still buy into it. The government knows that now and can be completely blatent about their actions. As long as they say 2 different things while doing 1 - they\'re asses are covered because there\'s enough ignorance that either story will be bought regardless. \r\n\r\nWhatever.\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nOh that\'s right. You\'re the one who opened the political discussion. Fuck, I forgot that shit. Seriously man, I had to look it up.\r\n\r\nBut more importantly, you should calm down man. This is why people aren\'t suppose to discuss religion and politics in polite company. In real life, we could probably have a decent conversation/debate. But in this medium, we both struggle to make our points but it is easy to get distracted and forgetfull. Everything is alright. hehe\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36309,'99c5bcb583','I got both, turns out the cashier guy who was helping was into R/C\'s too, so he gave me a 15% discount, so I was able to afford both.  The Evo VIII is beautiful and the ZZMT is wonderful.  Only problem is, is it\'s a little low on power, and likes to flip and roll.  I\'m so happy.\r\n\r\nI was thinking of doing a board swap with my SE, but I\'m not sure how to get it to work.  Mainly getting it to work with the motor, servo and what to do to charge batteries.  I was thinking Iwaver board for the SE.  I want to get started by stripping everything out of the car, so what can I take out that won\'t be needed for a new board, and what wires should I be careful wth?\r\n\r\nFor the ZZMT I\'m thinking I just need a better motor, a higher RPM motor, have you noticed it\'s a little low on power?  I\'m in Canada so I don\'t think we have any MT upgrades just yet, don\'t know if they are going to continue selling or getting new stuff or stopping.  For me it\'s just a touch too little, sometimes it gets stuck on some obstacles, like going over my bed or over rough carpet because of not enough power.  What could I do, it\'s already 2-celled (right?) unless i can change to better cells.'),(36321,'05dd8a9e3d','[quote:05dd8a9e3d=\"45tr0\"]well that just blew my mind!\r\n\r\nI\'ve been trippin around at a dance festival all weekend, covered in mud and higher than Edmund Hilary, and i come home to find a placing waiting for me in the blowout!  What a trip!\r\n\r\nI never woulda thunk it.\r\n\r\nThanks for having us all around Cabo - this is one fine place you\'ve got here.  Its my home on them internets. \r\n\r\nAnyways, anough of my drug induced warm-n-fuzzball sentiment! Now to collect my shiat!\r\n\r\nMy postal address is:\r\n\r\nMichael Frawley \r\nPO BOX 2010\r\nTOOWONG QLD 4066\r\nAUSTRALIA\r\n\r\nThanks again for making this whole she-bang possible cabo.  you rock![/quote:05dd8a9e3d]\r\nNo sweat pimp. You did an amazing job - well deserved win.\r\nAll guys did increadible jobs, without you guys helping to inspire others - none of this would be nearly as fun.\r\nGood work dude.\r\n\r\nYou prize will probably go out sometime this coming week.\r\nI\'ll let ya know when it\'s shipped.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36322,'e2a2cd1fc3','Ive never done the iwaver board swap so you are going to have to do some searching on the site to find out the info (its there, i just cant remember where its at)\r\n\r\nA new motor in the SE is fairly simple, I normaly use a toys r us superslick motor(much larger) you will have to grind out some plastic to mount it properly and solder the leads from the pcb to the motor to get it to work. \r\n\r\nAs far as servos go, there arent any in the zipzaps.  The SE just uses a POT and a motor with some gears to steer (im not very learned on how it all works though)  \r\n\r\nFor the MT, it is only running on 2 cells stock but you an upgrade to up to 4 i think.  Mine has three in it and works great but you will need a better motor and gearing if you want it to go fast.  If you want it to just have more torque and climbing power then you can gear it down with the stock motor by using another bit gear in there (there are threads on this on the site, use the search button)  \r\n\r\nLet me know if that helps any\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36323,'fcc82448ad','[quote:fcc82448ad=\"DarkTari\"]Congratulations Pimp!  Great work once again!\r\n\r\nI got yo info, I\'ll get it out to you 1st thing Monday.  :-o[/quote:fcc82448ad]\r\n\r\nthanks a ton man the contest was great I appreciate the work ya\'ll went to, to put it on! \r\n\r\nthat was a hard choice glad I was not the one to try and make it!\r\n\r\nthanks again man!  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37447,'d355eba1af','the steering is a little sluggish, i put it down to the weakness of the iwaver steering curcuit.\r\nyou\'ll notice all those servos have the motors swapped out, from memory the bpnsx still has a stock servo motor. try using a stock (red) zz motor instead.\r\n\r\nanother reason for the sluggishness is the front springs press hard on the knuckles making them harder to turn, press on the front shocks then twiddle the steering. you\'ll probably find it a bit snappier. this means when it\'s on the ground and running the steering works better due to the suspension sag.\r\n\r\ni\'m pretty sure there\'s no broken parts, it\'s just the combination of the suspension, weak curcuit and weak motor. softer springs and a better servo motor is what i\'d try :-o \r\n\r\nany other problems or questions, just gimme a yell :-)'),(36329,'04069d8606','Yeah, the 1:16 can handle pretty much any 130 size motor. Probably could handle a 10 turn silver magnet wire. lol\r\n\r\n$218 is ok. paypal joseph.yarbrough@gmail.com and I\'ll ship her out tomorrow!\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37608,'5443835dd1','Fine. BTW, I\'m not a bible-thumper... I don\'t know what gave you that idea.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37623,'9d29cea220','I\'ve got the Saleen on an Iwaver MM.  It fits perfectly.  The MM setup actually has a longer chassis.  The Saleen body is a long body compared to most other bodies.  It may be the longest body available for all I know, but the wheel wells are still in the same place as most other MM bodies.\r\n\r\nMy MR-02 has a RM setup with an NSX body and it\'s shorter.  This surprised me as I always thought the RM setup would be longer.  But, the MM setup needs more space in between the main chassis and the wheels to account for the motor to be positioned there.\r\n\r\nAs far as which ones better, not sure.  I guess it depends on how you\'re gonna race.  So far it doesn\'t seem to make much difference.  If you want the weight of the motor farther back then go with the RM.  You would think that with the weight farther back it would help with traction and also help wip the back around if you want to slide/turn or drift, but it\'s not like your massively changing the balance with this adjustment so the difference in performance is nominal.  Although, more distance between the front and rear wheels would help keep the car straight during acceleration and actually help some with consistancy in cornering, but again the difference is nominal.\r\n\r\nOne more issue; The motor position of the MM does keep more crap out of the motor.  I noticed that with a hot motor/better magnets more metal debri gets picked up.  The MM setup covers the motor a little better so the metal debri just gets stuck to the bottom of the car instead of directly to the motor.  Not a big deal if you\'re gonna be racing it on a track and not on a dirty concrete parking lot.\r\n\r\nBy the way, I gave the MR-02 and the Iwaver 02 a healthy comparison on a concrete parking lot yesturday.  They accelerate exactly the same and have exactly the same top speed.  I\'ll be giving them some more comparison evaluation today on a tile floor and focusing on handling/cornering.  I already know the MR-02 has cleaner steering, but how much is the question.'),(36341,'23c12c6152','Thanks once again you have come through. It looks like I am going to keep my MR-02 stock for now. I want it for indoor racing: fun but still competitive.\r\n\r\nThe Gen1 needed some sort of a boost. I think with these here fets, and perhaps two more cells, the thing should roar nicely.\r\n\r\nThanks!');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36344,'2dc7d678cb','Robert Wilson\r\n1550 Tomcat Blvd. Ste. 150\r\n\r\nOrder 221 (I think)\r\n\r\nIt\'s probably already sent as I ordered it aprox 10 days ago.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you still have it.  I would like to add/change some stuff if I can.'),(36345,'52fd2dd5a9','Ok, no problem, thanks.  I can\'t wait to get started on this.\r\n\r\nLast question for now, what did you find was the best way to cut the plastic?'),(36346,'a62a0e1fdc','most of the time i use the zipzap package for the plastic so a good set of scissors works well and to touch up i use my dremel drill with a sanding bit or something\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36354,'6a8b140a3f','Hey, :-) \r\n\r\nSorry to take so long but sometimes time just runs away.  \r\n\r\nAnyway are you still interested, if so I have one with a motor combo that I think you would appreciate, the only bad thing is that when word gets out about how well the motor combo in it works Im going to owe some kid a MRCC an apology.   Do you have a particular body preference?  Let me know if you are and if the address is still correct and I can have it in the mail today.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nPhilip (LBRC)'),(36355,'89c9e616dc','[quote:89c9e616dc=\"LBRC\"]Hey, :-) \r\n\r\nSorry to take so long but sometimes time just runs away.  \r\n\r\nAnyway are you still interested, if so I have one with a motor combo that I think you would appreciate, the only bad thing is that when word gets out about how well the motor combo in it works Im going to owe some kid a MRCC an apology.   Do you have a particular body preference?  Let me know if you are and if the address is still correct and I can have it in the mail today.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nPhilip (LBRC)[/quote:89c9e616dc]\r\nHey man all is cool I have been away for a bit in Florida so have only been back a week time has also gotten away from me. \r\nI am still vary interested! Are you going to send some bodies for me to paint along with the epoch? Oh and the body I am interested in is a mini cooper if you still have one (I thought I saw one in the pics you sent me) I have some extra bodies here at the house if you dont want to send a body with the chasses if no mini cooper anything is fine.\r\n\r\nThe address is still good; if you send the bodies to be painted let me know if you want some of them painted with certain colors or scheme.\r\n\r\nOh and if its a kid on MRCC I would not worry to much its just MRCC  :lol: \r\n\r\nthanks man oh and let me know when you want me to write up a review so I don\'t let any cats out of any bag to early! \r\n\r\nthanks so much!  :-) \r\nAaron');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36356,'89c9e616dc','[quote:89c9e616dc=\"LBRC\"]Hey, :-) \r\n\r\nSorry to take so long but sometimes time just runs away.  \r\n\r\nAnyway are you still interested, if so I have one with a motor combo that I think you would appreciate, the only bad thing is that when word gets out about how well the motor combo in it works Im going to owe some kid a MRCC an apology.   Do you have a particular body preference?  Let me know if you are and if the address is still correct and I can have it in the mail today.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\nPhilip (LBRC)[/quote:89c9e616dc]\r\nHey man all is cool I have been away for a bit in Florida so have only been back a week time has also gotten away from me. \r\nI am still vary interested! Are you going to send some bodies for me to paint along with the epoch? Oh and the body I am interested in is a mini cooper if you still have one (I thought I saw one in the pics you sent me) I have some extra bodies here at the house if you dont want to send a body with the chasses if no mini cooper anything is fine.\r\n\r\nThe address is still good; if you send the bodies to be painted let me know if you want some of them painted with certain colors or scheme.\r\n\r\nOh and if its a kid on MRCC I would not worry to much its just MRCC  :lol: \r\n\r\nthanks man oh and let me know when you want me to write up a review so I don\'t let any cats out of any bag to early! \r\n\r\nthanks so much!  :-) \r\nAaron'),(36357,'b72679f8b1','I send your stuff out this weekend. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36358,'b08e2fda5b','On their way, made sure there was a Mini Cooper Lexand body for you, and put a blue legacy on the chassis.  I put extra bodies in the box only paint the ones you want or feel like, I have no preference except maybe the 1/28 Willys.\r\n\r\nAlso included a 345 mAh Lipo, the chassis has a 180 NiMH in it charged and is ready to go, when using an Epoch charger with the 180 just double charge.  I know there is no need but have to say it none the less, do not use the Epoch charger on the Lipo. To replace the battery simply loosen the bottom three screws and gently pull/push the battery out, there is a slot on the other side so you can use a key or suitably blunt tool to push, it helps save the battery wires.\r\n\r\nAside from the motors and ball bearing motor mount, I replaced the steering servo motor for much quicker and steadier steering on a track, like a 4 cell it will freak out when you turn it on but as soon as you turn the steering wheel it will stop.\r\n\r\n\r\nI didnt glue the wheels on but you may want to, I have found that a small drop of lock-tight works great and still lets you get them off when needed.\r\n\r\nThere are no secrets in your car, however no one other than Apex, and Hendrix motor sports (Hendrix is a bit of a secret) has ever seen one with this particular motor setup, it is unfortunately a bit difficult to reproduce in quantity, the bearing and motors have to sit too close together.  Which is too bad, when you see and try the motors you will understand why I wanted to be able to make a mount that they would just pop into.\r\n\r\nHope you like it.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nPhilip (LBRC)'),(36359,'b08e2fda5b','On their way, made sure there was a Mini Cooper Lexand body for you, and put a blue legacy on the chassis.  I put extra bodies in the box only paint the ones you want or feel like, I have no preference except maybe the 1/28 Willys.\r\n\r\nAlso included a 345 mAh Lipo, the chassis has a 180 NiMH in it charged and is ready to go, when using an Epoch charger with the 180 just double charge.  I know there is no need but have to say it none the less, do not use the Epoch charger on the Lipo. To replace the battery simply loosen the bottom three screws and gently pull/push the battery out, there is a slot on the other side so you can use a key or suitably blunt tool to push, it helps save the battery wires.\r\n\r\nAside from the motors and ball bearing motor mount, I replaced the steering servo motor for much quicker and steadier steering on a track, like a 4 cell it will freak out when you turn it on but as soon as you turn the steering wheel it will stop.\r\n\r\n\r\nI didnt glue the wheels on but you may want to, I have found that a small drop of lock-tight works great and still lets you get them off when needed.\r\n\r\nThere are no secrets in your car, however no one other than Apex, and Hendrix motor sports (Hendrix is a bit of a secret) has ever seen one with this particular motor setup, it is unfortunately a bit difficult to reproduce in quantity, the bearing and motors have to sit too close together.  Which is too bad, when you see and try the motors you will understand why I wanted to be able to make a mount that they would just pop into.\r\n\r\nHope you like it.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nPhilip (LBRC)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36360,'f3b7251b04','HEy, \r\n\r\nGuess who\'s back  :cool: . I have been working on a scale model of a remote control &quot;volvo ocean racer&quot; sailing boat. Stupid me because now I also missed the end of the year blow out, while having three entries lying around  :sad: . \r\nBut YEAH , I still want them  8-) .\r\nmy adress: \r\nJoris de Iongh\r\nCipreslaan 48\r\n3053nd\r\nRotterdam, the Netherlands\r\n\r\nJust shove them into an envolop between two cards if you are going to send the coils only. Unless you send me the chassis in total. \r\nYou\'ll figure something out. Bad luck with the car accident man!\r\n\r\nTnx in advance,\r\n\r\n :)'),(36870,'804f436a1e','$100+ WOW. Now I know why custom chassis are sold so expensive. \r\nThis is already getting too expensive. I know I can cut more than one chassis from a 12x12 sheet, but that\'s a $52 sheet!!. Then $100 to cut it out?\r\n\r\nI\'m going to continue designing the chassis in any case. Can a CNC mill cut out my name in the chassis? \r\nAnd do they charge extra for logos?\r\n\r\nCrap!!\r\nMaxx'),(37030,'6d700515a4','Naw bro, not interested right now, but good luck on ebay. Shit man ... i seen your track DAMNNNNNNNNN that thing is sick.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37032,'ab22f723a0','It\'s cool b...\r\n\r\nThanks! the track is takin us some time, it looks a lil different i might take some pictures tonight...We need some races now'),(37044,'17609bab61','Got off my lazy ass today, went to the damn post office and told the bitch at the counter get my boi skylinekid his stuff...\r\n\r\nshe said my.mafiaS, it will be 7-10 days.\r\n\r\nI said...bitch make it 5 days, or your kids gon get it ahah!\r\n\r\nAnyways man your stuff is sent\r\n\r\nthree bodies are in there and I put in some nice lil extra\'s.\r\n\r\nBTW do you have the front gear for the prop shaft? I really need that...any part of AWD transformation is needed man. Thanks.'),(36431,'d892c43248','did not want to clutter the boards. Thought 1 on 1 would be better.\r\n\r\nWell, You are saying if I get the pro board than i could only run the hottest Iwaver motor correct? But if i were to run anything hotter I would still have to solder stronger FETS? like a spider or something?\r\n\r\ni could just add the other fets on the Pro board later right?\r\n\r\nAs for the Xmod question, I saw B.K\'s post. \r\n\r\nNow I could swap the Pro board into my Xmod, use the Iwaver controller with my xmod. This will increase my Xmods speed, and also turning correct?'),(37857,'00e5135627','Hey what\'s up? Just another one of my, &quot;Hey, let\'s bug hue, see what he\'s up to.&quot; PMs.\r\n\r\n\r\nI hate my new computer, it pisses me off at least twice a week, but it does burn CDs really fast, like 2 minutes. I\'m used to 20. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo i\'m gonna be burning you some music, probably make you some MP3 cds because there just so much shit I\'ve meant to send you.\r\n\r\nJust recently ben listening to The Subways. They are kinda garage-y, really fluffy kinda pop, sometimes really heavy. I dig them, but they wear kinda thin on repeat listenings. Artic Monkeys, this is my second time through this album as I type this. I\'m loving it. Kinda hard to decribe, modern punk, winda poppy, hints of funk, occasional little bits that remind me of The Jazz Butcher. Interesting. Matchbook Romance, they\'re hard for me catagorize. Going by their single &quot;Monsters&quot;, you\'d place them in the Fallout Boy category, but the overall album has more of a heavy metal style to them to me anyways, but the funny thing is the metal head at work hated them, told me he didn\'t care for punk, so I\'m over here listening to it over and over trying to hear where he hears the punk. The best I can figure is the beat, but this guy like Green day and Blink 182, so I\'m not getting it. I think it sounds metal. :lol: \r\nAnyways, I got off track on that band, but speaking of Fallout Boy, saw them on SNL, I thought, &quot;That was kinda cool.&quot; So I downloaded all three of their albums... it all sound the same, kinda boring after awhile. :lol: \r\nGot the Black Sabbath Black Box set DLed. The complete 70-78 Sabbath if you\'re interested. :-o \r\n\r\nRight after I got my computer Torrentspy apparently became a pay site or something. I figured what the hell, I\'ll pitch them $18 if it makes them happy and I can keep DLing the way I have been. I forgot to click a box, and accidently paid an extra $14.99 for their software, but oh well, I think I\'ve DLed hundreds of $$$ of music since then. Funny thing is when you search from their software it searches mininova.org, and I was billed by Supernova.org, I\'m guessing they own Torrentspy too. At anyrate if anyone ask, I thought I was DLing music legally, being as I paid for it and all. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHate to say it, but, after playing with my new Losi mini LST, all my smaller cars just seem like cheap POS. :lol: \r\nI still love my bits, but if you want to get serious, you shoud look into 1/18th scale, and the nearby racing scene. The step up in quality is really that noticable, and I\'m looking forward to gwtting out to race occasionally. I\'ll still be playing with little cars though, that\'s part of my plan. I\'m gonna save my pennies until I can afford a charger that will do LiPos too. Easier to rationalize that when I have the Losi, than just for a few ZZ SEs. Then when I upgrade the servos, I\'ll have a pair of servos to tear down for projects. I realized a while ago that the reason why people like LBRC kick ass at that shit is because they are into the bigger cars, and have access to shit.\r\n\r\nSo that where I\'m at. Things are pretty good here. I got work straightened out, wife\'s being cool, kid\'s goofy as ever, bud\'s stoney, no complaints.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37046,'896bc4af36','I will send all my xtra AWD stuff ur way tommorow, you\'ll like it garenteed :-)'),(37054,'0d6ddf4f8b','[quote:0d6ddf4f8b=\"Maxximum Attack\"]Cool, I may double this order soon, but don\'t commit me to that yet I have to find out if my friend has the money to pay for them before he gets the $$$ in Feb. He\'ll need at least $300. So I\'ll find out and get back to you.[/quote:0d6ddf4f8b]\r\n\r\nIs that $300 USD or BBD?'),(36445,'d67085b14a','No, No, and no.  Unless you have a custom chassis, they wont fit.  Even so, the 81 is too large.  You would need an HS-55.\r\n\r\nI will check out the track tonight, so drop me a PM and I will hook you up.\r\n\r\nThanks'),(36441,'f38d48b47f','What did/do you use to cut up the ZZ\'s?  I was thinking dremel with a cutting bit....\r\n\r\nPhotos?  Sorry, I\'m getting really anxious.  I just need to see the lines that you took to cut.\r\n\r\nlemme know if I\'m getting annoying (I don\'t mind), I get that when I\'m anxious.'),(36442,'5ad5abfda6','I used a dremel for most of my cutting.  I dont have too many shots but these should help a little.  I used the epoch suspension as inspiration.  \r\n\r\nNot sure if this pic helps much, this is the underside,, i used some aluminum to dress up the arm (its plastic under it)\r\n\r\n[img:5ad5abfda6]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10078/underside.jpg[/img:5ad5abfda6]\r\n\r\n[img:5ad5abfda6]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10078/lancer-suspension-4.jpg[/img:5ad5abfda6]\r\n\r\nThis one should show you pretty much how i went about setting it up.  You may have less room with an SE so some artistic liberties will need to be taken for sure.\r\n\r\nI think your best option will be to make some sort of a suspension plate/pivot plate like the mini z\'s have or like betty K did on some of his full suspension bits.  ITs simple and it works great.  At this scale you dont need much more than the springyness of the plastic quite honestly\r\n\r\nhope that helps\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36443,'1eed82a92f','one more shot that sould show you how i did all of the pivots with the tubes.  it pivots up and down as well as left and right.\r\n\r\n[img:1eed82a92f]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10078/suspension-in-progress-evo.jpg[/img:1eed82a92f]\r\n\r\nstg'),(36687,'ef1dadb082','Hey!\r\n\r\nYou can ignore the pic in that auction.\r\n\r\nHe will send you a a full bag of similar 103/104 caps.\r\n\r\nthey work great.'),(37061,'4af42c6f58','Well, you can always revert to RWD if you don\'t like AWD. Looking at the Zs it seems you dont need AWD for good handling, but that\'s cuz they have really good diffs and a wide variety of rubber. Read [url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7372]HACHI-RYOKU\'s review[/url] on the three 1:28 cars that he has, and see what he says. It was VERY informative to me.\r\n\r\nDo iWavers have brakes? Do mini-Zs have brakes?\r\nI\'d like to know that, I was thinking of a PCB swap but I kinda like brakes on my Xmod.\r\n\r\nMaxx (not Maxxa :-))'),(37073,'29db99bad2','Im going up to Canada this weekend, how far is whre u live from Cambridge, ON???? Matbe we could race or sumthing, MAYBE* :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37075,'3c1c27f106','Cambidge, that is near missisauga I believe.\r\n\r\nI live in the greater Toronto Area...known as Vaughan, more specifically in the town of Woodbridge.\r\n\r\nI am about 45 minutes away from Cambridge. lol'),(37895,'0e20fd9a59','I wouldn\'t mind helping you out, but I have just enough for one in each test car right now.  I\'ve got to keep one in each car to do the comparison essay I\'ve been working on.  Also the parts for each are starting to get scarse.  If I let one go, there\'s no garauntee that I\'ll get another anytime soon at a decent price.\r\n\r\nSorry to be a taco, but if it helps any, after I finish the next two cars reviews I\'m going to take a break from all the comparisons and go into motor construction.  I\'ll be making hand wounds, plasma-atomics and other types of motors and selling them.  There just isn\'t enough people that do that.  I know, that doesn\'t really help you out now.\r\n\r\nHave you looked into an Uberdash?  Also, an Anima modified motor or &quot;Fatboy HC&quot; as they call it at Atomic mods is also a good second.'),(36453,'4444bce7e2','I\'ve been busy with hospital trips the last day or so. :sad: \r\n\r\nI will look ASAP for you for those items. :-o \r\n\r\nI should have a chance on my next days off, Mon and Tues, next week.  Unless the DOC makes me take a Vacation today.  I really need one bad!!\r\n\r\nI won\'t forget ya. :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\nSG\r\n\r\n\r\nP.S.  Even if I don\'t find the Trans Am bodies at RS, I think I have a spare set somewhere that I can give up.  Just gotta see what I have on hand buried in drawers. 8-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37090,'25889706dd','Yeah 45mins, i dunno but if my dad agrees i might be able to come 2 race ya or sumthing, might, i dont think he\'ll let me though :sad:'),(37093,'cb0ab6991c','Yo, is that guy your friend? If so could you give me his email i\'m interested in his bits. I\'ll offer him $25 shipped, since he\'s in Canada. I\'m just pming you in case he left the site, and doesn\'t get my pm.'),(37095,'b05330c444','lol, u have a track and i dont =('),(37514,'5ab037f7e5','Im VERY Interested in this, i just have a few questions like does it come withe the original manuals and instructions? Does it come with the Porshe Body? And can i see a few more pics of it? Also does it come with battery and charger?'),(36489,'88fe083c2d','Never mind the spider.  I just found out PH2T was selling his nellys again.  No offense to you, but I gotta get one of those.  Don\'t worry though.  I\'m getting ready to hit your store for some more parts.  In fact I\'m gonna head there now.\r\n\r\nOut for now.\r\nHachi'),(37189,'16bb2827eb','Well I like my Iwaver real well! I had an older Mini-Z and I think that I like my IWaver much more! Its on the workbench right now as I am trying to build that Back to the Future body for it!  :grin:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36494,'dcd6fc3ad7','Thats cool, a little body work is a simple thing to fix anyways.  I was just wondering if i could take it off your hands,, i only need the evo body.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nSTG'),(36547,'a1d228c268','The key is to keep it cool.  I\'ll build you a special Spider (version 2) which is smaller than previous one and a little neater to mount.  I would look at ways you could make it cooler - small stick-on heatsink perhaps?  \r\n\r\nThe FETs will take the current etc pretty much no worries as long as they don\'t overheat.\r\n\r\nYou\'re right about the 02 being a problem for that, there\'s not much air space aroudn the FETs and no venting.\r\n\r\nI\'ll send the order with tyres today and the Spider will go in the next mail - it\'ll be a little special ;)\r\n\r\nA&gt;'),(36555,'a45b1d00c5','Thanx man.  I apreciate it.'),(36559,'8ad1283b58','I believe I have everything else in there. I am going to clean up the workshop tonight and sort everything. It\'s possible there is something else left behind, but I\'ll be sure to include it.\r\n\r\nI\'m really very sorry about the mistake man. That sucks. I hope you have another TX for the mean time (any AM 27 is cool)\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(36560,'5b67b93ae6','Hey, I\'ll buy your stretched SSMT if it isn\'t sold yet.  PM me back.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36561,'5b67b93ae6','Hey, I\'ll buy your stretched SSMT if it isn\'t sold yet.  PM me back.'),(36562,'2dcb39fde1','[quote:2dcb39fde1=\"Bitmodder27\"]Hey, I\'ll buy your stretched SSMT if it isn\'t sold yet.  PM me back.[/quote:2dcb39fde1]\r\n\r\nIts sold.'),(36569,'4dccfb3ad6','Dave \r\n\r\nWhats up dude - just put a quick post in the Misc section about a new Wally World vehicle.  Thought you might be interested\r\n\r\nLater\r\n\r\nVik'),(36570,'cc13d0a593','Your prize got shipped today.\r\nThey said 4-7 days, but I\'ve never had anything get down under that quick - usually takes a few weeks.\r\n\r\nHere\'s a tracking #: LC150747561US\r\n\r\nLet me know when you get it so I know it got there safe and sound.'),(37309,'12270e6e3d','good choice, you won\'t be disappointed :-o'),(36574,'8798c8f8b7','lol hey man....Nice PM...\r\n\r\nNaw i never got my stuff  :???: \r\n\r\nAnd I sent it to December 31st?\r\n\r\nI never even checked that trackig numba, I dont even know if I got one for you.\r\n\r\nAll i know is that it was like 8 bucks to ail mail it to ya...and it was sent my man...'),(37313,'4412888b85','[quote:4412888b85]Just sold some Xmod shit,[/quote:4412888b85]\r\n\r\nme too, i\'ll be visiting rcmart :lol:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36578,'cc56175806','A logical approach.\r\n\r\n1. Since the Iwaver Pot (short for Potentiometer) will not fit in the SE gears you will obviously want to leave the SEs Pot in place and use it.\r\n\r\n2. But since the Iwaver circuit board just has 2 wires and a Pot is just a variable resistor not some mystical piece of electronic wizardry it should be wired to the Iwaver circuit board just like the Iwaver pot was.\r\n\r\n   So far its a no-brainer, however:\r\n\r\n3. Since the Iwaver potentiometer and the SE potentiometers do not have the same resistance values (a guess I dont remember) and the desired steering limits are bound to be different you have to make changes in the perceived resistance value to set the limits where you want them.  There are several ways to do it I chose to put a 2.2K ohm resistor between the Center and Clockwise (C) potentiometer posts, in other words the yellow and blue Iwaver Pot wires.  Then with a few adjustments of the centering pot on the IW circuit board and the position screw of the SE I centered the steering, with the result being that the wheels stop turning just a hair shy of hitting the chassis, an electrical stop is always preferable to a mechanical one.\r\n\r\nThe photo should give you an idea what the posts on the Pot are/do.  CC is the Counter Clockwise post, and C is the Clockwise post, the down arrow is the Center post.\r\n\r\n[img:cc56175806]http://lbspd.com/v-web/gallery/albums/album49/Potentiometer.sized.jpg[/img:cc56175806]\r\n\r\nAnd here is a good link to help you understand how parallel resistors work.  \r\n[urlhttp://www.physics.uoguelph.ca/tutorials/ohm/Q.ohm.intro.parallel.html[/url] [/url]'),(37546,'c0f8aaca8d','no, sorry :-(');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37549,'4185812979','FYI - I sent that Jeep body out this afternoon via regular mail I guess.  I\'m not too familiar with the services the Post office offers.  Should get to you in a couple days though.  Thanks.'),(37550,'47d9b4f3fa','FYI - I sent that Civic body out this afternoon via regular mail I guess.  I\'m not too familiar with the services the Post office offers.  Should get to you in a couple days though.  Thanks.'),(36580,'28c9994dbd','What the hell?....\r\n\r\nHonestly man I am in school there is no way I could have accepted that mail at that time. Unless they delivered it to my house and I am still unaware of it. It is the 13th right now, and I still never got a hold of my stuff. That is fuckin wierd! \r\n\r\nIf I am not home what usually happens is that they deliver to my house, and then if not there to accept it I have it saved at the local post officer (Shoppers Drug Mart) Then I get a notice in the mail saying I have to pick it up, but I did not even get that? \r\n\r\nThe only thing I can think of is that my dad accepted it, and has not told me that I recieved a package. The only problem is.....why havent you recieved your stuff? This is pissing me off because I did not want to waste my money shippin stuff, especially to you becuase it was a smoothe agreement. \r\n\r\nRight now it is 11:30, once my dad gets home from thier dinner dance night or w.e, I will ask him if anything came through.'),(36582,'70b342cf44','Sure do. :-o \r\n\r\nI guess you need a set. :idea: \r\n\r\nWhats your addy?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37382,'9f33624834','Thats quite a bit of stuff there man. Looks good too. My guess would be $150 US or so, but I\'m not to sure(I\'m not the best at guesstimating prices). If i had the money to spare, i might just take it off your hands, but I\'m saving for a RC10TC4 RTR, and a few things to get my DSM running. Ask around, maybe some one can buy it from you. If it isnt sold later and I have the money, I might just buy it.'),(36587,'60af59e655','Wow, in this post: http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7272 you say u used putty? Where?! its so neat, lol i cant notice.'),(37564,'6b2a9adc91','no thanks, some other stuff arose :('),(37567,'de47d0c902','I just heard back from the guy, and it\'s off so anything that\'s &quot;ON HOLD&quot; is available.  I can\'t update the post from work because our proxy blocks off that link.  Go ahead and take your picks, let me know and I\'ll try to send it off tomorrow.'),(36589,'9cca0b2338','lol the Murc? You mean Murcielago....you never asked for it man?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36590,'1db47a88ba','Thanx.  There\'s putty for the side skirts, front and back body kit and there\'s is putty added to the foil to make it intigrate with the sides of the body smoothly.  The foil was originally for a bit celica.  There is also a peice of plastic from some packaging that makes the bottum of the front body kit.  I just cut it to shape and epoxied it on.  I don\'t have a picture of it before modeling it, but it\'s a bit AE86 Trueno.  You may be able to find a picture of it somewhere.  I looked, but I couldn\'t.'),(37390,'b6d9b57747','[quote:b6d9b57747=\"MafiaS\"]SuperFly I am trying to sell my Xmod stuff here is the list, i wanted to ask you how much you thought I could get for it...just looking around for opinions...Thanks for your time\r\n\r\n- 6 Cell Nissan 350z Xmods Chassis \r\n- Aluminum rear diff joints \r\n- aluminum front diff joints \r\n- Never used stock motor \r\n- Stock motor \r\n- Stage 2 white motor \r\n- ATOMIC PERFECT SHAFT (long) \r\n- Bearings set x 2 \r\n- Foam tires and Xmod rim package \r\n- Tons of extra slicks and tredded (soft) \r\n- Extra stock diff \r\n- Five star rims, (corvette) and 350 rims \r\n- Short (1), and Long (2) drive shafts \r\n- Aluminum Heat sinc \r\n- two extra plastic heat sincs \r\n- Stock steering rods (2) \r\n- Two extra sets of front and rear plastic arms \r\n\r\nadding to the list \r\n\r\n- AWD rear and front arms \r\n- AWD Differentials (X2) \r\n- Steering rod for better handling on turns (red one) \r\n\r\nBodies that come with the bundle.. \r\n\r\n- 350z (used on my custom track) \r\n\r\n- Black RSX body and body kit, put together and never ran (my model) \r\n\r\n- Used Skyline plus body kit \r\n\r\n- Subaro Impreza Cop car (Custom painted black with fake lights) \r\nplus comes with body extra\'s (blue and silver) \r\n\r\n- Mustang body custom painted, plus body kit \r\n\r\nAlso included in the bundle is... \r\n\r\nExtra PCB board, SERVO, and Chassis, I have included some of the parts to get it running. It needs the frequencies, and battery cases...[/quote:b6d9b57747]\r\n\r\nIt\'s really hard to say. I\'d guess at minumum $60, and maybe as much as $110. The thing that kills the value is that there\'s a newer model available.\r\n\r\nI\'m kind of in the same boat, I have a gen1 xmod with one of every original RS upgrade that I haven\'t driven in two years. I also have 3 MR01 Mini-Zs that I\'m thinkng about bundling up and selling. If I can\'t get a reasonable price, I\'ll just rip the boards out for other projects.'),(36595,'fa0707a1f5','Eh man I am dying over here for an EVO...how did you get it for free?\r\n\r\nIf you could scrunge up another one I would trade big for it, just let me know what kinda things you want and if you can still get it...\r\n\r\nPeace');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36597,'cb97ad8e52','sg219@hotmail.com is my Paypal\r\n\r\nWhatever to cover postage.  A buck or two.  Don\'t sweat it.\r\n\r\nI\'ll send them out monday. :-o'),(37558,'c50c3fa57b','I\'m updating the list because someone asked me to hold a bunch of bodies.  I\'ll mark them on the main thread.  But anything on the list is open for negotiation.  I also have some red, blue and a couple yellow ZZ motors.  \r\nI\'m gonna follow up with him to see if he\'s gonna get them or not.\r\n\r\nCome to think of it, he has me holding a lot of bodies so I\'ll message him now.  Let me know if anything he has on hold is something you\'re interested in.  I do have multiples of some of them and was gonna hold it for myself.'),(36605,'0899f7bcab','Wow, thanks dude! also..\r\n\r\nPintakasi is a traditional leisure time in every town fiesta (much like the palenque in Mexico) which originally meant Patron Saint, far from its present day meaning as a three-day cocking festival on the occasion of the town\'s feast for the saint patron. Up to now, no town fiesta is complete without a pintakasi. It has so captured the Filipinos\' fancy that during the Spanish times, one could hardly say which came first - the saints or the roosters. \r\n\r\nThe passion for sabong is rooted in the Filipino\'s fondness for fast and exciting action. By nature, it reflects the Filipino culture of brevity. The gaffs or the thin and keen slasher knives attached on the cock\'s heel are like the sharp, shining, long bolos that our brave forefathers used against the Spaniards.'),(36613,'93a6f952a5','[quote:93a6f952a5=\"sg219\"]Got 4 right here in my hand. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n$2.19 and they\'re yours.  Seriously, why not 219?   :wobble: \r\n\r\nIf you gotta do MO, thats fine.\r\n\r\nDrop me your addy and I\'ll get them out Monday afternoon.\r\n\r\nMike Smalley Jr.\r\n3918 Inland Ave.\r\nWest Mifflin, Pa  15122[/quote:93a6f952a5]\r\n\r\nCan I send ya cash as its not that much?\r\n\r\naddy:\r\nAaron W. Olmsted\r\n1941 Sayers Road\r\nBastrop, Texas 78602\r\n\r\nthanks man if cash is ok I will get it out monday! Appreciate the deal.  :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37825,'ddbf9947e6','[quote:ddbf9947e6=\"SuperFly\"]hey man-\r\n\r\nI\'ll take the IW04 parts. How about if you package that up and send it to me and let me know how much actual shipping was and I\'ll paypal ya $5 + shipping. Don\'t want you to use up all the loot just shipping it.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nsuperfly[/quote:ddbf9947e6]\r\n\r\nIt went out today.\r\n\r\nstuff+PP fees+shipping.....$7.00 total\r\n\r\nsg219@hotmail.com\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike'),(37587,'627f228204','If you want to save some money then wait until I get the Firelap 2.0 modded and running.  So far stock it\'s pretty much the same thing as the Iwaver 02.  The chassis, tires and springs are exactly the same.  It even says &quot;This is Iwaver&quot; on the bottom.  The PCB is different, but it seems to operate pretty much the same.  It has the same steering strength and after I get the fets and hot motor installed it will probably run very similar.  I\'m still waiting on parts for the Plasma-atomic motor and the ball differential which should be here within the next five days or so.  I already have the fets and will probably get them installed Saturday.\r\n\r\nJust remind me about Wed. or so.  Otherwise the Iwaver 02 is a safe bet.  Just stay away from the Porsche Concept body.  I had that originally.  It was crap.  Didn\'t fit on the chassis correctly, the tires rubbed on the body in the front and the back.  And when you hit a bump the lip on the front of the car grabs the ground and ends up cracking off eventually.  One side was higher than the other too.  I had to rip off the body clips and epoxy them back in the right place after dremmeling a little.'),(36920,'d02fc497be','I\'m bored and thought I\'d give a howdy. :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nSo that contest judging was a clisterfuck huh? I glad you spoke up. I wanted to say something in the last contest even, but before I was a mod I was one of the ones that threw a bitch, and questioned their judging in that middle of the road contest, so I just didn\'t want to be the bitch that always bitches. :lol: \r\n\r\nAnd how about DT with that Big Kahuna is back shit?  :lol: \r\nApparently he\'s still trying to comprehend what you meant about passive aggressive BS. Dense ass mofo. :roll:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBeen digging my Xmod H2. Now that I think about it, I haven\'t charged anything else since I got it. \r\n\r\nBeen bored with music. Been mostly just listening to the Reverend Horton Heat lately, because it reminds of the old school rods. Man, you gotta check out that Car Kulture Deluxe mag if you come across it. The whole mag just has that really retro, but at the same time kinda punk attitude. I\'ve been getting it at Wakmartm its bi-monthly. I always wanted to build a rat rod, and looking through this mag really makes me wish I had a place to work on a project. I want an old Model A to sand rust off of on the weekends. :-(');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37657,'11f42ac284','Try this;  Soft suspension in the front and hard suspension in the back.  \r\n\r\nYou see, when you slow down, for example before cornering, the weight of the car is transfered to the front, puting more weight on the front wheels.  This can create over-steer.  Over steer is when you try to turn and it turns more than you want or spins out.  With more weight on the front wheels, you have more friction/traction on the front wheels.  Softer springs should help that as it will give with added pressure instead of puting more weight on the front wheels.  You can\'t stop all the weight transfer though.\r\n\r\nYou\'ll notice during acceleration you loose a little steering until you get up to speed.  That\'s because the weight is transfered to the back of the car, therefore taking weight off the front wheels.  With less weight you get less traction/friction.  So, you should get more under steer during acceleration.  Hard springs in the back will put more pressure on the back wheels. This helps to take advantage of the torque.  Softer springs will give and you\'ll loose some traction.  Also, hard spring in the back keep some of the weight from transfering back so the front wheels don\'t loose so much traction during acceleration.\r\n\r\nAlso, you can adjust the steering power on the transmitter.  This helps the steering give a little instead of jerking the car.  I have my Kyosho adjusted somewhere between 80~90% power and continue to adjust it depending on terrain.\r\n\r\nIf you still have oversteer with this setup, then try throwing on some soft tires in the back and hard/slick tires in the front.  You may end up with understeer, but you can get use to it and learn to race with it as opposed to over steer which makes you spin out.\r\n\r\nThe other thing that I have and I love is a rear oil shock for my Kyosho.  That thing is cool as hell.  When I hit a bump the car doesn\'t bounce as much so I don\'t loose so much traction.  This doesn\'t completely relate to balancing the damper system except you can get different oils to make the suspension stiffer or softer as well as you can still use springs with the oil shock to stiffen the suspension.  So it makes the rear suspension more adjustable.\r\n\r\nA ball diff can also help.  I have an Iwaver ball diff and it works very well.  You can adjust those as well to help with cornering.  Tighten them for more torque or loosen them for better cornering.  My Atomic ball diff is crap.\r\n\r\nLastly, tires.........  Tire wear like you\'ve noticed plays a part, but not as big of a part as people think.  Tire quality on the other hand is a different story all together.  My answer to that is Gandini foams, at least in the back.  If the tires you have are working good on the track, then you probably don\'t need them.  But, if you want to make this car faster via fets, hot motor and/or lithiums, the Kyosho and Iwaver line of tires wont cut it.  They don\'t have enough traction.\r\n\r\nUltimately this is all theory.  Track time is going to be the end all.  You should go with the theory, but be prepared to adjust.  There are many things that affect balance and steering as you can tell.  You may find that on the surface that you are driving on you only need medium springs in the front instead of soft.  OR etc., etc., etc......\r\n\r\nHope this helps and I\'m jealous.  I currently need a racing partner.  I\'ve been utilizing my wife and a few other people to run comparisons.  It gets the job done, but they\'re not seasoned racers by far.\r\n\r\n :-)'),(36662,'3542ca49cc','So far I\'ve found the road radials with the kyosho hard foams, some titanium screws and stock diff parts, the gpm front gearbox, and the radio of course. damn. I screwed up a little man. These will be out ASAP.\r\n\r\n-JNY');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36855,'6694eb8bdb','Thanks for the link, I was wondering where I was gunna get it cut:???: but these ppl do it for you. As soon as I get my design concrete, I\'ll let them have it.\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(37932,'d89fa965a7','[quote:d89fa965a7=\"HACHI-RYOKU\"]Can do.  It will be a few months before I really get into production mode, but if I produce one that kicks ass before then, then I\'ll send it to you for free if you give it a review.  In fact, the first one I want to work on will be a spiral armeture.  With a spiral armeture, fat comm and winding for torque with some good neo mags and a bb case it should have some interesting performance.  That may be exactly what you want.  Wont know until I make it though.  I\'ll keep everybody posted.\r\n\r\nI don\'t mind giving a few out for free at first so I can get some reviews on my motors from other people besides myself.  If I really want to sell these motors and make a few ducks off it, then I need to get some good advertisement.\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to send one out to you first.[/quote:d89fa965a7]\r\n\r\nSounds promising, i would be more than happy to do a full write up etc. I also have a speedchecker i could test it out on.\r\n\r\nSo are these mainly going to be torque motors or top speed?\r\n\r\nMaybe make the winds for top speed 25 or so, then slap some neo\'s in there to make the torque jump.\r\n\r\nJust throwing out ideas.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37635,'ae6a0dc832','Well then I\'ll just take the iW board. \r\n\r\nYou wouldn\'t happen to have any MRS4 stuff you\'d like to get rid of, maybe some electronics or alloy? (I already have a TX)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36680,'a8c99833f9','Pleasure doing bizz with ya!'),(37237,'dc5f12b567','[quote:dc5f12b567=\"DarkTari\"]I\'ll see what they have in stock.  As far as returned stuff, I lucked up on that Evo, they don\'t get too much stuff back at the one by the job.\r\nI\'ll letcha know next week sometime!\r\n\r\n :cool:[/quote:dc5f12b567]Thanx DT, only cars tho no trucks :o\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx'),(37868,'34438f0cf0','[quote:34438f0cf0=\"MafiaS\"]The Skyline is black, with yellow side add ons or w.e, im not sure if its the whole body upgrade but there is quite a bit.\r\n\r\nit\'s condition, if your picky like me you\'d wanna touch it up with your own personality, but its not that bad at all, could actually make it look really good.\r\n\r\n350 sick is copper as you know, and its condition has been run before, not that bad...\r\n\r\nshow me an offer and its yours man![/quote:34438f0cf0]\r\n\r\nThat info is really shallow, would you be able to get any pics?'),(37844,'fd77c7e24f','[quote:fd77c7e24f=\"HirotoR34\"]definitely, I was thinking deans would do charging duties...I\'ll do you up a custom shell. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to add a bit o green :-o[/quote:fd77c7e24f]\r\n\r\nI\'ll get them out ASAP. :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37689,'6119c8372f','sounds great to me. Let me know when you are ready....thanks pimp :cool:'),(36763,'75df8f7e3c','Hey hachi sorry to bother ya. I know you got a ton of things to do including that sweet project you are performing with all the comparisons. I just wanted to ask for your opinion on this.\r\n\r\nThe other night i was playing with my Gen1 xmod and after a good half hour of play I realized one wheel was not giving its full potential of power. \r\n\r\ni am currently running the car on RWD. And when I hold the car up and rev only one tire spins nice and free, the other seems to not spin as fast. I am pretty sure there is a problem with my stock diff, but should I try and fix it, and how can I do it?\r\n\r\ni heard of replacing the stock diff with the AWD diff...Could I put an AWD diff in the front and back? Would that work properly? \r\n\r\nWhat is your best opinion on this? \r\n\r\nThanks for your time!'),(36764,'420aff8802','is this a program? it sounds cool can I get  a link to it? \r\n\r\nthanks man! \r\n\r\nAaron');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37253,'4a932101bd','Thanks so far, I really want to body tops to do some Xmod refurbishing and resale here on the island. The lights are just sos we can race till later in the evening :-o\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(36712,'94cb4fded7','Alright man just keep me posted. If you have any questions just ask ok man!'),(36966,'4366444b4f','Skyline kid, I was wondering...if you still wanted those Zipzap bodies.\r\n\r\nI need pieces for the AWD kit. I have the aluminum shafts in the front, just need the arms and the little pin connecting the diff. You have any extra AWD pieces? Let me know what you got.\r\n\r\nDo you have any hard springs, or suspension parts?\r\n\r\nJust let me know what you are willing to give off and the stuff will be sent ASAP...I can actually send them tomorrow after school. Hope you get this soon man!'),(36968,'f87ffdde6f','Hey have you gotten a chance to ship the stuff yet?\r\n\r\nAnd another thing i noticed the break when using my friends Kyosho controller only works from reverse-foward would this be fixed by using a half eight controller?'),(37845,'74d22a1381','[quote:74d22a1381=\"steelwoolghandi\"]Hey man just wanted to check if Bird and you got the stuff I sent? I never heard and just wanted to check.\r\n\r\ngot the lights man working on hooking things up! if I could ever get a little time off from working all the time.\r\n\r\noh kamen emailed me says he wants to buy some stuff from you and is personal check ok?  :lol:[/quote:74d22a1381]\r\n\r\nTotally forgot to drop you a PM.  The stuff came and I gave it all to Bird.  He said thanks.\r\n\r\n\r\nRemember this, its a hobby.  No need to rush on a project. :-o \r\n\r\nKamen. :o \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLater, \r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37846,'bda757953f','you never told me if the Fets from your friend were upgrade fets. And wheather I should try a stack and if it would make a difference.'),(36715,'56f29fbb21','I believe I still have the 2.7 motors...Anything else? What you offerin bud?'),(37289,'9349e502e8','No I don\'t. I dont realy know if I can drift better than you or not on a game-will never know till we go head to head. I was just saying that to bullshit; you were getting on my nerves with your drifting sigs. \r\n\r\nHowever, I said I could drift better than you in real life, with a real car, and a drivers liscence. I\'ve drifted a minivan(I\'m real proud of that). You\'re not even old enough to drive.'),(37692,'0880855300','Its a orange fade to green, you\'ll see, im guessing u havent got it yet :-)'),(36725,'ec3d11f834','ma boi!\r\n\r\nI got three of them I wanna let go...they are in perfect, i mean mint condition...I ran my zipzap chassis without the bodies. I broke the chassis real early and then threw it out, and i never had those bodies running at all.\r\n\r\nI have the yellow Mitsubishi EVO\r\n\r\nNew Corvette (Maroon or w.e)\r\n\r\nand the old stingray vette ....\r\n\r\nLet me know if you want em I can ship them out as soon as you say go buddy!'),(36726,'776e19a9ad','[url]http://www.mini-zracer.com/forums/showthread.php?p=212219#post212219[/url]');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37696,'059d2cdf6e','so how\'s $10 + shipping grab ya?'),(36926,'6d6e7c62ea','None local here in Vancouver, kinda sucks.  But I\'ll give you all of the local forums so you can look around.  All of the R/C shops are pretty far away, Richmond, Surrey, Burnaby, Coquitlam and whatever else.  There\'s a couple other shops, you can maybe find those in the phonebook.  There\'s Racing Devil, MagicBox Hobbies (Kerrisdale; only a couple kits, mainly model kits), and someother places too.\r\n\r\nYou really should go tomorrow to Nanospeed (really close, should be a 15minute drive for you), there\'s some Iwaver/Mini-Z racing going on.  It\'s really cool and a lot of friendly people.  I\'m not going to make it because I\'m still not better, it really sucks.  Here\'s the link to all the info: http://www.minirc.ca/forums/showthread.php?t=163\r\n\r\nwww.minirc.ca\r\nwww.nanospeed.ca\r\nwww.iwaver.ca\r\nwww.savagerc.com\r\nwww.rcpistop.com\r\nwww.vmar.ca\r\n\r\nIf you are really into off-road, the scale crawling and all that jazz, go to www.ripper7racing.com and talk to Davemud.  He\'s the pro when it comes to all that stuff.\r\n\r\nIf ya need any more info, lemme know.'),(36917,'e94218687f','Yo man, are there any other rc places in vancouver that i should know about? I live right downtown, (Homer &amp; Smithe)\r\n\r\nOr other rc people for that matter, heh');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36918,'6d6e7c62ea','None local here in Vancouver, kinda sucks.  But I\'ll give you all of the local forums so you can look around.  All of the R/C shops are pretty far away, Richmond, Surrey, Burnaby, Coquitlam and whatever else.  There\'s a couple other shops, you can maybe find those in the phonebook.  There\'s Racing Devil, MagicBox Hobbies (Kerrisdale; only a couple kits, mainly model kits), and someother places too.\r\n\r\nYou really should go tomorrow to Nanospeed (really close, should be a 15minute drive for you), there\'s some Iwaver/Mini-Z racing going on.  It\'s really cool and a lot of friendly people.  I\'m not going to make it because I\'m still not better, it really sucks.  Here\'s the link to all the info: http://www.minirc.ca/forums/showthread.php?t=163\r\n\r\nwww.minirc.ca\r\nwww.nanospeed.ca\r\nwww.iwaver.ca\r\nwww.savagerc.com\r\nwww.rcpistop.com\r\nwww.vmar.ca\r\n\r\nIf you are really into off-road, the scale crawling and all that jazz, go to www.ripper7racing.com and talk to Davemud.  He\'s the pro when it comes to all that stuff.\r\n\r\nIf ya need any more info, lemme know.'),(36938,'3f0a92070e','[quote:3f0a92070e=\"hue35\"]\r\nYeah, where the hell did that even come from? It was just all of a sudden DT is in full-tilt action... everytime I read that muthafucka\'s writing, I hear it as 50% Foghorn Leghorn + 50% Mr. T... [b:3f0a92070e]&quot;I say.. I say... HERE\'S HOW IT\'S GONNA BE, PIMP!!!&quot;[/b:3f0a92070e] Jesus Christ already.[/quote:3f0a92070e] :lol: :lol: That\'s funny as shit. \r\n\r\nI just got a crazy idea. Ya know, you had that killer ass prize package put together... What if just out of no where you\'re alternate ego popped up out if no where and ran his own contest. Might cause some controversy, would at least give DT a taste of his own medicine. Hell, you\'d probably be able to get Cabo behind it, and have Chedderspreader announce it. Maybe with it being all MS stuff, it coulf be an OG Bit themed contest.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know, just something that happened to pop into my head. :???: \r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e][quote:3f0a92070e=\"crazydave\"]Been digging my Xmod H2. Now that I think about it, I haven\'t charged anything else since I got it.  [/quote:3f0a92070e]\r\nYeah man, I\'ve been diggin\' the looks of those... yours in particular. The silver H1 SSMT chop is badass. I\'ll have to check one out at the shack. I\'m just reluctant to open the door to a new platform. How much do you have into yours?[/quote:3f0a92070e]Oh shit, you just opened a can of something. :lol: \r\nLet\'s see\r\n$60 car\r\n$17 motor\r\n$20 bearings\r\n$16 offroad set\r\n$16 second offroad set after I screwed the first dyed job :lol: \r\n$16 AWD\r\n\r\nSo that\'s what? $145? Son of a bitch, I could of had a Mini-t. :lol: \r\n\r\nThat\'s ok, I dig how the Xmod is more true to scale, and its plenty for indoors. :-o \r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e][quote=&quot;crazydave&quot;]There was a great episode of &quot;Rides&quot; a few weeks back that was basically a top-notch documentary on the Rat Rod scene... it\'s almost too much of a scene for me. Like, those folks just [i:3f0a92070e]know[/i:3f0a92070e] they\'re the coolest motherfuckers on the planet... and they are, but they don\'t have to [i:3f0a92070e]know[/i:3f0a92070e] it.  :lol:[/quote:3f0a92070e]I wish I caught that episode, I\'ll have to keep an eye out.\r\n\r\nI hear ya about those guys being just a bit too cool. I could see myself, even if I built my dream rat rod, I\'d probably be ripped for using a 350 and not a flat head, or using a fiberglass body panels, when I couldn\'t find or afford steel ones. Its like you can\'t just jump into that scene half assed. :-( \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e]Work has been about to fucking kill me dead.... the pressure is just too much. I\'m working on this brochure that was WAY the fuck over-estimated by our account execs, but the client bit. Now the pressure is on me to make this 8-page POS look like it\'s worth the 90k it\'s gonna cost, and that doesn\'t even include printing... it\'s about 3x more expensive than it should be. The folks around here who sold this nightmare don\'t really understand the problem, but they sense my stress level... they\'re scared as shit, which is where half of my stress comes from in the first place. [/quote:3f0a92070e]I can totally ralate, but on a much smaller level. When I was doing banner ads, the customers were only paying $30. I know people doing work of my quality charge much more, so I wasn\'t too stressed, but I had a hard time even rationaling making it worth $30 to them. Then my buddy dropped a $200 logo design in my lap, and I just had to make it worth $200. I don\'t really know what  $200 logo looks like. I think I kinda dropped the ball on that one, because my buddy had to tweak it to their taste... but a 90k catalog! :shock: I feel your stress.\r\n\r\n[quote:3f0a92070e]And, on top of that, we got a new designer dude,..[/quote:3f0a92070e]I\'ve been dealing with this POS for over a year now, shows up a half an hour late, making me late to pick up my kid from school. On top of my job, I do 90% of his job for him, just so the whole night crew don\'t get screwed, then he spends an hour a day just to bitch that I do nothing. So fuck that, I want all crazydave on his ass this last week, stopped doing his job, and he\'s about an inch from getting fired.\r\n\r\nGo hue35 on his ass dude, I\'m telling ya, I ready to kill all the dipshits.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36939,'ac63023a53','found a flash plugin for DW on the exchange. makes great little gallery swf files.\r\n\r\nstoli.ca\r\n\r\npassword is bumbum.'),(36943,'4772ce04c5','Nah, that wasn\'t me man.'),(37569,'5a52641091','sup man?\r\n\r\nJust letting you know, you\'re posting alot. And they\'re all useless posts. I\'m not getting on your back or anything, but post count means nothing here. Plus the pimps don\'t like it when useless stuff is posted. Also your digging up oldish threads and posting stuff like &quot;sweet ride&quot;. Doesn\'t fly here.\r\n\r\nAgain, I\'m not getting on you, just giving you a heads up for how things are done here. \r\n\r\n\r\nKeep cool\r\nMaxx'),(36950,'8abb8e0f86','http://k-mac-plastics.net/\r\n\r\nthis looks promising.'),(36951,'aba123ffa1','[quote:aba123ffa1=\"pimpsmurf\"]I rule, or suck depending on how you look at it. I found the kyosho board. Sorry about that. I\'ll go ahead and include all this stuff I picked up on sale.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:aba123ffa1]\r\n\r\nDo you think you will be able to ship all that stuff you found etc. this week?\r\n\r\nAlso i was wondering if you knew where i could find replacement screws for the gpm parts, looked at the screw packages on rcxmini but they didnt appear to have the right threads.'),(36979,'ec45c488fb','Cool, that\'s kinda what I was thinkin, but what do you mean by &quot;tubby&quot;?\r\n\r\nDid you mean the body, or chassis, cause he wanted it cause of the MM chassis over the RM one.\r\n\r\n\r\nthanks for the insight.  He also ordered the 911 Carrera body to go with it, that fucker..');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (36989,'356c344eb8','Can you sell me the skylinefront clip?'),(36990,'ed0db50142','Sorry where did you see the front clip?'),(37173,'d542c6530a','i\'ve never seen that mount, looks like a great idea! if it does what it says then you should be fine.\r\nyou will most likely use mr02 h plates with it (either mm or rm, there\'s a difference).\r\nthe back end of 01 and 02 h plates are the same, it\'s only the front bit that screws to the main chassis that is different.\r\n\r\nyup, the foams rock! and we were both running them in that vid. they grip everything except rcp tracks i\'m told (by superfly).\r\nthe differences between the soft/med/hard are minor, kinda like fine tuning adjustments.\r\ni\'ve tried em all, the softs wore quicker than the others but not by a lot. you should be fine with the mediums.\r\ni only run em on the rear, rubbers up front.'),(37634,'07b10ce030','[quote:07b10ce030=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I can make the payment now, I was just making sure of my purchase. What can i use the lipo pack on? Can I charge it with the cheapo chargers that come with lith pro kits?[/quote:07b10ce030]\r\n\r\nIf your talking about the black cell phone type charger that would be a no.\r\n\r\nI reccomend this type charger to use for it.\r\n\r\nhttp://teammnm.net/product_info.php/products_id/70?osCsid=94bb28890e6f1c490de162bc4d31bc35\r\n\r\nYou can use the lipo pack on basically anything that will get a good runtime off of it. Since it has a very good discharge rate it is able to power very hot motors without pulling a muscle.'),(37621,'6c2a8af979','Which body do you have? I noticed my friends Saleen body to be rather long for an MM fit, it was longer than my F50 Ferrari RM fit.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37642,'3b5cebe04e','[quote:3b5cebe04e=\"Maxximum Attack\"]I would like it, but I don\'t want to buy a charger etc. I\'ll buy that stuff when I\'m shopping for batts.\r\n\r\nI only wanted it cuz I had the cheapo charger doing nothing. Plus I\'d need a board harness.\r\n\r\nSo just the board. I\'ll send you $13, shipping for phatboi was under a buck. That cool? \r\n\r\nHey, you got any Xmod stuff? Since I last asked?\r\n\r\nMaxx[/quote:3b5cebe04e]\r\n\r\nYeah sounds like a deal man!\r\n\r\nNah dont have much xmod stuff since last time, only thing i have thats noticebly cool is some blue alloy xmod rims from betty K. Beat up around the edges. They use mini-z tires.'),(37172,'c19e3414e6','Later generation 01 pcb\'s have brakes (not 100% they were made available in ready sets as the only ones I\'ve ever personally seen were boards only)...mine\'s an older one without though.\r\n\r\nre:motor mount....  http://www.pnracing.us/new/product.php?show=product&amp;id=90\r\n\r\nI was going by this.  Say\'s it\'s usuable with the MR01 or an MR02-RM and can use either the MR01 ball dif or add another bearing(?) and use a MR02 ball diff.\r\n\r\nI would guess it requires some modification to a MR01 H-plate to fit the narrow chassis mount on the MR02. That\'s easily done though.\r\n\r\nWhen I \'stopped\' with the MR01 the MR02 hadn\'t been released so it\'s like learning all over again.\r\n\r\nre:foams\r\n\r\nYes, yes.  had a look at those on Ausmicro!  Looks like must have items!  Not sure I\'d have a use for the softs (just how soft are they?) but the mediums and hards got my attention.  You were running them on the chassis you were racing in ph2t\'s back yard right? The conrete racing video..'),(37512,'de45723866','holy crap! that could explain it! :lol: \r\n\r\nmakes me wonder if that\'s why the steering was weak for me!\r\n\r\ni used to run it on a 1:10 scale track so the shorter travel, slower responding steering didn\'t matter so much.\r\n\r\nif i was to try for more throw with the servo i\'d get a resistor with a value around 5kohm (4.7kohm is more common, it\'s good enough). you want to solder it between the 2 servo pot wires. you can do that on the pot or on the pcb. whenever i\'ve done it i\'ve used a surface mount resistor and soldered it on the pcb, across the 2 servo pot tabs.\r\n\r\nwhat this does is electronically fool the servo into moving more than it thinks it is.\r\nyou\'ll probably find it\'s too much throw and will need to adjust the steering sensitivity accordingly.\r\n\r\nonce you swap out the motor and add the resistor i think we might have it worked out.\r\ni\'d personally swap the motor first and see how it reacts before adding the resistor when you add the mr01 pcb. the kyosho pcb has a much stronger steering curcuit.\r\n\r\nkeep me posted :-)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37169,'2f65e3e2a7','Hi\r\n\r\nCool, hope to see some modded ZZMT pics from you then.  :-o \r\nI picked up the jeep body off ebay, as radio shack doesnt make it\r\nanymore. Cost me an arm and a leg for it.  Xmods are pretty neat,\r\nIve got a few. 3 mustangs(cobra,65,06) and both trucks.\r\n-clint\r\n\r\n[quote:2f65e3e2a7=\"spanky\"]whats up me and my friends have bought zip zaps mt and we found the supension artical and was wondering two things. One is where did u get the jeep body and have u herd about xmod. This my first time login on to the bitpimps web page so im not sure on how im gonna get this message.\r\nThanks \r\n\r\nSpanky grin[/quote:2f65e3e2a7]'),(37620,'a19a9e1e1f','nah man, no need to pm.\r\n\r\ni\'m glad you pointed out my error, we\'re all about correct information here at bp\'s :-) \r\n\r\nkeep up the good work :-o'),(37688,'048f6c51b3','twenty shipped is cool, i\'d say another 10 or so for the controllers\r\n\r\njust checkin with my uncle to see if u can send the money to his paypal account...\r\n\r\nmsg me back and we can further discuss this later i have work'),(37105,'b4e4b7768b','Hello Clint\r\n\r\nHere is what I got you down for:\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver \r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET	$7.74	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET	$0.00	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET 	$15.54	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS -\r\n1PC SET 	$7.74	1\r\n\r\nSub	$34.11	\r\nS&amp;H 	$3.00	\r\nTotal	$37.11	\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.59 off of GPM\'s regular\r\nprice.\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me now as\r\nsoon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com. \r\nPlease include your user name in the notes on PayPal.	\r\n\r\n\r\nThank You\r\nCJ\r\n\r\nBTW your email address on here didn\'t work.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37787,'57aa2be894','Hello,\r\n\r\nI took a look into the postage, seems like for a package up to a pound in weight the shipping is $17.50 (air mail parcel post).  Not sure if it\'s worth it at that price.  I can check with UPS to if you would like.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nRich'),(37788,'d13ff81118','Hi mate!\r\nThanks for checking the shipping, it\'s a lot of $$.\r\ndid you meant 17$ with boxes?\r\nI think it should weight less without them,I\'m just interested in the bits, have none with boxes.\r\nWould you sell even a few bits?\r\n\r\nsee ya and thanks a lot,\r\n\r\nMax'),(37789,'d13ff81118','Hi mate!\r\nThanks for checking the shipping, it\'s a lot of $$.\r\ndid you meant 17$ with boxes?\r\nI think it should weight less without them,I\'m just interested in the bits, have none with boxes.\r\nWould you sell even a few bits?\r\n\r\nsee ya and thanks a lot,\r\n\r\nMax'),(37167,'221817ccef','If I\'ve been reading right I can simply swap a MM mount with a RM mount? Then I\'d just have to switch from a MM body to a RM body?\r\n\r\nmy plan...\r\n\r\nBuy a MR02-MM ready set. Drive the snot out of it while I\'m here and then when we move drop the stock rear end back into my MR01 and put a MR01/MR02RM motor mount into the 02 and use my 01 ball diff.\r\n\r\nEver try tin-car rears on a Z? \r\nAll the ones I\'ve got a 13mm wide, but narrowing them is a breeze. Vary from soft to quite firm, but dirt cheap ($1-2US/pair).'),(37164,'7cdf7834af','struth!! it better be good then! :-) \r\n\r\ni\'m pretty sure you\'ll be happy, they do everything they\'re supposed to. and they do it well.\r\nafter bb\'s your next upgrade should be a ball diff, helps immensly with traction control :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37703,'42e38a7914','Sounds good, remind me later on 2morrow...'),(37704,'cd9ea11158','I have a extra unopened Iwaver02 New design I\'d be willing to part with for your testing.  I\'ll take $79.99 + S&amp;H and even through in an extra chassis plate.'),(37191,'6480e47d2d','lol That\'s gonna look sweet man!'),(37684,'f3291460cf','Your package was shipped today give it the usual 1-2 weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37199,'','hey when u made ur mt to flex, was the stiring a problem after u put it back together? The antenna is kinda in the way and the stiring does not want to spring back. Do u have any solutions  :???:'),(37200,'6f3593baba','[quote:6f3593baba=\"spanky\"]hey when u made ur mt to flex, was the stiring a problem after u put it back together? The antenna is kinda in the way and the stiring does not want to spring back. Do u have any solutions  ???[/quote:6f3593baba]\r\n\r\nsteering wasnt a problem after the mod...but in general that steering motor is weak.\r\n\r\nyou can replace the steering motor with a stronger red zz motor.'),(37690,'be83880bc2','[quote:be83880bc2=\"Maxximum Attack\"][quote:be83880bc2=\"Tuner1989\"]Your package was shipped today give it the usual 1-2 weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:be83880bc2]Thank you[/quote:be83880bc2]\r\n\r\n\r\nNo problem man let me know when you get it. :-o');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37209,'cf6454774f','&quot;&lt;--- working on new sig, can someone give this an effect of motion. It looks like an action shot, but can someone add some motion blur in photoshop or something. Thanx &quot;\r\n\r\ndude, do you still need that done? i saw it today(monday). got it done.\r\ni can e mail it to you. see if you like it. what\'s your e mail?'),(37210,'e447bbbcec','it\'s cool man, sessiz did it for me already :-) thanx pimp'),(37301,'c83c73728f','Just picked up the package today. Nice birthday gift ahha! \r\n\r\nThanks for everything. The spring set too, thanks alot!\r\n\r\nWhich steering rod did you give me? Is it better for turning, or for straights?'),(37781,'9ff9ef8e12','Hey man just got your pm now...\r\n\r\nok as for price big guy I feel your judgement is good enough, i\'m not sure how much shipping costs are but what ever you feel is right is cool.\r\n\r\nsend you cashity cash to \r\n\r\nsstirpe@sympatico.ca\r\n\r\nDon\'t forget your address! lol...I should be able to ship in the next few days!!!\r\n\r\nTake it easy'),(37318,'b18d85c4dd','[quote:b18d85c4dd=\"sg219\"][quote:b18d85c4dd=\"cj\"]These were not in the first order.\r\n\r\nPART ID	DESCRIPTION	Price 	Silver	Black	Green\r\nXME012A	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME012B	ALLOY FRONT GEAR BOX BACK COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET	$0.00	0	0	1\r\nXME013A	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX FRONT COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$15.54	0	0	1\r\nXME013B	ALLOY REAR GEAR BOX REAR COVER WITH SCREWS - 1PC SET 	$7.74	0	0	1\r\nXME330LAN	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR LANCER) - 1PC	$5.90	0	0	1\r\nXME330MUS	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR MUSTANG) - 1PC	$3.84	0	0	1\r\nXET330FORD	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR TRUCKIN) - 1PC	$6.90	1	0	0\r\nXET330HUM	ALLOY FRONT BODY LOCK PLATE (FOR HUMMER) - 1PC	$5.90	1	0	0\r\n\r\nActual	$53.54	 	 	 \r\n10.00%	$5.35	 	 	 \r\nSub	$58.89			\r\nS&amp;H	$3.00			\r\nTotal	$61.89			\r\n\r\nThat is a Savings of $13.41 Off of GPM\'s regular price.\r\n\r\nIf you have any additions or corrections let me know as soon as possible.  My PayPal is cjellis@yahoo.com.  Please include your user name in the notes on PayPal.\r\n\r\nIf you do reply by February 11th  your request will not be ordered.[/quote:b18d85c4dd]\r\n\r\nJust silver and green.\r\n\r\nI won\'t be able to pay until this Saturday, after P-day clears.\r\n\r\nWhats the status of everything else?  The rest of the silver, all the green and the diffs?\r\n\r\nI need a complete set so I can start putting things together.\r\n\r\nHow much longer?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nMike[/quote:b18d85c4dd]\r\n\r\nGot you just Silver and Green.\r\n\r\nI have recieved so far from the first DXME009T(2), XME018A(Silver), XME039F(Silver), XME039R(Silver),  XME303(silver), XET021(Silver), XET022(silver), XET028(silver), XET030(Silver), XET114R(2 Silver), XET331F(Silver).  Some I may have sent you.\r\n\r\nI hope in the next shipment from them I get some green.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37320,'dc07c86e63','ok If you have a ps2 and need for speed undeground 2 that would be fun to drive on just messin around i understand now.'),(37344,'49ddeb725f','[quote:49ddeb725f=\"SHAUN\"]Would you be a moderater on my forum. I\'m thinkin your gonna say no cause i dont think ya like me.[/quote:49ddeb725f]\r\n\r\nOK.  I\'ve contacted you few times already and you have yet to reply.\r\n\r\nHow do you expect to run a forum if you don\'t let people sign-up or even reply to any questions or problems. :o \r\n\r\nThats allright, you just keep signing in and out of BP and ignoring PMs.   :-x \r\n\r\n\r\nI tried.  You didn\'t. :thebird:'),(37353,'ad64d673f3','Sorry, I just got the message I\'ll look into the problem.\r\n\r\nlata,\r\nshaun'),(37355,'10d5ce4cb2','It seem\'s to me that you have not activated your acoutn yet .'),(37356,'040b17b821','Hey man, i saw a post about you needing a set of zzse lights?  Do you still need some or did you get your hands on a set?\r\n\r\nTHey still had a set or two up at my RS,, if you cant get your hands on a set just let me know,, \r\n\r\nSTG'),(37808,'a2596c018e','I sent the stuff today...sorry for the delay...I woulda\' sent it right away...but school and homework was in the way...\r\n\r\nlol 7-10 days bro enjoy');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37816,'1edc344fbd','hey man-\r\n\r\nI\'ll take the IW04 parts. How about if you package that up and send it to me and let me know how much actual shipping was and I\'ll paypal ya $5 + shipping. Don\'t want you to use up all the loot just shipping it.\r\n\r\nthanks,\r\nsuperfly'),(37800,'359f3919ac','no worries man your stuff is still here..just let me know exactly when your pronto and the stuff will be shipped!'),(37801,'c80367f92b','Spamming shit (meaning putting up a link to something you\'re pushing/selling) aint cool round here. Maybe if you\'ve been here for awhile we\'ld be cool with you promoting your music but putting up a pic and a link to your shit on your first post aint gonna fly. If you don\'t understand I can elaborate. :-)'),(37805,'cb3a1c4370','You didn\'t offend me and if you think that\'s me going nuts, well, ya aint seen nothing yet. :-)'),(37864,'e4f355c01c','hey there! :-) \r\nyou\'re correct, the wheels were from a hot wheels car, &quot;tunerz&quot; to be exact.\r\nthis was around 3 years ago and i bought it locally (australia) so i\'m not sure if you\'ll find them around anymore. but i\'m sure there is plenty of toys out there to plunder with wheels that are just as good if not better :-o \r\n\r\ngood luck with the project, feel free to ask any questions :-)'),(37859,'b2c31db030','Thanks bro, the motor came a few days ago and looks great.  Ive never seen that much bubble wrap crammed into suck a tight space  :-o  lol\r\n\r\nThanks again, always a pleasure\r\n\r\nSTG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37388,'9f33624834','Thats quite a bit of stuff there man. Looks good too. My guess would be $150 US or so, but I\'m not to sure(I\'m not the best at guesstimating prices). If i had the money to spare, i might just take it off your hands, but I\'m saving for a RC10TC4 RTR, and a few things to get my DSM running. Ask around, maybe some one can buy it from you. If it isnt sold later and I have the money, I might just buy it.'),(37389,'f5fb91c693','That\'s cool man...If you want it when you got the chance you can have it for about 100 U.S.\r\n\r\nIt might still be here so no worries.'),(37854,'1fce917324','What\'s up, sorry i havent got back to you, ive been driving across cities for a few days back and forth playin soccer, and the tourny is finally over for me to relax.\r\n\r\nAnyhow i checked my emails today and my uncle confirmed he recieved the money, so hopefully tomorrow, or for sure monday your stuff will be shipped...\r\n\r\nHope that\'s cool and take care!'),(37399,'425cfad327','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7241&amp;start=30\r\n\r\nHey in the above thread you talk about using blue builders foam. Could you tell me the actual product name if you remember. I am in Toronto (Canada) and I am trying to find some. I went to home depot and they don\'t have anything like that (well anything that I or the staff could help me find.)\r\n\r\nTIA');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37401,'31c2239150','in your burning prog there should be a way to set the gap between audio tracks, check preferences or something.'),(37402,'8b2449b497','Bird has two sets he\'s willing to trade.  I\'m going over there tonight to pick them up.\r\n\r\nHe was wondering about some of the decals like you sent me.  He\'s not picky.  He said to be creative when trading.  (catch my drift?) :wink: \r\n\r\nI\'ll send them out sometime in the next couple of days. :-o'),(37841,'e74350e129','[quote:e74350e129=\"HirotoR34\"]definitely, I was thinking deans would do charging duties...I\'ll do you up a custom shell. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll be sure to add a bit o green :-o[/quote:e74350e129]\r\n\r\nWent out a few minutes ago.\r\n\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nMike'),(37842,'6f2213a0f3','Hey Darktari!\r\n\r\nHope everythings doing good. I just remembered that I needed to send you pics of what I have left. Are you still interested in anything? \r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJDM'),(37407,'bfcfcc6089','[quote:bfcfcc6089=\"blackranger3d\"]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7241&amp;start=30\r\n\r\nHey in the above thread you talk about using blue builders foam. Could you tell me the actual product name if you remember. I am in Toronto (Canada) and I am trying to find some. I went to home depot and they don\'t have anything like that (well anything that I or the staff could help me find.)\r\n\r\nTIA[/quote:bfcfcc6089]\r\n\r\nwell dont know the true name its insulation foam they put it behind walls like behind siding (outside walls) I got mine at Home Depot in the lumber section. The foam sometimes comes in pink and green but main color is blue. I think its called Celotex or close to that. Hope that helps let me know if you need more help.\r\n\r\nSWG');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37410,'3aa7c5b57a','[quote:3aa7c5b57a=\"steelwoolghandi\"][quote:3aa7c5b57a=\"sg219\"]Bird has two sets he\'s willing to trade.  I\'m going over there tonight to pick them up.\r\n\r\nHe was wondering about some of the decals like you sent me.  He\'s not picky.  He said to be creative when trading.  (catch my drift?) :wink: \r\n\r\nI\'ll send them out sometime in the next couple of days. :-o[/quote:3aa7c5b57a]\r\n\r\n\r\nwill do man do you want me to send my creativity to you or to bird? just let me know. I am on the road right now (selling) but when I get back will send some creativity out!\r\n\r\nthanks man!\r\n\r\nAaron[/quote:3aa7c5b57a]\r\n\r\nYou can send it to me.  \r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\n\r\nMike Smalley Jr.\r\n3918 Inland Ave.\r\nWest Mifflin, Pa 15122'),(37416,'5e90dbf532','[url]www.imageshack.com[/url]\r\n\r\nThat\'s free web hosting.'),(37443,'822139f470','Hey, I was wondering if you were looking for an MZM? I thought you were from MZR.'),(37444,'6eca7c833c','[quote:6eca7c833c=\"BoneyskinX5\"]Hey, I was wondering if you were looking for an MZM? I thought you were from MZR.[/quote:6eca7c833c]\r\n\r\nUm, yeah, sort of. I wasn\'t actively shopping for one, but if a good deal came along, I\'d consider it. You have one for sale?');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37445,'4b6d681893','From my last post I was thinking; out of that 5 dollar &quot;package&quot; the body would be 3 bucks, motor 1 and rims &amp; gears 1.  Since you want 16 bodies that would be 48 for just the bodies.  \r\nFor a volume discount, 40 and I\'ll take care of s&amp;h to you.'),(37434,'02cb671a14','Have you gotten that prize yet?\r\nI\'m guessing not. I just tried tracking the package and still has the same information as the day it was excepted.\r\nRidiculous.'),(37452,'7b7864938b','[quote:7b7864938b=\"SuperFly\"][quote:7b7864938b=\"BoneyskinX5\"]Hey, I was wondering if you were looking for an MZM? I thought you were from MZR.[/quote:7b7864938b]\r\n\r\nUm, yeah, sort of. I wasn\'t actively shopping for one, but if a good deal came along, I\'d consider it. You have one for sale?[/quote:7b7864938b]\r\nYes. It has an Xspeed motor, alloy rims, Proline 1/18th tires, Pti body, and LSSM. \r\n\r\nIf your interested, make me an offer.'),(37454,'0e27b1a1e4','How much would you want for the two Initial-D FD-RX7s, the yellow ones?\r\n\r\nI\'m looking to do an Initial D collection and dont have KT. I would like the cards, and the matching wheels and spoilers too, If thats not asking for to much.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37455,'2715fad915','5 bucks for both.  I\'ll look around for the rims, I have a big pile of them.  I DON\'T have the cards for those.'),(37533,'27d75272eb','I\'m having a little trouble figuring out what to do with my servo wires. The Gen1 has 3 wires and the iWaver has 2 I think. How did you wire up your board? Pics would help.\r\n\r\nHow do I tell the difference between 01 and 02 boards?\r\n\r\nThanx\r\nMaxx'),(37458,'63e626351a','Ok, sounds fair for shipped. Is a money order ok?'),(37465,'3195150390','My name is Rogelio Hernandez II. Or Roy as my common name. \r\n\r\nThe boddies are the yellow Initial D RX7s FD3S. I should be able to send it off by next weekend; I\'m flat broke right now.'),(37466,'10fbf61339','1x Starsky and Hutch Torino \r\n1x Silver Ford F150 \r\n1x f&amp;f green eclipse \r\n1x f&amp;f Orange Supra \r\n1x Yellow Trans Am 2002 or something \r\n1x Blue PT Cruiser \r\n1x f&amp;f evo\r\n1x 2f2f Purple Conv Eclipse \r\n1x f&amp;f rx7 red w/gray and black spoiler \r\n1x 2f2f rx7 red w/ yello no spoiler\r\n\r\nI have narrowed my needs down to 10 bodys and will offer $20 shipped, thats $2 a body, the amount RS is selling NEW ones for.'),(37467,'3195150390','My name is Rogelio Hernandez II. Or Roy as my common name. \r\n\r\nThe boddies are the yellow Initial D RX7s FD3S. I should be able to send it off by next weekend; I\'m flat broke right now.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37469,'e8ae2a400e','That sounds good.  Like I said, I was never in it to make cash so didn\'t know what reasonable would be for people.  Can you do paypal or plan on MO?  If paypal, my account is clxfiles@yahoo.com\r\nif MO send it to\r\n\r\nattn: Rodney Tapia\r\n7208 Johnson Dr.\r\nPleasanton, CA 94503\r\n\r\nWhat\'s your real name so I know who to expect from and what to send when I receive?\r\nAlso, what address do I send it to?'),(37470,'e8ae2a400e','That sounds good.  Like I said, I was never in it to make cash so didn\'t know what reasonable would be for people.  Can you do paypal or plan on MO?  If paypal, my account is clxfiles@yahoo.com\r\nif MO send it to\r\n\r\nattn: Rodney Tapia\r\n7208 Johnson Dr.\r\nPleasanton, CA 94503\r\n\r\nWhat\'s your real name so I know who to expect from and what to send when I receive?\r\nAlso, what address do I send it to?'),(37471,'f4c6039e8c','Hey that\'s cool.  I took a closer look at the bodies and one of them is about perfect with the rims that came with the original set.  The other one is good, would be perfect but I put an extra hole in the back window because I put a guitar string antenna for that car.  It does NOT have rims but if it\'s cool, I can put together a set of star rims that were slightly different from the ones it came with.  Probably look about the same.'),(37472,'12d31aff9c','http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/images/article_images/mods/flames_crazydave/flames_stencil.jpg');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37473,'894b54b233','Yeah I took a look at the Jeep body and I think it\'s in perfect condition.  I also found the rims and will send that with.  Please send the MM Camaro to:\r\n\r\nRodney Tapia\r\n128 Via Bellagio\r\nAmerican Canyon, CA 94503\r\n\r\nLet me know if you want to make any other arrangements.'),(37474,'87099e6c82','Yea, ill add it in the deal.  I just didn\'t think you would want it.  I\'m kinda new at this stuff and I dont really know the names of any parts.'),(37475,'2bb9bc8b7c','Ill trade for basically any of those bodies except for a couple.  like the pt cruiser, any jeeps or trucks or any cars that look like trucks or vans.  I\'m more into cars that look like cars, if you know what i mean.'),(37476,'e7b73d550b','I suggest you calm the fuck down.'),(37479,'975f88ee5d','you are a gaylord. o boy just get off the forum and yes this is the nicest i will be. and you suck at skating i will guaranteelly will do any trck better than you. haah gaylord. :noob:'),(37480,'975f88ee5d','you are a gaylord. o boy just get off the forum and yes this is the nicest i will be. and you suck at skating i will guaranteelly will do any trck better than you. haah gaylord. :noob:');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37481,'430fc47940','Ok.  I am typing how all of you type.  Are you happy now?  I just have one quick question:  Why did you spend all of your time typing that up?  I\'m not trying to criticize you or anything or say your a slow typer, I was just wondering.'),(37482,'35953b6835','Cuase I got other things going on. That\'s also why you piss me off by wasting my fucking time with your lil kid bullshit. Now take my lil bit of advice or don\'t. Your choice to make.'),(37483,'88f91a5558','gaylord? you have really good disses, yea fucking right. i bet you are just like the rt of all the nerds on this site.  your only friend is on guide wars or w/e its called. beotch'),(37485,'88f91a5558','gaylord? you have really good disses, yea fucking right. i bet you are just like the rt of all the nerds on this site.  your only friend is on guide wars or w/e its called. beotch'),(37491,'87099e6c82','Yea, ill add it in the deal.  I just didn\'t think you would want it.  I\'m kinda new at this stuff and I dont really know the names of any parts.'),(37492,'2bb9bc8b7c','Ill trade for basically any of those bodies except for a couple.  like the pt cruiser, any jeeps or trucks or any cars that look like trucks or vans.  I\'m more into cars that look like cars, if you know what i mean.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37508,'0b202c6fbf','mcg - beer - grog squad'),(37496,'f4c6039e8c','Hey that\'s cool.  I took a closer look at the bodies and one of them is about perfect with the rims that came with the original set.  The other one is good, would be perfect but I put an extra hole in the back window because I put a guitar string antenna for that car.  It does NOT have rims but if it\'s cool, I can put together a set of star rims that were slightly different from the ones it came with.  Probably look about the same.'),(37497,'894b54b233','Yeah I took a look at the Jeep body and I think it\'s in perfect condition.  I also found the rims and will send that with.  Please send the MM Camaro to:\r\n\r\nRodney Tapia\r\n128 Via Bellagio\r\nAmerican Canyon, CA 94503\r\n\r\nLet me know if you want to make any other arrangements.'),(37498,'c76e04302b','Will send the body out next week!\r\n\r\nlook forward to the trade.\r\n\r\nAddress:\r\nAaron Olmsted\r\n1941 Sayers Road\r\nBastrop, Texas 78602 \r\n\r\nthanks man!  :-)'),(37501,'e74e444546','&quot;i recently set up a workmate with a kyosho half 8, essential alloy is usually shock towers and knuckles. at this scale you want to minimize unsuspended weight like alloy arms. just see what (if anything) breaks&quot;\r\n\r\nyeah mate, I got thinking about the weight thing a little more and decided I wanted to focus more of performance (on both mini T &amp; Z).  Basically staying away from alloy as much as possible.  Found the stock suspension arms pretty durable (and super cheap to replace) so I\'ll be sticking with them for a while. Picked up a carbon front tower last weekend and it\'s already busted. Replaced it with a Dynamite alloy front tower today (same LHS as the CVD\'s, same discounted price). Speaking of CVD\'s picked them up today and holy shit what a difference. Easily makes the list of money well spent.\r\n\r\nNext on the list of upgrades is a new set of turnbuckles but I haven\'t decided which.  Is either going to be the Losi titanium or a set of Lunsford Punishers.  Lunsford\'s will be heaps stronger and come with a lifetime bend/break guarantee but I\'m curious to see what kind of breakage it\'ll result in.  The stock turnbuckles become pretzels with a decent hit no doubt absorbing much of the impact, Lunsfords won\'t meaning something else will have to give.  \r\n\r\nAt any rate, I\'ll have something race ready to beat around downunda.  Still waiting for the MR-02 to ship :/ Not too pleased with that but am holding off going off until I get the car.\r\n\r\nI arrive in Oz Aug 10 and spend the night of Aug. 11 at the MCG drinking at the Essendon vs. Collingwood match.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37502,'1e47fc811e','sounds like a hot little rig! i\'ll have to do some work on my mt just so i can keep up! :lol: \r\n\r\nmcg drinkin\' beer? bloody bewdy! :-o \r\nyou\'ll get a sneak peek during the commonwealth games 8-)'),(37515,'0e7cb308da','Comes with everything in the kit.  Stickers, body, everything.  I\'ll throw a battery in if I can find it.  No charger.'),(37516,'0686ffaf71','MRS4 $50 I\'d like it to be by money order.  Are you in the US?'),(37517,'0e7cb308da','Comes with everything in the kit.  Stickers, body, everything.  I\'ll throw a battery in if I can find it.  No charger.'),(37518,'f7c4a3fb12','Im sorry to be such a pain in the ass, but im not to familiar with the MRS4 so would it come with the ESC, RTR or does it still need some stuff to be RTR? thanks ahead :-o'),(37519,'ed98be5e82','I\'ll take the rolling chassis and I can give you the any of the following:\r\n\r\nThe list goes \r\nZZ bodys \r\n1x f&amp;f evos \r\n1x 2f2f Purple Conv Eclipse \r\n1x red porsche \r\n1x black porsche \r\n1x Orange 350z \r\n1x Purple PT Cruiser \r\n1x 2f2f Orange Challengers \r\n1x blue rx8 \r\n1x Xmen Chrome RX8 \r\n1x beat up mustang body 2000 or something actually ok shape just layers of paint. \r\n1x Yellow Civic \r\n1x Blue Civic \r\n\r\nZZSE bodies \r\n1x Trueno \r\n1x Levin \r\n1x Silver Escalade \r\n1x 2003 Mustang concept gray \r\n1x blue Audi TT\r\n\r\nWhen you decide let me know and send me your address.\r\nSend the Chassis to\r\n\r\nRodney Tapia\r\n128 Via Bellagio\r\nAmerican Canyon, CA 94503'),(37520,'592b7d6650','Ok.  Send the Yellow Honda Civic to:\r\n\r\nKent Andryski\r\n2728 132nd Lane NW\r\nCoon Rapids, MN, 55448\r\n\r\nThanks.  It might be about a week before you get it.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37522,'27430559f2','It\'s a &quot;kit&quot;.  It\'s not a rtr, only comes with servo and motor. And you have to rebuild the car.'),(37523,'0686ffaf71','MRS4 $50 I\'d like it to be by money order.  Are you in the US?'),(37524,'1082a594f9','Dude, I\'m sorry about that. I\'ll change my post too. I didn\'t see the money order thing, plus I\'ve already got too many toys. I don\'t know what I was thinking.\r\n\r\nYou won\'t have a problem selling it at that price however.\r\n\r\n-JNY'),(37526,'088ca1cc27','[quote:088ca1cc27=\"pimpsmurf\"]Dude, I\'m sorry about that. I\'ll change my post too. I didn\'t see the money order thing, plus I\'ve already got too many toys. I don\'t know what I was thinking.\r\n\r\nYou won\'t have a problem selling it at that price however.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:088ca1cc27]\r\n\r\nDo you use paypal?  That\'s my only problem, I don\'t have paypal.'),(37527,'592b7d6650','Ok.  Send the Yellow Honda Civic to:\r\n\r\nKent Andryski\r\n2728 132nd Lane NW\r\nCoon Rapids, MN, 55448\r\n\r\nThanks.  It might be about a week before you get it.'),(37528,'088ca1cc27','[quote:088ca1cc27=\"pimpsmurf\"]Dude, I\'m sorry about that. I\'ll change my post too. I didn\'t see the money order thing, plus I\'ve already got too many toys. I don\'t know what I was thinking.\r\n\r\nYou won\'t have a problem selling it at that price however.\r\n\r\n-JNY[/quote:088ca1cc27]\r\n\r\nDo you use paypal?  That\'s my only problem, I don\'t have paypal.');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37529,'27430559f2','It\'s a &quot;kit&quot;.  It\'s not a rtr, only comes with servo and motor. And you have to rebuild the car.'),(37531,'a64b9e8368','Why do you not like me I am just couris.'),(37536,'5f015c5ef3','i waver board got 4 wires 2 for motor and 2 for pot.\r\nxmod got a same thing. green and orange are for propo and blue and red are for motor. i used mini-ts servo, it also has 4 wires\r\ni\'ll send you pictures of the set up i have and pics of i waver board i used. in couple of days i will get some timeto dig it all up.\r\nmainly i have mini-zs electronics. the i waver conversion was done for a friend of mine. the ONLY bug about iwaver board is- weak steering. i think fet replacement would fix that .\r\ni wouldn\'t know about difference of i waver board gen1 or 2'),(37537,'345ac7709b','I got some help over msn from betty.k, so thanks, no need to dig up or tear down for lil ol me :)\r\n\r\nMaxx'),(37654,'2ecf29ca0f','Sorry to hear that, man.\r\n\r\nWhen my father was still alive, he and I had trouble talking, too.\r\n\r\nI feel for you man.\r\n\r\nNext time you\'re in the area, just say so.  If you wanna grab a coffee and talk XMODS or whatever, let me know.\r\n\r\nPaul');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37655,'2cdee31294','Yeah, I\'ll drop you a line if I\'m in the area.'),(37660,'723a57869c','Great fuckin info!!!\r\n\r\nThank you once again man...\r\n\r\n\r\nWell it looks like i am going to land myself an iwaver ball diff, and perhaps use the iwaver spring sets as well...\r\n\r\nI am going to look further into the oil damper, that is probably the best thing.\r\n\r\nLastly save up for some Gandini\'s....best places to buy them all is my next question big guy?'),(37661,'82cc0718b6','Hey man, I just received the body today.  Thanks a bunch.  I can\'t wait to see what you do with the Jeep.  I\'m a big fan of your work.'),(37662,'a836c5d501','My paypal addy is  skylinekid91@gmail.com  \r\n\r\nAnd what color would you like the CD cases in, and thanks very much for the support :-o'),(37664,'c7facb097f','[quote:c7facb097f=\"skylinekid\"]My paypal addy is  skylinekid91@gmail.com  \r\n\r\nAnd what color would you like the CD cases in, and thanks very much for the support :-o[/quote:c7facb097f]\r\n\r\nI\'m thinking about the colors and particular types of designs, will get back to you in a day or two. Thanks!'),(37667,'f54a927ecf','hi');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37669,'6eafe27116','Just wanted to confirm that you got the Civic body.  I haven\'t received anything yet but I can wait.  If you haven\'t got it, I did put a track on it.  go to www.usps.com and look up the trace number \r\n\r\n03052200000122175291'),(37670,'6eafe27116','Just wanted to confirm that you got the Civic body.  I haven\'t received anything yet but I can wait.  If you haven\'t got it, I did put a track on it.  go to www.usps.com and look up the trace number \r\n\r\n03052200000122175291'),(37680,'04d0bbcb6b','I don\'t remember if I told you or not but that deal with Skylinekid fell through so most everything in my list is available except the Jeep body and the yellow Civic.  Oh yeah, someone wanted me to hold the 2 yellow SE RX-7s.  He wants to do an Initial-D thing. \r\n\r\nSo whatever you want on my list.  Send me your address also so I can send them off t you.\r\n\r\nThanks'),(37682,'048f6c51b3','twenty shipped is cool, i\'d say another 10 or so for the controllers\r\n\r\njust checkin with my uncle to see if u can send the money to his paypal account...\r\n\r\nmsg me back and we can further discuss this later i have work');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37683,'f3291460cf','Your package was shipped today give it the usual 1-2 weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt'),(37685,'bb57955192','[quote:bb57955192=\"Tuner1989\"]Your package was shipped today give it the usual 1-2 weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\n---Matt[/quote:bb57955192]Thank you'),(37721,'f79508d385','That\'s cool pimp. If you want I will keep em aside for you? \r\n\r\nLet me know when you send the dough, and give me your mailing address when you are ready.\r\n\r\nTake care pimp'),(37772,'5e52184af4','Now I feel stupid, I had about half those pics on my HD already.   I\'ll take and post up some new ones for you right after I finish dinner.\r\n\r\nI\'m interested in seeing where this project goes'),(37773,'5e52184af4','Now I feel stupid, I had about half those pics on my HD already.   I\'ll take and post up some new ones for you right after I finish dinner.\r\n\r\nI\'m interested in seeing where this project goes'),(37774,'7b722dd43b','Shipped :cool: \r\n\r\nYou gonna be seein it by the end of the week :)');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37778,'57aa2be894','Hello,\r\n\r\nI took a look into the postage, seems like for a package up to a pound in weight the shipping is $17.50 (air mail parcel post).  Not sure if it\'s worth it at that price.  I can check with UPS to if you would like.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nRich'),(37871,'ab2aa352b2','...alright \r\n\r\nWhat\'s your email I will snap a few of the bodies and send em 2morrow...cool?'),(37891,'0e20fd9a59','I wouldn\'t mind helping you out, but I have just enough for one in each test car right now.  I\'ve got to keep one in each car to do the comparison essay I\'ve been working on.  Also the parts for each are starting to get scarse.  If I let one go, there\'s no garauntee that I\'ll get another anytime soon at a decent price.\r\n\r\nSorry to be a taco, but if it helps any, after I finish the next two cars reviews I\'m going to take a break from all the comparisons and go into motor construction.  I\'ll be making hand wounds, plasma-atomics and other types of motors and selling them.  There just isn\'t enough people that do that.  I know, that doesn\'t really help you out now.\r\n\r\nHave you looked into an Uberdash?  Also, an Anima modified motor or &quot;Fatboy HC&quot; as they call it at Atomic mods is also a good second.'),(37892,'0c760ffe9e','Someone asked that about the original spider turbo and a bunch of aussies got all ancy and started going off with &quot;Aaron did all the R&amp;D on this himself....blah blah blah&quot;. Then when someone, I forget who, got a defective one that blew his car, the car was sent to ph2t for repair. There\'s something about that in the throw \'em under the bus thread.\r\n\r\nSo I personally think its just a another group effort aussie marketing scheme. Those guys are always looking to cut a buck... but then again, they are a penal colony, kinda makes sense. :lol:  \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO `phpbb_privmsgs_text` (`privmsgs_text_id`,`privmsgs_bbcode_uid`,`privmsgs_text`) VALUES (37916,'8eb5a401bf','Redrustbucket posted this a coupla days ago... 4 posts down from yours.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=7607');
